      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_utxo%20rpc.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for UTxO RPC Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nEMURGO, as a DRep, supports the “UTxO RPC: Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration” proposal and votes YES on this governance action.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\nUTxO RPC plays a crucial role in the Cardano ecosystem by offering a standardized and developer-friendly interface for interacting with UTxO-based blockchains. EMURGO recognizes the importance of this tool in powering integrations for key applications such as Lace, Mesh, and Amaru. Continued development and support for UTxO RPC ensures stability, performance, and accessibility for projects building on Cardano. The proposal outlines a sustainable path forward with dedicated developer resources and community involvement, and its open-source nature ensures transparency and continuous innovation.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, EMURGO supports this initiative as a key infrastructure layer that enhances developer experience and supports long-term growth of Cardano’s technical ecosystem.",
