    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for UTxO RPC Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmauAkNy1zL28oXuJNabMUgrGDnTWtxgGwnLfbMVKwreoG -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for UTxO RPC Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nUTxO RPC is an important piece of open infrastructure that simplifies and standardizes how developers interact with UTxO-based blockchains like Cardano. Though still early, its adoption by major projects such as Lace, Mesh, and Amaru shows promising traction and ecosystem alignment.\r\n\r\nThis funding will allow the addition of 0.5 FTE blockchain developer and 0.125 FTE tech lead to sustain development and maintain momentum over the next 12 months. The entire development process will be public and open-source, supporting transparency and community contribution.\r\n\r\nGiven the importance of standardization, current adoption, and the robust accountability structure in place, I believe this proposal deserves support.\r\n\r\n本提案にYES票を投じます。\r\n\r\nUTxO RPCは、CardanoのようなUTxOベースのブロックチェーンとのやり取りを簡素化・標準化する、重要なオープンインフラです。まだ初期段階ではありますが、Lace、Mesh、Amaruといった主要プロジェクトによる採用が進んでおり、エコシステムとの整合性も見られます。\r\n\r\n今回の資金は、0.5人月のブロックチェーン開発者と0.125人月の技術リードの雇用に活用され、今後12ヶ月間の継続的な開発を支えるものです。開発プロセスはすべて公開・オープンソースで進められ、透明性とコミュニティからの貢献が促進されます。\r\n\r\n標準化の重要性、すでに見られる採用実績、そして信頼性ある体制を踏まえ、本提案は十分に支持に値すると判断します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/07_UTxO_RPC_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for UTxO RPC Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO casts a YES vote for the proposal “UTxO RPC: Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration” for the following reasons:\r\n\r\n1. Critical Infrastructure for Cardano Integration\r\n\r\nUTxO RPC provides a standardized interface for interacting with UTxO-based blockchains like Cardano. Already adopted by key projects such as Lace, Mesh, and Amaru, it plays a critical role in enhancing integration efficiency, reusability, and interoperability across the ecosystem.\r\n\r\n2. Reasonable and Essential Budget for Continued Maintenance\r\n\r\nThe proposal seeks funding for 0.5 FTE blockchain developer and 0.125 FTE tech lead—an appropriate investment to maintain and evolve a foundational component. Continuous updates and responsible resource allocation are vital to keep the tool secure, performant, and aligned with ecosystem needs.\r\n\r\n3. Trusted Vendor with Open-Source Commitment\r\n\r\nTxPipe, the vendor, has a strong record of delivery within the Cardano ecosystem, including successful Catalyst proposals. Their work is public and open-source, ensuring transparency and accountability throughout the development process.\r\n\r\n4. Secure and Transparent Fund Management\r\n\r\nThis proposal is managed by Intersect through rigorously tested smart contracts (developed by Sundae Labs and audited by TxPipe and MLabs). Milestones, fund disbursements, and delivery are overseen by a third-party assurance mechanism with on-chain transparency, ensuring proper and secure use of treasury funds.\r\n\r\n5. Developer Experience and Ecosystem Growth\r\n\r\nBy simplifying integration with Cardano, UTxO RPC lowers the entry barrier for new developers and projects. Its ongoing development will contribute significantly to a more accessible and developer-friendly ecosystem, which is essential for long-term growth.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO believes this proposal constitutes a strategic and justified expenditure that supports the infrastructure, security, and usability of the Cardano ecosystem, and therefore votes YES.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、「UTxO RPC: Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration」提案に賛成票を投じます。その理由は以下の通りです。\r\n\r\n1. Cardanoにおける重要なインフラ整備の継続\r\n\r\nUTxO RPCは、UTxOベースのブロックチェーンとのインターフェースを標準化するための仕様であり、Cardano特有の構造に適したRPC実装です。Lace、Mesh、Amaruなどの中核プロジェクトに既に採用されており、その重要性は明らかです。これらプロジェクト間での開発効率向上やコードの再利用性、相互運用性を大幅に高める役割を担っています。\r\n\r\n2. 開発と保守の継続に必要な適正予算\r\n\r\n今回の提案は、0.5 FTEのブロックチェーン開発者と0.125 FTEのテックリードを確保するための資金です。Cardanoエコシステムにとって基盤的なツールを持続的にアップデートし、セキュリティと性能を確保するには、開発の継続性と責任あるリソース配置が不可欠です。\r\n\r\n3. TxPipeによる信頼性の高いオープンソース開発体制\r\n\r\n提案者であるTxPipeは、Catalystにおいて過去にも複数の成功事例があり、Cardanoエコシステム内で継続的な貢献を行ってきた信頼ある開発者集団です。全ての成果物はオープンソースで公開され、透明性の高い開発が期待できます。\r\n\r\n4. 透明性と安全性のある資金管理\r\n\r\nIntersectが主導する本提案は、Sundae Labsが開発・TxPipeとMLabsが監査したスマートコントラクト群により、資金の分配、進捗管理、マイルストーン達成の検証がオンチェーンかつ第三者保証付きで実施されます。このような高度な管理体制は、Cardano財源の適切な使用を保証します。\r\n\r\n5. カルダノ全体の開発者体験を向上\r\n\r\nUTxO RPCの進化と保守は、CardanoにおけるdApp開発の敷居を下げ、開発者がより容易にエコシステムに参入できる環境をつくります。これは、持続的なエコシステム成長において極めて重要な要素です。\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、SIPOはこの提案がCardanoエコシステム全体の発展にとって重要かつ正当な支出であると判断し、賛成票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVaUuUjQhRzQTYEYEErBPXbEv6wTe5gisCpTtK77Ys2ZV -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for UTxO RPC Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious has voted in favor of all 39 Treasury Withdrawal proposals submitted. These proposals were selected through a well-defined process, and we fully support them out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
