      "voter": "DeepStatecraft",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeTPLiw2b9kwu98vZb5pD3XDumznCMUZAJhQmvEGGUg8c -->\r\n# DeepStatecraft\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Pallas Sustaining Critical Rust Tooling for Cardano\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfr0cur4guksjd6whxe5mltcaksqqhzd85dnq6lfk8ex7qs5mlcye`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n✅ Pallas Rust Tooling – ₳220,914\r\n\r\nWhy I voted YES:\r\nPallas is a foundational Rust toolkit for Cardano, powering essential infrastructure like Aiken, Mithril, Lucid, and Amaru. With 591 commits and 39 contributors, it’s one of the most active and widely used open-source libraries in the ecosystem. Continued funding ensures protocol compatibility, performance, and security as Cardano evolves.\r\n\r\nKey benefits:\r\n• 🧱 Provides core blockchain primitives for Rust development\r\n• 🔧 Enables rapid dApp/tooling creation without reinventing the wheel\r\n• 🚀 Actively used by major projects across the ecosystem\r\n• 🧑‍💻 Maintains open-source transparency and collaboration\r\n• 🔄 Keeps up with protocol changes and critical bug fixes\r\n\r\nSustaining Pallas means supporting the foundation that many Cardano-native tools are built on. It’s a small but vital investment in ecosystem health and developer experience.",
