    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Pallas Sustaining Critical Rust Tooling for Cardano\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRBoz9GMRRUyRPhp4SdV8WjNFueVFuCxrR53jY27Mn8Gm -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Pallas Sustaining Critical Rust Tooling for Cardano\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this treasury withdrawal proposal for Pallas.\r\n\r\nPallas is actively used by key projects such as Aiken, Lucid, and Mithril, serving as a core Rust-native toolkit for blockchain development. This funding supports 0.5 FTE blockchain developer and 0.125 FTE tech lead, and the cost appears reasonable.\r\n\r\nGiven its open-source nature and community-inclusive development model, I believe this proposal will enhance the developer experience and foster innovation across the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nこのPallasに関する財務引き出し提案に賛成（YES）票を投じます。\r\n\r\nPallasは、Aiken・Lucid・Mithrilなど多くの主要プロジェクトに活用されており、Rustベースの開発環境を下支えする中核的なライブラリです。今回の資金は、0.5人分のブロックチェーン開発者と0.125人分のテックリードの継続稼働を支援するもので、コスト妥当性もあると見ています。\r\n\r\nオープンソースでの開発継続や貢献の受け入れ体制も整っており、開発者体験の向上やイノベーションの土壌づくりに資する提案として支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/06_Pallas_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Pallas Sustaining Critical Rust Tooling for Cardano\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO casts a “Yes” vote on the proposal to withdraw ₳220,914 for the Pallas project. The reasons are as follows.\r\n\r\nPallas is a critical open-source Rust-native library that provides foundational blockchain components—such as cryptographic primitives and CBOR encoding—for the Cardano ecosystem. It plays a vital role in powering projects like Aiken, Lucid, Mithril, and Amaru, enabling developers to build robust tools and infrastructure with reduced complexity and increased reliability.\r\n\r\nThis proposal requests funding to sustain Pallas through 0.5 FTE of a blockchain developer and 0.125 FTE of a technical lead, ensuring ongoing maintenance, protocol updates, bug fixes, and feature development.\r\n\r\nMaintaining and enhancing Pallas is essential to the health and growth of the Cardano developer ecosystem. It improves developer experience (DX), fosters third-party tool diversity, and ensures that ecosystem tools evolve alongside the Cardano protocol itself. Its open-source nature, with 591 commits and 39 contributors, demonstrates both its maturity and strong community participation.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the budget is administered by Intersect with rigorous contract oversight, milestone verification, and the use of audited smart contracts for disbursement. The involvement of a third-party Assurer and external Oversight Committee ensures transparency and accountability in fund usage.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO believes this proposal represents a strategic and highly justified investment into the long-term sustainability of critical developer infrastructure on Cardano, and therefore supports it with a “Yes” vote.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、提案「₳220,914の資金をPallasプロジェクトのために引き出すこと」に賛成票を投じました。その理由は以下の通りです。\r\n\r\nPallasは、CardanoエコシステムにおけるRustベースの基盤ツールとして、極めて重要な役割を果たしています。暗号プリミティブやCBORエンコードといったブロックチェーンの基本機能を、Rustネイティブで再利用可能なコンポーネントとして提供することで、多くの開発者が高機能なウォレット、エクスプローラー、ノード実装等を迅速かつ安全に構築できるようになっています。\r\n\r\n本提案では、AikenやLucid、Mithril、Amaruなどのプロジェクトを支えるPallasの継続的な保守と機能追加を目的に、0.5人分のブロックチェーン開発者と0.125人分の技術リーダーの工数を1年間確保するための資金提供を求めています。\r\n\r\nこのような基盤的開発ツールが中長期的に持続可能であることは、Cardanoの開発者体験（DX）の向上、サードパーティ開発の活性化、ツールエコシステムの多様性と健全性の維持において不可欠です。Pallasがオープンソースであり、39人のコントリビューターと600近いコミット数を誇る事実も、コミュニティに根ざした活動の信頼性を示しています。\r\n\r\nさらに、資金管理・契約・マイルストーン報告はIntersectのスマートコントラクトシステムの下で厳格に運用され、第三者による検証体制も確保されています。この点においても、財務の透明性と説明責任が担保されており、安心して資金供給できる体制が整っています。\r\n\r\nしたがって、SIPOは本提案がCardanoエコシステムの基盤技術と開発者層の持続的成長に直結する重要な投資であると判断し、「Yes」票を投じました。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
