      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTGXDGNArKstZM8HWfBmyyaScfcXA2JEK3FXtP4DhUo5i -->\r\n# CardaFlow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough I was planning to support this proposal in previous Ekklesia's temp check, recent thoughts and warnings raised by Dave, the 4th of Aug: \"While the IceBreakers network appears community driven, it still continues to route all transaction traffic through Blockfrost’s Gateway,  giving them a technical edge over all other submission methods on Cardano. This creates a further technical advantage over anyone submitting transactions independently. We have to trust they do not use this solely for their own advantage. And most importantly, the revenue generated does not return to the treasury. Instead it strengthens Blockfrost dominant position. \". I may support it at a later point upon potential clarifications from Blockfrost.",
