      "voter": "Crypto_Oaj",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPDinMEyvMeCanPGwhUDAdijCkZNHQUussyKWJ7MyoSmq -->\r\n# Crypto_Oaj\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwlmrm6ksc8sa5fdhm63prqve6hjzvghdc3053zwz6hyeg0ayhg2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMany Cardano dApps rely on Blockfrost for accessing on-chain data. While Blockfrost has served the ecosystem well, its centralized nature creates a potential bottleneck and single point of failure — something that contradicts the long-term vision of Cardano's decentralized infrastructure.\r\nThis proposal introduces an open-source, decentralized alternative built on top of Blockfrost. By enabling the community to access on-chain data without relying solely on a centralized service, it strengthens the ecosystem’s resilience and promotes healthy infrastructure pluralism.\r\n\r\nWhile I believe the requested amount is relatively high — especially considering that Blockfrost has received prior investment from IOG and operates on a revenue model — I still vote YES because the strategic value of decentralizing access to on-chain data outweighs the cost concern. The proposal contributes directly to the robustness and sustainability of Cardano’s developer ecosystem.",
