      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmbCoFXhBjk1DzofvjrBDocErPrzwi9SYQok37LRcqCeko -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmWG5y7k2NgtV2RwzL4qEBGHCwSMAoKES8dDJ3xUA5eeB6\r\n\r\nI am voting **NO** due to the severe centralization risks this architecture introduces at the transaction submission layer.\r\n\r\nentralizing the `/tx/submit` endpoint through a single gateway creates a privileged \"pre-mempool.\" This gives one entity the power to censor transactions, front-run users, and perform MEV attacks. This architecture fundamentally undermines Cardano's core promise of being a **permissionless and censorship-resistant** network. The risk to users and ecosystem integrity is simply too great.\r\n\r\nDisappointing proposal.",
