      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmY9Wuq9zSvhhRepEyFFYe6G9qiaZAoHbZMCWcn9f1qNbe -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn alignment with my voting on the 2025 Cardano Budget Reconciliation process through Ekklesia platform, I support this withdrawal and therefore vote YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/blockfrost%20treasury%20withdraw.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Krypto Labs, engaged in the 2025 budget process since February, I am voting YES on the ₳1,300,000 Blockfrost Platform proposal.\r\nThis decision stems from Blockfrost's critical role in simplifying blockchain access, having powered most of transactions at peak on Cardano, and the urgent need to decentralize it via the Icebreakers program.\r\n\r\nThe proposal's strengths open sourcing components, rewarding SPOs with revenue sharing, and integrating for micropayments directly address centralization risks while empowering developers and operators.\r\nMilestones like 100 active Icebreakers by year end, tracked transparently on GitHub with audits, ensure accountability. Community endorsements from DReps emphasize its alignment with core engineering, decentralization priorities and potentially boosting adoption.\r\n\r\nMy involvement in workshops revealed Blockfrost's ecosystem value; approving this accelerates a resilient, SPO-driven network, fostering Cardano's growth without excessive risk.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kyle Solomon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adosiawolf/drep-rationale/refs/heads/main/0012 -->\r\n# Kyle Solomon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzshxuma6cwrnlv2ucyclfqw3k4nu4nuudmh2z87j9hncsk9dhy4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted YES on the current proposal to decentralize Blockfrost. Blockfrost is critical infrastructure for startups and lean initiatives looking for a viable entry point to engage with Cardano. I created Cardano's first token claim UX using Blockfrost APIs a few months before launching DripDropz",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LallyMcClay",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LallyMack/Drep-it/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(9).jsonld -->\r\n# LallyMcClay\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2dptycrks2ggae95leeh66m0l0svet98c44hl4rmaec7as6hgpp3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES to fund the Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal. This initiative supports decentralization of a critical API service through the Icebreakers program, empowering SPOs and node operators to deliver Cardano data in a more distributed, resilient way.\r\n\r\nThis aligns with my priorities as a DRep: strengthening open-source infrastructure, reducing centralization risks, and supporting long-term sustainability for developers building on Cardano.",
      "vote": "YES"
