    {
      "voter": "Reshma_Mohan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/resgsh/drep-mainnet/refs/heads/main/voting-activity/5.Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Reshma_Mohan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfcgvh8rum7a9ma4gwgwuwutdu0dnrzaj98jytwyfqzd87q2nehvm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOverall Rationale for Voting on Treasury Withdrawals\r\n\r\nAs a DRep participating in on-chain governance under the Voltaire framework, I have reviewed each of the 39 treasury withdrawal proposals currently up for vote.\r\n\r\nThis document outlines my generic voting rationale. My vote on each individual proposal—whether Yes, No, or Abstain—has been guided by the following considerations:\r\n\r\nWhen I Voted Yes\r\n\r\nI have supported proposals that clearly satisfy all of the following:\r\n\r\n1. Relevance\r\n   The proposal addresses a clear and meaningful need in the Cardano ecosystem—whether it is developer tooling, community infrastructure, governance, or research.\r\n\r\n2. Reasonableness of Budget\r\n   The requested amount is proportional to the scope and deliverables. Proposals that show cost breakdowns and attempt to maximise value for money are given priority.\r\n\r\n3. Credibility of the Team\r\n   Preference is given to teams with a proven history of delivery in the Cardano ecosystem, open-source contributions, or community engagement. In case of newer teams, supporting references or associations are considered.\r\n\r\n4. Alignment with Voltaire Governance Goals\r\n   In the Voltaire era, legitimate, transparent use of the treasury is essential. I support proposals that help establish or strengthen governance processes and infrastructure.\r\n\r\nWhen I Voted No or did not vote\r\n\r\nI have voted No where one or more of the above criteria are not met, such as:\r\n\r\n* Lack of clarity or relevance to Cardano’s needs\r\n* Justification regarding budgets\r\n* Weak or unknown team background\r\n* Vague deliverables or lack of public transparency\r\n\r\nIn some cases, proposals may be promising but are premature or underdeveloped at this stage.\r\n\r\nWhen I Abstained\r\n\r\nI have chosen to Abstain when:\r\n\r\n* The proposal shows potential but lacks enough information for a confident decision\r\n* There are mixed signals—e.g., a good idea but poor planning, or credible team but vague milestones\r\n* There may be overlap with other initiatives already underway\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nThis is a generic decision-making framework I have followed across all 39 proposals. Votes are cast independently for each proposal, and the default is not Yes. Instead, each proposal must make a clear case on its own merits.\r\n\r\nI remain open to feedback and discussion from delegators or community members regarding any specific vote.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nList of Proposals and My Vote\r\n\r\nMLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement: Cardano.nix - 45,217 ADA - Yes\r\nMidgard - Optimistic Rollups administered by Intersect - 2,162,096 ADA - Yes\r\n2025 Input Output Engineering Core Development Proposal - 96,817,080 ADA - Yes\r\nBlockfrost Platform community budget proposal - 1,300,000 ADA - Yes\r\nHardware Wallets Maintenance administered by Intersect - 424,800 ADA - Yes\r\nPallas: Sustaining Critical Rust Tooling for Cardano - 220,914 ADA - Yes\r\nUTxO RPC: Sustaining Cardano Blockchain Integration - 220,914 ADA - Yes\r\nLucid Evolution Maintenance administered by Intersect - 130,903 ADA - Yes\r\nzkFold ZK Rollup administered by Intersect - 1,161,000 ADA - Yes\r\nDolos: Sustaining a Lightweight Cardano Data Node - 220,914 ADA - Yes\r\nLedger App Rewrite administered by Intersect - 300,000 ADA - Yes\r\nComplete Web3 developer stack to make Cardano the smart contract layer for Bitcoin - 600,000 ADA - No\r\nOSC Budget Proposal - Paid Open Source Model for Sustainable Development - Not specified - Yes\r\nGerolamo - Cardano node in typescript - 578,571 ADA - Abstain\r\nMLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement: Plutarch - 243,478 ADA - Abstain\r\nTWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project... - 11,070,323 ADA - No\r\nCexplorer.io -- Developer-Focused Blockchain Explorer... - 266,667 ADA - Yes\r\nA free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers - 605,000 ADA - Yes\r\nAdaStat.net Cardano blockchain explorer - 212,000 ADA - Yes\r\nA MBO for the Cardano ecosystem: Intersect - 15,750,000 ADA - Yes\r\nBeyond Minimum Viable Governance: Iteratively Improving on Cardano Voltaire - Not specified - Yes\r\nCatalyst 2025 Proposal by Input Output - 69,459,000 ADA - Yes\r\nInput Output Research (IOR): Cardano Vision - Wor... - 26,840,000 ADA - Yes\r\nBloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement - 99,600 ADA - Yes\r\nCardano Product Committee: Community-driven 2030 Cardano... - 750,000 ADA - Yes",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZKZY5q1VqDyoUrwC6fhTyw5f9ms6u88uDSJ7XrAJFkNf -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this Treasury Withdrawal.\r\n\r\nBlockfrost has become a core part of the Cardano developer experience, providing reliable infrastructure to interact with the blockchain without the need to run a full node. This proposal supports the continued decentralization and open-sourcing of the platform through the Icebreaker program, allowing SPOs to process API requests and receive a share of the revenue.\r\n\r\nThe project is backed by trusted teams, including Five Binaries (the original developers), and is administered through Intersect with strong legal and delivery assurance structures. Milestones, contracts, and disbursements are managed transparently on-chain.\r\n\r\nThis is a strategic infrastructure investment aligned with Cardano’s long-term goals, and I support it.\r\n\r\nこのトレジャリー引き出し提案に対し、YES票を投じます。\r\n\r\nBlockfrostは、フルノードを稼働させることなくCardanoと連携できるインフラとして、開発者にとって重要な存在となっています。本提案は、SPOがAPIリクエストを処理して報酬を得られる「Icebreakerプログラム」を通じて、Blockfrostの分散化とオープンソース化をさらに推進するものです。\r\n\r\n開発元であるFive Binariesを含む信頼性の高いチームにより実施され、Intersectによる法的契約や進捗管理も整備されています。マイルストーンや支払いはスマートコントラクト上で透明に管理され、コミュニティによる監査も可能です。\r\n\r\nCardanoの長期的インフラ強化に資する戦略的な投資であり、支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/04_BlockfrostPlatform_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO voted “Yes” on the Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal.\r\n\r\nThe primary reason is that this is a “Withdraw” proposal, and we believe it is important to move forward with already-approved initiatives rather than allow them to stall. The Blockfrost team has played a significant role in supporting developers and the wider Cardano ecosystem, and this proposal represents an effort to decentralize their infrastructure — an important goal aligned with the Cardano Vision 2025.\r\n\r\nWhile we recognize the community concerns regarding centralization risks and potential transaction visibility issues, we reviewed the proposal in detail and noted several safeguards:\r\n\t•\tAll deliverables will be open-sourced, including the infrastructure and gateway.\r\n\t•\tThe Icebreaker system is designed to include SPOs and node operators as participants and revenue recipients.\r\n\t•\tThe roadmap explicitly includes a transition toward a Hydra-based micro-payment and decentralized service model.\r\n\t•\tGovernance mechanisms such as a future DAO and tax-based competition between gateways are under exploration.\r\n\t•\tRegular public reporting (monthly and quarterly) and a third-party security audit are planned.\r\n\r\nSIPO views this proposal as an initial phase of decentralization rather than entrenchment of central authority. Therefore, we support it with the expectation of visible progress and ongoing community scrutiny. We believe it is vital to test and iterate on such models as part of Cardano’s evolution.\r\n\r\nWe remain committed to monitoring implementation milestones and ensuring transparency throughout the process. Should the implementation deviate from the roadmap or fail to deliver on its decentralization goals, we will voice our concerns accordingly.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは「Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal」に対して「Yes（賛成）」票を投じました。\r\n\r\n主な理由は、この提案が「Withdraw（引き出し）」フェーズのものであり、すでに承認されたプロジェクトを停滞させず、スケジュールを前に進めるべきと判断したためです。Blockfrostチームは、Cardanoエコシステムと開発者コミュニティを長年支えてきた重要な存在であり、今回の提案はそのインフラを分散化するという、Cardano Vision 2025 にも合致した目的を持っています。\r\n\r\n中央集権的な構造やトランザクション可視化の懸念についても、私たちは提案内容を詳細に確認し、以下のような複数の安全対策が盛り込まれていることを確認しました：\r\n\t•\tインフラやゲートウェイを含むすべての成果物がオープンソースとして公開されること\r\n\t•\tIcebreaker システムは SPO やノードオペレーターを参加者・報酬受取者として組み込む構造であること\r\n\t•\t将来的に Hydra を活用したマイクロペイメント型の分散サービスモデルへの移行がロードマップに明記されていること\r\n\t•\tDAOやゲートウェイ間の「税制競争」など、さらなる分散化に向けたガバナンス構想が探索中であること\r\n\t•\t月次・四半期ごとの公開報告と、外部によるセキュリティ監査の実施予定があること\r\n\r\nSIPOとしては、この提案は中央集権の強化ではなく、「分散化への第一段階」と位置づけており、その前向きなステップとして賛成しました。ただし、進捗状況や運用体制については引き続きコミュニティ全体で監視し、透明性が保たれることが必要です。\r\n\r\n今後、提案されたロードマップに沿った進行がなされない場合や、分散化の方向性が損なわれる場合には、私たちも適切に意見を表明してまいります。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVaUuUjQhRzQTYEYEErBPXbEv6wTe5gisCpTtK77Ys2ZV -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious has voted in favor of all 39 Treasury Withdrawal proposals submitted. These proposals were selected through a well-defined process, and we fully support them out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfP7Q2FPBC8D289JwMaEUwehfi8v1KnQ91ikfBesbKzKg -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBlockfrost is a proven infrastructure provider that has meaningfully contributed to developer adoption on Cardano. This proposal aligns strongly with STORM Partners’ objectives by enhancing ecosystem efficiency and decentralizing access to critical APIs. The move to open-source and integrate SPOs through the Icebreaker program directly supports decentralization and reduces single-point-of-failure risks. We support this continuation of core infrastructure decentralization efforts.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SudoScientist",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arpradio/drep/refs/heads/main/Ecosystem%20Budget/blockfrost.jsonld -->\r\n# SudoScientist\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wtls7xh3a8gyepk540dgtzjzalk086gp4www6y0k0xjmqyk6gma`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile Blockfrost may in fact be the backbone of many web-apps, this proposal spends most of the time explaining what Blockfrost is and little describing what such a budget allocation would be utilized on.  Instead of requiring funds to ensure they can distribute their dominance, the decentralization of APIs is already upon us- alternatives like Koios have existed in parallel, and APIs like ANVIL are likely to shift the dynamics that the proposer builds their case from.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(7).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMy Vote: YES\r\nProposal Title: Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform Community Budget Proposal\r\nGovernance Action ID: gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlqyxzxz7k\r\nGovernance Action Type: Treasury Withdrawal\r\nSubmitted by: Intersect on behalf of Blockfrost\r\nLinked to Approved ₳275M Ecosystem Budget\r\n\r\nSummary of My Rationale\r\nAs a dRep, I have cast a YES vote on this treasury withdrawal because it funds essential infrastructure that powers a wide range of Cardano-based applications and services.\r\n\r\nBlockfrost provides developer-friendly access to the Cardano blockchain via APIs, removing the need for individuals or teams to run full nodes. It has been a critical enabler of dApp development across our ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThis proposal specifically supports:\r\n\r\nThe Icebreakers Program: A decentralization initiative that rewards Stake Pool Operators (SPOs) and node operators for handling API traffic, reducing centralization risks.\r\n\r\nOpen-source delivery: All tools and infrastructure funded by this proposal will be released under open-source licenses to ensure transparency, prevent vendor lock-in, and foster community innovation.\r\n\r\nAudited, milestone-based treasury disbursement: The ₳1.3M requested will be managed under strict legal contracts, released only upon verified completion of milestones, and tracked via smart contracts audited by MLabs and TxPipe.\r\n\r\nThird-party oversight: Intersect manages this project under the supervision of an independent Oversight Committee, including trusted entities such as Cardano Foundation, NMKR, and Xerberus.\r\n\r\nThis treasury withdrawal aligns with the approved ecosystem budget (gov_action1u9x73...), fulfills all constitutional requirements, and supports Cardano’s long-term goals of decentralization, developer accessibility, and infrastructure resilience.\r\n\r\nI believe this proposal is in the best interest of the Cardano ecosystem and its future.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Dutch Drep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmcNLzi6TjRSGFPJS7N7ghZifSkVaFw9giCupqfwC7GNRK -->\r\n# The Dutch Drep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yvve4554njxyun2s5p9q70v88d5jl7r0h34pjhw5f5tmw3sjtrutp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, The Dutch Drep, vote Yes on this withdrawal governance action for Catalyst 2025 Proposal by Input Output: Advancing Decentralised Community Innovation Funding & Infrastructure, administered via intersect. It is crucial for smaller development teams—especially those excluded by current thresholds—to be able to contribute to and grow with Cardano, as this grassroots onboarding drives innovation and problem-solving that fuels the ecosystem’s broader growth.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmPm8GZAySzVdvQLv3yG1MvYU6ctrzse5kMPwvVc683e1m -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmZkuQDhSG4M6zNdcebxGXKVgCSKF7RnAbh9c7vWFec8td\r\n\r\nA couple of months ago, I supported the resolution to bundle all of the Intersect Budget Proposals into 1 or 2 formal on-chain governance votes.\r\n\r\nEach of these proposals has already undergone extensive scrutiny and received 50% or greater support from the active DReps in the ecosystem, and I will honor that prior decision and the work these prospective developers have put in by voting yes on all the proposals from the Intersect Budget team.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmY3gUofxNQx8PmYPXZ4JGwysneYKcGiRtKSMUVARPtvzu -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes on the proposal to withdraw ₳1,300,000 to fund the Blockfrost Platform community budget. Blockfrost provides critical infrastructure that enables developers to build on Cardano without having to run and maintain their own nodes, significantly lowering the barrier to entry and accelerating ecosystem growth. This proposal outlines a broad commitment to making the service freely available to the community, which directly supports decentralized application development and experimentation. Given its proven utility, wide adoption, and the potential to amplify developer activity across the ecosystem, I believe this funding represents a high-leverage investment of Treasury resources.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXd99A6DgceUPRWnkZoKSyLkMJbfBCn3rBE7zremWZk23 -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBlockfrost is critical infrastructure but currently too centralized, risking Cardano’s core values. The Icebreakers initiative offers a promising decentralization approach but lacks measurable milestones, clear impact metrics, and a phased, accountable roadmap. \r\n\r\n₳1.3 million is a significant ask without sufficient proof of concept or alternatives considered. I vote NO. The proposal needs sharper KPIs, delivery milestones, independent validation, and risk mitigation before treasury funds should be committed.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNcwHAoMSM1ptLAB3U4fQ3hCxcz6y718csZnVU7Cn78QD -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBlockfrost delivers a secure and reliable API infrastructure and deserves support.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZQmF85v3McJCNZNvbc1TqwN9m6wPPYkGDiqYvN6qCNZ1 -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal aims to decentralize a key Cardano API through the Icebreakers program, I’m voting \"nay\" due to concerns about its necessity, unclear financials, and competing priorities. Moreover, I believe the Cardano treasury should prioritize projects with transparent budgets, immediate ecosystem impact, or support for existing decentralized alternatives like Koios. I encourage refining the proposal with a clear budget, evidence of SPO commitment, and a stronger case for why Blockfrost’s API is essential over alternatives.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Voice of the People",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DRepVoiceOfThePeople/VOP_Repo/refs/heads/main/VC20250718BlockfrostPlatformcommbudget.jsonld -->\r\n# Voice of the People\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ecrj7jd9alaxumvm49hgng9rp239nda5ucegd05ndvxfqftwr9f`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt's a good step in the good direction in order to decentralize API access via Icebreakers, boosting SPO revenue and developer usability",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Intersect_TWGA4.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: This is a general rationale we have prepared to support our “yes” vote on all the 39 treasury withdrawal actions. This follows careful review and consideration of the metadata of these treasury withdrawal proposals and hence is not a blanket voting practice.\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep Committee, have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawal governance actions currently live on-chain and submitted under the administration of IntersectMBO. These actions are the necessary implementation step following the community's approval of the ₳275.3 million Cardano Ecosystem Budget, the necessary budget info action that precedes the treasury withdrawal process. Our support reflects not only continuity with our earlier \"yes\" votes on the overarching budget info action and its constituent proposals but also our confidence in the smart contract guide and project execution mechanisms Intersect has established as an administrative body for these proposals.\r\n\r\nEach of these 39 withdrawals corresponds directly to proposals that have already passed a respective Budget Info Action with wide community and DRep support of 64.23%. As Wada DRep, we reviewed, scored, and supported many of these initiatives during the budgeting phase, using our internal ₳280M Net Change Limit framework. Our endorsement of the full ₳275.3M package was not a blanket approval but the outcome of detailed deliberation. Therefore, we see it as our responsibility to honor those community-approved funding decisions by affirming these follow-up Treasury withdrawal governance actions.\r\n\r\nImportantly, we are confident in Intersect’s role as the administrator of these treasury disbursements. We have independently reviewed the Smart Contract Guide, disbursement architecture, and accountability structures associated with these withdrawals. The use of milestone-gated smart contracts, multi-signature treasuries, and on-chain/off-chain tracking mechanisms provides strong assurance of transparency, risk management, and community accountability. We are particularly satisfied that Intersect has adopted security-audited contract templates and provides public documentation on how treasury funds will be administered, paused if necessary, and even returned if unused.\r\n\r\nIn our view, rejecting or abstaining from these Treasury Withdrawals at this stage would risk destabilizing delivery timelines, undermining community trust, and introducing administrative conflicts that may violate the spirit of the Constitution’s Articles on budgeting. We believe that treasury funding is not just about allocation; it’s about consistent and credible execution. As such, the DRep role requires continuity and follow-through, especially when prior voting outcomes have clearly mandated action.\r\n\r\nTherefore, in alignment with our constitutional responsibilities, community-aligned decision-making, and our assessment of Intersect’s administrative protocols, we have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawals Governance Actions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/18_2_default.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm defaulting to voting yes because there is some degree of consensus already achieved on each of these. So unless I have a significant issue with one of these proposals I will be voting yes on it.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPUbiAfxQBoZDxuBh5Sr9NziEyWGLqNHuoMbDAt3d4bK4 -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nYoroi as DRep votes YES on the governance action to fund Blockfrost Platform Community Budget Proposal based on the rationale below.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nAlignment with Decentralization: This initiative reduces reliance on a centralized API provider, empowering SPOs through the Icebreaker network.\r\n\r\nBuilder-Centric Impact: As a widely adopted platform, Blockfrost plays a key role in supporting developers. This proposal enhances that reliability.\r\n\r\nLayer 2 Integration: The inclusion of Hydra-powered micropayments supports efficient scaling and introduces a future-ready monetization path.\r\n\r\nWe believe this proposal directly advances Cardano’s technical goals and decentralization principles. Yoroi encourages ongoing delivery transparency and metric reporting as the program scales and has voted Yes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUNsjSzMu4HfpytqRLvRcbFMYVzsgH4R2GtH3PkP4mZW5 -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,300,000 for Blockfrost Platform community budget proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote as necessary to help Cardano grow into a platform that supports the economic identities of billions of people. This proposal charges a fair price to achieve what is needed to achieve that. \r\n\r\nThere are no significant matters that affect the neutrality of my decision-making.\r\n\r\nDetailed rationale and the improvements I would like to see made to the proposal are attached in the following spreadsheet \"TW vote #01\" or PDF.\r\n\r\nSpecifically with regards to bundled proposals, next time I would request that one of the following be implemented:\r\n\r\n1. Bundled proposals should be subject to a temperature check vote for each item. \r\n2. I would like bundled proposals to be verified or created by entities, consortia, or individuals selected by the DRep.\r\n\r\nSpreadsheet:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1M8JAuAntJOa7Z6j3GfC2hWFl4kbZLkzEel_cN4-kymw/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nPDF:\r\nipfs://bafkreianp5xhbo3ojlxqjjah4kyimr6u62uwnxd2t3lwwu3qmpn4jf4n5a\r\n\r\n私はCardanoが数十億人の経済アイデンティティを支えるプラットフォームへ成長していくために必要な投票を行います。この提案書は、それを達成するために必要な事項を実現するための正当なコストを請求しています。\r\n\r\n私の意思決定の中立性に影響を与える重大な事項はありません。\r\n\r\n根拠の詳細と、提案書について私が改善して欲しい点は、次のスプレッドシートの「TW vote #01」またはPDFに添付されています。\r\n\r\n特に、バンドル型提案書に関しては、次回は、次のいずれかが実施されることをリクエストします。\r\n1. バンドル型提案書は、内訳別の温度チェックの投票を行うこと。\u20282. バンドル型提案書は、DRepにより選出されるエンティティやコンソーシアムや個人により、検証または作成されるようにして欲しいと思います。\r\n\r\nSpreadsheet:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1M8JAuAntJOa7Z6j3GfC2hWFl4kbZLkzEel_cN4-kymw/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nPDF:\r\nipfs://bafkreianp5xhbo3ojlxqjjah4kyimr6u62uwnxd2t3lwwu3qmpn4jf4n5a",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    }
