      "voter": "DeepStatecraft",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qme3LShAN9xxEyjwPBSKNnaAjRzgiQBTaL7SsZ39vTgZFd -->\r\n# DeepStatecraft\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳15,750,000 for a MBO for the Cardano ecosystem Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfr0cur4guksjd6whxe5mltcaksqqhzd85dnq6lfk8ex7qs5mlcye`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n✅ Vote: YES on Intersect’s 2025–2026 Treasury Proposal\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES to fund Intersect, Cardano’s member-based coordination hub, for another critical year of decentralized governance and infrastructure support.\r\n\r\nWhy it matters:\r\n🧱 Core Infrastructure Stewardship\r\nIntersect maintains Cardano’s Haskell codebase, coordinates node releases, and leads safe network upgrades (Chang, Plutus V3, Conway).\r\n\r\n🔐 Governance Execution\r\nThey carry out the Administrator role defined in the Constitution — enabling treasury contracts, managing proposal vetting, and delivering legal oversight at scale.\r\n\r\n🤝 Community Coordination\r\nIntersect supports 30+ working groups, 8 elected committees, and formalizes participation through stipends, elections, and onboarding resources for DReps, SPOs, and the Constitutional Committee.\r\n\r\n📈 Roadmap & Budgeting\r\nThey facilitate long-term planning, rebuild budgeting processes, and enable scalable RFPs — including support for future plural Administrators.\r\n\r\n💡 This proposal reflects a new strategic direction under Jack Briggs, reaffirming Intersect’s mission as a neutral, accountable, and community-serving enabler of decentralized progress.\r\n\r\n🔗 Proposal on Ekklesia\r\n🔗 Intersect Knowledge Base\r\n🔗 Budget Info Action via GovTool\r\n\r\nWe need reliable execution, transparent governance, and operational continuity during Cardano’s most transformative phase. This is how we get it.\r\n\r\n#Cardano #Voltaire #Governance #Intersect #CardanoNode #OpenGov #VoteYES",
