    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BrianLee12/Cardano-Governance/refs/heads/main/NCL-2025/300M/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA NCL of 300 Million ADA is too high to be considered fiscally responsible. Submitted budgets have not reasonably proven this amount of ADA is necessary, so I cannot in good conscience approve this level of spending. \r\n\r\nI am willing to approve a NCL of ~200 Million ADA, and will do so if a GA is submitted to support this. \r\n\r\nIf we had community pooled GA supported tooling from Intersect / gov.tools / IOG this would be a non-issue, as average Cardano community members would have been able to submit their own GAs and this would be done already.\r\n\r\nI'm disappointed that this necessary tooling has been withheld and was promised as part of a compromise for a 100 Million ADA deposit for GAs",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Gnobudy Special",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gnobudyspecial/Cardano-dRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20NCL%20no.jsonld -->\r\n# Gnobudy Special\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygd5gumlv8jnramte9z2zvksvncgt06hyds4k6naq52hq7c05svs5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe proposed NCL's were not adequately informed by an open community engagement process.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXCR4W3hQKZfA9Z4onnpDUFA68g5z6SUvYUMuh14V1QUL -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES because:\r\n\r\n✅ The proposed Net Change Limits align with forecasted treasury inflows (≈300M ADA for 2025, ≈265M ADA for 2026), helping to keep expenditures within a safe range and ensuring responsible, sustainable treasury management.\r\n✅ It does not hinder Intersect’s operating budget (~260M ADA) while leaving room for strategic investments that support ecosystem growth.\r\n✅ Setting NCLs for both 2025 and 2026 helps prevent front-loading of spending into one year, promoting long-term, transparent budget planning.\r\n✅ Approving a baseline NCL now avoids the worst-case scenario where no limit is set—something that could invalidate budget proposals under current governance rules.\r\n✅ This is a community-led proposal, not initiated by founding entities, and demonstrates the growing maturity and self-governance of the Cardano community.\r\n\r\n💡 In the long term, I agree that the NCL should be defined as a percentage of treasury revenue to improve flexibility and predictability. However, at this stage, the proposed fixed amounts are a practical and necessary step to ensure budget continuity for 2025 and 2026.\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nVietnamese\r\n-------------------------\r\nTôi bỏ phiếu YES vì:\r\n\r\n✅ Phù hợp với dự báo thu ngân sách kho bạc (≈300 triệu ADA năm 2025, ≈265 triệu ADA năm 2026), giúp giữ chi tiêu trong ngưỡng an toàn và đảm bảo quản lý tài chính bền vững.\r\n✅ Không cản trở ngân sách hoạt động của Intersect (~260M ADA), đồng thời vẫn tạo dư địa cho các khoản đầu tư chiến lược nhằm mở rộng hệ sinh thái.\r\n✅ Việc thiết lập NCL cho cả hai năm giúp tránh việc dồn chi tiêu vào năm 2025, khuyến khích lập kế hoạch ngân sách dài hạn và minh bạch.\r\n✅ Việc phê duyệt NCL ngay bây giờ ngăn chặn kịch bản xấu nhất là không có giới hạn nào được thông qua – điều này có thể khiến các đề xuất ngân sách mất hiệu lực.\r\n✅ Đây là đề xuất do cộng đồng khởi xướng, không đến từ các thực thể sáng lập, thể hiện rõ sự trưởng thành trong năng lực tự quản của cộng đồng Cardano.\r\n\r\n💡 Về dài hạn, tôi đồng ý rằng NCL nên được tính theo tỷ lệ phần trăm doanh thu kho bạc để tăng tính ổn định và dễ điều chỉnh. Tuy nhiên, trong giai đoạn hiện tại, phương án đề xuất là thực tế và cấp thiết để đảm bảo tiến độ ngân sách năm 2025–2026 không bị gián đoạn.\r\n\r\n-------------------------\r\nJapanese\r\n-------------------------\r\n私は以下の理由から、このガバナンス提案に賛成票（YES）を投じます：\r\n✅ 提案されたNet Change Limit（NCL）は、予測されるトレジャリー収入（2025年：約3億ADA、2026年：約2億6500万ADA）と整合性があり、支出を安全な範囲に保ち、責任ある持続可能な財務管理を確保するものです。\r\n ✅ このNCLは、Intersectの予算（約2億6千万ADA）を妨げることなく、エコシステムの成長を支える戦略的投資の余地を残しています。\r\n ✅ 2025年と2026年の両年度にわたってNCLを設定することにより、支出の前倒しを防ぎ、長期的かつ透明性のある予算計画を促進します。\r\n ✅ NCLを今この段階で承認することで、何の制限も設定されない最悪の事態を回避できます。そうした場合、現行のガバナンスルールの下では予算提案が無効になる可能性があります。\r\n ✅ この提案はコミュニティ主導であり、創設団体によって提出されたものではありません。Cardanoコミュニティの自律性と成熟度の高まりを示しています。\r\n\r\n💡 長期的には、NCLはトレジャリー収入に対する割合（パーセンテージ）として定義されるべきだと考えています。これにより、柔軟性と予測可能性が高まります。ただし現時点では、今回提案されている固定額は、2025年および2026年の予算の継続性を確保するための、実用的かつ必要なステップです。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmbAHLS2ryA3Z8mF8kcd4rECHcDN7o5FbwQvDrWLaTaubh -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting Yes on a treasury net change limit of 300 million ADA for 2025 and 250 million ADA for 2026. This is a conservative maximum that only allows to spend what the treasury will earn in these years according to my predictions in https://forum.cardano.org/t/fundamental-critcism-of-the-budget-process/143519#p-367722-net-change-limit-2 (which are even cited in the proposal).",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Homer J",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hodlonaut/a/9d9f71f0db75534d92e75703da0f85114e83a3da/vote3.jsonld -->\r\n# Homer J\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rvnp40ea4zsl4hqm0ev4qju205jx7mz57u2vwjzzrf50c24jca9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNot a fan of giant bulk withdrawals from treasury, prefer larger number of smaller withdrawals that would get approved based on their merit by the community governance. Furthermore, if the community feels strongly enough we need to have these sorts of limits, I'd recommend implementing it at the protocol parameter level, so the values can be managed/adjusted without resorting to InfoActions or even being able to be dynamically adjusted based on some other variables/parameters.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/InputEndorsers/DRep-InputEndorsers/refs/heads/main/VoteNCL-2025-2026.jsonld -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile there seem to be some open questions surrounding the definition of NCL in the Cardano constitution, I will sidestep that issue here. \r\nThe reason why I am voting against the proposed governance action is because it wishes to set a Net Change Limit for two years in one swoop. \r\nThis not only weakens the chances for the motion to pass, but it also makes it less clear what needs to be corrected if the motion fails. \r\nFuture proposers should probably focus on proposing a Net Change Limit for one year, due to the slow nature of decentralized governance. \r\nFinally, I was not convinced by the motion that there is an absolute need to set an NCL for 2026 this early, as it is March 2025. A lot can happen between now and 2026, setting a 2026 limit seems premature - hence a bad precedent. \r\nI welcome the attempt by the proposers to highlight a need for conservative spending, by roughly limiting the NCL to the volume of of Cardano annual treasury inflows in 2025 and 2026.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "JNTHN_BRGS",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JonathanBRGS/DRep/refs/heads/main/ID_AG_7f320409d9998712%2B%2B%2B.jsonld -->\r\n# JNTHN_BRGS\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2yppwm9hvwdnh38fznaug4qy86zfvsmsrqlyvdqk22s2xgmqn42k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile we agree with the need for predictability and sustainability in Cardano’s Treasury, we do not agree with the proposed measures. Establishing percentage limits would be the best way to provide predictability and sustainability to the Treasury. See Constitutional Amendment No. 95 of 2016 of the Federative Republic of Brazil, which establishes that the growth rate of public spending will be limited to the percentage growth of the national GDP. Despite the many problems of the Brazilian administration, Constitutional Amendment No. 95 of 2016 is commendable. We do not consider it prudent to approve GAs that require subsequent approvals. The proposed results and effects of GAs should depend as little as possible on the approval of other GAs. Despite the negative response, we commend DRep’s intention to promote stability and predictability in the Treasury. We respectfully ask you to improve the proposal so that we may agree in the future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_NCL_300M.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting no on this net change limit action because I believe it is too low of a treasury expenditure when faced with the current development requirements of the Cardano ecosystem.  My primary focus in decision making currently revolves around increasing transactions in both volume and type.  Cardano has not yet fully realized the original road map and still needs to fully implement Basho era advancements and upgrades.  Current restrictions on speed and transaction volume are severely inhibiting adoption of the Cardano ecosystem and its overall marketshare of the crypto domain space. The Cardano treasury is projected to grow by about 320 million ADA in 2025, therefore setting a NCL of 300 million ADA is too conservative at this stage in Cardano's development.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/19APR2025-ljxu5/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote no on this “Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA” Info Action for the following reasons:\r\n\r\n1. Interpretive ambiguity and arguable establishment of a perpetual-until-superseded 250M ADA net change limit beyond 2026.\r\n\r\nIf passed, this Info Action would set net change limits of 300M ADA for 2025 and 250M ADA for 2026. While the Info Action states “The Net Change Limit beyond 2027 is not defined in this governance action” and “The Net Change Limit shall be effective for the period specified in this action,” it also provides that “In the event that a mutually agreed Net Change Limit is not established for subsequent periods, the most recently approved Net Change Limit shall remain in force by default.” Taken together, these statements are in tension and create unnecessary ambiguity. If interpreted in light of the latter statement, and unless a subsequent NCL Info Action superseded it, this Info Action would set a default NCL of 250M ADA in perpetuity. \r\n\r\nIn effect, this Info Action would remove the first stage of deliberative friction in the Treasury Withdrawal sequence of NCL Info Action, to Budget Info Action, to Treasury Withdrawal Action. Whether or not this reduced friction would serve the long-term interests of Cardano and our Community is an open question, and we lack the benefit experience to evaluate the need for such a change. Given the historical propensity of wide swings in ADA-fiat conversion value, fluctuations in the Treasury’s balance, and a multitude of other intrinsic and extrinsic variables, I’m of the opinion that a more intentional exploration of this change and additional experience should precede such a change. While I’m not inherently opposed to multi-year NCL Info Actions, I am opposed to setting a perpetual, default 250M ADA NCL beyond 2026 at this juncture.\r\n\r\n2. Misstating the NCL Info Action passage threshold\r\n\t\r\nThe relevant guardrail, TREASURY-01a, is found in Appendix I, Section 3: “A net change limit for the Cardano treasury’s balance per period of time must be agreed by the DReps via an on-chain governance action with a threshold of greater than 50% of the active voting stake.”\r\n\r\nThis Info Action misstates the relevant threshold when asserting: “In accordance with the Constitution, this action shall be considered ratified with a threshold of greater than 67% of the delegated ada to DReps voting in favor.” While endeavoring to garner 67% approval is a positive goal, the relevant guardrail controls — meeting a threshold of greater than 50% results in passage.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kronoshus/KevinMohr/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20Net%20Change%202.jsonld -->\r\n# Kevin G Mohr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe net change limit is too high for each year defined in this governance action. I will be voting no.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/ycxpn5tz -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting YES on setting the Net Change Limit to 300M ADA for 2025 and 250M ADA for 2026. Below, I'll briefly explain my reasoning in a way that's easy to understand, balanced, and respectful to everyone involved.\r\n\r\nWhy YES?\r\n\r\nResponsible Spending: Approving a clear spending limit ensures we only use funds that come into the treasury, avoiding the risk of rapidly draining resources we've carefully built up over time. It's similar to spending only what you earn, which helps keep finances healthy for the long term.\r\n\r\nFinancial Stability: This approach keeps our reserves intact, ensuring that we always have resources available to support important and worthwhile projects in the future. It’s like maintaining savings for unexpected or valuable opportunities rather than spending it all at once.\r\n\r\nClear Boundaries: Setting explicit limits provides clarity for everyone involved. It makes future budget decisions easier, clearer, and more transparent.\r\n\r\nPossible Concerns & Counterpoints\r\n\r\nCentralization Concerns: Some are concerned that Intersect or any specific organization might gain too much control over how funds are distributed. This is a fair concern—central control can create inefficiencies or lead to decisions that don't align with the broader community's interests. I acknowledge this worry and share the view that future allocations must remain transparent, decentralized, and closely monitored.\r\n\r\nFear of Bureaucracy: There's also a concern about overly complex procedures that might slow down decision-making or reduce transparency. It's important that future processes remain simple, clear, and easy to follow for everyone involved.\r\n\r\nBalanced Perspective\r\n\r\nThis YES vote doesn't mean automatic trust in any organization; rather, it's a practical first step toward responsible financial management. It sets a sensible boundary for spending, ensuring funds are used thoughtfully and sustainably. Future proposals on specific budget items must still undergo careful review, transparent discussion, and broad community agreement.\r\n\r\nTo those voting NO or having doubts: your concerns about centralization, transparency, or spending oversight are valid and important. My YES vote aligns closely with these principles, aiming to protect our treasury and ensure financial responsibility for the benefit of the entire Cardano community.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kit Willow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYNavCunPd5j2QMtFxEiD8afgiB5VT1FQqzkD97WgBJHU -->\r\n# Kit Willow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygk7qax0ztrv7a7unzgs4apj5mhk5a0058ne3fgfftj4tmgvuk5a7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI didn’t vote “YES” on this governance action for Net Change Limit because of the fact that it fixed this year, 2025 NCL to be way more than next year, 2026 at 300 million ADA to\r\n250 million ADA respectively. I thought it’d have made more sense for the reverse (ie; 250 for this year and 300 for next year) since — to my understanding — we only have about six months to execute this year’s budget and a full year for next year. \r\n\r\nOther than that fact, however, I find no other issue with this proposal, but since I could not — in good conscience — ignore the discrepancies with the number and also at the same time dismiss the rest of the proposal by voting no because of that. Hence, I hereby vote “ABSTAIN”",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/05/NCL25_26.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI decided to vote YES on this \"Info Action\" for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nMy approach on budget spending is relatively conservative. I am in favor of being watchful on how funds are spent.\r\n\r\nI recognize that this is the first time we are doing this procedure and we would make errors along the way. I've come to accept that we would be far from perfect in allocating the funds on the first year but we would learn from our mistakes and optimize.\r\n\r\nA budget of 300 million ADA doesn't mean we have to spend it all. It's just a cap to ensure we don't overspent. I've seen in the corporate world how leftover budgets often get wasted at the end of the year just to avoid having a smaller budget the next year. While this isn't exactly the same with Cardano (since we have a say in individual proposals and have a vested interest in protecting the treasury & Cardano's price), it's still a risk we need to manage.\r\n\r\nThe reasoning behind setting the budget at 300 million ADA for this year and 250 million for next year makes sense. It's based on the money coming in from transaction fees. Essentially, we're not spending more than we earn each year.\r\n\r\nI would have preferred to decide on the 2026 budget separately after we've gone through the 2025 process and gained some experience. However, since we can always vote again and change next year's limit later, I'm okay with this proposal.\r\n\r\nThe blockchain space is super competitive right now, and it's crucial that we invest enough to stay ahead. Even though I'm generally cautious about spending, I believe we need to invest more now to gain momentum. We can always be more conservative later.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/NCLfirstInfoAction.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nKrypto Labs, a Cardano DRep, backs the NCL of 300 million ADA for 2025 and 250 million ADA for 2026, matching forecasted inflows (300M, 265M). Favoring a fixed amount over a percentage for clarity, this aligns with Article IV and Appendix I’s guardrails (TREASURY-01a),  threshold of greater than 50% of the active voting stake. It ensures treasury sustainability, funding growth to boost Cardano’s layer 1 status, while allowing future adjustments. As community members, Krypto Labs warns delays risk opportunity loss, urging approval to maintain financial stability and ecosystem appeal, per the Constitution’s decentralized governance principles.",
