      "voter": "Martin Lang",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gitmachtl/cardano-related-stuff/refs/heads/master/vote_21032025.json -->\r\n# Martin Lang\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwmwvtd0a8lr45ssner2tjxzv5y8q03w3606yeald9mdmgmwecja`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, i have voted ✅NO at this point in time, because we are lacking a fundamental definition about what this 'Net Change Limit' actually is. We need a written and approved text for that first. Is is just the Sum of all Treasury Withdrawals in a year? Is it the change of the absolute Treasury balance which also includes new inflow from tau taxes? When does a 'year' actually start? From the moment a proposal like this is voted on, from the first action doing a Treasury Withdrawal, from the moment the first Rewards are getting transfered? I'am sorry, but this is too unspecific for me.",
