      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmbYSJ681XnfZJ5zS7zkbrZzWfLi2y3CnXeefAMeLDq52w -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Voting Rationale\r\n- Governance Action ID: gov_action10ueqgzwenxr39le68n0se9peu92r7gm2846xwehh3u0ahc0qd0uqqyljxu5\r\n- Metadata Anchor URL: https://github.com/blockchainada/ga/blob/2aa3ae45702caf35560eed2846f825b1d4846b90/ga01.jsonld\r\n- Metadata Anchor Hash: a2fa375274a2c5efa985a1e9811f27ea1ebf8b8dd88cdf9931a5aa856c73832a\r\n- Title: Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n- My Vote: NO\r\n\r\n### Reason for Voting NO\r\nMy decision stems from the mutability of the metadata anchor URL provided. On March 16, 2025, the hash of the metadata file at the provided URL briefly did not match the provided metadata anchor hash `a2fa375274a2c5efa985a1e9811f27ea1ebf8b8dd88cdf9931a5aa856c73832a`. Although the proposers later reverted these changes (see commit https://github.com/blockchainada/ga/commit/2aa3ae45702caf35560eed2846f825b1d4846b90, where the metadata was restored to its original state), the metadata remains mutable and could be altered at any time.\r\n\r\n### Why This Matters\r\nAll governance action metadata files should be hosted on immutable storage solutions such as IPFS, Filecoin, or Cardano-specific platforms like IAGON. Immutability ensures the integrity and trustworthiness of the information. Allowing metadata to be altered post-submission undermines the democratic process, opening the door to manipulation or misinformation. This is not only highly problematic but also violates the core principles of transparency and accountability that are fundamental to decentralized governance.\r\n\r\n### Recommendation\r\nI appreciate the proposers’ quick action to revert the metadata changes. However, I strongly urge them to adopt immutable storage solutions for all future governance actions. This step is essential to uphold the integrity of the governance process and maintain trust within the Cardano community.",
