    {
      "voter": "Peter Horsfall",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/peterhorsfallblockchain/DRep/refs/heads/main/Gov_Proposal_PH_Net_change_limit.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Horsfall\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set 2025 Net Change Limit of 300M ADA, 2026 Net Change Limit of 250M ADA\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytfas4axhm8yzrqqh4ru2uuqesu87zeq6fwg5pq8azqf7ecu4nu8s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter evaluating this governance action, I would vote \"Yes\" because the proposed Net Change Limits of 300M ADA for 2025 and 250M ADA for 2026 align conservatively with forecasted treasury inflows, ensuring sustainable spending while allowing flexibility for future adjustments if higher limits are deemed necessary. To improve this Info Action, I suggest including a clear mechanism or timeline for reviewing and adjusting the Net Change Limit mid-period if unexpected changes in treasury inflows or ecosystem needs arise, enhancing adaptability. For consideration, we (DReps should weigh whether the fixed ADA amounts might limit responsiveness to ADA’s price volatility, potentially justifying a supplementary percentage-based approach in future proposals to better account for economic fluctuations.",
