    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZMKP78R32N1nFthoW5Lpj2mahDKYaUwJFjNrAKKKryrC -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSecuring the .ada and .cardano generic top-level domains (gTLDs) strengthens Cardano’s global identity and digital infrastructure. It protects critical naming assets from third-party control, ensures long-term brand integrity, and opens new possibilities for ecosystem-wide innovation — including verifiable Web3 integrations, decentralized identity, and trusted domain-based services.\r\n\r\nAs this initiative is funded entirely by the Cardano Foundation and does not draw from the treasury, it poses no financial risk to the community. The proposed Community Advisory Group and public reporting commitment further align with decentralization and transparency principles.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Cypherpunks",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaxgnsvyzeuynakipj6jiyddiatchsq7vlyzrbamtpmfp2trmjdra -->\r\n# Cardano Cypherpunks\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23wk4w6f2aumc92vl9m3x74xzm6jh4ha9wdq09yfq2sl6q8zlv4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWill vote no as long as the foundation does not allow community participation",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Feed",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreic7gqa26u26ih3drtsw6h5bzvzilv2hjpemh5auyyimdhtqn2bsiu -->\r\n# Cardano Feed\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftjewhpvtdd8t7swtmtp44px94ns3laytmjc3u7f93qvhswmwv5f`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this initiative from the Cardano Foundation to register the .ada and .cardano gTLDs with ICANN. This is a strategic move to strengthen Cardano’s digital identity, enhance visibility, and create new opportunities for innovation and interoperability between Web2 and Web3. By using its own resources and involving the community through transparent governance and advisory structures, the Foundation demonstrates responsible leadership and long-term vision for the ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmeV9f2ooWxUwyJ45U1kkK9xvb3fnFf2Sn2A8tRVMtFBnU -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmaSJguB46QP11NRHsB91stkzdojBsdMoEBJhz1QtYRHjb\r\n\r\nThis info action, submitted by the Cardano Foundation, serves a clear purpose: to gauge on-chain community sentiment and gather a formal record of support for a potential ICANN application for the .ada and .cardano gTLDs.\r\n\r\nOur decision to vote \"YES\" on our own proposal is based on the following:\r\n- **Our Role as a Community DRep:** The purpose of this info action is to measure community support. As a DRep, the Cardano Foundation represents not only its own organizational stance but also the will of the community members delegating their ada to our DRep. We are a part of the community, and we are voting for this strategic initiative on behalf of our delegators as we believe it would be a positive course of action.\r\n- **No Cost to the Treasury:** This is not a request for treasury funds. The Cardano Foundation has committed to using its own financial resources for the entire ICANN application and management process. This info action is purely a request for community endorsement, making it a simple and high-value proposition for ada holders to support. \r\n- **Strategic Importance:** Securing the .ada and .cardano gTLDs is a rare, time-sensitive opportunity that aligns with the upcoming ICANN application window in Q1 2026. These gTLDs are vital for the ecosystem's long-term brand protection, digital identity, and ability to foster Web2-to-Web3 innovations.\r\n- **Commitment to Community Governance:** The Cardano Foundation, as a non-profit dedicated to the development of Cardano as a public digital infrastructure, is the right long-term steward for this project. The proposal's plan to establish a dedicated Community Advisory Group to guide the gTLDs' development ensures this project will be managed in the ecosystem's best interest.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmTbKoFT7NJH41n1GS5HKuvgz6Ugx216zcvcueqGcejf8E -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/Qmd8fDvvZ1Apjq51Fajv4L8KXD5c8moM2GXMAv8DcQbLqq\r\n\r\nSecuring “.ada” and “.cardano” prevents other parties from registering those top-level domains, thereby reducing phishing risks, brand dilution, and confusion.\r\n\r\nA verified .cardano TLD could help users visually identify trusted services at a glance. If the Cardano Foundation (CF) strictly controls who can register under \".cardano\" or \".ada\", then users can reasonably assume that \"myapp.cardano\" or \"wallet.ada\" is officially connected to the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThis is similar to \".gov\", \".edu\", or \".bank\" — restricted domains that communicate legitimacy because registration is verified and centrally governed.\r\n\r\nHaving ecosystem-specific domains enables use cases such as human-readable wallet addresses (e.g., “yourname.ada”) and domain tokenisation, as well as decentralized identity integrations.\r\n\r\nThese domains should be owned by the Cardano community. Only legally established entities can claim ownership of these domains, so it is necessary that one of the founding entities, such as CF, technically owns the domains.\r\n\r\nI assume that the costs of securing the domains will be covered by Genesis coins. This is a desirable use of resources. I appreciate that CF is seeking DReps' approval for this operation. I also appreciate that CF is not seeking ADA from the Treasury and is committed to covering the annual operating costs associated with maintaining the domains in the estimated amount of $350,000.\r\n\r\nCF owns the Cardano brand, so it is a suitable entity to manage the domains.\r\n\r\nCF becomes the registry operator, meaning it controls all second-level domains. CF has not yet given a detailed plan for subdomain access or policy.\r\n\r\nIn the proposal, CF promises to establish a Community Advisory Group (CAG) to define policies and oversee responsible operation. Unfortunately, it is not defined how many members the committee will have, what their composition will be, whether DReps will participate in the decision-making, and who will have the final say (whether CF or CAG).\r\n\r\nIt should also be clarified whether it will be necessary to pay for obtaining a subdomain and what the potential revenue streams will be. Furthermore, how the profit will be used.\r\n\r\nI believe in the good intentions of the Cardano Foundation regarding the management of top-level domains. They were the first to take the initiative, and they want to manage the domains and will even cover the costs associated with the acquisition and operation of the domains. I support this initiative.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
