    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA072-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action15dh2lt4qskmhl97vat8s0l552ruvddrlasa0jndg7lg43g0uju3qq78hvja), pois ela tem como objetivo fortalecer a identidade digital do ecossistema Cardano, garantindo que os domínios .ada e .cardano permaneçam sob gestão da comunidade. A iniciativa amplia a visibilidade do ecossistema, estimula a inovação entre os mundos Web2 e Web3 e assegura transparência e governança aberta, beneficiando toda a comunidade Cardano. Além disso, a proposta define que os fundos a serem utilizados serão aqueles já empenhados pelo tesouro à Fundação Cardano, não gerando, portanto, novos gastos ou ônus adicionais.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action (gov_action15dh2lt4qskmhl97vat8s0l552ruvddrlasa0jndg7lg43g0uju3qq78hvja), because it aims to strengthen the digital identity of the Cardano ecosystem, ensuring that the .ada and .cardano domains remain under community management. The initiative enhances ecosystem visibility, promotes innovation between Web2 and Web3, and ensures transparency and open governance, benefiting the entire Cardano community. Furthermore, the proposal clarifies that the funds to be used are those already allocated by the treasury to the Cardano Foundation, thus not creating new expenses or additional financial commitments.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "punkr",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigthirba4iyg2l72lkqsjjeekjftjtdlsxjplp63ro2hqyqa7skdi -->\r\n# punkr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfyl9j6amk940g76r7ujnn5gywnjenv3kmun3a5tr5a83psl4vv64`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation securing .ada and .cardano domains with their own money is a smart, no-cost way for the community to protect and boost Cardano's brand.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWvLeMLbfVP3bYEpEJsHsrxERRSBWZ5j5LoBW2ZRd9wTV -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am choosing to **Abstain** on this Info Action. While I understand the strategic interest in securing the .ada and .cardano top-level domains, and I recognise that this proposal is constitutionally sound and funded entirely by the Cardano Foundation, there are important areas of uncertainty that prevent me from endorsing it at this stage.\r\n\r\nAlthough gTLD ownership may offer long-term benefits to Cardano’s digital identity and public presence, the proposal leaves several key aspects of future governance undefined. The Cardano Foundation positions itself as the long-term operator of these domains, yet the framework for how this control will be exercised has not been clearly established. Issues such as policy-making authority, pricing, dispute resolution, and integration with on-chain identity systems remain open-ended. The proposed Community Advisory Group is mentioned, but its role, selection process, and actual influence are unspecified.\r\n\r\nThese gaps may seem minor today because this action does not enact anything directly. However, the implications for Cardano’s future identity infrastructure are significant. Without clarity around stewardship, accountability, and the boundaries of centralized authority, I am not comfortable offering an explicit endorsement. My abstention reflects the need for a more detailed governance structure before moving from community sentiment-gathering to implementation.\r\n\r\nThis decision should not be read as opposition to the idea itself. Rather, it signals caution. The action is framed as a simple request for community support, but I sense that its downstream impact could be more substantial than the proposal communicates. Until there is more transparency around how these domains will be governed and how the community’s interests will be protected, I cannot vote Yes with confidence.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, RCADA Abstains, and encourages clearer governance definitions and oversight mechanisms before future steps are taken.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiarvkrtrtbmtwqxircb3jr7jt7dwwxvmrxiedxyykbbcnlwdl6lbm -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of this info action. I appreciate the fact that the Cardano foundation has decided to consult with the community before making this decision. I have reservations about the impact of this action but one thing I am sure of is that the blockchain space has a serious image problem with regular people. Having our own domain names is a small but positive step to improve the image of our particular corner of the space and I think it would be worth doing.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTcbCssRZnwh1UHFySjZacbhRpNg57dpgvV8nDj6hL9vQ -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES.\r\nSecuring .ada and .cardano is an important step for Cardano’s digital presence and future.\r\n\r\nWith community oversight and transparent operational rules, I would feel fully confident moving forward.\r\nYES, with that expectation.\r\n\r\n僕は YES に投票します。\r\n.ada と .cardano の取得は、Cardano の存在感と将来にとって重要な一歩です。\r\n\r\nまた、コミュニティによる監督と透明な運用ルールが整えば、より安心して前に進めると考えています。期待を込めて YES です。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaomsizkbk6o5zttanwop6cnmtu5eyup5t2afkhy3qruinezf73da -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO votes YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nI see this initiative by the Cardano Foundation to secure the .cardano and .ada generic top-level domains (gTLDs) as a meaningful and strategic step toward strengthening Cardano’s digital sovereignty and global presence.\r\n\r\nFrom SIPO’s perspective, this proposal beautifully aligns with Cardano’s founding values of trust, transparency, and institutional integrity—principles that have guided the ecosystem since its inception.\r\n\r\nWhy SIPO supports this proposal\r\nIn today’s digital world, controlling one’s namespace is as fundamental as owning a nation’s domain (.jp, .us).\r\nBy registering .cardano and .ada under ICANN, the Cardano Foundation will ensure that our ecosystem has a secure, officially recognized digital identity—protecting it from impersonation, fraud, and misrepresentation.\r\n\r\nThis is not just about brand protection.\r\nIt’s about positioning Cardano as a reliable, institutionally integrated blockchain, capable of bridging the traditional Web2 world with Web3 innovations.\r\nThe Foundation’s decision to fund this initiative entirely from its own financial resources—without drawing from the community treasury—makes this proposal both low-risk and high-impact.\r\n\r\nStrategic significance (SIPO’s view)\r\nShort-term:\r\nSecuring .cardano and .ada gTLDs protects the Cardano brand from misuse and establishes a trusted namespace for official ecosystem entities, DApps, and projects.\r\n\r\nMid-term:\r\nThese domains can evolve into gateways for DID (Decentralized Identity) integration—enabling individuals, companies, and even municipalities to connect their digital identities to Cardano through verified domain-based trust layers.\r\nProjects like Veridian and collaborations such as Chainlink ACE could directly benefit from this foundational infrastructure.\r\n\r\nLong-term:\r\nIn the future, .cardano could become the foundation of a decentralized DNS (dDNS) layer—bridging Web2 and Web3 through Cardano’s unique governance and consensus mechanisms.\r\nIt represents an Internet-level unification of blockchain identity, policy, and governance under one interoperable trust system.\r\n\r\nAddressing possible concerns\r\nSome may argue that ICANN registration introduces a centralized element.\r\nHowever, SIPO views this as a hybrid institutional approach—one that complements Cardano’s decentralized ethos with real-world recognition and regulatory compatibility.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the Cardano Foundation’s commitment to:\r\n\t•\tPublish transparent operation data, and\r\n\t•\tEstablish a Community Advisory Group\r\n\r\nensures accountability and community oversight throughout the process.\r\n\r\nBroader implications\r\nThis proposal marks an important milestone in Cardano’s “Constitutional Era.”\r\nBy securing its namespace at the highest level of the Internet infrastructure, Cardano takes a step closer to becoming a globally trusted digital institution—an ecosystem that not only runs decentralized finance and identity, but also embodies the principles of legitimacy and public trust.\r\n\r\nSIPO believes this initiative will:\r\n\t•\tStrengthen Cardano’s brand protection and credibility\r\n\t•\tEnhance ecosystem interoperability\r\n\t•\tSupport global adoption through recognized institutional frameworks\r\n\r\nand, most importantly, demonstrate that Cardano stands for trust, transparency, and responsible governance.\r\n\r\nFinal stance\r\nSIPO votes YES\r\nBecause this proposal isn’t just about domains—it’s about Cardano claiming its rightful place in the fabric of the Internet itself.\r\n\r\nA blockchain that aims to serve governments, institutions, and communities must also anchor itself in the digital systems those actors trust.\r\n.cardano and .ada are not vanity names—they are the next foundation for a verifiable, interoperable, and future-proof Web3 identity ecosystem.\r\n\r\nSIPO proudly supports this initiative.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOはこの提案に対して 賛成（YES） の立場を取ります。\r\n\r\nカルダノ財団が .cardano と .ada のジェネリックトップレベルドメイン（gTLD）を確保しようとしているこの提案は、\r\nカルダノの「デジタル主権」と「グローバルな存在感」を確立するうえで、非常に象徴的かつ戦略的な一歩だと考えています。\r\n\r\nSIPOは、この動きがカルダノが掲げる 信頼（Trust）・透明性（Transparency）・制度的整合性（Institutional Integrity） の価値観と完全に一致していると感じています。\r\n\r\nSIPOがこの提案を支持する理由\r\n現代のインターネットでは、「名前空間の主権を持つ」ことは、国家が自国ドメイン（.jp や .us）を持つのと同じくらい重要です。\r\n.cardano と .ada をICANNの正式なgTLDとして登録することは、カルダノが公式なデジタルIDを確立し、\r\n詐欺やなりすましからエコシステムを守るための基盤を築くことにつながります。\r\n\r\n単なるブランド防衛にとどまらず、\r\nWeb2とWeb3の橋渡しを行う「制度的に信頼されたブロックチェーン」として、カルダノを次の段階へ導くものです。\r\n\r\nさらに、この取り組みはカルダノ財団の自己資金によって実施され、トレジャリー資金を使わない点でも、コミュニティにとってリスクの少ない前向きな提案です。\r\n\r\nSIPOの戦略的評価\r\n短期的意義（ブランド防衛）\r\n.cardano と .ada の取得により、カルダノブランドの信頼性を守り、公式プロジェクトやDAppのための安全なドメイン空間を確保できます。\r\n\r\n中期的意義（DID統合基盤）\r\nこれらのドメインは、将来的に 分散型ID（DID） と統合されることで、\r\n個人・企業・自治体が「ドメインを通じて信頼を証明する」Web3インフラとして機能します。\r\nCardano Foundationの「Veridian」や、Chainlinkの「ACE」といった提携領域でも、この基盤が大きく活かされます。\r\n\r\n長期的意義（インターネット層統合）\r\n将来的には .cardano が 分散型DNS（dDNS） として機能し、\r\nWeb2とWeb3をカルダノのガバナンス層を通じて統合する未来も見えます。\r\nこれは、ブロックチェーンの制度的信頼と技術的分散性を結びつける新たなモデルです。\r\n\r\n懸念への対応\r\nICANNとの契約が「中央集権的ではないか」という指摘もありますが、\r\nSIPOはこれを制度的信頼と分散性を両立させるハイブリッド型アプローチと捉えています。\r\n\r\n財団はすでに以下を明言しています：\r\n\t•\tドメイン運営データを定期的に公開すること\r\n\t•\tコミュニティ諮問グループ（Community Advisory Group） を設置すること\r\n\r\nこれにより、透明性とコミュニティの監視体制が確保される点を高く評価します。\r\n\r\n広い文脈での意義\r\nこの提案は、カルダノが進む「憲法期（Constitutional Era）」における重要な制度整備の一例です。\r\nカルダノがインターネット基盤そのものにおいて、自らの名前空間を確保することは、\r\n“公共としてのブロックチェーン” を世界に示すシンボリックな行動だとSIPOは考えています。\r\n\r\nこの取り組みにより：\r\n\t•\tカルダノのブランド信頼性が高まり\r\n\t•\tエコシステム全体の相互運用性が向上し\r\n\t•\t公的機関・企業・市民が安心して接続できる“制度的Web3”が構築される\r\n\r\nと確信しています。\r\n\r\n最終コメント\r\nSIPOはYESを投票します。\r\nこの提案は単なるドメイン取得ではなく、\r\nカルダノがインターネットそのものの中で、自らの信頼構造を確立するための第一歩 だと考えています。\r\n\r\n政府・企業・自治体と共に歩むブロックチェーンであるために、カルダノは現実社会の制度的枠組みとも接続する必要があります。\r\n.cardano と .ada はそのための新しい「信頼の入口」なのです。\r\n\r\nSIPOはこの取り組みを強く支持します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcbwWrnQ7gf5HmzYjtw6HTpjPsY8bHDKejh35vX9MzFR2 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe voted in favor of this proposal. Securing the .ada and .cardano domains will help protect Cardano’s brand identity, improve discoverability, and ensure trusted representation of the ecosystem on the internet.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTvR5wJiPiTEpMU4wgu2EHstmJLV7i17CuxQkkHxtQQnz -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSTORM Partners is voting YES to support CF’s proposal to secure the .ada and .cardano domains for the ecosystem. The initiative aligns with CF’s stewardship of the Cardano trademark and strengthens the network’s digital identity. It could enable meaningful integrations between Web2 and Web3 by bridging traditional DNS infrastructure with projects such as Handshake, ADA Handle, and other emerging identity or decentralized naming solutions. CF is well-positioned to manage these domains responsibly and ensure they serve the ecosystem’s collective interests. By bringing this initiative on-chain, CF seeks community input that reinforces its legitimacy and increases the likelihood of successfully securing the registrations through ICANN.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SudoScientist",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arpradio/drep/refs/heads/main/top_level_domains.jsonld -->\r\n# SudoScientist\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wtls7xh3a8gyepk540dgtzjzalk086gp4www6y0k0xjmqyk6gma`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I can see the interest in obtaining such domains, I do not believe that leveraging such \"unique\" domains achieves any meaningful outcome.  The task of expanding our ecosystem, in my opinion, is not achieved by showcasing domains that would indicate exclusivity.  There are cases where others may want to obtain vanity domains, but this is not a pursuit that provides many benefits to the ecosystem as a whole, and therefore, should not use treasury funds to pursue.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidodzc6cwdrh3l3qwsdi4ds37b5zvdc7gixv3a5orxyq3jokd5fvy -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on this Governance Action.\r\nHere’s why:\r\n\r\nZero cost to the treasury – The Cardano Foundation(CF) is fully self-funding the $185k+ ICANN application and all ongoing registry costs. The ecosystem risks nothing and gains everything.\r\n\r\nPermanent brand sovereignty – Securing .ada and .cardano in the Q1 2026 window locks in our identity before speculators can squat or dilute it. We control our digital front door.\r\n\r\nReal utility & adoption flywheel – Native domains enable human-readable addresses (you.ada), decentralized sites, and seamless Web2 to Web3 onboarding. This is infrastructure, not vanity.\r\n\r\nIronclad community safeguards – The Cardano Foundation commits to:\r\n\r\ni. Public dashboards on registrations & revenue\r\nii. A Community Advisory Group with real policy influence\r\n\r\nMissing this window could mean paying millions later or never getting the names at all.\r\nVoting YES costs 0 ADA and secures a generational asset. I urge every SPO, DRep, and delegate to do the same.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfVt8pnFXVEvMocfztNDR6YkoLW2KxBTdChPkugUEHKRJ -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile this is potentially useful and we appreciate the fact that CF is consulting DRep even if they are not required to.\r\nHowever Cardano ecosystem is in dire need to support developer ecosystem, RWA and DeFi so CF should spend every single resource working on those to save Cardano from dying a slow death.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Terminada",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://terminada.io/gov-acts/20251022-securing-domains/vote-context.jsonld -->\r\n# Terminada\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytf9f78k7rkwk4cu6l2nvna22keu9yus4kqzc0hqspd36uszu0xc2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCardano Foundation asserts that it operates independently of the community and its board members are not elected or appointed by the Cardano community.  Cardano Foundation's decision making process lacks transparency.  IntersectMBO is a better entity to manage these top-level domains.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmT9d2GUQE1SAgGcuHqcfCedRWJkGE39AgT8tZr1wHchnN -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting YES because this protects Cardano's brand at zero cost to the treasury. The Foundation is self-funding this effort while the rare ICANN application window is open. Securing these domains prevents misuse and enables future innovations in user experience and identity.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TOPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifd2b7xvhozpubmnuyjk7kqnnqhoix5enz2r5xmlzrzcd6zk5g7fq -->\r\n# TOPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt5qwxtmcsns42cjtn7w97ws4vxvxs28hr85rfkn7gd7gmgypa5d7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDefinitely a great idea, I wanted to do this myself at some point.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUDmj7KyxHKtSbFuwe82gFLNXyEcWFPLWELBh99YyhhJv -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Foundation argues for digital presence and infrastructure positioning, and I accept the premise that owning strategic TLDs can confer branding and control benefits. However, **Cardano’s marginal returns from a gTLD, even if secured, are speculative compared to direct investments in developer grants, tooling, Hydra/L2 growth, or enterprise integrations. **The proposal does not quantify expected ecosystem value (revenue, user adoption, developer activity) relative to alternative uses of Foundation effort and community attention.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, **ICANN gTLD ownership is not the only, nor necessarily best, route to achieving the stated objectives. **The Foundation must justify why owning the TLD is superior to these options (e.g. strategic agreements with blockchain-native naming providers such as Unstoppable Domains) and creating seamless resolver bridges to Cardano wallets.\r\n\r\n**Owning .ada and .cardano could be valuable, but only if justified by demonstrable demand, robust risk mitigation, and a clear alternatives analysis showing gTLD ownership is the best way forward and necessary for adoption. **\r\n\r\n**The Foundation covering costs is laudable, but that alone does not justify asking the community for an endorsement that would commit our reputation and governance machinery to a materially risky program.** ICANN gTLD applications may expose the ecosystem to significant, uncertain financial burdens (contention auctions, legal/IP disputes, and ongoing operational scaling) and reputational/legal liabilities absent rigorous contingency planning and governance safeguards.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdCuPF9382u9fpQVoLtTGrYXQtL3PfR5jGrsMP4rwCY14 -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support the Cardano Foundation's initiative to register and utilize the two gTLDs, particularly since the Foundation will fund and manage the costs using its own ADA holdings. My sole concern is the absence of details on average domain pricing for potential buyers compared to existing market rates. Nevertheless, I have faith that all aspects will be executed in the collective interest of the Cardano ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbNFpEZRoPPWUzsyUa9WgXouwQwmjv3eDkFaRMVFnpVgY -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this proposal because securing the .ada and .cardano gTLDs represents a strategic opportunity to strengthen Cardano’s digital identity and bridge Web2 and Web3. It’s especially encouraging that the Cardano Foundation is funding this initiative entirely from its own resources, minimizing financial risk to the community. The commitment to transparency and community guidance through an advisory group further reinforces trust in the proposal’s long-term value.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiej6ytxiliedhryqxa3zsnrynateh4ymmbyaaf2itleoex5zfubtq -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe have reviewed the governance action to secure the .ada and .cardano top-level domains and find it to be a strategically necessary step for the long-term health of the Cardano ecosystem. The application window for generic TLDs opens only once every decade or more, and missing it would leave these namespaces vulnerable to commercial capture, domain squatting, phishing misuse, or fragmentation across unrelated entities. Ensuring that these domains are held by an ecosystem-aligned organisation is therefore a matter of digital self-determination rather than branding convenience, and we recognise the Cardano Foundation’s intention to protect these namespaces for community use rather than any proprietary purpose.\r\n\r\nWe also recognise that this proposal does not request treasury funds. The Cardano Foundation commits to financing the ICANN application from its own resources, meaning this governance action is solely a request for ecosystem endorsement. In our view, this is an appropriate moment for such consultation because the decision carries long-term implications for public-facing identity, trust, and cohesion across Web2 and Web3 ecosystems. A lack of ecosystem backing would weaken the legitimacy of the application, while community support strengthens the case that these domains serve a public-interest function rather than a corporate one.\r\n\r\nThe extended discussion on the Cardano Forum hosted by CF provides valuable context. Stakeholders broadly support the strategic intent, while raising questions about governance, transparency, and long-term operational models. The Foundation’s responses: its commitment to establishing a Community Advisory Group, publishing operational metrics, and treating the namespace as public infrastructure, indicate a willingness to incorporate community influence into the process. These early conversations give confidence that the Foundation acknowledges the public-good nature of the TLDs and is prepared to steward them in a participatory manner.\r\n\r\nWe note that this Info Action is intentionally high-level, as many operational details cannot be defined until after ICANN approval. Choices around pricing, allocation, dispute procedures, or registrant eligibility fall naturally into the post-approval phase when the constraints and obligations of the contract are known. We expect those specifics to be co-developed with the community through the promised advisory structures and future governance actions. Given the nature of the ICANN process, seeking detailed operational plans at this early stage would be premature. What matters now is the strategic decision to secure the namespaces before the window closes.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, we are satisfied that the idea presents a clear strategic benefit with minimal risk and aligns with the broader ecosystem’s interest in safeguarding public infrastructure. We therefore vote yes in support of this info governance action, with the expectation that the Foundation follows through on its commitment to transparent, community-guided management of the TLDs once acquired.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreif2446ea27ksxgndv7gzxijuhn2dkxmcslfsygncrqz2swfoglcem -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Securing Generic Top-Level Domains for the Cardano Ecosystem\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Summery\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation wants the community to commit to supporting their effort to acquire the rights to the `.ada` and `.cardano` domain names. They say nothing about sharing revenue from the sale of such domains with the treasury.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Conclusion\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIt would be inappropriate to grant the Cardano Foundation more control over the ecosystem. These domain names would serve as appeals to authority. If they were under the control of the Foundation, it would give them influence over who is perceived as credible and who is not. I am voting against this.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
