      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaUTE4Tw3AQ3gTxWHnVQTr9LZyYgUeqwwHZqvv3tAFAJa -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Net Change Limit (Epoch 613 to Epoch 713)\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA Net Change Limit is required by the Constitution. Without it, treasury withdrawals cannot proceed.\r\n\r\nThis sets a cap, not a spend. Each withdrawal still requires its own vote and scrutiny.\r\n\r\nThe amount reflects realised inflows and prior DRep-approved budgets. The extended period improves governance continuity and can be adjusted later.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I vote YES.",
