    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmU3UNvNJDeaZig7e8VeMkPidP5WftfHCYYsPVFjxQK8kZ -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Dolos Sustaining a Lightweight Cardano Data Node\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmbP4SdF3PkdY7o97aQTVqAt6QadFcWftLXApW6yCVvgtm\r\n\r\nI am voting a strong **YES**. This is a direct investment in the **decentralization** of Cardano's infrastructure layer.\r\n\r\nThe high cost of running a full node is a centralizing force. By providing a lightweight alternative, Dolos empowers more developers and teams to run their own backends, reducing reliance on a few large API providers. This enhances ecosystem resilience and **sustainability**. My continued confidence in the TxPipe team to deliver critical, open-source public goods makes this an easy decision.",
