    {
      "voter": "Maureen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTaLw4YkJki4ihprtYqsQtrTSkjMKbCmBM9jk43FXZF1p -->\r\n# Maureen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Dolos Sustaining a Lightweight Cardano Data Node\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y22hlaj8wuyygpnjy5cf96tg9tgvjrz39kxvqgv898uj9scfc55t7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTxPipe builds quality tools, but we already have a confusing array of node options. Developers regularly ask \"which node should I use for what?\" Adding another specialized implementation doesn't help that confusion, it makes it worse.\r\nFocus on making the existing tools better and more accessible instead of proliferating options.",
