    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Dolos Sustaining a Lightweight Cardano Data Node\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmP3XNtbmKFYveoUrfW7Sh1cbBZShHJB4daFhLLoQUhzp8 -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Dolos Sustaining a Lightweight Cardano Data Node\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nDolos is a lightweight Cardano data node designed to serve as a reliable backend for dApps, providing efficient, resource-friendly access to ledger data. Unlike full Cardano nodes, Dolos minimizes infrastructure costs while maintaining data integrity and responsiveness. Its open-source development is active, with contributions from over 20 developers and increasing adoption within the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThe funding will support ongoing development with 0.5 FTE for a blockchain engineer and 0.125 FTE for a tech lead, ensuring Dolos evolves with upcoming Cardano upgrades.\r\n\r\nGiven the rising need for scalable and developer-friendly backend solutions across the ecosystem, continued support for Dolos is technically sound and strategically aligned with Cardano’s growth.\r\n\r\n本提案に YES 票を投じます。\r\n\r\nDolos は軽量なCardanoデータノードとして、dAppのバックエンドに適した信頼性の高い台帳アクセスを実現します。フルノードとは異なり、リソース消費を最小限に抑えつつ、高い応答性とデータ整合性を維持する設計が特長です。すでに20名以上の開発者が参加する活発なオープンソースプロジェクトであり、採用も進んでいます。\r\n\r\n本提案により、ブロックチェーンエンジニア（0.5人月）とテックリード（0.125人月）の人員が確保され、今後のCardanoアップグレードに対応する開発が継続されます。\r\n\r\n軽量で開発者フレンドリーなデータ基盤はCardanoエコシステムにとって重要なインフラであり、Dolosへの継続支援は戦略的にも技術的にも適切と判断します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/10_Dolos_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳220,914 for Dolos Sustaining a Lightweight Cardano Data Node\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports the proposal to fund Dolos with ₳220,914 because it provides a lightweight, efficient, and open-source data node solution that directly benefits the Cardano developer ecosystem.\r\n\r\nDolos addresses a specific and important infrastructure need: providing real-time, trusted access to ledger data with minimal resource usage. Unlike a full node, Dolos offers optimized performance tailored for backend use in dApps and light clients. It is already gaining adoption, with over 360 contributions from a growing open-source community.\r\n\r\nThe requested funding will support 0.5 FTE for a Blockchain Developer and 0.125 FTE for a Tech Lead to ensure Dolos continues evolving alongside Cardano’s protocol updates. This maintenance is essential as Cardano grows in complexity and transaction volume.\r\n\r\nThe proposal is submitted by Intersect and will be managed under a legally binding contract with full transparency and milestone-based disbursement. Intersect’s oversight mechanisms and third-party assurance provide a robust framework to ensure accountability and delivery.\r\n\r\nDolos reduces operational costs and development barriers for dApp teams and ecosystem services. Supporting this proposal aligns with SIPO’s principles of infrastructure sustainability, decentralization, and developer enablement within the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、本提案「Dolos: 軽量Cardanoデータノードの維持」に対する220,914 ADAの資金提供を支持します。なぜなら、これはカルダノ開発者エコシステムにとって、効率的で軽量なインフラを提供する重要なオープンソース・プロジェクトだからです。\r\n\r\nDolosは、フルノードとは異なり、リソース消費を抑えつつ高い応答性と信頼性のある台帳データへのアクセスを可能にする特化型ノードです。dAppsのバックエンドなどに適しており、すでに採用事例も増えており、コミュニティ貢献も360件以上と活発です。\r\n\r\n今回の資金は、ブロックチェーン開発者（0.5FTE）および技術リーダー（0.125FTE）の活動を支えるためのもので、Cardanoプロトコルの進化と連動した継続的な保守・機能拡張を実現します。\r\n\r\nIntersectによって提案され、法的契約に基づいてマイルストーン制で資金が支払われる設計となっており、サードパーティの検証機関も含めた厳格な監督体制により、透明性と責任が確保されています。\r\n\r\nDolosの普及は、開発者のインフラ負担を軽減し、dApp構築のハードルを下げ、Cardano上のサービス発展を促進します。本提案は、インフラの持続可能性、分散性、開発者支援というSIPOの投票原則と一致しており、賛成に値すると判断しました。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
