    {
      "voter": "42",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ada42btc/DRepADA/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_gov_0002.jsonld -->\r\n# 42\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26ppxzudkhtak4y7kc2rag9ezq7szje78aetxge3pg5w7qwthkqv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe governance action in question is about defining Cardano's vision and roadmap for 2025 and beyond, a critical step for the blockchain's future development. This roadmap outlines plans to improve scalability, expand Layer 2 solutions, and enhance developer experience, all of which are vital for Cardano's growth. Voting \"Yes\" supports these strategic initiatives, which could make Cardano more competitive and user-friendly. For example, enhancing scalability could mean faster transactions, benefiting everyday users. I do consider Leios, Hydra and Midgard as some of the top priorities.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "8Ball",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmavLdS818SK7XXSWhodnBMNZNKLFM6xvmoRioNtknqC12 -->\r\n# 8Ball\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y296z8tm7y7elwsmsewn4q2tdr5gu0fqztq97yttlpv7zycvsl554`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n1. Scalability: I approve that the Cardano 2025 Vision Roadmap prioritizes scalability through initiatives like Leios, Midgard, Hydra, and Peras, while also focusing on performance optimization.\r\n2. Multi-Node: I support a decentralized ecosystem where multiple nodes compete based on merit. I trust that Stake Pool Operators (SPOs) have the expertise to effectively evaluate and oversee these implementations.\r\n3. Bitcoin DeFi, zkProofs, and Nested Transactions: I endorse these forward-looking developments.\r\n4. Criticisms: The absence of specific timelines for Leios, a key scaling component, leaves its implementation uncertain.\r\nThe focus on Layer 2 expansion—such as AVS linked to Midnight and the introduction of Minotaur—seems premature for Cardano.\r\nI support the SPO incentive enhancements, like min-margin and pledge-benefit curves, but they warrant more attention and a broader scope.\r\n\r\nDespite these reservations, the roadmap’s emphasis on scalability, multi-node development, and zkProofs justifies my support with a yes vote.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "A Diamond",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Andre-Diamond/drep-repo/refs/heads/main/vote_context/01_Roadmap_2025/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# A Diamond\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt85v0tczccl7aj84sjg0cl0y9mgvnhna5e0dw8k6zsgqrczqmfgu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe roadmap is compelling because it lays out a comprehensive strategy that addresses both technical innovation and ecosystem growth. By focusing on key areas such as scalability, security, and developer experience, the roadmap ensures that Cardano is well-positioned to handle increasing transaction volumes and evolving market demands. The emphasis on optimizing the L1 engine through innovations like the Leios protocol—along with robust improvements to L2 solutions such as Hydra and Midgard—demonstrates a clear commitment to enhancing network performance without compromising on decentralization. Additionally, the plan’s focus on formal methods, modular design, and diverse node implementations significantly boosts the platform’s reliability and resilience.\r\n\r\nThis forward-thinking approach not only encourages innovation within the Cardano community but also fosters strategic partnerships that are essential for real-world adoption. The roadmap's balance between technical advancements and community engagement creates a sustainable foundation for Cardano’s future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaLovelace777",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/2025-Cardano-Roadmap-Vote/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(4).jsonld -->\r\n# AdaLovelace777\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygehgu65kchqm929zp69xhl06hqkpcjv0rzy44sx40qhufqgh3xv2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m excited for Cardano’s plans to increase liquidity with zero-knowledge proofs and introduce Babel Fees, making transactions more accessible without needing ADA initially. The L2 expansion with the AVS layer, alongside scaling Hydra and the Midgard rollup, will bring even more flexibility and efficiency to the platform. I’m also looking forward to faster transaction finality with Peras and an enhanced developer and user experience through improved tools, APIs, and decentralized services. The new programmable assets will unlock exciting use cases, and the focus on supporting multiple node implementations will make the network even more resilient and decentralized. As for the other upgrades, I’m excited for the scaling of L1, the Leios protocol, codebase optimization, and Mithril decentralization. Plus, I can’t wait to see the improvements to SPO incentives and the architectural excellence Cardano is striving for. 2025 is going to be big. Hi from the past.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://silver-secret-ermine-629.mypinata.cloud/ipfs/bafkreiccemnrbc3l4zt5ke3czpot2ymtzlsbrxcczsp7xk6lbnilwztdke -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTaking a high level view, the roadmap describes a comprehensive set of technical objectives that, if delivered upon, positions Cardano well going forward. To that end, I vote \"Yes\". That isn't to say that there are not valid criticisms of the proposal or that a full roadmap might not include additional information. For example, I'd like to see the roadmap include additional details around resources required and proposed milestones (i.e. more 'how'). I'd also like to see greater linkage between deliverables and intended end-user impact (i.e. more 'why'). My 'YES' vote is an endorsement of Intersect to continue building out this roadmap.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote5.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn general I support the Cardano Vision and Roadmap. My doubts, however, were caused by the fact the Reference link leads to the website that may change at any time. But after much consideration, I decided that it is not so important for the Info type, because it is not the kind of thing that leads to changes in the protocol or something like that, but only needed to the temperature checking. Hence, Yes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmdzi7yGDzTMUQQ24rtCJPppkTV4YEytXGCRk6BqifgL6B -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCardanoの中長期的な成長には、技術的基盤の強化と開発者・ユーザー体験の向上が欠かせません。本提案には、これらの課題に真摯に向き合い、未来に備えようとする前向きな姿勢が感じられます。私はこのビジョンに共感し、賛成票を投じます。\\n\\nFor Cardano's medium to long-term growth, strengthening its technical infrastructure and improving the experience for both developers and users are essential. This proposal demonstrates a sincere and forward-looking approach to addressing these challenges and preparing for the future. I resonate with this vision and cast my vote in favor.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Anonymous",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AnonymousDRep/AnonymousDRep/refs/heads/Vote-Context/Vote_Context%202025%20Roadmap.jsonld -->\r\n# Anonymous\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytm2zedqf54prqf5kfvzq56dgr7s3p4h53w8z428z6l2c8cj8e33y`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting No because this is clearly an unfinished product. I think it is a great start and I look forward to voting Yes on the finished product in the future. I think the SPO incentive improvements needs to be long term. We need to ensure SPOs continue to receive adequate incentives as Cardano continues to evolve.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/GARoadmap20250301/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nカルダノの適応的攻撃者に対する耐性を高めた証明可能安全性が「量子耐性」として、一般の人々やメディアにもわかりやすく明示的に表現されるべきだと考えています。現在、カルダノはOuroboros Praosプロトコルにおいて適応的攻撃者に対する耐性を高める取り組みを行っていますが、この取り組みが量子耐性とどのように関連するのかを明確に示すことが、エコシステムにとって重要だと思います。そのため、このテーマに対する明確な表現が進むことを期待しつつ、現時点では中立的な立場を取ります。\r\n\r\n******************************\r\n\r\nI believe that the provable security enhancements made to resist adaptive attackers should be explicitly expressed as \"quantum resistance\" in a way that is clear and understandable to the general public and the media. Currently, Cardano is working on improving its resistance to adaptive attackers through the Ouroboros Praos protocol, but it is important to clarify how this work relates to quantum resistance. I hope that this topic will be more clearly articulated moving forward, and I am maintaining a neutral position at this time.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tulibra1510/lotrinhcardano2025/refs/heads/main/lotrinhcardano2025.jsonld -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n+The roadmap is clear and detailed.\r\n+L1 scaling is a very important goal. It will help Cardano become one of the best blockchains in the industry.\r\n+Key features focused on: Bitcoin DeFi, Babel Fee, L2 solutions.\r\n+Improved user and developer experience",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "canopus-n",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/canopus-n/voltaire/refs/heads/main/GovAction_Roadmap_2025_Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# canopus-n\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt67l7we0xtkl9v8krjlkjm6g9g9khqvecndevz44n3lcdc9rg2ur`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNothing in the roadmap seems controversial, these are all well socialized and are required to help Cardano achieve its promise.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmbvRbKukDfP5DzNBfJ3KNxiB328ehipEiX9bEmLBMpFiX -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation's decision to vote “Yes” on the governance action defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond (Action ID: gov_action12meeq4r43udremwpm6fzt4nt7fctvt0ah7798x036m2r4nhlccmqqhmr9wx) reflects measured support for an essential step forward. We recognize the importance of a roadmap for aligning short-term objectives with long-term strategic goals.\r\n\r\nWe support several promising initiatives outlined in the roadmap, including Layer 1 scaling improvements (Leios), deeper integration of Mithril, innovations like Actively Validated Services, multiple node implementations, and programmable assets. These initiatives offer significant potential for enhancing network performance, resilience, and overall ecosystem growth.\r\n\r\nHowever, we also note concerns regarding certain elements in the roadmap. Specifically, the proposal revisits longstanding areas such as LSM Integration, which has been in progress for several years. Utilizing established industry-grade solutions would enhance reliability, reduce development risks, and accelerate delivery compared to rebuilding it from scratch. Additionally, the inclusion of zero-knowledge proofs to enable Cardano as a decentralized DeFi layer for Bitcoin appears misaligned with core roadmap priorities, given that the Plutus Virtual Machine already provides the necessary building blocks. While Leios is a promising initiative, many of the highlighted preparatory steps have already been completed, leaving limited new promise for 2025. Finally, the plan to generate libraries in various languages and empower developers to create custom chain indexers raises undue complexity and developer experience concerns. Additionally, achieving proposed or future roadmap items requires exploring innovative funding mechanisms beyond current models and increasing transparency and accountability in capital allocation.\r\n\r\nThe mutable nature of the provided reference link poses a risk to governance accountability. To address this, we have pinned the file currently hosted at https://product.cardano.intersectmbo.org/vision-roadmap-2025-static/ to IPFS and Filecoin (https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmUocoa7WkmpyGyiEp2qZbqR9qtM9YViEppNgotQXBhCpL).",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmct9eUjeEeDKKJQjiCFomGJE3dg5hoNuMipncpibpmsCw -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe imminent area of focus for Cardano in my opinion needs to be scaling, which is the focus of >50% of this roadmap, emphasising all the key technical initiatives in this area (Hydra, Leios, Midgard, Peras). Strongly support.\r\n\r\nThat said - The wording around Leios seems somewhat vague and doesn't explicitly commit to full delivery, which I know we're unlikely to see in 2025. But I think it would be worthwhile to make things more specific in terms of tangible outcomes and a timeline for Cardano users, and feel free to be conservative in it. \r\n\r\nE.g. \"in 2026 we aim to have a very first rough iteration of a Leios testnet ready, in 2027 we will deliver it on mainnet\" and further explain why the intermediate steps in 2025 are critical to get there. Transparency is key here.\r\n\r\nA final note is that in my view the text around multiple node implementations reasons from a perspective of centralisation, e.g. \"Ensuring node conformity (...) concrete, actionable instructions and guidelines for building and configuring nodes (...) This combination of precise specifications is essential for maintaining the integrity and stability of the Cardano network, guaranteeing that all participating nodes operate according to the agreed-upon rules and protocols.\" \r\n\r\nTotally understood on the concerns in this area, but at the same time Cardano is decentralised and I think patronising language like this is best avoided.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Satuchac/DRep/refs/heads/main/003_My%20Rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES for the 2025 Vision & Roadmap. I'm glad this document was created to allow the community to agree on Cardano's future direction.\r\n\r\nThe biggest emphasis is on both L1 and L2 scalability, which we all agree should be prioritized. Completing the Basho era is crucial in the context of the previous roadmap from 2017.\r\n\r\nI am not entirely sure about building the PartnerChain Framework in addition to Ouroboros Leios, Peras, Hydra, and Midgard simultaneously. \r\n\r\nScalability is addressed from three sides, which might be unnecessary. I understand the importance of the PartnerChain Framework and appreciate that it's being considered.\r\n\r\nMaybe we should focus on only 2 things now and not chase too many hares at once.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, it's good to be prepared for all eventualities. Successful applications are starting to consider building their own blockchains, so having a framework that seamlessly connects all chains could be advantageous.\r\n\r\nUltimately, I don't mind that the PartnerChain Framework will be built. I see it as support for the Midnight project. I would like to see more focus on privacy directly in the Cardano protocol. If Midnight is delivered, Cardano can adopt some of the technologies once we deliver scalability.\r\n\r\nI was pleased to see the emphasis on modular design. The Ethereum ecosystem has adopted this approach, offering high flexibility and adaptability.\r\n\r\nProgrammable Assets will bring new possibilities to the ecosystem, including minting USDC and USDT and building soul-bound tokens. \r\n\r\nCardano should be as flexible as possible to accommodate various use cases, even those not entirely aligned with Satoshi's ideals. Ideals and real business don't always align, and from the user's perspective, having the ability to choose is important.\r\n\r\nThe document mentions using ZK Proofs for building Bitcoin DeFi on Cardano, which is a direction worth supporting. In the Cardano ecosystem, we already have wallets that allow holding ADA and BTC, and further integration is desirable.\r\n\r\nSupporting multiple client implementations is essential for a decentralized ecosystem. Combined with the focus on modularity, this is a good approach for future development.\r\n\r\nCurrently, staking rewards are not optimal. This issue will be addressed by introducing the min-margin parameter and modifying the pledge-benefit curve for a0.\r\n\r\nI largely agree with the Vision & Roadmap described in the document. \r\n\r\nHowever, in my opinion, the document could have included an approximate delivery time horizon and a rough estimate of costs. \r\n\r\nI assume this will be a topic for further debate.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQKrqTYeyG3m6vPbRkBhcaFAiS54xf242MheN5R26uLHx -->\r\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is definitely a yes for me, that the Cardano community usually don't have a transparent roadmap. Usually at the Cardano Summit at Q4 of the previous year, which spent most of the time on the rewards and recognition instead of focus on the agenda for next year.\r\nThis together with the clear roadmap and prioriites\r\nhttps://forum.cardano.org/t/cardano-foundation-sebastian-cardanos-roadmap-a-tier-list-summary/144669 thank to good developers from Cardano Product Committee of Intersect \r\n(i.e  such as KtorZ - Techincal Director CF and Sebastian - ex IOG CTO and Giorgio Zinetti CTO from CF)\r\nThis is for me is the Cardano Constitution in pratical with clarity and the Cardano Roadmap in Action with Priority \r\nNeeds to be repeated every year not just 2025. Onwards with clarity in priorities",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/Info_5.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting yes on the Info Action proposal to define the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond. I believe the proposed roadmap covers the majority of essential improvements and technologies necessary to advance Cardano.\r\n\r\nHowever, there are additional items I would like to see considered, including bootstrapping P2P-DeFi, seeding stablecoin liquidity from the treasury, and further enhancements to SPO incentives. I have submitted issues and a pull request on GitHub proposing the inclusion of some of these items in the roadmap.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I note that the metadata attached to this proposal is not immutable, as it ideally should be. Nevertheless, since this is an Info Action and does not alter the ledger state, it does not affect the outcome of my vote.\r\n\r\nFor transparency and accountability, I include the SHA-256 hash of the raw text found at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IntersectMBO/product-website/refs/heads/master/src/pages/vision-roadmap-2025.mdx at the time of this vote: 72ac255dba0114b51d54d384016e0042e3a3ccab1648fa839e313ac5cfa007cc",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_03282025.jsonld -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRe-affirming my YES vote, while there is a disconnect in the Vision an Roadmap when it comes to community engagement and involvement.  Otherwise, I'm satisfied with this.  While it's a short-term focus Info Action, it's important that we can look ahead to the roadmap and see where it aligns back to the overall vision.  The vision aims at scalability, development security/research, and community needs.  However, the roadmap focuses in on all those things except seemingly community.  There are no real deliverables defined for the later in the roadmap.  This is not a problem, per-say, and to an extent it's a nitpick.  While the roadmap supports the visions technical aspects, it doesn't address the community-driven, ecosystem-building aspects that the vision deems necessary.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb5WPyHqsTh628FUoatQUKpgfusFCd9boTU8zY5Hy7EqM -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on the proposed 2025 Vision and Roadmap for Cardano due to its comprehensive and strategically robust approach toward enhancing scalability, security, and usability, which are crucial for Cardano's long-term success. The roadmap clearly addresses key community priorities, including Layer 1 performance optimization through Leios, expansion of Layer 2 solutions such as Hydra and Midgard, and enhancements in developer and user experience, which is essential to Cardano's adoption and, I personally believe, has been overlooked in the past.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, the introduction of Leios is particularly promising as it targets significant scalability improvements through parallel block creation, potentially positioning Cardano as a leading blockchain for high-throughput applications.\r\n\r\nThere are certain items within the roadmap that appear subjective, in my opinion, but I welcome further research, community feedback, and refinement on these topics as indicated by the iterative nature of the roadmap.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dmitrii Gartung",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZM3UyeHiAdwPu5YDEpE6tRoALo2hEHZkdyosCsQzBP7v -->\r\n# Dmitrii Gartung\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytd8ewnp38xz5469g63yw34ev9q9cch2hcyp332t8cqpzzqh23ykc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nClear vision and roadmap are needed.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "DraculaDAO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dracula-DAO/cardano-drep/refs/heads/main/2025/2025-02-28_Cardano_Vision_Roadmap.jsonld -->\r\n# DraculaDAO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygs99wsy49h9vydggncfeck2xwmngyeltp66pvgzl6jz63s6qmu3p`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDracula DAO is generally in favor of most of the items in this roadmap and we respect the effort being put in by the Intersect Product Committee.  We believe Leios, Hydra, Midgard and developer tools / experience are items that definitely belong on the near-term roadmap.\r\n\r\nThe roadmap as a whole is hard to distill down into a simple Yes / No vote, especially without any budgets and timelines.  However, since this is simply a non-binding info action we are choosing to vote \"Yes\" to indicate to the governance community our general support of the roadmap as presented.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1y2sz79r6c4lc0sl468pdtdmtsnsmx3sahggtqtc9hzear5se6mwel",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/apestchanker/drep_votes/refs/heads/main/ga_12meeq4-qhmr9wx.jsonld -->\r\n# drep1y2sz79r6c4lc0sl468pdtdmtsnsmx3sahggtqtc9hzear5se6mwel\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2sz79r6c4lc0sl468pdtdmtsnsmx3sahggtqtc9hzear5se6mwel`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am not sure that there is a clear USE CASE for the proposed technical implementations. In order to have a true roadmap for Cardano, even if it is just for the current year, a clear case on WHY we will be building what we are building, shall be clearly stated. \r\nThe future of our blockchain depends on adoption and real use cases, I see a very vague description of those use cases in the proposal, therefore I have no rationales to approve the proposal. Also as the proposal identifies several very well known expected evolutions of the technical protocol and because the proposal comes from the Intersect's product committee I do believe there are strong technical reasons for the proposed changes, though they are not really explained in detail in the proposal or accompanying documentation, so I cannot either vote against this.\r\nI hope next proposals from the committee's will be more complete, professional and with the users at the top of their mind, so we can really see WHY we are doing what we are doing.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
