      "voter": "drgov01",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafkreia6qc4vuqm23fvjxmea45hqmijf4vrktffrqgcigk2lezw724eoei -->\r\n# drgov01\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts04qdwf2vcyap5590pujzhzc9fhlz9usn39erzpwdkrtqk95e66`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGood Roadmap.\r\n\r\nThe points in the roadmap do not include specific time-frames or deadlines, but I assume this was intended and it is fine without. Who is responsible for ensuring that each task is worked on?\r\n\r\nI think the roadmap versions should be on IPFS, because I think this current roadmap on the website can just be changed because only the link to the website is in the hash of this proposal, but I might be wrong about that.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dumpling🥟",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bullishdumpling/roadmap/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Dumpling🥟\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rtf58m0lv9spcqx5mads20gpfulf6l97w57ecdy00vjdq0klh4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本提案要求 Cardano 投票代表（DReps） 对 Cardano 未来发展路线图 进行投票。该路线图由 Intersect 旗下的 Cardano 产品委员会 与关键技术利益相关方共同制定，明确了技术优先事项、发展方向和战略目标。\r\n\r\n一个明确的发展方向是必要的， \r\n1. 能确保资源优化，最大化开发工作的影响力。\r\n 2.  增强社区治理：表达社区意愿，确保发展方向符合持币者的集体利益。\r\n 3. 影响未来预算规划：该路线图将指导 Intersect 未来的预算分配，确保资金用于优先事项，推动关键技术升级。\r\n\r\n综合来看，支持该提案，投赞成票。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifmyslsg4kfjkibkrtxq7ls2jcva6ssrgpurxawsarakhzzmimady -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGA: Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n\r\nhttps://gov.tools/governance_actions/56f39054758f1a3cedc1de9225d66bf270b62dfdbfbc5399f1d6d43aceffc636#0\r\n\r\nhttps://adastat.net/governances/56f39054758f1a3cedc1de9225d66bf270b62dfdbfbc5399f1d6d43aceffc63600\r\n\r\nAction ID: gov_action12meeq4r43udremwpm6fzt4nt7fctvt0ah7798x036m2r4nhlccmqqhmr9wx\r\n\r\nVote: Yes\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nRegarding the Governance Action “Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond” with the Action ID (gov_action12meeq4r43udremwpm6fzt4nt7fctvt0ah7798x036m2r4nhlccmqqhmr9wx), EMURGO has decided to vote “Yes.”\r\n\r\nWe believe that a few core tenets in this roadmap for 2025 and beyond align with EMURGO’s near-term objectives in select key focus areas, which can facilitate greater commercial adoption of Cardano while being flexible enough to accommodate long-term variables that may necessitate further discussion.\r\n\r\nWhile this may leave the door open to later changes that can cause greater debate, especially about Treasury management and funding, EMURGO expresses support for the following mentioned key areas that we believe will help to accelerate the commercial and user adoption of Cardano:\r\n\r\nEnhancing Cardano’s Technology\r\n\r\nThe Actively Validated Services (AVS) Layer for Partner Chains enhances Cardano’s ability to broaden its DeFi accessibility and scalability. This can unlock much-needed cross-chain asset management and facilitate greater DeFi activity in Cardano by supporting cross-chain DeFi applications and asset bridges to integrate with other widely adopted applications on other networks. Users can enjoy increased access to liquidity and financial services, helping to grow Cardano’s TVL and drive more assets into the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nLayer-1 Improvements\r\n\r\nLeios can enhance Cardano’s security and fairness, particularly for dApps and DeFi platforms. The introduction of anti-grinding mechanisms can prevent users from exploiting vulnerabilities in consensus protocols, ensuring that the network remains more resilient to malicious activities and grows its dApps and TVL sustainably.\r\n\r\nExpanding the Developer Community\r\n\r\nCardano’s long-term expansion is mutually aligned with the continued growth of its developer community. The roadmap includes various measures to reduce technical barriers and enable greater developer activity in Cardano. These include multiple node implementations, support for popular programming languages (Rust, JavaScript, and Python), and wider integration with Web2 and Web3 infrastructures. The roadmap also focuses on improving developer documentation, tooling, and SDKs.\r\n\r\nFor full transparency and to ensure an accessible backup of the originally proposed roadmap in case of any alterations, we have hosted a PDF version on IPFS (https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafybeifaehl6mc44cikuucohxranujivnrj4ttmcjfxj7jq6bq66ur4r4i)",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00007_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTLDR; We agree with the TSC's plan of how to evolve the Cardano blockchain. It's crucial to implement better solutions for scaling and finality, more than one node implementation for resilience etc.",
