    {
      "voter": "intertreeJK",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmV4j5HvqG4Y8FJkjGaSxpW9dQpsY91WMoQGHGpXvQtZDB -->\r\n# intertreeJK\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfkg5ryqwaleunwqg0dtcj8g8yw8sgd9kskg2zlzdr8355gpghcvv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThese two quotes from this Action’s Text concern me greatly:\r\n\r\n“… the Product Committee will iterate upon the roadmap based upon DRep feedback, adjusting the referenced roadmap.”\r\n\r\n“While the referenced roadmap develops, DReps should consider submitting multiple votes to signal approval across versions.”\r\n\r\nThe idea that a Yes OR a No Vote could end up being recorded as a DRep's Official Position on an On-Chain Voting History when a Governance Action *itself* clearly states that the content of what is being Voted on can change *midway through* the On-Chain Voting Process gives me the ick (to put it mildly). \r\n\r\nIt puts me in the position of not being able to place a *definitive* Vote on my *actual* position as a DRep on this Action. \r\n\r\nAs my Yes, or indeed my No, Vote by the end date of this On-Chain Action could have been intended for an older version of the, since updated, ‘referenced roadmap’.\r\n\r\nI appreciate the *idea* that an Action could have multiple Voting Rounds following version revisions based on DRep feedback but, in order for this to work *properly* mechanically, each new version of the Action should *necessarily* start from a blank slate of DRep Voting Data, while still capturing the DReps’ Voting Record prior to the version change.\r\n\r\nIt should most definitely NOT carry forward previous the Voting Positions of the DReps *as if* they have stayed the same. \r\n\r\nAs this could end up being *grossly* misrepresentative of the *actual* DRep Consensus once the Action has reached its final version within its Lifespan.\r\n\r\nDue to this issue with not being able to actually interpret the *reality* of this Governance Action’s final Voting Outcome, I cannot in good conscience Vote *either* Yes OR No on this Action. \r\n\r\nSo I have chosen to Abstain this time. Unfortunately.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Jakub Szyca",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jakubszyca/Cardano-Drep/refs/heads/main/Raw-Votes-Context/Vote_Context_3.jsonld -->\r\n# Jakub Szyca\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytee8ue66qdqkfquq5c9hld7trhxvqdra5plfhyuragcfsgrqen4n`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI believe this roadmap focuses on key improvements that should be made to the Cardano blockchain, making it the primary roadmap for the foreseeable future. Scalability, fast transaction finality, and increased throughput are much-needed enhancements. Obviously, we need to achieve these without compromising our core values, such as decentralization, which this roadmap takes into account.\r\n\r\nWith Leios and the improvements leading up to it, I believe developers can achieve the goals set in this roadmap and effectively address the blockchain trilemma. Alongside Layer 2 solutions, partner chains, and developer-focused enhancements, Cardano should be well-positioned to thrive and attract a vast number of new users through its superior experience compared to other blockchains.\r\n\r\nInput Output and other developers working on different parts of the roadmap have already demonstrated their capabilities in the past, and I am confident they can deliver again. With new developers joining Cardano and growing interest in our blockchain ecosystem, these advancements are highly achievable, even though they are at the cutting edge of technology and have required years of research.\r\n\r\nI hope the majority of the roadmap can be completed this year, but I am glad it also looks ahead, focusing on the long-term growth of the ecosystem and ensuring Cardano's technological superiority for years to come—all while benefiting every community member.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "JNTHN_BRGS",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JonathanBRGS/DRep/refs/heads/main/ID_AG_56f39054758f1a3c%2B%2B%2B.jsonld -->\r\n# JNTHN_BRGS\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2yppwm9hvwdnh38fznaug4qy86zfvsmsrqlyvdqk22s2xgmqn42k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe welcome Intersect’s development plan outlined for Cardano, as it will provide modern tools for developers as it improves the network and promotes its evangelism.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kronoshus/KevinMohr/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20Defining%20the%20Cardano%20Roadmap.jsonld -->\r\n# Kevin G Mohr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI believe the proposed roadmap is very vague and there is nothing wrong with this. I approve of the roadmap but not necessarily what will come after this. I would like follow up votes and future votes on big or important proposals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/37yxfutu -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on the 2025 Vision & Roadmap for Cardano because it outlines a well-structured and ambitious plan to enhance scalability, decentralization, and usability. The roadmap presents a strong commitment to technical excellence, including advancements such as Leios for improved transaction throughput, Hydra and Midgard for L2 scaling, and innovations in programmable assets.\r\n\r\nThese developments will strengthen Cardano’s position as a leading blockchain ecosystem by fostering developer engagement, increasing interoperability, and driving real-world adoption. The work done by the community, developers, and governance members is commendable, and I fully support these improvements to ensure a sustainable and decentralized future for Cardano.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kit Willow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTJ5gd8SkeC7chxBBSqbXr6jiogSd7ajArCurGNW8BmrY -->\r\n# Kit Willow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygk7qax0ztrv7a7unzgs4apj5mhk5a0058ne3fgfftj4tmgvuk5a7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe vision roadmap shows a proactive and good approach towards development and investment in scaling and growth of the Cardano ecosystem. With that in mind, I think it’s a good enough roadmap",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/4/2025roadmap.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support all the initiatives on the 2025 Vision/Roadmap, hence I am voting \"Yes\" in this Info Action. The right emphasis is given to all of those items that will move Cardano forward, such as the work on scalability with Leios, the ZK proofs that will enable us to become a DeFi layer of Bitcoin (which has the potential to increase liquidity by a lot!), work on Babel Fees, Programmable Assets, Multiple Node Implementations and many other work items that I don't need to list one by one herein. My main concern was the lack of quantum resistance for which I had initially voted \"No\". After receiving feedback from the Intersect Product Committee, I understand that this item is on the list of research items (on the Research Working Group) and it's ongoing. So although we don't have a solid solution right now, we are on track for quantum readiness with quantum-resistance algorithms such as one-shot signatures and quantum key distribution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/CardanoVisionandRoadmap.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nKrypto Labs the DRep for the Nordic community, we support voting yes on the Cardano Vision Roadmap 2025, as it aligns with our needs and enhances the blockchain’s future.\r\n\r\nKrypto Labs has engaged our community via YouTube and Facebook, explaining the roadmap transparently. We’ve also joined roadmap presentations, asking questions to clarify details. Community feedback highlights enthusiasm for faster transactions, Bitcoin integration, and new dApps—goals the roadmap directly targets, solidifying our yes vote.\r\nThe roadmap boosts Layer 1 scalability with the Leios protocol and codebase optimization, promising quicker, cheaper transactions. This is vital for handling growing demand, ensuring Cardano remains efficient for users in payments and smart contracts. Interoperability is another focus, integrating Bitcoin via zero-knowledge proofs and Babel Fees. This could bring Bitcoin’s liquidity into Cardano’s DeFi ecosystem, offering users more yield and utility while attracting new participants.\r\nConcerns about complexity—like implementing Leios or tweaking SPO incentives—are real but manageable. Cardano’s methodical, research-backed approach, paired with phased execution and governance input, reduces risks and keeps the community involved. This balance of ambition and practicality underpins its likely success.\r\nVoting yes supports a scalable, interoperable, and innovative Cardano, matching our community’s vision. It’s a strategic move to ensure the platform thrives, benefiting the Nordic region with a robust ecosystem. Through our engagement, I’ve seen the excitement for these changes. We are confident this roadmap will drive Cardano forward.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LallyMcClay",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LallyMack/Drep-it/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(1).jsonld -->\r\n# LallyMcClay\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2dptycrks2ggae95leeh66m0l0svet98c44hl4rmaec7as6hgpp3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn my view, the 2025 Vision & Roadmap for Cardano is a well-rounded strategy that balances immediate improvements & long-term development goals.\r\nKey areas like scalability improvements, the modular design, and  functionalities informed my yes vote rationale balance, detailed below: \r\n\r\nPoints in Favour\r\nScalability Focus:\r\nI appreciate that the roadmap has an emphasis on scaling solutions for both Layer 1 and Layer 2. In my view, this approach is good for handling increased demand and supporting real-world applications.\r\nModularity, Flexibility:\r\nThe modular design is a positive for me because it supports future integrations (like ZK proofs for Bitcoin DeFi, enhanced privacy features) and a range of use cases -  important for maintaining a competitive edge.\r\nCommunity and Governance Alignment:\r\nThe roadmap was developed through consultations with stakeholders and includes mechanisms for ongoing feedback from DReps. This transparency and community involvement ensure a collective voice gets heard and that development stays aligned with the Constitution. \r\n\r\nStrategic Budget Alignment:\r\nIn my view,  supporting this document helps ensure resources be directed towards initiatives with high impact, so supports efficient and effective development.\r\n\r\nConsiderations for Improvement\r\nClarity in Timelines and Deliverables:\r\nSome initiatives could benefit from clearer, more tangible milestones. Breaking down the phases could improve transparency and set clearer expectations.\r\n\r\nAmbition v Focus:\r\nThe roadmap proposes a wide range of scalability initiatives, & I do have some concerns about spreading resources thinly or, intentions versus reality. Focusing on a couple of key priorities now might enable more immediate and less vague or perceived benefits, while planning for additional functionalities later.\r\n\r\nCost and Delivery Estimates:\r\n Including more detailed approximations regarding timelines and costs would provide a better picture of the required resource commitment. I understand these details may evolve, but a rough estimate would certainly add to the document's clarity and community confidence.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nOverall, I believe that despite some areas where additional specificity would be beneficial, the roadmap is a robust and inclusive plan for advancing Cardano’s ecosystem. Its focus on scalability, modular design, and community-driven governance aligns well with the vision for Cardano’s long-term success. For these reasons, I support a yes vote.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Latam Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LatamCardanoDRep/DREP/refs/heads/main/V2.jsonld -->\r\n# Latam Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytgsdkfznvjnwdxrzvf8x6tn4ctfukqqphsammzkfwatgsqgnpf2w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe roadmap proposed by the Intersect Product Committee is a good starting point. It should not be interpreted as perfect, complete or exaustive of future amendments. \r\nNOTE: the official roadmap link provided in the metadata (https://product.cardano.intersectmbo.org/vision-roadmap-2025/) points to mutable web content. To establish a fixed reference for this vote (which ends March 30th, 2025), Nicolas Cerny has pinned the current content of that page to IPFS: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafkreifbloze4ln3jkseiqrkcpuonilvnah37lllf2xhzrzyqvtjq555ou. Our assessment and affirmative vote pertain specifically to this archived version.\r\n\r\nLa hoja de ruta propuesta por el Comité de Producto de Intersect es un buen punto de partida. No debe interpretarse como perfecta, completa ni exhaustiva respecto a futuras modificaciones.\r\nNOTA: El enlace oficial a la hoja de ruta, proporcionado en los metadatos (https://product.cardano.intersectmbo.org/vision-roadmap-2025/), apunta a contenido web mutable. Para establecer una referencia fija para esta votación (que finaliza el 30 de marzo de 2025), Nicolas Cerny ha fijado el contenido actual de esa página en IPFS: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafkreifbloze4ln3jkseiqrkcpuonilvnah37lllf2xhzrzyqvtjq555ou. Nuestra evaluación y voto afirmativo se refieren específicamente a esta versión archivada.\r\n\r\nO roteiro proposto pelo Comitê de Produtos Intersect é um bom ponto de partida. Ele não deve ser interpretado como perfeito, completo ou exaustivo de futuras emendas.\r\nNOTA: o link oficial do roteiro fornecido nos metadados (https://product.cardano.intersectmbo.org/vision-roadmap-2025/) aponta para conteúdo da web mutável. Para estabelecer uma referência fixa para esta votação (que termina em 30 de março de 2025), Nicolas Cerny fixou o conteúdo atual dessa página no IPFS: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafkreifbloze4ln3jkseiqrkcpuonilvnah37lllf2xhzrzyqvtjq555ou. Nossa avaliação e voto afirmativo dizem respeito especificamente a esta versão arquivada.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "lido",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmWUSo953oiSvit9AiSFuejuhp9JSiep3Scr2KLv6cPUQo -->\r\n# lido\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg7s3wsvh4jmmv5fys6hrsnrkch8x6zfamgd8nhfvhz5r2ctdy57k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe agree with the proposal view of Cardano\\'s vission: a future where it serves as the robust and scalable foundation for a decentralized global economy.\r\n\r\nWe voted yes because the priorities and details in the proposal addresses this vision well. I will move the needle and set us up well to be competitive in both the short and long term.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LloydDuhon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRiaNMX3rELtyDZb5F3kGpoE8fL6oHrcjvkKwS3JUn5ae -->\r\n# LloydDuhon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfvw769lf7g5p4hx0cl2f8jxdcufdcqqj36u0n9escjcwdswcj4h6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI absolutely agree with this community driven technical roadmap. I feel this sets the community off on the right foot for our next development steps.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Long Hồ",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeB4E8i1SiShqd4WCEby5A42wHuKAK4vdkpTCezuVAnGh -->\r\n# Long Hồ\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttfrpngasw7yrdryydsg66gzv8znkj0stjngm5a8hs353stdeml6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I vote YES for this GA, and my rationale is as follows:\r\n\r\n1. Strategic Direction and Long-Term Vision:\r\n\r\nThe 2025 and Beyond Roadmap lays a robust foundation for Cardano's future, focusing on key elements like scalability, modularity, interoperability, and governance improvements.\r\nIt aligns with Cardano's long-term mission of financial inclusion, decentralization, and technological excellence.\r\n\r\n2. Focus on Scalability:\r\n\r\nPrioritizes Layer 1 and Layer 2 scaling solutions (Ouroboros Leios, Hydra, Midgard) to support mass adoption.\r\nA multi-faceted approach to ensure Cardano remains at the forefront of blockchain technology.\r\n\r\n3. Enhancing Modularity and Network Resilience:\r\n\r\nModular design improves upgradeability, enhances decentralization, and strengthens security.\r\nReduces reliance on a single entity through multiple client implementations.\r\n\r\n4. Expanding the Ecosystem and Real-World Applications:\r\n\r\nIntegrates programmable assets, stablecoins (USDC, USDT), and zero-knowledge proofs to expand DeFi capabilities and real-world applications.\r\nStrengthens interoperability with other blockchains (Bitcoin).\r\nSoul-bound tokens for verification and identity applications.\r\n\r\n5. Improving Governance and Economics:\r\n\r\nAddresses issues related to staking rewards (min-margin parameter, pledge-benefit curve modifications) and governance efficiency.\r\nEnsures the community has an active role in decision-making.\r\nThe development roadmap is updated based on community feedback.\r\nAims for efficient and transparent budget allocation.\r\n\r\n6. Strengthening Cardano's Competitive Position:\r\n\r\nInvests in research and development to ensure security and interoperability.\r\nBalances infrastructure development with user experience improvement.\r\nEnsures continuous innovation and development to maintain a leading position.\r\n\r\n7. Transparency and Community Participation:\r\n\r\nThe roadmap is built through consultation with stakeholders and includes feedback mechanisms from DReps.\r\nEnsures that collective voices are heard and that development aligns with the Constitution.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0005 -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n🗳️ Voting Rationale for the 2025 Vision & Roadmap Proposal\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on this proposal because it outlines a strong technical vision for Cardano, with clear priorities in scalability, modular architecture, L2 expansion, and developer experience. The roadmap demonstrates a deep understanding of the technological evolution needed to position Cardano at the forefront of blockchain innovation. The emphasis on Leios, Midgard, Peras, and modular node implementations is exactly what we need to ensure security, performance, and decentralization at scale. 🚀\r\n\r\nHowever, a great product needs more than just technical excellence—it needs a clear commercial vision. While this roadmap lays the foundation for a powerful, scalable blockchain, it does not yet address where we want to take Cardano in the market, who we are building this for, and how we plan to communicate its value.\r\n\r\nWhat’s Missing? A Commercial Vision I believe. \r\n\r\nTo truly drive adoption, we must define the strategic positioning of Cardano in the global blockchain economy:\r\n\r\nWho are our primary users? Enterprise? Governments? DeFi users? Developers?\r\n\r\nWhat problem are we solving for them? Scalability? Compliance? Cost-efficiency?\r\n\r\nHow do we market these innovations? We need a narrative around why Leios, Hydra, and AVS matter to real-world users.\r\n\r\nHow do we engage businesses and institutions? We should proactively work on business development strategies alongside this technical roadmap.\r\n\r\nRight now, Cardano has some of the best technology in the space, but without a clear go-to-market strategy, the risk is that we build an amazing product that struggles to find adoption. We must complement this roadmap with a focused effort on adoption, partnerships, and commercial viability.\r\n\r\nVOTE0005",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Manuel SNAKE",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/asnakep/repo/refs/heads/master/docs/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Manuel SNAKE\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt56tpzpzu58zy7pz4zwfp32rq95tj3xfxmdrg8k3qhxjlccp47cn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES because this roadmap presents a holistic, ambitious, and community-driven strategy to solidify Cardano’s position as a leader in decentralized infrastructure. This vision balances technical excellence with ecosystem growth, ensuring Cardano remains adaptable, scalable, and foundational to the decentralized future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Marketing DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZuHyjEbGk6YAw1d6eZHiKGvPyLw2YFL57pG1Z63WLRpf -->\r\n# Marketing DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23kumvpqgal3t6v4tamwrprjya453p3djam0eqg63usm9su77hjl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a marketing-focused DRep I had initial reservations about supporting this governance action and planned to abstain. Because it was released alone without complimentary roadmaps from other Intersect committees I first assumed that this roadmap was to function as the sole illustration of how Cardano will move forward with expansion and growth, therefore the clear lack of marketing support for the product was problematic. \r\n\r\nAfter chatting briefly with one of the authors of this document, the purpose of the road map was made clearer. In the future it would be appreciated to see the committees work more closely together, to release materials like this in unison to avoid confusion and to foster greater inter-committee cooperation. \r\n\r\nAs it stands, this roadmap is well delineated, is clearly orientated toward supporting expansion of Cardano’s adoption and further enabling its existing use case through improved programmability, better focus on user experiences, enhanced scalability and speed, and further stable coin implementation. For this reason I’m voting “Yes” on this governance action and I suggest other committees study this roadmap and release similar documents to clearly inform the community about what goals they wish to achieve, and how they will achieve them.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Martin Lang",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gitmachtl/cardano-related-stuff/refs/heads/master/vote_02032025.json -->\r\n# Martin Lang\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwmwvtd0a8lr45ssner2tjxzv5y8q03w3606yeald9mdmgmwecja`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, i have voted ✅YES on the current info action. This roadmap sounds solid to me as it is written. I think the comments about paralellization are important, the node was not optimized in that manner forever. We all have modern CPUs, lets utilize there full potential. Multi-Node development is important yes, but please don't overdue it, would just slow down our upgrade path imo. I would have loved to read a mention about post-quantum research in there, but i also think this is out of scope for a 2025 roadmap. I don't see a blocker in this one atm..",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Medusa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adawallet.io/public_files/votes/56f39054758f1a3cedc1de9225d66bf270b62dfdbfbc5399f1d6d43aceffc636.jsonld -->\r\n# Medusa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg5pzxhp0lu0m7757ww2hke8qhcuqgqt3c2ezphngwytz4gjr6yge`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe can't vote for the URL because its content may change at any time in the future, but our votes cannot.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmWxxSB2nX85DBZmmPYisq2wuLYLTUh1Wd8kbBErCXQgXP -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe roadmap proposed by the Intersect Product Committee offers a compelling starting point for unifying the community's direction. I find it thoughtfully balanced, strategically positioning Cardano to achieve product-market fit and serve as a foundational operating system for future applications.\r\n\r\nHowever, I strongly urge a higher priority for quantum resistance. \"Q-Day\" represents a significant near-term technological challenge, with credible expert timelines placing it potentially within the next ten years. Ensuring Cardano's resilience against quantum threats is not just prudent planning; it is likely to become essential sooner rather than later.\r\n\r\nA critical procedural note: the official roadmap link provided in the metadata (https://product.cardano.intersectmbo.org/vision-roadmap-2025/) points to mutable web content. To establish a fixed reference for this vote (which ends March 30th, 2025), I have pinned the current content of that page to IPFS: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafkreifbloze4ln3jkseiqrkcpuonilvnah37lllf2xhzrzyqvtjq555ou. My assessment and affirmative vote pertain specifically to this archived version.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Oomfie",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Birdlord69/Roadmap2025/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(4).jsonld -->\r\n# Oomfie\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt7vr9r0ay4h7fagkgwkvwdll3etupc40vn5tmeqf46x0sq63mk3a`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI don't know who the Product Commitee is and I've begun to distrust a lot of people here. I don't really want to go into hours of research just to be gaslit, so I'm abstaining from this vote.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZEc2ssHuU8GiQjgbvrU5wZEM5SZBUyCF1vM9M5WAhs1m -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA supports the Info Action regarding the 2025 Cardano Product Roadmap. The roadmap outlines a solid direction for improving Cardano’s scalability, performance and infrastructure through initiatives like Leios, Mithril enhancements, modular node architecture and Actively Validated Services. These are meaningful developments for the health and resilience of the network.\r\nAs a member of the Climate Neutral Cardano Alliance, I encourage the Product Committee to collaborate with CNC to model the energy and hardware implications of protocol changes like parallelization early in the process. This would support informed decisions and reinforce Cardano’s commitment to sustainability.\r\nClearer delivery milestones—particularly for Leios—would help the ecosystem plan more effectively and track progress. I also recommend that governance-linked documents use immutable references such as IPFS, rather than mutable URLs, to ensure long-term integrity and transparency.\r\nThe roadmap’s inclusion of a zero-knowledge bridge to Bitcoin is promising. This initiative, connected to the BitcoinOS project, has the potential to link Cardano’s smart contract platform with Bitcoin’s liquidity in a secure and decentralized way. I recommend naming BitcoinOS directly in the roadmap to better communicate its relevance and technical rationale.\r\nFinally, I support the introduction of governance-enabled parameters like a minimum margin and adjustments to the a0 pledge-benefit curve. These changes would help rebalance incentives and create a healthier, more decentralized staking environment. Giving this work more visibility in the roadmap would demonstrate a commitment to supporting smaller, yet highly active, stake pools.\r\nOverall, I support the direction of the roadmap and look forward to seeing it evolve with continued community input.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RudianosDrep/RudianosDrep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%203.jsonld -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter reviewing the proposed info action roadmap, I have decided to vote Yes. To me, the most crucial aspect of a document like this is its overall direction. While an info action isn’t strictly enforceable, its general direction carries significant weight from a governance perspective, and I’m pleased with the trajectory this document lays out.\r\nThe roadmap’s primary focus on core infrastructure is spot-on. To keep Cardano at the forefront of the blockchain space, we must prioritize scalability and interoperability. I’m encouraged to see key infrastructure projects like Leios, Mithril, Hydra, Midgard, and Peras highlighted, alongside a clear direction for other improvements to the chain’s foundation.\r\nAnother positive is the commitment to updating priorities based on community feedback, which is emphasized right at the start. This roadmap is designed as a short-term guide, and priorities will naturally shift as the community evolves. Acknowledging this shows that the authors understand the importance of adaptability and are dedicated to staying aligned with community needs.\r\nI’m also happy to see SPO rewards included as a focus area. The community has long recognized the need for updates here, and prioritizing this in the roadmap is a meaningful step forward.\r\nMy only reservation is that governance isn’t highlighted as a near-term focus. I believe getting governance right is vital for Cardano’s long-term health, and I would have liked to see it addressed more prominently. That said, this omission isn’t enough to sway my vote. The roadmap remains well-oriented and forward-thinking overall.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nagamarupanda/Drep-voting/refs/heads/main/Cardano%20Vision%20and%20Roadmap%20for%202025.jsonld -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI decided to vote in favor of the proposed definition of the Cardano vision and roadmap beyond 2025 because I believe it contains many important elements that will facilitate Cardano's technological evolution and ecosystem growth.\r\n\r\nIn particular, we are very excited about the increased transaction processing capacity offered by Leios. The introduction of parallel processing will enhance network scalability and allow us to process more transactions faster and more efficiently. We also believe that the application of the Active Validation Service (AVS) layer is very important because it has the potential to increase the diversity of the ecosystem by promoting collaboration with privacy-enhancing blockchains such as Midnight.\r\n\r\nExpanding liquidity through zero-knowledge proofs is another attempt to make Cardano function as a DeFi layer for Bitcoin, creating new market opportunities. Furthermore, the introduction of Babel Fees will lower the barrier to entry and make Cardano more accessible to more users, especially if users who do not have ADA are able to trade. The improved Ouroboros Praos protocol is also expected to enhance use cases that require immediacy, such as DeFi, by improving the settlement speed.\r\n\r\nThe implementation of distributed identity with soulbound tokens will contribute to the development of distributed identity (DID) solutions and will be an important element in supporting the foundation of Web3. This is an essential measure to support sustainable network operations.\r\n\r\nThis roadmap incorporates a balance of scalability, interoperability, and user experience improvements that will both advance Cardano's technical evolution and expand its ecosystem. Against this background, I vote in favor of this proposal.\r\n\r\n\r\n僕は、2025年以降のCardanoビジョンとロードマップの定義の提案に、カルダノの技術的進化とエコシステムの成長を促進する重要な要素が多く含まれていると考えたため、賛成票を投じることを決めました。\r\n\r\n特に、Leiosによる取引処理能力の向上には大きな期待を寄せています。並列処理の導入によりネットワークのスケーラビリティが強化され、より多くの取引を高速かつ効率的に処理できるようになります。また、アクティブバリデーションサービス（AVS）レイヤーの適用は、Midnightのようなプライバシー強化型ブロックチェーンとの連携を進め、エコシステムの多様性を高める可能性があるため、非常に重要だと考えています。\r\n\r\nゼロ知識証明を活用した流動性の拡大も、カルダノをビットコインのDeFiレイヤーとして機能させる試みであり、新たな市場機会の創出につながります。さらに、Babel Feesの導入によって、ADAを持っていないユーザーでも取引できる仕組みが整えば、新規参入障壁が下がり、より多くのユーザーがカルダノを利用しやすくなるはずです。Ouroboros Praosプロトコルの改良による取引確定時間の短縮も、決済速度の向上を通じて、DeFiなど即時性が求められるユースケースを強化する施策として期待できます。\r\n\r\nまた、ソウルバウンドトークンによる分散型IDの実装は、分散型アイデンティティ（DID）ソリューションの発展に寄与し、Web3の基盤を支える重要な要素になります。SPOインセンティブの改善も、カルダノの分散性とセキュリティを維持し、持続可能なネットワーク運営を支える施策として必要不可欠です。\r\n\r\n今回のロードマップは、スケーラビリティ、相互運用性、ユーザーエクスペリエンスの向上をバランスよく取り入れ、カルダノの技術的な進化とエコシステムの拡大を両立する内容になっています。こうした背景を踏まえ、僕はこの提案に賛成票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sidan-lab/DRep/refs/heads/main/voting-history/ga09/ga09-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIDAN Lab Votes YES on the Cardano 2025 Vision & Roadmap SIDAN Lab supports this governance action as it provides a clear direction for Cardano’s growth by focusing on scalability, developer experience, interoperability, and governance improvements. Key Rationale for Supporting the goernance action:\r\n- L1 & L2 Scalability: Hydra, Leios and Midgard improve transaction throughput and efficiency.\r\n- Developer & Ecosystem Support: Stronger APIs, tools, and funding for dApp growth.\r\n- Governance & Decentralization: SPO incentives and multiple node implementations strengthen network resilience.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/info/20250315/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nReasons for SIPO’s Yes Vote\r\n\r\nAs a Cardano DRep, SIPO has decided to vote “Yes” on this governance action. The reasons are as follows:\r\n\r\nClear Vision and Strategy\r\n\t•\tThe 2025 roadmap serves as a crucial guideline for Cardano’s long-term development and technological innovation.\r\n\t•\tIt includes comprehensive strategies to enhance Cardano’s evolution, covering L1 and L2 scaling, developer support, and governance improvements.\r\n\r\nEnhancing Scalability and Performance\r\n\t•\tStrengthening the Leios protocol, Hydra, and Midgard will significantly improve transaction processing capacity and enhance the user experience.\r\n\t•\tDecentralization of Mithril and the introduction of LSM trees will reduce node load.\r\n\r\nSupporting Developers and the Ecosystem\r\n\t•\tStrengthening APIs, enriching development tools, and providing developer programs will invigorate the entire ecosystem.\r\n\t•\tThe promotion of decentralized application (dApp) development is expected.\r\n\r\nImproving Interoperability and Liquidity\r\n\t•\tIntegration with Bitcoin and the introduction of Babel fees will lower entry barriers for new users.\r\n\t•\tStrengthening interoperability with other blockchains will enhance competitiveness in the DeFi market.\r\n\r\nAdvancing Governance and Decentralization\r\n\t•\tTransparency in governance and the stabilization of the voting process are progressing.\r\n\t•\tImprovements to SPO incentives and the implementation of multiple node versions will establish a healthier decentralized network.\r\n\r\nEstablishing a Long-term Vision and Sustainability\r\n\t•\tA framework for defining the roadmap beyond 2026 has been presented, ensuring sustainable development.\r\n\t•\tStrengthening collaboration between research and the community will maintain Cardano’s technological superiority.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO supports this governance action with a “Yes” vote, contributing to the future growth of Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNSscimjP1cjHc9Zo4q2sXc8nBg9Ag5vJ9VmYJGDjHCHq -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond**\r\n\r\nA clear and community-backed roadmap is essential for Cardano’s long-term growth and success. This governance info action provides a valuable opportunity for DReps to contribute their perspectives on the proposed roadmap, developed in consultation with key technical stakeholders.\r\n\r\nThis roadmap clarifies development priorities, technological advancements, and strategic goals, while also influencing future budget proposals. By voting, DReps help optimize resource allocation and ensure a well-defined direction for the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, we appreciate the iterative feedback process, where the roadmap will continue to evolve based on DRep input during the voting period. This ensures that the roadmap is not just a static plan but a living document that adapts to the needs and insights of the Cardano community.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, we believe that every item in this roadmap contributes meaningfully to realizing Cardano’s vision. It supports innovation, strengthens decentralization, and fosters ecosystem growth—critical elements for Cardano’s long-term success.\r\n\r\nA Yes vote on this proposal is a commitment to shaping Cardano’s future together. A clear vision and roadmap bring focus to development efforts and unify the ecosystem. Therefore, Socious supports this action and votes Yes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUX9H1u3PBkEDDqdNb36wx3s93mWsapQoehaEGY56Rh2s -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAny onchain governance action voting should be based on immutable content! Using a web2 website that proposer can update and change anytime as the basis to record onchain voting is faulty and unconstitutional!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TobiasIlskov/IntersectBudgetInfoAction/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(2).jsonld -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile this proposal itself does not outline all the specifics of this plan and there have been some doubts about Intersect, particularly its proposed budget, I am encouraged by recent progress in communications between the DRep community and the team at Intersect. I believe that Cardano's ecosystem development is extremely time-sensitive, and Intersect, in collaboration with the community's appointed DReps, represent our best option at this time. I hope that communication and process refinements continue to improve over the coming years.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "VNEconomics",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRgTUtafFSTGYzJa4anec961DCX276iPMGij5MBnHojCi -->\r\n# VNEconomics\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rajzp3da0scf8whz35eug0grlfn284f54ldlwnxx97fjg2xpcwt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYes, but team should add more detail timeline, expected results, and how to measure successful of the key tasks in this roadmap",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Cardano_Roadmap_Vote_Rational.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are voting YES on this governance action not because the various line items listed in the proposal’s external documentation meet or address all instances of growth and development of the ecosystem. Instead, as Cardano has transitioned fully into a new era, we believe that the volume of responsibility bestowed on us as a community to own and manage the ecosystem is one that is really heavy and plentiful; hence, the availability of a realistic vision, backed by a time-bound roadmap to guide our development and expenditure, is crucial to prevent us from doing things that would destruct the organic growth, security, and sustainability of the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nWe believe the line items spelled out in the roadmap are all crucial for the ecosystem’s growth. Our only feedback is that whereas the roadmap gives a lot of attention to development, a good amount of attention should also be given to educating the community about the need for these developments. We should also look at training a lot more developers for effective inclusion in the development of the ecosystem. Africa has a lot of potential in that regard, where the ecosystem could tap in by simplifying the development process and encouraging the young and vibrant minds of the region to engage through the creation of technical educational opportunities.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/master/vote_context/7a_roadmap.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Suggested Additions To The 2025 Roadmap\r\n\r\n>March 4, 2025\r\n\r\nThe relevant info action (*gov_action12meeq4r43udremwpm6fzt4nt7fctvt0ah7798x036m2r4nhlccmqqhmr9wx*) requests that dReps provide feedback with their vote and consider voting repeatedly after revisions. \r\n\r\n    During the lifetime of the governance action, the Product Committee will iterate upon the roadmap based upon DRep feedback, adjusting the referenced roadmap. DReps are encouraged to attach metadata to their votes, providing rationale; these rationales will be reviewed by the Product Committee. A yes vote for this action signals support for the proposed roadmap. A no vote on this action signals a lack of support for the roadmap. An abstain vote means signals neither in favor nor against. While the referenced roadmap develops, DReps should consider submitting multiple votes to signal approval across versions.\r\n\r\nWith this in mind I am tentatively voting against this roadmap and offering three suggestions for what I believe should be prioritized in addition to what has already been outlined. \r\n\r\n- Post Quantum R&D\r\n- Ouroborus Genesis\r\n- Ouroborus Chronos\r\n\r\n## Post Quantum R&D\r\n\r\nQuantum computers are coming sooner than anticipated and the first practical application will be breaking the elliptic curve cryptography Cardano depends on. We need a plan beyond mere disaster recovery. I suggest we start by drafting an inventory of everything that needs to be upgraded, funding the development of competing solutions (hash-based and lattice-based), and hiring cryptographers to design domain specific signature schemes for use in blockchain. \r\n\r\n[Post Quantum Cardano By Charles Hoskinson](https://www.youtube.com/live/nozlBDEzhZE)\r\n\r\n## Ouroborus Genesis\r\n\r\nThe ability to bootstrap from Genesis has the potential to differentiate Cardano from other proof-of-stake networks and eliminate all lingering dependency on centralized actors. From what I understand, work on Genesis is nearly complete, making this an easy win. \r\n\r\n[Genesis Paper](https://iohk.io/en/research/library/papers/ouroboros-genesis-composable-proof-of-stake-blockchains-with-dynamic-availability/)\r\n\r\n## Ouroborus Chronos\r\n\r\nWhen paired with Genesis, Chronos will provide feature parity with proof-of-work blockchains. Implementing Chronos before Leios and multiple node implementations would be prudent. I fear Chronos is not sufficiently discussed and may otherwise never be implemented. \r\n\r\n[Chronos Paper](https://iohk.io/en/research/library/papers/ouroboros-chronos-permissionless-clock-synchronization-via-proof-of-stake/)\r\n\r\n## Conclusion\r\n\r\nIncluding **Post Quantum R&D** would be enough to make me change my vote to YES. However I would very much like to see Genesis and Chronos included as I believe they *complete* a significant goal of the Cardano project which is to prove that proof-of-stake can be just as secure as proof-of-work. This would not only help by improving Cardano's security but would have the added benefit of differentiating Cardano in an increasingly competitive blockchain industry. \r\n\r\nSigned William Doyle\r\n\r\nYour friendly neighborhood DRep! <br>\r\n$computerman <br>\r\ndrep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreie4jnvdiioopdme3ftllrw4oggpeyprgyml6bjttggp2ymizqmqcu -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGA: Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n\r\nhttps://gov.tools/governance_actions/56f39054758f1a3cedc1de9225d66bf270b62dfdbfbc5399f1d6d43aceffc636#0\r\n\r\nhttps://adastat.net/governances/56f39054758f1a3cedc1de9225d66bf270b62dfdbfbc5399f1d6d43aceffc63600\r\n\r\nAction ID: gov_action12meeq4r43udremwpm6fzt4nt7fctvt0ah7798x036m2r4nhlccmqqhmr9wx\r\n\r\nVote: Yes\r\n\r\nRationale\r\nYoroi has cast a “Yes” vote in favor of the “Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond” Governance Action with the Action ID: gov_action12meeq4r43udremwpm6fzt4nt7fctvt0ah7798x036m2r4nhlccmqqhmr9wx.\r\n\r\nConsidering Yoroi’s focus as an integral open-source infrastructure product for user usability, the roadmap provides critical initiatives specifically on two fronts that are in line with Yoroi’s future development plans for greater adoption.\r\n\r\nYoroi aims to unlock and provide increased utility through programmable assets\r\n\r\nProgrammable assets extend Cardano’s use cases far beyond simple transactions, offering advanced on-chain functionalities already seen in other chains. These offer more opportunities for users and businesses to leverage Cardano for services such as decentralized identity, royalty and revenue mechanisms, tokenized access membership, and regulated stablecoins. Yoroi can work to develop functionalities and features alongside these priorities if the roadmap is approved, maximizing wallet user experience and adoption of Cardano.\r\n\r\nYoroi advocates for Layer-2 Solutions to drive scalability and handle high-volume transactions\r\n\r\nThe roadmap shows a multi-layered approach to drive scalability, which is critical for managing high-volume transactions. Hydra’s state channels allow for microtransactions, while Midgard focuses on data-heavy dApps. This multi-layer technical architecture provides solutions for different user needs, from fast payments to more complex DeFi-related activities. This increased flexibility in Layer-2 scaling solutions allows developers to utilize tools to create high-performance applications and enables Yoroi to grow and develop more versatile services to target an expanding user base that has increasingly different specific needs.\r\n\r\nTo maintain full transparency and provide a reliable backup of the originally proposed roadmap in case of any modifications, we have uploaded a PDF version to IPFS (https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafybeifnemav24kbi5lybmejayjz6yx36w7ff2l6clbsi2gnnqbk4ujifm)",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoz/drep/refs/heads/main/ga10/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano Vision and Roadmap for 2025 and beyond\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote YES.\r\nHowever, I would also like to hear honest opposing opinions from developers and researchers.\r\nI may change my vote based on that during the voting period.\r\n\r\n[1]Rationale -\r\n1) My pledge as a DRep and the following, which have been listed in the metadata since I registered my DRep. \"I vote to help Cardano grow into a platform that supports the economic identities of billions of people.\"\r\nAll of the items on this roadmap will hopefully help achieve this vision.\r\n\r\n2) I have had conversations with people who have been critical on some items, and I have heard some cautious opinions on Hydra, Nested Transactions, and Partner Chains etc. Despite these critical comments, I believe these ideas are worth pursuing and I support this roadmap and the inclusion of these items in the Cardano Budget.\r\nHowever, I believe the \"amount\" of funding needs to be considered after further input from developers and researchers. Ideas with more negative aspects may warrant a smaller budget amount. Conversely, it may be worthwhile to consider whether items that are receiving less opposition can be given more budget to further accelerate their development.\r\n\r\n[2] Conflict of interest - There are no conflicts of interest. While there may be some potential benefits to me in the broad interpretation of this roadmap, the straightforward interpretation is that I do not intend to be a vendor on any of the items.\r\n\r\n私はYESを投じます。\r\nただし、開発者や研究者からの率直な反対意見も聞きたいです。\r\n投票期間中にそれに基づいて投票を変更する可能性があります。\r\n\r\n理由\r\n1) DRep としての私の誓約として、DRep を登録してからメタデータにリストされている内容は以下のとおりです。\r\n「Cardano が数十億人の経済的アイデンティティをサポートするプラットフォームに成長することを支援することに投票します。」\r\nこのロードマップのすべての項目が、このビジョンの実現に役立つと考えています。\r\n\r\n2) 一部の項目に批判的な人々と会話をし、Hydra、ネストされたトランザクション、パートナー チェーンについて慎重な意見を聞きました。これらの批判的なコメントにもかかわらず、私はこれらのアイデアを追求する価値があると信じており、このロードマップとこれらの項目を Cardano 予算に含めることを支持します。\r\nしかし、Budgetの「額」については、開発者や研究者からのさらなる意見を踏まえて検討する必要があると思います。より否定的な側面を持つアイデアには、より少ない予算額が妥当となるかもしれません。逆に、より反対意見の少ない項目には、より多くの予算を投じてさらにブーストするようなことができるか検討する価値があるかもしれません。\r\n\r\n利益相反 - 利益相反はありません。このロードマップを広範に解釈すると潜在的には何かの利益が私にあるかもしれませんが、素直に解釈するとどの項目のベンダーにも私はなる予定がありません。",
      "vote": "YES"
    }
  ],
  "CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.4": [
    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/gov_action1jxne7hynfd7frcczwumd2eggps4kvy0msjztz9t0mutpy870ksgqqp6vp3p.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.4\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis seems like a constructive maturation of the current version of the constitution. These changes add clarity and more formalized treasury management while maintaining the same ethos of the current version. The most impactful changes are:\r\n- Treasury governance becomes much more structured and auditable with mandatory disclosure, audit, and administrator requirements\r\n- Monetary policy expands from a simple supply cap to actively seeking to preserve Ada's utility\r\n- Anti-corruption measures prohibiting vote-buying by dReps\r\n- Enhanced transparency through immutability requirements and role overlap disclosures\r\n- Clarified rights for Ada owners in the governance process",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "$Khale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmahsiXxrgUXrWobG83yv7yGypYsWCTHtwSrt2ExyuyJqW -->\r\n# $Khale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.4\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ltat8kjqrmnff3lkkpxy0j5tn66d3m0gy64dc92asft5g6dl9ws`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nConstitution v2.4 retains and strengthens the governance architecture introduced in earlier versions, particularly the clear definition of roles and thresholds, the standardized and immutable governance‑action document model, and the comprehensive guardrails around protocol changes and treasury withdrawals.\r\n​\r\nBy formally removing non‑binding “expectation” and “encouragement” clauses and the mandated CC code of conduct from the constitutional text, this version focuses the Constitution on enforceable rules and on‑chain guardrails, while leaving codes of conduct and tooling expectations to be defined and evolved through community practice and separate processes. This is more consistent with a durable, technology‑aligned constitutional document.\r\n​\r\nThe removal of the Budget Info Action mechanism, combined with the re‑assignment of its audit, administrator, and reporting safeguards directly to all Treasury Withdrawal actions, simplifies governance while materially improving accountability. Every withdrawal must now meet the same high standard for transparency, auditability, and administrator responsibility, which aligns with best practices for treasury risk management.\r\n​\r\nThe targeted reversions from v2.3 to restore the original v1.0 wording on ada “owners”, custodians, and independent audits address EMURGO’s specific concerns without weakening the underlying constitutional requirements for custody and oversight. This adjustment supports broad stakeholder acceptance and practical ratifiability while preserving the substantive protections introduced in later versions.\r\n​\r\nTaken as a whole, v2.4 is a carefully scoped refinement rather than a structural redesign. It maintains the improvements I previously supported in v2.3, clarifies and simplifies where experience has shown friction, and strengthens the link between on‑chain governance actions and immutable, auditable documentation. For these reasons, it merits a YES vote as the most coherent and operationally sound version of the Cardano Constitution to date.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSSh72UvS249qbwiWFmSKEQBi3uGri4WPZMKDDkrCQxKH -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.4\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI had voted previously in affirmation of the v2.3 changes. The change list here from v2.3 to v2.4 is relatively minor and I see no issues.",
