    {
      "voter": "CardaFlow",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidtplbsdgqx3anqhtghnff3hkue7g6fqy6qbk3xjvc7rbsstmb4vm -->\r\n# CardaFlow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.4\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAmendment in line with 2025 incremental concurrent efforts to harmonize wording, to remove ambiguities (ADA owner vs ADA holder, removal of some inspirational clauses) and simplify TW E2E process (TW approval substituting to preliminary GA approval).",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdQShRw2Z6y3EpgxQrnsSz9NXWpkSfviYWNMAY8nwwy78 -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.4\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe support these constitutional updates because they strengthen governance clarity, treasury accountability, and proposal integrity without expanding central authority. Removing redundant mechanisms, enforcing immutability of proposal documents, and applying audit safeguards uniformly across all treasury withdrawals improves long-term sustainability and reduces governance risk. Overall, this is a pragmatic hardening of Cardano’s governance framework that benefits DReps, builders, and the ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
