      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYduCA1ixLC2gSo7GpsPcP7T88mjpqa17ey1gn3vXqRf1 -->\r\n# Dan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Global Listing Expansion - Powered by Snek\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfsgx4dqfcxxs0ms533twzs7w0cvw8vq8qwzmjyrp280jfsl8gusv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting Abstain as it has been indicated this is going to be resubmitted as an info action, possibly with a different approach: [https://x.com/goofy_crisp/status/1951735721103925507]()",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmeVFiXWpTfFdufPHzPk6gnrXmt7UXUJhKVyd7juw6TUbS -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Global Listing Expansion - Powered by Snek\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmNQhPEowPKM9sMN9aX7Zq2RkB38P3z4NxGsh875ecNkvY\r\n\r\nI am a huge supporter of SNEK, its team, and what they contribute to Cardano. Their self-funded success is exemplary. However, I will be voting a principled **NO** on this proposal.\r\n\r\nMy reasoning is crucial for treasury **sustainability**: when public funds are used for a project's commercial growth, a clear pathway for treasury replenishment must be included. This proposal lacks such a mechanism. I fully support SNEK's mission, but I cannot support a funding model that socializes costs without a plan to return value to the community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "DeepStatecraft",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcZQJYTstNJ2n5drifx8cWScqLAJudu6how9f64ApdU3A -->\r\n# DeepStatecraft\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Global Listing Expansion - Powered by Snek\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfr0cur4guksjd6whxe5mltcaksqqhzd85dnq6lfk8ex7qs5mlcye`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVote: NO – Snek Global Listing Expansion (5M ADA)\r\n\r\nI appreciate the Snek Foundation’s achievements (Kraken, Crypto.com listings, $4M self-funded investment), but I cannot support this treasury withdrawal for the following reasons:\r\n\t•\tSingle-token focus – Funds are concentrated on SNEK, with benefits to the broader ecosystem indirect and uncertain.\r\n\t•\tHigh cost vs. ecosystem ROI – 5M ADA is a significant treasury outlay for CEX listings, a marketing strategy that often produces short-lived volume spikes without sustainable adoption.\r\n\t•\tCentralized exchange dependency – This approach prioritizes CEX access over strengthening decentralized infrastructure, DeFi liquidity, and developer tooling that benefit all projects.\r\n\t•\tOpportunity cost – These funds could back initiatives that provide shared infrastructure, onboarding pipelines, and reusable tech for every Cardano builder.\r\n\t•\tMarket risk – Memecoin-driven strategies can amplify volatility and reputational risk for Cardano if sentiment turns.\r\n\r\nI believe treasury funds should focus on network-level adoption drivers and foundational infrastructure—not single-token promotion—no matter how strong its community or track record.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
