      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmY3QQJed6nN5KMYkmbeeq48zSq124JiwbveCQV4T5C5ap -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs per the budget that I previously approved. Cardano needs node decentralisation, this plays a big part in turning the page and moving forward while shedding some of the baggage from the past.\r\n\r\nPerhaps not the best forum to elaborate on this, but since I’ve discontinued posting on X, I’ll do it here:\r\n\r\nRecent discussions have made it clear to me that some groups have designs on the treasury. This comes at a time where Cardano is perhaps at its most vulnerable, as anyone who can “read” crypto markets can tell you. \r\n\r\nI am done being gaslighted about how much spending is needed to “save Cardano DeFi” etc. \r\n\r\nFrom here on out I am in fiscal hawk mode, protecting the treasury with all my might, and spending it only on things that truly can make a material technical difference. This is the only way Cardano stands a chance, for now.",
