    {
      "voter": "Luc₳s @ 45B.io (Direct Voter)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPfYWXhc23EvwCMj9FA9Qpym9HQvCsywZRj1x3cY7xezh -->\r\n# Luc₳s @ 45B.io (Direct Voter)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Pebble + Gerolamo - HLabs 2026 Budget\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygltkznfvhpf722s50kan2pnsskpxz3vccdtvmcmx5mw4lssz7w7t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting on this is a no-brainer after understanding the use cases this will enable, which are impactful and unique on Cardano and the broader Web3 space.\r\n\r\nPebble is an idea driven by extremely deep insight on Cardano Dev tooling history and state-of-the-art regarding smart contract development. Bringing us a fresh and modern solution in the most commonly adopted coding language.\r\n\r\nGerolamo, having nodes running client-side, communicating with the network and each other, will be an amazing step forward in allowing truly decentralized apps.\r\n\r\nThis project complements others progressing on Cardano to greatly decentralize our infrastructure, bringing it to edge devices (browsers / mobile). The proposer's background on Cardano is unquestionable, and the proposal's value is reasonable.\r\n\r\nI'll stand behind this, however many times it needs to be resubmitted, because I believe in this proposal. Have a listen to the proposer here: https://x.com/pedrolucasnet/status/2049506813125525891",
