    {
      "voter": "Medusa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmYGuF5p53PVe6Erh7U1vBsAoyNUZ6q8nGRdLUbyxFecbz -->\r\n# Medusa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Budget Process Framework (facilitated by Intersect)\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg5pzxhp0lu0m7757ww2hke8qhcuqgqt3c2ezphngwytz4gjr6yge`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNo, no, no - once again, no. Monopolizing the budget is a terrible idea. It was a bad idea last time, and it is a bad idea now. No. We know where this leads - 90% of the funds will go to 9,000 promises from IOG (with a very low completion rate), and the remaining 10% will go to “Raid the Treasury”-style proposals, which are largely useless for the network. No.",
