      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/r/25/250812_zkbridge_a9376f98df3e.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal directly addresses a critical gap in Cardano's interoperability by delivering a zero-knowledge bridge with open-source smart contracts, protocol documentation, and a proof-of-concept deployment. It enables secure, trust-minimised asset and message transfers with other blockchains, removing reliance on centralised validators. The vendor has proven cryptographic and Aiken smart contract expertise, and the project is part of the approved 2025 Cardano budget. Funding aligns with ecosystem priorities for cross-chain connectivity and future zkRollup capabilities.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQ1KCPQHEHoiSkEebQVACqqyUGNBo8LFrLwZg9QADuoBu -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis ZK Bridge initiative addresses one of Cardano's most pressing challenges: secure and trustless cross-chain interoperability. By building a zero-knowledge bridge and providing open-source circuits, smart contracts, and detailed technical documentation, the team lays a solid foundation for broader adoption and future zkRollup integration.\r\n\r\nThe vendor, Eryx, has proven technical expertise in zk systems and Aiken development, and the implementation plan includes concrete deliverables on the Cardano testnet.\r\n\r\n本提案にYES票を投じます。\r\n\r\n本ZKブリッジ提案は、Cardanoが直面する重要課題である「安全かつ信頼不要なクロスチェーン接続」に対する実践的な解決策です。ゼロ知識証明ベースのブリッジ構築、サーキットやスマートコントラクトのオープンソース化、詳細な技術文書の提供など、将来的なzkRollupとの統合にもつながる重要な土台を築く内容となっています。\r\n\r\nベンダーであるEryxは、ZKシステムやAiken開発における高い技術力を持ち、Cardanoテストネット上での具体的な成果物提出も明記されています。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/17_ZK_Bridge_administered_by_Intersect_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports the ₳700,000 treasury withdrawal for the ZK Bridge project because it addresses one of the most critical gaps in the Cardano ecosystem: secure, trustless, and modular cross-chain interoperability.\r\n\r\nCurrently, Cardano lacks native infrastructure for zero-knowledge (ZK) bridges. Most existing bridges rely on centralized or multi-signature schemes, which have proven vulnerable in other ecosystems. This proposal offers a fundamentally different and decentralized approach by implementing a ZK bridge that allows secure messaging and asset transfer between Cardano and any isomorphic blockchain.\r\n\r\nThe benefits of this proposal are multifold:\r\n\t1.\tSecurity and Trust Minimization: By using zero-knowledge proofs, the bridge eliminates the need for centralized validators or long challenge windows.\r\n\t2.\tLiquidity and Composability: It enables seamless integration with external ecosystems and access to their liquidity and tools.\r\n\t3.\tModular Interoperability Framework: The design allows other blockchains to easily integrate with Cardano by implementing the counterpart smart contracts.\r\n\t4.\tFuture zkRollup Enablement: The bridge infrastructure lays essential groundwork for native zkRollups on Cardano.\r\n\t5.\tOpen-source and Reusable Components: All code, circuits, and documentation will be published to enable reuse by other projects.\r\n\r\nSIPO also recognizes the credibility and deep expertise of the vendor, Eryx Coop, whose team has contributed to multiple ZK projects, including Plonky2 and Aztec’s Noir. Their prior work in Aiken and EUTxO ZK integrations demonstrates strong alignment with Cardano’s architecture.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the proposal is contractually governed and managed by Intersect with robust on-chain treasury controls, milestone verification, and third-party assurance, all of which contribute to transparency and accountability.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO believes this proposal is a strategic investment that will significantly enhance Cardano’s interoperability, scalability, and competitiveness in the zero-knowledge space.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、₳700,000のトレジャリー引き出しによるZK Bridgeプロジェクトを強く支持します。なぜなら、これはカルダノにとって最も重要かつ未解決な課題である「安全・信頼不要・モジュール型のクロスチェーン相互運用性」を直接的に解決するからです。\r\n\r\n現在、CardanoはネイティブなZKブリッジ基盤を持っておらず、多くの既存ブリッジは中央集権型バリデーターやマルチシグを利用しており、他のエコシステムで多数の脆弱性・攻撃事例が報告されています。本提案は、Cardanoと他のアイソモーフィック・ブロックチェーン間の安全な通信と資産転送を可能にするZKブリッジを構築し、これらの課題を根本から解決します。\r\n\r\nこの提案には以下のような多くの利点があります：\r\n\t1.\tセキュリティと信頼最小化：ZK証明を活用することで、中央集権的な管理者や長期間のチャレンジ期間が不要になります。\r\n\t2.\t流動性と合成性の向上：他のエコシステムとスムーズに統合でき、より多くの流動性やツールへアクセス可能になります。\r\n\t3.\tモジュール型の相互運用フレームワーク：他のチェーンもCardanoと接続しやすくなります。\r\n\t4.\t将来のzkRollup実装の基盤整備：ZKブリッジ構築は、将来的なカルダノネイティブのzkRollup実現にもつながる重要なステップです。\r\n\t5.\tオープンソースと再利用性：コード、回路、ドキュメントすべてが公開され、他プロジェクトによる応用・活用が容易です。\r\n\r\nまた、提案を実施するベンダー「Eryx Coop」は、Plonky2やAztec’s Noirなど数々のZK関連OSSに貢献しており、AikenやEUTxOモデルに関するZK統合の知見も深く、Cardanoとの技術的整合性があります。\r\n\r\nさらに、このプロジェクトはIntersectによって契約的・制度的に管理されており、オンチェーンでの資金管理、マイルストーンの達成確認、第三者による監査が組み込まれています。これは透明性と説明責任のある運営を担保します。\r\n\r\n以上の理由により、SIPOはこの提案がCardanoの相互運用性・スケーラビリティ・ZK領域における競争力を大幅に向上させる戦略的投資であると確信し、賛成票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVaUuUjQhRzQTYEYEErBPXbEv6wTe5gisCpTtK77Ys2ZV -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious has voted in favor of all 39 Treasury Withdrawal proposals submitted. These proposals were selected through a well-defined process, and we fully support them out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPYjtdSC8YG3u7eTmz4f4ExNND9F5543Lk63meLpp2HAH -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA ZK bridge framework positions Cardano to interact credibly with external ecosystems while laying the groundwork for future zkRollup infrastructure.\r\nThe technical scope is ambitious but justified, and the vendor (Eryx) brings strong ZK expertise with relevant contributions in both the Cardano and Ethereum ecosystems. This aligns with STORM Partners’ mission to support high-leverage infrastructure that attracts capital, talent, and developer adoption while expanding Cardano’s narrative as a privacy and security-first chain.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(14).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal funds the development of a zero-knowledge (ZK) bridge to enhance secure and trust-minimized interoperability between Cardano and other blockchains. It directly addresses one of Cardano's critical gaps—the lack of native, decentralized cross-chain infrastructure—by providing a ZK-proof-based mechanism for secure asset transfers.\r\n\r\nThe vendor, Eryx Coop, is a well-qualified team with a proven track record in ZK cryptography, Aiken development, and open-source contributions, including the Lambdaworks library and CircleSTARKS. Their solution leverages Cardano’s native capabilities and lays groundwork for future ZK rollups, privacy-preserving apps, and scalability features.\r\n\r\nThis initiative aligns with the approved Intersect-administered budget and will follow strong delivery assurance and milestone-based accountability under legal contract. Given the pressing need for secure interoperability and the vendor’s expertise, this project is a strategic investment in Cardano’s future.\r\n\r\nI am voting YES to unlock Cardano’s interoperability potential with a secure ZK bridge.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Terminada",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TerminadaDrep/vote-contexts/refs/heads/main/20250725/004.jsonld -->\r\n# Terminada\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytf9f78k7rkwk4cu6l2nvna22keu9yus4kqzc0hqspd36uszu0xc2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIOG is already building bridge technology required for Midnight which will be released soon.  We should wait for this development before funding similar initiatives.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdATSqc8oYHJprML7MSzcH388gucMcn9qZg349UH8CSqi -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA couple of months ago, I supported the resolution to bundle all of the Intersect Budget Proposals into 1 or 2 formal on-chain governance votes.\r\n\r\nEach of these proposals has already undergone extensive scrutiny and received 50% or greater support from the active DReps in the ecosystem, and I will honor that prior decision and the work these prospective developers have put in by voting yes on all the proposals from the Intersect Budget team.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmenGHPQeTjt9Ah27EF5LXsA8tqci2eRQoZQN1W2ATuMLj -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting No on the proposal to withdraw ₳700,000 from the Cardano Treasury to fund a ZK bridge administered by Intersect. While the development of zero-knowledge interoperability is conceptually aligned with Cardano’s long-term goals, this proposal appears premature and potentially duplicative of ongoing efforts by Input Output Global (IOG). Without clear differentiation or coordination with IOG’s roadmap, this initiative risks fragmentation and wasteful overlap. Furthermore, the proposal does not establish a compelling or time-sensitive justification for immediate funding, nor does it outline transparent governance, execution milestones, or long-term maintenance plans. Given the Treasury’s finite lifespan, large discretionary outlays must meet a high bar of strategic clarity and ecosystem consensus. I am not opposed to supporting a ZK bridge in the future, but it should follow a clearer demonstration of need, coordination, and timing. For now, this proposal does not warrant approval.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmeq8gDf6GReUzhek63BYcdJqdrzNGTEv62pjPE1m2fKJp -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn a landscape where Cardano must adopt a business-minded, strategic approach to safeguard its treasury and scientific foundation, this proposal feels premature and insufficiently grounded. The ecosystem would benefit more from incremental, well-scoped interoperability projects that leverage existing Layer 2 and ZK research, rather than a large upfront bet on an unproven ZK bridge framework.\r\n\r\nThe proposal’s abstract and motivation are heavy on buzzwords—“zero-knowledge,” “modular,” “trustless,” “isomorphic blockchains”—yet conspicuously light on concrete technical differentiation or demonstrable competitive advantage. Cardano’s existing ecosystem is already advancing with Hydra, optimistic rollups, and ongoing research in ZK proofs. What exactly sets this implementation apart? The rationale claims superiority over optimistic bridges by touting reduced latency and trust assumptions, but fails to engage with the inherent complexity and security challenges of ZK bridges, especially in a multi-chain environment. The devil is in the details, and those are missing here.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the vendor’s profile, while impressive in academic credentials and prior cryptographic work, lacks specific evidence of delivering production-grade cross-chain ZK bridge infrastructure. Contributions to libraries and protocols are not synonymous with having built a secure, scalable, and battle-tested bridge compatible with Cardano’s unique eUTxO model. The proposal does not clarify how the ZK circuits will interact with Cardano’s accounting model or how they will handle the notoriously difficult problem of finality and state synchronization in a trust-minimized way.\r\n\r\nThis is a \"No\" from my side!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTHeAhbGcqSBGsW6GnhmWRGawjvgjur3yf8fFH9MbmkSD -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI endorse all proposals incorporating zero-knowledge solutions and technologies.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaLFhdJadHE1WwVqFK9fyB974CajEu7FCNpDc6y4yw2My -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote against the ZK Bridge proposal requesting 700,000 ADA due to significant overlap with Input Output Global’s (IOG) ongoing ZK bridge development for Midnight, Cardano’s privacy-focused partner chain, set for mainnet launch in early 2025. While Eryx’s expertise and the proposal’s focus on a modular, open-source toolkit are commendable, funding a parallel effort risks redundancy and inefficient resource allocation. Without clear differentiation or a detailed plan to complement IOG’s work, the Cardano ecosystem would benefit more from consolidating efforts to enhance existing interoperability solutions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Intersect_TWGA17.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: This is a general rationale we have prepared to support our “yes” vote on all the 39 treasury withdrawal actions. This follows careful review and consideration of the metadata of these treasury withdrawal proposals and hence is not a blanket voting practice.\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep Committee, have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawal governance actions currently live on-chain and submitted under the administration of IntersectMBO. These actions are the necessary implementation step following the community's approval of the ₳275.3 million Cardano Ecosystem Budget, the necessary budget info action that precedes the treasury withdrawal process. Our support reflects not only continuity with our earlier \"yes\" votes on the overarching budget info action and its constituent proposals but also our confidence in the smart contract guide and project execution mechanisms Intersect has established as an administrative body for these proposals.\r\n\r\nEach of these 39 withdrawals corresponds directly to proposals that have already passed a respective Budget Info Action with wide community and DRep support of 64.23%. As Wada DRep, we reviewed, scored, and supported many of these initiatives during the budgeting phase, using our internal ₳280M Net Change Limit framework. Our endorsement of the full ₳275.3M package was not a blanket approval but the outcome of detailed deliberation. Therefore, we see it as our responsibility to honor those community-approved funding decisions by affirming these follow-up Treasury withdrawal governance actions.\r\n\r\nImportantly, we are confident in Intersect’s role as the administrator of these treasury disbursements. We have independently reviewed the Smart Contract Guide, disbursement architecture, and accountability structures associated with these withdrawals. The use of milestone-gated smart contracts, multi-signature treasuries, and on-chain/off-chain tracking mechanisms provides strong assurance of transparency, risk management, and community accountability. We are particularly satisfied that Intersect has adopted security-audited contract templates and provides public documentation on how treasury funds will be administered, paused if necessary, and even returned if unused.\r\n\r\nIn our view, rejecting or abstaining from these Treasury Withdrawals at this stage would risk destabilizing delivery timelines, undermining community trust, and introducing administrative conflicts that may violate the spirit of the Constitution’s Articles on budgeting. We believe that treasury funding is not just about allocation; it’s about consistent and credible execution. As such, the DRep role requires continuity and follow-through, especially when prior voting outcomes have clearly mandated action.\r\n\r\nTherefore, in alignment with our constitutional responsibilities, community-aligned decision-making, and our assessment of Intersect’s administrative protocols, we have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawals Governance Actions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/18_2_default.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm defaulting to voting yes because there is some degree of consensus already achieved on each of these. So unless I have a significant issue with one of these proposals I will be voting yes on it.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb1RQdqqCdFUypDR4vV4peWHarwXGWbBreUQ4JC3RpdUG -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nYoroi votes YES on the governance action to fund ZK Bridge administered by Intersect.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nInteroperability boost – This proposal addresses a critical gap by enabling trustless cross-chain interactions, which could drive both liquidity and user expansion for Cardano.\r\n\r\nZK-native advantage – A modular ZK bridge positions Cardano to catch up with and eventually rival ecosystems like Ethereum in privacy and scalability features.\r\n\r\nStrong team backing – Led by Eryx, a team with deep expertise in zero-knowledge cryptography and Aiken, the project shows strong potential for timely and reliable delivery.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nDespite the complexity, Yoroi sees this as a strategically important step to strengthen Cardano’s Layer 2 future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUNsjSzMu4HfpytqRLvRcbFMYVzsgH4R2GtH3PkP4mZW5 -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳700,000 for ZK Bridge administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote as necessary to help Cardano grow into a platform that supports the economic identities of billions of people. This proposal charges a fair price to achieve what is needed to achieve that. \r\n\r\nThere are no significant matters that affect the neutrality of my decision-making.\r\n\r\nDetailed rationale and the improvements I would like to see made to the proposal are attached in the following spreadsheet \"TW vote #01\" or PDF.\r\n\r\nSpecifically with regards to bundled proposals, next time I would request that one of the following be implemented:\r\n\r\n1. Bundled proposals should be subject to a temperature check vote for each item. \r\n2. I would like bundled proposals to be verified or created by entities, consortia, or individuals selected by the DRep.\r\n\r\nSpreadsheet:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1M8JAuAntJOa7Z6j3GfC2hWFl4kbZLkzEel_cN4-kymw/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nPDF:\r\nipfs://bafkreianp5xhbo3ojlxqjjah4kyimr6u62uwnxd2t3lwwu3qmpn4jf4n5a\r\n\r\n私はCardanoが数十億人の経済アイデンティティを支えるプラットフォームへ成長していくために必要な投票を行います。この提案書は、それを達成するために必要な事項を実現するための正当なコストを請求しています。\r\n\r\n私の意思決定の中立性に影響を与える重大な事項はありません。\r\n\r\n根拠の詳細と、提案書について私が改善して欲しい点は、次のスプレッドシートの「TW vote #01」またはPDFに添付されています。\r\n\r\n特に、バンドル型提案書に関しては、次回は、次のいずれかが実施されることをリクエストします。\r\n1. バンドル型提案書は、内訳別の温度チェックの投票を行うこと。\u20282. バンドル型提案書は、DRepにより選出されるエンティティやコンソーシアムや個人により、検証または作成されるようにして欲しいと思います。\r\n\r\nSpreadsheet:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1M8JAuAntJOa7Z6j3GfC2hWFl4kbZLkzEel_cN4-kymw/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nPDF:\r\nipfs://bafkreianp5xhbo3ojlxqjjah4kyimr6u62uwnxd2t3lwwu3qmpn4jf4n5a",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
