  "Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth": [
    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/gov_action13836fuy3yttxn4hkeqka398q9qnwsjtmul4sxc3nht7qae8uvejsqm7ukh8.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nL1 marketing to primarily retail users and small businesses is not a focus of funding at this point in time for me. One enterprise adoption agreement could bring a much higher quantity of consistent users to the L1 than any region-focused retail growth initiative. We should be looking for more network usage, not more token holders.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXubSZbv2xnLJobZASMuk9JiFt7JqYvqNXtQvontVK6md -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe just went through a budget proposal / community vote / treasury withdrawal cycle, and I didn't see this one competing with those proposals. It should. Outside of that, go to Catalyst for funding.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote62.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI find the Info action step adds unnecessary delays and confusion, given that 67% approval is already required at the final vote. But since it's now a mandatory part of the process, I'm voting Abstain just to let it proceed - the actual decision will be made at the final vote. It's worth noting that I voted Yes on this proposal earlier, for the reason mentioned above. However, after several discussions within the team and with other DReps, I came to the conclusion that Abstaining is the more appropriate option in this case. A Yes vote might create the false impression that I fully support the proposal, which isn't necessarily true. I simply don't want to take part in the preliminary vote, but at the same time I don't want the default No from non-voting DReps to negatively affect the proposal.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPJSaH1Nm7QUaNdNKhaEcTZA6iSLSuSfKwAHx9HJZKfxY -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本提案に反対します。オセアニアでの活動は価値があるものの、財務資金を投じる優先度としては限定的だと考えます。予算の大部分は基盤技術やガバナンス強化など、Cardano全体に直接波及する取り組みに優先して使われるべきです。\\n\\nI vote No on this proposal. While community-building in Oceania has value, I believe the treasury should prioritize initiatives that directly strengthen Cardano’s core infrastructure and governance. The budget allocation here offers limited ecosystem-wide impact compared to higher-priority needs.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AltcoinOracle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSbXLL2jnSy6QrM5AE9CoA4XbcxCEZXpXL1rsk3jcE98x -->\r\n# AltcoinOracle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygvgk3899qm38zth07z5clhfjvzfhe2mf2kvkqrfxp93r5srjre5s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I focus on core engineering first. I don’t support using treasury capital for events, marketing, or exchange listings.\r\n\r\nStrength and honor.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AustinAnthony",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmP7u8RKe1YvEgzMvukKB8fSwmMLiy77qwaxZSodP53Yym -->\r\n# AustinAnthony\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg5v33dh3pvf9xelauyd5l9qsa3yd6lezf4u7kccp3xqwjspcz3py`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting down on this Oceania strategic plan because Cardano should prioritize urgent matters like scalability, client node diversity, DEX liquidity and core technology upgrades to ensure the platform’s long-term success. Catalyst is an excellent outlet for funding initiatives like this, resources should focus on the network’s infrastructure first.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "benzio",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfTMt2AV5zbskTvXmdstEK3nceWKsyKrzyFu1uoQVNnkc -->\r\n# benzio\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwge9pgkeyd5eawz4y07mvkt09jkmx9d2levdzdcr6xl7s2nr4hy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIf you’d like to support an independent developer who is actively learning and preparing to contribute to the Cardano ecosystem, consider making a donation.\r\nYour support will help me dedicate more time to study, build, and grow within the Cardano community.\r\nThank you,\r\nBenzio\r\n\r\nAddress for donations: addr1qy3tfm8gj8sxtkql7p5m4rvsc55l96cv5lwlz6pf3fde4wdtmhg0ztuweefsawjtsl3yhy32ma0ym8k3765wp6ml34jq8evqeu",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Big Lazy Cat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://doc.biglazycat.com/drep/89e3a4f09122d669d6f6c82dd894e02826e8497be7eb036233bafc0ee4fc6665_0.jsonld -->\r\n# Big Lazy Cat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffcjs0njfea09xhs6up429rhya5pxd7qz7hvmwq6vqy2nczwpj3g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the proposal presents a well-structured regional strategy, I find it difficult to clearly measure the real impact of community events, hackathons, and marketing activities. Without stronger, quantifiable KPIs tied to adoption and on-chain results, it is challenging to evaluate whether the requested budget will achieve sustainable outcomes. Therefore, I choose to abstain.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Blockjock (James Meidinger)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPe4XHLByrbUP3DorWPCPKscZwYhWnLFk9WqUEYhAgCYX -->\r\n# Blockjock (James Meidinger)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnypzfv2v8fmfelthahvn0rqyh54sf6z2aa5m7f3fkjgqqt8l2qq`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI do feel as though this proposal mirrors a few others already funded but it does come from a very good team and I do not doubt their competency level. With that said I will be abstaining on this proposal and wish the team all success in this and future endeavors.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiayy5gp637norlerddxz5uqob3e3s36titr6toucpzkkgsapoltom -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n賛成票。 本提案を地域DAO戦略のテンプレートとして支持します。規模は中規模で実証に適しており、モデル検証にふさわしいバランスの取れたパイロットです。オセアニアでの成功は、地域コミュニティ主導のモデルが世界各地に拡張し、カルダノが多様で分散したローカルエコシステムを通じて成長する未来を示すものです。\r\n\r\n—\r\n\r\nYes. I support this proposal as a template for regional DAO strategies. At a moderate, practical scale, it offers a balanced pilot for proving the model. Success in Oceania can demonstrate how community-led initiatives scale globally, enabling Cardano to grow through diverse, decentralized local ecosystems.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeqGK4VisYXJXaodRPWYxJLyvyEwiecCcx5FdZbgFNper -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe impact this proposal has is not big enough for the budget they are asking for. We are hoping for a more global marketing strategy.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Captain Crypto",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreicgtl2za46ew72db7tb2yfbkqv5562aqqaz2mwludigeieh6nz3de -->\r\n# Captain Crypto\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2x0d3jgae3xs7kdagq2w74kmzlgktw3l5th2lusrgn7m6gg52x78`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES on this proposal because it represents a well-structured, regionally focused strategy that aligns with Cardano’s mission of decentralisation, inclusion, and sustainable adoption.\r\n\r\nReasons for support:\r\n\r\nStrategic Regional Growth – Oceania offers a diverse environment for piloting community-driven adoption models that can be replicated globally. Strengthening Cardano’s presence here reduces geographic concentration and improves network resilience.\r\n\r\nComprehensive Approach – The plan balances investment across people (capacity building, education), projects (hackathons, pilots, partnerships), and promotion (storytelling, marketing), creating a virtuous cycle that drives long-term adoption.\r\n\r\nTransparency & Accountability – Milestone-based funding, GitHub/IPFS evidence storage, public reporting, and the option for DRep-led dispute resolution ensure funds are managed responsibly and in alignment with the Constitution.\r\n\r\nCommunity Empowerment – By engaging underrepresented voices, local institutions, and grassroots communities, the proposal strengthens governance participation and broadens Cardano’s diversity.\r\n\r\nChecks & Balances – The inclusion of an independent auditor, constitutional guardrails, and neutral treasury address management provides safeguards against misuse of funds.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nThis initiative demonstrates a thoughtful balance of vision and practical mechanisms for oversight. By supporting it, we affirm Cardano’s commitment to global inclusion and sustainable ecosystem growth.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardaFlow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmatdEATkbMATKoAKFFVqcwPwYdeidMXbu6jY8zpiQ5fH5 -->\r\n# CardaFlow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMy threshold for budget spending in 2025 is reached",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Africa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreic7asfrsqsqptocd4ikmeb6dm47bqnl267yat2ggceihnrzwh6xey -->\r\n# Cardano Africa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytj9kz0n5yamacgcj8jr6apn36hx5suzqpefxvhy4cvfqmsqangtx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe have voted No for the proposal Cardano in Oceania: A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth. While the initiative outlines an ambitious vision for strengthening Cardano’s presence in the region, we believe the current design raises more concerns than it resolves.\r\n\r\nThe requested budget of 778,000 ADA feels disproportionate when weighed against the activities described. Community-building, hackathons, and awareness campaigns are valuable, but their impact is often difficult to measure, and the return on investment is not clearly demonstrated. Without stronger guarantees of tangible adoption or measurable on-chain activity, this level of funding is hard to justify.\r\n\r\nWe are also cautious about the heavy reliance on a single administrator, selfdriven Services. Although the proposal describes checks and dispute resolution mechanisms, entrusting so much control to one entity introduces risks of centralisation and inefficiency. A broader coalition of administrators would have provided greater confidence.\r\n\r\nFinally, while Oceania is important, other regions currently show stronger demand and higher growth potential. Given limited treasury resources, we believe Cardano’s focus should remain on areas where adoption barriers are higher and impact is clearer. For these reasons, we cannot support this proposal in its current form.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Cypherpunks",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiechmohfr4wshgctgwujququugr45fck67fbeyo6tmz3apvzyclky -->\r\n# Cardano Cypherpunks\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23wk4w6f2aumc92vl9m3x74xzm6jh4ha9wdq09yfq2sl6q8zlv4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNot critical enough or shows promise of high ROI for the trasury",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmcweTgtvgw4bA9VKRA1G4cJWgoubgTjYLE7p9EqYW8R4h -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmV485zWtLjm5VqbsSzSCgqhUAPftFCuCCcgczkhbQNChe\r\n\r\nThis proposal is a professional and grassroots effort to create a regional hub for Cardano. The plan to develop a repeatable model for ecosystem growth is a valuable strategic objective. We also note the inclusion of a milestone-based funding model and a framework for KPIs, which demonstrates a commitment to accountability. The team consists of active and credible community members.\r\n\r\n## Recommendations for a Treasury Withdrawal Proposal\r\nWhile we support the direction of this info action, a subsequent treasury withdrawal proposal or revised info action should be significantly strengthened by addressing the following areas:\r\n1. A More Focused Scope: The current strategy is broad, aiming to deliver initiatives across multiple verticals (government, enterprise, non-profits) at once. Our recommendation is to narrow the focus of this proposal to one or two key areas where the team has existing networks. This would likely yield faster, more tangible results and build a stronger foundation for later expansion.\r\n2. Establishment of Baseline Data: The proposal outlines KPIs for growth but lacks baseline data on the region's current status (e.g., DRep participation, developer activity). To accurately measure the impact of the initiative, we would expect a treasury withdrawal proposal to include this starting-point data.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanolotus",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaUYWPVnE6rgy1zNVojvf1DhqJ4AY1bLMWqFcYheCsUs2 -->\r\n# Cardanolotus\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt7hfdllz0l707unkh9g2fs9e35dl6d94tvjynnh4t5gw6gcmn4jn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is too vague.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmcgvTP6zYPFJXH4EpYDyNyhKoAm26rwKETHNARjmPcCgM -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmYj2R7ZBE6ABkacm9hcoQrjd4b2AzbVX5NKGg8FZ79x1D\r\n\r\nRecently, 37 out of 39 proposals were approved, which means a significant portion of the budget has already been allocated. Many of these proposals focused on booths, marketing, and support for local communities. Meanwhile, Fund14, where hackathon-related proposals could be submitted, has just closed.\r\n\r\nWhile I appreciate the intent behind this new proposal and believe it could have a positive impact, I think projects within the same category should be submitted and reviewed together. That way, they can compete on equal footing, making it easier to select the strongest ideas and manage total spending for the year.\r\n\r\nIn my view, this proposal should have been submitted earlier, alongside the others that were recently approved. As it stands, it feels like it overlaps with initiatives that have already received Treasury funding.\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I’ve committed to prioritizing support for builders over marketing initiatives. Rejecting this proposal aligns with that commitment, especially during the first year of on-chain governance.\r\n\r\nSoon, a major proposal will request 50M ADA to inject liquidity into Cardano DeFi—and possibly another to support Bitcoin DeFi. These initiatives are far more critical to ecosystem growth. With this year’s NCL set at 350M ADA, we need to be selective and strategic. I’d strongly prefer not to see us approach that limit too quickly.\r\n\r\nI’d prefer to see this proposal submitted next year, once the new NCL is approved and we begin planning the 2026 budget. That timing would allow it to be properly evaluated alongside other initiatives and ensure more strategic allocation of funds.\r\n\r\nUntil then, the team can think about using Catalyst Fund15.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/Info_15.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCardano is a global network, and treasury spending should be guided by neutral, impact-first criteria.  Not geography. This proposal targets one region without a convincing strategic rationale (e.g., binding partnerships, regulatory advantages, or meaningful co-funding) that justifies prioritizing Oceania over any other region.  I worry that approving it would set a precedent for generic regional asks from everywhere.  For these reasons, I am voting no on this proposal.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUsKddUDH3cwFyTMXYvTWx5AWDe94C1PXtHcrirasJNZs -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting yes on this proposal for a few key reasons.  Instead of a broad or sweeping growth initiative it's focused on a region, Oceania. From there this team has put forth a clear proposal on the who, what, how, and why. The funding ask, 778K ADA, to me seems to be about as lean as possible. I reached out to the team for feedback on this and it's intentional - minimum required to get the tasks completed. Ultimately, this proposal should help to establish putting down roots in the region and overall awareness for Cardano. We should be able to support this localized initiative for Cardano for these costs and look forward to 2026-2027 budgeting to determine if it's something we want to continue.\r\n\r\nOne line item that would have seen this proposal come down another 100K, which did raise an eyebrow, was the 100K reimbursement for the Ikigai action. I personally had thought that issue was resolved but if not, it should be reimbursed - just not sure it needed to happen bundled with this proposal.  However, given the team involved I don't have any concerns around this line item - it's the right thing to do - and up to this point it has not been addressed by anyone else.\r\n\r\nOver time, I've come to not want to vote no anymore on any project that could have gone another avenue for funding (ie. Project Catalyst). The reason being is that it pigeon holes it to a specific process that not everyone may be using or want to. The treasury is more open and available to all in my opinion, so I will always review a proposal as is.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris-O",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreid6lfmxonrd6gdofev4ggvwkilaxcsv3uf6dv4kjitienh6y6v7fm -->\r\n# Chris-O\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y25xtvu3d0gaf6cxktr9pkfgnywmqsh4fum93s8m3hlp4aqj3uqdp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCardanoの生きがい - Ikigai - Deposit Reimbursement should be a separate proposal and not bundled with this proposal. Need estimate ROI on ADA spend based on data from similar activities to justify.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Crypto Eats Legacy",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmacxyRvXmdBJcHcnFbmotFt6aca9rdSZyEHzXSkE1QnLV -->\r\n# Crypto Eats Legacy\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytd2mf58tfqv78z7e99fy0gnmfep0kscclnwpvx7qvwpc5srxwg5g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m supporting this Info Action because it combines accountability with ambition, testing adoption in Oceania through measurable milestones, and laying the foundation for a model that can drive Cardano’s growth across the world.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTLwZAz9jcJymQmsseNfbAXNPLKbEkLQRjNAnvCpK2847 -->\r\n# Dan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfsgx4dqfcxxs0ms533twzs7w0cvw8vq8qwzmjyrp280jfsl8gusv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes on this proposal because I see strong potential in Oceania as a testbed for Cardano adoption. The region combines diverse economies, cultures, and industries, and has historically been used as a proving ground for new technologies. The team has put forward a structured plan that invests in people, projects, and outreach, and the funding ask is reasonable given the scope and ambition. I believe this initiative can demonstrate how decentralised, community-led growth models work in practice and create a repeatable template for other regions.\r\n\r\nThat said, given that this Info Action appears unlikely to pass at this stage, it may be best for the team to pursue Catalyst funding in the short term. This would allow them to deliver visible, high-impact results, build measurable traction, and strengthen confidence before seeking a treasury withdrawal. Nonetheless, I support this initiative because at this stage in Cardano’s growth we need more pathways for real-world adoption. Cardano is already a technical achievement, but without tangible use cases and compelling success stories, adoption risks falling behind other chains. Oceania is well-positioned to help close that gap, and this proposal is a step in the right direction.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmWhEi3fLyjkrewqLxPeP4QL6nXwV5s5Hnou8X3bZEaGNU -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/Qmc6E5Rb2qAHzR3BjxL3HztdqQq8c3PDAaTvHgT4o6nkuP\r\n\r\nI want to credit the team for this excellent proposal, which has made this a difficult decision. However, I will be voting a reluctant **NO** out of fiscal prudence.\r\n\r\nHaving already supported a number of proposals, I am cautious about the total budget being approved. While I support regional **growth**, the high cost of this single-region pilot makes it a less efficient use of funds than a global framework. Given the need to be selective with the remaining budget, I cannot justify this particular expenditure at this time, despite its merits.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl",
