    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Oceania.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep votes to ABSTAIN on the governance action to fund Cardano in Oceania: A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nWe appreciate the proposer’s transparency and the good-faith action to reimburse the ₱ 100,000 Ikigai deposit, demonstrating accountability to the community.\r\n\r\nWhile regional engagement is important, the proposal’s focus on events, hackathons, and community activities seems better suited for Project Catalyst. Catalyst provides a collaborative environment to test, refine, and scale these types of initiatives, giving them the best chance to thrive and deliver meaningful impact.\r\nFor these reasons, Yoroi DRep chooses to abstain from this governance action.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmevPNeAQ4Ww25Kjz74KMzXASJ7NrnDSgiiutoADtZsS1H -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano in Oceania A community-led strategic plan for investing in growth\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\"Cardano in Oceania\" is an inspiring, community-led initiative, and I deeply respect the team’s passion. However, I voted No, as I believe it would be more appropriate to start with a smaller budget through Catalyst.\r\nWhile the vision is compelling, its success heavily depends on the team’s execution. Factors such as content quality, DRep development, business partnerships, and local transaction growth are all difficult to forecast and require significant trust.\r\nMany similar initiatives have received funding in the past, yet few have delivered clear, measurable outcomes. Therefore, I recommend starting small and building up success incrementally.\r\n\r\nhttps://cardano-in-oceania.github.io/how/\r\n\r\nKPI-related Concerns:\r\n1. Tracking wallets and transactions specific to Oceania seems difficult and potentially impractical.\r\n2. The goal of onboarding three new Catalyst participants feels modest compared to the ecosystem’s scale.\r\n3. Government or partner collaborations should be proposed with specific scopes and budget allocations.\r\n4. BD training plans should identify candidates, their backgrounds, and expected results up front.\r\n5. Since Oceania is largely English-speaking, global outreach in English may be more effective than region-specific campaigns.\r\n\r\n\r\n「Cardano in Oceania」は、地域コミュニティ主導の素晴らしい取り組みであり、チームの情熱に深く敬意を表します。しかし私は、Catalystを通じてより小規模な予算で始める方が適切だと考え、反対票を投じました。\r\nこの提案のビジョンは魅力的ですが、成功はチームの実行力に大きく依存します。コンテンツの質、DRepの育成、ビジネス連携、ローカルのトランザクション増加など、どれも予測が難しく、信頼が前提となります。\r\n過去にも同様の提案が資金提供を受けましたが、明確で測定可能な成果を上げた事例は多くありません。そのため、まずは小さな規模で始め、実績を積み重ねるアプローチを推奨します。\r\n\r\nhttps://cardano-in-oceania.github.io/how/\r\n\r\nKPIに関する懸念点：\r\n1. オセアニア地域に限定したウォレット数やトランザクション数の追跡は、現実的に困難と思われます。\r\n2. Catalyst参加者3社という目標は、エコシステム全体の規模に対して控えめに感じられます。\r\n3. 政府や団体との連携は、具体的な内容と予算を明記した形で提示すべきです。\r\n4. BD人材の育成については、候補者のプロフィールや期待される成果を事前に示すことが望ましいです。\r\n5. オセアニアは主に英語圏であるため、地域特化よりグローバルな英語圏全体を視野に入れた発信の方が効果的かもしれません。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    }
  ],
