    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Midgard%20Optimistic%20Rollups.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳2,162,096 for Midgard - Optimistic Rollups administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nEMURGO as DRep votes YES on the governance action for Midgard – Optimistic Rollups, based on the rationale below.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\nMidgard presents a bold, deeply Cardano-native approach to rollups, directly leveraging the strengths of the eUTxO model to enable permissionless, non-custodial, and censorship-resistant L2s. Unlike many Ethereum-based alternatives, Midgard’s architecture allows for simplified, single-party fraud proofs and seamless fee alignment with L1 via ADA-based transactions.\r\n\r\nIts tokenless design, L1-fee contribution model, and support for decentralized operators make it a potential cornerstone for scalable Cardano dApps. The proposal is highly technical but aligns with the core goals of L2 expansion, and the team at Anastasia Labs has a proven open-source track record.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nGiven the innovation, alignment with Cardano’s architecture, and the potential for long-term L1 economic value, EMURGO supports this proposal and votes Yes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
