    {
      "voter": "Musa Ridwan Itopa",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaT1LehCFwBZQaV1DybqmGiZx2doM4y1C6p8hkUNDidyf -->\r\n# Musa Ridwan Itopa\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yggumgdxdpa2dgr85etak35s4v00k07vdhvn5y3xxw33yac77c9hp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting Abstain on Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5.  As a Nigerian DRep, Unified Cardano Student Club President in Nigeria, and advocate for transparent, inclusive governance that amplifies underrepresented voices like Africa and students, I see the real risk: a single resignation could halt ratification of critical actions (like security updates or hard forks), and we've seen this play out before. The proposal offers a practical buffer while staying within constitutional guardrails (3–10 range).  But I'm not fully convinced yet lowering the min size could weaken separation of powers in low-participation times (easier collusion with fewer members), and recent CC challenges (resignations over compensation, failed size increases) point to deeper issues around engagement, diversity, and incentives that we should fix first. I need more conviction that this truly enhances resilience without unintended centralization risks.  Abstaining to signal thoughtful engagement while the community discusses further. Let's prioritize solutions that strengthen decentralization and inclusion for all not quick fixes. Open to evolving my view with stronger rationale or broader consensus. Delegate if you value careful, principled representation!",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRwFbSJnCcWEXD6X6be8Ld1GpjhHKZJLk7bBmua9TYh8c -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGuardrails are good. Having more members on the CC means more eyes are on Governance and the treasury, helping ensure they are safe.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, we are creating more work for people in the ecosystem. Reducing the number can increase participation, but it also centralises control.\r\n\r\nBecause I'm for decentralisation and representation, I'll vote NO and keep the number at 7. Keep us in check and ensure we are operating within the bounds of the Constitution.",
