    {
      "voter": "Rich King",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifxvkgs2vydbgicout7cuigboxzxdzi2c67mj4p2sl5gcsjrh6d7q -->\r\n# Rich King\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2j8r9slasj3pyyyp7rf273ekvc258pmrqalhvdadla75rq9npeku`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n5 is probably good enough. Some don't vote which blocks the whole process so don't want too many.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihuvoy2rkvg5cfw6rdhhvj4z47ayhqkczrt4a3qkp45nmb3gjbzum -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am in favor of this change. The current min size of 7 paired with an actual committee size of 7 creates an inflexible point of failure for Cardano governance. The departure or resignation of a single member immediately pauses our ability to pass important actions. This operational fragility could force the community into rushed elections, which compromises candidate vetting.\r\nIn my view the community has a choice between two reasonable paths: maintaining a min size of 7 with an actual committee size of 9, or reducing the minimum to 5 while maintaining the committee size of 7, as is suggested by this proposal. Either would work but I prefer the latter. Seven members to me is optimal and the risk of temporarily operating with 5 or 6 members is negligible compared to the very real risk of governance paralysis or the poor decision-making that stems from emergency appointments. Either way the main risk I see here is failure to move off of the 7 and 7 scenario we are currently in. If this action does not pass I would gladly support a change to a min size of 7 and a committee size of 9.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SAGAN Stake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTikWivNiLtH3qJmFxYhMhFXR2d2TXyukHG9w82WXoXz1 -->\r\n# SAGAN Stake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y290s8rwsezxkct6urmqne8tc92wqtltal8dfxfk45xj6eqn2mgfx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nReducing the minimum requirement is never the way to achieve the desired consensus. It's the path toward centralization. Do not support this.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcYMoyQ8bN1BCeFHvQhwC94tZsi614VUZ2Jp5fQoYaoVW -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI understand the intention behind this proposal to improve operational resilience by reducing the minimum size of the Constitutional Committee. Mitigating the risk of governance inoperability due to temporary unavailability or resignation of members is a reasonable objective, and I acknowledge that the proposal complies with the relevant guardrails from a technical and formal perspective.\r\n\r\nHowever, I do not view this as merely a numerical adjustment. In my view, it represents a meaningful shift in governance design.\r\n\r\nI do not currently perceive the Constitutional Committee to be in a state of critical dysfunction. At the same time, I believe the overall governance structure is still evolving. In particular, I observe concentration dynamics within DRep voting power. In such an environment, lowering the minimum size from seven to five may increase the relative influence of individual members and, over time, heighten the risk of centralization. This is a concern for me from a structural governance perspective.\r\n\r\nWhile operational continuity is important, I believe it should not be achieved by reducing decentralization safeguards. If strengthening functionality is necessary, I would prefer exploring options that expand committee capacity while maintaining a strong minimum threshold, rather than lowering the minimum requirement.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I cannot support this proposal.\r\n\r\n僕は、本提案の趣旨である「運用上の可用性向上」という目的自体は理解しています。委員の一時的な不在や辞任によってConstitutional Committeeが機能停止に陥るリスクを軽減したいという考えは合理的であり、技術的・形式的にもGuardrail要件を満たしていることは確認しています。\r\n\r\nしかし、僕はこの変更を単なる数値調整とは捉えていません。制度設計の方向性に関わる重要な変更だと考えています。\r\n\r\n現時点でConstitutional Committeeが重大な機能不全に陥っているとは認識していません。一方で、ガバナンス構造全体は依然として発展途上にあり、特にDRep投票においては投票力の集中傾向が見られるというのが僕の認識です。そのような環境下で最小人数を7から5に引き下げることは、将来的に相対的な影響力が強まりやすくなり、中央集権化リスクを高める可能性があると僕は懸念しています。\r\n\r\n僕は、可用性の向上は重要である一方で、それが分散性の安全余白を縮小する形で実現されるべきではないと考えています。もし機能強化を図るのであれば、最小人数を下げる方向ではなく、奇数を維持しつつ委員数を拡張するなど、分散性を強める設計の方がより健全だと考えます。\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、僕は本提案には賛成できません。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcKPCEf5MyLR7KW9ZPeBRwzV7Vdb8ku6f3HDh5CJB3oZW -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCurrent CC selection process is not ideal, done offchain with limited DReps participation, so quality of CC members are not yet certified, hence reducing CC size now is not preferred. Constitutional changes should be slow and steady, and should not be optimized for efficiency and may cause mistakes",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWND2w3GtkETfkrvX3mVmKCTS7Ud1greTAxf6MWcaAsjg -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support maintaining the current minimum of 7 Constitutional Committee members. Reducing this number to five, is both risky and unnecessary.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "wolf31o2 (Chris Gianelloni)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWWoZFHhEcWRsffFzVTLGzbqRPzta6xgMkorNAtM1XSmX -->\r\n# wolf31o2 (Chris Gianelloni)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfa8r8r36x7x05htftce7qhafrn5nzzr6vazy95pzy6y5dqac0ss7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIncrease the number of CC members instead of reducing the minimum size. Replace seats who aren't active and blocking governance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeRwgBX8yiWmEWP3Sziv9Pp8i2cYSxeMgoSMUTQvuKXhC -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote YES on [Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5].\r\n\r\nCurrent Risk\u2028\r\nAt present, the actual number of Constitutional Committee (CC) members is equal to the minimum required size. In this situation, if even one CC member resigns, the committee would fall below the minimum threshold and become non-functional. This would prevent not only ordinary governance actions but also critical actions such as urgent security updates. This represents a serious structural risk that must be addressed urgently.\r\n\r\nAvailable Options\u2028\r\nIn principle, there are only two ways to mitigate this risk (or a combination of both):\u2028(1) Increase the actual number of CC members\u2028(2) Reduce the minimum CC size\r\nI support option (2) reducing the minimum CC size.\r\n\r\n1. Addressing Concerns About Reducing the Minimum CC Size\u2028\r\nI acknowledge concerns that lowering the minimum CC size could lead to future concentration of power. However, this change affects only the minimum threshold. As long as the actual CC size remains at seven members, there is no change from the current situation. Even if the number temporarily drops to six or five, an election can be held to restore the CC to seven members. In addition, as stated in the metadata, the original rationale for setting the minimum CC size to seven no longer applies under current conditions. Therefore, the argument that lowering the minimum CC size would immediately lead to centralization is an oversimplification.\r\n\r\n2. Why Increasing the Actual CC Size Is Not Supported\u2028Increasing the actual CC size requires a highly costly and complex process. In practice, a previous attempt to increase the CC from seven to eight members failed to obtain DRep support, and some DReps called for even more costly procedures. In most cases, an election would be required, and consensus would first need to be reached on whether such costs are justified. This issue is not something that can be addressed “eventually”; it is an urgent risk. However, in reality, there are no individuals or entities willing to commit the necessary resources to actively pursue an increase in the actual CC size.\r\n\r\n3. Alignment With CC Compensation (TENET 4)\u2028Increasing the actual CC size would further complicate the implementation of TENET 4 regarding CC compensation. Last year, a CC member resigned and the CC fell below the minimum size because DReps did not approve compensation even for five CC members. In simple terms, many DReps judged compensation for five CC members to be too high. Given this voting behavior, it is likely to be even more difficult to support compensation for eight or more CC members, making this approach politically and practically unviable.\r\n\r\nConclusion\u2028The current situation allows a single resignation to potentially halt the entire governance process. Increasing the actual CC size is not a realistic or timely solution. From the perspective of immediacy, feasibility, and risk mitigation, reducing the minimum CC size is the most practical option. For these reasons, I will vote YES on [Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5].\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5] に YES を投票します。\r\n現在のリスク認識\u2028現在、実際の憲法委員会（CC）人数が最小CC人数と一致しています。この状態では、CCメンバーが1人でも退任すると最小CC数を下回り、CCが機能不全に陥ります。その結果、通常のガバナンス行為だけでなく、セキュリティ上の緊急アップデート等も実行できなくなる可能性があり、これは早急に対処すべき深刻な構造的リスクです。\r\n\r\n解決手段の選択肢\u2028このリスクを解消する方法は、原理的に次の2つ（またはその組み合わせ）しかありません。\u2028(1) 実際CC人数を増やす\u2028(2) 最小CC人数を減らす\r\n私は、このうち (2) 最小CC人数の減少 を支持します。\r\n\r\n1. 最小CC人数減少に対する懸念への整理\u2028最小CC人数の減少が、将来的な権力集中につながる可能性があるという懸念は理解します。ただし、これはあくまで「最小値」の変更に過ぎません。実際のCC人数が7名のままであれば、現状と何も変わりません。仮に6名または5名まで減少した場合でも、選挙を実施することで7名へ回復させることは可能です。また、メタデータに記載されている通り、当初「最小CC数＝7」とした理由は、現在の状況には当てはまりません。したがって、「最小CC数を下げる＝直ちに権力集中」という主張は、過度に単純化された議論だと考えます。\r\n\r\n2. 実際CC人数の増加を支持しない理由\u2028実際CC人数の増加は、非常に高コストかつ複雑なプロセスを伴います。実際に、7名から8名への増加は一度DRepの支持を得られず失敗しており、その際には、より高コストな手続きを求める意見もありました。多くの場合、選挙の実施が必要となり、そのコストを正当化するための合意形成自体が困難です。本件は「できれば改善したい」話ではなく、今すぐ対処すべきリスクですが、現実として、実際CC人数の増加に積極的にリソースを投下しようとする個人やエンティティは存在していません。\r\n\r\n3. CC報酬（TENET 4）との整合性\u2028実際CC人数の増加は、TENET 4 に基づくCC報酬設計の実現をさらに困難にします。昨年、CCが1名退任し最小CC数を下回った背景には、5名分のCC報酬に対してDRepの賛同が得られなかったという事実があります。多くのDRepは、5名分の報酬ですら「高すぎる」と判断しました。この投票傾向を踏まえると、実際CC人数を8名以上に増やし、それに見合う報酬を支えることは、政治的・実務的に成立しにくいと考えられます。\r\n\r\n結論\u2028現状は、CCメンバー1人の退任によってガバナンス全体が停止し得る危険な状態です。実際CC人数の増加は現実的な選択肢とは言い難く、即効性と実行可能性を考慮すると、最小CC人数の減少が最も現実的なリスク対処策です。以上の理由から、[Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5] に YES を投票します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "π Lanningham",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://www.314pool.com/votes/dfdac5921ab657241fce58583d61bef59a369e01d2ba78191d6df6632a07fdfd00.jsonld -->\r\n# π Lanningham\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reduce minimum Constitutional Committee size (committeeMinSize) from 7 to 5\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2sld9e4nmasqfpusd5e67rwczj4l20d3653jgs38r4mams52y4jx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on governance action dfdac5921ab657241fce58583d61bef59a369e01d2ba78191d6df6632a07fdfd, which adjusts the minimum constitutional committee size. I agree with the direction of this change, but it was prepared without consideration of the memory limit budget, which I voted yes for, and thus these two would conflict.\r\n\r\n You can find a larger writeup of my beliefs and values [here](https://314pool.com/posts/constitution-vote-1).",
      "vote": "NO"
    }
  ],
