    {
      "voter": "Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Agora-Cardano/dRep_metadata_storage/refs/heads/main/Governance_Actions/CBCE_7.5M_CB.jsonld -->\r\n# Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9dq806jcm56wzhnv2yrf6gcyq7h4gap8gxewfykk0dtfs7vf843`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI do not support this governance action due to critical gaps in constitutional compliance and governance execution.\r\n\r\n1. Violation of Article IV.2 of the Cardano Constitution:\r\nThis budget Info Action fails to define any process for administering the ₳7.5M requested. No administrator, smart contract, multisig mechanism, or execution framework is mentioned — nor even an intention to define one. This directly violates the requirement that every budget must include a process for administering funds.\r\n\r\n2. No coordination across overlapping bundles:\r\nSeveral proposals in this action are also present in the 39-proposal Intersect info action bundle. Without any coordination or clarity on how overlapping proposals will be handled, there is a risk of duplicated withdrawals or conflicting execution paths.\r\n\r\n3. Retroactive application of threshold:\r\nThe 2.69B ADA voting threshold used to filter which proposals were included was not communicated clearly to dReps during the Ekklesia voting phase. Applying it retroactively undermines the legitimacy of the signaling process and introduces procedural unfairness.\r\n\r\n4. Weak quality of signaling:\r\nMany dReps either abstained or voted No without reviewing individual proposals. This resulted in high-visibility proposals dominating the outcome, while lesser-known contributors were excluded — not necessarily due to lack of merit, but lack of attention.\r\n\r\n5. All-or-nothing structure suppresses representation:\r\nThis budget is bundled. dReps are forced to accept or reject all included proposals, with no ability to make granular decisions. This limits representative governance and incentivizes strategic voting rather than thoughtful review.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nWhile I support funding high-quality community-led proposals, this action does not meet the required standards for constitutional compliance, coordination, or transparent execution. I vote NO until these gaps are addressed.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZvVjW8wHLV8CBJqu6CoA4BQCYiHozpCzYQuJLZFBgoqQ -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私は本提案を棄権します。本提案に含まれる内容は評価しておりますが、内容が類似した別の提案との関係性も踏まえ、今回はあえて棄権する判断をいたしました。今後の議論や予算編成において、こうした重複や整合性の扱いがより明確になることを期待しています。\\n\\nI abstain from voting on this proposal. While I appreciate the content included, I have chosen to abstain in consideration of its relationship to another similar proposal. I hope that future discussions and budgeting processes will offer greater clarity on how to handle such overlaps and maintain consistency.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/DRepdata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context20250515BudgetForComBuil.jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私はこの提案にYES票を投じます。\r\n本提案は、草の根レベルで活動するCardanoコミュニティビルダーによるプロポーザルを、明確な支持基準（2.69B ADA以上の賛同）に基づいて厳選し、小規模かつ高インパクトな7件の提案に対して7.5M ADAを配分するものです。\r\n　このアプローチは以下の観点から極めて評価できます：\r\n分散性の実現：大きな企業やCardanoを作った組織ではない、ふつうの参加者の声が、きちんと予算の支援を受けて実現に向かっている点。\r\n投票正当性の担保：すべての提案が、アクティブステークに基づいた過半数支持を明示的に得ており、Cardano憲法に準拠していること。\r\n持続可能な財政運営：7.5M ADAという極めて控えめな金額により、財政負担が最小限に抑えられていること。\r\n　この提案は、CardanoのVoltaireフェーズにおける新しい市民主体ガバナンスの象徴としても機能するものです。私はこの方向性を強く支持します。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI cast a YES vote on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis proposal allocates 7.5 million ADA to seven carefully selected proposals submitted by grassroots Cardano community builders. Each proposal met a clear support threshold—more than 2.69 billion ADA in voting stake—and represents small-scale but high-impact initiatives.\r\n\r\nThis approach is highly commendable for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nDecentralization in action: It ensures that the voices of everyday participants—not large corporations or founding entities—can move forward with proper financial support.\r\n\r\nLegitimacy of the vote: All proposals explicitly secured majority support based on active stake and are in full compliance with the Cardano Constitution.\r\n\r\nFinancial sustainability: The total allocation of 7.5 million ADA is a very modest amount, keeping the financial burden on the Treasury to a minimum.\r\n\r\nThis proposal also serves as a symbol of the new citizen-led governance envisioned in Cardano's Voltaire phase. I strongly support this direction.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
