    {
      "voter": "Captain Crypto",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webnettricks/CaptainCrypto/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(1).jsonld -->\r\n# Captain Crypto\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2x0d3jgae3xs7kdagq2w74kmzlgktw3l5th2lusrgn7m6gg52x78`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHere’s my summary of what I’m voting for, based on the Cardano 2025 Budget Info Action, written as if I’m reviewing it myself and choosing to vote YES:\r\n\r\nI’m voting on a Cardano 2025 budget that allocates 7,568,810 ada to fund seven community-driven projects. This budget is part of a community-led, constitutionally guided process to spend Cardano’s treasury within a 350 million ada Net Change Limit, aiming to drive growth and hit the 2025 roadmap goals. After reviewing it, I’m voting YES because I believe these projects, backed by strong community support, will push Cardano forward.\r\n\r\nWhat’s in the Budget?\r\nThe budget funds these seven projects, each with over 2.69 billion ada in Ekklesia’s off-chain polling (50% + 1 Lovelace of the 5.38B active voting stake):\r\n\r\nMidgard - Optimistic Rollups (2.16M ada, 3.58B ada votes): Scales Cardano with rollup tech.\r\nStarstream: Next Gen VM (2M ada, 3.47B ada votes): A new virtual machine for better apps.\r\nBlockfrost Platform (1.3M ada, 3.19B ada votes): Tools to help developers build on Cardano.\r\nzkFold ZK Rollup (1.16M ada, 3.20B ada votes): Zero-knowledge rollups for faster, private transactions.\r\nHardware Wallets Maintenance (424,800 ada, 3.43B ada votes): Keeps wallets secure and updated.\r\nLedger App Rewrite (300,000 ada, 2.83B ada votes): Upgrades Cardano’s Ledger support.\r\nDolos: Lightweight Data Node (220,914 ada, 2.70B ada votes): Maintains a lean node for the network.\r\nTotal: 7,568,810 ada (~$4.16M at ~$0.55/ada). These are community projects, not from founding entities like Intersect, IOG, Cardano Foundation, or Emurgo, which must submit their own proposals separately.\r\n\r\nWhy I’m Voting YES\r\nThis budget is Cardano’s chance to live up to its Voltaire vision—decentralized, community-driven governance. With 3.92 billion ada cast in Ekklesia (72% of active voting power), the community showed up in force. Each project cleared a tough 2.69B ada threshold, proving they’ve got broad support. That gives me confidence I’m backing what the ecosystem wants.\r\n\r\nThe projects themselves hit key areas for 2025: scalability (rollups, VMs), developer support (Blockfrost, Dolos), and security (wallets, Ledger). These are the kinds of investments that can help Cardano compete with bigger chains and grow adoption. The budget’s small size (~2% of the 350M ada cap) means it’s not overreaching, and the Net Change Limit keeps spending in check.\r\n\r\nI also like how this budget fixes past governance hiccups. It only includes proposals that hit the proper 50% + 1 Lovelace threshold (2.69B ada of active stake), avoiding the risk of weak projects sneaking through on low turnout. Kicking out founding entities’ proposals ensures fairness—everyone plays by the same rules. Plus, Intersect’s role as administrator, with standardized submissions and public Ekklesia data, adds transparency, and the Constitutional Committee’s oversight (needing 5/7 votes) keeps it legit.\r\n\r\nMy Lingering Thoughts\r\nI’m not 100% worry-free. Some X posts mentioned Ekklesia’s clunky interface—DReps had trouble with online wallet requirements, which might’ve limited who voted. That’s a bummer, but 72% participation is still solid. I’m also curious why this budget is so focused and small compared to the 275M ada one I saw earlier. It’s not a dealbreaker, but I’ll want to see how it fits into the bigger picture.\r\n\r\nThere’s also a tiny market risk—7.5M ada is only ~0.03% of the 22.7B circulating supply, but I’m counting on Intersect to space out withdrawals to avoid price dips. And while Intersect’s running the show as administrator, the fact that they’re not funding their own projects here makes me feel better about their neutrality.\r\n\r\nMy Vote\r\nI’m voting YES on this Budget Info Action. These seven projects, backed by strong Ekklesia votes, are a smart bet to boost Cardano’s scalability, developer ecosystem, and security. The process feels fair, transparent, and aligned with the Constitution, and I’m excited to support community builders who might not have the 100k ada deposit to go it alone. This is a step toward the decentralized, thriving Cardano I want to see in 2025.\r\n\r\nI’ll stay active, though—watching Intersect’s fund management, checking the community dashboard for updates, and voting on treasury withdrawals to ensure every ada is well spent. If this passes, these projects could give Cardano a real edge, and I’m happy to help make that happen.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmW4PmBc9BtcCHWSBexvwLrazv6UE9ux2HPCFHzduK3KHT -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmdUrFByXZ246fHtZB3F71aCzKzdgpknybGguDvtUK7mEt\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation supports the principle of empowering community builders and recognizes that many of the individual projects within this bundled submission could hold considerable merit for the ecosystem. However, for the allocation of Treasury funds, proposals must adhere to high standards of administrative clarity, oversight, and operational soundness to ensure accountability and responsible stewardship, in line with the principles outlined in the Cardano Constitution and our own \"Our Cardano\".\r\n\r\nOur decision to vote 'NO' on this specific budget proposal is based on the following key considerations:\r\n\r\n- **Administrator Designation and Project Consent:** The proposal's plan for Intersect to administer all bundled funds encounters a significant operational challenge. It has been indicated by the proposers of Starstream (one of the key projects named in this bundle) in their own budget proposal submission on GovTool, that they do not consent to Intersect administering their budget. For a bundled budget to be viable, in our view, the consent of all co-proposers to the administrative framework is required. A budget proposer cannot unilaterally assign an administrator to sub-projects without their explicit agreement.\r\n\r\n- **Insufficient Clarity in Administrative Framework and Audit Provisions:** The proposal, in its current form, does not provide sufficiently detailed administrative guidelines for the management and disbursement of the 7.5 million ada across the seven diverse projects. Furthermore, the absence of explicit provisions for independent audits is a critical omission.\r\n\r\n- **Clarity on Execution and Coordination:** Further clarification is required regarding the proposal's execution plan, the specific mandate of the proposer in bundling these initiatives, and its coordination with broader, established budget processes. \r\n\r\nWhile the Foundation values initiatives that aim to support community projects and potentially offer more granular budget reviews, the current proposal does not yet meet the necessary standards for administrative and operational robustness. Our 'NO' vote pertains to the structure and execution of this specific bundled governance action, rather than a negative assessment of the individual merits of the underlying community projects.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSc2GYcqtBtQny9EAyuFSo7tXCdK4ktoiD6pjGYgV7pZg -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI endorsed all 7 of these in the flawed intersect budgeting process and will do so here again. Items like Midgard and Starstream are what I consider some of the highest potential first governance era ex-IO technical advancements of Cardano, in similar spirit to Aiken etc. Note that if all funds I have thus far approved on-chain are withdrawn, total spend on my account will be 9m ADA. I am working towards a personal budget of max 150m ADA on a rolling 1y basis.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Satuchac/DRep/refs/heads/main/009_My%20Rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES for the Ecosystem Budget for Community Builders.\r\n\r\nRationale:\r\n\r\nA total of 7,568,810 ADA is needed to fund seven community builder projects that have surpassed the 2.69B ADA threshold, which represents 50% + 1 Lovelace of the active registered voting stake.\r\n\r\nIn GovTool and Ekklesia, I supported six out of the seven projects—but all seven are expected to have a positive impact on the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nFrom Ekklesia’s voting results, it’s clear that DReps overwhelmingly support these projects, and that should be acknowledged.\r\n\r\nThree of the seven projects—Midgard, Starstream, and ZK Rollup—specifically address scalability, which is the most pressing need for the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nGiven this context, voting YES was the only logical choice.\r\n\r\nFounding Entity Proposals:\r\n\r\nProposals from founding entities that also met the threshold were intentionally excluded from this governance action. Instead, they are invited to submit their own governance actions for budget requests.\r\n\r\nI fully support this decision, as it aligns with the ongoing community debate about the Net Change Limit (NCL).\r\n\r\nThe current NCL is set at 350M ADA, but a reduction is expected. Two governance actions have been submitted to adjust the NCL to 200M or 300M ADA.\r\n\r\nTo minimize spending, it’s best to decide on-chain for each proposal individually, rather than bundling multiple proposals into a single governance action.\r\n\r\nThis approach prevents situations where DReps who support IOG’s budget feel obligated to also back community proposals they disagree with.\r\n\r\nGiven the circumstances, Intersect has made the right decision, and I appreciate their approach.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/Info_11.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this budget because every included proposal surpassed the 50% + 1 lovelace quorum and is on track to clear the 67% withdrawal threshold, demonstrating unmistakable grassroots backing. The package also excludes low-support or founding-entity items, avoiding the temptation to bundle weaker proposals together with popular ones merely to secure passage. Although I generally prefer pure line-item votes, this focused grouping of only high-support initiatives is a reasonable compromise that preserves transparency, respects constitutional thresholds.  I believe it is a sound, community-aligned allocation of treasury funds.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/Vote_Rationale_05222025_communitybuilders.jsonld -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI could be more supportive of this proposal if we saw a more consistent method for how the off-chain voting was going to translate into smaller proposals like this.  I've voted yes to most of the projects included here, not all. That said, I would rather support a somewhat larger group proposal maybe categorized to areas of the roadmap - or something other than what's happening here.  If the governance process shifts to be more in line with something like this I could be more in favor once all those proposals are understood in how they would be submitted. For now, I will vote abstain, being more in favor of an all encompassing budget proposal with a more granular and broken out treasury withdrawal process.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmd9PZFYm655L2yV4EkYYGFDFvLXQ1dCqt9TxFbSNc1Kx8 -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI strongly support several key proposals in this Info Action, particularly Midgard, Starstream, Dolos, and certain others included. These initiatives reflect community priorities and the kind of innovation Cardano governance should fund.\r\n\r\nHowever, I am voting NO against this bundled proposal. I believe each proposal should be voted on individually to allow for more precise and democratic decision-making. There was no clear consent from the named administrator, and at least one project, Starstream, publicly stated they did not currently agree to be included under Intersect’s administration.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPPbtNqbfcVubBkWqVSsZNzaiPyovqdKUze81YYcT9cc9 -->\r\n# drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\ndont like that they are bulked, and not at all that it doesnt talk about how money is distributed, managed, etc. , but I already voted yes for those on Ekklesia.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dumpling🥟",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmY9YXj6wGuuQAZ8E4fKbmAVE1QTTSMtCiK4qUUPU36vYd -->\r\n# Dumpling🥟\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rtf58m0lv9spcqx5mads20gpfulf6l97w57ecdy00vjdq0klh4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n支持社区开发者，为Cardano未来打造更多有潜力的项目，不依赖现有开发者团体，也可以降低风险。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/7.5M.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEMURGO upholds the importance of transparent, constitutionally grounded treasury processes that support sustainable growth for community-driven initiatives. While we strongly support grassroots contributions and have voted in favor of most within this governance action, not all included proposals align with our criteria for support.\r\n\r\nIn particular, we note that all of the initiatives listed are already being considered for funding under the Intersect MBO 2025 framework. Proceeding with an overlapping Info Action introduces the risk of duplicated funding efforts and compromises the clarity and accountability we strive for in treasury allocation.\r\n\r\nTo maintain consistency, prevent redundancy, and reinforce the integrity of Cardano’s budgetary systems, EMURGO has chosen to vote ‘No’ on this governance action. We continue to encourage all proposals to follow the established, transparent channels to ensure long-term fiscal responsibility and alignment with the community’s governance model.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmdrbkqniv2jSRnQ52bweTRsmZtyM5R1be8BKzaAPJd4ap -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting yes based on the spirit of the proposal - this segment of the GA covers a key issue of the Intersect budget proposal that has been deliberately glossed over:\r\n\r\nA key issue in the initial budget process was the misapplication of the participation threshold. The 50% + 1 Lovelace threshold was calculated based on total ada participating in the vote, rather than the active voting stake—which significantly alters the democratic weight of participating DReps. This discrepancy risks enabling governance distortion through low-turnout manipulation, akin to gerrymandering.\r\n\r\nTo safeguard against such vulnerabilities and uphold the integrity of Cardano’s governance process, this Info Action includes only those proposals submitted by community builders (that might not have 100k ADA deposit) and met the corrected threshold of 2.69B ada, equivalent to 50% + 1 Lovelace of the active registered voting stake. This ensures that community-driven proposals with broad support are prioritized.\r\n\r\nThere is obvious overlap with Intersect, and a fund manager has not been chosen, but this is easily remedied. I would expect that this GA would take precedent over the Intersect budget, and a fund manager would be chosen prior to any distribution of ADA.\r\n\r\nPreserving the integrity of our voting process is essential, and Intersect has deliberately sidestepped this, which needs to be remedied.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb4wJ491emG7ctKzCUNb2awwFmoFh67NvpR5YSLUBjK8F -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES because:\r\n\r\n1) All proposals in this budget surpassed the 2.69B ADA threshold on Ekklesia, reflecting broad consensus among DReps and the Community.\r\n\r\n2) Midgard, Starstream, and zkFold directly address scalability — Cardano’s top priority. The other projects strengthen infrastructure and developer tools.\r\n\r\n3) The total budget of 7.5M ₳ is within the 2025 spending cap (350M ₳) and complies with governance procedures.\r\n\r\n*Future treasury withdrawals should still be assessed individually per proposal, with clear milestones and verifiable deliverables.\r\n\r\n-------------------------------------------------\r\nJapanese Translation\r\n-------------------------------------------------\r\n私は賛成票（YES）を投じます。理由は以下の通りです：\r\n\r\n1) この予算に含まれるすべての提案は、Ekklesia上で2.69B ADAの閾値を超えており、コミュニティの広範な合意を示しています。\r\n\r\n2) Midgard、Starstream、zkFoldは、カルダノにとって最優先課題であるスケーラビリティに直接対応しています。他のプロジェクトもインフラや開発ツールの強化に貢献しています。\r\n\r\n3) 総予算7.5M ₳は、2025年の支出上限（350M ₳）内であり、ガバナンス手続きにも準拠しています。\r\n\r\n※将来的な財務引き出しについては、各提案ごとにマイルストーンと検証可能な成果に基づいて個別に評価されるべきです。\r\n\r\n-------------------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese Translation\r\n-------------------------------------------------\r\nTôi bỏ phiếu YES vì:\r\n\r\n1) Tất cả các đề xuất trong ngân sách này đều vượt ngưỡng 2.69B ADA trên Ekklesia, thể hiện sự đồng thuận rộng rãi từ các DRep trong giai đoạn tham vấn ý kiến cộng đồng.\r\n\r\n2) Midgard, Starstream và zkFold giải quyết trực tiếp bài toán mở rộng – ưu tiên hàng đầu của Cardano. Các dự án còn lại củng cố hạ tầng và công cụ phát triển.\r\n\r\n3) Tổng ngân sách 7.5M ₳ nằm trong giới hạn chi tiêu năm 2025 (350M ₳) và tuân thủ quy trình quản trị.\r\n\r\n* Việc rút ADA từ kho bạc sau này vẫn cần được đánh giá riêng theo từng proposal, gắn với các mốc và kiểm chứng cụ thể.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmSvX8wyjjPpoaPpKhFggdyhHAVx4Yrq76suPiY6aucQsS -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting No on the 'community builder' budget because I don't want part of the included projects – Midgard, Starstream, zkFold – to be funded. I don't think that they are worth our ADA and greenlighting that budget that combines a lot of different proposals could (and I fear will) be seen as a precedence that they then also have the 'right' to get those ADA in later treasury withdrawals. Large omnibus budgets were a phenomenally bad idea and the 'budget committee' was not open to change paths at all.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU9eNGdxWekPKKa1YbREq4DrFGWUmoe8GL2TwMQHtpxEZ -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe proposal lacks to prove how the funds will be managed in transparent manner. This proposal would be considered as unconstitutional.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTXTAiopXsxYXJdAxLYTaJRPyh3xctsHUtwm3Y7JX6y1N -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe seven proposals bundled together in this motion have all received very high approval ratings from DReps in the off-chain temperature check process that took place over the Ekklesia tool developed for Intersect MBO a few days ago. \r\n\r\nDuring the Ekklesia voting stage I voted YES for all 7 proposals that are now bundled and as all 7 have received a lot of YES votes compared to the total participating DRep poewr in Ekklesia (I checked and saw that one of the top voted on proposals (2025 Input Output Engineering Core Development Proposal) was voted on by a participating stake of Total voting power: 4,009,632,409 ADA \r\n\r\nThe proposals listed in this budget action have received YES votes from at least 2,695,223,782 ADA that took part in Ekklesia voting. This indicates a support of more than half of the DRep voting power. \r\n\r\nYes, governance is still performing baby steps, however, support for these proposals has been clear and there is no evident need to slow them down by requiring a mandatory bundling of these 7 into a larger budgetary package now that the action has been proposed. \r\n\r\nAs regards the constitutionality of this proposal, the true measure of its constitutionality will be given by the Constitutional Committee. As a DRep, my impression is that this proposal does not have glaring omissions that would require us to stall the DRep process. The CC will address the constitutionality in its own right.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_7.5M_Community_Builders -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting no on the 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders.  This proposal is submitted by a third party without providing evidence of formal agreements with all the parties named to undertake the proposed commitments.  It therefore does not satisfy the requirement for a specified administration partner.  I also find this proposal flawed in that, it lacks transparency and I have concerns about how accurately the proposal reflects the intentions of the named contributors. Therefore I don't have confidence in the proposal’s ability to deliver on its goals effectively and responsibly.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/08JUN2025-mepzl/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote No on the proposed “2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders” Info Action (Governance Action ID: Gov_action1mmalzkcxpyn33t05hml2hxpwq0ffv6uu4mhe8sv7guz5nmm4afysqlmepzl). As a threshold matter, this Budget Info Action fails to “specify a process for overseeing use of funds from Cardano Blockchain treasury withdrawals including designating one or more administrators who shall be responsible for such oversight” as required under Article IV, Section 2 of the Cardano Constitution.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kronoshus/KevinMohr/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20555.jsonld -->\r\n# Kevin G Mohr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI want the 100k ADA requirment removed. We don't need some external system like this to do that.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/ytc36jus -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO because this request duplicates projects that are already scheduled to receive funding in the main 2025 Intersect budget, yet appoints Intersect as fund administrator without explicit consent from every team and without a shared framework for milestones, reporting, or claw-backs; approving it now would create overlapping custody arrangements, invite double payments, and add unnecessary complexity to a governance process that is already spread across GovTool, Ekklesia, and on-chain actions. I will support these same initiatives once they are presented through a single, coherent budget or as individual InfoActions with clear terms, but until then the prudent choice is to preserve treasury clarity and vote NO.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/11/7.5M_community_builders.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Rationale for Voting ABSTAIN on 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n\r\nI have decided to vote **ABSTAIN** on this Info Action.\r\n\r\nWhile I support funding the individual proposals included in this Budget Info Action, I believe the way this Governance Action is structured is unconstitutional. Each budget proposal must have a named administrator responsible for managing disbursement, oversight, and reporting of funds. This is a key requirement of the Cardano Constitution.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, these proposals are already part of the 275M ADA budget Info Action, which is submitted and administered by Intersect. If both Info Actions are approved, it could create confusion and overlap in fund management.\r\n\r\nI also understand the motivation behind submitting this budget Info Action - ensuring that only proposals with clear majority support (over 50% + 1 Lovelace of the 5.38B active voting stake) are included. However, I do not fully agree with the claim that the 275M Budget Info Action contains proposals lacking majority consensus. It is the responsibility of DReps to participate in Cardano governance and for delegators to choose their representatives. If some DReps did not vote on Ekklesia, I consider their non-participation as a form of abstention. Therefore, the 3.92B ADA voting participation in Ekklesia should be regarded as the effective active voting stake for this process.\r\n\r\n**For these reasons (support of proposals, but unconstitutionality and duplication of the Info Action), I have chosen ABSTAIN.**",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/7-5mill%20budget%20for%20builders.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nKrypto Labs acknowledges the vital importance of transparent, constitutionally aligned treasury allocation for community builders. While we support the spirit of empowering grassroots initiatives, we will be voting 'No' on this Info Action. Our decision stems from the understanding that the projects listed within this proposal are already slated to receive funding through the established IntersectMBO 2025 budget process. Approving this separate action would create redundancy and potential for double-funding, undermining the integrity of our budgetary framework. We advocate for a singular, clear funding path to ensure fiscal responsibility",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kyle Solomon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adosiawolf/drep-rationale/refs/heads/main/0004 -->\r\n# Kyle Solomon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzshxuma6cwrnlv2ucyclfqw3k4nu4nuudmh2z87j9hncsk9dhy4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted NO on the current proposal.\r\n\r\nThe proposal author is unaffiliated with any of the projects initiatives being proposed and has not submitted this proposal on behalf of the stated budget administrator.\r\n\r\nI find introducing this degree of bureaucracy unwelcome and both detrimental and disrespectful to governance process.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LallyMcClay",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmd6AjBXRk3VAKkWPvJmctvvWnRWZaYuhfr8fJj2qFVVre -->\r\n# LallyMcClay\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2dptycrks2ggae95leeh66m0l0svet98c44hl4rmaec7as6hgpp3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote no on the proposal requesting 7.5 million ADA for Community Builders initiative. While I strongly support efforts to grow and strengthen Cardano’s community, I find this particular proposal flawed on several critical fronts.\r\n\r\nFirst, it lacks transparency and professionalism. It references a number of projects including at least one that has not requested to be administered by Intersect yet here  citing Intersect as administrator.  I do not see evidence of coordination or consent from those initiatives. This raises concerns about how accurately the proposal reflects the intentions and needs of the named contributors.\r\n\r\nSecond, the grouping of disparate initiatives into a single budget request without clear governance, delivery mechanisms, or accountability structures diminishes confidence in the proposal’s ability to deliver on its goals effectively and responsibly.\r\n\r\nIn its current form, I do not believe this is a credible or well-structured funding request. I encourage future proposals in this space to prioritize consultation, coordination, and clarity in their design, our community deserves nothing less.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Latam Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LatamCardanoDRep/DREP/refs/heads/main/Vote%205-6-25.jsonld -->\r\n# Latam Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytgsdkfznvjnwdxrzvf8x6tn4ctfukqqphsammzkfwatgsqgnpf2w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are voting ABSTAIN because we already voted yes to Intersect's budget proposal which includes all the proposals in this one (plus others)\r\nWe do not think it is convenient to approve two budgets with some of the same proposals.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0012 -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDRep Voting Rationale — Vote: No\r\n\r\nThis proposal reflects a strong commitment to expanding access to treasury funds for community builders, a goal that is central to Cardano’s decentralized future. It respects constitutional safeguards by applying the 2.69B ADA participation threshold and excludes founding entity proposals.\r\n\r\nHowever, I am voting No based on a key governance concern: the risk of duplication with the Intersect budget. Given that Intersect has been closely involved in assembling their own budget proposal which is currently live up for voting on chain and close to being ratified. My concern with approving this proposal is getting a proposal funded twice. Of course, for that to happen it would need a withdrawal action too.\r\n\r\nAdditional Perspective on Treasury Withdrawal Structure\r\n\r\n- As a DRep, I also wish to express my broader view on the upcoming Treasury Withdrawals structure:\r\n\r\n- I am strongly in favor of greater granularity in funding decisions to allow more nuanced and accountable governance.\r\n\r\n- Although I value pragmatism in governance operations, I am most comfortable with Option D (five brackets from Ekklesia), which strikes a strong balance between decentralization and operational feasibility for Intersect. It might be argued that this discredits Intersect's budget process, but I prefer to be on the safe side and get additional results, especially this being Cardano's 1st budget.\r\n\r\n- I would also be willing to review 39 individual proposals (Option E) if necessary, despite the heavier governance load, because it offers the maximum clarity. Option C (two support brackets split across 2025 and 2026) is acceptable to me too. Sticking to D, though.\r\n\r\nVOTE0012",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Marketing DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYQkhS7fiQCPAHJppkP3A4nhyh1zDKUdp6F9R1tcbsbfM -->\r\n# Marketing DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23kumvpqgal3t6v4tamwrprjya453p3djam0eqg63usm9su77hjl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDid we not just conclude a rather lengthy budget proposal process via Intersect that covers many of the initiatives outlined in this submission? Let's keep the governance proposal process as streamlined as possible. Submit proposals that clearly fill a gap in existing initiatives for Cardano. If the approved budget for 2025 doesn't create the outcomes the proposer would like to see, they are encouraged to resubmit for next year's budget.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Maureen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQ2SAZh4UqbmJGKA9SQRZjMpfVYFWuVX3icru9TX7mHY5 -->\r\n# Maureen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y22hlaj8wuyygpnjy5cf96tg9tgvjrz39kxvqgv898uj9scfc55t7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal brilliantly solves the collective action problem plaguing early-stage governance systems. Rather than forcing each builder to navigate the byzantine process of individual on-chain submission (creating governance fatigue), this approach establishes a repeatable pattern for efficiently allocating resources to promising initiatives with proven community support.\r\nWhen future blockchain historians analyze Cardano's evolution, they'll point to this moment as when we transcended theoretical governance discussions and started building tangible infrastructure. The 7.5M ADA allocated here will likely generate 10x returns through ecosystem growth, user adoption, and technical advancement.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmbhS6k2Df731ykXmri6U8U9jgcmJo4LMf8KdkL62qBZts -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on the governance action \"2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\" (`gov_action1mmalzkcxpyn33t05hml2hxpwq0ffv6uu4mhe8sv7guz5nmm4afysqlmepzl`) due to a critical administrative flaw that makes it unworkable, as well as significant deficiencies in its overall structure.\r\n\r\nThe primary issue is that the budget's proposed administrative plan cannot be executed. The budget proposer has designated Intersect as the single administrator for all seven bundled proposals. However, one of the included proposers (Starstream) has explicitly and publicly stated, in their proposal submission on GovTools, that they do not consent to Intersect managing their funds.\r\n\r\nThis creates a dead end. Intersect's policy is to only administer funds for projects that provide explicit consent. Since a core component of this budget package withholds that consent, the entire administrative framework as proposed is invalid. A budget proposer cannot unilaterally assign an administrator to another party's project without their agreement.\r\n\r\nBeyond this flaw, the budget itself is severely lacking in quality from a governance perspective:\r\n\r\n1. No Administrative Guidelines: The proposal omits clear guidelines detailing how the 7.5M ₳ in treasury funds will be managed, disbursed, and overseen.\r\n\r\n2. Lack of Accountability: There is no mention of independent audits, which are essential for ensuring transparency and the responsible use of community funds.\r\n\r\nWhile some of the individual proposals within this bundle may be strong, they are contained within a budget that is procedurally flawed and administratively unworkable. Approving such a deficient proposal would be a disservice to the community and would set a poor precedent for treasury governance.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://nimuepool.io/metadata/context-20250524.jsonld -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMy votes for the currently active budget governance actions are as follows:\r\n- ✅ YES on the 275M Intersect Budget\r\n- ✅ YES on the Amaru Node Development Budget\r\n- ❌ NO on the 7.5M Community Builders Budget\r\n\r\nThe Intersect budget includes a broad set of proposals that are generally positive for the Cardano ecosystem. While I may have reservations about some individual proposals, approving the budget doesn't automatically release funds. I can re-evaluate specific items later when the associated treasury withdrawal actions are submitted on chain. I strongly recommend avoiding overly grouped treasury withdrawals, bundling too many proposals together can result in good initiatives being blocked due to a few contentious ones.\r\n\r\nAs for the Amaru Node Development Budget, if it had been included in the recent Ekklesia vote, it likely would have passed, and I would have supported it then as well. That's why I will support it now too. For better clarity, I recommend including the requested budget amount in the governance action title next time.\r\n\r\nI would've preferred to vote on the Community Builders Budget after seeing the outcome of the Intersect budget. If that last one were to fail, I might have considered supporting the community one, but since it was submitted beforehand, that option is off the table now. More importantly, this budget doesn't include the proposals from founding entities and there are no separate gov actions for those. It doesn't make sense to fund only this subset of proposals in isolation imho. So for now I can only assume the Intersect one will pass, which renders this budget unnecessary. Additionally, this budget appoints Intersect as the administrator, yet includes the Starstream proposal, which will not use Intersect as an administrator. For these reasons, I cannot support the Community Builders Budget at this time.\r\n\r\nI'm aware that some of my reasons for voting NO on the community budget could also apply, to some extent, to the Amaru budget. However, the Amaru budget doesn't overlap with another Budget.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "No stress",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmd3hnPSe2V9i1heWUfgD3dqD2Bj6FP6F7FgeQgWBgJfhK -->\r\n# No stress\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t3t35yx7j8nnh3wkqn2zzhgwqksksn85zv62pjrwzjawczwgyv7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYall are getting paid?",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action1mmal/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted Abstain on this proposal because, while I support the projects included, I don’t believe there’s a strong need to submit a separate Governance Action for proposals that were already included in the main Intersect-led budget.\r\n\r\nAt this early stage in Cardano’s on-chain governance journey, it's important to keep the process simple and clear. Having multiple Governance Actions for the same set of projects — even if they’re well-supported — adds unnecessary complexity and could confuse voters, without offering clear added value.\r\n\r\nA single coordinated budget process, with transparent inclusion criteria and community signalling (like what Intersect facilitated), is the better path for now. This helps build trust, avoids fragmentation, and gives the ecosystem a cleaner, more unified way to manage treasury allocations.\r\n\r\nPlease reduce my workload, don't increase it.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA017-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"Não\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action1mmalzkcxpyn33t05hml2hxpwq0ffv6uu4mhe8sv7guz5nmm4afysqlmepzl), pois não foram estabelecidas as métricas de controle de qualidade que o Intersect utilizaria para acompanhar a execução das propostas, bem como os condicionantes para liberação dos recursos solicitados.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"No\" on this governance action (gov_action1mmalzkcxpyn33t05hml2hxpwq0ffv6uu4mhe8sv7guz5nmm4afysqlmepzl) because the quality control metrics that Intersect would use to monitor the execution of the proposals were not established, nor were the conditions for the release of the requested funds.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWeeqboFzwSu2BLgXMVCURUaL1mWD36ThZe9FeTAg4M5P -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am choosing to **abstain **from voting on this proposal, not out of opposition to the individual initiatives it includes—many of which I support—but due to concerns around the structure, process and constitutional clarity of the proposal as a whole. While I recognise the community support for specific sub-proposals such as Midgard, zkFold, and Dolos, the decision to package them into a single Governance Action introduces governance ambiguity and limits my ability to vote accurately on each initiative’s merits. More concerning is the lack of explicit administrative confirmation from all included projects, such as Starstream, which raises legitimate constitutional questions—something reflected in the Cardano Foundation’s “No” vote and IOG’s assessment of unconstitutionality.\r\n\r\nMoreover, this proposal arises amidst overlapping budget Governance Actions, which, while well-intentioned, are contributing to confusion and procedural fatigue among DReps and the wider community. I appreciate the proposers’ attempt to correct earlier threshold misapplications in the budgeting process, but I am not convinced this bundling and resubmission fully addresses those concerns without introducing new ones.\r\n\r\nCasting a “Yes” would endorse a flawed procedural model; casting a “No” risks sending a signal of rejection to community-led initiatives that deserve support and funding. **Neither outcome reflects my position accurately**. Therefore, I am abstaining from this vote to signal the need for future budget proposals to be more procedurally sound, clearly administered and unbundled where possible, allowing for more precise and principled decision-making in line with Cardano’s constitutional standards.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RudianosDrep/RudianosDrep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%2010.jsonld -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have decided to vote in favor of this proposed budget. There is no limitation on the amount of budgets that can be approved and since this budget is simply looking to fund projects that have high community support and are already part of the intersect budget proposal there is no added cost to the ecosystem. I see this proposed budget mostly as a failsafe to approve high support proposals in the event that intersect fails to get an approved budget or bundles spending proposals in a way that the community does not support. In the event of that happening this is a good backup option.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTGw4S124fhQ4WgFxCCjk9yNiVkJiHY18LkKn5Ny6fW7U -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIDAN Lab votes No on 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget – 7.5M ₳ for Community Builders\r\n\r\n- **Bundling Risk and Coordination Complexity**\r\n    \r\n    While the total requested funding (7.5M ₳) is relatively small, bundling proposals into a single governance action introduces risk. As the number of projects grouped together increases, so does the complexity of coordinating delivery timelines, reporting standards, and fund oversight. This approach may set an undesirable examples for future governance actions.\r\n    \r\n- **Support for the Projects, But Reservations on Process**\r\n    \r\n    We recognize the significance of the included projects and the strong community support they’ve received during prior temperature checks.\r\n    \r\n- **Lack of Constitutional Compliance on Oversight**\r\n    \r\n    The proposal does not meet the oversight standards required by the **Cardano Constitution, Article IV, Section 2.** \r\n    \r\n    It fails to outline any type of administrator or process for how oversight would be carried out.\r\n    \r\n    Due to the unresolved constitutional and structural concerns, we are unable to vote yes on the proposal in its current form. We would welcome a revised submission that provides clearer oversight mechanisms and better aligns with governance expectations.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/info/20250517_05/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO votes ABSTAIN on the “2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget – 7.5M ₳ for community builders” proposal.\r\n\r\nSIPO fully recognizes the community-driven nature of this budget and supports the underlying principles of fairness, inclusion, and bottom-up governance. However, at this stage, SIPO believes that further clarification and safeguards are needed to ensure effective execution and to avoid unintentional overlap with the already-approved 275M ADA Intersect budget.\r\n\r\nIn particular, SIPO identifies the following concerns:\r\n\t•\tSome proposals appear in both budget packages, raising concerns over potential double allocation.\r\n\t•\tThe execution frameworks across the bundled proposals vary significantly and may lack the standardization of oversight and smart contract-based disbursement mechanisms established by Intersect.\r\n\t•\tThere is currently no unified process for selecting which version of a proposal should proceed to Treasury Withdrawal.\r\n\r\nTherefore, SIPO abstains not out of opposition, but as a call for procedural refinement. SIPO would strongly support a revised version of this budget that aligns with a unified execution framework or is integrated under Intersect’s smart contract governance model. SIPO believes this will strengthen transparency, prevent redundancy, and build a sustainable funding precedent for community-led innovation.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSDPYTmDz8yPpkXGT3zHeVcUFtspc72o7pUbz85xFw12S -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe abstain from voting on this proposal. While we understand the intent of the proposal, we believe careful consideration is needed at this time, taking into account its relationship with other budget proposals and overall alignment with the comprehensive funding plan. We will continue to monitor the development of these discussions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(4).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this ₳2.16M treasury withdrawal to fund Midgard – Optimistic Rollups, a novel Layer 2 framework uniquely built for Cardano’s UTxO architecture. This project delivers scalable, permissionless rollups without centralized sequencers, leveraging Cardano’s local state model to enable efficient fraud proofs and enhanced throughput. It inherits full L1 security, uses Ada as gas, and channels more on-chain activity and fees to the base layer.\r\n\r\nThis funding is part of the approved ₳275M ecosystem budget and follows constitutional processes, with milestone-based disbursement, third-party assurance, and on-chain treasury contract oversight. This is a strategically aligned investment in Cardano-native scalability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPHwsViD6pFHdCd3t8esho3Tq4i3qao7mapEFkg2gyM4s -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThese proposals are key components for Cardano to attrach more developers and improve UX for Cardano dapps, passed the temp check with more than 50% Dreps approval off-chain, and also come at very reasonable cost.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Terminada",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSq4VicnuavNaZy6c1bxbxFwRitNUXepDcoM3dKGKnYYT -->\r\n# Terminada\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytf9f78k7rkwk4cu6l2nvna22keu9yus4kqzc0hqspd36uszu0xc2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will individually approve many of these budget items but I don't approve of commingling service providers and bundling as an omni-bus budget proposal.  Furthermore, I don't support wasting software development resources on devices, such as Ledger, that haven't fully open sourced their code.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Dutch Drep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdMt6xcQEzj7Yo2tA53ohFb9wUJa2ZKyCiDeXLMMrmZQA -->\r\n# The Dutch Drep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yvve4554njxyun2s5p9q70v88d5jl7r0h34pjhw5f5tmw3sjtrutp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Dutch DRep, vote No on this budget Info Action.\r\n\r\nWhile we support funding for community-driven initiatives, we have strong reservations about including proposals that introduce protocol-level changes—specifically zkFold and Starstream.\r\n\r\nBoth propose ambitious technologies that would require significant modifications to Cardano’s ledger and core protocol. These kinds of changes demand deep coordination with the broader development community and should not be funded without clear technical alignment, ecosystem consensus, and process transparency. Yet, neither proposal provides sufficient clarity on integration challenges, dependencies, or risk factors—and neither team has meaningfully engaged in Cardano’s open CIP process.\r\n\r\nAs a constructive path forward, we strongly encourage both teams to initiate a CIP (Cardano Improvement Proposal) and, where appropriate, a CPS (Cardano Problem Statement) that formally outlines their proposed changes. A clear example to follow would be the approach taken by the Leios and Alba proposals, which have demonstrated how protocol innovations can be transparently introduced and evaluated within the community.\r\n\r\nWe would also recommend this path for proposals like Midgard, which touches on optimistic rollup design and may similarly intersect with future ledger evolution. Proposals of this scope should first be explored through the CIP/CPS process before treasury funding is considered.\r\n\r\nWe also invite fellow DReps to demand greater technical rigor and transparency from high-impact proposals. When millions of dollars in treasury funds are at stake, big claims—especially those involving protocol changes—should not be taken at face value. They must be supported by clearly articulated implementation paths, risk analysis, and evidence of engagement with Cardano’s open governance and development processes.\r\n\r\nOur stance is not a rejection of the innovation of zkFold and Starstream. Rather, we believe treasury support for protocol-level initiatives should be contingent on demonstrated ecosystem alignment and technical diligence. In contrast, other proposals included in this budget—such as Blockfrost and the Ledger/hardware wallet initiatives—are narrower in scope, do not require consensus-layer changes, and are much better suited for direct funding at this stage.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmX3McRvjaVGLDPGdqmDzRucGj7bKxHEqEZxeLCZENk6VC -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the intent to facilitate community builders’ access to treasury funding without the burden of a 100k ADA deposit is well-meaning, it fundamentally undermines the rigor and security that the threshold was designed to uphold.\r\n\r\nThe 100k ADA deposit is not an arbitrary barrier; it serves as a critical economic signal that aligns incentives, deters frivolous or low-quality proposals, and protects the treasury from dilution by projects lacking sufficient skin in the game. Removing or lowering this threshold risks opening the floodgates to a proliferation of proposals that may fragment community focus, dilute scarce resources, and ultimately erode public confidence in the governance process.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the constitutional safeguards embedded in the Cardano budget framework—including the 50% + 1 Lovelace threshold of active voting stake—are designed to ensure that only proposals with demonstrable, broad-based community support proceed. Relaxing the deposit requirement while relying solely on voting thresholds may expose the system to strategic manipulation, especially given the complexities and nuances of voter participation and stake delegation patterns.\r\n\r\nThe long-term resilience and legitimacy of Cardano’s treasury governance depend on maintaining a disciplined, business-minded approach that prioritizes quality over quantity. While we must encourage innovation and community participation, this cannot come at the expense of the protocol’s foundational principles of decentralization, transparency, and accountability.\r\n\r\nI firmly believe that preserving the 100k ADA deposit threshold is essential to safeguarding the treasury, ensuring meaningful commitment from proposers, and upholding the integrity of our governance process. Therefore, I will vote No on this proposal, advocating instead for a governance model that balances accessibility with responsibility and strategic foresight.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20_7.5MADA_for_community_builders.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Wada DRep, we represent a decentralized and globally connected network of Cardano community builders, innovators, and voters, many based across Africa and the diaspora. Our role in constitutional governance is to act in the best interests of the ecosystem while reflecting the priorities of our community and honoring our internal deliberative frameworks.\r\n\r\nWhile we deeply value the intentions behind the proposal titled “2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget – ₳7.5M for Community Builders,” we have made the decision to abstain from voting on this Budget Info Action. Our abstention is not a reflection of disagreement with the proposals listed. On the contrary, we voted “Yes” on each of these individual projects during the community review phase and maintained strong support for their impact and alignment with Cardano’s long-term vision.\r\n\r\nHowever, we must also act in a way that preserves clarity and coordination within Cardano’s treasury governance process. All of the individual proposals bundled in this ₳7.5M package also appear in the larger ₳275.3M aggregate budget proposal administered by Intersect, titled “Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget – 275M ADA Administered by Intersect.” That proposal includes the same community-approved projects, has passed DRep signaling, and has been carefully structured to align with treasury guardrails, milestone management, and transparent disbursement practices.\r\n\r\nAs such, casting a “yes” vote on both Budget Info Actions creates a risk of administrative and treasury access conflict if both are passed. There is no clearly defined resolution process for managing overlapping budget actions that authorize separate administrators for the same set of proposals. In this context, a dual approval may create confusion around which administrative pathway—Intersect’s structured oversight framework or an alternate, undefined one—should take precedence.\r\n\r\nOur abstention reflects our desire to avoid contributing to that ambiguity while still honoring our prior support for these proposals. We continue to recognize and affirm the tremendous contributions of the community builders represented in this budget. However, we believe that the best path forward is to endorse a single, unified administration for the 2025 budget cycle, specifically, Intersect, which we have already decided to support in the broader ₳275.3M proposal.\r\n\r\nWe encourage our fellow DReps to consider the importance of administrative consistency and treasury process integrity when casting their votes on overlapping Budget Info Actions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/14_community_budget.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 7.5M ₳ for community builders\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Intersect proposal took place off chain using a service called \"Ekklesia\" to collect votes from dReps and decide which budget items should be included in its omnibus budget. The authors of this proposal express concerns regarding the legitimacy of the Intersect proposal.\r\n\r\nThis proposal requests ₳7,568,810 and aims to fund seven high quality projects. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/willpiam/drep/blob/master/vote_context/markdown/14_community_budget.md",
