    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote72.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Reimburse Ikigai Info Governance Action Deposit\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough I fully support the idea of refunding the deposit for the Ikigai proposal, in this particular case I voted No, because I have no clear understanding of who exactly is submitting this proposal and what relation they have to the original author of the Ikigai proposal - this is not specified anywhere in the description. It is also unclear whether the author of the Ikigai proposal actually wants the deposit to be refunded. Since the author has never directly requested it (even though the community generally supports the idea, as it has been discussed multiple times), there is a possibility that the deposit was not lost by mistake but intentionally left as a donation to the treasury. Therefore, I would like to see confirmation from the original author of the Ikigai proposal that they indeed wish to have the deposit returned. I'll be happy to change my vote to Yes once I get clarification on these points.",
