    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmPBGiZqActvHzbhs8wYuQ3wgWfc96adg2HjqNPedPnFCy -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support setting the Net-Change-Limit (NCL) for 2025 at 350 000 000 000 000 lovelace (₳350 million), roughly reflecting the Treasury inflows recorded in 2024.\r\n\r\nOver the longer term, the NCL should be implemented as a protocol parameter and defined as a percentage of the live Treasury balance rather than a fixed number. A percentage-based guardrail would scale automatically, enabling smoother withdrawals and preventing a scenario where a large, fixed cap, potentially hundreds of millions of ada, could be withdrawn in a single action once a Treasury withdrawal governance proposal is approved.",
