    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWjEyrFw6UqrwqAwSRjTinrsyhNkjUL9Z7xzb9KTP7rN5 -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am abstaining on the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy Info Action.\r\n\r\nThis document articulates an ambitious and largely well-aligned framework for Cardano’s development toward 2030. It touches on many areas RCADA supports — ecosystem sustainability, developer education, SPO diversification, enterprise adoption, and measurable KPIs. The intent is positive: to provide a unified strategic compass for Cardano’s post-Voltaire evolution.\r\n\r\nHowever, this particular submission carries procedural and authorship ambiguities. While the content originates from the Product Committee, this on-chain action was submitted independently by a community member rather than the Committee itself. Product Committee members have since clarified that this version was not formally sanctioned. For governance legitimacy, strategy-level documents should reflect verified authorship, internal sign-off, and transparent public consultation prior to appearing on-chain.\r\n\r\nSubstantively, while the document presents a structured and cohesive outline, much of its content consolidates initiatives already underway rather than introducing forward-looking strategies suited for the 2030 horizon. It offers limited discussion of emerging priorities such as advanced privacy technologies, quantum resilience, AI-integrated governance, or frameworks for regional governance participation. These omissions make the document more of a state-of-progress summary than a true roadmap for the next era of the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThe inclusion of transaction-volume KPIs (e.g., a target of 250,000 daily transactions) further reflects a narrow measure of success. Transaction count is a poor proxy for adoption; it can be inflated, cyclical, and disconnected from real-world impact. More meaningful indicators would measure user engagement, active governance participation, decentralized infrastructure health, and real-world integrations. These would better capture the Constitution’s intent for accountable, participatory growth.\r\n\r\nMy abstention should therefore not be read as opposition to the Cardano 2030 vision itself. I view this proposal as a valuable starting point that deserves refinement and formalization. It demonstrates an ecosystem moving toward strategic cohesion, but governance excellence requires both clarity of process and depth of foresight.\r\n\r\nI encourage the Product Committee and Intersect to resubmit this initiative officially — with validated authorship, broader community involvement, and a roadmap that extends beyond current programs into truly future-oriented innovation.\r\n\r\nThis vote follows RCADA’s established principle of constructive abstention: supporting intent and direction, while signaling the need for greater procedural rigor, constitutional alignment, and visionary scope in Cardano’s long-term strategy.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidyhmxqcqtzex5z4wy4fe4aee5icjzsf2k4mjdfdpbiq75qxptssi -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI understand the value of this sort of goal orientation but I simply don't think it fits well with our current ecosystem. There are so many projects moving in so many different directions that setting a priority list for the entire ecosystem doesn't make sense. This would be a better fit for an organization or DAO in my opinion. As such I am voting no on this proposal.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRgBvNguWHP4LR1VfNVVhXp5kusB6AcpdraQvLde5YNZ1 -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis vision provides an inspiring direction for Cardano, but the current proposal feels incomplete. KPI targets, such as the $200M L1 revenue goal, lack clear calculation methodology or ADA price assumptions, making them difficult to evaluate as concrete objectives.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the strategy reads more like a comprehensive wishlist of everything we hope to achieve, rather than a focused plan that prioritizes initiatives and allocates resources in a way that is realistically actionable.\r\n\r\nMost importantly, the concept of an “active, managed treasury” represents a significant strategic shift. Before the community can align around such a change, a detailed governance and risk management framework is needed to ensure decentralization, operational security, and protection of community assets.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I am voting NO as a constructive signal, not as a rejection of the vision itself, but as a request for a more detailed, measurable, and debate-ready version of this plan. My vote may change if a more complete and transparent proposal is presented in the future.\r\n\r\n僕はこの提案に対して反対（NO）票を投じます。\r\n\r\nこのビジョンはCardanoにとって非常に魅力的で、進むべき方向性として共感できますが、現状の提案は不完全に感じます。KPI（例：L1収益2億ドル）については、算出方法やADA価格の前提が明示されておらず、具体的な目標として評価するには不十分です。\r\n\r\nまた、この戦略は「やりたいことリスト」に近く、優先順位やリソース配分が明確でないため、現実的に実行可能な計画とは言いづらいと感じます。\r\n\r\n特に「アクティブ運用型トレジャリー」は非常に大きな戦略的転換であり、導入前にガバナンス設計やリスク管理の枠組みが必要です。コミュニティ資産の保全や分散化を確保する仕組みが示されない限り、採用には慎重であるべきです。\r\n\r\nしたがって、今回のNO票はビジョンそのものを否定するものではなく、より詳細で、測定可能で、議論可能な形に再提示してほしいという建設的なメッセージです。将来的に、より完全で透明性のある提案が出された場合には、投票を変更する可能性もあります。",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://Qmf5fH2NLv1cVLEgbKDAHN881uL6je3zANgdjvk1EYaVF8 -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmbAxQDfPd1U2WnK4QtcX7Wc79T1qGS86JRjZDu3rDZfib\r\n\r\nThe document is too ambiguous. The lack of author on the documents further added ambiguity and uncertainty.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidobccswyw2c6chr7hg4727w7o7dpg5idklpitmwn62omuwpggday -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal, but with conditions.\r\n\r\nAs SIPO DRep, I support the initiative to establish a shared long-term vision for Cardano through on-chain governance. This process reflects the essence of liquid democracy and empowers the community to co-define the future direction of the ecosystem. However, my support is conditional upon expanding and deepening the current vision to include concrete strategic priorities and philosophical foundations.\r\n\r\nThe proposed vision should not only present general aspirations but also define how Cardano will operate as decentralized public infrastructure for real economies, communities, and governance systems. It must show how technology and society will align toward a civilization-scale objective.\r\n\t1.\tPublic Infrastructure and Regional Economies\r\nCardano must evolve beyond financial applications to support real-world governance and community infrastructure. Regional projects such as AIRA (Izanami) in Japan demonstrate how blockchain can connect local governments, citizens, and businesses. The 2030 vision should officially recognize such initiatives as prototypes of Web3 public infrastructure.\r\n\t2.\tStablecoin and DeFi Liquidity Layer\r\nA sustainable economy on Cardano requires stable and transparent liquidity systems. Stablecoins such as USDA and protocols like Liqwid, Optim, and Minswap form the foundation of a decentralized financial layer that combines sovereignty with regulatory trust. The strategy must explain how Cardano will balance open finance and compliance to build a resilient economy.\r\n\t3.\tZK, AI, and Hydra/Leios Integration\r\nTo achieve both scalability and privacy, Cardano must integrate Hydra and Leios for throughput, Zero-Knowledge proofs for verifiable privacy, and AI-driven governance for adaptive decision-making. Together, these technologies create the foundation for Cardano as a “Civilization Operating System” — a platform that supports human and institutional coordination at a global level.\r\n\t4.\tConstitutional Governance and Intersect Alignment\r\nThis proposal should act as a pre-constitutional foundation for the upcoming Cardano Constitution. The governance architecture must ensure that the community’s long-term vision drives institutional design, not the other way around. Transparency, inclusiveness, and accountability should remain central to every layer of governance.\r\n\r\nThis vote therefore supports the process of defining the 2030 vision but urges a broader and deeper approach that unites technology, governance, and society. Cardano must position itself not merely as a blockchain but as a decentralized public sphere — a network of trust and coordination that serves humanity’s collective progress.\r\n\r\nFinal Position:\r\nVote: YES (Conditional Support)\r\nMessage: Support the process of defining the 2030 Vision & Strategy, while urging inclusion of public infrastructure, regional economy integration, DeFi and stablecoin liquidity, and ZK-AI-enabled governance.\r\nGoal: To help Cardano evolve into a Civilization Operating System — a decentralized architecture for economies, communities, and governance beyond borders.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOとして本提案に賛成票を投じます。ただし条件付きの賛成です。\r\n\r\n本提案は、カルダノの長期ビジョンをオンチェーン上で共有し、コミュニティの合意に基づいて定義する重要な試みです。流動的民主主義（liquid democracy）の理念を体現し、DRepとADA保有者が共にエコシステムの進路を決めるという点で意義があります。しかし、この賛成は、現在のビジョンをより具体的かつ包括的に拡張することを前提としています。\r\n\r\nビジョン文書は抽象的な目標だけでなく、カルダノがどのようにして現実社会・地域経済・ガバナンスの基盤として機能するのか、その構造と優先順位を明示すべきです。カルダノが文明的な規模で社会を支えるための具体的な指針を持つ必要があります。\r\n\t1.\t公共インフラと地域経済の統合\r\nカルダノは単なる金融ネットワークに留まらず、現実の社会インフラと地域経済を支える分散型基盤として発展すべきです。日本で進行しているAIRA（イザナミ）などの事例は、地方自治体・住民・企業をつなぐWeb3公共圏の可能性を示しています。2030ビジョンはこうした実例を正式に位置づけるべきです。\r\n\t2.\t安定通貨とDeFi流動性基盤\r\nカルダノ経済の持続性は、透明で安定した流動性インフラの上に成り立ちます。USDAなどのステーブルコインやLiqwid、Optim、Minswapのようなプロトコルは、金融主権と規制信頼を両立させる新しい金融レイヤーの基礎です。戦略には、この分野をどのように発展させ、経済の安定と透明性を確保するのかを明確に示す必要があります。\r\n\t3.\tZK・AI・Hydra/Leiosの統合\r\nスケーラビリティとプライバシーを両立させるには、HydraとLeiosによるスループット拡張、ZK技術による検証可能なプライバシー、AIによる動的ガバナンスの導入が不可欠です。これらを組み合わせることで、カルダノは「文明のためのオペレーティングシステム（Civilization OS）」へと進化できます。\r\n\t4.\t憲法ガバナンスとIntersect整合性\r\nこの提案は今後のカルダノ憲法制定に向けた前段階として位置づけられます。プロダクト委員会やIntersectなどの組織設計は、コミュニティによる長期ビジョンに従う形で構築されるべきです。ガバナンスの全レイヤーで、透明性・説明責任・参加型設計が担保される必要があります。\r\n\r\nこの投票は、2030ビジョンの策定プロセスを支持するものですが、同時にその範囲をより広く・深く拡張することを求めます。カルダノは単なるブロックチェーンではなく、人間社会の信頼と協調を支える分散型公共圏へと進化するべきです。\r\n\r\n最終立場：\r\n投票種別：賛成（条件付き）\r\n主旨：カルダノの2030ビジョン策定プロセスを支持しつつ、公共インフラ、地域経済、DeFi・ステーブルコイン流動性、ZKとAIによるガバナンス統合の観点を加えることを提案します。\r\n目的：カルダノを「Civilization Operating System」— 国境を超えて経済・社会・ガバナンスを支える分散型基盤へと進化させるためです。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQX5L3Sc5rvT4fm2mgpnsV1zKnKU99kBhKreZZXwKTJT3 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe abstained on this proposal. The vision and strategy for Cardano 2030 are important, but we believe further discussion and refinement are needed before expressing clear support or opposition. Abstaining leaves room for the community to continue shaping the direction together.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibjefiunsbnwqor6w6xtu5y4hncis2rztplejd4a6styzlez7gede -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support the \"Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\" Info Action because it fosters a unified, community-backed vision for Cardano’s long-term success. A \"yes\" vote endorses a clear strategic direction, aligning development efforts to enhance adoption and ecosystem growth. This action promotes transparent, on-chain governance, empowering DReps to reflect constituent priorities while setting a precedent for inclusive feedback. After reviewing the vision document, I believe it aligns with Cardano’s goals of scalability, interoperability, and sustainability, benefiting the entire community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmavsTp8Bxh5sQbmhKeoStwKiyAjeRtPKkwpcp4hZMrx6j -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a significant change for Cardano, and the proposal feels more aspirational than concrete.  More work is needed for such a significant change, particularly forming a full fledged governance framework for the fund.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTy84krxaRd8Zot7qXL9Pi5t34JEFWPMxBQBRErjv3cgp -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Everybody has a \"vision,\" yet few these days have a clear \"mission.\"**\r\n\r\nOh well. **The document presents many sensible high-level goals, but it lacks prioritization, measurable realism, and protects neither treasury discipline nor implementation clarity**; endorsing it now would prematurely green-light a strategic umbrella without required trade-offs, accountability frameworks, or a defensible cost/benefit basis.\r\n\r\nIt's not all bad, though. The ambition aligns with Cardano’s long-term value proposition: enterprise-grade, censorship-resistant public infrastructure with scientific foundations. The focus areas are broadly correct: abstraction for UX, L2 + scalability, SPO health, developer onboarding, enterprise/national integration, and treasury sustainability. Lastly, the KPI list identifies relevant vectors (L1 revenue, daily meaningful transactions, enterprise integrations), which is better than many prior high-level statements.\r\n\r\nThe devil is in the details, or lack thereof. **The document is a strategy-lite manifesto with lots of desirable outcomes and pillars but no prioritized trade-offs. Strategy must choose what not to do. This plan does not. **Without hard choices, we will diffuse resources across everything and achieve little. Sounds like present-day Cardano, huh? Pursuing both “world-class L1 scalability” and extensive Layer 2 expansion is fine, but the document does not define sequencing, resource allocation, or critical-path dependencies. The proposed KPIs are aspirational but not actionable or credible. For example: $200M annual L1 revenue and 250k daily meaningful transactions are headline-worthy but lack baseline assumptions (time horizon, sources of that revenue, what counts exactly as meaningful transaction).\r\n\r\nThe call for an “active, multi-asset, managed treasury” is sensible in principle, but the doc provides no governance guardrails, risk appetite, or conflict-of-interest mitigation. Converting long-term public-good funds into actively managed assets without strict governance, independent oversight, and loss limits is hazardous, to say the least. A phrase like “investments that lead to paying clients” needs concrete investment criteria; otherwise grants and “strategic investments” become opaque subsidies that reproduce past inefficiencies. Also sounds like present-day Cardano—another check here.\r\n\r\nGet real and get realistic! Claiming Cardano is “the only viable option” for enterprises demanding high assurance is rhetorical overreach. Enterprises judge platforms on verifiable compliance, SLAs, vendor ecosystems, and ecosystem maturity; none of which are guaranteed by peer review alone. The document underestimates the engineering, legal, and procurement effort required to achieve SOC-type compliance, accounting/auditing integrations, and sovereign-grade SLAs. Those require resourcing and time, not rhetoric and wishful thinking.\r\n\r\nThe strategy asks the community to align, but offers no enforcement, funding prioritization process, nor escalation rules when initiatives drift. There is no explicit linkage between the strategy and on-chain governance levers (how will treasury allocations be tied to KPI milestones?).\r\n\r\n**I vote NO on this Action in its current form. I support the underlying ambition and many specific focus areas, but not the document as a governance mandate today. As always, and with all of my votes, I demand a tighter, prioritized, accountable, and data-driven strategy with concrete risk mitigation and treasury governance.**",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmf5TgG3G3h9HYW5u9vVmh9QpYNH2omJ7fBXgW9SvLDCHs -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe informational action, likely submitted by a member of Intersect's product committee, enables DReps to provide feedback on chain. I appreciate the general concept, as it theoretically represents the appropriate path forward. However, it holds no real value unless executed effectively in practice, which is the hard part.\r\nRegarding the text, I would prefer greater emphasis on the needs of the average person, along with guiding principles such as personal data protection (via Midnight) and transforming the current status quo. While partnerships with enterprises, KPIs, and similar elements are valid, Cardano is fundamentally a tool for the people, yet the text lacks sufficient focus on this human centered aspect.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVYJsYpAJRTEoQGxG7DEGdfb7uV3S79JpJNN9QutwXEGC -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOverall, this is a solid, forward-thinking blueprint that evolves Cardano from \"research lab\" to \"global infrastructure powerhouse\" without abandoning its ethos.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreib73fjgvawcmkedtievmgtfh7owfq7cfva3vdjmmknzs7blwa6xry -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe as Wada DRep votes \"yes\" on this info-action as we recognize the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy as a well-structured blueprint that captures many of the principles Wada stands for as a DRep, particularly its emphasis on decentralization, culture-first engagement, education, enterprise inclusion, and financial sustainability. Each of the seven strategic imperatives directly supports Wada’s broader vision of empowering local ecosystems and ensuring that Cardano’s growth is both equitable and globally inclusive. The culture-first and localized engagement pillar mirrors our ongoing efforts across Africa to embed blockchain adoption within cultural realities, while the focus on ecosystem capacity building and developer empowerment aligns strongly with our mission to foster self-reliant, regionally skilled communities. Likewise, the commitment to enterprise adoption, SPO incentives, and sound treasury management resonates with our advocacy for transparent and sustainable infrastructure development.\r\n\r\nHowever, we note that while decentralization and financial stewardship are featured, “Governance” is not explicitly included as a core strategic pillar. Given that governance underpins every facet of Cardano’s future; from constitutional oversight to participatory funding decisions, it warrants clear visibility within the strategy. We therefore recommend that a dedicated “Governance and Community Participation” imperative be incorporated in subsequent revisions of the 2030 roadmap. This should define measurable goals for voter participation, DRep diversity, delegation spread-out, transparency standards, governance education, etc. We believe that embedding governance as a strategic focus will ensure that the ecosystem’s evolution remains truly decentralized, inclusive, and accountable; principles central to both Cardano’s long-term viability and Wada’s continued advocacy within it.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreig3duqpajqlnmpbipgp5mvumqqafgggpuwxlyip3qaptmshbbl4xq -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAt this time I don't see the need for a group vision.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
