    {
      "voter": "YOADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreievthmuusnhuyyhaskntbudyztzzpdvnztyk3vvtbqek45reln4xq -->\r\n# YOADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26sfka2km0p4xw073ujdq406wxxczhdyfh9vw7yxpfselchzkdjn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI think this is a good Vision & Strategy and that is appropriate for the ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_CardanoVision2030.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep decides to ABSTAIN on the info action titled Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nYoroi values the effort to outline Cardano’s long-term vision, but voting now could lead to voter fatigue since an official governance action is already planned for the end of October.\r\n\r\nProceeding with multiple overlapping actions risks confusing delegators and diluting meaningful feedback.\r\n\r\nYoroi believes it is more effective to focus community attention on the finalized and official version, where feedback will have the greatest impact.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZnw5sRhzNfyppa8jWph18hV6Ns9wLCWS9168nMj3VvmL -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES for \"Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\" because I believe it can be considered a provisional Vision & Strategy and is appropriate for the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThe Vision and Strategy should naturally be constantly evolving, so if the Product Committee or other community members submit a better one, I will vote YES for it and overwrite the Vision & Strategy.\r\n\r\nI could go on and on about the endless shortcomings of this Vision & Strategy, such as it being lacking in X or Y. Many DRep members have pointed these out, and I agree with many of them.\r\n\r\nHowever, it seems to me that moving forward with Catalyst, Builder DAO, and other proposed governance actions with a blank Vision & Strategy poses a deeper risk.\r\n\r\nAs discussed in Las Vegas, we need a North Star, but the biggest problem is that neither Catalyst, Builder DAO, nor any other Treasury Withdrawal will wait for the perfect North Star to appear.\r\n\r\nIt's like an intern constitution. It may not be perfect, but it's better than nothing. At the very least, I haven't found any fatally harmful elements in the Vision & Strategy.\r\n\r\nSo I'm voting YES for the intern Vision & Strategy. If something better is proposed, I'll vote YES for it and override it.\r\n\r\n私は、「Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy」に、暫定的なVision & Strategyと認めることが可能かつエコシステムのためには適切と考えため、YESを投じることにしました。\r\n\r\nVision と Strategyは当然ながら常に変化し続けるべきものであるため、プロダクト委員会やその他のコミュニティが、より良いものを提出したらそれにもYESを投票し、Vision & Strategyを上書きします。\r\n\r\nこのVision & StrategyにはXが足りない、Yも足りない、という不足点を無限に列挙することはできます。多くのDRepがそれらを指摘しており、私はそれらに同意する点も多いです。\r\n\r\nただ、Vision & Strategyが空白の状態でCatalyst、ビルダーDAO、その他次々に提案されるガバナンスアクションが進行していくことのほうがより深いリスクを生じさせているように見えます。\r\n\r\nラスベガスで議論されたように私たちには北極星が必要ですが、最大の問題は、CatalystもビルダーDAOもその他のトレジャリーウィズドローも完璧な北極星の出現を待ってくれません。\r\n\r\nこれはintern憲法のようなものです。完璧ではないかもしれませんが、何もないよりあったほうが有益です。少なくとも致命的に有害な要素をVision & Strategyの中に見つけていません。\r\n\r\nよって、intern Vision & StrategyとしてYESを投票します。より良いものが提案されたらそれにYESを投票して上書きします。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Zacros",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihsf6cwyoen2bcgoojvqrcapt2ve52gy62oq3hmwps644p4xfl56e -->\r\n# Zacros\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Defining the Cardano 2030 Vision & Strategy\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2tp9q9vckglgkgkgcdc33jtahrstfzfj3c8ez926ysszjqp5r4ts`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOverall Panda thinks it is good. However Panda would love some more emphasis on keeping decentralization alive:\r\n- with SPO (supporting small pools and growing their numbers)\r\n- but also in Governance, since right now few keys hold enormous power (voting dynamics/power,  Dreps participation, processes improvement)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
