    {
      "voter": "Alex Maaza Planetmaaz",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRoC8TQD5i4euQHjw8m1axUgZaokcCXQNZ4FKJdDuZyii -->\r\n# Alex Maaza Planetmaaz\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Replace Interim Constitutional Committee\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwvktdg0mltrjjfyjjyygfsf053zyu70ttll6pz7ff4dls4n9m9d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## tl:dr rationale\r\n\r\nProtested MVG via DRep inactivity due to rushed, treasury-focused process over adoption/scalability priorities. **Now voting YES for Constitutional Committee to mature governanc**e.\r\n\r\n## Full Rationale\r\n\r\nSince registering as a DRep, I chose to remain inactive in onchain voting to protest how Minimum Viable Governance (MVG) was established on Cardano. I believe this process has concluded with the enactment of the 39 treasury withdrawal governance actions.\r\n\r\n### My Core Concerns\r\n\r\n* **Rushed Implementation**: the process was rushed and dominated by actors seeking outsized near-term benefits rather than serving the ecosystem. The focus appeared to be accessing the Cardano treasury rather than implementing comprehensive governance capabilities.\r\n* **Misplaced Priorities** I believe we should have prioritized Cardano adoption and reducing barriers to it, especially addressing scalability capabilities by completing the Basho roadmap era.\r\n\r\n### Moving Forward\r\n\r\nHowever, we must build from where we are. A key step forward is replacing the Interim Constitutional Committee (ICC) with a Constitutional Committee (CC).\r\nWhile I would have preferred immediate onchain elections, I understand the MVG compromise through Intersect. I hope:\r\n* Future elections occur onchain independently of a centralised actor\r\n* The elected CC neither calcifies nor becomes a chaotic risk to governance\r\n\r\n#### My Vote\r\n\r\nBy voting YES for this New Committee governance action, I vote to prevent interruptions to Cardano's governance and support its maturation.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AltcoinOracle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYii1GcvyHg1UkwCobLtDLWjLybFsw3JYfGyA7nyDaGJj -->\r\n# AltcoinOracle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Replace Interim Constitutional Committee\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygvgk3899qm38zth07z5clhfjvzfhe2mf2kvkqrfxp93r5srjre5s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for a smooth replacement.\r\n\r\nStrength and honor.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Andreas Sosilo",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmdswncqrhkp8b58DZs23GJBBAwGtjtt4u2r4EcZHx87ou -->\r\n# Andreas Sosilo\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Replace Interim Constitutional Committee\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y20w8vxwd3venlvp0muxwzmdlr7a006dpz580czmaj422sqng6fkg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote \"Yes\" on the Governance Action (GA) to replace the Interim Constitutional Committee (ICC) with the newly elected Constitutional Committee (CC) because this marks a necessary and meaningful step forward in Cardano's on-chain governance. The ICC served its purpose as a temporary oversight body during the initial phase of the governance framework, but it was always intended to be provisional. The recent election process, conducted between May and July 2025, was transparent, community-driven, and successfully selected seven qualified members through active DReps participation.\r\n\r\nRatifying the new CC ensures that Cardano’s governance remains operational and accountable beyond Epoch 580, while also affirming our collective commitment to decentralization and legitimacy. The newly elected committee members bring diverse backgrounds and perspectives, and their terms provide both continuity and resilience. By voting \"Yes\", we honor the outcome of the election and help solidify the constitutional process that underpins Cardano’s long-term success.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
