    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmbh8JTVKdXXYhQrUdM5YH1jkTMLFG6fSpjXnhnRERPwx2 -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Replace Interim Constitutional Committee\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on this governance action to endorse the results of the Constitutional Committee election held from May 5th to July 6th, 2025. This decision ensures the timely and seamless transition from the Interim Constitutional Committee to the newly elected members, in line with the Cardano Constitution’s mandate for staggered terms and continuous governance functionality. The election process was transparent, verifiable, and independently audited, fulfilling constitutional requirements. Approving this action prevents any governance gap after the current committee’s term ends in epoch 580 and strengthens the long-term stability of Cardano’s decentralized governance.\r\n\r\n本ガバナンス提案に対し、Yes として投票します。\r\n2025年5月5日から7月6日にかけて実施された憲法委員会選挙の結果を承認し、暫定憲法委員会から新たに選出された委員への円滑かつ期限内の移行を確実にするためです。これは、憲法で定められた任期の段階的交代とガバナンス機能の継続性を担保するものであり、選挙は透明性・検証可能性を備え、独立監査も行われています。本提案を承認することで、epoch 580で現委員会の任期が終了した後のガバナンス空白を回避し、Cardanoの分散型ガバナンスの長期的な安定性を強化します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVK4CWdpdyFJGNxaUkX5v1MGovBNwUPTU3qkNQMPRxZX3 -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Replace Interim Constitutional Committee\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**ARTICLE VII, Section 1** of the Cardano Constitution establishes the Constitutional Committee. Having participated in the election of these CC members, I can confirm that the process was free, fair and followed democratic principles. I therefore support this GA in replacing the interim CC with the newly elected CC, marking a significant step toward the full implementation of the CIP-1694 proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
