    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTbEGQEPMLsbHnaxctctwQgpC1Kqqvw5Kw5nenDQs3CpV -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Replace Interim Constitutional Committee\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes. The Interim Committee played an important role in getting the governance process off the ground, but Cardano must now transition to a more accountable, community-aligned structure. Replacing the interim members with those selected through transparent, participatory processes strengthens the legitimacy of on-chain governance and aligns with the principles outlined in the Cardano Constitution. This is a necessary and timely step toward a decentralized and representative governance model.",
      "vote": "YES"
