    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiba4ialqbuu3tdtq4wvkoeawvtxzk7tfxdbeu7wwfdun3oxc4gzcy -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI can find myself in most of the points; however:\r\n1/ I don’t consider a gap of more than five minutes in block production to be an outage. While the chance of having no blocks assigned for such a period is indeed extremely low, given the level of decentralization we have, we can and should account for some missed blocks, hence we indeed see some of those. I still see Cardano as having 100% uptime.\r\n2/ Total Value Locked is a stupid metric.",
