    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA080-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança \"Cardano 2030: Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\" (gov_action18fd7jwa06fksmwumlcvlft8v4guvaa672qsp6xgenekvs4kmvcqsq8cqks4), pois ela é o resultado de um amplo processo comunitário conduzido pelo Comitê de Produto do Intersect, que, em conjunto com a comunidade Cardano, promoveu workshops, reuniões, pesquisas, debates e diversas iniciativas de escuta ativa para construir e validar a Visão Estratégica da Cardano até 2030. O resultado é extremamente positivo, ao definir de forma clara os pilares estratégicos e os KPIs associados que guiarão a evolução da Cardano nos próximos anos. Além disso, o framework fornece uma base objetiva e robusta para que os DReps possam avaliar e filtrar ações de governança alinhadas ao propósito geral estabelecido pela comunidade, fortalecendo a coerência, a previsibilidade e a maturidade do processo decisório.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action \"Cardano 2030: Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\" (gov_action18fd7jwa06fksmwumlcvlft8v4guvaa672qsp6xgenekvs4kmvcqsq8cqks4), as it is the outcome of a broad community-driven process led by the Intersect Product Committee, which, together with the Cardano community, conducted workshops, meetings, surveys, debates, and multiple listening initiatives to build and validate Cardano’s Strategic Vision through 2030. The result is extremely positive, as it clearly defines the strategic pillars and associated KPIs that will guide Cardano’s evolution over the coming years. Moreover, the framework provides a robust and objective reference for DReps to assess and filter governance actions that are aligned with the overall purpose defined by the community, strengthening coherence, predictability, and maturity in governance decision-making.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "PRIDE",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihaxdi4rcfjdyrqgjtyczsbr3kebvhcx6ecysihubuwwtodtrtzn4 -->\r\n# PRIDE\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpazkd0aqex0kd3vrhk47sjy0jqgq3xu6h2zv9wevfequcxyynwv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am against funding DReps at this time, yet Pillar 3 G.1. recommends funding DReps.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUjisproVj252htLLB7Ab8h8Ma64baAZHmxWutrosxDXR -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis Info action reflects a substantial, good-faith effort by the Intersect Product Committee to articulate a shared long-term Vision, Mission, Strategy framework, and KPIs for Cardano under full on-chain governance. The process followed was extensive, consultative, and well documented, involving broad community participation across workshops, surveys, SPO engagement, and dialogue with founding entities. From a governance-process perspective, this work meets a high standard of legitimacy and transparency.\r\n\r\nRCADA agrees with the underlying motivation of the proposal. As Cardano transitions from protocol delivery into decentralized treasury governance, the absence of a commonly articulated strategic reference point increases the risk of fragmented decision-making, inconsistent resource allocation, and reactive governance driven by short-term narratives. The intent to provide DReps with shared language and long-term framing is reasonable and directionally aligned with the maturation of Cardano’s governance model.\r\n\r\nHowever, RCADA does not believe this proposal, in its current form, is sufficiently actionable or decision-constraining to warrant an affirmative endorsement.\r\n\r\nWhile the Vision and Mission statements are broadly aligned with Cardano’s historical identity, they remain highly abstract and do not meaningfully narrow governance decision space or establish explicit trade-offs. The five strategic pillars describe important domains of activity, but they are additive rather than prioritised, offering limited guidance on what should be de-prioritised or declined when resources, attention, or governance capacity are constrained. As such, the framework functions primarily as a consensus narrative rather than a governance tool.\r\n\r\nRCADA places particular emphasis on decentralization as an active governance risk, not a background assumption. Although the strategy acknowledges decentralization and includes quantitative indicators—such as DRep voting power distribution, multi-client requirements, and a target of more than 500 independent stake pools—these thresholds are aspirational rather than disciplinary. From an SPO perspective, the “500 independent pools” target is especially concerning: it is a very low bar relative to Cardano’s current and historical decentralization levels and risks becoming a rhetorical shield for stake concentration rather than a safeguard against it. Large multi-pool operators could readily meet such a threshold while further marginalizing small, independent single-pool operators, using the KPI itself to justify outcomes that weaken decentralization in practice.\r\n\r\nMore broadly, the proposed KPIs, while more concrete than purely narrative statements, remain weakly coupled to governance decisions. They are useful as diagnostic or communicative indicators, but they do not clearly constrain treasury approvals, trigger corrective action, or define failure conditions that would materially discipline power or spending. This creates a risk that alignment with the strategy can be asserted rhetorically without demonstrable accountability or causality.\r\n\r\nRCADA also notes that much of the strategic detail and iteration occurs off-chain as a living document. While this is appropriate for exploratory strategy development, it reinforces that this Info action functions primarily as acknowledgment rather than as a governance instrument. Endorsing such a framework on-chain without stronger decision hooks risks establishing soft precedent, where strategic narratives gain informal authority without corresponding mechanisms for challenge, revision, or enforcement by DReps.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, RCADA has chosen to abstain on this action.\r\n\r\nThis abstention should not be interpreted as opposition to the intent, the process, or the value of strategic reflection. Rather, it signals that while this work represents a constructive and serious starting point, it does not yet meet the threshold of governance usefulness, decentralization protection, and decision discipline required for a supportive “Yes” vote. RCADA would welcome future iterations or follow-up actions that narrow scope, embed decentralization more explicitly, raise the bar on decentralization metrics, and more clearly link strategy and KPIs to concrete governance and treasury decisions.\r\n\r\nRCADA remains committed to thoughtful, disciplined governance and to supporting approaches that strengthen Cardano’s long-term resilience, decentralization, and credibility. This abstention is intended as a constructive signal toward that end.\r\n[https://brolloks.github.io/rcada-drep-votes/votes/2026/cardano-2030-vision-mission-strategy-framework-and-kpis.html]()",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Reshma_Mohan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/resgsh/drep-mainnet/refs/heads/main/voting-activity/9.Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Reshma_Mohan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfcgvh8rum7a9ma4gwgwuwutdu0dnrzaj98jytwyfqzd87q2nehvm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES after reviewing the full 2030 Vision, Strategy and KPI framework in detail. This proposal is not vague direction setting; it clearly defines what success means for Cardano by tying long-term goals to concrete metrics such as network reliability targets, active usage, governance participation, treasury sustainability and real-world adoption. What matters to me is that it prioritises protocol robustness, multi-client resilience, scalable UX and economic self-sufficiency before chasing growth numbers. As an Intersect OSC committee member, I have seen the depth of work, consultation and iteration that has gone into this strategy, and I am confident in Intersect’s ability to steward this framework responsibly with community oversight. This Info Action gives the ecosystem a shared reference point to make better funding, governance and product decisions over the coming years, without prematurely locking the protocol into rigid commitments.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidfhhutfxdomkdsncrbjk2l56wh3g2vjggu7csqdnu3p35kkzbrdm -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of this info action. The overall goal of the info action is a good one. In general a vision document is valuable to have to focus efforts towards a common goal, and I believe this should be supported. The vision outlined is also well thought through and aligns with my view of where Cardano should move towards in the future. The pillars identified are all important but are not assigned a particular order of priority. This does make the vision slightly less focused but is reasonable since there would be significant disagreement on that front. I do appreciate, however, that the main focus is on branding Cardano as a mission-critical, high-assurance protocol, and this focuses on its legitimate strengths. This is a good decision in my view, as we need to stop comparing all blockchains using the same metrics. Cardano's focus should be on decentralized stability and security. All the pillars in the action support that goal. The KPIs are an interesting component. I don't actually think that KPIs are required for this type of vision document, and I can't say I fully agree with the KPIs listed. I only say this in the context that this space moves so quickly that I don't think KPIs can stay relevant for a 5 year period. That said, I don't see anything that is incorrect in terms of focus and the KPIs can always change in the future if they become irrelevant and the community agrees to change the focus. Overall a solid proposal that I am happy to support.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaQg5rKF4bBRnKHhaBTFdgiFtbMvBHpRHoaZcdAp53s6M -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI understand this proposal as the first long-term vision and strategic framework that organizes where Cardano aims to go toward 2030 and the value axes along which it seeks to evolve, through a community-led and formally recognized governance process. The involvement of more than 700 participants, multiple rounds of input collection and review, and the fact that it was developed under authority and funding delegated by DReps all support the assessment that this initiative carries a meaningful degree of legitimacy and process integrity.\r\n\r\nThe proposed Vision clearly positions Cardano around its core strengths—security, reliability, and censorship resistance—by defining its role as the foundational infrastructure for mission-critical applications. I consider this a reasonable and coherent differentiation strategy in the competitive Layer 1 landscape. Furthermore, the inclusion of a Mission statement, five strategic pillars, and associated KPIs provides a shared vocabulary and reference framework that can support DReps in evaluating future proposals and treasury allocations, thereby contributing to more consistent and accountable governance decision-making.\r\n\r\nIt is also important that this proposal is explicitly positioned as a strategic document rather than a constitutional one, and that it does not bind or compel DReps to vote in any particular manner. While there is a need to remain cautious about the potential for Vision statements or KPIs to become overly rigid or mechanically applied over time, the proposal is designed to be iterative and subject to future revision through subsequent Info Actions. On this basis, I consider the risk of undue constraint at this stage to be limited.\r\n\r\nOverall, in the context of Cardano’s transition to full on-chain governance, I view this proposal as a meaningful foundation for aligning community efforts and enabling DReps to make more strategic and explainable decisions. For these reasons, I support this proposal as an initial step toward sharing a long-term strategic direction for Cardano.\r\n\r\n本提案は、Cardanoが2030年に向けてどの方向を目指し、どのような価値軸で発展していくのかを、コミュニティ主導かつ正式なガバナンスプロセスを通じて整理した初の長期ビジョンおよび戦略フレームワークであると理解しています。700名以上の関与、複数回にわたる意見収集とレビュー、そしてDRepから委任された予算と権限のもとで策定された点からも、本提案は一定の正統性と再現性を備えた取り組みだと評価します。 提示されているVisionは、Cardanoの強みである安全性、信頼性、検閲耐性を軸に、「ミッションクリティカルな用途」を支える基盤としての立ち位置を明確にしており、他のL1との競争において差別化を図る方向性として妥当だと考えます。また、Mission、5つの戦略的ピラー、KPIまでを含めて整理されている点は、今後DRepが提案や予算配分を評価する際の共通言語や参照軸として有用であり、ガバナンスの質を高める効果が期待できます。 一方で、本提案は憲法文書ではなく、DRepの投票判断を拘束するものでもないことが明確にされており、あくまで戦略的な指針として位置づけられている点も重要です。VisionやKPIが将来的に硬直化したり、機械的に運用されることには注意が必要ですが、本提案自体が更新可能であり、将来のInfo Actionを通じて見直される前提で設計されていることから、現時点では過度なリスクは限定的だと判断します。 総合的に見て、本提案はCardanoが完全なオンチェーンガバナンス体制へ移行した現在において、コミュニティ全体の努力を一定の方向に束ね、DRepによる意思決定をより戦略的・説明可能なものにするための土台として意義があると考えます。そのため、本提案をCardanoの長期的な指針を共有するための第一歩として支持します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab Testing DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmc1wpLVVJqmb8kfuZVRvDihWML1YXkckPw3rf8aCjd3MT -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab Testing DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjrttn43cyz6sde85shqvl33k22ynjxx85j2h6h5ns42tqafqudl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt is a testing governance voting transaction only.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
