    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sidan-lab/DRep/refs/heads/main/voting-history/ga81/rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe have attended the workshops and discussed with various community members. After careful consideration, we decided to vote yes for the proposal as we believe the KPIs specified are the key metrics for measuring the success of Cardano in upcoming years.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigu7m5biu6ylkt2mdf52xymdc5p27irb4kcrx5vrumvnfhcel4x7a -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep Vote Rationale\r\n\r\nPosition: YES (Conditional Support)\r\n\r\nAs SIPO DRep, I cast a YES (conditional support) vote for the Info Action\r\n“Cardano 2030: Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs.”\r\n\r\nThis proposal does not amend the Constitution, enforce rules, or authorize treasury spending. As an Info Action, it aims to provide a shared long-term direction and strategic reference point for the Cardano ecosystem. With that understanding, I support this proposal as an important step in the maturation of Cardano governance.\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Why I Support This Proposal\r\n\r\nThis is the first community-led, governance-native effort to articulate a long-term Vision and Strategy for Cardano after the transition to full on-chain governance. The process involved more than 700 contributors and extensive consultation across the ecosystem, which I see as a clear signal that Cardano governance has entered a more mature phase.\r\n\r\nI particularly value that this proposal:\r\n\t•\tClearly positions Cardano as\r\n“the most secure, reliable, and censorship-resistant blockchain for mission-critical applications.”\r\n\t•\tMoves beyond technical roadmaps to articulate\r\nwhy Cardano exists and who it is built for\r\n\t•\tProvides DReps with a strategic measuring stick for evaluating future proposals and treasury allocations\r\n\r\nI believe this shared strategic clarity is essential if Cardano is to grow coherently over the long term.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Significance in the Broader Blockchain Landscape\r\n\r\nMany Layer-1 ecosystems today compete primarily on speed, cost, or compatibility. Far fewer clearly position themselves as infrastructure for mission-critical economic and societal systems where reliability and decentralization are paramount.\r\n\r\nThis Vision positions Cardano as:\r\n\t•\tLong-term public infrastructure\r\n\t•\tNot driven by short-term hype cycles\r\n\t•\tDesigned for high-stakes, real-world use cases\r\n\r\nIn my view, this positioning represents one of Cardano’s strongest differentiators among L1 blockchains.\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Why This Is “Conditional” Support\r\n\r\nMy support is explicit and comes with important clarifications.\r\n\r\n(1) This is a strategic guide, not a binding rule\r\nThe Vision, Strategy, and KPIs should:\r\n\t•\tInform DRep judgment\r\n\t•\tNot mechanically constrain future votes\r\n\t•\tNot be used to exclude legitimate alternative approaches or experimentation\r\n\r\nI see this document as a decision-support framework, not a governance mandate.\r\n\r\n\r\n(2) KPIs must remain adaptive\r\nWhile KPIs improve transparency and accountability, they must:\r\n\t•\tAvoid becoming centralized or rigid scorecards\r\n\t•\tReflect ecosystem diversity and real-world data\r\n\t•\tEvolve as Cardano matures\r\n\r\nKPIs should function as living indicators, not fixed targets.\r\n\r\n\r\n(3) Adoption should be interpreted broadly\r\nAdoption should include not only enterprise and government use cases, but also:\r\n\t•\tLocal economies\r\n\t•\tSmall and medium-sized initiatives\r\n\t•\tGrassroots and community-driven deployments\r\n\r\nI expect this Vision to be applied in a way that preserves Cardano’s openness to bottom-up innovation.\r\n\r\n\r\n4. My Forward-Looking Approach as SIPO DRep\r\n\r\nBy supporting this proposal, I intend to use the 2030 Vision constructively when evaluating future Catalyst proposals and budget decisions, asking:\r\n\t•\tWhich strategic pillar does this advance?\r\n\t•\tWhat long-term public value does it create?\r\n\t•\tHow does it reinforce Cardano’s unique strengths?\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Conclusion\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I vote YES (conditional support) as SIPO DRep on this Info Action.\r\n\r\nI see the Cardano 2030 Vision not as a final answer, but as a shared starting point—a common language that can evolve with data, experience, and community input as Cardano moves into the next decade.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nPosition: YES（条件付き賛成）\r\n\r\nSIPO DRepとして、私は本Info Action\r\n「Cardano 2030: Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs」\r\nに対し、「条件付き賛成（Yes）」を投じます。\r\n\r\n本提案は、憲法改正や予算執行を伴うものではなく、Info Action（情報提供型ガバナンスアクション）として、Cardanoが2030年に向けて共有すべき方向性と評価軸を示すことを目的としています。その性質を踏まえた上で、私は本提案をガバナンス成熟にとって重要な第一歩として支持します。\r\n\r\n\r\n1. 賛成の理由（なぜ支持するのか）\r\n\r\nまず本提案は、完全オンチェーン・ガバナンスへ移行したCardanoにおいて、初めてコミュニティ主導で策定された長期的なビジョンと戦略フレームワークです。\r\n700名以上の関係者が関わり、ワークショップ、調査、創設組織との対話を通じてまとめられたこのプロセス自体が、Cardanoのガバナンスが次の段階に進んだことを示していると私は考えています。\r\n\r\n特に、以下の点を高く評価しています。\r\n\t•\tCardanoを\r\n「最も安全で、信頼性が高く、検閲耐性のある、ミッションクリティカルなアプリケーションのためのブロックチェーン」\r\nと明確に位置づけた点\r\n\t•\t技術的ロードマップではなく、\r\n「なぜCardanoが存在するのか」「誰のための基盤なのか」を言語化している点\r\n\t•\t今後、DRepsが提案や予算配分を評価する際の\r\n共通の戦略的な物差し（Strategic Measuring Stick）を提供している点\r\n\r\n私は、短期的なトレンドや一時的なナラティブに左右されず、Cardanoを長期視点で社会インフラとして育てていくために、このような共通認識は不可欠だと考えています。\r\n\r\n\r\n2. ブロックチェーン全体の文脈における意義\r\n\r\n現在のL1エコシステムでは、「高速」「低コスト」「互換性」といった軸での競争が激化しています。一方で、国家・自治体・公共分野・基幹産業など、失敗が許されない領域を本気で担うビジョンを明確に掲げているチェーンは多くありません。\r\n\r\n本提案が示すVisionは、Cardanoを\r\n\t•\t投機中心のプラットフォームではなく\r\n\t•\t一時的な流行に依存するものでもなく\r\n\t•\t経済と社会を支えるミッションクリティカルな基盤\r\n\r\nとして位置づけるものです。私はこの点こそが、Cardanoが他のL1と明確に差別化できる強みだと考えています。\r\n\r\n\r\n3. 「条件付き賛成」とする理由（重要な前提）\r\n\r\n私は本提案を支持しますが、同時に以下の点を明確にした上での賛成であることを表明します。\r\n\r\n① 本提案は「拘束力を持たない」戦略文書であること\r\n本Vision・Strategy・KPIは、\r\n\t•\tDRepsの投票を強制するものではなく\r\n\t•\t将来の提案を機械的に縛るルールでもありません\r\n\r\n私は、この文書を\r\n「判断を助ける指針」として活用すべきであり、\r\n「異なるアプローチや新しい実験を排除する根拠」として使われるべきではないと考えています。\r\n\r\n\r\n② KPIは進化し続けるべきであること\r\nKPIを設定すること自体は、透明性と説明責任の観点から非常に重要です。ただし、\r\n\t•\t数値目標が目的化しないこと\r\n\t•\t中央集権的な評価装置にならないこと\r\n\t•\t地域差や発展段階の違いを無視しないこと\r\n\r\nが不可欠です。私は、KPIは固定された「採点表」ではなく、実データと現場の知見に基づき、継続的に更新されるべきものだと考えています。\r\n\r\n\r\n③ 採用（Adoption）の定義は広くあるべきであること\r\n私は、エンタープライズや政府レベルの採用だけでなく、\r\n\t•\t地域経済\r\n\t•\t中小規模の事業者\r\n\t•\t草の根コミュニティ\r\n\t•\tローカルな実装や実証\r\n\r\nも、Cardanoにとって重要な採用形態だと考えています。本Visionが、こうした分散的でボトムアップ型の価値創出を排除しない形で解釈・運用されることを期待します。\r\n\r\n\r\n4. SIPO DRepとしての今後の姿勢\r\n\r\nSIPO DRepとして私は、本提案を支持した上で、今後のCatalyst提案や予算議論において、\r\n\t•\tこの2030 Visionのどの戦略ピラーに貢献するのか\r\n\t•\tどのような公共性や持続性をもたらすのか\r\n\t•\tCardanoらしい差別化にどう寄与するのか\r\n\r\nという問いを、建設的かつ柔軟に用いていきたいと考えています。\r\n\r\n\r\n5. 結論\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、私はSIPO DRepとして本Info Actionに\r\n「Yes（条件付き賛成）」を投じます。\r\n\r\nこの提案はCardanoを縛るための文書ではなく、\r\nコミュニティ全体が同じ地図を共有しながら議論するための出発点です。\r\n\r\n私はこのVisionを、「固定された答え」ではなく、\r\n進化し続ける共通言語として育てていくことを支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmc7G7g38qd4Nd1VztELpUrvKQngjyB7ZfUQaZjinDdHA7 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious DRep supports the Cardano 2030 Vision and Strategy Framework to provide the ecosystem with the strategic discipline required for mature decentralized governance. Our \"Yes\" vote is based on three key factors:\r\n• A Strategic Measuring Stick: This framework provides DReps with a community-vetted filter to evaluate future treasury withdrawals. It ensures that resource allocation is prioritized for initiatives that drive measurable impact toward our 2030 goals.\r\n• Community-Led Legitimacy: The proposal is the result of an exhaustive, bottom-up process involving over 700 participants. This inclusive foundation ensures the vision reflects the collective intent of the ecosystem, rather than a top-down mandate.\r\n• Differentiation & Focus: By defining five clear pillars—Infrastructure, Adoption, Governance, Community, and Sustainability—Cardano moves beyond technical milestones toward a purpose-driven mission to power global economies and mission-critical applications.\r\nThis document serves as a vital \"living\" starting point that empowers the community to navigate the next decade with clarity, accountability, and unified purpose.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPrLymf3TZ6yM6fRjUkJaptAnwTjZSS3dfmtf3DKcAbN9 -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSTORM Partners votes YES on the Cardano 2030: Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs Info Action. We have followed this work firsthand through our participation in the process and have seen the volume and quality of community input across multiple workshops and feedback cycles. Cardano is entering heavier governance and treasury decision cycles, and doing so without a shared direction and a baseline set of KPIs creates a real coordination and fragmentation risk. We agree with critics that the KPI layer is still light and some definitions are too loose, making parts of it vulnerable to vanity metrics, but that is a reason to harden v1, not to block it. This is an Info Action, not a spend authorization, so approving an imperfect first version has limited downside in our view, while the upside is immediate by giving the wider community a common reference to pressure-test proposals for strategic fit starting now.\r\nWe also view the proposed high-value verticals as illustrative and non-exclusive signals of current focus, not as fixed or permanent constraints on innovation or future opportunity for Cardano. They should be treated as hypotheses that can evolve with data, market feedback, and changing conditions, rather than hard boundaries. We will treat this framework as one input, not a gatekeeping tool or checklist for all governance decision-making, and we expect follow-on updates, from both the Product Committee’s newly elected members and the wider Cardano community, to add clearer definitions, baselines, and higher-signal metrics around delivery quality, accountability, and sustainability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Talos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNcJv5tZ68wu5rQ9ESrRUkHkhXTQzjrXRLNLVWSEN7dXB -->\r\n# Talos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano 2030 Vision, Mission, Strategy Framework and KPIs\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfqt3wt0v2uvhawx9anzfqty4x7gwwu04wzr9ucga4yd7mct7dup8`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\ni’m voting no because this reads like a brochure: big claims, low specificity. “most secure” and “mission critical” are fine goals, but dreps can’t use goals to allocate capital.\r\n\r\nif the kpis aren’t defined in a way that resists sybils, wash activity, and mercenary liquidity, then the “measuring stick” becomes a scoreboard you can cheat.\r\n\r\nbring it back with:\r\n\r\nkpi definitions + data sources + anti-gaming rules\r\nexplicit tradeoffs (what gets deprioritized)\r\nclean process legitimacy (who approved, who maintains, how changes happen)\r\nright idea. not tight enough to ratify.",
      "vote": "NO"
