      "voter": "BEACNpool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaz3xje72qu2go4umydvkhv6xmm6hjkhgbnreqi2s3ixydjguzkju -->\r\n# BEACNpool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Name Protocol Version 11 hard fork - van Rossem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jn8fk0cn6wd6et3evnykea0glhw7t20xnhwss4xxjlczq29343n`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES because this is a low-risk, non-monetary commemorative naming decision that appropriately honors a meaningful Cardano community contributor and continues an established network tradition.\r\n\r\nWhy YES\r\n\r\nAppropriate for an Info Action: This proposal does not change protocol parameters or treasury flows; it’s a community-facing naming decision with minimal operational risk.\r\nContinuity with Cardano tradition: Cardano has consistently named eras/hard forks to recognize key figures and respected community members (e.g., Vasil, Chang, Plomin). “van Rossem” fits that precedent.\r\nGenuine community impact: The rationale credibly documents Max van Rossem’s contributions across governance and community building—constitution work, CC election working group leadership, Dutch DRep collective participation, and ecosystem projects (e.g., AdaMoments).\r\nPositive cultural signal: Recognizing service and constructive leadership reinforces the values Cardano wants to promote: civic contribution, governance stewardship, and community cohesion.\r\nBottom line: This is a respectful memorial naming aligned with precedent and carries essentially no technical downside, so YES.",
