    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA084-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Name Protocol Version 11 hard fork - van Rossem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança \"Name Protocol Version 11 hard fork - van Rossem\" (gov_action13pzmlsmmktmfareqpl3gzj9nm63ugwvmp3y7urkjhd8rf89tn6msq95mp3f), pois ela preserva e reforça a tradição da Cardano de homenagear pessoas que contribuíram de forma excepcional para o ecossistema. Max van Rossem teve um papel decisivo em marcos fundamentais da governança, promovendo debates e melhorias em momentos críticos, como a elaboração da primeira Constituição da Cardano e o estabelecimento do primeiro Comitê Constitucional. Além disso, em sua atuação como DRep, fortaleceu sua comunidade ao conectar pessoas e iniciativas relevantes para o ecossistema. Dar seu nome ao hard fork do Protocolo 11 agrega um valor simbólico e histórico importante, representando um gesto de gratidão, reconhecimento e memória comunitária.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action \"Name Protocol Version 11 hard fork - van Rossem\" (gov_action13pzmlsmmktmfareqpl3gzj9nm63ugwvmp3y7urkjhd8rf89tn6msq95mp3f), as it upholds Cardano’s tradition of honoring individuals who have made exceptional contributions to the ecosystem. Max van Rossem played a decisive role in key governance milestones, fostering discussions and improvements during critical moments, such as the drafting of the first Cardano Constitution and the establishment of the first Constitutional Committee. Furthermore, in his role as a DRep, he strengthened his community by connecting people and initiatives across the ecosystem. Naming the Protocol Version 11 hard fork after him adds significant symbolic and historical value, serving as an expression of gratitude, recognition, and collective memory within the Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTYFMucgeYHg5H4f4nCKA2MiDjTV8ewM6WiyuvDuxQEdF -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Name Protocol Version 11 hard fork - van Rossem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis governance action proposes naming Cardano Protocol Version 11 the “van Rossem Hard Fork” in memory of Max van Rossem, a respected contributor to the Cardano community and its governance foundations.\r\n\r\nRCADA recognises that naming hard forks has long served as a symbolic tradition within Cardano, reflecting milestones in the protocol’s evolution while honouring individuals whose contributions have had lasting impact. This proposal continues that tradition and has received broad support across the DRep community.\r\n\r\nMax van Rossem made meaningful contributions to Cardano’s governance development, including constitutional discussions, participation in the Constitutional Convention, and sustained community representation through the Dutch DRep Collective. He also contributed to the election process of the first fully community-elected Constitutional Committee and supported governance coordination efforts that will continue to shape the network’s future.\r\n\r\nFrom a governance perspective, this action is intentionally narrow in scope, constitutionally neutral, and non-precedent-expanding beyond the continuation of an established naming practice. It does not affect protocol rules, treasury access, or governance authority, and therefore does not raise concerns related to guardrails, fiscal discipline, or decentralisation resilience.\r\n\r\nRCADA also acknowledges the broader community sentiment expressed by many DReps in support of this proposal and supports the naming in that spirit. For these reasons, RCADA votes **YES**.\r\n\r\nRCADA's full vote assessment can be found here:  \r\nhttps://brolloks.github.io/rcada-drep-votes/",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiahflfeivfvkdh2lh5iympafetpunbd74wqhxedsvsd55fjcz2pq4 -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Name Protocol Version 11 hard fork - van Rossem\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis does not require an extensive rationale. Thank you to Intersect for putting forward the name of a valued community member for this, and I certainly support this governance action.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
