    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXJww65Yj3Aw2yrxnjNK9JYPakYZPcjXbJ6sc36ufcwq8 -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳5M for Cardano's Global Listing Expansion - Powered by Snek\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI own Snek, and recognize what they do for Cardano. This will likely go down as unconstitutional. My NO vote is because this proposal crosses a fuzzy line between private enterprise and public Cardano infra investment. If I were ever to vote YES on a proposal like this, there would have to be a direct return on investment back to the Treasury.",
