      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSUqCNxC6ygZVGXCSPDpyLPuySEEAvGgmqprSWqFFSnDy -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn the flawed off-chain voting exercise directed by Intersect earlier this year, which I nevertheless participated in to remain a constructive Cardano governance participant, I upvoted all items touching on Cardano's core technology. All of them put together, even if we included the excessive asks of Input Output's proposals, remained within an amount of spending (~150m ADA) that I deemed acceptable. I am currently heavily on the fence with regards to lending further support to IO whenever their proposals come out, but that makes supporting all the remaining non-IO tech proposals by groups like MLabs all the easier. This one in particular is a very modest ask, for a very critical part of the technological ecosystem around Cardano. Support with no further questions asked.",
