    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdqrFS7Nra3gJJyyzViRBokztXTR4RbUSdrCPtzUqyVNr -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA couple of months ago, I supported the resolution to bundle all of the Intersect Budget Proposals into 1 or 2 formal on-chain governance votes.\r\n\r\nEach of these proposals has already undergone extensive scrutiny and received 50% or greater support from the active DReps in the ecosystem, and I will honor that prior decision and the work these prospective developers have put in by voting yes on all the proposals from the Intersect Budget team.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaBofKb7nM9RqKVfohBzv8LoyfwYFDJGGfFPUs5Rd2QJ4 -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting No on the proposal to withdraw ₳45,217 from the Treasury for MLabs’ maintenance and enhancement of Cardano.nix. While I recognize the importance of infrastructure tooling like Cardano.nix, this proposal lacks the strategic urgency or ecosystem-wide justification to merit direct Treasury funding. The requested work—focused on maintenance, enhancements, and documentation—is valuable but better suited for Project Catalyst, where iterative tooling improvements can be more directly aligned with developer needs and community feedback. Treasury funds should be reserved for initiatives with broad, long-term protocol impact and clear governance alignment. This proposal, while well-intentioned, does not meet that threshold at this time.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbLdM8bmGkhqKMvtPMC1zopd3kvNAPPSrJ37Cp8NoRxEQ -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFrom a strategic governance perspective, I question whether this proposal aligns optimally with the timing and thematic focus of the broader Catalyst funding rounds. Catalyst’s iterative funding cycles are designed to empower community-driven innovation and rapid adaptation. Given that Cardano.nix is a toolset with active community engagement and evolving requirements, it may benefit from the iterative feedback loops and dynamic prioritization facilitated by Catalyst 14 rather than a fixed budget allocation through Intersect. This could enhance community oversight, foster broader stakeholder input, and potentially unlock complementary contributions or enhancements from the wider developer ecosystem.\r\n\r\nMoreover, integrating this funding into Catalyst could reinforce the principle of decentralized decision-making by allowing the community to evaluate the proposal’s evolving impact in real time. This would also align with our collective imperative to adopt a business-minded governance approach—making strategic choices that optimize treasury utilization while safeguarding the protocol’s long-term stability.\r\n\r\nI support the necessity of this work and recognize its critical role in Cardano’s infrastructure. Yet, I advocate for a governance model that leverages Catalyst’s adaptive funding mechanisms to ensure the community remains actively engaged in shaping the evolution of foundational tools like Cardano.nix. This is not merely a question of funding but of embedding accountability, transparency, and strategic agility into the heart of our treasury disbursements. Only through such disciplined, community-centric stewardship can we secure Cardano’s future as the most decentralized and scalable PoS network in the world.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXQnMiKokMzkDyY5Ts7xL39rg1ve6Fn1FLkCayM9343nL -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMLabs is an exceptional team that actively supports and contributes to Cardano's core infrastructure. I will support all their proposals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUaC2Tnmuy8XnxZ5CCdoRGcTBPxrpewB9MfDTszCiqmHX -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI plan to vote Yay on the Cardano.nix treasury withdrawal proposal for ₳45,217 because it supports a tool critical for maintaining reliable infrastructure used by key ecosystem components, including the Daedalus Wallet, which I personally rely on. The modest funding amount is reasonable for ensuring compatibility with Cardano node updates, fixing bugs, and enhancing usability for stake pool operators (SPOs), developers, and enterprises like IOG. This aligns with Cardano’s goal of robust infrastructure, as emphasized in the Cardano Foundation’s 2023 Financial Insights Report. However, I have caveats: the proposal lacks clear data on Cardano.nix’s user base or adoption beyond niche users like IOG and Daedalus, making it hard to gauge its broader ecosystem impact. Additionally, Nix’s specialized nature may limit its appeal, and the proposal could benefit from metrics demonstrating its necessity. Despite these concerns, the low cost and direct benefit to tools I use justify my support, though I encourage more transparency on usage in future proposals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Voice of the People",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DRepVoiceOfThePeople/VOP_Repo/refs/heads/main/VC20250717MLabsCoreToolCardanonix.jsonld -->\r\n# Voice of the People\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ecrj7jd9alaxumvm49hgng9rp239nda5ucegd05ndvxfqftwr9f`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt is necessary for maintaining critical Nix-based infrastructure, ensuring node compatibility and reliability with future developments",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Intersect_TWGA1.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: This is a general rationale we have prepared to support our “yes” vote on all the 39 treasury withdrawal actions. This follows careful review and consideration of the metadata of these treasury withdrawal proposals and hence is not a blanket voting practice.\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep Committee, have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawal governance actions currently live on-chain and submitted under the administration of IntersectMBO. These actions are the necessary implementation step following the community's approval of the ₳275.3 million Cardano Ecosystem Budget, the necessary budget info action that precedes the treasury withdrawal process. Our support reflects not only continuity with our earlier \"yes\" votes on the overarching budget info action and its constituent proposals but also our confidence in the smart contract guide and project execution mechanisms Intersect has established as an administrative body for these proposals.\r\n\r\nEach of these 39 withdrawals corresponds directly to proposals that have already passed a respective Budget Info Action with wide community and DRep support of 64.23%. As Wada DRep, we reviewed, scored, and supported many of these initiatives during the budgeting phase, using our internal ₳280M Net Change Limit framework. Our endorsement of the full ₳275.3M package was not a blanket approval but the outcome of detailed deliberation. Therefore, we see it as our responsibility to honor those community-approved funding decisions by affirming these follow-up Treasury withdrawal governance actions.\r\n\r\nImportantly, we are confident in Intersect’s role as the administrator of these treasury disbursements. We have independently reviewed the Smart Contract Guide, disbursement architecture, and accountability structures associated with these withdrawals. The use of milestone-gated smart contracts, multi-signature treasuries, and on-chain/off-chain tracking mechanisms provides strong assurance of transparency, risk management, and community accountability. We are particularly satisfied that Intersect has adopted security-audited contract templates and provides public documentation on how treasury funds will be administered, paused if necessary, and even returned if unused.\r\n\r\nIn our view, rejecting or abstaining from these Treasury Withdrawals at this stage would risk destabilizing delivery timelines, undermining community trust, and introducing administrative conflicts that may violate the spirit of the Constitution’s Articles on budgeting. We believe that treasury funding is not just about allocation; it’s about consistent and credible execution. As such, the DRep role requires continuity and follow-through, especially when prior voting outcomes have clearly mandated action.\r\n\r\nTherefore, in alignment with our constitutional responsibilities, community-aligned decision-making, and our assessment of Intersect’s administrative protocols, we have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawals Governance Actions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/18_2_default.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm defaulting to voting yes because there is some degree of consensus already achieved on each of these. So unless I have a significant issue with one of these proposals I will be voting yes on it.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Yoroi_Cardano%20Nix.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nYoroi votes YES to support the continued maintenance and improvement of Cardano.nix by MLabs. \r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nReproducible Infrastructure: Cardano.nix simplifies building and deploying Cardano nodes and infrastructure with Nix, ensuring reproducibility and reducing configuration errors for SPOs and developers.\r\n\r\nAdopted by Key Stakeholders: The tool is already used by major Cardano ecosystem players like IOG and the Daedalus team, indicating its established importance.\r\n\r\nProvide High Impact: The proposal is focused, clearly scoped, and led by a capable team (MLabs) with a reliable track record in ecosystem tooling and DevOps.\r\n\r\nYoroi believes the continuity of infrastructure tools like Cardano.nix is essential for a stable and scalable Cardano ecosystem. Supporting this initiative aligns with our value of fostering open-source reliability and developer-friendly environments.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUNsjSzMu4HfpytqRLvRcbFMYVzsgH4R2GtH3PkP4mZW5 -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Cardano.nix\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote as necessary to help Cardano grow into a platform that supports the economic identities of billions of people. This proposal charges a fair price to achieve what is needed to achieve that. \r\n\r\nThere are no significant matters that affect the neutrality of my decision-making.\r\n\r\nDetailed rationale and the improvements I would like to see made to the proposal are attached in the following spreadsheet \"TW vote #01\" or PDF.\r\n\r\nSpecifically with regards to bundled proposals, next time I would request that one of the following be implemented:\r\n\r\n1. Bundled proposals should be subject to a temperature check vote for each item. \r\n2. I would like bundled proposals to be verified or created by entities, consortia, or individuals selected by the DRep.\r\n\r\nSpreadsheet:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1M8JAuAntJOa7Z6j3GfC2hWFl4kbZLkzEel_cN4-kymw/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nPDF:\r\nipfs://bafkreianp5xhbo3ojlxqjjah4kyimr6u62uwnxd2t3lwwu3qmpn4jf4n5a\r\n\r\n私はCardanoが数十億人の経済アイデンティティを支えるプラットフォームへ成長していくために必要な投票を行います。この提案書は、それを達成するために必要な事項を実現するための正当なコストを請求しています。\r\n\r\n私の意思決定の中立性に影響を与える重大な事項はありません。\r\n\r\n根拠の詳細と、提案書について私が改善して欲しい点は、次のスプレッドシートの「TW vote #01」またはPDFに添付されています。\r\n\r\n特に、バンドル型提案書に関しては、次回は、次のいずれかが実施されることをリクエストします。\r\n1. バンドル型提案書は、内訳別の温度チェックの投票を行うこと。\u20282. バンドル型提案書は、DRepにより選出されるエンティティやコンソーシアムや個人により、検証または作成されるようにして欲しいと思います。\r\n\r\nSpreadsheet:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1M8JAuAntJOa7Z6j3GfC2hWFl4kbZLkzEel_cN4-kymw/edit?usp=sharing\r\n\r\nPDF:\r\nipfs://bafkreianp5xhbo3ojlxqjjah4kyimr6u62uwnxd2t3lwwu3qmpn4jf4n5a",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    }
  ],
  "2025 Cardano NCL": [
    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/gov_action10k0unljvaej0kd89w7pn0zkgdx59c7xkl0x5q78dzvdtd73u0kmqq5xl5y5.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n200,000,000 ADA is a much more reasonable spending limit than what has been proposed previously. As we are looking at a half-year budget at this late point in 2025, 200m ensures there won't be excessive spending.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "$Khale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CFMatrix/Metadata-storage/refs/heads/main/2025_200M_NCL_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# $Khale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ltat8kjqrmnff3lkkpxy0j5tn66d3m0gy64dc92asft5g6dl9ws`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGiven the current state of the Cardano ecosystem, I believe the proposed NCL amount is a far more practical option compared to previous iterations presented thus far.\r\n\r\nWhile a 200M NCL leaves little room for anything beyond core research, development, and operations in 2025, I am convinced this focus is precisely where our attention should be in the short to medium term.\r\n\r\nAs a community now fully responsible for the direction, scale, and pace of the ecosystem’s expansion and evolution, we must ensure a robust and comprehensive framework of policies, procedures, infrastructure, and auditing is in place before allocating significant resources to areas we are currently unprepared or unable to support.\r\n\r\nThis approach should be a priority across all areas of the ecosystem but is particularly critical for administration, governance, and funding, which currently lack substance, quality, and transparency.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "42",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ada42btc/DRepADA/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_gov_0003.jsonld -->\r\n# 42\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26ppxzudkhtak4y7kc2rag9ezq7szje78aetxge3pg5w7qwthkqv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe need to pass the budget for this year.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "8Ball",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVqzaBSfzM3cPZgus883MqYv2pPPtayPqSkv7N9EbKGhV -->\r\n# 8Ball\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y296zyw2r8rcsy7slkd7l687hh88xc0m6ac2y3h2r3mvsdgc9q6yy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe current immaturity and inconsistency of the voting process reinforce my commitment to fiscal conservatism. During the current Eckklesia Budget Poll, I supported proposals totaling approximately 196 million ada, which aligns with a more restrained spending approach.\r\nSetting a lower Net Change Limit (NCL) creates greater accountability and incentivizes proposers to deliver transparent bids. It also reinforces community oversight and discourages poorly justified allocations.\r\nThe argument that the NCL is \"just a limit\" and can be set higher is not persuasive. Accepting this reasoning opens the door to arbitrary increases, including the full use of the 350 million ada cap. This concern has already materialized in a plan to submit budgets that aim to use the entire 350 million ada.\r\nI voted No on the 2025 NCL of 350M ada, and while I voted Yes on the 2025–2026 NCL of 300M ada, this was done while expressing a preference for a lower limit of 200 million ada.\r\nI now cast a clear Yes vote for a 2025 NCL of 200 million ada, consistent with my belief in responsible treasury management.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "A Diamond",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Andre-Diamond/drep-repo/refs/heads/main/vote_context/2025/05_01_a/Vote_Context.jsonId -->\r\n# A Diamond\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt85v0tczccl7aj84sjg0cl0y9mgvnhna5e0dw8k6zsgqrczqmfgu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVery much agree with continuing to grow the treasury, especially in these early governance stages. 200 million is more than enough for a start",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaLovelace777",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/NCL-5.5.25/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(17).jsonld -->\r\n# AdaLovelace777\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygehgu65kchqm929zp69xhl06hqkpcjv0rzy44sx40qhufqgh3xv2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted No for the two prior Net Change Limits because we should not be allowed to withdrawal such a large portion of the Ada that we take in for the year. In that reasoning I suggested we save close to 50% of the fees we take in every year, since this is the first year of our governance experiment. We must be cautious and try to spend as little as possible like any wise person does. We must set a strong precedent early on. I am ecstatic to vote Yes for a proposal that I couldn't have written better myself. The only thing I would change is to make it 150 million Ada, but in negotiations, both sides have to give in a little. 200 million is a lot better than 350 million, especially when the year is 33% over. I hope we spend a lot less than the maximum we can withdrawal, then we could set the 2026 NCL for 200 million again, or hopefully less. The more savings, the better. Thank you all for voting No on the two prior NCL proposals. This one was worth the wait.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVANCvc4qEPBhznG4htmasmL5fofDyZxe7kq8QHT14HnA -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI believe an NCL of 200M represents a conservative limit that protects the long term interests of the Cardano Community yet supports mission critical investments.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Agora-Cardano/dRep_metadata_storage/refs/heads/main/Governance_Actions/NCL_200M.jsonld -->\r\n# Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9dq806jcm56wzhnv2yrf6gcyq7h4gap8gxewfykk0dtfs7vf843`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nComo dRep, voto NÃO na ação de governança para definição do NCL em 200M ADA. Apoio o NCL atual de 350M e aceitaria 250M-300M, mas só com  fatores condicionantes:\r\n\r\n1 Limite por entidade\r\n\r\nPara evitar o monopólio da IOG e garantir equilíbrio na alocação de recursos para a comunidade.\r\n(ex.: 50% do NCL total vigente)\r\n\r\n2 Limite por proposta\r\n\r\nPara evitar agrupamento de trabalhos diferentes dentro de uma única proposta (a.k.a bundling)\r\n\r\n(Ex.: Orçamento da proposta solicitado pela Entidade, Grupo ou Indivíduo < 10% do NCL total vigente) Isso reduziria a quantia máxima por proposta e desistimula bundling.\r\n\r\nPorém, tais fatores condicionantes poderiam ser considerados inconstitucionais, é uma área cinzenta aparentemente, por isso também estou sendo leniente a um orçamento maior em 2025.\r\n\r\nPor que rejeitar 200M ADA?\r\n\r\nUm NCL de 200M ADA sufocaria a comunidade, direcionando quase todo orçamento do tesouro  disponível em 2025 para a IOG (+190M ADA pedidos para Core Dev, Catalyst e Research).\r\n\r\nA IOG se mostrou irredutível a revisar seu orçamento, e a maioria dos dReps mesmo assim sinalizaram apoio, perpetuando a centralização e ignorando as necessidades do ecossistema de descentralização no desenvolvimento do core.\r\n\r\nO orçamento do Project Catalyst deve cair de 150M para 60M ADA/ano, impactando projetos essenciais e centenas de contribuidores que dependem desses fundos. Um NCL de 200M pioraria isso, limitando dApps, inovações e adoção. O NCL de 350M, embora não ideal sem limites por entidade, dá mais espaço para a comunidade crescer em 2025.\r\n\r\nPreocupações:  \r\n\r\nMonopólio:\r\n\r\nIOG domina (+90% dos pedidos). Um limite percentual por entidade é crucial para descentralizar recursos e apoiar projetos diversos.  \r\n\r\nTransparência:\r\n\r\nEntidades fundadoras (IOG, Emurgo, Cardano Foundation) devem divulgar gastos, reservas e fornecer dados financeiros mais transparentes para que a comunidade avalie se estão usando suas próprias reservas de maneira apropriada antes de acessarem o tesouro, que pertence a todos.\r\n\r\nConflitos:\r\n\r\nTodos os dReps têm conflito de interesses em algum nível. Quem apoia NCL maior pode buscar recursos para projetos pessoais; quem apoia NCL menor teme que quedas no preço de ADA desvalorizem os próprios investimentos. Iniciativas privadas, como parcerias com VCs, reduziriam a dependência do tesouro e esses conflitos.  \r\n\r\nTransição Lenta:\r\n\r\nNão há modelo claro para transferir o desenvolvimento da IOG à comunidade, o que perpetua a dependência e atrasa a descentralização.\r\n\r\nTesouro a Longo Prazo:\r\n\r\nA sustentabilidade do tesouro é crucial, mas não cabe nesta ação pontual de 2025, que já deveria ter sido resolvida. O foco agora é o orçamento imediato; a sustentabilidade deve ser discutida em outra ação de governança.\r\n\r\nPossiveis Soluções:  \r\n\r\n- Estabelecer um limite por entidade (50%) para evitar monopólios e garantir justiça na alocação de recursos do tesouro.\r\n\r\n- Implementar contratos de vesting para vendas de ADA oriundas do tesouro, minimizando pressão vendedora e protegendo o preço.  \r\n\r\n- Financiar simulações de impacto no preço do ADA para embasar decisões futuras.  \r\n\r\n- Exigir transparência das entidades fundadoras sobre gastos e reservas antes delas requisitarem recursos do tesouro.\r\n\r\n- Criar um modelo claro de transição para passar o desenvolvimento à comunidade, acelerando a descentralização.  \r\n\r\n- Incentivar financiamento privado (ex.: VCs, parcerias) para reduzir dependência do tesouro e fomentar sustentabilidade.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaGbcPjAnPJy9UqXotamzqQKnseveM1juspkg1QLwENXC -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nこのガバナンスアクション自体の意図には一定の理解を示すべきだとは思いますが、すでに次の期間（2025/3/26～2025/4/25）で提出された「2025 Net Change Limit」ガバナンスアクションが、DRep（76.18%）とICC（66.67%）によって可決されており、私も賛成票を投じています。純変動上限が確定しない限り次のステップには進めず、制度の停滞は避けるべきだと考えています。このタイミングで改めて別のNCLが提出される理由については理解できなくはありませんが、すでに可決された上限を尊重し、いまは次に進むべきだと考えています。以上を踏まえ、私はこの「2025 Cardano NCL」には反対票を投じます。\\n\\nWhile I recognize the intent behind this governance action, the \"2025 Net Change Limit\" governance action submitted during the period of March 26, 2025 to April 25, 2025 has already been approved by DReps (76.18%) and ICC (66.67%), and I also voted in favor of it. Without a confirmed Net Change Limit, we cannot proceed to the next steps, and I believe it is important to avoid governance stagnation. Although I can understand why a different NCL proposal is being submitted at this timing, I believe we should respect the already approved limit and move forward. Given these circumstances, I will vote against this \"2025 Cardano NCL.\"",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AltcoinOracle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfWKL7TqACAspAJtiE8rEBuWTjqAd3Quo4wGv4t9YgD4P -->\r\n# AltcoinOracle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygvgk3899qm38zth07z5clhfjvzfhe2mf2kvkqrfxp93r5srjre5s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes because we should be cautious for this first governance experiment. Setting a 200M ADA NCL allows us to start tight, protect the Treasury, and fund essential growth responsibly. This approach gives the community time to mature its budgeting and auditing processes.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ArcadianComputers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZgGUMjsvk1xqR2AnFrJSrG2E6ZTAfLRGsfT83mGBin1V -->\r\n# ArcadianComputers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg7xcypymvedd0nn2gcn3zhwhv2d25nfteuxs9re5a7j97c3v4dxw`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe need Treasury withdrawals for the continued maintenance and growth of the Cardano ecosystem. The constitution mandates the establishment of an NCL before any Treasury funds can be withdrawn. Without an approved NCL, the Treasury can't be used for its intended purpose. We have witnessed the NCL size wars and we appreciate the nuanced debate from all involved DReps, but we have to start somewhere. The NCL is a maximum spend limit, not a minimum spending requirement. Whichever value ultimately gets chosen, hitting that limit will still require voting to do so. Getting past the first hurdle is more important.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "benzio",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/boulayo/dRepBenzio/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# benzio\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwge9pgkeyd5eawz4y07mvkt09jkmx9d2levdzdcr6xl7s2nr4hy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIMHO there shouldn't be a \"treasury\" at all.\r\nBitcoin do not need a treasury.\r\nThe ecosystem should be substained with investments and volontary participation, not with \"taxes\" on transactions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Brent_Norris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DragonsBloodKush/ada/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context-gov-action-200m-ncl.jsonld -->\r\n# Brent_Norris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytqpw3yqgfw57vlx8sf7vevzgl8ksgdfjzqs9ducesyx99cwszkxj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis gov action is to set the NCL for 2025, Epoch 532 to the end of Epoch 604. The Net Change Limit would be 200M ADA. \r\n\r\nI'm glad I/we waited for a smaller NCL proposal.\r\n1. Smarter decisions can be made when the mind is free to focus on something besides how much money is in the treasury. It's a flavor of freedom. \r\n2. I promised conservative voting and I believe $200m is low enough to keep everyone focused on conservation of funds and doing more with less whenever possible.\r\n2. A larger treasury can be a deciding factor for sustainability. Blockchain is still a highly volatile industry. 99% of the same players kept their jobs at the SEC. Cardano must remain prepared to weather any storm at any time. Central banks currently have a large financial advantage in lobbying, the SEC, IMF, etc.\r\n\r\nI hope the world sees and experiences the enormous value that developers and others have built into Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BTBF_XSP",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTP3C1HEN49TyMVhJi9Xix38Bxs9S6keMeUCsx9LGgLx8 -->\r\n# BTBF_XSP\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2vyrqh0fa4qh4tmy7322va6ryk78uh6szppezaft0watyqp5hdwx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I agree with some of the arguments for a 200M ADA NCL, I voted No because the budget proposal I supported this term was for 250M ADA. Even though only half of 2025 remains, I believe 200M is a bit too low.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/DRepdata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context20250503.jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私はDRepとして、Net Change Limit（NCL）を200M ADAに制限する提案に反対（NO）票を投じました。\r\n 現在のCardanoは、Ouroboros Leios、Hydra、Midnight、Chain State、Bullet、AtlasといったCardano 2.0を構成する中核技術が同時に立ち上がる重要な転換点にあります。このような「初動期」には、個々の技術を孤立的に評価するのではなく、全体として技術的調和（technical harmony）を保ちつつ開発を進める柔軟な資金設計が不可欠です。\r\n 今回のNCL提案──すなわち「年間の財務変動上限を200M ADAに設定する」──は、そのような現実的資金需要と乖離していると判断しました。\r\n 第一に、Cardano Treasuryには既に年間約350M ADAのインフローがあり、200M ADAの上限はその6割弱に過ぎません。これは「健全な節度」ではなく、拡張期における機会損失のリスクを孕んでいます。\r\n 第二に、2025年予算ReconciliationでのDRep投票の傾向からも、実需は200M ADAを大きく超えていたことが明らかです。YES票が集まった提案群の合算規模だけでも300M ADAを超えており、PragmaやDC Spark、World Mobileといった多様な実装主体への期待が現れています。分散的エコシステムにおいては、資金需要もまた分散し、単一の低上限では成長機会を阻害します。\r\n 加えて、SolanaやzkSyncなど競合プロジェクトは、すでに数億ドル規模の成長予算を投入しており、スピードと資本力の両面で先行しています。Cardanoが競争優位を確立するには、「守り」ではなく「攻め」の投資姿勢が必要です。\r\n 以上を踏まえ、私は今回のNCL案にNO票を投じました。\r\n この立場は、2025年Cardano予算Reconciliationにおける私の投票傾向とも整合しています。私は194件中137件（約71%）にYES票を投じました。内訳は以下の通りです：\r\n- 「Core」（基盤技術・スケーラビリティ）…41件  \r\n- 「Marketing & Innovation」（RWA、ステーブルコイン等）…52件  \r\n- 「Governance Support」（Voltaire、GovTool支援）…13件  \r\n- 「Research」（中長期開発・標準化）…12件  \r\n- 「No Category」（AIRA等 地域戦略）…5件  \r\n- 「Advance Support」（SPO支援等）…2件  \r\n 私はすべての提案を以下の6つの基準に基づいて評価しました：\r\n1. Cardano 2.0に不可欠な技術的中核（Leios、Hydra、Midnight等）  \r\n2. GovToolを起点とする分散型ガバナンス機構の成熟  \r\n3. RWAやステーブルコインを通じた制度的実装への接続  \r\n4. AIRAなど公共性ある地域戦略の支援  \r\n5. 短期実装可能性と中長期的な持続性の両立  \r\n6. 成果目標と測定指標（contract-based clarity）の明確さ  \r\n 今回のNCL案は単なる財務枠ではなく、Cardanoの成長に対するスタンスを問う政治的選択です。私は、Cardanoが調和と競争力を備えたエコシステムとして進化するためには、柔軟かつ戦略的な予算執行能力を持つべきと考え、本提案には反対票を投じます。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I cast a NO vote on the proposal to cap the Net Change Limit (NCL) at 200 million ADA.\r\n\r\nCardano is currently at a pivotal turning point, where multiple core technologies that constitute Cardano 2.0—such as Ouroboros Leios, Hydra, Midnight, Chain State, Bullet, and Atlas—are being launched simultaneously. During such an early-stage phase, it is essential not to evaluate each technology in isolation, but rather to enable integrated development with technical harmony. This requires a funding design that is both sufficiently sized and flexible.\r\n\r\nFrom this perspective, the NCL proposal—which would set the annual treasury spending cap at 200M ADA—was, in my view, misaligned with actual funding needs.\r\n\r\nFirst, the Cardano Treasury already sees annual inflows of around 350M ADA. Setting a ceiling at 200M ADA means utilizing less than 60% of available funds. This is not “fiscal prudence” but rather a limitation that risks missing growth opportunities.\r\n\r\nSecond, the outcome of the 2025 Budget Reconciliation showed that actual demand far exceeds 200M ADA. The total requested amount for proposals that received majority YES votes easily surpassed 300M ADA, demonstrating strong expectations across diverse implementing entities such as Pragma, DC Spark, and World Mobile. In a decentralized ecosystem, funding demands are naturally distributed, and a single rigid cap can easily become a bottleneck for growth.\r\n\r\nMoreover, ecosystems like Solana and zkSync have already deployed hundreds of millions of dollars in growth funding, gaining a lead in both speed and capital strength. To remain competitive, Cardano must adopt an offensive investment posture, not a defensive one.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I voted NO on the NCL proposal.\r\n\r\nThis position is also consistent with my voting behavior during the 2025 Cardano Budget Reconciliation. I supported 137 out of 194 proposals (approximately 71%). The breakdown is as follows:\r\n\r\n- Core (infrastructure, scalability): 41 proposals  \r\n- Marketing & Innovation (RWA, stablecoins, integrations): 52 proposals  \r\n- Governance Support (Voltaire, GovTool): 13 proposals  \r\n- Research (long-term development and standardization): 12 proposals  \r\n- No Category (regional initiatives like AIRA): 5 proposals  \r\n- Advance Support (SPO engagement): 2 proposals  \r\n\r\nAll proposals were evaluated against the following six criteria:\r\n\r\n1. Whether they advance the core technical foundations of Cardano 2.0 (e.g., Leios, Hydra, Midnight)  \r\n2. Whether they strengthen decentralized governance, especially around GovTool  \r\n3. Whether they connect Cardano to institutional use cases via RWA and stablecoins  \r\n4. Whether they support public infrastructure and regional diversity, such as AIRA  \r\n5. Whether they balance short-term feasibility with long-term sustainability  \r\n6. Whether they present clear deliverables and metrics (contract-based clarity)  \r\n\r\nThe NCL proposal is not merely a financial parameter—it represents a political choice about Cardano's stance toward growth. I believe that Cardano should evolve into an ecosystem that balances harmony with competitiveness. For that reason, I advocate for strategic and flexible treasury execution, and I voted NO on this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tulibra1510/NCL200M/refs/heads/main/NCL200M.jsonld -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNCL is essential. 2025 is almost halfway through. We need to pass the budget as soon as possible so we can spend time developing the Cardano ecosystem. We fully support this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
