      "voter": "CoinCeylon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CoinCeylon/Drep/refs/heads/main/200MVote1_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# CoinCeylon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfg2u28p4xuh5u5lv839vcfd6k2knptfw0avtefpyw4x3dsu5pu25`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n🚨Decision Update - Coin Ceylon DRep has voted NO on the Cardano governance action “NCL – 200M” - We believe this decision deserves full context. To understand our position and the rationale behind our vote, read more at -🌐 - https://www.coinceylon.com/drep/#our-rationales",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Crypto_Oaj",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/omid235/Crypto_Oaj_DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Crypto_Oaj\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwlmrm6ksc8sa5fdhm63prqve6hjzvghdc3053zwz6hyeg0ayhg2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I am casting a **YES** vote for the **2025 Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Info Action** (Governance Action ID: `gov_action1mmalzkcxpyn33t05hml2hxpwq0ffv6uu4mhe8sv7guz5nmm4afysqlmepzl`). Below is my rationale:\r\n\r\n\r\n✅ Rationale for YES Vote\r\n\r\n 1. **Constitutional Integrity and Threshold Correction**\r\nThis Info Action directly addresses a critical flaw observed in the initial budget process—namely, the misapplication of the **50% + 1 Lovelace threshold**. By recalibrating the threshold against the **active voting stake (5.38B ADA)** rather than overall participation, the proposers restore democratic legitimacy and prevent governance distortion. Only proposals that met the corrected threshold of **2.69B ADA** are included, ensuring majority support and adherence to the **Cardano Constitution’s Article IV**.\r\n\r\n 2. **Empowering Community Builders**\r\nA core purpose of this action is to **lower barriers to entry** for builders and innovators who do not have the 100k ADA deposit required for individual proposal submission. By bundling proposals that surpassed quorum into a collective Info Action, this mechanism enables **grassroots participation** without compromising on quality or support levels. It’s a practical step toward a **more inclusive and decentralized treasury system**.\r\n\r\n 3. **Exclusion of Founding Entities for Fairness**\r\nThe deliberate exclusion of proposals from founding entities (Intersect, IOG, Cardano Foundation, Emurgo), even when they met the threshold, reinforces neutrality and safeguards against **institutional bias**. It sends a strong signal that **no actor is above the process** and that **community-driven proposals** are prioritized within the Net Change Limit (₳350M), in line with constitutional expectations.\r\n\r\n 4. **Clear Alignment with the Net Change Limit (NCL)**\r\nThe combined allocation of ₳7.56M remains well within the ₳350M cap for 2025. The budgeting is **fiscally responsible**, respects **long-term treasury sustainability**, and enables strategic experimentation (e.g., Layer 2 solutions, wallet infrastructure, node performance) without risking overspending.\r\n\r\n 5. **Transparent and Structured Process**\r\nThe entire process—from open submission to off-chain signaling (Ekklesia) to this on-chain Info Action—was handled with a high degree of transparency and community engagement. Proposals were **standardized**, **vetted**, and **backed by data**. This demonstrates maturity in Cardano's evolving governance and strengthens community trust.\r\n\r\n 6. **Real-World Relevance and Ecosystem Impact**\r\nThe proposals funded—such as **zkFold**, **Midgard Optimistic Rollups**, **Blockfrost Platform**, and **Hardware Wallet Maintenance**—align with Cardano’s roadmap in scaling, developer tooling, and security. They represent **tangible progress** in areas where Cardano must remain competitive and developer-friendly.\r\n\r\n ✅ Summary\r\n\r\nThis Info Action exemplifies **constitutional governance in action**—respecting thresholds, protecting the treasury, and empowering builders. It corrects past procedural missteps without disenfranchising the community. By voting **YES**, I support a **transparent, inclusive, and legitimate budgeting process** that aligns with the vision of Voltaire and the values embedded in the Cardano Constitution.\r\n\r\n\r\nOmid | Cardano DRep\r\n“Legitimacy through participation, sustainability through restraint.”",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPFWv4bhawD4pP1ZFfpRr5zyHdXiDLxd58SVZuNVP7YyF -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI previously voted NO on NCL proposals targeting 300–350 million ADA, as I felt those limits were too high for where Cardano governance is today. Ideally, I'd prefer a lower NCL around 100–150 million, and I hope we can look at that properly for 2026.\r\n\r\nThis proposal sets the NCL at 200 million, which is more reasonable given the circumstances. With the time pressure and the need to have an NCL in place to allow Treasury spending, I am voting YES on this proposal. It's not perfect, but it's a sensible step for now to keep Cardano moving forwards. \r\n\r\nI'd also like to thank the proposer(s) for bringing this together at short notice.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "DraculaDAO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dracula-DAO/cardano-drep/refs/heads/main/2025/2025-04-25_Net_Change_Limit_200.jsonld -->\r\n# DraculaDAO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygs99wsy49h9vydggncfeck2xwmngyeltp66pvgzl6jz63s6qmu3p`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDracula DAO strongly supports a conservative approach to budgeting and the lower NCL is better for the ecosystem long-term.  ADA not spent today is ADA available tomorrow when priorities and conditions change.  In general we also believe the treasury should provide funding in the form of incentive grants awarded upon project completion, and not a project's entire operating budget.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dumpling🥟",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeJwWxmCbyXyQNq7PneRA9tzQeeZ3VMjTzeUJmba5MSMw -->\r\n# Dumpling🥟\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rtf58m0lv9spcqx5mads20gpfulf6l97w57ecdy00vjdq0klh4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本次提案将预算上限调整为200M，相较之前的350M大幅降低，体现了更审慎的财务规划\r\n\r\n建立合理的预算上限对开发团队至关重要，这将使团队能够按计划支取Ada资金，确保项目持续、稳定地开发\r\n\r\n尽管我依然期望未来能够建立更完善、更成熟的支出监管机制，但当前阶段通过这一预算上限的设定是项目推进的必要步骤\r\n \r\n综上，投赞成票",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nEMURGO, as a DRep, votes No on this Info Action regarding the 2025 Cardano NCL (7d9fc9fe4cee64fb34e57783378ac869a85c78d6fbcd4078ed131ab6fa3c7db600).\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nEMURGO maintains its voting stance on the 2025 Net Change Limit (9b62b3c632f329016a968ac25211825bb4f84b12461121c7da3aa11df92370f900).\r\n\r\nRepeated attempts to redefine the cap may lead to delays in governance processes, which in turn pose a risk that critical funding will not reach the projects that need it. This could ultimately slow down the development of the Cardano ecosystem.\r\nIn conclusion, the 350M ADA proposed under the 2025 Net Change Limit, and approved by a majority of DReps, represents the maximum amount that can be withdrawn from the Cardano Treasury, but not a fixed amount that must be fully utilized. Therefore, we believe it is sufficient as an initial annual cap.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00010_vote_context_v2.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted NO on gov_action10k0unljvaej0kd89w7pn0zkgdx59c7xkl0x5q78dzvdtd73u0kmqq5xl5y5. 200m NCL for the remainder of 2025 would delay fund allocation for projects other than IOG's.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "FAIR Pool #01",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcsNfgSc2Xw5Aq3qyUcWyWknuqzuTMiUKb4rKAMequKb7 -->\r\n# FAIR Pool #01\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytamqncvuz2r0atkwxwgcn5zmgxm09j0g2lgcrp7ddqfsfcsgnr8s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I strongly support fiscal responsibility and sustainability, I do not support reducing the NCL from 350M to 200M ADA at this time, and thus vote NO on this proposal.\r\n\r\nFirst, I believe the NCL should not be changed frequently without a compelling shift in market, governance, or network conditions. Since the 350M limit was recently approved and no significant change has occurred, lowering it now risks undermining governance stability and the credibility of prior decisions. We must avoid sending the signal that every few months we will re-debate core parameters without new data.\r\n\r\nSecond, while I find 350M ADA somewhat high, I believe 200M ADA may be too restrictive. We need some headroom to accommodate important proposals that may arise later in the year or to adapt to changing market conditions. Development should not stall due to an overly conservative cap.\r\n\r\nThird, the NCL is only a ceiling, not a spending target. Treasury withdrawals still require DRep approval, and I trust the scrutiny and collective judgment of Cardano’s DReps to ensure responsible funding. With these checks in place, a higher cap does not equate to reckless spending, it provides flexibility and responsiveness, not excess.\r\n\r\nLastly, delaying or deferring critical infrastructure, tooling, or governance development at this stage could do long-term damage to Cardano’s competitiveness and momentum. I believe it is wiser to empower responsible growth within the ecosystem than to risk missing critical opportunities due to overly tight funding constraints.\r\n\r\nIn summary, I vote NO to preserve governance consistency, allow for strategic flexibility, and place trust in the decentralized checks already in place to ensure responsible treasury use.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BrianLee12/Cardano-Governance/refs/heads/main/NCL-2025/200M/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting yes for this NCL proposal, as it falls within my personal NCL of 200-250 Million ADA.\r\n\r\nI think this proposed NCL is fiscally responsible based on the budget proposals we have seen from all submitting members.\r\n\r\nI believe it is extremely important to be prudent with our spending in this first year of ADA governance, and I have not been convinced that a spend limit of more than 250 Million ADA is justified in any way.\r\n\r\nIf a NCL proposal of 250 Million ADA is at some point proposed, I will vote yes for that as well, but this proposal satisfies my desires for fiscal responsibility.\r\n\r\nThank you to the proposers who worked together to make this happen and were able to get a NCL that has community support submitted past the unnecessarily high submission threshold of a 100,000 ADA deposit.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Gnobudy Special",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gnobudyspecial/Cardano-dRep/refs/heads/main/NCL%20200%20reduction.jsonld -->\r\n# Gnobudy Special\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygd5gumlv8jnramte9z2zvksvncgt06hyds4k6naq52hq7c05svs5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe just passed an NCL last week with over 70% dRep approval. We now have more work to do with the budget reconciliation process and funding proposals.  But some people are dragging up the NCL discussion again and again and now wasting our time with this. Its annoying. Stop it.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXKkEZPrJ26LGsNkRfp3Z8sggyZDTt2HnoqJCaRDCNXFj -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote NO on this proposal for the following reasons:\r\n\r\n1) 200M ADA is too low to cover the essential budget needs already submitted, including Core Development (IOG), Catalyst, research, and infrastructure projects such as Hydra, ZK, Midgard, Lucid, and Chainlink. The total for these essential items already exceeds 200M ADA.\r\n\r\n2) A low NCL like this would block the approval of critical proposals, even those that are strategic for the growth and security of the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\n3) Reducing the NCL abruptly from the previously approved 350M ADA to 200M ADA creates instability and contradicts the governance direction, especially since there was no prior temperature check or broad community consensus.\r\n\r\n4) Cardano needs to invest meaningfully to stay competitive in the global top 10. Without sufficient funding to support product development, community builders, and user adoption, Cardano may fall behind—even if the tech is strong.\r\n\r\n💬 While I agree that spending must be responsible, budget discipline should come from reviewing each proposal carefully, not from imposing an excessively low, rigid NCL that limits flexibility.\r\n\r\n*I would support a moderate NCL in the 250–300M ADA range, which balances sustainability with real ecosystem needs. Let’s not restrict innovation with an artificial spending cap too early in the governance process.\r\n\r\n---------------------------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese Translation\r\n---------------------------------------------------------\r\nTôi bỏ phiếu NO cho đề xuất này vì các lý do sau:\r\n\r\n1) 200 triệu ADA là mức quá thấp để đáp ứng các nhu cầu ngân sách thiết yếu đã được trình bày trong các đề xuất hiện tại, bao gồm duy trì Core Dev (IOG), Catalyst, nghiên cứu, và hạ tầng cốt lõi như Hydra, ZK, Midgard, Lucid, Chainlink... Các khoản này đã vượt quá 200M ADA chỉ tính riêng các hạng mục được đánh giá là quan trọng.\r\n\r\n2) Việc thiết lập một NCL quá thấp sẽ làm đình trệ tiến trình phê duyệt ngân sách năm 2025, vì có khả năng khiến nhiều đề xuất vượt trần ngân sách bị từ chối bất hợp lệ, dù có giá trị chiến lược cho hệ sinh thái.\r\n\r\n3) Sự thay đổi đột ngột từ mức NCL 350M ADA đã được phê duyệt trước đó sang 200M ADA tạo ra sự bất ổn và mâu thuẫn trong tiến trình quản trị, đặc biệt khi không có cuộc thăm dò đồng thuận (temperature check) rõ ràng trước khi gửi lên chain.\r\n\r\n4) Cardano cần đầu tư nghiêm túc để duy trì vị trí cạnh tranh trong top 10 blockchain toàn cầu. Nếu không có đủ ngân sách để thúc đẩy phát triển sản phẩm, mở rộng quy mô, hỗ trợ cộng đồng builder và cải thiện trải nghiệm người dùng, thì Cardano dễ bị tụt lại dù có công nghệ tốt.\r\n\r\n💬 Trong bối cảnh thị trường vẫn còn nhiều biến động, chúng ta cần quản lý chi tiêu thông minh, nhưng không nên tự giới hạn khả năng đầu tư phát triển hệ sinh thái. Việc chi tiêu bao nhiêu ADA nên được kiểm soát bởi từng đề xuất cụ thể, không nên bị giới hạn bởi một mức NCL quá thấp và cứng nhắc.\r\n\r\n* Tôi đồng ý với quan điểm rằng việc chi tiêu cần thận trọng, nhưng điều đó phải đi kèm với trách nhiệm đánh giá chất lượng từng đề xuất ngân sách – chứ không phải hạ mức NCL một cách cực đoan. Thay vào đó, tôi ủng hộ một NCL ở mức trung bình như 250–300M ADA, phản ánh nhu cầu thực tế và vẫn giữ tính bền vững.\r\n\r\n---------------------------------------------------------\r\nJapanese Translation\r\n---------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n私は以下の理由から、この提案にNO票を投じます：\r\n\r\n1) 2億ADAでは、すでに提出された基本的かつ不可欠な予算項目を賄うには不十分です。Core Dev（IOG）、Catalyst、リサーチ、Hydra、ZK、Midgard、Lucid、Chainlinkなど、重要とされるプロジェクトの合計だけで200M ADAを超えています。\r\n\r\n2) このような低いNCLは、重要な提案の承認を妨げる可能性が高く、エコシステムの成長とセキュリティに必要な投資を制限してしまいます。\r\n\r\n3) すでに承認された350M ADAから突然200M ADAに下げるのは、ガバナンスの方向性と安定性を損ないます。事前の温度感調査（temperature check）や幅広い合意もなく進められた点も懸念材料です。\r\n\r\n4) Cardanoは、世界のブロックチェーン上位に留まるために十分な投資が必要です。製品開発、ビルダー支援、ユーザー拡大に資金が不足すれば、技術が優れていても競争に負けてしまいます。\r\n\r\n💬 責任ある支出は重要ですが、柔軟性を失うような極端に低いNCLではなく、各提案を丁寧に審査することで財政規律を確保すべきです。\r\n\r\n※私は、持続可能性と実際のニーズを両立できる250〜300M ADA程度の中間的なNCLを支持します。ガバナンス初年度において、過度な制限でイノベーションの芽を摘むべきではありません。",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmQvF2fAut2aqA87B9DBbXgLmAwDjaPq2RfLYK3R1L3CUW -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting Yes on a treasury net change limit of 200 million ADA for 2025. As argued in previous net change limit proposals and in https://forum.cardano.org/t/fundamental-critcism-of-the-budget-process/143519, I am very unsatisfied with how the budget process was handled by the 'budget committee' and the proposals we see so far contain much too much empty promises and grifts. A change limit that is as low as possible will at least reduce the sell pressure that is generated by these low quality wastes of ADA.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://coffeepool.jp/voting/rationale_NCL2025.json -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting “Yes” on setting the NCL to ₳200M. While this amount exceeds the previous budget ballots conducted by IntersectMBO, it does not grant unrestricted access to the entire amount within 2025. Each approved budget item will still be subject to further discussion and scrutiny regarding necessity and scale. To preserve the value of ADA, budget distribution must remain minimal or be justified as a cost shared by all holders. I strongly encourage all projects to reconsider and revise their requested amounts to stay within the new NCL. Additionally, I will continue to advocate for reducing the treasury cut in order to support small-scale, community-led governance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXwkPqgPB41F6d29Ffg2vU4wFfC3fCwsk4hD4ZwGe45xD -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are in 2025. I've been in Cardano since 2017. The general expectation that transaction fees would start contributing meaningfully to increasing the treasury has not yet materialized. This is today's reality. It is April 25, 2025. \r\n\r\nOur collective optimism about rapid widespread blockchain adoption - especially Cardano - was probably misguided. A lower limit in 2025 than the previously approved 350M ADA limit, essentially forces governance participants to focus on priorities that will give more bang for the buck. For ADA holders. \r\n\r\nThere are needs and there are wants. 200M ADA will cover the needs and not just basic ones. Reminds me of the debate of what is the purpose of art. What is the purpose of all this? \r\n\r\nReminder: ‘L’art pour l’art’ was a phrase and a philosophy that pushed back against the idea that art must serve moral, political, or educational functions. As ‘l’art pour l’art’ was challenged for ignoring purpose, so too we must challenge development for development’s sake. Treasury funds must serve real Cardano needs—not just the desire to build and develop through treasury subsidies.\r\n\r\n\"Développement pour développement”—development for its own sake funded by the treasury —is not a sustainable principle for Cardano’s treasury strategy. We will be best served by funding needs and clear common sense strategy, not  enabling endless creation and dependence without clear purpose or prioritization. Some teams may drop off, some products may not survive. \r\n\r\nEvery expenditure is risking funds. I still see lots or risks and few certain bets. \r\n\r\nI've read 100 or so Cardano 2025 budget proposals so far, or roughly half. An NCL of 200M ADA seems a better choice than the previously approved 350M ADA - from what I have read so far. I also share the concerns voiced earlier by Cardano Whale about releasing too much ADA into the market - especially as 200M ADA seems to be sufficient for 2025. The NCL can easily be raised in case of outstanding circumstances. \r\n\r\nMy only potential gains from the Cardano 2025 budget process are:\r\na. DRep compensation (I will vote against)\r\nb. milestone/community reviewer payments from Project Catalyst (I will abstain from voting on Project Catalyst - (this is just a personal decision - not advocating it to others!) to attempt to maintain a higher level of personal objectivity in the entire process)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_200M_NCL_2025.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting no on the NCL for 2025, covering the period from the start of Epoch 532 to the end of Epoch 604, set at 200M ada.  My reasoning for the no vote is based on the projected expenditure of about 275 million ADA voted on by a majority of DReps during the 2025 Intersect budgeting and socialization process.  To ask for greater funding than allocated in the NCL is irresponsible and would put undue constraints on development progress",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/29MAY2025-xl5y5/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote No on the proposed “2025 Cardano NCL” Info Action (Governance Action ID: gov_action10k0unljvaej0kd89w7pn0zkgdx59c7xkl0x5q78dzvdtd73u0kmqq5xl5y5). \r\n\r\nAs of the time of this vote, the in-force Net Change Limit for 2025 (start of Epoch 532 through the end of Epoch 604) is 350M ada (Governance Action ID: 9b62b3c632f329016a968ac25211825bb4f84b12461121c7da3aa11df92370f9#0). \r\n\r\nI voted in support of the in-force Net Change Limit. Then, out of 194 proposals submitted through Intersect’s Ekklesia platform, I voted for 46 proposals totaling 269,236,866.57 ada. At the conclusion of voting, 40 proposals totaling 275,269,340 ada garnered sufficient support to advance to Intersect’s pending “Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget - 275M ada Administered by Intersect” Info Action (Governance Action ID: gov_action1u9x73kwufaxa70lfy59g4ynwyrcsaxdcd0gxzzmh67s9fxq4j8hqqk2phgh). This budget would, if passed, run from “the close of its voting period (13JUN2025) and continue for 73 epochs (52 weeks).” There is currently no in-force or proposed Net Change Limit Info Action covering 2026.\r\n\r\nOur governance system incorporates three checks on treasury withdrawals: The in-force Net Change Limit set via Info Action, in-force budget(s) set by Info Action(s), and specific Treasury Withdrawal Governance Actions. The decision to vote for an NCL — whether 350M ada or 200M ada — does not authorize or signal support for spending these full amounts in the given time period. To withdraw ada from the treasury, each Treasury Withdrawal Governance Action must achieve sufficient voting consensus, correspond to an in-force budget, and not exceed the in-force Net Change Limit. My rationale for the in-force Net Change Limit provides my reasons for supporting it, and I’m not aware of convincing reasons to lower the 2025 NCL at this time.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/3d458xbd -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on the 200M ADA Net Change Limit for 2025. This cap, well below the annual inflow of approximately 315M ADA, protects the treasury’s reserves of 1.71B ADA, aligning with my support for the 300M/250M NCL. Although the 200M ADA does not meet all budget proposals, it forces prioritization of high-impact projects, consistent with my vote for 350M to promote disciplined growth. The lower limit reduces selling pressure on ADA, addresses Stake Pool Operators’ concerns after their rejection of the 350M NCL, and supports price stability. By voting YES, I break the deadlock following the split over the 350M NCL, enabling treasury withdrawals before the May 30, 2025, deadline.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/07/NCL25_250M.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n\r\nAfter careful consideration, I have decided to vote **NO** on the proposed Net Change Limit (NCL) of 200 million ADA for the remainder of 2025.\r\n\r\nGithub Link of this file: https://github.com/kostaspanagias/drep/blob/main/voting/2025/07/NCL25_200M.md – You can visit this link to view the formatted version of these contents. The GitHub page provides a more user-friendly and human-readable format compared to the on-chain or Cardano Explorer metadata.\r\n\r\nBelow, I outline the reasoning behind my decision:\r\n \r\n## Rationale\r\n\r\n- **Consistency with Previous Positions:**  \r\n  I have already reluctantly supported a 350M ADA NCL, having previously expressed a preference for a more conservative limit around 300M ADA, which aligns with the projected inflow for 2025. However, a 200M ADA NCL is, in my view, excessively restrictive for the current stage of Cardano’s development.\r\n\r\n- **Need for Strategic Investment:**  \r\n  While I generally favor prudent treasury management, we remain in an early and critical phase of ecosystem growth. Cardano’s roadmap includes essential development initiatives-such as scalability upgrades (e.g., Leios), enhancements to programmability, and further work on interoperability and security-that require substantial investment. Setting the NCL too low could impede our ability to fund these priorities and maintain our competitive edge against other blockchain platforms.\r\n\r\n- **Alignment with Treasury Inflows:**  \r\n  The annual inflow to the treasury is approximately 300M ADA. It is both reasonable and sustainable to set the NCL in line with this figure, ensuring that we do not spend more than we accrue, while also allowing for meaningful ecosystem investment. A 200M ADA limit, while justifiable if our ecosystem were fully developed or if we were in a more resource-constrained phase, risks underfunding critical initiatives at a time when Cardano needs to accelerate its development.\r\n\r\n- **Budget Process and Parallel Execution:**  \r\n  Although only eight months remain in 2025, the logic of scaling the NCL down proportionally for the rest of the year is not compelling. Many budget proposals and ecosystem initiatives can be executed in parallel, regardless of the elapsed months. Restricting the NCL to a lower “remaining months” calculation could unnecessarily limit our ability to fund multiple concurrent projects, especially as the budget process matures and teams become more efficient at proposal execution.\r\n\r\n- **Consistency with My Previous Votes:**  \r\n  I have already voted in favor of 51 budget proposals totaling roughly 285M ADA via the “Ekklesia” (2025 Cardano Budget Reconciliation) process. Supporting a 200M ADA NCL would be inconsistent with my prior votes on these individual proposals and would undermine the intent to see these initiatives funded and executed.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nWhile I appreciate the caution behind the proposed 200M ADA NCL, I believe it is too restrictive for the current needs and ambitions of the Cardano ecosystem. A limit closer to the actual annual inflow-around 300M ADA-strikes a better balance between sustainability and the imperative to invest in Cardano’s future. For these reasons, I have decided to vote **NO** on this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/NCL%20epoch%20554%20voting%20no.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Cardano delegated representative Krypto Labs, we propose voting no to the 2025 Net Change Limit (NCL) proposal, submitted on April 25, 2025, as an \"Info\" governance action (ID: gov_action10k0unljvaej0kd89w7pn0zkgdx59c7xkl0x5q78dzvdtd73u0kmqq5xl5y5), setting the treasury withdrawal cap at 200 million ADA for Epochs 532 to 604 (approximately eight months of 2025). This decision is rooted in the Cardano Constitution, CIP-1694, and the need to ensure the long-term sustainability and stability of the Cardano blockchain ecosystem.\r\n\r\n1. Prior NCL Establishment\r\nOn April 24, 2025, in Epoch 553, a 350 million ADA NCL was approved and deemed constitutional by the Constitutional Committee. This prior NCL must guide budget actions to maintain consistency as the constitution says “Such budgets are expected to cover not less than a period of 73 epochs (approximately one calendar year) but nothing shall prevent the Cardano Community from proposing budgets for shorter or longer time periods”\r\nChanging the NCH now will make such expectations obsolete.\r\n\r\n2. Disruption to Budget Planning: Introducing a new 200 million ADA NCL is counterproductive, as it disrupts ongoing budget proposals reliant on the 350 million ADA limit. Vendors, suppliers, and proposers have proposed deliveries, KPIs, and milestones based on this established limit since March 2025. Changing the NCL mid-process undermines their ability to execute effectively, risking delays and reduced ecosystem productivity\r\n\r\n3. DRep Accountability and Consistency: Approving the 350 million ADA NCL was a deliberate governance action, not a trial. DReps must uphold consistency to foster trust and predictability in the ecosystem. Frequent NCL changes via \"Info\" actions erode confidence and contradict the Constitution’s emphasis on sustainable treasury management.\r\n\r\n4. Lack of Evidentiary Support: The 200 million ADA proposal lacks robust research to justify reducing the NCL. While it cites 2024 treasury replenishment models estimating 350 million ADA annually, it assumes a lower limit is safer without evidence that the higher limit would harm the treasury (Proposal Metadata). Proposars operating since March 2025 have relied on the communicated 350 million ADA framework, and altering it based on speculation disrupts their efforts.\r\n\r\n5. Need for Structural Governance Improvements: While audit and transparency are critical, reducing the NCL does not address these issues. Instead, it underscores the need for an 8th governance action to manage NCL and budget parameters on-chain, as discussed in CIP-1694’s Edinburgh debates. A treasury working group, yet to be formed, is essential to develop on-chain guardrails and ensure transparent, community-driven treasury management.\r\nVoting no preserves the established 350 million ADA NCL, supports ecosystem stability, and advocates for a dedicated governance mechanism to address treasury management comprehensively. This stance aligns with the Cardano Constitution’s principles and prioritizes the ecosystem’s long-term viability.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kyle Solomon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adosiawolf/drep-rationale/refs/heads/main/0001 -->\r\n# Kyle Solomon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzshxuma6cwrnlv2ucyclfqw3k4nu4nuudmh2z87j9hncsk9dhy4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted NO on the current proposal to set the NCL to 200M Ada. I firmly believe we need to establish a fiscally responsible annual NCL, but timing matters. The current timeline in the relevant proposal does not lend the ability to guarantee continuous funding as it forces larger proposals to consider multiple and subsequent treasury withdrawal actions to achieve target annual budgets, which are not guaranteed to successfully pass. Furthermore, I have previously voted YES on a 350M NCL, an amount which I believe may be a necessary contingency to account for unexpected delays in scaling (Leios) by permitting the ecosystem latitude to focus on Praos enhancements.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LALKUL",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Juana-Attieh/lalkul/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(3).jsonld -->\r\n# LALKUL\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytnjaqmwq9qk9yv2a5ff79qj2r2mgmcmpm0683993ssy86s77kavf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLalkul is voting NO on this proposal to reduce the Net Change Limit (NCL) to 200 million ADA. A limit of 350 million ADA has already been approved for 2025, and introducing repeated changes to this parameter without clear urgency creates unnecessary churn in the governance process.\r\nAs active DReps, we have already begun evaluating and approving a number of budget items within the context of the previously established 350 million ADA limit. Reducing the NCL by such a significant margin midway through this process creates additional complexity and undermines the consistency needed for informed decision-making. It is both operationally cumbersome and procedurally disruptive.\r\nWhile we are not opposed to a future reduction in the NCL, a more structured and gradual approach would better serve the goals of stability and effective treasury management.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Latam Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LatamCardanoDRep/DREP/refs/heads/main/Vote%20May%203%202025.jsonld -->\r\n# Latam Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytgsdkfznvjnwdxrzvf8x6tn4ctfukqqphsammzkfwatgsqgnpf2w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBeing consistent with our view expressed in previous NCL proposals we are voting NO because we believe the NCL should be defined as a maximum percenual change of the balance of the treasury in a dynamic window of time so it doesn't need to be approved every year.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0008.jsonld -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Vote: **NO**\r\n\r\n**Proposal**: # 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Rationale for Opposition\r\n\r\nThis proposal’s cautious 200M ADA ceiling, while fiscally conservative, risks underfunding a foundational year in Cardano’s constitutional and governance evolution. 2025 is not a maintenance year—it is a strategic inflection point. Underspending could lead to half-measures across core infrastructure, developer tooling, and ecosystem growth.\r\n\r\nI tend to view Cardano as a startup still searching for product-market fit—not just as a blockchain, but as a governance-layered ecosystem. I don’t believe we, as an industry, have reached that fit yet. In this early phase, investment in talent, experimentation, and feedback loops is critical. We do not yet know the full cost of sustainable, decentralized governance. Arbitrarily capping expenditure without operational precedent is not prudent—it’s blindfolded restraint.\r\n\r\nStarting with a low ceiling risks disrupting development continuity and creating political friction over reallocations and perceived scarcity. In conclusion, this is not the year to constrain the ecosystem’s ability to act. It is the year to learn what it takes to responsibly fund and operate an open protocol. A vote _against_ this proposal is not a call for reckless spending, but a recognition that 200M ADA is too low to support the needs of a maturing, self-governing ecosystem in its most formative year ever. Based on community sentiment I’ve observed, expectations for a reasonable 2025 NCL orbit between 200M and 350M ADA. I prefer to position us safely in the middle of that range, rather than risk underspending at the floor. \r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I also believe Treasury constraints should be informed by real experience and evolving risk management mechanisms—not early-stage caution that may inadvertently stall progress. I hope to see more maturity and responsiveness in the 2026 budget cycle as our governance capabilities evolve.\r\n\r\nVOTE0008",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Manuel SNAKE",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/asnakep/repo/refs/heads/master/docs/Vote_Context03.jsonld -->\r\n# Manuel SNAKE\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt56tpzpzu58zy7pz4zwfp32rq95tj3xfxmdrg8k3qhxjlccp47cn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYES – We supports GA “2025 Cardano NCL”. Setting a 200 M ADA Net Change Limit for epochs 532-604 is a cautious, data-driven safeguard: it protects Treasury principal, satisfies Article IV guardrails, and still unlocks funds for essential maintenance, scaling, and ecosystem expansion. This cap lets the community test new budgeting and audit workflows, gather metrics, and refine the process before defining 2026 limits.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Marketing DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSsFUyGYK4iWNyEpLWdEm9YzbWTbajbvN53rzYLzV3ua4 -->\r\n# Marketing DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Cardano NCL\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23kumvpqgal3t6v4tamwrprjya453p3djam0eqg63usm9su77hjl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThough I voted in support of a previous NCL that sought to cap 2025 spending at 350 million ADA, this new proposed governance action calls for a logical reduction in that amount given the time remaining in 2025 to pass the budget, disperse funds, and for proposers to execute on contracts.",
