      "voter": "DanShipps_HarborStakePool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreicwrmim432xmk7lpthqqtswky6vg5dmolmqargrmsrzhxgpywxfne -->\r\n# DanShipps_HarborStakePool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygxu629f9zzm0r6fm8m2rtn3qglgtstvfxvt7nj68hxmdpcrwphte`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting to approve Constitution v2.00.\r\n\r\nThis update strengthens Cardano governance by:\r\n\r\nReaffirming ada’s hard cap and role as currency\r\n\r\nAdding transparency requirements for treasury spending, compensation, and governance actions\r\n\r\nClarifying responsibilities for DReps, SPOs, and the Constitutional Committee\r\n\r\nIntroducing audits, oversight, and immutable documentation for proposals\r\n\r\nWhile the changes introduce more process overhead, they are essential safeguards to protect the treasury and ensure decentralization, sustainability, and trust in Cardano’s governance.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I support ratification of Constitution v2.00.\r\n\r\n— DanShipps_HarborStakePool",
