      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmcatvyxQbiRZCJ6bdypiMQjb6XHThrCUUZmzUd7cNwaU6 -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmasvfczziVs9Wx3ANKr43Qs38evgfZ6G8MhRNRDtwDFPG\r\n\r\nI support this constitution as a beneficial advancement for Cardano. I welcome this update with the understanding that it is not a final, static document, but a foundational framework designed for continuous improvement.\r\n\r\nThe constitution itself is structured as a \"living document\" that is expected to evolve. It establishes a clear on-chain governance process for amendments, allowing it to adapt over time as new technical insights are gained and the needs of the ecosystem change. This capacity for constant updates is crucial, and I welcome this approach to governance.\r\n\r\nI would also like to thank YUTA for his effort and the community for their contributions.",
