    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Constitution2.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nEMURGO as DRep votes to ABSTAIN on the governance action to ratify the Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Constitution v2.0.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nWe appreciate the effort to improve the Constitution through amendment, especially the attempt to clarify definitions and introduce additional oversight standards. These updates show a genuine commitment to strengthening governance and moving the ecosystem forward. \r\n\r\nAt the same time, we remain concerned with both the process and content. The proposal moved on-chain while significant feedback was still emerging, showing that broader consensus has not yet been reached. On substance, removing the budget Info Action weakens the link between treasury withdrawals and long-term priorities. In addition, changes to the auto-abstain safeguard create ambiguity around the influence of treasury funds on governance outcomes.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nGiven these open concerns and the need for wider deliberation, EMURGO chooses to abstain at this stage. This decision reflects a call for further discussion and refinement before bringing forward such an important revision.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00048_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted NO on gov_action1ypajyms3pcfmkx93r87dxy6jpc8u6pst90ylhxj7t0rwjj43puasq0x9jrw;\r\n\r\nProcess of going through the changes:\r\n\r\nGeneral: Have an LLM check the grammar and spelling, please; e.g. Block vs block, missing spaces after commas etc.\r\n\r\n- 24 Delegated Representative (DRep). The individual or entity registered to vote with respect to on-chain governance actions for its own behalf or on behalf of other owners of ada.\r\n+ 24 Delegated Representative (DRep). The individual or entity registered to vote with respect to on-chain governance actions for its own behalf or on behalf of other Ada Holders.\r\n\r\n- 26 Net Change Limit. Means the maximum amount or percentage by which the Cardano Treasury may not be reduced by in a given period.\r\n+ 26 Net Change Limit. Means the maximum allowed amount of Lovelace removed from the Cardano Treasury in a given period.\r\n\r\n- 28 Stake Pool Operator (SPO). An individual or entity that manifests intent through the signed transactions of a Stake Pool.\r\n+ 28 Stake Pool Operator (SPO). An individual or entity who directly controls the cold key(s) to a Cardano block producing node.\r\n\r\n30 Block(s) vs block(s)\r\n\r\n87 - Three independent voting bodies - DReps, SPOs, and the CC - participate in on-chain voting; anyone holding multiple roles must publicly disclose such overlaps before engaging in any on-chain governance actions.\r\n--- This is not enforcable. An anonymous DRep could also be an anonymous SPO.\r\n\r\n>>> Now leaning towards ABSTAIN.\r\n\r\n92 - DReps may vote on all types of governance actions.\r\n--- A bit of a non-sensical one. While they can vote on everything, hardforks are not determined by them.\r\n\r\n94 - DReps shall ensure that any compensation received in connection with their activities as a DRep is publicly disclosed in a timely manner through relevant governance communication channels.\r\n--- Again, not enforcable. What do you want to do, if you find out a DRep did not disclose it? Ban them by ledger rule?\r\n\r\n95 - DReps shall not offer or provide compensation to an Ada Holder or in exchange for being appointed as a DRep or for voting on their behalf.\r\n--- Again, not enforcable. Same as 94.\r\n\r\n101 - SPOs shall publicly disclose if they are simultaneously voting as a DRep on the same governance actions.\r\n--- This is not enforcable. An anonymous DRep could also be an anonymous SPO. \r\n\r\n>>> Now leaning towards NO.\r\n\r\n103 vs 99. Almost same content, can that be shortened?\r\n\r\n106 - ... The document hosted by such a URL shall be immutable in nature and incapable of being altered after submission of the proposed governance action for on-chain voting.\r\n--- This reduces the hosting options dramatically. As long as the hash is correct and the document wasn't altered, the action should be valid.\r\n\r\n135  - Treasury Withdrawal Recipients shall use treasury withdrawals for the purpose set out in Section 7, paragraph 1 above.\r\n--- Makes no sense.\r\n\r\n- 148 - ... owners of ada.\r\n+ 148 - ... Ada Holders.\r\n\r\n153 - ... no confidence will result.\r\n--- No proper English.\r\n\r\n357/359/1141 ada holders vs Ada Holders. (It's a definition and should be capitalized). Please check 'owners of ada' and 'ada holders' in the whole document and replace it with Ada Holders.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
