    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/r/25/250812_const-v2_207b226e.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES. This update improves clarity and accessibility of the Constitution, removes outdated clauses, and simplifies processes without weakening decentralised checks and balances. Core safeguards - including DRep, SPO, and Constitutional Committee approvals - remain intact. While removing the Budget Info requirement reduces one procedural step for treasury withdrawals, overall transparency is maintained, and any issues can be addressed in future governance actions.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peter Horsfall",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUW2cFnNFsSpmBxbRU5rr1gf4v8egy86FD3QzNx5cuZrT -->\r\n# Peter Horsfall\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytfas4axhm8yzrqqh4ru2uuqesu87zeq6fwg5pq8azqf7ecu4nu8s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on the v2.0 Cardano Constitution. Having proudly signed the original Constitution in Argentina, I can attest that this updated version effectively eliminates unnecessary barriers to entry, enhances overall clarity, and positions Cardano for unprecedented growth and success. It is also the first truly community-refined Constitution. I fully anticipate additional refinements as our ecosystem continues to evolve and mature.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Phil UPLC",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibrfrgugn63skhduj5ozchun2yzd4bb3y7s3dui7sp6c2jbkppgqi -->\r\n# Phil UPLC\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg343cyuckglj48a6gpcey7fkfcy5x5f9g65wme3ne9q2mgaedmkm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTo be honest, this isn't ideal from my perspective. The scope of changes proposed is too large. In the future I would prefer constitutional amendments to be extremely focused, ie. to change a single item. It's very hard to get community consensus on a bundle of proposed changes (ie. some voters might like one change, but dislike another and thus choose not to vote for it). The only way we can get rapid iteration is via many proposals that have small scope (if the change proposed is about a single item, and the majority of stake agrees with the single item change then it will be accepted). That said, redundancy in the current situation is so unbelievably bad (budget & withdrawals being separate proposals) and is wasting an immense amount of money & time for the ecosystem, that I am compelled to vote for this proposal simply because it removes the concept of budget info actions from the constitution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
