    {
      "voter": "Reshma_Mohan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/resgsh/drep-mainnet/refs/heads/main/voting-activity/6.Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Reshma_Mohan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfcgvh8rum7a9ma4gwgwuwutdu0dnrzaj98jytwyfqzd87q2nehvm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting yes.\r\nThe changes make the Constitution clearer.\r\nOutdated rules are removed.\r\nSafeguards are stronger for treasury funds. Treasury use will be more transparent.\r\nIt will be easier to follow and trust.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreic527jw7fsh5du3akkpublveq3twxbazdob2gxjdxahkehob2olbe -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter careful review of this governance action, I have decided to vote no on this proposal. \r\nI will start by saying that I like almost the entirety of this proposal, and there are many excellent changes. I would like to commend the work that was done to clean up the constitution, add definitions etc. While most issues are positive, there remains some issues around enforceability of some clauses. Requirements to disclose compensation and SPO/DREP overlap are simply not enforceable and should not be in the constitution. It's one thing if people would like to make it part of the social contract and simply advise against delegation to people who fail to provide these things but enshrining this in the constitution is fundamentally foolish without enforcement and against principles of freedom and inclusivity that I would hope are core to any blockchain community. That said I recognize that this is already an issue of the constitution in it's current form and if it was only this then I could look past it.\r\nThe main red line for me as to why I cannot vote for this proposal is the removal of the budget info actions. I believe the community made a fundamental error in how we handled our very first budget, which caused us to make the budget info action redundant. The budget info action was meant to separate funding into tranches, and then those tranches would be administered by groups chosen by the voters through that same budget info action. We failed to utilize it as intended and instead crammed proposals into the budget info action then voted again for the same proposals. We also voted to increase granular control of DReps in approving individual proposals which was ill-advised. The fact that we failed to utilize the budget info action properly does not mean it should be removed. Without a budget info action we will simply be conducting a \"catalyst version\" project run on funds as soon as a net change limit is approved. For various reasons, this is not an outcome that I feel will improve the ecosystem at all. \r\nI would very much recommend that this proposal be resubmitted with the important but less contentious improvements only and that more contentious elements like removing the budget info action done individually for a full and fair discussion on each.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTpNuQpHuZJnJmzyudYDheRsXVqYHP55Ff18sp38xEwJR -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis change removes the largely procedural Budget Information Action and allows the process to proceed with only the Withdrawal approval.\r\nPreviously, the process required two on-chain approvals — \"Budget Information → Withdrawal\" — which created significant burdens for both DReps and proposers, with limited practical benefits.\r\n\r\nIn practice, the Budget Information Action often became a formal step without substantial impact before the Withdrawal approval. Under the revised process, necessary discussions and evaluations will take place off-chain or in appropriate forums, and the final decision will be made with a single on-chain approval.\r\n\r\nI consider this a reasonable measure that will improve the overall efficiency of governance.\r\n\r\n今回の変更は、形式的になっていた予算情報アクションを省き、Withdrawal承認のみで進められるようにするものです。従来は「予算情報 → Withdrawal」という二段階のオンチェーン承認が必要でしたが、これはDRepとしても、また提案者にとっても負担が大きく、実務的にはデメリットがありました。\r\n\r\nこの二段階形式は、事実上、予算情報アクションが形式的なステップに留まり、Withdrawal承認に至るまでの実質的な意味を持ちにくい構造になっていました。今回の改訂により、必要な議論や評価はオフチェーンや適切な場で行い、その結果を踏まえて一度だけオンチェーンで承認する流れに簡略化されます。\r\n\r\nこの変更は、ガバナンス全体の効率化につながる合理的な措置であると考えます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Sebastien Guillemot セバ",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWVaccfC3Y4xSoGVzMwh533S4QwPrTbonbt3n1eQUUSvv -->\r\n# Sebastien Guillemot セバ\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2csyxt7u2hl4674pl9cef5lknafaw5nraxvyx033kmd0es3awuv0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI agree with the changes in principle, but I don't like the idea of replacing the info action with a new \"roadmap\" info action as I believe this will be too limiting and too prone to have the process captured and centralized",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmccJhFy7nnLbLk4j6YHZFg6jhzN2FXbEACqDBpGxmcZPE -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nPursuant to **ARTICLE VIII** of the Cardano Constitution, the amendment process is clearly outlined; therefore, this GA is in line with the constitutional provisions, and I support it as an opportunity for the community to review the constitution. More importantly, the process leading toward Constitution 2.0 has been transparent and community-oriented, although limited effort was made to reach other members beyond the usual channels. Participation was mainly driven through posts on X and the Cardano Forum.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/Update_to_the_Constitution/CARDANO_BLOCKCHAIN_ECOSYSTEM_CONSTITUTION%20_v2_0/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO’s Voting Rationale\r\n\r\nSIPO casts a Yes vote on the “CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0.”\r\n\r\nThe reasons are as follows:\r\n\t1.\tClarification and Refinement\r\n\t•\tThe proposal fixes typos, improves consistency, and simplifies redundant wording.\r\n\t•\tKey definitions have been clarified, making the constitution more coherent and easier to interpret.\r\n\t2.\tRemoval of Outdated Clauses\r\n\t•\tUnused provisions such as the DRep/SPO Codes of Conduct are removed.\r\n\t•\tThis avoids unnecessary complexity and ensures that the constitution reflects current governance practices.\r\n\t3.\tImproved Treasury Flexibility\r\n\t•\tThe requirement for a budget information action when withdrawing from the treasury has been removed.\r\n\t•\tThis allows faster, more flexible treasury operations while maintaining accountability.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this constitutional amendment because it enhances clarity, transparency, and practical governance efficiency within the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOの投票理由\r\n\r\nSIPOは「CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0」に対してYes票を投じます。\r\n\r\nその理由は以下の通りです。\r\n\t1.\t憲法の明確化と整理\r\n\t•\t提案は、誤字や不整合を修正し、冗長な表現を簡潔化しています。\r\n\t•\t曖昧だった定義を明確化し、全体の読みやすさと一貫性を向上させています。\r\n\t2.\t不要条項の削除\r\n\t•\t実際には使われていないDRepやSPOの行動規範の条項を削除し、現実に即した構造にしています。\r\n\t•\tこれにより、憲法が実効性を持ち、形骸化を避けられると判断します。\r\n\t3.\t財務の柔軟性\r\n\t•\tこれまで必要とされていた「予算情報アクション」を伴う財務支出要件が撤廃され、トレジャリーからの引き出しがシンプルになります。\r\n\t•\tこれは意思決定と資金配分の柔軟性を高め、迅速な対応を可能にします。\r\n\r\n結論\r\n\r\nSIPOは、この憲法改正がカルダノ・エコシステムにおける 透明性・明確性・実効性の向上 に資すると考え、Yes票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVDfzYdjrhgNB2Kjy9bECq3p8LSQnodECorpdcmgCpCEJ -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are abstaining on this proposal. Constitutional amendments are an important process for the community, but in our view this proposal has not undergone sufficient debate. We believe that rather than forcing a Yes or No, it is more appropriate to abstain, leaving room for further discussion and for the community at large to make its judgment.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUMRDvkV3aJnTfyXJYPhWrR4giaSz8qiZaDpSheLPzptL -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe support the adoption of the Cardano Constitution v2.0.\r\n\r\nWhile the changes appear largely structural (improving clarity, fixing typos, and removing redundancy) one modification carries real governance implications: eliminating the requirement to submit a Budget Information Governance Action (BIA) prior to any treasury withdrawal.\r\n\r\nWe believe this is a positive change. The BIA mechanism was a well-intentioned but ultimately redundant safeguard. Its removal does not eliminate treasury oversight. Removing this bottleneck improves operational agility for builders without compromising systemic integrity.\r\n\r\nWe encourage fellow DReps, SPOs, and ecosystem participants to self-organize and maintain off-chain codes of conduct and community norms, which can be upheld through social consensus and delegation behavior, and that ultimately represent what we consider best-practices for on-chain governance participants.\r\nWe believe v2.0 is a net-positive step toward a more legible and functional governance framework. We vote YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SudoScientist",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arpradio/drep/refs/heads/main/Constitution-2_0/const-2_0.jsonld -->\r\n# SudoScientist\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wtls7xh3a8gyepk540dgtzjzalk086gp4www6y0k0xjmqyk6gma`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs one of the delegates that fought for the inclusion of Article VIII, the following amendment's effort is welcomed, yet fails to meet the intended pathway for such changes to occur:\r\n\r\n\"The Cardano Community is encouraged to periodically review and debate its\r\nprovisions, and when so desired, come together in such forums as the Cardano\r\nCommunity may deem appropriate, to propose amendments to this Constitution.\r\nAmendments may be made as provided in this Article VIII.\"\r\n\r\nAt the time of writing, it was brought up that amendments issued by singular entities would, and probably should, experience a high level of scrutiny, making it very difficult to pass.  This is why it was important, in my view, to make amendment proposals as a group, with as much engagement of the community as possible.  The following being presented by a representative of high stake should not be taken lightly, particularly in the vulnerable stages of governance we currently reside.\r\n\r\nThe proposed changes are viewed highly inconsequential:\r\n\r\n1. Perceived \"typos\" and \"clarifications\" add no further influence on the CC's interpretation of the Constitutional text\r\n\r\n2. Definitions have no direct authority over the CC's determination and therefore should not be part of the text. \r\n\r\n3.  The perceived \"requirement\" of Info Actions within the Budget Process is the interpretation of the proposer that is already contrary to the terms declared within the Constitutional text.  \"Expected\" is not a requirement, yet a strong suggestion that may welcome scrutiny when not followed.  \r\n\r\n4.  The \"Code of Conduct\" is not something I ever wanted within the text, but this was already voted on the community to be included, despite pushback.  I initially was concerned about the weaponization of such text by blocking dRep votes, but the CC is not afforded this capability, and this reveals the fact moderation happens at the delegator level- delegators will judge dReps/delegates based on their perceived \"Code of Conduct\" with or without this being included in the text, and therefore has no affect aside from the already existing social pressure delegators are subject to.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreieapeyedp5ywyb4sfngca5trv4t625tjl3quq46dud5nogw4mvz2m -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis update cleans up the Cardano Constitution by fixing wording, clarifying definitions, removing outdated rules, and simplifying treasury withdrawal procedures.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmafkQZD4WM9C9Dtm4squDDuMPAEGZsH3HerbuEUm8ppHx -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis constitution while not perfect is the first TRULY COMMUNITY DRIVEN constitution that was openly developed and discussed. This is also a significant improvement from the current Constitution which was hastily ratified due to time constraint. We vote YES for this and expect Constitution to be continued to improved further after each iteration!",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiedgy7tmyf5o6ulnz4ulguhkkhui5fxygeo3ljbhg7a7lyrp6tvqy -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThese changes seem reasonable, and I agree the original Constitution could use some polishing.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSyQxzypEH1n6DVxzcBXKSLHQ8K6yG5v5reXyAeqwjJga -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAt first glance, the proposed amendments appear modest, mostly wording refinements, clarifications, and removal of outdated or redundant clauses. This is not inherently problematic; streamlining documentation is beneficial. However, **the devil is in the details, particularly regarding treasury withdrawals** and the removal of the Budget Information Action (BIA) requirement.\r\n\r\nThe rationale to remove BIAs for treasury withdrawals under 1 million ADA within two years, accompanied by the relaxation of audit requirements, is deeply troubling. **Audits are a fundamental control mechanism in any prudent financial governance framework. Labeling audits as “burdensome conditions” as DRep YUTA states, betrays a lack of appreciation for sound business management principles.** This signals a potential weakening of financial oversight that will invite misuse or misallocation of funds, contrary to the fiduciary responsibilities we hold as DReps!\r\n\r\nMoreover, **the removal of BIAs and audit requirements will almost certainly incentivize proposers to fragment larger budgets into multiple sub-1-million ADA requests, circumventing meaningful scrutiny.** This creates a loophole ripe for exploitation by less scrupulous actors, increasing the oversight burden on DReps and diluting treasury protection.\r\n\r\nThe proposal’s motivation to support builders more efficiently is understandable, efficiency cannot come at the cost of financial rigor. The constitution should reinforce, not erode, mechanisms that ensure transparency and accountability. The added disclosure requirements are insufficient substitutes for formal audits and structured budget reviews.\r\n\r\nThis proposal does not demonstrate the necessary strategic foresight or business acumen to safeguard Cardano’s treasury and governance framework. It underestimates the complexity and risk of financial management in a decentralized ecosystem. I do not see this as a step forward but rather a step sideways, potentially backward.\r\n\r\nVote: NO",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmX1fhYAsDHM7MCBHT5jPqKRCLfSYBjX7mSdv1nFb1dDrY -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support the removal of the Budget Info Action requirement. We have multiple protecting mechanisms, but this was less helpful and more time consuming.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWz4XSnQnorHj7CwTkP3LtxH28o8rCHaFRAByNMN2Ptn7 -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe removal of the Budget Info Action Requirement reduces a layer of transparency and strategic alignment, raising valid concerns about potential misuse, favoritism, and governance overload. While safeguards like voting and smart contracts remain, the change shifts more responsibility to the community to vet each withdrawal, which could be challenging given current participation levels. Because I'm concerned about these risks, take my \"nay\" vote as a push for more consultation or alternative safeguards.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Viet_Cardano_Community",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPmQGBSAv6saL3gwT6cy7PFvfAnkFPEJx5hBGFpiYenJH -->\r\n# Viet_Cardano_Community\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygpzpm4q38rfueu2use5te4ylykn4smvs7cxj2ggvktcjkqpxhvf4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote YES. v2.0 mainly relaxes and clarifies treasury withdrawal rules, removes Budget Information Actions, and adds minimal disclosure requirements that don’t create extra work for proposers.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreib5if7mstl2vd2mddyf36wgtczoft2bi2lksvusrjaiv65c2yujcm -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are abstaining to avoid creating procedural blockage for a largely beneficial update while signaling a clear preference for a more inclusive, better-timed, and better-communicated amendment process. Substantively, we recognize meaningful improvements in v2: clearer defined terms, simplified language, and removal of outdated provisions, alongside alignment updates such as eliminating the standing requirement to attach a Budget Info Action to treasury withdrawals. These are quality-of-life corrections that reduce ambiguity and technical debt in the text, and we acknowledge the effort behind them. \r\n\r\nOur abstention is therefore not about content rejection; it is about process. Although we appreciate Yuta’s sincere attempts to invite participation, the practical window and venues for engagement did not, in our view, provide sufficient reach and attention for broad community input. Given the Constitution’s foundational role, we believe updates of this magnitude should be preceded by a clearly signposted and widely accessible consultation cycle (e.g., advance timeline, multilingual summaries, regional office hours, written comment periods, and transparent diff mapping). The motivation text in the v2 materials themselves underlines that the revision tackles clarity, definitions, and pruning of unused clauses, precisely the kind of changes where broad review helps catch edge cases and social implications before adoption. \r\n\r\nWe also advise that v2 explicitly include a clear, community-ratified amendment process. As it stands, the path to initiating, socializing, and finalizing constitutional edits is not sufficiently standardized, which makes inclusive participation fragile and uneven across regions and time zones. To address this, we recommend the creation of a community-mandated Constitutional Review Committee tasked to (i) monitor constitutional effectiveness in practice; (ii) steward amendment proposals end-to-end; (iii) publish consultation calendars and stakeholder engagement reports; and (iv) maintain a public change log and rationale archive.\r\n\r\nFinally, we note one material policy shift: the removal of the Budget Info Action requirement for treasury withdrawals warrants heightened governance hygiene. We recommend that the essential parts of the budget info actions must be integrated in the treasury withdrawal actions to preserve trust and accountability while streamlining the budgetary process and reducing the burden on DReps as we transition. Our abstention keeps the door open for these procedural refinements without impeding progress on the underlying textual improvements. Should the community adopt v2, Wada stands ready to support implementation of the above process enhancements and to contribute beyond our DRep role to ensure the Constitution remains both clear and genuinely community-driven.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifuxpmfyqa6m7snub5xi6qbdiq26mxli2bqtno2gokcosxmeqwfku -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis revision to the constitution changes too many things at once.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "wolf31o2 (Chris Gianelloni)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfKEMZhLCkcpe5Ns2DSorCKhgfCKzvTsMBXc6eujexy98 -->\r\n# wolf31o2 (Chris Gianelloni)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfa8r8r36x7x05htftce7qhafrn5nzzr6vazy95pzy6y5dqac0ss7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHard disagree on forced identity and location disclosures. There's no reason to force ecosystem builders to lower their personal security to obtain funds.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Constitution%202.0.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep votes to ABSTAIN on the governance action titled Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Constitution v2.0.\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nWe value the effort to improve the Constitution, especially the clarifications and cleanup of definitions.\r\nAt the same time, removing the budget info action weakens financial transparency around treasury withdrawals.\r\n\r\nThe changes to the auto-abstain safeguard reduce clarity on its role, and these updates weren’t broadly discussed with the community. The proposal moved on-chain while feedback was still being raised, signaling that consensus has not yet been reached\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nAbstaining allows Yoroi DRep to recognize the improvements made, while also signaling that more discussion and ecosystem input are needed before proposing such important constitutional changes. We encourage continued dialogue and active participation from all stakeholders to build stronger alignment for future updates.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yosh",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU5zgoqXqQCPh1LCp67z5g6LAbcfy3ecocoTEZARXzWMQ -->\r\n# Yosh\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytd7s3he5rgxhkx0t2vnun25wy3t263877czxw8nelcld8ce66v4c`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the proposed amendment does a good job of improving clarity and cleaning up definitions, I am voting No on this proposal.\r\n\r\nMy concern is that replacing budgets with roadmaps removes the detailed financial oversight we currently have. Roadmaps are too broad to judge funding requests on their own, which risks making treasury withdrawals being more fragmented and less disciplined. I do think there are opportunities to improve the process, but I don't feel this has been debated enough. Removing codes of conduct also weakens formal accountability, and shifting more weight onto the Constitutional Committee creates additional risk by concentrating too much discretion in the hands of a small group. \r\n\r\nThese are significant governance changes that haven’t been discussed enough by the community, and I don’t believe the current Constitution justifies such a quick amendment.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmefZtkEP4UQgszB1quZLJ1Agqw9p12t2748yPyY1ZFeJ2 -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting YES on [CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0].\r\n\r\nWhile there are many areas for improvement, the biggest reason is to support builders more efficiently while strengthening the protection of financial soundness.\r\n\r\nCONSTITUTION v2.0 makes no major changes to the text other than adding and relaxing conditions for treasury withdrawals and removing Budget Information Actions.\r\n\r\nIn exchange for removing the Budget Information Actions, several disclosure requirements have been added for treasury withdrawals.\r\n\r\nHowever, most of this is merely clarification of the items to be disclosed, and nothing will significantly increase the burden on proposers. For treasury withdrawals totaling less than 1 million ada within two years, several burdensome conditions, such as audit requirements, have been removed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[ CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0 ]にYESを投票します。\r\n\r\n多くの改善点が残っていると思いますが最大の理由はビルダーをより効率的に支援すると同時に、財務健全性の保護を強化しているためです。\r\n\r\nCONSTITUTION v2.0 は、トレジャリー引き出しの条件追加および緩和とBudget情報アクションの削除の以外の条文に大きな変更はありません。\r\n\r\nBudget情報アクションが削除される代わりにトレジャリー引き出しの要件について、いくつか開示すべき要素が追加されています。\r\nただし、ほとんどは記載項目の明確化であり、提案者の大きな負担増につながる項目はありません。\r\nまた、トレジャリー引き出しに関して、2年以内に合計100万ADA以下のトレジャリー引き出しに関しては大幅に監査要件などが除外されています。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Zacros",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihlzvyhjzigmc63hwunb2qa3xkoroa2ma5dm5krc36amdifq5u644 -->\r\n# Zacros\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.0\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2tp9q9vckglgkgkgcdc33jtahrstfzfj3c8ez926ysszjqp5r4ts`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nPanda voted NO solely for this piece:\r\n\r\n>> Treasury withdrawal governance actions must. [...] , the location and the identity of the recipient.\r\n\r\nPanda is not sure what it means and entails \" location and the identity of the recipient.\".  Might be too broad and general and force unwanted consequences",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    }
  ],
