    {
      "voter": "Musa Ridwan Itopa",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXuRg4V2JRXbYjhn3xuUBmCkB3Vs6zKz2rSrCkxHsfNQh -->\r\n# Musa Ridwan Itopa\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano x Draper Dragon Orion Fund\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yggumgdxdpa2dgr85etak35s4v00k07vdhvn5y3xxw33yac77c9hp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting YES on Cardano x Draper Dragon: Orion Fund (Treasury Withdrawal – Tranche 1).As an elected member of the Cardano Civics Committee, President  of Unified Cardano Student Club Nigeria, and a DRep deeply focused on inclusion, transparency, sustainable growth, and real-world adoption — especially for Africa and student communities — I have decided to support this proposal.\r\nWhat finally gave me full conviction:\r\nThis is not a blank cheque for $75M. We are only voting on the first tranche (50M ADA / ~$15M). Every future tranche requires a separate on-chain governance action with full DRep review.\r\nThe proposer has committed to a public on-chain dashboard with clear, measurable KPIs that will show whether the fund is actually delivering:\r\nGrowth in on-chain activity and fee revenue\r\nContribution to TVL targets (RWA + DeFi)\r\nNew developers and builders entering the ecosystem\r\nVenture studio output and accelerator results\r\nInstitutional attention and strategic partnerships\r\n\r\nThis structure gives the entire DRep community real oversight and veto power at every stage. If Year 1 performance is not strong, Tranche 2 can (and should) be rejected.\r\nFor someone like me who pushes hard for education, onboarding, and adoption in emerging markets, the potential upside is significant: attracting serious institutional capital, incubating new Cardano-native projects, bringing more developers, and driving real on-chain utility that benefits students and builders in Africa and beyond.\r\nI will be watching the dashboard closely and holding them accountable. Transparency + staged governance = responsible use of treasury.\r\nLet’s give this strategic partnership a fair shot while keeping strong guardrails in place.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreicmgudokfhyjue64y5p2kvglzgyy426glg47vxv66d4nt7ijmkqcy -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano x Draper Dragon Orion Fund\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile some aspects of the proposal remain unclear at this stage, I appreciate its overall concept and believe it has strong potential to benefit the Cardano ecosystem. The involvement of the Cardano Foundation adds credibility, and the inclusion of third-party capital alongside treasury funds is something I like too. Based on these considerations, I have decided to vote YES on this proposal.",
