    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/DRepdata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context2250707GovToolInfoAction.jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私はこのInfo Actionに賛成（Yes）します。\r\nGovToolは、カルダノのオンチェーンガバナンスにおいて、DRepの委任、提案、投票、結果確認などを可能にする中核的な公共インフラです。その継続的な開発と保守は、Voltaire期における分散型ガバナンスの実現に不可欠です。\r\n本提案では、コミュニティからのフィードバックを反映した段階的な予算構成と、Intersectによるスマートコントラクトを用いた透明性の高い資金管理が示されています。₳1.15Mという請求額は、対象業務のスコープ、工数、構造に照らして妥当であると判断します。\r\nこの提案は、GovToolの維持と進化を通じて、カルダノのガバナンス文化をより開かれたものに育てていくための重要な一歩です。\r\n\r\n*************\r\n\r\nI support this Info Action with a Yes vote.\r\nGovTool is a core piece of public infrastructure for Cardano’s on-chain governance, enabling DRep delegation, proposal submission, voting, and result tracking. Its continued development and maintenance are essential to realizing decentralized governance during the Voltaire era.\r\nThis proposal presents a tiered budget structure that incorporates community feedback, along with a transparent fund management system using smart contracts overseen by Intersect. The requested amount of ₳1.15M is considered reasonable given the scope, workload, and organizational structure involved.\r\nThis Info Action represents a crucial step toward strengthening Cardano’s governance culture by ensuring the continued support and evolution of GovTool as an open and inclusive public good.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmePR9ojgg2MfvTt7kL2nmAvRW3HAKmsUxwUXDnEimQTRv -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote yes for this proposal because Govtool has been a strong driver of Cardano governance in its early stages. It is a useful tool in supporting governance, open participation, and decentralization.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Africa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Abdulazizkarma1/Cardano-Africa-DRep-Data/refs/heads/main/govtool%20proposal.jsonld -->\r\n# Cardano Africa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytj9kz0n5yamacgcj8jr6apn36hx5suzqpefxvhy4cvfqmsqangtx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs clearly defined in the proposal, Govtool provides the open, user-friendly experience needed for all ADA holders (existing and future) to register, delegate, propose, vote, and see outcomes transparently. \r\n\r\nThis proposal is well detailed and included all key details, some of which, as a Drep, I was not aware of. Govtool interface provides ecosystem-wide participation. \r\n\r\nNow the budget requested is 1.15M ADA, which is relatively low as compared to their earlier proposal budget. The budget breakdown is clear with the promise that any unused funds will be returned to the treasury. \r\n\r\nAs stated, Intersect is going to be the administrator, and a portion of the budget (L2) will be hosted on Andamio. How do we track these funds for audit purposes, especially the level 2 funds, which Andamio is going to be hosting?\r\n\r\nGovtool is a great tool for the community, and kudos to the 5 community builders who have worked tirelessly for this project. \r\n\r\nCardano Africa DRep responsibly supports this proposal",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://bafybeidmmqyzytfdisten7t5oknspxttwczsbbbdmq2i5al5dds4j3bviq.ipfs.dweb.link/ -->\n# Cardano Foundation\n\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\n\n---\n\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\n\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmYZpFKsSU6NTLUivvGFaiNQVdEwxhYKwGPJrmrHwTVhkc\n\nWhile acknowledging valid concerns, this is a pragmatic decision based on GovTool’s strategic importance as an open-source public good, ensuring accessibility to Cardano's decentralized governance model.\n\n**Rationale Statement**\n\nThis decision follows a detailed review of the governance action and consideration of diverse viewpoints within our governance advisory team. Our support is based on a pragmatic assessment of GovTool’s role in the ecosystem, balanced against its acknowledged areas for improvement.\n\n**Reasons for a YES Vote:**\n\n1. **Strategic Importance for Governance Accessibility:** A core principle in \"Our Cardano\" is Accessibility, ensuring participation in governance is open to all. GovTool is the primary, non-commercial tool that currently fulfills this mission, providing a neutral and open-source public good for every ada holder to engage in governance. Maintaining its viability at this time, while governance is in a critical stage, is important for Cardano’s governance model, as it prevents reliance on proprietary, closed-source alternatives.  \n2. **Commitment to Open Source and Ecosystem Growth:** The proposal reinforces a commitment to open-source principles, which prevents vendor lock-in and fosters a competitive environment. Furthermore, the budget’s Level 2 funding earmarks 250,000 ada for direct community contributions and to support other open-source governance tools, an approach that should benefit the entire ecosystem.  \n3. **Pragmatic Support for a Proven and Improving Team:** While the tool has known user experience and technical shortcomings, the consortium has a proven track record of consistently delivering and maintaining this infrastructure. They have demonstrated responsiveness to feedback and a commitment to improvement. For lack of better alternatives, supporting this established team represents the most viable path to retaining and enhancing the value GovTool provides.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmabxz9sWvNxvr7ABfNeL8pWjNzEr4XtJna3n744oT2Po6 -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDecentralised funding for open source, modular community tooling that benefit us all and slot into various other platforms, with well documented asks (that don't break the bank) and outcomes. While we can debate the details of the proposal endlessly I can think of no better way to spend Cardano treasury funds. So I will support this.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmZxmREvXMkgFahNqzF1wTy7ZX1zpHocQMen1L2Ety3ixc -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmNSh35XtrTKFrzCVAnpBAC45U9DzpSzD7RLR57s4QXSMz\r\n\r\nInitially, I was leaning toward voting NO or Abstain, as the request for 1.15 million ADA (approx. $920,000) to fund 5.75 FTEs seemed quite steep for a community-driven open-source project. This concern appears to be shared by many, based on discussions I’ve followed across X.\r\nIt’s worth asking whether maintaining and evolving a single governance tool should really cost $1 million per year—especially when multiple governance tools are now in development. Each of these projects will likely request funding from the Treasury. In that context, I believe $1M should be enough to support several tools, not just one.\r\nI believe that as these tools mature and stabilize, their maintenance costs will naturally decrease. \r\nMore broadly, I think the development of governance infrastructure needs better coordination. Without it, we risk fragmentation and inefficient use of resources.\r\nIn the end, I chose to support the proposal.\r\nGovernance is still a relatively new component of our ecosystem, and early-stage support is essential. Many tools are still in development—some are incomplete, others don’t function as expected, and improvements are clearly needed.\r\nEffective on-chain governance depends on robust infrastructure. Cardano has committed to building governance on-chain, and to succeed, we must bring its infrastructure to a mature, reliable state.\r\nI recall that navigating budget proposals in GovTool was noticeably less intuitive compared to Ekklesia. We saw governance actions submitted incorrectly. Many DReps don’t provide rationales for their votes, and technical hurdles may be a contributing factor.\r\nAll that is evidence that the tooling isn’t yet where it needs to be.\r\nBetter-designed tools can encourage stronger engagement from DReps and delegators. \r\nAnother reason I support this project is its commitment to being fully open-source. In a decentralized ecosystem, open access is key to building trust.\r\nOne final reason I’m supporting the proposal is simple: GovTool is my go-to platform for governance. It’s the tool I rely on most, so it feels natural to stand behind something I actively use.\r\nThat said, I’d really like to see the team optimize GovTool over time so that it becomes less costly to maintain. As the platform matures, I hope its upkeep will become more efficient.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQQp3NPWgEuVBWWCzv9Ek6iytqVsD1yQtJDKn1oxfv5Fk -->\r\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOn behalf of CASIA team, I’m voting no on this proposal — not because I don’t support GovTool (I do), but because the ₳1.15M ask feels too high right now (~ 100k ada/ month)\r\n\r\nI get that a lot of work has gone into it, and the team clearly cares, but jumping straight to the top funding tier without trying a more phased or leaner approach first just doesn’t sit right. Especially with Treasury funds, I think we need to be a bit more cautious.\r\n\r\nWould love to see a trimmed-down version, maybe start with just maintenance + community incentives, then build up from there based on progress. That would make a yes vote much easier.\r\n\r\nPlus cost benchmarking to prove value for money for community is a plus point",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/Info_14.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis was a tough vote for me.  Initially I was inclined to vote NO due to the steep asking price and the history of UX issues.  After some more thought, I started to lean toward ABSTAIN because the UX issues have improved substantially and because GovTools happens to be one of few open-source governance platforms on Cardano.  I also think that GovTools having a budget of its own is overkill and that it would be better suited as part of another budget such the OSC's (Open Source Committee).  But after reading through the longer, detailed version of the proposal linked at the end, I've come to understand a few more key features that may justify the higher price tag.\r\n\r\nIn particular, the integration with CoSponsor to develop a smart contract solution to crowdsource governance action deposits is sorely needed.  That development on its own is likely to require a substantial amount of effort beyond developing and maintaining the GovTools site.  Other features like performing multiple votes in a single transaction and improvements to the proposal discussion section are also in the works.\r\n\r\nGiven these additional considerations, I am casting a vote of YES on this info action on the condition that the features proposed are delivered adequately, and that any future asks from the Cardano treasury are significantly smaller in scope.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/Vote_Rationale_07072025.jsonld -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAt the end of the day this tool needs to exist and we should support it to ensure governance in Cardano is sustainable and viable solution for users to use.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Christopher Erckert Dotare",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeWMSz8n7tkW5NiuJUur8jHyyjwSrCbq2H4HRLmP8vmpF -->\r\n# Christopher Erckert Dotare\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg8aktnf09gdd0jpyhuz3fy22mfjrqrg2ru52907zeeeeqcra6xhe`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile there are other tools out there, this is an investment in continued innovation for governance infrastructure. Supporting diverse approaches strengthens the whole ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CoinCeylon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTPPb5ziybpjvjJ9yjyfvpRAVT2831RAvPTCztgieGKrZ -->\r\n# CoinCeylon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfg2u28p4xuh5u5lv839vcfd6k2knptfw0avtefpyw4x3dsu5pu25`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFor more in-depth information on our voting rationales you can visit our DRep page at - www.CoinCeylon.com/Drep",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
