    {
      "voter": "Dumpling🥟",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVd1rVsPXC8aA9bJFWsyqBd1ARNp8FqW9FLuyqabUd1iD -->\r\n# Dumpling🥟\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rtf58m0lv9spcqx5mads20gpfulf6l97w57ecdy00vjdq0klh4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n这是一个由多个长期参与 Cardano 治理工具建设的开发者组成的联盟发起的提案，目标在未来 12 个月内持续开发和维护 GovTool 这套开放式治理工具系统。\r\n\r\nGovTool 致力于为 Cardano 提供一个中立、可扩展的 DRep 治理界面，降低普通用户参与治理的门槛，并减少当前对钱包推荐和社交曝光的依赖。 此次提案还规划了多项功能更新，包括 DRep 投票历史展示、群体 DRep 支持、联合发起治理提案（CoSponsor）、预投票调查机制，以及支持多语言参与的 AI 工具，都旨在提高治理透明度和 DRep 参与率。\r\n\r\n预算方面相较此前版本有所缩减，并引入模块化结构，便于阶段性评估和监督。\r\n\r\n有反对者主要指出：当前已有其他替代平台，且预算偏高，部分基础设施支出被认为高于市场平均水平；也有声音呼吁更强的财政控制，建议缩减后再提交。\r\n\r\n但综合考虑 GovTool 的中立性、开源，以及未来在推动治理参与方面的潜力，我认为利大于弊，因此投出赞成票。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Govtools_.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n\r\nEMURGO as DRep abstains from the governance action to fund Cardano GovTool – Budget for 12 months of full active maintenance and development.\r\n\r\nRationale:\r\nWe recognize that GovTool plays a vital role in shaping Cardano’s on-chain governance experience. The proposal outlines clear intentions and presents ongoing improvements in transparency and accessibility. However, there are still areas that need deeper clarity, particularly regarding execution risk and delivery accountability.\r\n\r\nThe timing of this proposal coincides with a pivotal moment in Cardano’s governance development. While the team behind the proposal is respected and has been involved since the tool’s inception, this context places even more importance on demonstrating operational resilience and clearly defined milestones. As it stands, the proposal leaves room for doubt regarding whether the team can sustain momentum and meet expectations in this critical phase.\r\n\r\nWe abstain from voting at this time, not out of opposition, but out of caution. We invite the proposers to strengthen their narrative around execution strategy and delivery assurance to ensure lasting trust in Cardano's foundational governance infrastructure",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00015_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted ABSTAIN on gov_action1n5sn54mgf47a7men2ryq6ppx88kta4wvenz2qkl4f9v6ppje8easqxwm88m; The requested amount is way too high for the proposed work and what has beed delivered so far. Eternl could help hosting gov.tools in it's current state, if no other solution is available.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ferdz",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://defendf7.github.io/drep/votes/Vote_Context_00002.jsonld -->\r\n# Ferdz\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2tf4f0ls404aenhhjqmyh4zvklzy8azqmpxseqea2sd4esfc2d5z`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFerdz has been using the Cardano GovTool for his DRep activities, so I would naturally vote Yes for this tool in support to its community builders.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Florian Volery",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQSfW3njNr7E7gNFEC6NzNQW61sgTwsgpju6GkBhydUuu -->\r\n# Florian Volery\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yguh6dsgx0g58v8pqmxgfrkq0x8vfv6tcp92uzzjrykwy8cjmelsy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo voting system has been developped quickly and is really good. No sure GovTool competes with Tempo.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZWw5HSsazcsxavEQpj3oHPe5MhnBViLu2e4EeDpjurDD -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGov.tools remains buggy with minimal features and poor UI/UX when compared to other community governance tools available (tempo.vote, ekklesia). Thankfully there have been some minor improvements, but the service has a long way to go.\r\n\r\nThe amount requested is extremely high when compared to the budget requested by competitor product tempo.vote . The amount asked for maintenance costs for a gov.tools service that plans to add no features for $330K /  ₳412.5K is ridiculous.\r\n\r\nI would much rather support competitor services financially when they are willing to continue to maintain their products and add new features for less than this in a 6 month period of time.\r\n\r\nGov.tools still does not even have a proper bug ticketing/reporting system, as there is no way to get email correspondence or follow-up for any bugs that are encountered and not resolved.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmR4iyxynoQjc1GEgsLpyoAMjoEVgWPgeh9VnNm8k1tGpb -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for the following reasons:\r\n1.** GovTool remains core infrastructure:** Despite UI limitations, GovTool's API is still referenced by tools such as 1694.io and cardanobudget.com. Maintaining GovTool ensures continuity for existing services built on top of it.\r\n\r\n2. **The revised budget is more transparent and cost-effective: **Compared to the previous ₳2M proposal, this version reduces the budget by 43%, introduces a tiered structure, and uses milestone-based smart contracts to improve transparency and control.\r\n\r\n3.** Community feedback has been integrated: **After 4 weeks of consultations, the proposal now includes support for open contribution and funding for complementary governance tools — not just GovTool itself.\r\n\r\nSupporting this proposal does not imply GovTool is perfect, but acknowledges its current role in governance infrastructure and the need to maintain it while improvements continue.\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\nTôi bỏ phiếu YES vì các lý do sau:\r\n\r\n1. **GovTool vẫn là hạ tầng cốt lõi:** Dù còn bất tiện về giao diện, API của GovTool hiện vẫn được nhiều nền tảng như 1694.io và cardanobudget.com tham chiếu. Việc duy trì GovTool đảm bảo sự ổn định cho các dịch vụ đang hoạt động.\r\n\r\n2. **Ngân sách được điều chỉnh rõ ràng, minh bạch hơn:** So với đề xuất ₳2M trước đây, phiên bản mới giảm chi phí 43%, chia theo các cấp độ và sử dụng hợp đồng thông minh theo mốc, giúp tăng tính minh bạch và khả năng kiểm soát.\r\n\r\n3. **Tiếp thu phản hồi cộng đồng:** Đề xuất đã được chỉnh sửa sau 4 tuần tham vấn, có cơ chế hỗ trợ đóng góp từ cộng đồng và tài trợ cho các công cụ bổ trợ khác – không chỉ riêng GovTool.\r\n\r\nViệc ủng hộ đề xuất này không có nghĩa GovTool đã hoàn hảo, mà là sự công nhận vai trò hiện tại của nó trong hạ tầng quản trị và nhu cầu duy trì hoạt động trong khi tiếp tục cải tiến.\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\nJapanese\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n以下の理由により、YESに投票します：\r\n\r\n①GovToolは依然として中核的なインフラです。UXに課題はあるものの、GovToolのAPIは現在も1694.ioやcardanobudget.comなどのガバナンスツールで使用されています。GovToolを維持することで、既存サービスの継続性が確保されます。\r\n\r\n②予算構成が改善され、透明性が向上：以前の₳2M提案に比べて、コストは43%削減され、階層化された構造とマイルストーンベースのスマートコントラクトが導入されています。これにより、資金管理の透明性と柔軟性が向上します。\r\n\r\n③コミュニティからのフィードバックを反映：本提案は4週間の意見収集を経て修正され、外部貢献者の支援やGovTool以外のツールへの資金提供も含まれています。\r\n\r\nこの提案を支持することはGovToolが完璧であるという意味ではなく、ガバナンスインフラにおける現在の役割を認め、改善を進めながらも維持する必要があることを示すものです。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://Qmf2bhMawst64W8ir975b3cwRSHpTzc3F7AX1guMuiLi1s -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNo! This budget is *much* too large for the little that has been delivered so far and especially in comparison to other tools that provide the same, often even better functionality in governance portals as well as just as additional functionality of wallet apps. It's just not worth it. This is an example of a project that has grown *way* out of reasonable proportion when everything was centralised at IOG and Intersect. Let's scratch that!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmat8aDbCQMyRp8RvYGiZxEyY8dZbsWeodnsJ9LEoVRLAU -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough GovTool needs more UI improvements, I agree with that our ecosystem must have a non-profit form governance tool development. However, this still needs more explanation on the budget detail that require the large amount of funds.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Homer J",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hodlonaut/a/refs/heads/master/vote4.jsonld -->\r\n# Homer J\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rvnp40ea4zsl4hqm0ev4qju205jx7mz57u2vwjzzrf50c24jca9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I've used gov.tools website from time to time and have seen some areas improve based on feedback (thanks for that),, the amount requested seems a bit excessive - would be good to see a more detailed breakdown of current costs, ditching the 'incentivization' component and more succinct explanation on what the money is to be spent on... yes, I see four pillars being defined, but what're the expected deliverables under each pillar for 12 month timeframe (which starts when exactly - when treasury withdrawal is submitted on-chain?). \"Any unused funds will be returned to the Cardano Treasury\" is also not binding/enforceable presumably.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HOSKY",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmQGhhyYj1CrpePwnxDdspW3yYbqRM49QJvAXoks9GMzVt -->\r\n# HOSKY\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf2jzhuc4f7eu2yay9d9ta3dykxxcwn34wz8kak7nhd7vcgrxn7ns`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmUsh8MLfRCkqxF7jrZKDNWdD4nUF9rUtoT3n6hJfC97gK\r\n\r\n## **Rationale for Voting Against the GovTool Budget Proposal**\r\n\r\n### **Commitment to Cardano’s Long-Term Success**\r\n\r\nAs a DRep aligned with the principles of **Cardano First**, my role is to ensure that treasury funds are deployed responsibly, with clear justification and demonstrable community benefit. This responsibility is rooted in both the **Cardano Constitution** and the **HOSKY DRep Platform commitments**. Fiscal conservatism, sustainability, and decentralization are my guiding principles.\r\n\r\n### **Past Performance Must Inform Future Funding Decisions**\r\n\r\nGovTool has been an important experiment in governance tooling, but its actual performance to date raises serious concerns. The platform has consistently faced:\r\n\r\n* **Reliability issues** that have impacted governance participation.\r\n* **User experience problems** that create barriers rather than reducing them.\r\n* **A track record of instability** despite previous funding rounds.\r\n\r\nFunding decisions should not be based on intentions or potential alone. They must consider **prior execution and delivery**, especially when large sums of community treasury funds are involved.\r\n\r\n### **The Proposal Lacks Sufficient Justification for Renewed Investment**\r\n\r\nWhile the GovTool budget proposal outlines a **tiered funding model** and claims cost reductions, it remains focused on further expanding GovTool’s footprint. However, it fails to adequately address the core problem: **the current tool has not proven stable or reliable enough to justify this level of additional investment**.\r\n\r\nSpending millions of ADA to continue building on a foundation that has yet to meet basic expectations is **not fiscally responsible**. The community deserves a higher standard of performance before further committing significant resources.\r\n\r\n### **Decentralization Requires Supporting Diverse Solutions**\r\n\r\nOne of Cardano’s core constitutional tenets is **decentralization**, not just in block production or voting but also in the tooling ecosystem. Concentrating treasury funding into a single governance platform—especially one with unresolved technical issues—risks creating a **de facto monopoly on governance interfaces**, which undermines healthy competition and decentralization of tooling.\r\n\r\nThere are **other governance tools emerging in the ecosystem** that are showing promise, including platforms with better uptime, more focused scope, and innovative approaches. Treasury funds should encourage a **competitive and diversified governance ecosystem**, not reinforce reliance on a single solution.\r\n\r\n### **Fiscal Conservatism Protects the Treasury for Long-Term Needs**\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I take my duty to safeguard the **Cardano Treasury** seriously. The Treasury belongs to the entire community and must be preserved for initiatives that have:\r\n\r\n* **Clear, measurable impact**\r\n* **Proven operational success**\r\n* **Alignment with long-term decentralization and security goals**\r\n\r\nGovTool has not yet demonstrated that it meets these criteria. Approving additional funding without clear evidence of past success would set a dangerous precedent for how we manage communal resources.\r\n\r\n### **Conclusion: A Vote for Accountability and Diversity**\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I will vote **against the current GovTool budget proposal**. This decision is not anti-GovTool but pro-accountability, pro-diversification, and pro-Cardano. I support funding governance tools, but only when they have proven their reliability, demonstrated clear return on investment, and contributed to a competitive ecosystem that protects decentralization.\r\n\r\nI encourage the community to **support a broader funding strategy that rewards proven results and fosters multiple governance options**, ensuring resilience, competition, and the best outcomes for Cardano’s future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/InputEndorsers/DRep-InputEndorsers/refs/heads/main/GovTools%20budget%20Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this reworked and improved GovToools proposal. \r\n\r\nThe original proposal for Cardano GovTool that was rejected by DReps was worth ₳2 million. I voted NO on that previous one (earlier this year) due to concerns about the size of the budget request and a perceived (from my point of view) lack of agility and responsiveness of GovTool to the concerns from DReps who were one of the end user categories of their tool. \r\n\r\nMy key concern was mainly the inability to vote in a smooth and orderly and uninterrupted fashion over GovTools. The user experience was not there. However, my NO vote was mostly a message - that they need to go back to the drawing board. \r\n\r\nI originally voted NO mainly because of: (a) perceived high cost vs what we were using (b) lack of engagement by GovTools team to proactively prevent voting disruptions on their platform. \r\nMy impression is that the GovTool team rolled with the punches and managed to turn what was a major loss into a much better proposal and improved approach to how GovTools should be developed (with community feedback). \r\n\r\nEqually importantly for me - the new budget info action adds up to ₳1.15 million. The Tier 3 (most robust) version encompassing full active dev & maintenance (for ₳1.15 M) delivers the same five-pillar (Proposals Pillar, Delegation Pillar, Voting Pillar, Outcomes Pillar and Budget Discussions Pillar) coverage for 43 % less ADA. Savings mainly come from slimmer FTE assumptions and sharing ops overhead.\r\n\r\nThey regrouped, refocused, held Twitter spaces and consultations with the community. They now submitted this budget info action - separately from Intersect. Although the details of the administration process are aligned with the structure provided by Intersect as administrator. \r\n\r\nThe new proposal was drafted with users after four weeks of feedback. It also dedicates funds to grassroots contributors and companion tools. This is an important concession and a strong match for Cardano’s decentralized and participatory ethos. This should remain part of GovTools philosophy as we progress. \r\nI welcome the team's idea to introduce a tiered structure and streamed contracts - allowing DReps to dial spending up or down and stop payment quickly if milestones slip.\r\n\r\nThe explicit grants for projects like 1694.io or Tempo.vote and cardanobudget.com also are encouraging for creating \"an ecosystem of complementary front-ends\" rather than a single monopoly tool.\r\n\r\nAs regards the constitutionality of this proposal, I defer the ultimate judgement of this aspect of this proposal to the Interim Constitutional Committee.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Jakub Szyca",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jakubszyca/Cardano-Drep/refs/heads/main/Raw-Votes-Context/Vote_Context_5.jsonld -->\r\n# Jakub Szyca\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytee8ue66qdqkfquq5c9hld7trhxvqdra5plfhyuragcfsgrqen4n`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote yes for this proposal because I believe open-source, neutral, and community-owned governance tools are essential to keeping governance alive and improving participation. I think the full amount (Level 3) should be allocated not only to maintain but also to improve the tool. Other governance tools, like Tempo, offer features that I believe GovTool should implement, some of which are already included in the proposed roadmap and require funding. Overall, GovTool provides a much stronger foundation and has a proven track record. It's good to have multiple options for users, but I see GovTool as the backbone of Cardano governance, and as such, it should be prioritized for development. I was disappointed that it wasn't included in the Intersect budget for 2025, and I hope this new proposal will be approved.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Jday1100",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNsvcJS2vM1PZxz2YRoVRbCX49WeSQZxcVy8yjQek7NWt -->\r\n# Jday1100\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygustv8e9wtn00z98vhrz86n4qwcvvv97t7q659ufvxpnkq24mnjg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn general I am of similar mind to others who have voted yes here. Governance needs to get better in general and I think supporting this will make everything easier in the future. The more support governance gets the better it is for Cardano overall.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kyle Solomon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adosiawolf/drep-rationale/refs/heads/main/0007 -->\r\n# Kyle Solomon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzshxuma6cwrnlv2ucyclfqw3k4nu4nuudmh2z87j9hncsk9dhy4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted NO on the current proposal to fund GovTool.\r\n\r\nThe proposal addresses areas well-beyond foundational maintenence, and into needs not yet defined by the community. Furthermore, lights-on maintenence should cost sub ~$50k anually with adequately scalable serverless infrastructure. GovTool failing to support CLI-based voting out the gate reveals a great deal of incompetance around Cardano governance and inconsideration for our community and ethos. Hard NO fam.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kylix",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWFS3D9GwxtLUY4d425KmycVQ2S6Nk76RBmSws6Vys2YM -->\r\n# Kylix\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzdvw4eqvkt050ul07jrycxfrgyqcqvzsclgwx9v6wmm7qx2gf50`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI do not support the GovTool budget proposal in its current form for the following reasons:\r\n- I think the budget is too high for the complexity of the project\r\n- I think some of the things that are being proposed in the budget do not justify their cost\r\n- I believe the GovTool team's past performance and that of their competition (namely Tempo.vote) demonstrates that there are more competitive teams out there capable of building more stable and usable alternatives at a lower cost for Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LallyMcClay",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LallyMack/Drep-it/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(4).jsonld -->\r\n# LallyMcClay\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2dptycrks2ggae95leeh66m0l0svet98c44hl4rmaec7as6hgpp3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting Yes to support this proposal because I believe maintaining and developing open governance tools like GovTool is essential for Cardano’s ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThis proposal meets the criteria outlined in the Constitution, including Article III Section 4, which connects to the ecosystem budget, and Article IV Section 1, which supports tools that maintain and grow the blockchain ecosystem. It also contributes directly to participatory and decentralized governance, which is at the heart of Article III overall.\r\n\r\nGovTool is a public good. It’s not owned by a company, it’s not commercial, and it exists to make Cardano governance accessible and fair for everyone. It’s open source, built with input from the community, and designed to be reused and built upon. That approach takes more time and coordination, but it's the right one for a decentralized ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThe proposal includes a clear breakdown of costs, covering 12 months of work across all environments (Dev, QA, Preview, PreProd, Mainnet). It also explains how funds are allocated and provides historical cost data for transparency. Most of the real effort sits in the backend and infrastructure that powers not just GovTool’s interface, but many other governance tools in the ecosystem too.\r\n\r\nThis funding will help ensure that GovTool remains a reliable, community-owned platform for participation.\r\n\r\nI also note that any unused funds will be returned to the treasury, which shows good practice.\r\n\r\nFor all these reasons, I believe this is a fair and necessary proposal that strengthens Cardano’s ability to govern itself.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Latam Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LatamCardanoDRep/DREP/refs/heads/main/Vote%20govtools%2021-07-25.jsonld -->\r\n# Latam Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytgsdkfznvjnwdxrzvf8x6tn4ctfukqqphsammzkfwatgsqgnpf2w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal has our full support. GovTool is an indispensable public good for the Cardano ecosystem, crucial for fostering accessible and fair governance for every participant. Unlike commercial ventures, GovTool is an open-source, community-built platform, designed to be reused and expanded upon by the community. While this collaborative development demands more time and coordination, it is unequivocally the right approach for a decentralized ecosystem like Cardano.\r\n\r\nThe proposal provides a meticulous breakdown of costs for 12 months of work across all environments (Dev, QA, Preview, PreProd, Mainnet), clearly explaining fund allocation and offering historical cost data for complete transparency. This funding is vital to ensure GovTool remains a stable, community-owned hub for participation. Furthermore, the commitment to return any unused funds to the treasury demonstrates exceptional fiscal responsibility. For these compelling reasons, we consider this a fair and absolutely necessary proposal that significantly strengthens Cardano's ability to govern itself.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LloydDuhon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbcnXE8ipE5sFP9q4SpMGCwnaeYRgfyB1Cw9kRXPyjmNS -->\r\n# LloydDuhon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfvw769lf7g5p4hx0cl2f8jxdcufdcqqj36u0n9escjcwdswcj4h6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGovTool is a critical component to our governance system. Most of the other governance tools rely on the APIs of GovTool to function.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0014/Vote_Context%20(4).jsonld -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this Info Action because GovTool is essential infrastructure for Cardano’s decentralized governance. It enables ADA holders to participate in governance actions—registering, delegating, proposing, and voting\r\n\r\nMaintaining and improving GovTool is critical for inclusive, accessible, and decentralized governance. Supporting this proposal means investing in the foundation that makes Cardano governance work—for everyone.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Medusa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adawallet.io/public_files/votes/9d213a57684d7ddf6f3350c80d042639ecbed5ccccc4a05bf54959a086593e7b.jsonld -->\r\n# Medusa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg5pzxhp0lu0m7757ww2hke8qhcuqgqt3c2ezphngwytz4gjr6yge`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a developer and DevOps specialist, I believe the requested amount is significantly overestimated and does not reflect the actual needs of a project of this type.\r\n\r\nI also run an independent node and indexer. The Medusa cluster consists of 5 servers: one server running cardano-db-sync with 12 cores and 64 GB of RAM; three servers running cardano-node, providing redundancy and data to the db-sync, each with 8 cores and 24 GB of RAM; and a frontend server with 4 cores and 4 GB of RAM. Each server is connected to a reliable 2 Gbps channel.\r\n\r\nThe cluster operates stably and without interruption, serving around 600 unique users per day on average, with peaks reaching 1,000 at epoch boundaries. While that may not sound like a lot, wallet synchronization happens continuously, and in reality, the cluster processes tens or even hundreds of thousands of requests daily — even when users take no active actions after logging in.\r\n\r\nI pay around $100 per month in total for this infrastructure.\r\n\r\nYou are requesting approximately $27,500 per month for infrastructure and maintenance(I’m not even considering the other items or amounts — only this one), based on the current exchange rate.\r\n\r\nEven if all 948 DReps registered in the Cardano network — and we both know that’s objectively impossible — accessed your service and voted, it wouldn’t produce even 1% of the load my cluster handles. That’s assuming they all logged in and voted on the same day, which is also highly unrealistic. Voting events are infrequent and spread over time. Yes, nodes and db-sync do operate between voting periods as well — but so do mine, even when nobody is accessing them. Three nodes and one db-sync — all for $100 per month.\r\n\r\nSo my answer is “NO.”",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmT5tSfpZvjFQPjSgh6jtR7BV8z31hMrGG4mHLsFFUQZXt -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/Qmdpr8pymrR5fYnKf6p3bH6nc411vbPBMom828jgV7QtXE\r\n\r\nI believe the core value of governance accessibility is key, meaning that any ada holder should be able to participate in Cardano Governance, regardless of their technical proficiency. GovTools makes Cardano governance accessible, it allows the normal ada holder to directly participate: register as a DRep, delegate to a DRep, vote as a DRep, and even proposing governance actions.\r\n\r\nGiven my commitment to accessibility, I have a responsibility to support initiatives that uphold and strengthen this principle. The GovTools budget info action requests 1.15M ada, with a notable allocation of 250k ada specifically designated for direct community contributions. This earmarked amount (level 2 funding) supports not only GovTools but also other governance tool builders, which is commendable and beneficial for fostering a diverse ecosystem.\r\n\r\nAnother compelling factor is that GovTools operates as open-source software. Funding from the treasury would therefore support a public good available to all, rather than proprietary software benefiting only a select group. This openness encourages further innovation, allowing others to build upon GovTools and develop competing governance tools, thus reducing the risk of monopoly.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the GovTools team has demonstrated transparency and community-mindedness by proactively sharing tutorials on how to deploy individual instances of GovTools(https://docs.gov.tools/cardano-govtool/run-govtool-locally/getting-started). Such transparency enhances trust and ensures broader community participation and oversight.\r\n\r\nHowever, I would advise the GovTools team to maintain a clear focus on essential governance functionalities: delegation, voting, governance action submission, and providing a robust data layer for on-chain governance. Prioritizing these core areas, along with ensuring adherence to open data standards, will help avoid creating isolated silos, further promoting interoperability and ease of use within our governance ecosystem.\r\n\r\nUltimately, this proposal represents a valuable investment in sustaining and enhancing accessible, and transparent governance on Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
