    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA020-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"Sim\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action1n5sn54mgf47a7men2ryq6ppx88kta4wvenz2qkl4f9v6ppje8easqxwm88m), pois o GovTools é a principal ferramenta de participação na governança, fornecendo as funcionalidades que algumas carteiras ainda não têm disponíveis, como a carteira Lace. Portanto, sua manutenção e continuidade são essenciais para o amadurecimento da governança, favorecendo o aumento de participação da comunidade.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"Yes\" on this governance action (gov_action1n5sn54mgf47a7men2ryq6ppx88kta4wvenz2qkl4f9v6ppje8easqxwm88m), because GovTools is the main tool for participating in governance, providing features that some wallets, such as Lace, do not yet offer. Therefore, its maintenance and continuity are essential for the maturation of governance and to foster increased community participation.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRrN9s4v4KrXd1hmgoa8SH8mAE9dpALozuNL5rJscikC1 -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA is abstaining from voting Yes or No on this Info Action, **while signaling general support** for the continuation of GovTool as a cornerstone of Cardano’s decentralized governance. This decision is made in the spirit of constructive feedback, intended to encourage improvements before a follow-up Treasury Withdrawal proposal is submitted.\r\nGovTool plays a vital role in enabling open, non-custodial and inclusive participation in on-chain governance. Its development to date has been largely community-led and the proposal’s updated modular budget structure, combined with working group feedback mechanisms, is a step in the right direction. The value provided—both through its interface and API infrastructure—is real and has been critical in onboarding new DReps and participants.\r\n\r\nThat said, I remain concerned about aspects of the proposal’s execution plan. The Level 2 incentives remain too vague in their allocation criteria, lacking specificity around expected outcomes or eligibility. The milestone-based funding disbursements could benefit from stronger definitions of deliverables and while the proposal references smart contract safeguards, it does not make clear how unused funds will be transparently returned. I also remain cautious about the current governance structure of GovTool, which—though community-led in principle—relies heavily on a small, tightly coordinated group of builders. If this is to scale as public infrastructure, decentralizing its stewardship must become a priority.\r\n\r\nImportantly, the current DRep approval rate is now over 44%, which is encouraging and suggests growing confidence in the proposal. My abstention is not opposition—it is a constructive request for clarity. With stronger articulation of milestone criteria, incentive logic and guardrails, I would be prepared to vote Yes on a follow-up Treasury Withdrawal.\r\n\r\n>>>>>\r\n**RCADA Rationale 02.08.2025 - Update**:\r\n\r\nI would like to thank the GovTool proposers for thoughtfully addressing the concerns raised in my previous rationale. Their clarifications regarding the Level 2 incentives—particularly the use of bounty-based platforms like Andamio for open-source contributions—and their commitment to define clearer milestone-based disbursements ahead of any Treasury Withdrawal proposal are encouraging signs of a responsive governance process.\r\nI also acknowledge their clear intent to decentralize development and scale community participation and I recognize the current modular architecture as a strong foundation for long-term resilience.\r\n\r\nIn light of these clarifications, I am updating my vote to a **Conditional Yes**, in support of the value GovTool brings to the ecosystem and its importance as public digital infrastructure. However, my continued support for any **Treasury Withdrawal proposal remains contingent** on follow-through: specifically, the inclusion of measurable deliverables, transparent fund allocation and a clearer roadmap addressing **long-term financial sustainability** and a strategy for reducing ongoing reliance on Treasury funding. It will be important that GovTool does not become a permanent funding dependency without cost controls or alternatives for long-term maintenance.\r\n\r\nI offer this vote as a signal of cautious optimism and constructive collaboration.\r\n\r\n**Side-note for proposers:**\r\nI’d like to recommend that future iterations of this proposal or its roadmap include a structured campaign to address the ongoing issue of low governance participation across the Cardano community. \r\nWhile GovTool is a vital infrastructure layer, its impact is ultimately limited unless we grow the number of ADA holders actively participating—through delegation, proposal review, and voting.\r\nI encourage the proposers and Intersect to incorporate a community engagement and onboarding strategy within the funding scope or support it as a parallel initiative, possibly via Level 2 incentives. \r\nAddressing this gap will improve representation and strengthen the legitimacy of on-chain decisions.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Reshma_Mohan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/resgsh/drep-mainnet/refs/heads/main/voting-activity/4.Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Reshma_Mohan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfcgvh8rum7a9ma4gwgwuwutdu0dnrzaj98jytwyfqzd87q2nehvm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES because this proposal strengthens an already functional and essential governance platform—GovTool—through clear, community-led improvements.\r\n\r\nIt enhances user experience and reliability based on real feedback, and introduces dedicated development across key governance areas: proposals, delegation, voting, outcomes, and budget discussions. It also adds full end-to-end testing and continues to follow an open, transparent development model.\r\n\r\nGovTool is vital for inclusive governance—without it, participation risks becoming fragmented or limited to closed systems. This proposal ensures continued access, usability, and clarity for all Ada holders.\r\n\r\nThe platform’s open-source nature offers ecosystem-wide benefits. Its code and APIs are already used by other tools, and ₳250k is earmarked to support external contributors and open governance tools building on it.\r\n\r\nFunding is structured through tiered levels and smart contracts, ensuring transparency, cost-efficiency (nearly 50% lower than earlier proposals), and responsible allocation. Unused funds will return to the Treasury.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons—continued platform improvement, increased governance efficiency, and ecosystem-wide open-source value—I strongly support this proposal and vote YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rod G",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdsPFjGaXbD7Jcg33saLUYSU9GR162WEoDataJPSUxm77 -->\r\n# Rod G\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwscks2yt0na4fqpcdyqn0fare5v48y0mjgn2g478lnx8gue393e`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe need these governance tools and GovTool has been instrumental in this first iteration.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RudianosDrep/RudianosDrep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%2013.jsonld -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving this proposal. At first glance the budget seems high, but it is significantly lower than the initial proposal, which was made during the intersect proposal process. Additionally, there are good explanations with this proposal on why the funds requested are required, and this comes from a significant amount of community interaction, which answers most open questions not answered by the first proposal. For anyone interested, check the full long-form proposal, as it has many additional details that helped me make an informed decision. The most important consideration for me, however, is simply one of protecting the integrity of the Cardano voting system. There are no monetary incentives at this stage for anyone to build governance tools. Therefore, having a treasury funded, community based, open source system is very important. It may be that as time goes on this need will no longer be there, but for now this is the prudent option, and I believe it is well worth the costs outlined.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmStQPrECjwRfyLagtHA3osPi7eGLM3Ejy7T24wdB9FFRD -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nGovTool is the primary interface for decentralized governance on Cardano and a critical public good. This proposal ensures 12 months of continued maintenance and development, led by a trusted consortium of community builders under an open, transparent, and modular funding model.\r\n\r\nThe budget is well-structured, cost-reduced from previous versions, and backed by Intersect’s smart contract-based fund management. It also supports external contributors and open-source tools through clear incentive pathways.\r\n\r\nFor Cardano governance to remain inclusive, neutral, and accessible to all, investing in GovTool is not optional—it’s essential.\r\n\r\n\r\n僕はこの提案にYES票を投じます。\r\n\r\nGovToolはCardanoにおける分散型ガバナンスの主要なインターフェースであり、重要な公共財です。この提案は、信頼あるコミュニティ主導のコンソーシアムにより、今後12ヶ月のメンテナンスと開発を継続するものです。資金設計は透明性が高く、前回提案からコスト削減されており、Intersectによるスマートコントラクト制御付きで運用されます。\r\n\r\nまた、外部貢献者や他のOSSツール支援も含んだ柔軟な資金設計となっており、コミュニティ主導の開発がより拡張される基盤になります。Cardanoのガバナンスを中立的かつ誰もが参加可能な形で維持するには、GovToolへの投資は不可欠です。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Sebastien Guillemot セバ",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZtCWhqw9kcdfrxii86iuimYvTCSCNyzMeEk7Vjkegfco -->\r\n# Sebastien Guillemot セバ\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2csyxt7u2hl4674pl9cef5lknafaw5nraxvyx033kmd0es3awuv0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe user interface has always been confusing and burdensome. It's a lot of money to ask for a product which I think has delivered a bad experience - especially when there are alternatives that I think work better",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbsuiTbEWWFsEamvWC3TE9ybAgfZgJaF3gSR7YNhy1krG -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough GovTool has laid the foundation for DRep registration and delegation, and play a crucial role in the implementation of CIP-1694, I am unable to support this proposal due to the amount being requested.\r\n\r\nRequesting 1.5m ada for 12 months of maintenance and continued development in my view is excessive. While I acknowledge the importance of improving GovTool’s UI and UX, **the size of the budget and the duration of funding are the primary reasons for my decision.**\r\n\r\nAs a DRep who has consistently advocated for smaller NCL this year and has already approved a budget of approximately 280m ada within an NCL of 300m, I will **abstain **from this vote and leave the decision to my fellow DReps.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/info/20250712_01/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nStatement from SIPO DRep\r\n\r\nWhy I Intend to Vote YES — with Conditions — on the Cardano GovTool Budget Proposal\r\n\r\nGovTool is a critical piece of public infrastructure for decentralized governance on Cardano. I believe it plays an essential role in realizing our shared vision of democratic, participatory, and transparent governance. Supporting its continued development is a necessary step as we move into the next phase of Cardano 2.0.\r\n\r\nIn reviewing this proposal led by Intersect, I recognize several important strengths:\r\n\t•\tThe formation of a new GovTool Consortium that brings together active developers and contributors\r\n\t•\tA strong commitment to open-source, reusable, and community-led development\r\n\t•\tDeep integration with the broader ecosystem, including tools like 1694.io and budget.cardano.africa\r\n\r\nI also note that this proposal comes at a pivotal moment: the Intersect Board has, for the first time, reached a majority of elected members. This signals the beginning of a truly community-governed institution. I believe now is the time to take the next step.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I intend to vote YES, with the following conditions:\r\n\r\n\r\nConditions for My Support:\r\n\t1.\tClear KPIs and Roadmap\r\n I would like to see well-defined, measurable KPIs for each development pillar under Level 3, along with a transparent roadmap and quarterly progress reports.\r\n\t2.\tMidterm Review at 6 Months\r\n While this is a 12-month proposal, I believe a formal midterm evaluation at 6 months is essential to assess progress and maintain accountability for the second half of the funding period.\r\n\t3.\tTransparent Allocation of External Incentives\r\n The process and criteria for distributing the ₳100k for external governance tools and ₳150k for individual contributors should be clearly documented and publicly available to ensure fair and open access.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTo me, GovTool is not just a frontend—it’s the civic gateway to Cardano’s on-chain governance. It must remain open, neutral, and collectively governed by the community it serves.\r\n\r\nI will continue to advocate for a governance system that reflects these values: transparency, inclusion, and accountability. This vote is one step in that direction.\r\n\r\n—\r\nSIPO\r\nDelegated Representative (DRep)\r\nCardano Governance\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep声明\r\n\r\nGovTool開発予算提案に対するSIPOの判断について（条件付き賛成）\r\n\r\nカルダノの分散型ガバナンスの中核インフラとして機能するGovToolは、我々が目指す「参加型・透明性・公共性を備えた民主的ガバナンス」の実現において不可欠な社会的基盤であり、その維持・拡張はCardano 2.0時代への移行にとって重要なステップです。\r\n\r\nSIPOとしては、Intersectが主導するこの提案が、以下の点において前向きな方向性を示していると判断します：\r\n\t•\tガバナンスツール群を構成する開発者・団体による新たな「GovToolコンソーシアム」の発足と透明性の高い提案構造\r\n\t•\tオープンソース・再利用性・分散開発を重視した公共財モデルの継続\r\n\t•\t1694.ioやbudget.cardano.africaなど既存エコシステムとの高い相互運用性\r\n\r\nまた、Intersectが選挙で選ばれた理事が初めて過半数を占める新体制に移行したこのタイミングは、カルダノが真に「分散型で自律的な意思決定構造」へと踏み出す出発点であり、GovToolの維持・発展を通じて、その動きに確かな実行力を与えるべきだと考えます。\r\n\r\nよって、SIPOは以下の条件を付した上で、本提案に賛成票を投じます。\r\n\r\n\r\n【条件事項】\r\n\t1.\tKPIとロードマップの明示\r\n　L3レベルにおける各ピラーの進捗や成果を定量的に可視化するKPIを設定し、四半期ごとの進捗報告をコミュニティに対して行うこと。\r\n\t2.\t中間レビューの制度化（6ヶ月時点）\r\n　12ヶ月満額支出の中で、6ヶ月経過時点での中間レビューを実施し、後半の資金執行に対するガバナンス的チェックポイントを設けること。\r\n\t3.\t外部貢献者支援の配分透明性\r\n　提案内に含まれる ₳100k（外部ツール支援）および ₳150k（個人貢献者支援）の評価基準・配分ルールを文書化し、申請者にとって公平性が担保される仕組みを設けること。\r\n\r\n\r\nGovToolは、カルダノの未来における市民的参加を保証する「公共アクセスインフラ」です。私たちはそれを単なるアプリケーションではなく、分散型民主主義を体現するプラットフォームと捉えています。\r\n\r\nSIPOは今後もこの理念を支え続け、DRepとしてコミュニティの信託に応えるべく、積極的な監視・対話・改善提案を行ってまいります。\r\n\r\n—\r\nSIPO\r\nDRep（Delegated Representative）\r\nCardano Governance",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVkpnRHFYLCB7qyJeDti4iuVgUwFNETFAJSrcLdawYaBw -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe cast a YES vote on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis proposal supports 12 months of maintenance and development for GovTool, a key public infrastructure enabling participation in Cardano’s on-chain governance. It has been jointly submitted by developers including LidoNation, ByronNetwork, WeDeliver, and DQuadrant, and takes into account interoperability with other governance tools.\r\n\r\nIts tiered budget structure, provision for unused fund returns, and smart contract–based fund management and audit mechanisms coordinated by Intersect contribute to decentralization and transparency.\r\n\r\nWe believe this proposal is a vital step toward strengthening Cardano’s decentralized governance culture, while also encouraging wider interoperability and open contribution to governance tooling. Therefore, we support it.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfBNUhZyVJMsq2io7tLg9ZFPcJJe28KmHFx8oLu4WqHNQ -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSTORM Partners is voting “YES” on the Cardano GovTool Budget Info Action.\r\nGovTool plays a critical role in enabling decentralized on-chain governance. As the main interface for governance participation across Cardano, it has become an absolute necessity for the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nWe appreciate that the team went back to the drawing board, listened to community input, and reduced the original request from 2M to 1.15M ADA. That shows responsiveness, maturity, and willingness to adapt according to community needs.\r\n\r\nWhile we still consider the revised budget relatively high for the number of FTEs involved, the impact and reach of GovTool - especially the number of governance tools and platforms that rely on its APIs - justify continued support at this early stage.\r\n\r\nThis proposal helps sustain the backbone of Cardano’s governance, while keeping the door open for improvement. With a commitment to open-source code, transparent communication, a dedicated Intersect WG, and an incentivized contribution model, the community can actively shape GovTool’s future and improve on its weaknesses to create an accessible and open platform for everyone to build upon.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(2).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on the Cardano GovTool Budget Info Action. This proposal ensures the uninterrupted maintenance and development of the core infrastructure that enables inclusive, decentralized governance on Cardano. It is aligned with the Constitution, reflects broad community feedback, offers lean and modular budgeting, and sustains the open-source culture essential to Cardano’s success. Without GovTool, Cardano governance risks becoming inaccessible and fragmented. This is a necessary investment in our collective future.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Dutch Drep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://Qmacoh2x9JRbMdfQN4qANdjz9DVVVXGNhCPRp1qkYdzqHi -->\r\n# The Dutch Drep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yvve4554njxyun2s5p9q70v88d5jl7r0h34pjhw5f5tmw3sjtrutp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Dutch DRep, vote YES on the Govtool budget proposal by the Govtool consortium.\r\n\r\nTransparency Disclosure: One of our Dutch DReps represents Dquadrant, a Govtool consortium member, in community forums. While this relationship informs our understanding, we believe the proposal stands on its own merits and advances Cardano’s governance goals.\r\n\r\nThe Govtool consortium—coordinated through Intersect and backed by trusted community teams—has a proven track record of delivering accessible, constitutionally sound governance tools since CIP‑1694. Their proposal is transparent, well‑structured, and firmly rooted in Cardano’s principles of accountability and community‑driven decision‑making.\r\n\r\nGovtool’s planned enhancements will:\r\n\r\nGuarantee open access for all ADA holders, lowering barriers to participation.\r\n\r\nFoster community ownership through open‑source code and public APIs, enabling developers to build complementary governance solutions.\r\n\r\nSupport a distributed development model by funding multiple teams and encouraging community contributions.\r\n\r\nEnsure the roadmap remains responsive to ADA holders’ needs via transparent, community‑driven prioritization.\r\n\r\nTogether, these improvements will strengthen Cardano’s decentralized governance, boost transparency and efficiency, and align with our long‑term vision of inclusivity and innovation.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TobiasIlskov/GovToolsInfoAction/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(5).jsonld -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGov tools is an open source backend used by many other governance interfaces, both open and proprietary. Improving Gov tools seems like a rising tide for all the governance boats in the race.\r\n\r\nSome of the features to be added include:\r\n- CC vote history and rationale presentation \r\n- Drep voting history interfaces\r\n-Support for Group / Multi person DReps\r\n- Group / Multi person proposers for on-chain actions \r\n- Introduce CoSponsors to Crowdfund ADA for governance action deposits.\r\n- Pre-governance polling, to gauge DRep sentiment before on-chain actions.\r\n- Integration of AI tools to aid in translation, etc to make multi-national involvement in discussion more feasible.\r\n\r\nI like what I see here, and while the proposed budget is larger than I would prefer, I think it will be worth it if the teams involved deliver on all these features well. \r\n\r\nThis is all new; and teams need chances to prove themselves. I am comfortable giving them a year of funding. I will make sure to confirm all these features are delivered before extending their funding next year.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSEWEjczxjCga4eDHFzipJCsK4tYJGZ2ZDoWCt5j4rk8u -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I deeply value the intention behind sustaining and expanding open-source governance infrastructure for Cardano, I am voting No on this proposal primarily because it fails to meaningfully integrate or harmonize with the development of Tempo.vote. \r\n\r\nTempo.vote has emerged as a lightweight, efficient, and highly usable interface for ADA holders and DReps alike. It demonstrates clearer design, improved delegation flows (particularly for hardware wallet users), and a stronger focus on transparency and accessibility for end-users. Despite this, the GovTool proposal does not recognize Tempo.vote as a foundational pillar in the broader governance UX ecosystem, nor does it propose coordinated development pathways or shared architecture.\r\n\r\nCardano’s governance tooling should be modular, interoperable, and responsive to actual community usage patterns. A continued siloed approach—where parallel tools are developed independently without shared planning, funding, or architectural coherence—risks fragmentation, wasted treasury spending, and stagnation in UX innovation.\r\n\r\nUntil proposals like this actively align with promising ecosystem tools like Tempo.vote and build toward an interoperable, composable governance UX stack, I believe treasury funding should be withheld. I strongly encourage a revised proposal that recognizes Tempo.vote not just as a dependent or adjacent application, but as a core strategic component of Cardano’s governance infrastructure.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPaGqPHFNyng4mXNhQ3q1ERiA6W4ghUeU4jBzhK4uCwTU -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFrom a strategic governance perspective, this proposal to continue funding GovTool’s active development and maintenance raises significant concerns regarding the fragmentation and duplication of governance infrastructure within the Cardano ecosystem. While GovTool undeniably plays a critical role as an open-source, community-owned interface facilitating on-chain governance participation, the coexistence and overlap with other platforms—most notably tempo.vote—cannot be ignored. This parallelism risks diluting user engagement, confusing stakeholders, and ultimately weakening the unified governance experience that Cardano must strive to deliver.\r\n\r\nThe proposal’s emphasis on GovTool’s modularity, open APIs, and broad ecosystem integration is commendable; however, it insufficiently addresses the strategic imperative of consolidation. The Treasury resources allocated here—up to ₳1.15M annually—represent a substantial investment that must be justified by demonstrable efficiency gains and a clear roadmap toward interoperability or unification with other governance tools. The absence of explicit plans to harmonize GovTool with tempo.vote or to rationalize overlapping functionalities leaves the community vulnerable to redundant expenditures and operational inefficiencies.\r\n\r\nCardano’s governance strength lies not only in decentralization but in coherence and scalability. Supporting multiple competing governance frontends fragments the community’s attention and complicates the user journey, undermining the inclusivity and accessibility that Voltaire envisions. It is imperative that the Governance Tools Working Group and the GovTool Consortium prioritize strategic alignment with existing platforms, fostering interoperability standards or even converging development efforts to create a singular, robust, and user-friendly governance interface.\r\n\r\nMoreover, from a business-minded stewardship standpoint, we must scrutinize the proposal’s tiered funding structure and ensure that every tranche of expenditure directly contributes to sustainable and scalable governance outcomes. While the modular approach and community feedback integration are positive steps, they do not substitute for a comprehensive strategic framework that safeguards the Treasury and maximizes long-term value for Ada holders.\r\n\r\nIn advancing Cardano’s governance infrastructure, we must reject proliferation in favor of strategic consolidation. The future stability of the protocol and the vitality of its community participation depend on decisive, coordinated action to unify governance tools. Therefore, I support funding GovTool only on the condition that the proposal includes a binding, transparent roadmap for integration or harmonization with tempo.vote and other governance platforms. This is non-negotiable if we are to preserve Treasury resources, enhance user experience, and uphold Cardano’s scientific and decentralized governance ethos.\r\n\r\nI firmly believe that governance tools must empower and unify, not divide, our community. It is time for us, as stewards of Cardano’s future, to make strategic choices that protect our treasury and build a truly scalable, coherent governance ecosystem—one platform, one vision, one Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYCmH7pumU8X3pYDCfM3LG4SuuhyFMkGKAbjDrEVyC6rh -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBy voting \"yay\" I am supporting the allocation of ADA from the Treasury to fund GovTool’s development and maintenance for the next 12 months. This investment ensures that Cardano’s governance infrastructure remains robust and accessible, which is vital for the ecosystem’s success. The requested ₳1,050,500 seems reasonable given the proven track record of what they have delivered so far. If it wasn't for GovTools I wouldn't be here voting today as that's how I got onboarded as a DRep.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Voice of the People",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DRepVoiceOfThePeople/VOP_Repo/refs/heads/main/VC20250703InfoGovtool2025.jsonld -->\r\n# Voice of the People\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ecrj7jd9alaxumvm49hgng9rp239nda5ucegd05ndvxfqftwr9f`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGovTool is Cardano’s primary governance interface, critical for CIP-1694 and Voltaire. This would ensures accessible governance, supports DReps, users...",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_GovTools_BIA.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep, have voted yes on the “Cardano GovTool Budget – 12 Months Full Active Maintenance and Development” proposal. Our support for this request is based on two core principles: governance maturity and community value. This proposal represents a critical step forward in preserving open access to Cardano’s on-chain governance while also modeling how community-funded initiatives should engage, respond, and evolve based on input from stakeholders.\r\n\r\nThe GovTool team has demonstrated remarkable responsiveness to the feedback gathered from DReps, contributors, and the broader community during the 2025 budgeting process. After submitting their initial proposal, they undertook several rounds of consultations through the Governance Tool Working Group, community forums, and open development calls. As a result, the final proposal reflects thoughtful, community-aligned adjustments that meaningfully improve both its scope and its strategic value.\r\n\r\nOne of the most important improvements was the introduction of a tiered funding structure, Levels 1 through 3, which now makes the budget modular and transparent. This allows the community to understand what features and activities are funded at each level of support, from baseline infrastructure maintenance to full-featured active development and incentive programs. This structure reflects a realistic and scalable vision for public goods development under decentralized governance.\r\n\r\nBeyond the process, the features that GovTool will deliver under this proposal stand to benefit the Cardano community in tangible, far-reaching ways.\r\n\r\nGovTool is the primary open-source frontend for Cardano governance, already used by over 48,000 ADA holders across more than 170 countries, as hinted in the proposal. It powers vital governance actions, DRep registration, delegation, proposal creation, voting, and outcome tracking, and integrates with other public tools such as 1694.io, cardanobudget.com, and governancespace.co, etc. Continued investment in GovTool ensures that every ADA holder, not just the technically fluent, can participate meaningfully in Cardano’s governance era.\r\n\r\nThe proposal also strengthens the ecosystem by introducing and funding community incentive pools. These include ₳150K for contributors to the GovTool GitHub repository and ₳100K for developers building interoperable tools using GovTool APIs. This move expands the circle of contributors and helps grow a governance developer ecosystem that is open, competitive, and sustainable.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the team is committed to open APIs, quality assurance (QA), user experience testing, localization efforts, and enhanced support for wallet integrations and backend reliability. These improvements directly address pain points raised during the beta testing phase and will result in a more robust and user-friendly experience for everyone participating in on-chain governance.\r\n\r\nWe are also encouraged by the team’s adherence to constitutional best practices. The proposal is administered through Intersect, using milestone-based smart contracts, and includes refund clauses for unused funds. It complies with all relevant sections of the Cardano Constitution, particularly Articles IV.1 to IV.4.\r\n\r\nIn short, this proposal reflects not just a strong technical project but a governance-aware, community-integrated initiative that has developed through delivery, transparency, and collaboration. It keeps Cardano’s governance layer accessible, protects the neutrality of core infrastructure, and empowers new contributors to build and improve on shared foundations.\r\n\r\nFor all these reasons, its strategic importance, its transparent evolution based on community feedback, and the wide set of features it will deliver for ADA holders, we have voted yes and encourage others to support this essential proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/16_govtools_budget.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGovTools is starting to succumb to feature creep. The scope of GovTools should be restricted to proposing and voting on governance actions. A much more modest budget is appropriate.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Govtools.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep votes YES on the governance action to fund Cardano GovTool – Budget for 12 months of full active maintenance and development.\r\nRationale:\r\n\r\nGovTool is a critical, open-source governance infrastructure that supports the full on-chain process from DRep registration to proposal submission, voting, and outcomes. It aligns closely with Cardano’s CIPs, community-first ethos, and does not pursue commercial interests.\r\nThe team responded transparently and promptly to recent bugs, expanding test coverage, refactoring outdated modules, and improving debugging workflows. These improvements, combined with a growing contributor base, reflect clear lessons learned from past challenges.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nYoroi DRep acknowledges that GovTool still has areas for improvement, particularly in delivery structure and operational clarity. However, we support this proposal because we believe in its mission, its community alignment, and its evolving commitment to reliability and transparency.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmew2WVCmuPjd7hJuMGtjvmpASmPZJU5z87rdz5mtvCNrz -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES for the Govtool proposal.\r\n\r\nHere are the reasons:\r\n\r\nThere are still very big concerns about the barriers to participation in Cardano governance. In particular, the majority of Cardano wallets are reluctant (low priority) to improve governance functions. As a result, a large number of DReps are abstaining and governance participation rates are declining. This needs to be resolved.\r\n\r\nIn particular, only Eternl, Typhon, and Gero wallets meet all of the following criteria.\r\n\r\nDisplay list of DRep in wallet\r\nDRep Name Search Delegation UI\r\n4 clicks + under 30 seconds DRep delegation\r\n\r\nOf these, only Typhon meets DRep Neutrality.\r\n\r\nTo implement these features within the wallet, cooperation from wallet providers is essential, but it may be possible to speed up implementation using Govtool's API and services.\r\n\r\nIn addition, there are few DRep search tools in use. After all, most ADA holders delegate to DReps they have seen on social media or DReps recommended by their wallet providers. A neutral tool to improve these situations is needed.\r\n\r\nAlso, most DReps do not attach the reason for voting, which is related to UI issues. DRep is busy.\r\n\r\nGovtool has promised to manually prioritize the implementation of these features based on DRep/community feedback. I think the cost is not cheap, but considering that Govtool currently provides the most features, there is a high risk of eliminating this.\r\n\r\nI want to ensure that feedback on feature implementations is collected and prioritized to some extent before Treasury Withdrawals.\r\n\r\nーーー\r\n\r\n私はGovtool提案書にYESを投票しました。\r\n\r\n理由は次のとおりです。\r\n\r\nCardanoのガバナンスの参加障壁は非常に大きな懸念が残っています。特にCardanoウォレットの大多数はガバナンス機能の充実化に消極的（優先順位が低い）です。結果として大量の棄権DRepの発生とガバナンス参加率の低下が起きています。これを解決する必要があります。\r\n\r\n特に、次の全てを満たすウォレットはEternl、Typhon、Geroのみです。\r\n\r\nDisplay list of DRep in wallet\t\r\nDRep Name Search Delegation UI\r\n4 clicks + under 30 seconds DRep delegation\r\n\r\nDRep Neutralityを満たすのはその中で、Typhonのみです。\r\n\r\nこれらをウォレット内部で実装するためには、ウォレットプロバイダーの協力が不可欠ですが、Govtool のAPIやサービスなどで実装を早めることが可能である可能性があります。\r\n\r\nまた、結局DRepの検索ツールで使われているものはまずありません。結局のところほとんどのADAホルダーはSNSなどで見かけたDRepまたはウォレットプロバイダーが推奨するDRepに委任しています。これらの状況を改善する中立的なツールが必要です。\r\n\r\nまた、投票理由をほとんどのDRepが添付していませんが、これはUI上の問題が関係しています。DRepは忙しいのです。\r\n\r\nGovtoolはこれらの機能実装をDRep/コミュニティのフィードバック手動で優先順位づけすることを約束しています。コストは安くないと思いますが、しかし現状で最も多くの機能を提供しているのがGovtoolであることを考えると、これを廃止するリスクの方が高い状況にあります。\r\n\r\n私は、トレジャリー引き出しまでに一定程度、機能実装に関するフィードバックが収集され、優先順位づけされていることを確認したいと思います。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
