      "voter": "Musa Ridwan Itopa",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYBzbhiAMwubkxNteZZEUKhLMVpiUzFUTp3pUdPXeB3cp -->\r\n# Musa Ridwan Itopa\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Net Change Limit of 300 Million ADA for Epochs 613–713\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yggumgdxdpa2dgr85etak35s4v00k07vdhvn5y3xxw33yac77c9hp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting YES on Net Change Limit (Epoch 613 to Epoch 713) - 350M ADA cap. As elected Cardano Civics Committee member, Unified Cardano Student Club President in Nigeria, and advocate for Africa/student inclusion, this sets a sustainable treasury ceiling (~Feb 2026–Jul 2027) without blocking governance. No NCL = no withdrawals for education/DeFi/real adoption in emerging markets like ours (**as the treasury is not endless**). Cap averages below inflows for net growth, forces transparency/prioritization, and enables smart spends (e.g., stablecoins for remittances, student tools). Let's protect the treasury while building inclusively not freeze progress.",
