    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihy4m543n624fsrgtp5ceakd6bjacsbfzlqwmcod7q5molwcdlppa -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe support this proposal because adding an additional Constitutional Committee member strengthens governance resilience and reduces the risk of future ratification deadlocks. With the 66.7% approval threshold now in place, a larger CC also raises the absolute bar for approval, improving checks and balances. This action has no treasury impact, does not change CC powers or rules, and helps ensure stable, continuous governance operations.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Feed",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifj3n2do7gy237z7ryej4wet4tkz65rwk5mk2wczn5gyswnndtafe -->\r\n# Cardano Feed\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftjewhpvtdd8t7swtmtp44px94ns3laytmjc3u7f93qvhswmwv5f`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes. This proposal strengthens governance continuity by adding an extra Constitutional Committee member, reducing the risk of delays if a member becomes inactive. It respects the Cardano Constitution, CIP-1694, and prior governance actions, and supports a resilient, permissionless governance process.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmUddPgnyoTnEmwM3v4Cd1LTTz812xq2PDa8G1Ly85Gsxd -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/Qmf2zBcXuNTQLy7C2rBGHsHG4JPU9AMVrsMsz4sygNGL5d\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation recognises that the minimum required size for the Constitutional Committee (CC) is seven members, and that the appointment of Christina Gianelloni would increase the total membership to eight. \r\n\r\nWe acknowledge that increasing the total CC size to eight members has implications for CC approval thresholds, as the two-thirds majority requirement increases the absolute number of aligned votes needed for CC decisions, from five aligned votes, to six aligned votes, thereby marginally increasing individual members' veto power and may introduce additional coordination challenges, especially in scenarios of lower participation.\r\n\r\nNotwithstanding these implications, the Cardano Foundation supports this governance action based on the qualifications of the proposed candidate. Christina Gianelloni brings a strong track record in stewardship, operational leadership, and open-source governance through her roles as COO of Blink Labs and Head of the Board at PRAGMA. Her experience in governance processes is well aligned with the demands of the CC member.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb1QksH6NtCBikZvXySuKjF4mZht2J7TQTj3GMjNLc7h1 -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I voted YES for the proposal: Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina.\r\n\r\nIn the Snap election, Cardano Curia won with a slight lead over Christina. Christina received a large support from the community. Both of these candidates had by far the most votes over the others.\r\n\r\nIt is wise to increase the number of CC members above minCommitteeSize, as this will strengthen governance. In case a CC member suddenly retires, governance will remain operational.\r\n\r\nChristina would become the third among the eight CC members who handle this role individually. This balances the ratio between councils and individual CC members.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/new_committee_2.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is an easy YES for me.  Christina is a valued member of the Cardano community and would make for an excellent CC member.  In addition, the off-chain vote was extremely close and I believe that it will be a huge win for the whole community to have an extra seat on the CC.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Change_The_World_With_Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreic4ljaqtzlb7lkej6usmrkdqupqwqgmenl6d2lwhyu4izhqhteboa -->\r\n# Change_The_World_With_Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7wnxu07kkxpyeul6mq5d20uuvk6m73rfgt3atsgtgg4hgfqgkyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe more in the committee the better for decentralization and fairer voting",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
