      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/New-CC-member/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(68).jsonld -->\r\n# drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCongrats Christina!!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Duc Tiger",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUfQdVZUZMc1apoBwqjq3W1bpMHTuGg8FntBXeC42wDTQ -->\r\n# Duc Tiger\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt0cvg2649d34afclefrxvyn2ctys87a5jt84ckczyjlvgcu7nxyr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the underlying election and its subsequent audit appear to have been conducted with professionalism and transparency, this Governance Action asks the community to ratify the appointment of the second-place candidate, Christina Gianelloni, while completely disregarding the legitimate winner.\r\nAccording to the official audit results provided, the candidate \"Cardano Curia\" won the election with a final, validated voting power of 1.679 billion ADA. Christina Gianelloni finished in second place with 1.402 billion ADA.\r\nTo ignore the clear outcome of a democratic election is an act that runs contrary to every core principle of Cardano and the Voltaire era. Our duty as dReps is to ratify the expressed will of the electorate, not to subvert it.\r\nIf there were legitimate reasons to disqualify the winning candidate, those reasons would need to be presented transparently and debated publicly in their own separate Governance Action. Until such a process occurs, proposing the runner-up for ratification is procedurally unacceptable.\r\nThis NO vote is cast to defend the integrity of the very governance process we are all charged with upholding.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dynamic Strategies",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmZfTy6ZPjVMGCWn1vxbXXMNd7gMkWgZ4pFy9TPgWLkupw -->\r\n# Dynamic Strategies\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr93aecehnm95wr7ufpd2m6jyh2mc8vnr77f0w33g8upyc6m8ayz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmdL86XLwZoBrUQz8GteG6Le6nTRampc6E2dER4ZgddouE\r\n\r\n-",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/New%20Committee-Christina.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nEMURGO, as a DRep, votes NO on the governance action to add an additional Constitutional Committee member, with rationale below.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nWhile we acknowledge the qualifications of the proposed individual, Christina Gianelloni, and the good intentions behind the proposal, the Intersect snap election was explicitly conducted to elect one Constitutional Committee member, and Cardano Curia was the clear winner of that process. Adding the runner-up cannot be considered an outcome of that election.\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Constitution does not clearly permit or prohibit expanding the committee beyond replacing a resigning member, placing this proposal in a procedurally ambiguous area. Expanding the committee from seven to eight members also carries concrete implications, including changes to decision thresholds and potential additional compensation costs, which should not be introduced without a clear basis. \r\n\r\nAs DReps, we consider it reasonable to vote based on constitutional interpretation to avoid setting an unclear precedent. For these reasons, EMURGO votes NO.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00064_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted YES on gov_action1aw809r9gpk7eemt02alszw7lceyf0505uvntavm62rakkckr3nxsqd54zm8;\r\n\r\nChristina was our choice for the additional seat and more people taking a role in the CC would be beneficial. Even if this proposal won't pass, we want to signal our support for Christina's candidacy.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmcg9fE75gr2MeFQo6YMiuFWedk9DRxqKfzPaE4ZRsdHzb -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThere is already a process in place to add Constitutional Committee members, and that process should be followed. We already had an election and a successful candidate was selected. If there is a desire to add more CC seats, then this should be socialized and submitted as a change request to the CC size instead.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmThzxcaU96ZBTXcScT2TpByx48ty6AaTcpEawf7PDjUU6 -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I vote YES on this governance action.\r\n\r\nI previously raised concerns regarding **procedural clarity**, as the recent snap election was publicly framed to fill a single Constitutional Committee seat. Those concerns remain valid. However, after further consideration, I believe **the risk of governance disruption due to an insufficient number of active Constitutional Committee members is more immediate and significant.**\r\n\r\nI also support Christina as a candidate. Christina has demonstrated strong commitment to Cardano’s decentralized governance and received meaningful community support during the election process. Supporting capable and motivated contributors is especially important given that this role is **unpaid and responsibility-heavy.**\r\n\r\nThis YES vote **should not be interpreted as endorsing the current process as ideal**. Rather, it reflects a pragmatic decision to preserve governance continuity while acknowledging the need for improvement.\r\n\r\nI strongly encourage the community and relevant bodies to follow up with an **Info Action** to clearly define:\r\n\r\n* When and how the Constitutional Committee size may be expanded,\r\n* How off-chain election outcomes should be interpreted in such cases,\r\n* And how to avoid ambiguity or retroactive expectations in future appointments.\r\n\r\nStrengthening procedural clarity alongside operational resilience is essential to maintaining long-term trust in Cardano governance.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HenriqC",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiflha3crdavd4ozpqk5o7dfj2ccpku5nvs5jnv7xozx55azxiqzbm -->\r\n# HenriqC\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2f5m5mn48q65xkw65q2kfd2tkakz3lh8553ugmcsq0ahnsl2nfcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCurrently, I think the expectation is that there is a reasonable process first to decide about the increase of the number seats and then choose a new member(s). The previous election was about one member.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNM6gLpMz48KYThaiVVpYmMco9uiQ4qWgyfcCdLumCp4e -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting No on this Governance Action to add Christina as the 8th Constitutional Committee member. While I initially supported the idea, constitutional concerns have since emerged. Article 7 Section 3 of the Constitution clearly states that the Cardano Community shall \\\"establish and make public a process\\\" for the election of Constitutional Committee (CC) members. The Snap Election process was publicly announced and structured for the selection of one seat. Submitting a GA after the election to retroactively add a second seat appears inconsistent with that established and published process. Voters cast their votes under the assumption that only one seat was being filled. Retroactively modifying that outcome undermines procedural integrity and risks setting a precedent where off-chain elections can be overridden via Governance Actions. Such practices could lead to confusion and erosion of trust in governance mechanisms. While it's possible to interpret the addition as part of a new process, doing so without establishing and publicly communicating such a process raises questions about constitutional consistency. I support committee expansion in principle, but such a change must follow a clearly established and public process. I urge that any future expansion be preceded by an Info GA that sets expectations and allows the community to align. Based on these concerns, and recognizing that DReps are responsible for assessing the constitutionality of GAs, I am voting No. [Japanese version follows] 私は、Christina氏を8人目の憲法委員として追加する本ガバナンスアクションに対して反対票（No）を投じます。当初はこの提案に賛成していましたが、その後、憲法上の懸念が浮上しました。カルダノ憲法第7条3項には「コミュニティは憲法委員選出のためのプロセスを確立し、公開しなければならない」と明記されています。今回のSnap Electionは、1議席のみを選出するプロセスとして明確に構築・公開されていました。選挙後に2議席目を追加するガバナンスアクションを提出することは、既存のプロセスと整合していないように見えます。有権者は1議席を選ぶ前提で投票しており、事後的な変更は手続きの正当性を損ないます。このような例が前例化されれば、オフチェーン選挙の意味が形骸化しかねません。結果として、ガバナンス全体の混乱や信頼の低下につながる恐れがあります。今回の追加を「新しいプロセス」と解釈する見方もありますが、正式な確立と公開を経ていない点で、憲法との整合性に疑問が残ります。私は委員会の拡大には基本的に賛成ですが、それは確立された公開プロセスに基づいて行われるべきです。今後、Info GAを通じた事前共有を行い、コミュニティの合意形成を経たうえでのGA提出を望みます。こうした懸念を踏まえ、DRepが合憲性を判断すべき立場にあることを認識し、今回はNo票を投じます。",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HOSKY",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://Qmdq965BcyFccerpoNt88qMgegPisJpsmqZuE12nm4hDvM -->\r\n# HOSKY\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf2jzhuc4f7eu2yay9d9ta3dykxxcwn34wz8kak7nhd7vcgrxn7ns`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmYGJ41pHMdLihLKiop4YaMadcPwoc8vu7YU7vEBHtkvks\r\n\r\nVoting YES. Expanding the Constitutional Committee above the minimum size improves continuity and resilience. If a member resigns or is unavailable, the CC can still function without delays, ensuring uninterrupted constitutional review and governance stability.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaqnsyfm6aq6h4633qonj54ac3z6sshkey7vaxq7vqd4p2f4w33tu -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOne approach to blockchain governance will be to mimic the rigidity of constitutional systems seen in the legacy world. The word \"constitution\" itself is loaded - as it brings about images of constitutional courts, togas, and supreme authority. However, the Cardano constitution is essentially a rulebook. We want to make sure we are playing by a set of pre-agreed rules. That's it. \r\nSo, yes we can still experiment and show that our nascent governance system is fair but also flexible. Having an extra CC member - above the bare minimum - makes sense for a global decentralized system, especially as one CC member can easily be incapacitated for a certain period of time. Allowing a small buffer might be prudent. \r\nOverall, having more individuals who want to dedicate their free time to governance is a net benefit for Cardano. Thank you for your service all former and current CC members. All of you received a lot of community support - and in this case the recent Ekklesia poll  showed this to be true for this candidate as well. \r\nWhy stop an apparently committed candidate from helping the other 7 CC members? It's a thankless job as it is - and having a small buffer above the minimum CC number will probably help relieve some pressure from the other 7 members who are under a (thankless) spotlight with every word of their rationales being scrutinized around the globe.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreieic62whverguinybdvkh3dgtw2y3bbzexnsol2jxxriufdgyhume -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting no, not as a rejection of Christina's qualifications, which are beyond dispute, but because this proposal bypasses necessary governance design discussion in favor of ad hoc committee expansion that introduces structural problems without resolving underlying concerns.\r\nChristina has consistently demonstrated thoughtful, principled contributions to Cardano governance. Her capability and integrity are not in question. This vote reflects disagreement with the mechanism and timing of this action, not the candidate's merit. She would serve competently, but that doesn't make this the right process or the right moment to expand the Constitutional Committee.\r\nThe proposal frames itself as strengthening governance resilience by adding a member above the minCommitteeSize threshold of seven, reducing ratification delay risk if someone resigns. That's superficially reasonable, until you examine what it actually does. Moving from seven to eight Constitutional Committee members shifts from odd-numbered to even-numbered composition, introducing the possibility of tied votes. Tied outcomes complicate decision-making rather than strengthening it. An odd-numbered body ensures resolution; an even-numbered one creates deadlock scenarios requiring additional tiebreaker mechanisms that don't currently exist in our governance framework.\r\nThe snap election between Christina and Cardano Curia was indeed close, but Curia was selected through the established process. Revisiting that outcome via permissionless governance action sets precedent that close electoral results justify adding runner-up candidates post hoc. That's not resilience; it's governance drift that undermines electoral finality.\r\nIf the Constitutional Committee's minimum size is genuinely problematic, the solution is modifying the minCommitteeSize parameter through deliberate governance action with ecosystem-wide input, not incrementally expanding membership through individual Update Committee actions every time someone loses narrowly. This proposal conflates candidate merit with structural governance design, treating committee expansion as if it's purely additive when it fundamentally alters decision dynamics and precedent.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kronoshus/KevinMohr/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Kevin G Mohr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis wasn't approved through a proper election. No.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/24dvh9z9 -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Constitution sets a minimum of seven members for the Constitutional Committee, but no maximum, so adding Christina after her close tie with Curia in the snap election fits the rules and boosts resilience—if someone quits, the committee stays above seven and avoids delays in approving actions. Christina adds enthusiasm and fresh ideas, helping users and developers on Cardano, and this follows the permissionless system where anyone can propose changes for more freedom and decentralization. On the downside, with eight members (an even number), decisions need 67% approval, meaning at least six yes votes out of eight; a 4-4 split or close votes could block actions more often, leading to slower governance, and while there's no pay for members now, a bigger group might cost the treasury more later if compensation starts, making it less efficient. Still, I vote yes because the gains in stability and inclusion outweigh the risks.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
