    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA079-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action1aw809r9gpk7eemt02alszw7lceyf0505uvntavm62rakkckr3nxsqd54zm8), pois concordamos que a inclusão de um membro adicional no Comitê Constitucional traz maior segurança e maturidade ao processo de governança, reduzindo o risco de interrupções causadas pela eventual desistência de um membro em momentos críticos ou urgentes de votação. A indicação da Christina Gianelloni Gianelloni para o cargo se justifica pelo fato de seu nome ter sido previamente referendado em uma consulta off-chain aos DReps, realizada recentemente na plataforma Ekklesia. Entendemos, portanto, que o voto on-chain representa a instância final e decisória desse processo, conferindo legitimidade e fechamento institucional à escolha.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action (gov_action1aw809r9gpk7eemt02alszw7lceyf0505uvntavm62rakkckr3nxsqd54zm8), because we agree that adding an extra member to the Constitutional Committee brings greater security and maturity to the governance process, reducing the risk of disruptions caused by a member stepping down during critical or urgent voting periods. The nomination of Christina Gianelloni for the role is justified by the fact that her name was previously endorsed through an off-chain consultation with DReps, recently conducted on the Ekklesia platform. We therefore understand that the on-chain vote serves as the final and decisive instance of this process, providing legitimacy and institutional closure to the decision.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZxMJdUaiFSWdTBVj4D3mRWCQ4MKcWLfWe6eevLi58qib -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA previously voted YES on the Update Committee action that added Cardano Curia to the Constitutional Committee. That decision was grounded in a clear and principled position: a sitting committee member had retired, the Committee had fallen below the `committeeMinSize `parameter, and the snap election facilitated by Intersect produced a single, auditable outcome. Although RCADA supported a different candidate during that election, we upheld the result because safeguarding process integrity and restoring constitutional functionality takes precedence over individual electoral preferences.\r\n\r\nImportantly, in that prior rationale RCADA also explicitly acknowledged a broader structural issue: a Constitutional Committee operating without buffer seats is fragile, and a single resignation should not temporarily impair the system’s ability to ratify governance actions. We stated then that governance resilience should be addressed through appropriate, constitutionally compliant channels, such as a deliberate review of committee sizing or the committeeMinSize parameter, rather than through ad-hoc or reactive measures.\r\n\r\nIt is against that same framework that we assess the present action.\r\n\r\nThis proposal is constitutionally valid and well-intentioned. It does not negate the Curia outcome, does not remove or replace any member, and correctly respects ledger ordering. RCADA also recognises the genuine governance risk it seeks to mitigate and does not question the qualifications or good faith of the proposed candidate.\r\n\r\nHowever, this action introduces a different governance dynamic than the one RCADA previously supported. Rather than executing a single, final election outcome to restore minimum functionality, it expands committee membership in response to the narrowness of an earlier off-chain result. While understandable, this mechanism risks establishing a precedent where close electoral margins become grounds for post-hoc committee expansion. Over time, such a pattern could weaken election finality and blur the boundary between outcome execution and outcome revision.\r\n\r\nRCADA’s abstention should therefore not be interpreted as opposition to the candidate, nor as a retreat from our prior vote. On the contrary, it reflects consistency with that earlier position. We supported the Curia action because it faithfully enacted a necessary and final outcome. We abstain here because we believe long-term committee resilience should be addressed through neutral, system-level design choices, not candidate-specific corrective actions tied to past elections.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, RCADA abstains — affirming constitutional validity and governance intent, while signaling the need for a more principled, forward-looking approach to Constitutional Committee resilience.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreic5bzm7i4d2s5sjnmqbu7h62pqzqrc2fwvm6xfs2e2dolg3exme5q -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter careful review, I have decided to vote in favor of this action. The increase in committee size has a real benefit to the overall robustness of governance on Cardano, and Christina would be a worthy addition to the CC, in my opinion. I do have some slight concerns about leaving the CC size at 8 members, given the threshold of 2/3. This is relatively minor in the larger picture, but I would prefer to increase it to 9 if we are going to increase it; however, this action does not in any way stop this from being discussed by the community at a later date. The benefits of having a one member buffer above the committee min size and bringing on board a capable new CC member certainly outweighs my minor concerns in this case.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qme5KSwr1Ggf19PRzsekEyJM4nEif9nCZXL3RUSDxrocNK -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThe Constitutional Committee is designed in a way that its ability to ratify governance actions depends on maintaining a minimum number of active members. For this reason, operating slightly above the minimum required size is a reasonable and prudent approach to improving governance continuity and stability. This proposal increases resilience without changing the existing voting threshold or the current terms of committee members, making it a safe and well-scoped enhancement.\r\n\r\nDuring the snap election, Christina received strong support from the community, with the outcome being decided by a very narrow margin. This proposal acknowledges that reality and addresses it transparently on-chain. By doing so, it strengthens representation through a community-initiated process that aligns closely with Cardano’s permissionless governance model.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I consider this proposal to be a sound measure that improves governance stability and long-term resilience, and I support it.\r\n\r\n僕は、本提案に YES で投票します。\r\n\r\n憲法委員会は、メンバー数が一定数を下回ると承認機能が止まってしまう仕組みになっています。そのため、最低人数を少し上回る体制を取ることは、ガバナンスの継続性と安定性を高めるうえで合理的です。今回の提案は、投票閾値や既存メンバーの任期を変更することなく、安全にレジリエンスを高める設計になっています。\r\n\r\nまた、スナップ選挙では Christina に対しても非常に強いコミュニティ支持が示されました。本提案は、その事実をオンチェーンで透明に扱い、コミュニティ主導で代表性を補強しようとする、Cardanoのパーミッションレス・ガバナンスの精神に沿った取り組みだと評価しています。\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、本提案はガバナンスの安定性と将来耐性を高める健全な施策であり、僕はこれを支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreictiz7vnwslnlbm3utzcmullkzfhjq7ggbrqgl2vdy4uyvg75dtga -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep votes Yes on the proposal “Add Constitutional Committee Member – Christina.”\r\n\r\nThis decision is not an endorsement or rejection of any individual candidate.\r\nIt is based on a structural and institutional assessment of what best supports the long-term stability and functionality of Cardano’s on-chain governance.\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Governance Continuity and Operational Resilience\r\n\r\nUnder the current protocol parameters, if the number of active Constitutional Committee (CC) members falls below minCommitteeSize (7), governance actions requiring CC ratification cannot proceed.\r\n\r\nWith full on-chain governance activated under CIP-1694, a stalled governance process itself becomes a systemic risk.\r\n\r\nThis proposal:\r\n\t•\tDoes not remove or replace any existing CC member\r\n\t•\tAdds one member above the minimum threshold\r\n\t•\tReduces the risk of governance paralysis due to resignation or inactivity\r\n\r\nFrom a DRep perspective, this is a practical and proportionate measure to strengthen governance resilience.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Non-Conflict With Prior Governance Decisions\r\n\r\nSIPO places significant importance on the fact that this proposal:\r\n\t•\tExplicitly references the previously ratified Update Committee action that added Cardano Curia as its previousGovActionId\r\n\t•\tCannot be ratified unless the Curia action has already been ratified\r\n\t•\tDoes not override, invalidate, or negate any existing decision\r\n\r\nThis is not a re-election nor a reversal.\r\nIt is a structurally safe additive action that respects ledger ordering and governance consistency.\r\n\r\n\r\n3. A Healthy Example of Permissionless Governance in Practice\r\n\r\nThe essence of CIP-1694 is not merely that “anyone may submit a proposal,”\r\nbut that community members can do so correctly, transparently, and fully on-chain.\r\n\r\nThis proposal:\r\n\t•\tIs independently submitted by community participants\r\n\t•\tClaims no institutional mandate\r\n\t•\tDemonstrates clear understanding of constitutional and ledger constraints\r\n\r\nSIPO views this as a concrete example of permissionless governance functioning as intended.\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Absorbing Narrow Electoral Outcomes Within the System\r\n\r\nThe snap election facilitated by Intersect resulted in a very narrow margin between Christina and Cardano Curia.\r\n\r\nSIPO fully respects the fact that Curia was selected and ratified.\r\nAt the same time, a governance system should consider whether narrowly expressed community support can be acknowledged without undermining prior outcomes.\r\n\r\nThis proposal:\r\n\t•\tPreserves the existing decision\r\n\t•\tAligns term expiration epochs\r\n\t•\tUses a limited and transparent mechanism to improve representation and continuity\r\n\r\nIt reflects an attempt to resolve tension through structure rather than politics, which aligns with Cardano’s governance philosophy.\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Important Limitations and Clarifications\r\n\r\nSIPO’s Yes vote does not imply:\r\n\t•\tThat runner-up candidates should generally be added to the CC\r\n\t•\tThat CC expansion should become routine\r\n\t•\tThat off-chain election outcomes should be casually modified on-chain\r\n\r\nThis decision is specific to a narrow-margin, transitional governance context.\r\n\r\nSIPO strongly encourages future governance actions to address:\r\n\t•\tFormal rules for CC vacancies\r\n\t•\tClear separation between off-chain elections and on-chain actions\r\n\t•\tReassessment of minCommitteeSize design\r\n\r\n\r\n6. Conclusion\r\n\r\nFor the reasons above, SIPO DRep votes Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis vote reflects:\r\n\t•\tA structural, not personal, judgment\r\n\t•\tA commitment to governance continuity\r\n\t•\tA focus on long-term institutional integrity\r\n\r\nSIPO will continue to act as a DRep with an emphasis on durable governance design over short-term outcomes.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep は、本提案「Add Constitutional Committee Member – Christina」に対して、Yes に投票します。\r\n\r\n本判断は、特定の個人への支持・不支持を表明するものではなく、Cardano のオンチェーン・ガバナンスが長期的に安定し、機能し続けるための制度的・構造的観点から行ったものです。\r\n\r\n\r\n1. ガバナンス継続性とレジリエンスの観点\r\n\r\n現在の Constitutional Committee（CC）は、protocol parameter である **minCommitteeSize（7）**を下回った場合、\r\nCC の承認を要するガバナンスアクションが事実上停止する構造になっています。\r\n\r\nCardano はすでに CIP-1694 により「完全オンチェーン・ガバナンス」の段階に入っており、\r\nガバナンスが停止すること自体が、ネットワークの制度的リスクとなります。\r\n\r\n本提案は、\r\n\t•\t既存メンバーを削除・置換するものではなく\r\n\t•\tCC を最小人数より 1名多い構成にすることで\r\n\t•\t予期せぬ辞任・不在があっても、ガバナンスが止まらない状態を確保する\r\n\r\nという、極めて実務的かつ合理的なレジリエンス強化策であると評価しています。\r\n\r\n\r\n2. 既存ガバナンス決定との非衝突設計\r\n\r\nSIPO は、本提案が以下の点を厳格に守っていることを重視しています。\r\n\t•\tCardano Curia を CC に追加する既存の Update Committee Action を\r\npreviousGovActionId として明示的に参照していること\r\n\t•\tそのため、Curia の決定を上書き・否定・無効化する構造になっていないこと\r\n\t•\tLedger ordering とガバナンス一貫性を尊重していること\r\n\r\n本提案は「再選挙」でも「結果の覆し」でもなく、\r\nすでに確定した決定を前提条件として、その上に追加する設計です。\r\n\r\nこのような構造的安全性は、DRep として評価すべき重要なポイントです。\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Permissionless Governance の健全な実践例である点\r\n\r\nCIP-1694 の本質は、\r\n\r\n「誰でも提案できる」ではなく\r\n「誰かが、ルールを理解したうえで、実際に提案し、オンチェーンで完結させられる」\r\n\r\nことにあります。\r\n\r\n本提案は、\r\n\t•\t特定組織の委任ではなく\r\n\t•\tコミュニティ個人による自発的提出であり\r\n\t•\t憲法・CIP・台帳制約を踏まえた内容になっています\r\n\r\nSIPO は、この点において、本提案を permissionless governance が実際に機能している具体例として評価しています。\r\n\r\n\r\n4. 僅差だった民意を「制度内」で吸収する試み\r\n\r\nIntersect が実施したスナップ選挙において、\r\nChristina と Cardano Curia の得票差は非常に僅差でした。\r\n\r\nSIPO は、\r\n\t•\t選挙結果として Curia が選出・承認された事実を尊重します\r\n\t•\t同時に、僅差で示された支持が「完全に切り捨てられる」構造が、\r\n必ずしも分散型ガバナンスにとって最善とは限らない\r\n\r\nとも考えています。\r\n\r\n本提案は、\r\n\t•\t既存結果を侵害せず\r\n\t•\t任期を揃え\r\n\t•\t人数追加という限定的手段で\r\n\t•\t代表性と継続性を両立させようとするもの\r\n\r\nであり、対立を政治ではなく構造で処理しようとする試みとして、一定の合理性があると判断しました。\r\n\r\n\r\n5. 同時に明確にしておきたい留意点\r\n\r\nSIPO は、本提案への Yes が、以下を意味しないことを明確にします。\r\n\t•\t選挙で次点だった候補を常に追加すべき、という一般原則\r\n\t•\tCC を無制限に拡張する前例\r\n\t•\tオフチェーン選挙結果をオンチェーンで容易に修正できる、という慣行\r\n\r\n本件は、\r\n\t•\t僅差\r\n\t•\t欠員リスク\r\n\t•\t過渡期のガバナンス体制\r\n\r\nという限定的な文脈における判断です。\r\n\r\nSIPO は、将来的には、\r\n\t•\tCC 欠員時の明確な制度ルール\r\n\t•\t選挙とオンチェーン修正の役割分担\r\n\t•\tminCommitteeSize 設計の再検討\r\n\r\nが、別途ガバナンスアクションとして整理されることを強く期待します。\r\n\r\n\r\n6. 結論\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、SIPO DRep は本提案に Yes を投じます。\r\n\r\nそれは、\r\n\t•\t個人への支持ではなく\r\n\t•\t感情的判断でもなく\r\n\t•\tCardano のガバナンスを止めないための\r\n構造的・制度的な選択\r\n\r\nです。\r\n\r\nSIPO は今後も、\r\n「誰が選ばれたか」よりも\r\n「どのようなルールと構造が残るか」\r\nを重視して、DRep としての判断を行っていきます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRVXMn5XVxZKmAT2rrPyJkr7HeXFr5QkxA3twmmhbsMz2 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Socious DRep** votes **NO** on the governance action: *“Add Constitutional Committee Member – Christina.”* While we hold the candidate in high regard and recognize her as exceptionally well-qualified for the Constitutional Committee (CC), we believe that structural changes to the committee must follow a legitimate and transparent process to maintain the integrity of Cardano’s governance.\r\n\r\n### Rationale\r\n\r\n**1. Candidate Merit vs. Procedural Integrity**\r\nWe wish to state clearly that **Christina is well-qualified**, and we would likely support her candidacy in a standard election or a specifically designed expansion process. However, a \"NO\" vote is necessary here because the process used to propose her appointment bypasses established community expectations.\r\n\r\n**2. Adhering to the Election Mandate**\r\nThe Intersect snap election was held to fill **one** specific vacancy. Cardano Curia was selected by the community through that competitive process. To appoint a second member from the same election—without a pre-defined \"runner-up\" rule—sets a precedent where the scope of an election can be changed retroactively.\r\n\r\n**3. Strategic Expansion Requires Consensus**\r\nIf there is a strategic need to increase the CC size to mitigate operational risk, that decision belongs to the ecosystem. We believe an **Info Action** should be the first step to:\r\n\r\n- Formally propose an increase in committee size.\r\n- Gather community feedback on the criteria for such an expansion.\r\n- Establish a fair and predictable process for filling those new seats.\r\n\r\n### Conclusion\r\n\r\n**Socious DRep** remains supportive of qualified individuals like Christina joining the Constitutional Committee in the future. However, we cannot support a governance action that prioritizes expediency over a robust, community-aligned process. We encourage a return to a structured approach that ensures all structural changes are backed by a clear ecosystem mandate.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYWpkqpqqvaLzAPzWMwuxo5tUx39qYB2PSeaVFtJisBYg -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSTORM Partners votes YES on this Constitutional Committee update.\r\nThis action strengthens governance continuity by adding a buffer above the minimum committee size, reducing the risk of disruption if a member steps down or becomes inactive. While expanding the committee from seven to eight members increases the absolute two-thirds approval threshold, we consider this a reasonable tradeoff in light of past governance precedents, with the Atlantic Council CC stepping down and temporarily stalling decision-making.\r\nWe had the honour to meet Christina in person during the Cardano Summit in Berlin, and we are confident in her expertise, judgment, and ability to contribute constructively to the Constitutional Committee’s work. Her experience aligns well with the responsibilities of the role, and we thank her, as well as Cardano Curia and all candidates, for stepping forward during the recent Constitutional Committee elections.\r\n\r\nOverall, this is a low-risk action that improves institutional resilience and helps ensure Cardano’s governance remains functional and credible throughout the current mandate.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Suzhou Capital",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreih26f7viqe4iprodwlbhh3v454tmp5l6cbmyrbjarspnklcx572oq -->\r\n# Suzhou Capital\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytm8770aqd0xqn8f30y3cc3wtsah59vqg5u4ju7xmphl4ecyn8cap`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nUnnecessary",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZxqUpy8FeJSSfWGHUkvoLGGE9uRuZcPDZUn3bw2ku448 -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a classic case of **outcome engineering masquerading as safety**. We held an election. The community established a process (Article IV, Section 40 of the Constitution requires a public process). That process yielded a binary result: one seat, one winner. Attempting to install the runner-up via a separate governance action immediately after the fact treats the election results as a \"suggestion\" rather than a mandate.\r\n\r\nThe proposal claims to \"strengthen governance continuity.\" I argue it **weakens social consensus**. If every close election results in the loser being proposed for a seat anyway under the guise of \"resilience,\" why hold elections at all? **We are establishing a precedent where on-chain governance is used to litigate off-chain disappointments.**\r\n\r\nIndeed, if we drop below 7 members, the CC enters a state of dysfunction where it cannot ratify actions. This is a real risk. However, **the solution to a brittle parameter is to fix the parameter or hold a new, dedicated election for an expanded seat** — not to arbitrarily appoint a specific individual who failed to secure the mandate in the designated contest.\r\n\r\n**If we want 8 members, we should have run an election for 8 members! We cannot \"patch\" election outcomes on-chain because we feel the margin was too tight. That is not resilience; that is instability.**",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmae4PZ1WtYPBEWLJRajxdRXrRHnXLVPKBn9tRGf8BMAFY -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe rules for CC member voting did not specify a runner up position. However, I am always in favor of improvising, to safeguard against future delays and bureaucratic hurdles. Maintaining the minimum number of CC members means stalling all governance processes and repeated elections if another member retires. Additionally, Christina gathered more individual votes, despite lower overall voting power. After careful consideration, I support the initiative to add her to the Constitutional Committee.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTxL3fxGqmuVkLRTMUqKZXtQ9mRKkYr75pZVjyhCaXZBm -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this community-initiated Update Committee action to add an additional Constitutional Committee member because it strengthens governance resilience by keeping the committee size above the minimum threshold of 7. This provides essential redundancy, reducing the risk of ratification delays or governance paralysis if a member resigns or retires mid-term. It is a prudent, low-risk measure that enhances operational continuity within Cardano's permissionless framework, balances representation between individuals and councils, and safeguards smooth on-chain governance without overriding prior community decisions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibwyb4unkz3fhpad2mvhv2loxzoqcoynza3iryjrxenj5zleybemq -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Wada DRep, we vote no on this governance action, and we do so with deep respect for the candidate involved. Christina has made consistently thoughtful, principled, and high-quality contributions to Cardano governance, and our confidence in her capability and integrity is not in question. This is clearly reflected in our position during the Intersect Snap Election, where we expressed strong support for her candidacy. Our decision here should not be interpreted as a rejection of Christina’s merit or suitability for governance roles within the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nWe also recognise the underlying merit of the idea being proposed. Strengthening the resilience of the Constitutional Committee is a legitimate concern, and increasing the minimum committee size to reduce the risk of governance deadlock is, in principle, a reasonable objective. At the same time, this proposal raises unanswered questions about governance design. It is not clear why the minimum size was originally set at seven, nor what the systemic implications are of moving from an odd-numbered committee to an even-numbered one. An even-sized committee introduces the possibility of tied outcomes, which may complicate decision-making rather than strengthen it. If the ecosystem is to revisit committee sizing, we would be more comfortable supporting an increase to an odd integer, such as nine, following a deliberate and well-reasoned process.\r\n\r\nOur no vote is ultimately grounded in respect for community processes and institutional legitimacy. Intersect utilised community resources to organise the snap election with a clear and narrow mandate: to enable the ecosystem to select a single replacement for the Cardano Atlantic Council following their resignation. We do not believe that process was skewed or designed to favour any particular candidate, and we therefore respect its outcome as an expression of the ecosystem’s will. Introducing a follow-up governance action that effectively reopens representation through an alternative pathway risks undermining the finality and trust placed in that collective decision.\r\n\r\nIf there is a broader concern about the adequacy of the current minimum committee size, we believe that issue deserves a more structured, ecosystem-wide discussion rather than being addressed through an ad hoc member addition. A principled approach to committee resilience, composition, and sizing would benefit from stewardship by an appropriate body, and we would welcome the Cardano Civics Committee taking this matter up to explore options that strengthen governance operations while setting sound precedent.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, while we hold Christina in the highest regard and acknowledge the good intentions behind this proposal, we are not able to support it in its current form. Our position reflects a commitment to process integrity, respect for community-driven outcomes, and a belief that structural governance changes should be approached deliberately and holistically.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Will Norris",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiet5273a2t4bufjm62oxse5xflu5c2cqw3amrtswh3jgjrtupngye -->\r\n# Will Norris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuufvd6maykgfcp20fxgpx7g6a9z2suchqehfejwdsx8cgpx80yg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on the proposal to add Christina as an additional Constitutional Committee member.\r\n\r\nThis action is fully compliant with CIP-1694 and the Cardano Constitution. Constitutional Committee size is not fixed, the proposal remains within existing guardrails, preserves the 67% voting threshold, and correctly references the prior Update Committee action that added Cardano Curia, ensuring proper ledger ordering and non-conflict.\r\n\r\nThe snap election to fill the vacant Constitutional Committee seat was implemented on-chain, and this proposal does not override, replace, or invalidate that outcome. Cardano Curia remains duly selected and ratified.\r\n\r\nFrom a governance-resilience perspective, adding an additional member above the current minCommitteeSize of 7 reduces operational fragility and lowers the risk of governance stalling due to resignation, inactivity, or term expiry during the current mandate.\r\n\r\nThe exceptionally close snap-election result provides reasonable justification for broader representation without undermining the original on-chain decision.\r\n\r\nCaveat: going forward, the community should clearly define whether snap-election processes are intended to be strictly single-seat outcomes, or whether close results may justify additional on-chain committee appointments. Expectations should be set in advance so that committee expansion remains principled rather than ad-hoc.\r\n\r\nOn balance, this proposal strengthens governance continuity while remaining aligned with both the letter and spirit of the Cardano Constitution.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifhw2j7twcwhl4k7jg5vlwzmj3qi5upvjzt3ec4m5kmqqmpihj75q -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Considerations\r\n\r\n- The governance action does not contain any explanation of Christina's motivations.\r\n- Having done a little bit of preliminary research on Christina, it is clear she has been involved in the Cardano community for quite some time.\r\n- I've reached out to Christina over Twitter via a direct message but have yet to receive a response.\r\n- I want more individuals on the CC instead of multisigs.\r\n\r\n## Statement\r\n\r\nChristina appears to be qualified for the role. I would have liked more explanation of her values and motivations. I prefer individuals on the CC because it makes for more direct personal responsibility. I am voting to make Christina a member of the CC because I want the CC to be mostly composed of individuals who will take direct responsibility for their actions with little insulation from consequences such as removal. I also want to avoid over-distilling the committee. Individuals come with unique perspectives and values, but large committees average out to mediocrity. \r\n\r\nSigned, \r\nWilliam Doyle\r\n\r\nYour friendly neighbourhood DRep! \r\n\r\nhttps://x.com/william00000010",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wistkey Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVurXKeCt4JZnhRDmuRNKV3CvG2wm9GWFihW1Vad439Vi -->\r\n# Wistkey Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt2g95nkd7q3kase2jdc92fjrhuyh7zgnj27mu8fu7n57yclhp5ts`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWistkeyLab is voting YES on governance action Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina. The Constitutional Committee is currently operating close to the minimum required size. Under this condition, the temporary loss of a member due to resignation, illness, or conflict of interest could impair the committee’s ability to function and delay or block governance actions.\r\n\r\nAdding one additional qualified member increases the committee’s operational resilience by reducing single-point-of-failure risk. This adjustment does not alter the committee’s mandate or fundamental role, but provides a buffer that helps ensure continuity and stability during critical governance periods.\r\n\r\nFrom this perspective, the proposed appointment is viewed as a pragmatic measure to safeguard governance operations while maintaining the committee’s existing responsibilities and structure.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_CC%20Christina.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep votes NO on the governance action titled “Add Constitutional Committee Member – Christina.” This decision reflects a cautious view on how risk mitigation measures should be shaped through broader ecosystem input.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nElection scope and mandate\r\n\r\nThe Intersect snap election was held to select one replacement Constitutional Committee member. Cardano Curia was chosen through that process, and the outcome does not provide a mandate to appoint an additional member.\r\n\r\nEcosystem alignment before structural change\r\n\r\nIf the intention is to mitigate operational risk by operating above the minimum committee size, this should be treated as a governance design question that involves wider community perspectives. Rather than proceeding through an ad hoc addition following a narrowly scoped election, an Info action could be submitted first to gather ecosystem feedback, evaluate alternatives, and build shared expectations before any New Committee governance action is proposed.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep votes NO on this proposal and encourages a community-informed, ecosystem-aligned approach before making structural changes to the Constitutional Committee.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaAAJx8of9hKpCWQgmCZMV58JTH3ZsuhVracaZQ8vtjkm -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES for \"Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina\" for three reasons:\r\n\r\n1) This would simply add Christina to the seven CC members, bringing the total to eight, and would not have any significant drawbacks.\r\n\r\n2) The minimum CC size is set at seven seats, and the current CC membership is seven entities. In this situation, if even one of these seven entities resigns, governance would cease, and a re-election would be necessary. Governance cessation would not simply result in issues such as treasury withdrawal; it would also make parameter changes and hard fork initiation difficult, potentially posing a significant risk to the Cardano chain. Therefore, improvement is necessary.\r\n\r\nIt is possible to reduce the CC minimum size, but this would require three months of off-chain consultation under the Constitution, and therefore cannot be changed until at least February 12th.\r\nhttps://forum.cardano.org/t/pcp-committeeminsize-yuta/151156/7\r\n\r\nTherefore, the current viable solution, at least in the short term, is to increase the number of CCs to eight or more.\r\n(We could consider amending the constitution to remove the three-month consultation requirement, but given that it's an important parameter and requires a three-month consultation, I doubt we'll be able to get community support easily.)\r\n\r\n3) I've reviewed Christina's background and believe she's an experienced and honest member.\r\n\r\n私は「Add Constitutional Committee Member - Christina」に次の３つの理由からYESを投票します。\r\n\r\n1) これは7名のCCメンバーにChristinaを追加して8名にするのみであり、重大なデメリットはありません。\r\n\r\n2) CC最小サイズは7席に設定されており、現在のCCメンバー数は７エンティティです。この状況では、この7エンティティのうち１つでも退任した場合、ガバナンスが停止し、再選挙などが必要になります。ガバナンスが停止するということは単にトレジャリーウィズドローなどの問題だけではなく、パラメータ変更やハードフォーク開始が困難になるため、チェーンに重大なリスクをもたらす可能性があります。そのため、改善が必要です。\r\nCC最小サイズを減らすことも可能ですが、これは憲法上、3ヶ月のオフチェーン協議が必要であるため、少なくとも2月12日まではこれを変更することができません。\r\nhttps://forum.cardano.org/t/pcp-committeeminsize-yuta/151156/7\r\nよって現状少なくとも短期的に可能な方法はCCの数を８以上にすることです。\r\n（3ヶ月の協議要件を削除するような憲法を変更する方法も考えられますが、当然ながら重要なパラメータでであるから3ヶ月の協議要件が要求されていることを考えると、コミュニティの指示が簡単に得られるとは思いません）\r\n\r\n3) Christinaの経歴を確認し、経験豊富かつ誠実なメンバーだと私は判断しました。",
      "vote": "YES"
    }
  ],
  "Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions": [
