      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXCNPww9wjrWqfXtS9DMrCz9oEaKYHqczrJyCC3naShMK -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmSfAxwPcDM79QFZEPnfJSNf8nzsjbA7ZTXB6KQvAG2pzr\r\n\r\nI plan to vote YES on most projects I’ve supported in Ekklesia. To stay transparent, I’ll rate each project across six categories, scoring 0 to 2 per category (max 12 points). Projects scoring below 6 won’t get my support. I’ll consider supporting those with 7–8 points, and will fully support any scoring 9 or more.\r\n\r\nThe categories are:\r\n\r\n- Key infrastructure, research, or essential funding: 0\r\n- Team strength, feasibility, and track record: 1\r\n- Impact on the Cardano ecosystem: 1\r\n- Value for money: 1\r\n- Cost compared to similar proposals: 1\r\n- Personal or community usage and benefit: 0\r\n\r\nTotal score: 4",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUNyvyPdEorRg4VCFMPdTMjy95fMnenxWV6YM3q7qnbvr -->\r\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES on all 39 Governance Actions — 39 times, 39 votes.\r\nBut I stand firmed on Exhinbition and Events\r\nSince I supported these during Ekklesia and saw no major changes or conflicts of interest, I still stand by those decisions. \r\n\r\nFor proposals with large budgets (>500k ADA), I paid extra attention to the justification and scope. Voting isn’t just a click — it’s a responsibility. I own mine, for myself and for our CASIA community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYss4ctFbkxDpNgxkZjqwhfgz7vo1r4rn3LVCyS4rWdGq -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis vote had me on the fence between NO and ABSTAIN.  Personally, I think marketing is a bit of a tough sell on Cardano at the moment and that we need to have some killer projects step forward first so that we can market them.  My worry is that we try to market some projects that might not necessarily have anything overly innovative or revolutionary about them other than being built on Cardano.  That being said, I do believe it is incredibly important for Cardano to have a presence at other events and conferences, even more so than our own exclusive conferences.  For this reason, I have pushed my vote toward ABSTAIN.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTDY2q3SR77YNnJweR9UV599XMjsEbqwDNUib8EqkYb3B -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting decision was made to be consistent with my reconciliation back in May 2025;\r\nhttps://2025budget.intersectmbo.org/voters/drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg\r\n\r\nReady to move forward overall with the budgeting process and look forward to a smoother process next year. I voted for a lower NCL overall (200M), however found in supporting things that we really ought to have funded to keep momentum in development and enhancements on-chain (supporting both open and non-open-sourced projects) I came a bit higher than that (250M+). \r\n\r\nWe will need to strike a balance in treasury withdrawels for projects that push development forward (and therefore the chains efficiency, performance, resiliancy, and seucrity) -- and businsess that wish to participate, of any size, and extend the capabilities and real-world use cases of Cardano.\r\n\r\nMy votes, I hope, align with my overall goal as a DRep to see continuous improvement in the ecosystem. https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/mr_cata_gov%20.txt",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Crypto_Oaj",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSYBhKce2WACQCsH2NYeDHtsnufdiWgE3r5uakqsFeJXQ -->\r\n# Crypto_Oaj\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwlmrm6ksc8sa5fdhm63prqve6hjzvghdc3053zwz6hyeg0ayhg2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile building global visibility is valuable, allocating treasury funds to temporary event booths at exhibitions does not contribute to long-term infrastructure or technical advancement within the Cardano ecosystem. As a DRep, I believe our priorities must focus on lasting developer tools, infrastructure projects, and on-chain innovation—not ephemeral marketing placements with limited strategic impact.\r\n\r\nEvent booths do little to strengthen core protocol resilience, developer adoption, or decentralized growth. Without a clear path linking expense to lasting benefits, this proposal relies heavily on brand awareness that may not translate into real on-chain activity or measurable community growth. Therefore, I vote NO, believing that treasury resources are better spent on projects that deliver enduring value and technical substance.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
