    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVD7ndcUezSnfxcVK69tcgnHMDc26zcLWfVGFBidCGWXF -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA is voting **YES **on this proposal because it meets constitutional requirements for treasury withdrawals by providing a legal contract, milestone-based delivery and third-party oversight. Its purpose — improving Cardano’s presence at major exhibitions — is a legitimate and valuable activity within the scope of ecosystem growth.\r\n\r\nWhile RCADA’s primary funding priorities are often focused on upstream infrastructure, developer tools and dApp enablement, we recognize that strategic marketing can be a critical growth driver. This proposal aims to close the visibility gap for Cardano projects in global markets, giving them affordable access to events where investors, developers and users make decisions. By partially subsidizing participation costs, it enables smaller projects to gain exposure they might otherwise miss.\r\n\r\nThe proposer, operating under Supplyoneers FZ-LLC but widely known in the community as **Discover Cardano**, has a track record of sustained, self-funded marketing efforts. They have hosted educational spaces such as Cardano Over Coffee, created onboarding materials for new users, organized IRL events and represented Cardano at industry exhibitions even without treasury support. Their past initiatives — including giving multiple projects stage presence at a Dubai TradFi innovation event — demonstrate a commitment to filling marketing gaps left by founding entities, making them a credible operator for this initiative.\r\n\r\nThere are centralization concerns around Intersect’s role in administering these funds, but Intersect remains an open membership organization where any community member can participate in governance and contribute to operational oversight. The vendor’s shared-cost approach also helps mitigate risk by ensuring projects have their own stake in the effort rather than relying entirely on treasury funds.\r\n\r\nThe vendor’s decision to reduce the request from ₳1.11M to ₳889,500 shows responsiveness to community concerns. **However, we expect to see clear and publicly verifiable participant selection criteria, post-event reporting that measures tangible outcomes such as leads, partnerships, or developer sign-ups and coordination with other treasury-funded marketing to avoid duplication of effort**.\r\n\r\nThe sustainability of this initiative will depend on how effectively it equips participating projects with the skills and knowledge to maximize exhibition ROI without requiring repeated subsidies. The educational model at the core of this proposal gives it potential long-term value, but those benefits will only materialize if results and lessons learned are documented and shared openly with the community.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, RCADA supports this treasury withdrawal **on the condition that** it delivers transparent impact metrics, inclusive access for participants and effective coordination within the broader marketing strategy. **If these conditions are not met, it will directly influence RCADA’s stance on similar proposals in the future**.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qma1P5d5s4ZEucbYdLX4ZpycudJLtNCBj1fUwxhwJJRw1T -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn the Ekklesia vote, I initially voted No, but after further review and due diligence, I have decided to change my vote to Yes.\r\n\r\nMy initial concern was prioritization, particularly in relation to the NCL proposal. However, upon closer examination, I recognize the value this proposal offers in expanding global awareness of the Cardano ecosystem. Strategic presence at international exhibitions can play a critical role in attracting investors, developers, and users — a key area where Cardano has historically lacked visibility.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the proposal outlines a robust fund management structure through Intersect’s smart contracts, with external oversight and milestone-based disbursement. This provides a reasonable level of assurance in terms of accountability and execution.\r\n\r\nConsidering the broader potential impact on ecosystem growth, I now support this initiative and cast my vote as Yes.\r\n\r\nEkklesia投票では一度No票を投じましたが、精査の結果、Yesに変更する判断をしました。\r\n\r\n当初はNCLとの兼ね合いから優先順位を下げましたが、本提案はCardanoエコシステムのグローバルな認知向上に資する内容であり、特にマーケティングの側面からその意義は十分にあると考えます。展示会という場を活用し、投資家・開発者・ユーザーへの訴求力を高めることは、現在のCardanoにとって重要な要素です。\r\n\r\nまた、Intersectのスマートコントラクトを活用した資金管理体制や、第三者による監督・検証体制も整備されており、執行面においても一定の信頼性があると判断しました。\r\n\r\nエコシステム全体への波及効果を期待し、今回Yes票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/31_CardanoEcosystemPavilionsatExhibitions_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳889,500 for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO votes YES on the Treasury Withdrawal for Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions.\r\n\r\nReason for Support:\r\n\r\nSIPO recognizes the urgent need to expand Cardano’s real-world presence and outreach, especially in a global environment where brand recognition often does not translate into understanding or adoption. While “Cardano” is known, what is being built on Cardano is still largely unknown outside the core community. This proposal addresses this gap by supporting ecosystem participants to attend international exhibitions under a shared and professional Cardano Pavilion structure.\r\n\r\nSIPO particularly supports the partial subsidy model that encourages commitment and pre/post event efforts by projects, and values the professional experience of the vendor, Supplyoneers FZ-LLC, who has previously proven capable of high-impact exhibition operations.\r\n\r\nIn addition:\r\n\t•\tThe proposal is cost-optimized through partial funding and vendor-initiated budget reduction from ₳1.12M to ₳889.5k.\r\n\t•\tIt leverages a robust legal and smart contract-based accountability framework, including milestone verification by Intersect and a third-party assurer.\r\n\t•\tIt aligns with the overarching ₳275M Intersect-administered budget and contributes to raising Cardano’s global visibility, adoption, and investor/developer engagement.\r\n\r\nSIPO believes this proposal brings tangible ROI for the ecosystem and strengthens Cardano’s international strategic positioning.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは「Cardano Ecosystem Pavilions at Exhibitions」に対する889,500ADAのトレジャリー支出提案に賛成票（YES）を投じました。\r\n\r\n支持理由：\r\n\r\nSIPOは、Cardanoのリアルな世界への露出と認知拡大の必要性を強く認識しています。Cardanoという名前は広く知られている一方で、その上に構築されているプロジェクトや技術の実態は、依然として広く知られていません。本提案はこの課題を解決するものであり、グローバルな展示会においてCardanoのエコシステムとして一体感ある形でプレゼンスを示すための重要な取り組みです。\r\n\r\nSIPOが特に評価している点は以下の通りです：\r\n\t•\tプロジェクトに対する全額補助ではなく、一部助成型である点。これにより、参加プロジェクトの主体的な事前準備・当日活動・事後フォローが求められ、ROI向上につながります。\r\n\t•\tSupplyoneers FZ-LLCの実績と専門性に裏打ちされたオペレーション体制。すでに自費での展示ブース経験や、伝統金融機関向けのピッチ実績もあり、信頼に足る運営が期待できます。\r\n\t•\t当初提案よりも約20%削減（₳1,119,333 → ₳889,500）されたコスト最適化設計。\r\n\t•\tIntersect主導のスマートコントラクト・リーガル契約・マイルストーン管理を通じた高度なガバナンスと透明性。\r\n\r\nこの提案は、Cardanoの国際的ブランド強化、開発者や投資家との接点創出、エコシステム成長の加速に直結するものであり、SIPOとして確実に賛成する価値があると判断しました。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
