    {
      "voter": "drep1ytajpleue086e8jw0vetfl70qay0tgv8nccfv4aygkpt8xsjpgdys",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbtdfLVgjfNEDUFgRkVXxM5SHfECpKuTU2WBXCqrfvQhy -->\r\n# drep1ytajpleue086e8jw0vetfl70qay0tgv8nccfv4aygkpt8xsjpgdys\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Budget ₳5M Loan for Cardano's Global Listing Expansion - Powered by Snek\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytajpleue086e8jw0vetfl70qay0tgv8nccfv4aygkpt8xsjpgdys`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter careful considerations, evaluating the POVs from both the FOR & AGAINST sides of the argument, and did some digging on the financials, I have decided to change my vote for the proposal from \"NO\" to \"YES\".\r\n\r\nYou can read my previous rationale here.\r\nhttps://x.com/pizzadren/status/1964250649710747706?t=iAakoUAQS3e1URC1iDe6Pw&s=19\r\n\r\nMy reasoning for changing the vote to YES is based on the new rationale below:\r\n\r\n1) 1st concern: How is SNEK going to repay back the loan?\r\n\r\nI highly encourage ppl to visit https://whysnek.com/#revenue for more details on where their revenue sources come from.\r\n\r\nTo summarize, all the revenue sources mentioned actually go to these two handles here:\r\n\r\n$snek_labs\r\n$snekpit\r\n\r\nThey also have a handle called $snek, so if you check the asset balances for these three handles using pool.pm, they have the asset value as follows (as of Epoch 581): \r\n\r\nA) snek:\r\n- 651 mil SNEK = ~3 million ADA\r\n- 785k SPLASH = ~78k ADA\r\n- 51k ADA\r\n- total = 3.129 mil ADA\r\n\r\nB) snekpit:\r\n- ~10.63 mil SNEK = ~49k ADA\r\n- ~319k ADA\r\n- total = 368k ADA\r\n\r\nC) snek_labs:\r\n- ~10k SNEK = 46 ADA\r\n- ~21k ADA\r\n- total = 21k ADA\r\n\r\nWhich brings to a grand total of ~3.5 mil ADA (excluding the memecoins & other CNTs not mentioned), and it's also 70% of the 5 million ADA loan requested. If their loan is approved & administered, they'll get a total of 8.5 million ADA in total assets.\r\n\r\nNow let's talk about revenue streams. Snek's largest revenue stream is snekdotfun. \r\nhttps://x.com/goofy_crisp/status/1964306111961653664?t=FNW_zzlmqAaHo1hjHuFH6g&s=19 \r\nAccording to Goofycrisp, Snekdotfun can generate > 100k ADA per month in revenue, so I double checked his statement by going to Snekdotfun token launch page, they actually charge a 1% fee for each launch, and additional 100 ADA fee if you turn on the Hyped Launch toggle. \r\n\r\nFor a 100k ADA revenue & assuming 100 ADA in fees generated per token launch, Snekdotfun needs to launch 1,000 tokens per month or 33 tokens per day. I'll leave that up to you to decide if these numbers make sense to you, but IMO with such simple steps to launch tokens & monitoring closely to the number of new tokens launched daily, I think these numbers are achievable. Assuming if they can keep up to 1 year of doing this, they'll generate 1.2 million ADA revenue per year and around 4 years to breakeven and repay the full loan amount, just from snekdotfun alone.\r\n\r\nThe 2nd largest income source i can identify is from DEX LP fees. According to https://whysnek.com/#revenue , all the trading fees earned by snek are used to buyback snek & burn to reduce the supply. This revenue source can be indirectly tied to the price swings in CEXes. If there's huge price swings to trade SNEK in CEXes, the price changes also reflects in DEXes thus it will generate more trading volume among ADA traders, thus earning fee revenue from there. According to https://snekboard.com/ , their daily Snek DEX volume is around ~900k ADA, so assuming all the DEXes charged 0.25% LP fee & Snek owns approx 20% of the fees (taking the LP tokens own by $snek & divide by total LP tokens in Minswap) and they choose to repay the loan instead of buybacks & burn, that's 450 ADA in fees per day, 164k ADA per year & 821k ADA for 5 years. Listing on the largest exchanges like Binance & Coinbase can push this number higher.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, with the remaining revenue sources from snekx, snekbot, snekkies, snek figures & snek energy, not to mention they are still operating a SNEK SPO, I would say they are on track to be able to repay the loan + interest within 3 years.\r\n\r\nYou may also ask: \"Why can't they just pay the listings themselves, if they own so much assets ady?\". Well, if you're using assets to pay for listings, you're left with very little to grow the Snek ecosystem. As per what goofycrisp mentioned, they have already paid $4.5 mil (~5.5 mil ADA) for major listings like Kucoin, Huobi & Cryptodotcom, so the 5 mil ADA loan shall give them more leeway to grow the ecosystem & pay for listings in huge exchanges like Binance, Coinbase, Bybit, etc.\r\n\r\nI have said a lot on the revenue part and now I'm gonna answer the next biggest question: Can the treasury afford to pay for this loan? Short answer is of course.\r\n\r\nAccording to Cexplorer (Pots section), as of Epoch 580, the current treasury balance is 1.58 Billion ADA. Distributing a loan of 5 mil is only 0.3% of the treasury, and if you subtract the treasury amount for Epoch N - Epoch (N-1), you'll get an average of 4.3 million ADA is being added to the treasury every epoch for the last 50 Epochs (from 524 to 574), so currently the treasury is able to recoup 5 million ADA in about 1+ Epoch, and to fund Snek which has a huge proven track record of not just being a typical memecoin, but a memefied business & marketing venture for Cardano, even a 5 million grant is also worth the investment, not to mentioned that it's a loan. \r\n\r\nTo me, I would consider loaning 5 mil ADA to Snek as low risk, with high returns that Cardano can benefit from bringing in new users, generating high tx volume & fee revenue to Cardano & also Snek has the potential to do more within 5 years besides listing on CEXes if they can expand their token utility to mini games where users can pay & win SNEK by playing popular games like Snake, Tetris or pinball.\r\n\r\nWith both points addressed, the last big question will be: \"What about other CNT listings? Are each CNT gonna ask 5 million from the treasury and then the treasury depletes more & more until it's no more?\". I think as dReps, we must evaluate each CNT on a case-by-case basis, by evaluating their business model, what are the revenue streams, have them to buy handles & track their assets & movements. Just because Snek can get the loan, doesn't mean other CNTs will get it as we also need to evaluate again if they are able to sustain their business model & repay the loan.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
