      "voter": "Beyond DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leftThinker/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Beyond DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygz6d57tpcpnw3yym2ca2gxwumr53u7le7z6a7knv9akssqdt7mfa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote in favor of the Cardano Constitution because it establishes a structured, decentralized governance system that empowers the community, ensuring transparency and long-term stability. The extensive consultation process and the principles embedded in CIP-1694 provide a solid foundation for decision-making that aligns with the core values of decentralization, representation, and fairness.\r\n\r\nHowever, my support comes with reservations regarding areas that require further refinement, such as enhancing oversight of the Constitutional Committee, preventing power concentration among DReps, improving the efficiency of constitutional amendments, and ensuring full transparency in treasury allocations.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Brent_Norris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DragonsBloodKush/ada/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context-constitution.jsonld -->\r\n# Brent_Norris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytqpw3yqgfw57vlx8sf7vevzgl8ksgdfjzqs9ducesyx99cwszkxj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI could have been convinced to move 5%.\r\n\r\nBalanced and deeper rationale behind the no vote - help from ChatGPT:\r\n\r\nAssumption of Future ADA Price Appreciation:\r\n\r\nThe proposal argues that the treasury’s sustainability will depend heavily on future ADA price appreciation rather than transaction volume growth. This is a risky assumption and a classic case of wishful thinking or appeal to future possibilities. If ADA’s price does not appreciate as expected, the treasury might face significant funding shortfalls, potentially jeopardizing long-term development, ecosystem funding, and governance initiatives.\r\n\r\nOveremphasis on Staking Incentives as a Decentralization Solution:\r\n\r\nThe argument that increasing staking rewards will necessarily lead to greater decentralization is a hasty generalization. While higher rewards may attract more participation, they do not guarantee that large stakeholders won’t dominate the system. Centralization risks may still persist if the top stakeholders continue to control a large portion of ADA, undermining the decentralization goal.\r\n\r\nEconomic Sustainability Risks:\r\n\r\nReducing the treasury cut reduces the immediate inflow of funds into the treasury, even if staking incentives increase. This could lead to a false dichotomy by presenting the choice as either incentivizing staking or maintaining treasury health, without thoroughly exploring hybrid solutions or incremental reductions that balance both priorities.\r\n\r\nMisleading Precedent with Plutus V3 Cost Model Update:\r\n\r\nDrawing a parallel between this economic adjustment and the Plutus V3 cost model update could be a false analogy. The Plutus update focused on technical optimizations with minimal economic impact, whereas treasury adjustments directly affect the network’s financial foundation. The procedural similarity does not guarantee similar outcomes or levels of risk.\r\n\r\nPotential Undermining of Treasury-Funded Development:\r\n\r\nThe proposal assumes that lower treasury funding will drive developers toward building transaction-heavy applications to secure funding through fees, which is an appeal to incentive fallacy. Developers might instead move to ecosystems with more immediate and guaranteed funding sources, especially during bearish market conditions when transaction volumes typically decline.\r\n\r\nIssues Arising from Voting For the Proposal\r\n\r\nTreasury Funding Shortfalls: If ADA price does not appreciate as predicted, the treasury may struggle to fund essential network improvements, community initiatives, and long-term development projects.\r\n\r\nShort-Term Gains vs. Long-Term Stability: Increasing staking rewards offers immediate benefits to stakers but could compromise the network’s ability to invest in future growth and innovation, leading to stagnation.\r\n\r\nRisk of Overdependence on Transaction Fees: A reduced treasury cut might shift the focus towards generating high transaction volumes, potentially leading to spam-like behaviors or prioritizing quantity over quality in network usage.\r\n\r\nIssues Arising from Voting Against the Proposal\r\n\r\nMissed Opportunity for Enhanced Participation: Maintaining the 20% cut could discourage smaller stakeholders from participating due to relatively lower rewards, potentially limiting decentralization and network security.\r\n\r\nPerceived Inertia in Governance: Rejecting the proposal might signal resistance to adapting economic parameters despite the evolving maturity of the ecosystem, potentially alienating community members seeking more dynamic governance.\r\n\r\nConstitutional and Governance Alignment Issues\r\n\r\nAlignment with Constitutional Guardrails: The proposal claims to align with the new constitution, which permits treasury cuts between 10% and 30%​. However, documents like Getting to a Minimum Viable \r\n\r\nConstitution and Beyond emphasize the importance of balancing immediate changes with long-term governance stability​.\r\n\r\nOversight and Accountability: The interim and future Constitutional Committees are tasked with ensuring economic sustainability​. A sudden change in treasury parameters might create additional burdens on these committees, especially if future adjustments are needed due to unforeseen economic impacts.\r\n\r\nDecentralized Governance Challenges: With the newly established governance framework under SIP 1694, there are ongoing efforts to stabilize governance processes​. A major economic parameter change during this transitional phase might introduce unnecessary complexity and strain on governance bodies.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/DRepdata20250201Vote/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(2).jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私としてはカルダノ憲法に以下の意義を見出したため支持します。 カルダノ憲法は分散型ガバナンスの基盤を確立し、長期的な進化と透明性のある意思決定を可能にします。その意義は、①「バタフライ効果」として、小さな変化が長期的に大きな影響をもたらし、持続可能な分散型エコシステムを構築できること、②流動性民主主義の確立により柔軟な投票権の委任・回収を可能にし、ポスト国家的民主主義の発展を促すこと、③サイファーパンクの理念の実現を通じデジタル主権や検閲耐性を確保し、中央管理から解放されたガバナンスを構築すること、④シンギュラリティ時代のAIに対する「DNA情報」として技術発展が人類の利益に資する方向へ導き、中央集権型AIの暴走を防ぐ倫理的枠組みとして機能する可能性があります。さらに、憲法が確立するオンチェーンガバナンスは、意思決定の公平性と説明責任を強化し、ADA所有者がネットワークの発展に直接関与できる環境を整えます。短期的には、パラメーター調整の透明性が向上し迅速な意思決定が可能となるだけでなく、コミュニティの声がより直接反映されることで、エコシステム全体の信頼性と安定性が高まります。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Advocate",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://gitlab.com/thecardanoadvocate1/cardanoadvocate/-/raw/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Cardano Advocate\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfzqgvegtv8utkvlyhfa07u0un3dml0v9pvxjuumjcfswsgdfj50g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm concerned about the 1 token 1 vote voting model. \r\n\r\nIt is not representative of the will of the Community or even representative of the involvement and interest of the individual in the success of Cardano. \r\n\r\nIt is a flawed model as it was shown in the last round of Project Catalyst, a model that makes it very exclusive for newcomers. \r\n\r\nWould prefer a better model, that considers other things such as contribution to Cardano,  time spent in Cardano, knowledge on a certain topic, or even the percentage of wealth Cardano represents in the overall wealth of the voter. An algorithm that takes different to make some kind of weight voting.\r\n\r\nWe need to explore better and fairer models, and the first governance system should already include such fairer models. It shouldn't be biased from the start, as we risk not being able to change it later on.\r\n\r\nAdditionally and considering this is the voting model we will use from now onwards, I'm extremely concerned about the real possibility, that when we find a better, fairer, and more representative business model, we won't be able to upgrade it as large whales and token holders will likely not be receptive to losing voting power and influence regarding the future of Cardano, especially considering that there are several billion dollars at stake. \r\n\r\nFrom the Content of the Constitution, would like to see clearer boundaries and principles regarding the administration of funds from the budget.\r\n\r\nWhile there are other minor concerns with this Constitution, especially within the lack of a clearer more straightforward mention relative to decentralization and peer review research, it is the flawed voting model that is the major concern.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXo9gs9sbp9pJGsb42tLHhKSn8qcYGVafhF3hLoaLz3ey -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe delegate-approved Cardano Constitution is an improvement over the existing Interim Constitution. It reinforces the three-body governance model from CIP-1694 and establishes a token-based governance framework with checks and balances. In line with the Ethos and Principles outlined in  ‘Our Cardano’, particularly the core governance principle that Cardano’s governance processes must be accessible, transparent, decentralized, and adaptable, the new constitution upholds the resilient system of checks and balances anchored by ada and involving key governance groups, including the Constitutional Committee, Stake Pool Operators, and Delegated Representatives. For these reasons, the Cardano Foundation votes Yes on this governance action (Action ID: gov_action133jnaewfsq8x6v08ndd87l2yqryp63r30t2dkceacxx5cply5n7sqzlcyqf). The new constitution introduces several improvements compared to the interim version, including a set of ten Cardano Blockchain Tenets and a dedicated article for the Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget. These enhancements help address previous shortcomings and provide a more flexible, transparent, and accountable governance framework. In our assessment, the delegate-approved Cardano Constitution meets the procedural and substantive requirements set by the Interim Constitution. By using cardano-cli, we have verified that the hash of the delegate-approved Cardano Constitution is identical to the version voted on by delegates at the Constitutional Convention, ensuring complete consistency and integrity. While the new constitution marks an advancement, we stress that future amendments will be necessary as the ecosystem evolves. It is also likely that governance challenges will arise going forward and will need to be addressed. Finally, further improvements in structure and clarity would expand the accessibility of the Cardano governance model and enhance its long-term viability. The Cardano Foundation is committed to playing an active role in this ongoing process, continuously contributing to the refinement and improvement of the Constitution. In summary, the delegate-approved Cardano Constitution enhances governance, deepens community participation, and lays a foundation for future development, making it a clear improvement over the Interim Constitution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNgSxiwdBops75g6Cn5QqohEL6idSf1a2ZSeceqgS1PLk -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI find the constitution overly long, and would have preferred it to be a one page document. The long form potentially facilitates the creation of a Cardano bureaucracy, which I think is something we should avoid or at least minimise at all costs. \r\n\r\nI am not a fan of some specific aspects like the support for off-chain governance, the prominent role of the constitutional committee or the overly precise limits and guardrails, which I think would ideally be decided by individual votes.\r\n\r\nNevertheless, I agree strongly with the 10 tenets and with the overall tone and scope of the document, while I observe no items that clash directly with my principles. Hence I will vote in favour.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano-Ghost-001",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cardano-Ghost-001/Drep-ghost-info/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Constitution_Approval.jsonld -->\r\n# Cardano-Ghost-001\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytec0m7nhw498kzu5qvkqcn2gy2xxw5dwzr62zte9px262chpn3je`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile this constitution is not perfect, it is a necessary and well-thought-out step toward decentralization and increased participation in governance.\r\n\r\nThis vote isn’t about creating a flawless document right now—it’s about setting the groundwork for a governance system that can grow and adapt. Cardano’s governance supports ongoing refinement and progress, but that can only begin if we take the initial step.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Satuchac/DRep/refs/heads/main/001.jsonld -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRead the full rationale:\r\n\r\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/Satuchac/DRep/refs/heads/main/001_My%20Rationale%20for%20Approving%20the%20Cardano%20Constitution.txt",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cash",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cashpog/Cash-rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Cash\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygeyfh8nm03dnl5a2hxdtv09pu7uhep9l0cpg0zpr60jqys05cku2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a delegate, and participant in the definitions process, I am very pleased with the current state of the constitution. It is not perfect, but it is not impeding or harming the chain in it's current state. With continued workstreams planned, and people starting to pay attention to governance, i think we are ready to take this step and move towards a fully ratified on -chain constitution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/new_constitution_1.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter having participated in numerous Cardano Constitution discussions and reading various different drafts, as well as analyzing the current concerns about proposal & discussion availability on GovTools, I have decided to vote yes on the delegate-approved Constitution.  I still think that the Constitution and the platforms/tools that inform delegators need some work, but this draft is still a major step up from the Interim Constitution that is in place.  It is also worth noting that the Interim Constitution might REQUIRE this delegate-approved draft to be in place before other drafts can be proposed.  For these reasons, I am voting yes.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Daniel_Sullivan_(pyraic3)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pyraic3/pyraic3-constitution-vote-response/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Daniel_Sullivan_(pyraic3)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfhusw50g9ujptwg028zp38pmnnq80xa7l60g0vyhrsngsqns67xn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe third paragraph of the preamble attempts to divorce the constitution from “traditional nation states”, yet proceeds to outline itself precisely as a traditional nation state, with all the same characteristics, except without any national borders. Thereby creating a globalized, and centralizing one world government.\r\n\r\nThe nature of a traditional nation state is a system which governs people. The nature of a blockchain governance system ought to be a system to govern the blockchain. This document explicitly seeks to “guard the rights of those who utilize it”, (preamble paragraph 3) (without outlining what those rights are) and thus at best is an iteration of a traditional nation state, and not a new decentralized financial governance model that we all hoped for.\r\n\r\nThis document, both implicitly and explicitly, astonishingly exceeds the rights and authorities it ought to be imbued with.\r\n\r\n1. It ought to be explicitly forbidden to wage wars, inflict, promote, or fund violence against any person, place, or state.\r\n2. It ought to be explicitly forbidden that any “artificially intelligent” programs be elected into governance positions, specifically and especially members of the constitutional committee, but also otherwise wherever possible. There are multiple ways to enforce this.\r\n3. It ought to be explicitly forbidden to accumulate any outsized centralizing power. The CIP-1694 model directly allows for outsized centralization. The common response: “it’s not enforceable to prevent people from being a DRep, on the CC, and an SPO, so there is nothing that can be done”  is not a sufficient response. Nor is “community enforcement” sufficient as a “check-and-balance” as it is a standardized benefit across any model. If it’s not enforceable, we ought to construct an entirely different decentralized model that inherently doesn’t allow for the outsized accumulation, and centralization of power. It is especially bad, then, to also lie about the model citing “three independent governance bodies”, (Article III section II) when they are not, in fact, independent.\r\n4. It ought to be explicitly and implicitly congruent with a set of principles. The tenets are neither sufficient, nor are they congruent across the articles.\r\n5. It ought to be explicitly and implicitly understood that we are not creating a competing or combative model against traditional markets or market participants, whether they be governments, corporations, or people.\r\n\r\nAs an elected alternate for the convention, and active participant in this process, as well as within Intersect, I have seen many, many, many VERY concerning instances of censorship, severe lacks of transparency, dictatorial actions, amongst other numerous disturbing experiences. There is no need to detail them all here, but those experiences, the reasons I listed above, and the 350 million ada net change limit from the budget proposal that was just released, finalized my decision.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1y2gpgzktn3gcjkj4wem2sn7af44974r66gh2vcsh0u0jlagxu440s",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CryptoJimBo21/CardanoGovVotes/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# drep1y2gpgzktn3gcjkj4wem2sn7af44974r66gh2vcsh0u0jlagxu440s\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gpgzktn3gcjkj4wem2sn7af44974r66gh2vcsh0u0jlagxu440s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI, Brandon Cartwright, born Feb. 13, 1981 in Jackson, Tennessee and operating as DRep $CryptoJimBo votes Yes on \"Cardano Constitution To Replace The Interim Constitution.\" I am voting YES because it establishes a robust, decentralized, and self-governed framework aligned with my vision of Cardano. The new Constitution formalizes a participatory structure with DReps, SPOs, and the Constitutional Committee, ensuring distributed decision-making. It introduces clear guardrails, predictable fees, fair rewards, and financial sustainability within a 45B ADA cap. The governance process is fully on-chain, ensuring transparency and reducing corruption and centralization risks. The Constitution recognizes all ADA holders as stakeholders, preserving permissionless participation. As a living document, it allows on-chain amendments, ensuring adaptability. This Constitution strengthens governance, making it a necessary upgrade. A YES vote secures Cardano’s future as a fair, transparent, and decentralized ecosystem.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1y2sz79r6c4lc0sl468pdtdmtsnsmx3sahggtqtc9hzear5se6mwel",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/apestchanker/cardanoconstitutionvoterationale-Jan25/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# drep1y2sz79r6c4lc0sl468pdtdmtsnsmx3sahggtqtc9hzear5se6mwel\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2sz79r6c4lc0sl468pdtdmtsnsmx3sahggtqtc9hzear5se6mwel`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a pioneer at Civics Committee and Voltaire participant, I acknowledge this Constitution’s flaws—centralization risks and ambiguous tenets. Yet, rejecting it risks stagnation under weaker interim rules. The Plomin Hard Fork proves decentralized governance works. While imperfect, this framework empowers ada holders, replacing legacy control. I vote YES to advance self-governance, trusting the community will refine gaps (e.g., CC accountability, treasury safeguards).",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/ConstitutionVoteCardano/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a major milestone in the long term future of Cardano!!! I am thrilled to make history and vote YES!!!",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ytkt0vvxqlwmws5n04ud2q3sk0yu9lh65arkp2suaqdgmgqgrza6c",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRRCLb56zizmMxt9ch4sDTmhA44JfkBZNWx4FKoQptC19 -->\r\n# drep1ytkt0vvxqlwmws5n04ud2q3sk0yu9lh65arkp2suaqdgmgqgrza6c\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytkt0vvxqlwmws5n04ud2q3sk0yu9lh65arkp2suaqdgmgqgrza6c`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting yes to ratify the Delegate-Approved Cardano Constitution. It is time to move on from the Interim Constitution and embrace a governance model that reflects where Cardano is today and where it’s headed. This is a big step forward for Cardano’s governance!\r\n\r\nThe Interim Constitution was always meant to be temporary. A starting point to guide us while we figured out a more solid framework. Over time, the Delegate-Approved Constitution has evolved into something much stronger, shaped by community input, and a clearer vision for the future.\r\n\r\nThis isn't just a small update. It provides better structure, clearer decision-making, and a governance model that truly fits Cardano’s long-term goals. By ratifying it, we are making sure the ecosystem has a solid foundation to grow in a decentralized and transparent way.\r\n\r\nCheers!",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Duc Tiger",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmT6A9N8u7E36RH1eSrEXqwm1AswQ5dENk7qwCLBfe6ChX -->\r\n# Duc Tiger\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt0cvg2649d34afclefrxvyn2ctys87a5jt84ckczyjlvgcu7nxyr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI total agree and will vote Yes for this GA. The Cardano community has long awaited an official constitution. After more than two years of discussions, both online and offline, across various levels and countries, this constitution has been carefully considered and truly reflects the collective spirit of the community.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00005_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Eternl DRep Committee (EDC) votes YES on the first-ever Cardano Constitution as a living document and the foundation of community-driven governance. This marks the beginning of decentralized decision-making, ensuring adaptability and accountability. It is a prerequisite for Cardano’s development in 2025 and beyond, enabling structured governance and future improvements. The EDC supports this step toward a self-sustaining, decentralized ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "FAIR Pool #01",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmcm9BN72ygoeXxRe4KjDhhYxpf6PnGtUzuSqr5h7AVVnh -->\r\n# FAIR Pool #01\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytamqncvuz2r0atkwxwgcn5zmgxm09j0g2lgcrp7ddqfsfcsgnr8s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support the constitution because its framework is robust and transparent, with clearly defined guardrails that enhance the security and decentralization of Cardano while facilitating effective community governance. My primary concern is that the comprehensive detail and potential rigidity of the framework could limit the system's agility in addressing unforeseen challenges. Nevertheless, I consider it a promising foundation that warrants further refinement and clarification over time.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BrianLee12/Cardano-Governance/refs/heads/main/Cardano%20Constitution/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe current version of the Cardano Constitution is the result of efforts of a large number of Cardano community members, and is the best constitution we will get for now. \r\n\r\nThere is plenty of room for improvement, and while I may disagree with some aspects of the Cardano Constitution, it is time to move forward with what we currently have.\r\n\r\nWe will have plenty of opportunities to make improvements to the constitution in the future, and here are some areas I think merit serious attention going forward:\r\n\r\n\r\n- The overall lack of on chain enforceability of the constitution. We have already seen in the past that social pressure is not enough, such as with the centralization of Stake Pools, leaving us with ~20% of operators controlling ~80% of all stake.\r\n\r\n- The lack of choice for governance models other than 1 lovelace = 1 vote from the beginning. DIDs and quadratic voting would put us in a much better governance model that does not lead to centralized oligarchy or plutocracy, and we are sadly in this situation right from the start of governance, which was predetermined for CIP 1694.\r\n\r\n- It would be smart to encourage ADA holders financially to participate in governance. Using a carrot method instead of the current stick method (can't withdraw rewards until delegating) would get better results. Having a portion of treasury rewards allocated to ADA holders who actually delegate to a DRep vs Auto Abstain, and encourage decentralization by having overall better rewards if the DRep is not in the very top rankings by stake delegated. This would encourage more active participation and movement of delegated voting power.\r\n\r\n- Article 1, Section 1, TENET 9 and Article 2, Section 2 are already in violation by deliberately making it financially difficult to participate in governance. \r\n\r\nDRep and Direct Voter registration fees should be lowered significantly so that meaningful participation can happen. Finances alone are not an adequate determining factor for leadership or governance capabilities of a person, especially when Cardano is global and many cannot afford a 500 ADA deposit but could offer meaningful governance contributions.\r\n\r\nThe same goes for the *govDeposit* amount for submitting governance actions - 100,000 ADA is set deliberately high with the reasoning that it will limit spam. DReps and ADA holders were told that we would have ADA pooling tools available to mitigate this very high barrier to entry in order for meaningful participation to still happen - we did not get these tools, and still don't have them. We cannot have a deliberately high financial barrier to governance participation if we want true decentralized governance like what is preached. So either we need *govDeposit* to be lowered to ~5000 ADA, or we need the tooling that was promised to be present on gov.tools\r\n\r\n\r\n- Article 3, Section 5 has been violated by gov.tools already, so we need at least 1 alternative interface platform to gov.tools with similar functionality to ensure there is a second valid and useful option.\r\n\r\nWhenever I experienced technical issues with gov.tools, I filled out their support form and also contacted their support email. I received no response back on multiple occasions, but the issues were eventually quietly *fixed*. My governance dashboard is still broken and doesn't display my previous voting history. I expect a real tech support team for any governance dashboard for Cardano - one that can be effectively contacted and replies to emails.\r\n\r\nThere is also currently no way for a competing Cardano Constitution to be submitted in time on gov.tools, as this function will not be able to be enabled in time for whatever reason. A deliberate choice that was made which leaves no possibility of alternative constitution choice. I doubt we could have a better submission in time, but I expect transparency and undue influence / manipulation to be followed if it is supposed to be enshrined in this constitution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Gimbalabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://github.com/gimbalabs/gimbalabs-drep/blob/main/votes/constitution.md -->\r\n# Gimbalabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Constitution to Replace the Interim Constitution\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf05mscx9y53363vc2zqc6jk0gqn6yvh8rz4lznv64ewl3cnmpwqu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html\r\n  lang=\"en\"\r\n  \r\n  data-color-mode=\"auto\" data-light-theme=\"light\" data-dark-theme=\"dark\"\r\n  data-a11y-animated-images=\"system\" data-a11y-link-underlines=\"true\"\r\n  \r\n  >\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  <head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\r\n  <link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://github.githubassets.com\">\r\n  <link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com\">\r\n  <link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://github-cloud.s3.amazonaws.com\">\r\n  <link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/\">\r\n  <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://github.githubassets.com\" crossorigin>\r\n  <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com\">\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\n\r\n  <link crossorigin=\"anonymous\" media=\"all\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://github.githubassets.com/assets/light-2ff56e1b36116ee2.css\" /><link crossorigin=\"anonymous\" media=\"all\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://github.githubassets.com/assets/light_high_contrast-f7f95d7633592089.css\" /><link crossorigin=\"anonymous\" media=\"all\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://github.githubassets.com/assets/dark-2d1fe43dbc9adf1f.css\" /><link crossorigin=\"anonymous\" media=\"all\" rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://github.githubassets.com/assets/dark_high_contrast-d530ee188d165539.css\" /><link data-color-theme=\"light\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" media=\"all\" rel=\"stylesheet\" data-href=\"https://github.githubassets.com/assets/light-2ff56e1b36116ee2.css\" /><link data-color-theme=\"light_high_contrast\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" media=\"all\" rel=\"stylesheet\" data-href=\"https://github.g