    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/r/25/250812_adastat_4pgcp0jyh.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳212,000 for AdaStat.net Cardano blockchain explorer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal continues funding for AdaStat.net, a proven and widely used Cardano blockchain explorer. The project delivers decentralised, open-source, high-performance infrastructure that benefits SPOs, DReps, developers, and everyday users. It has a strong track record of consistent updates since 2019, offers free API access, and aligns with the approved Cardano Budget 2025 plan. Funding ensures long-term sustainability, improved features, and supports ecosystem transparency.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳212,000 for AdaStat.net Cardano blockchain explorer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU1LDiKvScxRv1bvdgziqNCP23iECJAxNkSWczUWyNjJy -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳212,000 for AdaStat.net Cardano blockchain explorer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nAdaStat.net is a long-standing and widely used Cardano blockchain explorer, serving users since the Shelley Incentivized Testnet in 2019.\r\n\r\nThis proposal ensures the continued development and support of AdaStat over the next 24 months. Key improvements include performance tuning, UI/UX updates, and integration of Cardano governance data—particularly valuable for DReps, SPOs, and governance participants.\r\n\r\nGiven AdaStat’s proven reliability, ongoing community use, and importance to ecosystem transparency, I believe continued funding is technically justified and strategically aligned with Cardano’s infrastructure goals.\r\n\r\n本提案に YES 票を投じます。\r\n\r\nAdaStat.net は2019年のShelleyインセンティブ付きテストネット以来、長期にわたり稼働してきた信頼性の高いブロックチェーンエクスプローラーです。\r\n\r\n本提案では、今後24ヶ月にわたってAdaStatの継続的な開発と保守が行われる予定です。パフォーマンス改善、UI/UXの強化、そしてCardanoの新たなガバナンス情報への対応などが盛り込まれており、DRep・SPO・一般ユーザーにとって価値のあるアップデートとなります。\r\n\r\nすでに実績と信頼性があるインフラであり、Cardanoエコシステムの透明性・アクセシビリティの向上にも貢献していることから、継続支援は妥当かつ戦略的に意義があると判断します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/22_AdaStat_net_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳212,000 for AdaStat.net Cardano blockchain explorer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this proposal because AdaStat.net plays a critical role in strengthening Cardano’s transparency, accessibility, and decentralization. As a well-established, independently operated, and technically efficient blockchain explorer, AdaStat enhances the ability of SPOs, DReps, developers, and users to monitor and interact with the Cardano blockchain.\r\n\r\nKey Reasons:\r\n\t1.\tReliable, High-Performance Infrastructure\r\nAdaStat’s horizontally scalable backend with real-time data access ensures consistent uptime and fast response, especially during network peaks. Its efficient frontend and use of modern frameworks (Vue.js, Tailwind CSS) make it lightweight and responsive across devices.\r\n\t2.\tOpen-Source, Independent, and Community-Oriented\r\nMaintaining a diversity of independently developed explorers is crucial to avoiding centralization risks. AdaStat is not only open-source but has also been trusted by the Cardano community since the Shelley testnet era (2019), showing long-term dedication and reliability.\r\n\t3.\tGovernance and Developer Support\r\nThis proposal includes planned improvements to governance tooling, including tracking of DRep and CC data. Furthermore, it offers developers free access to well-structured APIs, enabling broader tool development and third-party integrations.\r\n\t4.\tAligned with Strategic Treasury Budget\r\nThis proposal is part of Intersect’s approved ₳275M governance budget and adheres to Cardano’s constitutional requirements for contract-based funding, oversight by a third-party assurer, and treasury disbursement through smart contracts audited by MLabs and TxPipe.\r\n\t5.\tTransparent Milestone Delivery & Oversight\r\nThe vendor’s delivery will be governed by a legal contract administered by Intersect and overseen by third-party entities, ensuring accountability, timely delivery, and public transparency via metadata on-chain.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO believes AdaStat.net is an essential tool for the Cardano ecosystem and supports its continuous development as a public good.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは本提案に賛成票を投じます。なぜなら、AdaStat.netはCardanoの透明性・アクセシビリティ・非中央集権性を支える重要なインフラだからです。 この独立運営のブロックチェーンエクスプローラーは、SPO、DRep、開発者、一般ユーザーのすべてにとって、Cardanoと効果的に関わるための信頼性の高いツールです。\r\n\r\n主な理由：\r\n\t1.\t高性能かつ安定したインフラ\r\nAdaStatは、負荷分散された複数のバックエンドによって高可用性を実現しており、ピーク時でも安定したレスポンスを提供します。フロントエンドにはVue.jsとTailwind CSSを採用し、軽量かつ高速なUIを実現しています。\r\n\t2.\tオープンソース・独立開発・コミュニティ重視\r\nブロックチェーンエクスプローラーの多様性は、単一障害点や誤情報のリスクを回避するために極めて重要です。AdaStatは2019年のShelleyテストネット時代から稼働しており、長年にわたり信頼を築いてきたプロジェクトです。\r\n\t3.\tガバナンス機能と開発者支援\r\n提案には、DRepやCC（Constitutional Committee）に関するデータ可視化機能の強化が含まれており、ガバナンスの透明性を高めます。さらに、開発者向けにはJSON形式のREST APIを無償提供しており、外部ツールやアプリへの統合を促進します。\r\n\t4.\t戦略的な財務計画との整合性\r\n本提案はIntersectによる₳2.75億の予算枠の一部として承認されたものであり、Cardanoの憲法で定められた法的契約、第三者アシュアランス、スマートコントラクトによる資金管理の要件にすべて準拠しています。\r\n\t5.\tマイルストーンごとの進捗管理と透明性\r\nプロジェクトの遂行はIntersectによって法的契約に基づき管理され、外部の第三者による監査を通じて進捗が確認され、オンチェーンのメタデータにより公開されます。\r\n\r\n以上の理由により、SIPOはAdaStat.netをCardanoエコシステムの公共財として継続的に支援すべきであると判断し、本提案に「Yes」と投票します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
