      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_zkFold%20ZK%20Rollup.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,161,000 for zkFold ZK Rollup administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nEMURGO as DRep votes YES on the governance action to fund zkFold ZK Rollup.\r\nRationale\r\nWe believe that ZK rollups represent a key piece of Cardano’s long-term scalability roadmap. zkFold’s approach to compressing smart contract transactions into a single L1 interaction aligns well with the goals of reducing congestion, lowering fees, and supporting high-performance dApps.\r\nWith the team already building a prototype independently, this proposal is a timely opportunity to back an early mover in ZK infrastructure for Cardano. While technical execution in this domain carries complexity, the team’s experience in Rust, Haskell, and ZK proofs provides a credible foundation. EMURGO supports this proposal as part of Cardano’s broader commitment to competitive L2 innovation.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
