    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,161,000 for zkFold ZK Rollup administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU8bLD76MDMPiuhs4vfCd2ov5z6WBnfXBr4CJ95j32FWu -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,161,000 for zkFold ZK Rollup administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this Treasury Withdrawal.\r\n\r\nThis proposal aims to bring Zero-Knowledge Rollups (ZK Rollups) to Cardano, significantly enhancing scalability while preserving security and decentralization. It lays the groundwork for accommodating more dApps and users—marking an important step forward in Cardano’s Layer 2 strategy.\r\n\r\nIt also satisfies all constitutional requirements, including a legally binding contract, milestone-based third-party verification, and structured fund management through Intersect. Given zkFold’s technical progress and capability, this is a well-justified and strategic investment toward scalability, better UX, and ecosystem growth.\r\n\r\nこのトレジャリー引き出し提案に対し、YES票を投じます。\r\n\r\n本提案はCardanoにゼロ知識ロールアップ（ZK Rollup）を導入することでスケーラビリティを飛躍的に高め、より多くのdAppやユーザーを受け入れられる土台を整えるものです。セキュリティと分散性を維持しながら処理能力を向上させる設計は、Cardanoのレイヤー2戦略において重要な一歩と評価しています。\r\n\r\nIntersectによる信頼性の高い管理体制、法的契約、第三者検証を伴うマイルストーン管理など、憲法要件も満たしており、zkFoldの技術力・進捗状況からも妥当性が確認できます。スケーラビリティ・UX・dAppエコシステム発展に向けた戦略的投資として支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/09_zkFold_ZK_Rollup_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,161,000 for zkFold ZK Rollup administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports the treasury withdrawal of ₳1,161,000 to fund the zkFold ZK Rollup project administered by Intersect. zkFold presents a strategically significant solution to one of Cardano’s most pressing challenges: scalability.\r\n\r\nKey Reasons for Support:\r\n\t1.\tAddresses Scalability Bottlenecks\r\nzkFold leverages ZK rollup technology to batch hundreds of transactions into one. This dramatically reduces L1 congestion and allows higher throughput, lowering transaction costs and wait times.\r\n\t2.\tEnhances User and Developer Experience\r\nWith cheaper and faster transactions, dApps, DeFi protocols, and NFT platforms on Cardano become more user-friendly, boosting adoption.\r\n\t3.\tMaintains Cardano’s Security Principles\r\nZK rollups process data off-chain, but verify validity on-chain using zero-knowledge proofs. This upholds decentralization and trustless computation — essential Cardano values.\r\n\t4.\tTechnically Capable Vendor\r\nThe zkFold team has a strong background in Haskell, Rust, and cryptography, and has already built a working prototype that fits within Cardano’s execution units.\r\n\t5.\tTransparent Delivery & Governance\r\nThe project will be executed under a legally binding contract via Intersect and CDH, with milestones, audits, and payments clearly defined. Oversight is provided by independent entities like Sundae Labs and Cardano Foundation, and all fund flows are tracked on-chain.\r\n\t6.\tLong-term Ecosystem Benefits\r\nBy enabling efficient Layer 2 scaling on Cardano, zkFold contributes to the long-term competitiveness of the network against L2 solutions on other chains.\r\n\r\nSIPO believes that this proposal is a technically mature, governance-aligned, and strategically necessary investment in Cardano’s infrastructure.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、Intersectが管理するzkFold ZK Rollupプロジェクトに対して₳1,161,000の財務引き出しを支持します。zkFoldは、Cardanoが直面する最重要課題の一つであるスケーラビリティの問題に対する戦略的な解決策を提供します。\r\n\r\n賛成理由の要点：\r\n\t1.\tスケーラビリティ問題の解決\r\nzkFoldはZKロールアップ技術により、数百のトランザクションを一括化して1つのバッチとして処理します。これによりレイヤー1の混雑が軽減され、トランザクション処理能力（TPS）の向上と手数料の削減が実現します。\r\n\t2.\tユーザー・開発者体験の向上\r\n取引が早く安くなることで、dApps、DeFi、NFTなどのCardano上の利用体験が向上し、エコシステムの利用拡大が促進されます。\r\n\t3.\tCardanoのセキュリティ原則を維持\r\nZKロールアップはオフチェーン処理とオンチェーン検証を分離し、ゼロ知識証明によって正当性を保証します。これにより分散性と信頼性が確保され、Cardanoの理念を損なわずにスケーラビリティを実現します。\r\n\t4.\t実績ある技術チーム\r\nzkFoldチームはHaskell、Rust、暗号技術に熟達しており、既にCardanoの実行ユニット制限内で動作するプロトタイプを開発済みです。\r\n\t5.\t透明な実行・ガバナンス体制\r\nプロジェクトはIntersectとCardano Development Holdings（CDH）による法的契約の下で実施され、すべてのマイルストーン、監査、支払いは明確に定義されます。Sundae LabsやCardano Foundationなど、5つの第三者による監視体制もあり、資金の流れはオンチェーンで追跡可能です。\r\n\t6.\t中長期的なCardanoエコシステムへの貢献\r\nzkFoldはCardanoにおけるレイヤー2スケーリングの土台を築き、他チェーンとの競争力を高める基盤となります。\r\n\r\nSIPOは、この提案が技術的にも成熟しており、ガバナンス的にも適切で、Cardanoの持続的成長に資する重要なインフラ投資であると判断し、「Yes」と投票します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
