      "voter": "GOMA-DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bbandu/Amaru-Comment/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# GOMA-DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2cm9w2egseygejydtgdddnsw9zdpc6ayyf8xh5ascfq4tqkpj06v`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIntroducing a new node implementation for Cardano, the Amaru project appears to provide a balanced response to the blockchain trilemma. It seeks to improve security (through the use of Rust and rigorous testing), promote decentralization (by reducing reliance on a single implementation), and facilitate scalability (through optimized hardware resource management). Ultimately, this project aims to strengthen the Cardano blockchain while meeting the growing needs of the community and preparing the network to support wider adoption and continued growth.\r\n\r\nThis project can be seen as a solution that helps reconcile the tensions between these three principles, allowing Cardano to grow without compromising its core values.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSzVSi8boqwwRB8qNsXk96vyC5WM9MrfuKx2yrRQWDm2W -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for this proposal because:\r\n\r\n1) It aligns with the 2025 roadmap approved by DReps, where node diversity is a strategic priority to improve decentralization and resilience.\r\n\r\n2) Amaru reduces reliance on the Haskell node maintained by IOG, strengthening network security and fault tolerance—similar to how Ethereum benefits from multiple independent clients.\r\n\r\n3) The development team is highly reputable, with members from dcSpark, TxPipe, Cardano Foundation, and others. They are also actively coordinating with IOG’s Haskell team to ensure compatibility.\r\n\r\n4) The requested budget of 1.5M ADA (for 6 months) is reasonable, with clear smart contract-based fund management and oversight by PRAGMA.\r\n\r\n5) As an open-source public good, Amaru strengthens Cardano’s infrastructure and invites broader participation from Rust developers.\r\n\r\n* Amaru is not just an alternative node—it’s a strategic investment in a more decentralized, robust, and future-ready Cardano.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese Translation\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nTôi ủng hộ đề xuất này vì:\r\n\r\n1) Phù hợp với roadmap 2025 đã được DRep phê duyệt – trong đó “đa dạng hóa node” là ưu tiên chiến lược để tăng phân quyền và khả năng phục hồi mạng lưới.\r\n\r\n2) Amaru giúp giảm phụ thuộc vào node Haskell của IOG, tăng cường bảo mật và khả năng kháng lỗi – tương tự cách Ethereum đã làm với nhiều client độc lập.\r\n\r\n3) Đội ngũ kỹ thuật uy tín, đến từ các tổ chức như dcSpark, TxPipe, CF… và đã phối hợp với nhóm Haskell để đảm bảo tương thích, tránh xung đột.\r\n\r\n4) Ngân sách minh bạch, hợp lý (1.5M ADA cho 6 tháng), có cơ chế hợp đồng thông minh và quy trình giám sát rõ ràng thông qua PRAGMA.\r\n\r\n5) Amaru là mã nguồn mở, phục vụ cộng đồng, giúp củng cố hạ tầng dài hạn và thu hút nhà phát triển Rust vào hệ sinh thái Cardano.\r\n\r\n* Amaru không chỉ là một node thay thế – mà là nền tảng kỹ thuật chiến lược để xây dựng một Cardano phân quyền, bền vững và chống chịu tốt hơn trong tương lai.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nJapanese Translation\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nこの提案にYES票を投じる理由は以下の通りです：\r\n\r\n1) この提案はDRepが承認した2025年のロードマップと一致しており、ノードの多様性は分散性と耐障害性を高めるための戦略的優先事項です。\r\n\r\n2) AmaruはIOGのHaskellノードへの依存を減らし、ネットワークのセキュリティと可用性を強化します。これはEthereumが複数の独立したクライアントを持つことによって得ている利点と同様です。\r\n\r\n3) 開発チームは信頼性が高く、dcSpark、TxPipe、Cardano Foundationなどの主要メンバーで構成されています。また、IOGのHaskellチームと連携して互換性を確保しています。\r\n\r\n4) 要請された予算は1.5M ADA（6か月分）で妥当です。スマートコントラクトによる資金管理とPRAGMAによる監督体制も明確です。\r\n\r\n5) Amaruはオープンソースのパブリックグッドとして、Cardanoのインフラ強化とRust開発者の参加促進に貢献します。\r\n\r\n※Amaruは単なる代替ノードではなく、より分散化され、堅牢で未来に備えたCardanoを実現するための戦略的投資です。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmPPsFZh91wt6MUEZLVU5xEgSZTwUswnezzAPvQXQg8bXp -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting Yes on the budget for Amaru since the development of an additional node is one of the most crucial projects for Cardano to become truly decentralised and not be dependent on a single development team anymore. The Amaru team is highly qualified to realise this and the budget not being administrated by Intersect is a massive advantage. Moreover, a detailed budget proposal for one and only one project is exactly how I want treasury to be handled.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmcn9k25jyiXpyVfzdwdmnFGvQD6EyFVhcZNJ7txmxXSxW -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m supporting the Amaru Node project, which promotes alternative approaches to running Cardano nodes. Offering multiple ways to interact with the Cardano blockchain fosters greater diversity among development teams and strengthens technological decentralization. While improved transparency in financial management is still needed, this project represents a significant advancement for our blockchain ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUSJaxut41HcL34sbfuEUp6kpMvY3jJPww494VoauHhwe -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe provided rationale for a second node implementation is technically strong and strategically aligned with decentralization principles. Reducing reliance on the Haskell node is sound from both a security and governance standpoint. Of course this argument would not apply ad infinitum, as adding too many nodes may lead to wasted efforts. There’s a thin line between strategic redundancy and fragmentation. However, so far Cardano has put all eggs in the Haskell basket.  The Rust node will add resilience through implementation diversity and represent a new pathway to approach Cardano for dev teams.\r\nIs seems to be fairly priced by Web3 standards for a 6-month effort with a senior team.\r\nThe proposal takes governance seriously, with credible disbursement and reporting mechanisms. \r\nI further appreciate the direct submission and the avoidance of going through a much more convoluted process with many other proposals that need to be \"packaged together\" in one info action. This direct submission allows DReps to vote directly on this proposal and its own merits. \r\nLast but not least, the implementing team is quite capable and well-known for their quality contributions to the ecosystem through a myriad of different projects.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Amaru_Node_2025.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted yes on Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget: Amaru Node Development 2025.\r\nNode diversity is critical for decentralization and network resilience. Having multiple node implementations increases the network’s robustness, performance, and developer access. The Amaru team's funding request is reasonable, perfectly presented and clearly outlined. Furthermore this initiative strengthens and represents a healthy evolution of the Cardano network.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/08JUN2025-9kxxz/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on the proposed “Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget: Amaru Node Development 2025” Info Action (Governance Action ID: Gov_action1h4ygjv0hjfj3lmafcm76rpdzcm8vsvj9k5wejn3npyxwxm3fesnqqw9kxxz). I’m eager to see Amaru bring node diversity to Cardano in a high assurance manner, and the maintainer committee managing Amaru under PRAGMA comprises proven contributors to this ecosystem.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/38nr3he2 -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting YES because a second, Rust-based block-producing node adds vital resilience and removes the single-implementation risk currently hanging over Cardano. The maintainer committee—Blink Labs, dcSpark, Sundae Labs, TxPipe, Cardano Foundation, and Pi Lanningham—has a proven record of shipping high-quality infrastructure, so I trust their ability to deliver. The ₳1.5 M ask is bounded to six months, guarded by a smart-contract escrow and quarterly public reports; if milestones slip, unused funds flow back to the treasury. Rust's efficiency and built-in observability will lower hardware costs for small SPOs and give us better telemetry, while encouraging fresh contributors from the wider Rust ecosystem. Finally, backing PRAGMA alongside Intersect strengthens collaboration rather than rivalry—diverse teams, shared vision, stronger network. Let's fund this pilot, measure its progress, and reassess future budgets based on results.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/08/Amaru.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Rationale for Voting on “Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget: Amaru Node Development 2025” Info Action\r\n\r\nI am voting **YES** on the Amaru Node Development 2025 proposal.\r\n\r\nThe Amaru node will significantly increase Cardano’s resilience and improve network security. As Cardano continues to onboard thousands of new users, transactions, and greater value, it is essential to ensure the system has **no single point of failure**. Amaru directly addresses this by introducing node diversity, thereby strengthening the network against potential disruptions.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, Amaru is expected to lower hardware requirements for stake pool operators, which will **further promote decentralisation** of the network. The choice to develop Amaru in Rust - a widely adopted programming language - will also broaden our developer base and attract new contributors to the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nIn my view, the requested funding is fully justified by the value Amaru brings in terms of security, decentralisation, and network robustness. For these reasons, I am supporting this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/Amaru%20Node.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nKrypto Labs votes YES on the Amaru Node Development 2025 proposal. We believe node diversity is crucial for Cardano's long-term resilience and decentralization. Amaru's modular Rust implementation offers a promising alternative, enhancing interoperability and robustness. This project aligns with our commitment to fostering a healthy, innovative ecosystem. By supporting Amaru, we invest in a more secure and adaptable Cardano, mitigating single points of failure and encouraging broader participation. The project's transparent approach and focus on industry-standard observability further solidify our confidence in its potential to strengthen the network.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kyle Solomon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adosiawolf/drep-rationale/refs/heads/main/0002 -->\r\n# Kyle Solomon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzshxuma6cwrnlv2ucyclfqw3k4nu4nuudmh2z87j9hncsk9dhy4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted YES on the current proposal to fund Amaru.\r\n\r\nI firmly believe our absolute top priority must be establishing ecosystem sustainability. While introducing new alternative block-producing nodes certainly entails potential to introduce delays in releasing mission-critical scalability components due to the necessity of maintaining compatibility across nodes, I believe the Amaru initiative is critical to solidifying the censorship-resistance of the Cardano mission and introduces a potential path for more cost-effective node development in the long-term. I also believe learnings from building out an alternative node inherently lend to improve the overall integrity of the existing Haskell node.\r\n\r\nThe Amaru team is solid, reputable and well-deserving of the immense responsibility.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Latam Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LatamCardanoDRep/DREP/refs/heads/main/Vote%20Amaru%206-5-25.jsonld -->\r\n# Latam Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytgsdkfznvjnwdxrzvf8x6tn4ctfukqqphsammzkfwatgsqgnpf2w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote YES because this proposal significantly enhances Cardano's resilience by eliminating the risk inherent to having a single point of failure of only having one node for a modest cost.\r\nAmaru provides diversity, better performance, and improved tooling.\r\nReputation of the proposing team is high - Blink Labs, dcSpark, Sundae Labs, Cardano Foundation, and TxPipe.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LEADStakePool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lead-pool/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context1.jsonld -->\r\n# LEADStakePool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytnvazqpsj98pu7w6vtmeddcy9pnn6y6nl0psr5ajzge52s82zz8t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNode diversity has been a long time coming. An easy yes from me.",
