    {
      "voter": "Long Hồ",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaZ6ijyfJ6N22MNAUC4tgFP8RKxJsAmFtrkR5QvAByPaV -->\r\n# Long Hồ\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttfrpngasw7yrdryydsg66gzv8znkj0stjngm5a8hs353stdeml6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for this proposal because Amaru is a strategically important, ongoing project that directly contributes to the decentralization, performance, and sustainability of the Cardano ecosystem. The team has already invested resources and delivered tangible progress, and their transparent governance model, modular design, and commitment to open development make this a high-impact initiative worthy of further funding.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lourde",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQ3Q3u6FmRmnk194x5r7XK2XdCDesK5uBGh7p9ohaWunm -->\r\n# Lourde\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygtvnwgsucstvesms2hv9vc8hw3tye5zhzldmszrxqd2rxsje5c6m`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNode diversity is becoming a valuable approach to technological evolution allowing the SPO's current and future a new option to design of block production will lead to innovations that may help strengthen the entire community and bring light to paths to harden or solidify the security already inherent in the design. I find value in the Amaru proposal for the good of the blockchain. Being built by proven project heads and long time loyal community members this budget will give access to possible new technology. I vote yes for this request.\r\n\r\n-LOURDE-\r\nOuroborus\r\nImperator\r\nAeternalis",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0009 -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on the proposal Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget: Amaru Node Development 2025.\r\n\r\nThis proposal directly advances Cardano’s strategic objectives of enhancing decentralization, improving security, and ensuring the long-term sustainability of the network. By supporting the development of Amaru as an independent, interoperable node implementation, it addresses the systemic risk of relying on a single codebase and strengthens the network’s resilience, fully aligned with the constitutional principles of decentralization and robustness.\r\n\r\nThe initiative is led by a consortium of reputable ecosystem actors — Blink Labs, Cardano Foundation, dcSpark, Sundae Labs, and TxPipe — operating under PRAGMA’s not-for-profit governance structure. The maintainer committee is composed of recognized domain experts, each assigned clear scopes of responsibility. This structure ensures a high degree of technical competence and operational accountability, critical for a project of this complexity.\r\n\r\nMoreover, the broader impact of this initiative is significant. Increasing node diversity, improving observability with industry standards, and fostering a more inclusive development environment are critical to enhancing the operational robustness and decentralization of the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I support this proposal and cast my vote in favor.\r\n\r\nVOTE0009",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Maureen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNagi1LccvcFzvjhAomdH6XJWH6X2TtxUEjwhM6fXCzvw -->\r\n# Maureen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y22hlaj8wuyygpnjy5cf96tg9tgvjrz39kxvqgv898uj9scfc55t7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe benefits of having a second, independent, resource-efficient node implementation far outweigh the risks. The team has the right expertise, the budget is reasonable, and the project aligns perfectly with Cardano's core value of decentralization.\r\nPlus, bringing Rust developers into the Cardano ecosystem could significantly expand our developer community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmNTaK7GoEcuE6kmdn4ALtCXTBEkZs9XZAtopGYsHrRmr3 -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter a thorough review of the budget proposal for the Amaru Node Development project, I will vote **YES** on this governance action (gov_action1h4ygjv0hjfj3lmafcm76rpdzcm8vsvj9k5wejn3npyxwxm3fesnqqw9kxxz).\r\n\r\nThe Amaru project is of significant strategic importance to the Cardano ecosystem. Developing a second, Rust-based, fully interoperable block-producing node alongside the existing Haskell implementation is crucial for enhancing network resilience, furthering decentralization, and improving the overall robustness of Cardano. This initiative also promises to lower barriers for new developers to contribute to Cardano's core infrastructure by leveraging the Rust programming language. This aligns directly with the core development principles essential for the long-term health and sustainability of the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThe project is spearheaded by a highly capable and specialized maintainer committee, composed of individuals with proven track records within the Cardano community. The involvement of PRAGMA, a consortium of established ecosystem entities, further instills confidence in the project's governance and execution.\r\n\r\nFrom a fiscal perspective, the requested 1.5 million ada for the second half of 2025 represents excellent value for money, especially considering the scope and potential impact of delivering a second mainnet-capable block-producing node. The clearly defined scope and detailed budget breakdown facilitate a transparent assessment.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the proposed mechanisms for fund administration, utilizing an open-source smart contract with built-in failsafes and overseen by the maintainer committee, coupled with commitments to regular reporting and public demos, provide a strong framework for accountability and transparency. The proposal also appropriately addresses auditing provisions.\r\n\r\nGiven the strategic importance of node diversity, the strength of the team, the clear value proposition, and the robust governance measures outlined, I believe this budget proposal warrants strong support from the DReps. Funding Amaru is a direct investment in the future resilience, decentralization, and innovation of the Cardano blockchain.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://nimuepool.io/metadata/context-20250524.jsonld -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMy votes for the currently active budget governance actions are as follows:\r\n- ✅ YES on the 275M Intersect Budget\r\n- ✅ YES on the Amaru Node Development Budget\r\n- ❌ NO on the 7.5M Community Builders Budget\r\n\r\nThe Intersect budget includes a broad set of proposals that are generally positive for the Cardano ecosystem. While I may have reservations about some individual proposals, approving the budget doesn't automatically release funds. I can re-evaluate specific items later when the associated treasury withdrawal actions are submitted on chain. I strongly recommend avoiding overly grouped treasury withdrawals, bundling too many proposals together can result in good initiatives being blocked due to a few contentious ones.\r\n\r\nAs for the Amaru Node Development Budget, if it had been included in the recent Ekklesia vote, it likely would have passed, and I would have supported it then as well. That's why I will support it now too. For better clarity, I recommend including the requested budget amount in the governance action title next time.\r\n\r\nI would've preferred to vote on the Community Builders Budget after seeing the outcome of the Intersect budget. If that last one were to fail, I might have considered supporting the community one, but since it was submitted beforehand, that option is off the table now. More importantly, this budget doesn't include the proposals from founding entities and there are no separate gov actions for those. It doesn't make sense to fund only this subset of proposals in isolation imho. So for now I can only assume the Intersect one will pass, which renders this budget unnecessary. Additionally, this budget appoints Intersect as the administrator, yet includes the Starstream proposal, which will not use Intersect as an administrator. For these reasons, I cannot support the Community Builders Budget at this time.\r\n\r\nI'm aware that some of my reasons for voting NO on the community budget could also apply, to some extent, to the Amaru budget. However, the Amaru budget doesn't overlap with another Budget.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "No stress",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmezb3gBk35jh84L9yR5eoy7mxFwry8qYcQZa242bFcJtH -->\r\n# No stress\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t3t35yx7j8nnh3wkqn2zzhgwqksksn85zv62pjrwzjawczwgyv7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI think this is a well detailed proposal and the cost is reasonable for the value.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action1h4yg/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted YES because the Amaru project makes Cardano stronger and more decentralised. Right now, we rely on just one main node (written in Haskell) to run the network. If something goes wrong with that, the whole system could be at risk. Amaru gives us a second, fully working option, built in Rust, a language known for safety, speed, and flexibility.\r\n\r\nHaving more than one node makes the network more secure and reliable. It also opens the door for new developers and use cases that are hard to do with the current setup. The team behind Amaru includes trusted names in the Cardano ecosystem, and they’ve planned carefully with clear goals, budget, and reporting.\r\n\r\nThe funding request is fair, ₳1.5 million for six months of work, and includes smart contract controls to make sure the money is used properly. This kind of proposal is exactly what Cardano’s treasury should support if we want a stronger, more resilient ecosystem in the long term.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peyton",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigpey/CardanoGovernance/refs/heads/main/AmaruBudget -->\r\n# Peyton\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y20fpc0f6qjl4edtl9cxzrvqzd8jkzr6ja7p0p2n7cxragqkurae3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting 'yes' on this budget. The developers that will be funded from the treasury withdrawal after the possible approval of this budget are well known, highly capible, and accountable. The proposal iteslf is something that the Cardano community has desired for quite sometime. It offers node diversity, by creating a much needed alternative to the Haskell node. I also believe this is how a budget should be approved, it should be smaller items, and not a large budget that included a huge amount of unrelated proposals. When you vote 'yes' on this budget, and the treasury withdraw you are not required to fund other proposals that you don't find as valuable. I also hope to see this node require less resources so that it's easier for people to run cardano-node. The resource consumption on the node has been gradually increasing year after year, and it's not slowing down anytime soon.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA014-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"Sim\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action1h4ygjv0hjfj3lmafcm76rpdzcm8vsvj9k5wejn3npyxwxm3fesnqqw9kxxz), pois um software de nó alternativo ao oficial contribui para a saúde e resiliência da blockchain Cardano. Além disso, foram apresentadas métricas de controle de qualidade e execução do projeto, de modo a garantir o acompanhamento pela comunidade.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"Yes\" on this governance action (gov_action1h4ygjv0hjfj3lmafcm76rpdzcm8vsvj9k5wejn3npyxwxm3fesnqqw9kxxz) because an alternative node software to the official one contributes to the health and resilience of the Cardano blockchain. Additionally, quality control and project execution metrics were presented to ensure proper community oversight.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZbnDvCmBvMYYGSgNcKQBWF2MWUb16VyTbmWe3xuFYW7E -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting **Yes **on the Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget proposal for Amaru Node Development 2025. I believe this initiative represents a strategically important step toward strengthening Cardano’s decentralization and network resilience. Introducing a second block-producing node written in Rust addresses a critical concern around single-node dependency and improves system redundancy, interoperability and overall security. The project’s emphasis on modular architecture and industry-standard observability will also support a better operational experience for SPOs and infrastructure contributors.\r\n\r\nI have confidence in the team behind this proposal. The members of PRAGMA, including TxPipe, Sundae Labs, Blink Labs, and others, have demonstrated a consistent commitment to Cardano’s growth and have delivered meaningfully on past initiatives. Their leadership in developing Amaru is reassuring and lends credibility to the projected outcomes.\r\n\r\nThe budget request of ₳1.5M, which covers the second half of 2025, appears reasonable and well justified. At approximately ₳750K USD equivalent for 6 FTEs, the per-FTE cost falls well within industry norms. I also appreciate the transparency in breaking out previously Catalyst-funded components, ensuring there is no overlap in funding.\r\n\r\nThat said, my support is not without caveats. First, the smart contract framework proposed for fund administration is still incomplete. While I recognize the intention to finalize and audit it before the first disbursement, its current state introduces execution risk. Second, I believe the project would benefit from clearer, quantifiable KPIs or milestones that allow the community to objectively assess progress. Finally, as one of the first budget-oriented Info Actions under Voltaire, this proposal sets an important and excellent precedent. **Future actions should ensure even greater transparency, early community input, and enhanced reporting frameworks**.\r\n\r\nDespite these reservations, I find the proposal’s alignment with Cardano’s constitutional values and its potential long-term impact compelling. I am casting a Yes vote and will monitor future developments closely, particularly the implementation of the smart contract and progress reporting. I look forward to seeing this project contribute meaningfully to the robustness and decentralization of the Cardano network.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rod G",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rodg-drmz/DRep-Votes/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(1).jsonld -->\r\n# Rod G\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwscks2yt0na4fqpcdyqn0fare5v48y0mjgn2g478lnx8gue393e`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a major step towards \"node diversity through the development of a modular, high-performance, and interoperable block-producing node for Cardano\"\r\n\r\nIt makes Cardano more robust.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RudianosDrep/RudianosDrep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%207.jsonld -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have decided to vote in favor of this proposal. Node diversity is an important part of securing the network and this team is very well suited to complete the work described in the proposal. I also appreciate that Amaru will be acting as an administrator for this budget. Having groups step up to be administrators like this is also valuable for the ecosystem. For these reasons I believe the costs here are justified.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nagamarupanda/Drep-voting/refs/heads/main/Amaru%20Node%20Development%202025.jsonld -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nこの提案は、Cardanoの新たなRust実装ノード「Amaru」の開発を支援するものです。Amaruは、既存のHaskellノードとは異なる技術基盤からCardanoネットワークの堅牢性、可用性、分散性を高めることを目的としています。Cardanoの未来を見据えるなら、ノード実装の多様化は不可欠です。単一実装依存はリスクを高め、将来的な進化・セキュリティ・安定性を阻害しかねません。今回のAmaru開発チームは、Blink Labs、Cardano Foundation、dcSpark、Sundae Labs、TxPipeなど、信頼性と実績を兼ね備えた主要メンバーによって構成されています。また、オンチェーンのスマートコントラクトによる資金管理と、定期的な進捗報告を予定しており、透明性・説明責任も十分に配慮されています。この取り組みは、Cardanoの長期的発展と自立性を支える極めて重要なインフラ投資であり、短期的なリターンでは測れない本質的価値を持つものです。よって本提案には賛成し、未来のCardanoネットワーク強化を支持します。\r\n\r\nThis proposal supports the development of a new Rust implementation node for Cardano, \"Amaru.\" Amaru aims to increase the robustness, availability, and decentralization of the Cardano network from a different technical foundation than the existing Haskell node. Looking to the future of Cardano, diversification of node implementations is essential. Dependence on a single implementation increases risk and may hinder future evolution, security, and stability. The Amaru development team is composed of key members with a reliable and proven track record, including Blink Labs, Cardano Foundation, dcSpark, Sundae Labs, and TxPipe. In addition, funds will be managed by on-chain smart contracts, and regular progress reports will be made, with due consideration given to transparency and accountability. This initiative is an extremely important infrastructure investment that supports Cardano's long-term development and independence, and has intrinsic value that cannot be measured by short-term returns. Therefore, I support this proposal and support the strengthening of the future Cardano network.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb11E4Bk8EzmaZc5WkNrCkPCvDgLNfceq4XFeejN24K7a -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep focused on decentralization, developer education, and ecosystem growth, I support Amaru for its Rust-based, modular approach that enhances resilience, accessibility, and interoperability. Backed by trusted entities, it aligns with my goals of onboarding new talent and improving infrastructure diversity. Amaru strengthens Cardano’s decentralization while creating more opportunities for global and local community engagement.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQ5FVgx5BUBQEWsjX6KxpFa1by9brot4z8YoLS7f6WAZa -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe support this proposal as it directly addresses a long-standing risk in the ecosystem — reliance on a single node implementation — by funding the development of a modular, high-performance alternative written in Rust.\r\n\r\nWe believe a second, independently maintained node:\r\n\r\n- Strengthens the resilience and fault tolerance of the network\r\n- Expands developer accessibility through modern tooling and better observability\r\n- Reduces hardware costs for SPOs, improving participation at the edge\r\n- Enables platform interoperability with WebAssembly\r\n- Empower Cardano core infrastructure to access to wider talent pool with alternative implementation of a more modern programming language\r\n\r\nWe also appreciate the proposal’s financial transparency:\r\n\r\n- Clearly scoped per team member and responsibility\r\n- Budget guarded by a smart contract with refund logic\r\n- Quarterly public reporting and demo cadence already in practice\r\n\r\nSIDAN Lab is also interested in the possibility of expanding works into alternative Hydra node, where our team can participate in maintenance and collaboration in the future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/info/20250517_03/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs the DRep representing SIPO, SIPO vote YES on the “Amaru Node Development 2025” proposal.\r\n\r\nSIPO strongly support this initiative as a foundational investment in the long-term decentralization, resilience, and public infrastructure of the Cardano blockchain.\r\n\r\nOne of Cardano’s strengths—its robust Haskell-based node—also presents a critical centralization risk: dependency on a single codebase and implementation. Amaru directly addresses this concern by delivering a high-assurance, Rust-based, modular, and lightweight alternative node. The project also aims to be interoperable with emerging platforms such as WebAssembly and RISC-V, further increasing accessibility and diversity in node deployment.\r\n\r\nSIPO emphasize the following reasons for our support:\r\n\r\n1. Decentralization: This is the first major initiative to reduce single-client dependency within Cardano, providing infrastructure redundancy and removing central points of failure at the node level. A second, independently developed node aligns with the core principle of Byzantine-resilient decentralization.\r\n\r\n2. Public Good & Open Source: Amaru is maintained by PRAGMA, a non-profit open-source association comprised of reputable Cardano ecosystem contributors including Blink Labs, dcSpark, Cardano Foundation, TxPipe, and Sundae Labs. The project is fully transparent, publicly documented, and built for the entire community.\r\n\r\n3. Technical Innovation: The implementation in Rust ensures modern tooling, increased contributor accessibility, and long-term maintainability. The WebAssembly compatibility paves the way for broader deployment environments and novel use cases.\r\n\r\n4. Fiscal Responsibility: The proposal includes a clear and itemized budget, defined scopes per module owner, 25% contingency allocation, and an on-chain smart contract to control fund disbursement. Scope owners can return unused contingency funds to the Treasury. The reporting cadence (quarterly) and regular public demos show operational maturity and transparency.\r\n\r\n5. Constitutional Compliance: The proposal is aligned with the Cardano Constitution and falls well within the active Net Change Limit (NCL). The maintainers have thoughtfully included a constitutionality checklist to affirm legal and governance compliance.\r\n\r\nFrom a governance perspective, this proposal is exemplary in its clarity, structure, execution plan, and systemic benefit to the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nSIPO consider Amaru not just another software project but an essential national infrastructure for a resilient, multi-client Cardano. It sets a precedent for sustainable public goods development in a decentralized governance system.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, we enthusiastically vote YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYjxzrAC9n3xN8okPpiPmC88tbT2tfsrMmyxtrdKT15t4 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious Drep votes in favor of this proposal to diversify node implementations in Cardano. This initiative will enhance network stability and sustainability through multiple implementation options.\r\n\r\nWhile Cardano has relied solely on Haskell implementation so far, introducing a Rust-based node - despite being unprecedented - helps mitigate the risks associated with single-implementation dependency.\r\n\r\nThe lower operating costs for SPOs will reduce barriers to entry, promoting greater network decentralization.\r\n\r\nSubject to continued proper maintenance of development and quality control standards, we endorse this proposal as a positive step toward network decentralization and evolution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SudoScientist",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arpradio/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote%20Context_.amaru.jsonld -->\r\n# SudoScientist\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wtls7xh3a8gyepk540dgtzjzalk086gp4www6y0k0xjmqyk6gma`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt is clear the community feels the inclusion of this node is overall beneficial to the Cardano Community.  However, administration of the budget is an aspect that needs to be clearly defined prior to a proposal.  If the mechanism for administering this budget is not clearly defined, how can we properly determine it is sufficient?  This sets a precedent for future proposals to have text that may present promises yet have no means of qualification.  In my opinion, the administration of the budget remains one of the best suppliers of confidence within a community, and though I support the project in principle, administration should never be compromised.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(1).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal aligns with the Constitution, delivers community value, and is both feasible and urgently needed.\r\n\r\nCardano’s strength lies in its ability to decentralize both governance and infrastructure. Supporting Amaru is an investment in that future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRjFDaWyw8puZUisj85cWhVse4R9ov6YZocZFs5rQb3za -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDetailed proposal, reasonable cost for a team with strong track record",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Dutch Drep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXnQaF5CEF4xfhXczuX66LbdFoBsqjhqtCjrKGpUv2p3x -->\r\n# The Dutch Drep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yvve4554njxyun2s5p9q70v88d5jl7r0h34pjhw5f5tmw3sjtrutp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Dutch DRep, vote Yes on the Amaru proposal.\r\n\r\nThe team behind Amaru consists of trusted and experienced contributors with a strong track record of delivering critical infrastructure within the Cardano ecosystem. Their proposal is clear, transparent, and constitutionally sound, demonstrating a high standard of governance and accountability.\r\n\r\nWe believe the development of a Rust-based node brings meaningful benefits to Cardano. It strengthens decentralization, enhances interoperability, and broadens the developer base. Crucially, it also provides an independent implementation that can act as a constant cross-check of the existing Haskell node—serving as a form of ongoing audit that improves the security and correctness of both.\r\n\r\nIn our view, Amaru is a strategically valuable project that aligns well with Cardano’s long-term goals.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfUDeCkWzaqJsrf81p3t3mbm4R3951yi32QzqkqPwYkez -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Amaru proposal presents a carefully constructed initiative aimed at enhancing Cardano’s node diversity, resilience, and interoperability. While I recognize the merit in fostering innovation and expanding the ecosystem, I must emphasize that any strategic investment must be weighed against our overarching mandate to safeguard Cardano’s long-term stability, treasury health, and scientific rigor.\r\n\r\nFirst, the rationale for developing an alternative node implementation is compelling in principle: improved resource efficiency, industry-grade observability, and broader platform compatibility are undeniably valuable goals. Yet, the current Haskell node’s proven robustness and security over five years set an exceptionally high bar. Introducing a parallel node implementation inherently increases complexity and operational risk, especially when the new codebase is still nascent and unproven at scale.\r\n\r\nMoreover, while Rust offers attractive features such as fine-grained memory control and a vibrant ecosystem, it is crucial to rigorously validate that the Amaru node can match or exceed the Haskell node’s security guarantees without introducing new attack surfaces or subtle bugs. The proposal’s emphasis on conformance testing and specification alignment is reassuring, but this process is iterative and resource-intensive. We must be prepared for extended timelines and unforeseen challenges, which could strain resources and divert attention from other critical protocol improvements.\r\n\r\nDecentralization is rightly highlighted as a core value, and multiple node implementations can indeed reduce centralization risk. However, decentralization must not come at the cost of fragmenting developer focus or undermining the unified security model that the existing node provides. Our governance approach should ensure that the addition of Amaru is not merely a diversification for its own sake but a strategic enhancement that complements and strengthens the network.\r\n\r\nThe financial ask—₳1.5 million for six months of development—reflects a serious commitment but also demands scrutiny. Transparency and accountability mechanisms, including the on-chain smart contract and quarterly reporting, are positive steps. Yet, the proposal’s optimistic assumptions about effort and costs must be tempered by the reality of blockchain development’s inherent complexity. We must ensure that contingency budgets are not a buffer for systemic underestimation but a safeguard against genuine risks.\r\n\r\nStrategically, the Cardano community must maintain a business-minded discipline. We are custodians of a fixed supply, disinflationary protocol with a treasury that must be preserved to fund innovation sustainably. Supporting Amaru should be framed as a calculated investment with clear milestones, measurable outcomes, and a governance structure that can pivot decisively if progress stalls or risks materialize.\r\n\r\nI support the initiative to expand Cardano’s ecosystem and attract new contributors, but I insist that we proceed with rigorous oversight, continuous evaluation, and an unwavering commitment to the protocol’s foundational principles. Amaru’s success hinges not only on technical execution but on our collective ability to integrate innovation without compromising the stability and security that define Cardano’s unique value proposition.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmahbNoorDqZmpmmb4EmBd2GLmCjYesTtE7VZf8gkdscS4 -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Wada DRep, we represent a decentralized and globally connected network of Cardano community builders, innovators, and voters; many based across Africa and the diaspora. Our role in constitutional governance is to act in the best interests of the ecosystem while reflecting the priorities of our community and honoring our internal deliberative frameworks.\r\n\r\nAfter careful review and deliberation, we have voted YES on the Amaru Node Development proposal, which requests ₳1.5 million in Treasury funding to support the project’s second phase in 2025. The Amaru project represents more than a technical milestone; it is a foundational step toward realizing the full vision of a resilient, multi-client, and decentralized Cardano. It embodies constitutional alignment, budgetary discipline, and strategic foresight, and its success or failure will significantly shape the ecosystem’s credibility and progress.\r\n\r\nCardano currently operates with a single block-producing node, i.e.,the Haskell node maintained by IOG. While it has served the network well, relying on one implementation creates systemic risk:\r\n* \r\n\r\nA single point of failure, with no fallback in case of critical bugs.\r\n* \r\n\r\nLimited validation of protocol conformance and specs.\r\n* \r\n\r\nBottlenecks in innovation, observability, and integration across environments.\r\n\r\nAmaru addresses these by introducing a fully interoperable, modular node in Rust, which brings improved performance, memory efficiency, and cross-platform capabilities (e.g., WebAssembly, RISC-V). A second node implementation increases network resilience, fosters protocol transparency, and accelerates feature experimentation without compromising safety.\r\n\r\nThe Amaru proposal is a textbook example of what Voltaire-era BIA should look like:\r\n* \r\n\r\nIt complies fully with Articles IV.1 through IV.4 of the Cardano Constitution.\r\n* \r\n\r\nIt proposes a multi-signature smart contract system to manage disbursements.\r\n* \r\n\r\nEach scope of work has a clearly defined owner and budget.\r\n* \r\n\r\nSafeguards include milestone-gated releases, pause-payment mechanisms, refund capabilities, and credential rotation.\r\n\r\nAmaru is governed by PRAGMA, a nonprofit association formed by core ecosystem teams: Blink Labs, dcSpark, Sundae Labs, TxPipe, and the Cardano Foundation. This collaboration brings together some of the most experienced contributors to Cardano’s open-source tooling and node infrastructure. Moreover, the team has committed to:\r\n* \r\n\r\nQuarterly progress reports, made public via GitHub.\r\n* \r\n\r\nWorking demos every 4–6 weeks, showcasing real deliverables.\r\n* \r\n\r\nOngoing community visibility and documentation of all development efforts.\r\n\r\nThese commitments far exceed the transparency baseline expected of Treasury-funded initiatives.\r\n\r\nThe proposal seeks ₳1.5 million to fund 6 full-time contributors over six months. This includes a 25% contingency for complexity and overhead, based on a $0.50/ADA conversion rate. The networking scope, already funded via Catalyst, is excluded from this ask.\r\n\r\nIn relative terms, this is a small investment for a high-impact project, especially considering that community-signaled proposals totaling over ₳275 million is also up for vote.\r\n\r\nRejecting the Amaru Node proposal would have negative ripple effects:\r\n* \r\n\r\nIt would delay node diversity, exposing Cardano to prolonged infrastructure fragility.\r\n* \r\n\r\nIt would discourage developers from engaging in critical protocol-level work.\r\n* \r\n\r\nIt would undermine the credibility of the on-chain governance and treasury processes we are working to legitimize.\r\n* \r\n\r\nIt could stifle future-forward innovation, such as light clients, WASM support, and modular architecture.\r\n\r\nThe message it would send is that even the most constitutionally aligned, community-driven, technically sound proposals are not safe from political or procedural paralysis.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/11_amaru_budget_2025.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Budget Amaru Node Development 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBased on the relatively low cost of this budget, the quality of the team, and the value building a new node would bring to the ecosystem, I have decided to vote YES on the Amaru Node Development budget for 2025.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/willpiam/drep/blob/master/vote_context/markdown/11_amaru_budget_2025.md",
      "vote": "YES"
