    {
      "voter": "MREDGARCROSS",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreictnroabjpyaih4cpiadc6l2hit2emjeygs2hgbp2exerntcsjisa -->\r\n# MREDGARCROSS\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y269ehxj30k4vfzfc2z84v0xykd3amuy2xn0kv9zf8rhcec2fg2jr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n📢 **Vote: Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581–653**\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I **vote — NO**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### ⚖️ **My Reasoning**\r\n\r\nThe proposed budget of **₳1,000,000 ADA** (₳200,000 per CC member) is disproportionate to the actual scope of their work.\r\nThe Constitutional Committee performs a supervisory and legal function — verifying governance actions for compliance with the Constitution.\r\nThis is not development or product creation; it’s administrative work that doesn’t require full-time commitment or large team resources.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 💬 **Why I Vote NO**\r\n\r\n* ₳200,000 per member is 3–6× higher than typical DAO compensation (₳30–60k per year).\r\n* There are no public reports showing real workload or hours of CC activity.\r\n* Rewards should be proportional to contribution and transparently justified.\r\n* Such excessive spending weakens the sustainability and trust of the Cardano Treasury.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 💡 **My Proposal**\r\n\r\n* Reduce compensation to **₳30,000–₳60,000 per member per year**.\r\n* Introduce a measurable **CC activity metric** — number of reviewed proposals, meeting participation, and published reports.\r\n* Preserve fair reward principles but maintain balance, transparency, and strict auditing.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n🗳 **I vote “NO” on the Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581–653 proposal.**\r\n💬 My DRep ID: ➡️ **drep1y269ehxj30k4vfzfc2z84v0xykd3amuy2xn0kv9zf8rhcec2fg2jr**\r\n\r\nI’m registered as a DRep and ready to help shape the future of the Cardano ecosystem.\r\nOptimistic about building the world’s largest decentralized community. 🖤\r\nMore details here: [https://t.me/PROCENT666/338](https://t.me/PROCENT666/338)",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "MyCNFT DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaqplbz5g3tgwywfdqkstexm6e3wnb4yd74yexknw7pi5y43iplk4 -->\r\n# MyCNFT DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wwa9cqns95zzztmz9vw3jm7n8lpd3x8wfvg6wnvvt29ngdm0mlh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support the idea of compensating Constitutional Committee (CC) members as an important step toward sustainable and fair governance in Cardano. The CC’s work requires time, expertise, and independence, and establishing a transparent, smart contract–based compensation mechanism aligns well with the Constitution.\r\n\r\nHowever, the requested budget of 1,000,000 ADA — up to 200,000 ADA per member — seems relatively high for an initial funding round. At this stage, a phased or partial approach might be more appropriate, allowing the community to evaluate the model’s effectiveness before scaling further.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I generally support the concept but abstain from endorsing this specific budget to encourage more detailed justification of the compensation level and ensure a stronger balance between cost and outcome.",
