    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNckLnxsucRhTwT63YnXXUD7JPyYDMMsPsFHb8i2siHgg -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am choosing to ****abstain ****on this Info action for Constitutional Committee compensation.\r\n\r\nFirst, I want to be clear on principle: I fully support the idea that Constitutional Committee (CC) members can and should be compensated for their work. The Cardano Constitution explicitly anticipates compensation for governance roles, including CC members, and the reality of the workload is well known to anyone who has followed governance closely. Reviewing governance actions for constitutional alignment, drafting rationales, and operating across time zones is demanding work. It is neither sustainable nor fair to expect long-term, high-quality service to be carried out indefinitely on a purely voluntary basis.\r\n\r\nMy abstention is therefore not a rejection of CC compensation, but a response to the way this particular budget has been framed and introduced.\r\n\r\nThere are three broad concerns that prevent me from voting Yes:\r\n\r\nLack of clear justification for the requested amount.\r\nThe proposal asks for up to 200,000 ₳ per seat, but the on-chain metadata does not explain how this number was derived. There is no visible model of expected hours, rate assumptions, or comparison with similar public-service or governance roles. Without a transparent breakdown of workload and costing, it is very difficult for DReps or the wider community to judge whether the amount is proportionate.\r\n\r\nMissing accountability and performance framework.\r\nSeveral DReps have rightly pointed out that a durable compensation model should sit on top of a clear, public framework that describes the CC’s duties, minimum participation standards, and conditions for non-payment. This proposal relies primarily on smart-contract mechanics and peer oversight at the contract level, but does not yet define what “good performance” looks like from a constitutional governance perspective. I believe a CC code of conduct / SLA-style document should either precede or accompany a budget like this.\r\n\r\nFairness, precedent and ecosystem coherence.\r\nCC work is important, but so is the work done by DReps and SPOs. Approving a relatively large, CC-only compensation package—especially for a committee that accepted its term without an explicit compensation promise—risks setting an uneven precedent. Many in the community quite reasonably ask why CC compensation is being addressed in isolation instead of as part of a broader, coordinated framework for rewarding all governance roles. I share that concern and would prefer to see this discussion evolve into a more comprehensive, ecosystem-wide approach.\r\n\r\nI do want to acknowledge the positive aspects of the design. Using per-member smart contracts with vesting, clawback, and peer-controlled pause mechanisms is a strong architectural choice. Unused funds being swept back to the Treasury after expiry aligns with good stewardship of common resources. In many ways, the technical and contractual structure is ahead of the political and economic framing.\r\n\r\nHowever, the combination of an under-explained amount, the absence of a clear accountability framework, and the limited prior socialisation of this proposal means I cannot actively endorse it in its current form. A No vote from me would risk being interpreted as opposition to CC compensation itself, which is not my position. Instead, I am abstaining to signal conditional support for the principle while urging a revised, more mature proposal.\r\n\r\nI would be open to supporting a future submission that:\r\n\r\nProvides a transparent cost model for the requested amounts, including estimated workload per governance action type and per epoch;\r\n\r\nIs paired with a public-facing CC responsibilities and accountability framework, including minimum participation expectations and conditions under which compensation may be withheld;\r\n\r\nIs developed alongside, or at least clearly situated within, a broader conversation about compensation for other governance roles such as DReps; and\r\n\r\nIs better socialised with the community before submission, so that key details live in the proposal itself rather than scattered across social media threads.\r\n\r\nThis proposal has started an important conversation about how we sustain our governance institutions. My abstention is intended as a constructive contribution to that conversation: yes to CC compensation in principle, but not yet, and not quite like this.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibuxqgj6uynr62mkwjma7yyxtrba3au3mez25v4yeemwnqpzccv7q -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am reluctantly voting against this proposal. I am very much in favor of compensation for the activities of the constitutional committees however the amount of compensation matters and needs to be better examined. This proposal does not explain what the community is paying for in essence. Why was the amount of 200,000 Ada chosen? Why would the amount not be dependent on the number of actions examined by the committees? At this stage in Cardano's development I don't see how this function could be considered full time employment so why a set rate? Perhaps a set rate per proposal examined and a max cap of 200,000 Ada would work. I believe more work is needed before I can vote in favor of this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeBXvasb4JFk9WkDYYw12YFXJgFT1NfMgAsCWkC43rVS1 -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs I have a direct interest in this proposal, I would not be able to maintain neutrality in this decision. Therefore, I will abstain.\r\n\r\nThat said, I believe developing a sustainable and transparent compensation framework for the CC is important for the long-term health of Cardano governance, and I look forward to continued community discussion on this topic.\r\n\r\n僕は本提案に利害を有する立場であり、中立性を維持できないため棄権いたします。\r\n\r\nただし、憲法委員会の職務は、Cardano ガバナンスの健全性を支える重要なものであり、その持続に必要な仕組みや報酬体系の整備をコミュニティとして前向きに議論していくことを期待します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifedao3mcg26x7zb3sjjbb2w5pufvrr2wkujtodukaopdn5swjpdq -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n🗳️ SIPO DRep Comment — Abstain\r\n\r\nSIPO recognizes that this proposal — “Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581–653” — represents an important and necessary step in building a sustainable and fair governance framework for Cardano.\r\nIt aims to formalize a transparent compensation structure for the Constitutional Committee (CC), ensuring that committee members can continue their work independently, without relying on external or personal financial support. I fully acknowledge the motivation and good faith behind this effort.\r\n\r\nAt the same time, SIPO believes that the governance system as a whole is still in a formative stage. The Constitution, the replacement and review processes for the CC, and the standards for oversight and audit are all being tested for the first time in a real-world context.\r\nIn this phase, the most valuable action for the community may not be to finalize a financial structure, but to observe, measure, and refine the operational model through transparent and inclusive discussion.\r\n\r\nFrom SIPO’s perspective, defining a long-term compensation mechanism now — before the system’s full functionality and accountability processes are validated — risks fixing the institutional form too early.\r\nIt could unintentionally limit future flexibility or set precedents that later conflict with more mature governance norms.\r\nSIPO values the principle that “the system should evolve organically through experience and consensus,” not by early codification.\r\n\r\nWe also note that several current CC members themselves have declined compensation or expressed reservations.\r\nThis diversity of opinion within the Committee highlights the need for more dialogue and mutual understanding among CC, DReps, SPOs, and the broader community before formalizing such frameworks.\r\nTherefore, while SIPO supports the spirit of ensuring fair and independent governance, we consider this particular step to be premature in timing.\r\n\r\nIn light of these considerations, SIPO has chosen to Abstain from voting on this proposal.\r\nOur abstention does not mean opposition to the idea of CC compensation; rather, it reflects a desire to promote further consensus-building, transparency, and institutional maturity before establishing a permanent standard.\r\n\r\nWe encourage continued open discussion between all governance actors — CC members, Intersect, DReps, and community participants — to co-create a compensation framework that is both principled and adaptive to future governance evolution.\r\nSIPO remains committed to supporting the growth of Cardano’s governance ecosystem in a way that is inclusive, verifiable, and sustainable for the long term.\r\n\r\nIn summary:\r\nSIPO abstains, with respect for the intent of this proposal, and with a view toward the long-term health and credibility of Cardano’s constitutional governance.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、この提案「Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581–653」が、カルダノのガバナンスをより持続可能で公正なものにしていくための重要な一歩であることを理解しています。\r\nこの提案は、憲法委員会（Constitutional Committee, CC）のメンバーに対して透明性のある報酬構造を整備し、委員たちが外部資金や自己負担に頼らず、独立して活動を継続できるようにすることを目的としています。\r\nその意図や誠実な動機には、SIPOも共感しています。\r\n\r\nしかし一方で、SIPOは現時点のカルダノ・ガバナンス全体がまだ形成途上にあると考えています。\r\n憲法の最終的な定義や、憲法委員会の交代・監査・報告の手続きなどは、まだ初期段階で実験的に運用されている状態です。\r\nこのような時期に制度的な報酬モデルを先に固定してしまうことは、今後の制度設計の柔軟性を損ねるおそれがあると感じています。\r\n\r\nSIPOが重視しているのは、「制度はまず経験と対話を通じて成熟させ、その上で正式な形を整えるべきだ」という原則です。\r\n現時点では、報酬スキームを確定させるよりも、運用・監査・意思決定のプロセスをコミュニティ全体で検証し、長期的な信頼を積み上げていくことが大切だと考えています。\r\n\r\nまた、今回の提案においては、現職のCCメンバーの中にも報酬を辞退した方や、制度設計に対して慎重な意見を持つ方がいます。\r\nこの点は、委員会内部でも多様な見解が存在することを示しており、ガバナンス全体としてより広い合意形成と対話のプロセスを経る必要があることを示唆しています。\r\nSIPOはそのプロセスを尊重したいと考えています。\r\n\r\nしたがって、SIPOはこの提案に対して「Abstain（棄権）」の立場を取ります。\r\nこれは提案の理念や目的に反対するものではなく、「もう少し時間をかけて制度的な合意と成熟を進めたい」という意思の表明です。\r\nより健全で透明な仕組みを構築するためには、ガバナンスの各主体──CC、DRep、SPO、Intersect、そしてコミュニティ──が協力し、オープンな議論を続けていくことが重要だと考えています。\r\n\r\nSIPOは、カルダノの憲法ガバナンスが長期的に信頼される仕組みとして定着していくことを願っており、\r\n今回の棄権判断はそのための慎重で責任あるステップだと位置づけています。\r\n\r\n最終的に、SIPOの立場をまとめると次の通りです。\r\n\r\nSIPOは本提案に対し「Abstain（棄権）」の投票を行います。\r\nその理由は、制度の意義を尊重しつつも、ガバナンスの方向性をより多くの関係者と共に検証し、成熟した合意を築く時間が必要だと判断したためです。\r\nSIPOは今後も、カルダノのガバナンスがより包摂的で、検証可能で、持続的な仕組みとして発展していくよう尽力してまいります。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWGfpTStzMJe1yitjXrZwWfwufCq4aUd4AmtttpqZjZAp -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe abstained on this proposal. The compensation framework for Constitutional Committee members is an important governance matter. However, since some members of the Socious DRep are members of the Constitutional Committee, we determined that abstaining was the appropriate action to avoid any potential conflict of interest and to maintain impartiality.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUSoazfseMES8u1Mop3LJDie7p3mBptMTyamq7EqUHSxg -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSTORM Partners is voting NO on the CC Compensation proposal. We recognize the importance of fairly compensating governance contributors, including CC members, and agree that sustainability requires moving beyond purely voluntary participation. However, this proposal lacks the necessary transparency, consultation, and strategic framing expected of a treasury withdrawal of this scale. There was no prior public debate with DReps or the community, and the ₳1,000,000 allocation, while not excessive, was defined without clear benchmarking, scope definition, or performance expectations.\r\n\r\nOur position is not against compensation but against premature institutionalization. Governance funding should evolve through an open, data-driven process that defines how all bodies - CC, DReps, and others - are compensated within a lean and sustainable governance system. As emerging AI-assisted constitutional analysis workflows demonstrate, efficiency and automation can reduce manual overhead and cost over time.\r\n\r\nWe therefore oppose this proposal in its current form while encouraging a revised, community-endorsed compensation framework that balances fairness, accountability, and long-term fiscal responsibility.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiclncxw57a5cthquwxvv3lzgulze7cc7dzuw6532vfo5txfeiyqyq -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote yes because I prioritize institutional independence and constitutional compliance to build a robust, accessible Cardano Constitutional Committee. The proposal's transparency and safeguards (vesting, peer oversight, fund recovery) substantiate low risk of abuse, directly fulfilling the Constitution's intent for fair compensation.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXD2yzSFBnZDyqP6Y83MjVQkty2fXf5XgLFPYYUEn6nHt -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt is simply absurd for CC to ask for compensation when CC are not legally trained, not doing the hard work like DReps in analysing the benefit of proposal on Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Terminada",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://terminada.io/gov-acts/20251029-constitutional-committee-compensation/vote-context.jsonld -->\r\n# Terminada\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytf9f78k7rkwk4cu6l2nvna22keu9yus4kqzc0hqspd36uszu0xc2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCC members all volunteered without wage expectations.  DReps also required to judge constitution compliance.  Excessive amount requested and not tied to measurable performance.  Could set a precedent whereby members prioritise personal financial gain over broader community interests.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiddh32l7cfldzhgu2ekh556laei7jlf3btoyhduay4z34ugls757q -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCC duties are relatively simple compared to DReps. They primarily have to determine if an action complies with a concrete document, the Cardano Constitution. DReps, in comparison, have to deal with budget allotment, value determination and other strategic decisions. \r\n\r\nI have doubts as to whether or not DReps should be compensated, and if DReps are non-compensated I certainly feel the CC members should be.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYBiw4AiB2mocbeHv7wMSP6cyZQUk7xY3uZeDXhDQq8fZ -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting NO on this CC compensation proposal despite supporting compensation in principle. The inconsistency of some members accepting funds while others decline creates an inequitable and confusing precedent. Either all CC members should receive compensation for their governance work, or none should—this mixed approach undermines the fairness principle and makes it unclear whether CC service is voluntary or compensated labor. We should pass a compensation framework where all members are treated equally, even if individuals choose to donate their compensation back to the treasury.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRXj1s5wyPdjiafsbn5tpvTqFNTjvUNEVpFvSgQCNU64J -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI believe in equitable and open compensation for key governance roles. However, **this submission is premature, overbroad, and procedurally weak**. It asks for 1,000,000 ADA without sufficient justification, without parity to comparable roles (notably DReps and SPOs), and without an enforceable accountability framework that satisfies basic Treasury stewardship standards. \r\n\r\n**The proposal offers no benchmarking: no hourly estimates, no comparable compensation models (DRep stipends, SPO reimbursements, external committee rates), no CPI or FX sensitivity, and no breakdown of how 200k per member maps to time, effort, or deliverables.** A blunt “up to 200,000 ADA” figure per person is not a defensible ask for a public treasury.\r\n\r\nApproving this as-is risks precedent-setting spend, inequitable treatment of other contributors, and ambiguous governance accountability. **Cardano governance needs to guard against small-group exploitation and eliminate the risk of inadvertently forming an elite paid class. **Compensation is legitimate, but must be tied to transparency, parity, and accountability for CCs, DReps, and SPOs alike.\r\n\r\n***„The pigs did not actually work, but directed and supervised the others. With their superior knowledge, it was natural that they should assume leadership.“*\r\nGeorge Orwell, Animal Farm**",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUV66hYMfTTcehvcNqKaejTs79rKwMT4g9NtN2nTd9paQ -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I appreciate the time and effort required to serve as a CC member, the proposed 200,000 ADA compensation for five members/entities, with no allocation for the other two individuals, is excessive. I would support a maximum of 20,000 ADA per year per entity, contingent on unanimous agreement among all CC members. I believe Phil and KtorZ should have the option to donate their share to charity if they choose, but their agreement on this matter is essential, as it sets a precedent for future compensation discussions, such as those involving DReps.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRWaroT9Q3vmF3QawgUqYarXLX2AR8kJbJFgH3L6b3qNS -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote NO. CC must prove value first. DReps serve unpaid — lead by example. At least not now. Lets reconsider next year.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihocrbh5ubnvppagxbqi2tv5d2ucpw7p6xajso23sipxcwzwrguyq -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe have reviewed the proposal “Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581–653” and acknowledge the critical role the Constitutional Committee (CC) continues to play in safeguarding the governance process, interpreting constitutional provisions, and ensuring procedural integrity. The proposal requests ₳1,000,000 from the treasury to compensate five of the seven currently serving CC members for their work over a 73-epoch term. The intent to formalize fair remuneration for essential governance work is understandable and, in principle, supports professional accountability and sustainability within Cardano’s evolving governance system.\r\n\r\nHowever, we hold the view that governance equity must remain central to any compensation framework. Cardano’s governance ecosystem functions as an interconnected structure comprising DReps, SPOs, and the Constitutional Committee, each fulfilling distinct yet equally vital duties that sustain decision-making legitimacy. To compensate one body in isolation risks distorting that balance, particularly when the other two operate under similarly demanding workloads with significant community-level responsibility. A selective compensation model could introduce unintended behavioural biases or weaken the collaborative equilibrium among governance actors.\r\n\r\nWe therefore believe that compensation for governance roles should not be designed or approved unilaterally by any single body that stands to benefit from it. Instead, a comprehensive, community-driven compensation framework should be developed; one that establishes transparent standards, clear eligibility criteria, equitable rates, and peer-reviewed oversight for all recognized governance participants. Such a model would not only mitigate potential perceptions of privilege or self-authorization but also strengthen accountability and preserve fairness across governance layers.\r\n\r\nUntil such a unified and community-endorsed framework is introduced, we are unable to fully support isolated compensation actions. Our position is not a rejection of the Constitutional Committee’s value or effort but rather a principled call for parity, transparency, and collective design in how governance service is rewarded and we are more than happy to contribute to the development of a compensation framework that captures all governance actors. For this reason, we as Wada DRep will vote no on this proposal, while encouraging further dialogue to develop an ecosystem-wide compensation policy that treats all governance bodies with equal recognition and fairness.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreies5jkklsrtwvt4sm3otu47xal3647mc2onhzoolzaeuzgturkvcy -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe constitutional committee plays an important role in the governance of Cardano. To ensure that we can continue to rely on their contributions, it is appropriate to compensate the committee for their efforts. I find the amount proposed to be quite reasonable.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YOADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihnc5tcsvlmng7hgrlbqj4ttv36wxvrpdbuofdosrnyf622vtgkae -->\r\n# YOADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26sfka2km0p4xw073ujdq406wxxczhdyfh9vw7yxpfselchzkdjn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt's too soon to estimate the good amount of compensation in the governance of cardano (or if its needed at all)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/CC%20Compensation.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi votes ABSTAIN on the Budget Info Action to compensate Constitutional Committee members. We are strongly supportive of CC compensation, as outlined in the Cardano Constitution. However, several aspects of this proposal require further clarification before it can be fully endorsed.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nYoroi strongly supports ensuring that CC members receive appropriate compensation, consistent with the Constitution’s provision that CC members may be compensated for their efforts. Their constitutional responsibilities are central to maintaining Cardano’s governance and long-term system integrity.\r\n\r\nHowever, while we fully agree with the principle, the requested 1,000,000 ADA lacks a clear explanation of how the total was derived and what underlying assumptions it represents. Without this clarity, we find it challenging to understand the intended scope, proportionality, and sustainability of the model.\r\n\r\nYoroi believes that a structured discussion among relevant stakeholders would be valuable to mature the proposal. Such a forum would help clarify objectives, align expectations, and establish shared assumptions before progressing toward a Treasury Withdrawal.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, Yoroi supports the constitutional principle that CC members may be compensated but abstains on this version to encourage clearer details and aligned expectations before funding is requested. We also believe a focused stakeholder forum would help consolidate information and refine the assumptions needed for a well-structured compensation model.\r\n\r\nPotential Discussion Points for the Forum:\r\n\r\nTo support the development of a clear and shared compensation model, Yoroi suggests that a dedicated stakeholder forum could explore the following topics:\r\n\r\nHow should compensation be structured to incentivize timely and high-quality rationalization for proposers?\r\n\r\nWhat mechanisms should be used to determine appropriate compensation levels?\r\n\r\nOn what criteria should payment be triggered?\r\n\r\nShould compensation be paid in ADA or in stablecoins?",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRxdkcJZaC2bnLchrUppsoX9qPdhXeByVaPSZT2RqbqmT -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm going to vote conditionally YES on CC compensation.\r\n\r\nFirst of all, as a matter of principle, compensation should be provided. CC work is very important and, in some cases, requires a lot of time and highly technical consideration.\r\n\r\nHowever, the issue is the amount. Many DRep feel that it is too expensive, and to be honest, it's difficult to judge whether it is or is not.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I would appreciate it if you could provide the following points in your treasury withdraw. Presenting this does not necessarily mean I'll vote YES, but I will take it into consideration.\r\n\r\n1. Current effort by type of governance action and estimated future effort. Make it as clear as possible what is taking up time.\r\n\r\nThis will make it easier for DRep to determine the reasonableness of the amount.\r\n\r\nIn addition, you can identify governance action consideration items that are taking particularly long, and in some cases consider amending the constitution to reduce governance costs, such as removing clauses that result in unnecessary time spent on consideration but do not add much value. Budget info actions are, in my opinion, an example of an area of ​​constitutional reform where cost reductions can be made reasonably.\r\n\r\n2. Present an SLA: In particular, explain the differences in service between cases where a reward is received and cases where it is not.\r\n\r\nThis will discourage the idea that \"CC will evaluate governance actions regardless of whether a reward is received, so there is no need to provide a reward.\"\r\n\r\nFor example, the following: Providing the following services will benefit the entire ecosystem.\r\n\"If a reward is received, announce the planned voting date within two epochs of the submission of the governance action.\" (Not voting within two epochs!)\r\n\"If a reward is received, provide non-binding, casual constitutional advice on the constitutionality of draft governance actions sponsored by 20% of DRep's stake within three epochs.\" (Following all of the advice does not guarantee that the action will be constitutional!)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCC報酬について、条件付きYESの投票をしようと思います。\r\n\r\nまず原則論として、報酬の提供自体は、行うべきでしょう。CCの業務は非常に重要かつ場合によっては高度に技術的な時間をかけた検討が必要な場合もあります。\r\n\r\nただ、問題は、金額の多寡です。これを割高に感じるDRepが多く、また正直に言うとこれが割高なのかどうかの判断も困難な状況にあることです。\r\n\r\nよって次のような点をトレジャリーウィズドローで提示していただけますと幸いです。これを提示したから必ずYES投票すると言うわけではありませんが、考慮材料にします。\r\n\r\n1. 現在のところの１つのガバナンスアクション種類別の工数と今後の工数の見積もり。何に時間がかかっているのかできるだけ可視化します。\r\n\r\nこれによりDRepが金額の合理性を判断しやすくなります。\r\nまた、特に時間が余分にかかっているガバナンスアクションの検討項目を特定し、場合によっては不必要に検討に時間を要する結果をうむがそれほど価値のない条文を削除するなど憲法を改正してガバナンスコストを引き下げることも検討できます。Budget info actionは、私の考えでは合理的にコスト削減できる憲法改正分野の１つの例です。\r\n\r\n2. SLAの提示：特に報酬を受け取ったケースと受け取らないケースでどのようなサービスの違いが生まれるかについて説明します。\r\n\r\nこれにより「CCは報酬を受け取っても受け取らなくてもどちらにせよガバナンスアクションを評価するので、報酬は提供しなくて良い」と言う考え方を抑制できます。\r\n\r\n例えば、次のようなものです。次のようなサービスが提供されることはエコシステム全体にメリットがあります。\r\n「報酬を受け取る場合は、ガバナンスアクションの提出時から２エポック以内に投票予定日をアナウンスする」（２エポック以内に投票するではなく）\r\n「報酬を受け取る場合は、DRepの20%のステークにスポンサードされたガバナンスアクションのドラフトの合憲性について非拘束的でカジュアルな合憲性に関するアドバイスを３エポック以内に行う」（アドバイスに全て従っても合憲とするとは限らない）",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Zacros",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreico6rxorl35n77a7ux2vfufstofyfkff5pzac7thatq6rskjsi5bi -->\r\n# Zacros\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Constitutional Committee Compensation Epochs 581-653\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2tp9q9vckglgkgkgcdc33jtahrstfzfj3c8ez926ysszjqp5r4ts`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n0 to 200k in a blink. You might argue that many seats comprise several members and so 200k might be okish per head, however most of the overhead in voting/meetings/etc arise from their choice of forming the Constitutional Head that way",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    }
  ],
  "Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025": [
    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/gov_action1f9da8n2yaf4updxzmwc7fnw8ug2gwnpvqays5n3yw6nz0mu3z2qqq6ggge9.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis platform needs to mature a lot more before becoming treasury-funded. It is full of inaccuracies in its dApp tracking. It may benefit from removing all subjective and human-updated verdicts, moving to a purely on-chain-data-driven approach. It should be applying to be included in the Intersect budget rather than seeking direct treasury funding.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaLovelace777",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/tempoYES2/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(22).jsonld -->\r\n# AdaLovelace777\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygehgu65kchqm929zp69xhl06hqkpcjv0rzy44sx40qhufqgh3xv2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA mobile governance platform like Tempo.Vote could be a game-changer for Cardano. Mobile is where most people live their digital lives, and if governance is to be truly inclusive, it has to meet users where they are. By making it easier for people to participate in governance from anywhere, this project could significantly widen the circle of active voters and contributors. While they have not yet delivered a funded Catalyst project, this also means they are hungry to prove themselves — and the scope of this proposal suggests they’ve thought big about what’s possible. Their vision for integrated mobile governance and a lending pool for governance participation is bold and could inspire more innovation in this space. The requested budget, though substantial, reflects the complexity of building secure, reliable, and scalable governance infrastructure. Investing in a team willing to push Cardano governance into mobile-native territory could yield long-term dividends in participation, decentralization, and adoption. The features outlined — especially mobile-first governance actions and a governance-focused lending mechanism — show ambition and an understanding of gaps in current tooling. Backing them now could accelerate the pace at which governance on Cardano becomes truly global and always-accessible. In short, this proposal represents a high-upside bet on expanding participation, experimenting with new governance incentives, and positioning Cardano as the most user-friendly blockchain for decentralized decision-making.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmToCg3iVcDsy4bkmCYQKjsfsvwYxoewQv9PSiZh8MoZtJ -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI love what Tempo has been providing, and want to support them going forward. At the same time, this proposal seems very expensive for what is being provided, especially in terms of Infra.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote11.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSame as with any other preliminary Info action: I find this step adds unnecessary delays and confusion, given that 67% approval is already required at the final vote. But since it's now a mandatory part of the process, I'm voting Yes just to let it proceed - the actual decision will be made at the final vote. Also, I believe that a more detailed cost breakdown would help address some of the DReps' concerns and improve the chances of reaching the required threshold.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmass5Bh3p1xzbtQz8vUAVaorYwiWYVP6onnY1gvgwBVfK -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo.Voteが取り組んできた、モバイルフレンドリーなUI/UXや独立インフラを通じてガバナンス参加の裾野を広げようとする方向性には共感します。ただし本提案においては、資金の管理方法、開発体制、成果に関する客観的な指標など、依然として不透明な点が多く、判断に必要な情報が十分とは言えません。今後の改善に期待しつつ、今回は棄権とさせていただきます。\\\\n\\\\nI appreciate the direction Tempo.Vote has taken in aiming to broaden participation in governance through mobile-friendly UI/UX and independent infrastructure. However, this proposal still lacks sufficient clarity regarding fund management, development structure, and objective indicators of outcomes, making it difficult to make a fully informed decision. While I hope to see improvements in the future, I will abstain from voting on this proposal at this time.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AltcoinOracle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUqXuvqAAFR3EGQq6FvG19YbXV7Tnbkxfs6qi5k2PUmdk -->\r\n# AltcoinOracle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygvgk3899qm38zth07z5clhfjvzfhe2mf2kvkqrfxp93r5srjre5s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSupporting decentralized infra and mobile governance aligns with my values as a DRep. The budget is reasonable and the roadmap includes meaningful features like a lending pool. I vote YES, while encouraging a clearer roadmap, more transparency, and strong safeguards to prevent misuse of the lending system.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ARandomCardanoDrep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihzjfe2rdzquwhjirga3nevrhmv7bqijisx7de7qsrvat7c4lbt5q -->\r\n# ARandomCardanoDrep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfcmmdalgun0wekkk3md6xfx4dy956c9cpkrq9ux8casa3ggpt0hr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting Yes. Today, GovTool is the only interface for participating in Cardano governance, and it is maintained under the oversight of the Cardano Foundation. Tempo.vote offers an independent and complementary platform that improves visibility and usability of governance data through features like temperature checks, and their own indexer and node infrastructure.\r\n\r\nThis proposal directly supports ecosystem redundancy and resilience — both of which are critical in decentralized governance. By avoiding reliance on a single portal or infrastructure provider, we improve robustness and reduce systemic risk.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Atlanter",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNXvTmYK7XvPA9VdgsLdyYibmeUqgTGJXA8ixEKuQiLSq -->\r\n# Atlanter\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26k7hpkj26dnp8yznnsgpwu8l6pkgcdey4zd23dk655qcse26y3g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this initiative in general, although I'd like to see a bit more transparency and cost breakdown on the requested budget.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BAT Community",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alex-brave/Cardano-voting/main/Tempo%20Proposal%202025.jsonld -->\r\n# BAT Community\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hwk9gqua527ghfdysfjuzeuh4zcad7nveqzupm84h5adqjv22cu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe BAT Community DRep Committee has voted ABSTAIN of the Cardano GovTool Budget - 12 months full active maintenance and development, and ABSTAIN for the Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025.\r\n\r\nBoth proposals seek to enhance DRep infrastructure and broaden its accessibility, we believe that the domain of DRep voting should ultimately rest in the capable hands of innovative builders. This vision remains in its nascent stages—for instance, as evidenced by the Lace wallet's ongoing development of integrated infrastructure—yet it demands additional time for other creators to cultivate and refine. Consequently, a difficult choice between victors and contenders as both options support the DRep community. In light of this dilemma, we chose to ABSTAIN as we are in the early midst of DRep and the proliferation of DRep accessibility within the Cardano ecosystem. We love both options and support the outcome chosen by those with conviction.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "benzio",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfTMt2AV5zbskTvXmdstEK3nceWKsyKrzyFu1uoQVNnkc -->\r\n# benzio\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwge9pgkeyd5eawz4y07mvkt09jkmx9d2levdzdcr6xl7s2nr4hy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIf you’d like to support an independent developer who is actively learning and preparing to contribute to the Cardano ecosystem, consider making a donation.\r\nYour support will help me dedicate more time to study, build, and grow within the Cardano community.\r\nThank you,\r\nBenzio\r\n\r\nAddress for donations: addr1qy3tfm8gj8sxtkql7p5m4rvsc55l96cv5lwlz6pf3fde4wdtmhg0ztuweefsawjtsl3yhy32ma0ym8k3765wp6ml34jq8evqeu",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/DRepdata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context20250714TempoIA.jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私はこの提案に賛成（Yes）します。\r\nTempo.Voteは、スマートフォンからのガバナンス参加を可能にする数少ないツールの一つであり、Cardanoのオンチェーンガバナンスをより身近なものにしています。ノードとインデクサーを独自運用し、中央集権的サービスに依存しない設計は、分散型ガバナンスの理念とも合致しています。\r\n特に、モバイル端末からの提案提出・投票・結果確認の一貫対応は、広範なADAホルダーにとって非常に有用です。現時点で公式ウォレットであるLaceにモバイル版が存在しない中、Tempoはそのギャップを埋め、より多くのユーザーの参加を後押しする重要な存在となっています。\r\nまた、Lending Pool構想も、小規模保有者の声を政策に反映させるための仕組みとして期待できます。\r\nCardanoのガバナンスを真にグローバルで包摂的なものにしていくために、Tempoのようなユーザー起点のツールの進化は不可欠です。\r\n\r\n************************\r\n\r\nI support (Yes) this proposal.\r\nTempo.Vote is one of the few tools enabling governance participation from mobile devices, bringing Cardano’s on-chain governance closer to everyday users. Its independent operation of nodes and indexers—without reliance on centralized infrastructure—aligns with the principles of decentralized governance.\r\nIn particular, its seamless mobile experience for submitting proposals, voting, and checking results is highly beneficial to the broader ADA holder base. Given that the official wallet, Lace, currently lacks a mobile version, Tempo plays a critical role in filling that gap and encouraging broader participation from the community.\r\nAdditionally, the Lending Pool concept holds promise as a mechanism to amplify the voices of smaller holders in the governance process.\r\nTo make Cardano governance truly global and inclusive, the evolution of user-driven tools like Tempo is essential.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQ4NpeShhFMfT8q2r4RWuTJmJs6MN9yyH7fGLLyYfRNnw -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo is a useful app for governance. However, it is difficult for me to vote yes on their proposal. They should provide more detailed information about the budget. They should also provide specific arguments to convince Dreps to vote yes.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Africa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Abdulazizkarma1/Cardano-Africa-DRep-Data/refs/heads/main/Tempo_Vote.jsonld -->\r\n# Cardano Africa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytj9kz0n5yamacgcj8jr6apn36hx5suzqpefxvhy4cvfqmsqangtx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo.Vote wants treasury money to stay alive and build more features, but the proposal lacks depth, metrics, safeguards, and clarity, and yet wants 380k ADA.\r\nYou're not owed treasury funds just because you're passionate. You need to prove value, show your receipts, and deliver a plan the community can believe in.\r\nThe Cardano Africa Community Vote NO on this treasury withdrawal",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://bafybeiemor5uab4himgdjgv6w7c4lv7nms2znzy2z46gphr7m7ylwltmwi.ipfs.dweb.link/ -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmRHzT1ZuojMQ6DPUHC16H78tjvRoqxt9LdPLoAGAaMQRy\r\n\r\nThis is a pragmatic decision based on the strategic importance of fostering a competitive and diverse governance tooling landscape. While the proposal has flaws in its quality and detail, we believe the risk of creating a tooling monoculture currently outweighs these concerns.\r\n\r\n### **Rationale Statement**\r\n\r\nThis decision reflects a careful balance between the project's potential strategic value and the valid critiques of the proposal itself. Our support is conditional and comes with clear expectations for future funding requests.\r\n\r\n#### **Reasons for a 'YES' Vote**\r\n\r\n1. **Strategic Importance of Ecosystem Competition:** The primary driver for our support is the need for healthy competition in the governance tooling sector. tempo.vote provides another option for the ecosystem as a governance interface, allowing users to perform core governance functions like DRep registration and proposal submission. Having multiple options for such tooling supports decentralization, encourages innovation, and can help ensure tooling costs remain reasonable over the long term.  \r\n2. **Demonstrated Value and Community Use:** The tempo platform has demonstrated its value and agility, for instance, by quickly shipping a bulk-voting feature helpful to the community. This responsiveness helps justify the requested ₳380,000 for six months, which, while high, we view as a pragmatic investment to sustain this valuable tooling solution option.  \r\n3. **Supporting Ecosystem Diversity:** This vote serves as an important political signal that Cardano's governance and treasury are accessible to smaller, independent development teams. Fostering a diverse ecosystem of builders beyond the large, established entities is essential for Cardano's long-term health and decentralization.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmThRjUbr2q7gJgcPoJErjzMkE69QJQXQcDcFbWJRwqXKH -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs others have remarked, Tempo has built a great tool and there is a certain irony in voting no on this while using their own tool. However, I too would like to see some more details and a commitment to delivering open source results so that if the team behind this were to pack up the community is not left empty handed.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdGUXhsnJpcAQJp1NSfvGLdNA8ZtZZsuUEW6rPgL474ko -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXvpDxaGKJAhSudg7EiSFJAirZTVVfofM5U3JkKzTqjt6\r\n\r\nI do have a profile on Tempo.Vote and genuinely appreciate the service. I believe in supporting platforms I actively use. I also like the idea of offering a short-term loan of 100K ADA to help users submit governance actions and earn a modest return. Still, there are alternative ways to make this mechanism work.\r\n\r\nHowever, the requested 200K ADA to cover six months of infrastructure costs—roughly 33,333 ADA per month, or around $25,000 USD—feels excessive. Additionally, the proposal allocates 180K ADA to implement three new features, which also seems overvalued. I believe another team could deliver similar results more cost-effectively.\r\n\r\nIn my view, a comparable proposal could be executed with a budget up to ten times lower.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cash",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXbcTVajuyfBUNFHYZbc6rKLYfEQdv8agHNZJypRK6kh3 -->\r\n# Cash\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygeyfh8nm03dnl5a2hxdtv09pu7uhep9l0cpg0zpr60jqys05cku2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLove the tool, hate the proposal. Would love to see a better defined output for us to digest as DReps.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcxhbWXcTSVHgKQHHk3nyHEHP1qKnM247EPQ9D7esiGmL -->\r\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a slight yes for us to encourage the Tempo platform. However, we are more inclined towards suggestions for them to resubmit a better and clearer version.\r\n\r\nPlus points:\r\n1. Tempo offers a 100k loan to propose a GA\r\n2. The proposal is considered more cost-effective then that of Gov.tools\r\n\r\nNeed improvement\r\n1. Self-driven is completely new and lacks the how to manage accountability for the community\r\n2.  Imagine it as a proper catalyst proposal, which would require more well-planned and detailed articulations for the community (Timing/phasing/team resource/cost breakdown). A product development sprint (time/task/human resource + cost breakdown) would make it more convincing as a strong yes from the community",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUsnfFZUj7enAZqcjogLn8TDeRVrJxPryo6hQCmter6Pw -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI appreciate and support Tempo for the fantastic platform they have built and continue improving upon.  However, I think the treasury should prioritize funding core Cardano infrastructure that serves as a public good.  For me it is difficult to support funding for this proposal because it does not appear to have plans to open source.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/Vote_rationale_07262025_tempo.jsonld -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI want to support Tempo for another year and see where they go with development.  I think we're still in a crucial time to see these tools get built out and offer different takes on the overall UX. There's the added benefit that the total amount of ADA asked for is to support a fee-based lending pool for submitting future gov actions. The 2026 plan for Tempo is still ambitious at an estimated 400K (per their feedback), however that assumes further development of the portal.  It would be half as much if it was just for maintenance. Some more time will tell us whether there's demand for conintued support as other APIs are developed, additional open-source tooling becomes available, and community feedback on what ultimately users want to see. I have found Tempo useful as a DRep, and am voting in favor of their budget.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQCd9T77DhJCmHjFaaeXVZLeqUcPLcmRBohmwbjj5dKB4 -->\r\n# Dan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfsgx4dqfcxxs0ms533twzs7w0cvw8vq8qwzmjyrp280jfsl8gusv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting Abstain on this info action as while I support Tempo (currently using it to vote) there is very minimal detail on how the funds will be used.\r\n\r\nA 380k ADA ask for 6 months is quite significant so there needs to be more detail on how the funds will be used to justify the expense. I would also be keen to see a commitment to open source products if Tempo wants to use the treasury to fund operations.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmQSKfpbHsic9bMtjbYYqtZWRYG66GBiXrxpQi3ioPRY6E -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXtF4TRnDi3MhrzJx5x7seyTCYNRWms76X6sBp6DQmWpk\r\n\r\nI vote **Yes**. My positive experience using Tempo.Vote confirms its **reliability** and value. Their commitment to **accessible governance** for mobile users, coupled with independent infrastructure, is vital for **decentralization** and fostering broader participation. This directly supports Cardano's **growth and sustainability** through essential innovation. I will be closely watching the listed goals and will factor their achievement into future voting decisions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "DeepStatecraft",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRjQW6X9XcVwHnW94mqeFp6gAnubE4dsK6GnfGPD1vsy8 -->\r\n# DeepStatecraft\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfr0cur4guksjd6whxe5mltcaksqqhzd85dnq6lfk8ex7qs5mlcye`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n✅ Vote: YES\r\n📌 Proposal: Tempo.Vote Maintenance & Development (Info Action)\r\n🗳️ Governance Action ID: gov_action1f9da8n2yaf4updxzmwc7fnw8ug2gwnpvqays5n3yw6nz0mu3z2qqq6ggge9\r\n📅 Period Covered: August 2025 – January 2026\r\n💰 Planned Future Treasury Ask: ₳380,000\r\n\r\nRationale:\r\nTempo.Vote is one of the most accessible and effective tools we have today for engaging in Cardano governance. It provides mobile-native access, clear visuals, and real-time vote tracking — lowering the barrier for ADA holders to participate meaningfully on-chain.\r\n\r\nBy running its own node and backend infrastructure, Tempo ensures governance data is accurate and not reliant on third-party APIs. That kind of independence deserves support.\r\n\r\nThe proposed roadmap — including governance UX enhancements and a Lending Pool to help new proposers overcome the 100K ADA barrier — is highly aligned with decentralization and inclusivity.\r\n\r\nSupporting Tempo now helps secure the future of intuitive, decentralized governance for Cardano.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "DraculaDAO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dracula-DAO/cardano-drep/refs/heads/main/2025/2025-07-25_Tempo_Budget.jsonld -->\r\n# DraculaDAO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygs99wsy49h9vydggncfeck2xwmngyeltp66pvgzl6jz63s6qmu3p`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo is a good tool and needs UI work, however, the ask amount is overpriced for a 6 month operating budget. We run relay nodes, preview and preprod testnet nodes plus a midnight node for a small percentage of that. We also believe in general that development should be incentivized through the treasury, not have the entire budget come from the treasury.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSZq7HX38tSPecpxYwhYo41FRGgUaHv69GfwoVHkLQuQT -->\r\n# drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLook.. i like tempo, im using it rn (also on purpose) to vote, but this proposal is atrocious and unacceptable. Please include some accountability and dont expect a blank check.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/tempoYES/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(21).jsonld -->\r\n# drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA mobile governance platform like Tempo.Vote could be a game-changer for Cardano. Mobile is where most people live their digital lives, and if governance is to be truly inclusive, it has to meet users where they are. By making it easier for people to participate in governance from anywhere, this project could significantly widen the circle of active voters and contributors. While they have not yet delivered a funded Catalyst project, this also means they are hungry to prove themselves — and the scope of this proposal suggests they’ve thought big about what’s possible. Their vision for integrated mobile governance and a lending pool for governance participation is bold and could inspire more innovation in this space. The requested budget, though substantial, reflects the complexity of building secure, reliable, and scalable governance infrastructure. Investing in a team willing to push Cardano governance into mobile-native territory could yield long-term dividends in participation, decentralization, and adoption. The features outlined — especially mobile-first governance actions and a governance-focused lending mechanism — show ambition and an understanding of gaps in current tooling. Backing them now could accelerate the pace at which governance on Cardano becomes truly global and always-accessible. In short, this proposal represents a high-upside bet on expanding participation, experimenting with new governance incentives, and positioning Cardano as the most user-friendly blockchain for decentralized decision-making.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dumpling🥟",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmeb1FYonZ6NFRBBdsY6EExTFvWKEsxRnDLYv9VmfCS4XA -->\r\n# Dumpling🥟\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rtf58m0lv9spcqx5mads20gpfulf6l97w57ecdy00vjdq0klh4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo.Vote 致力于用好用的 UI/UX 设计和独立基础设施来扩大治理参与度的方向， 符合有益于Cardano发展的技术型提案。 但目前提案在资金管理以及成果的客观衡量指标等方面仍缺乏足够的清晰度，，希望未来能看到改进",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Tempo.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n\r\nEMURGO as DRep votes NO on the governance action to fund Tempo for Cardano Governance – Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nEMURGO appreciates and acknowledges Tempo.Vote’s intention to enhance Cardano governance accessibility, particularly its efforts in running independent infrastructure and offering mobile-friendly governance tools. These contributions align with Cardano’s long-term vision for decentralization and user empowerment.\r\nHowever, as this proposal functions as a Budget Info Action, which signals community intent for future treasury withdrawal, we believe it must meet a higher threshold of clarity and accountability. At this stage, the proposal falls short in several key areas:\r\n\r\nThe budget requested lacks sufficient justification. No clear roadmap, milestones, or timeline have been provided to track the proposed deliverables.\r\n\r\nDetails regarding the development team, their past contributions, or their public accountability mechanisms are missing.\r\n\r\nThere are no stated metrics for success or community impact, making it difficult to evaluate outcomes.\r\nAlthough Selfdriven is listed as the fund administrator, no governance process for fund management has been described.\r\n\r\nWhile we support the proposed features, such as mobile-friendly governance action creation and improved UX, the absence of structural elements and execution clarity limits our confidence in the proposal as a credible basis for future funding.\r\n\r\nConclusion \r\nWe encourage Tempo.Vote to revise and resubmit with stronger documentation, clearer financial breakdowns, and robust transparency mechanisms. The Cardano ecosystem benefits from tools like Tempo, and we look forward to seeing a future iteration that the community can confidently support.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00016_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted YES on gov_action1f9da8n2yaf4updxzmwc7fnw8ug2gwnpvqays5n3yw6nz0mu3z2qqq6ggge9; While the infrastructure cost is kind of high, we support further development of tempo.vote. This vote signals support for tempo, even if this very info action might be deemed unconstitutional by the CC. Submit a corrected action and we will vote YES again.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU6xSMwgkP1HhxKCaUrbrA4ujx5XXp74k3qZhwG33T4fW -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe amount requested by Tempo is reasonable for the time frame and product/work to be delivered. Tempo.vote serves as a much better and more cost effective alternative to gov.tools, and the team has proven to be trustworthy. They will use community funds responsibly to deliver for Cardano.\r\n\r\nThis proposal also falls within my personal NCL of 250,000,000 ADA.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTtfEGBu9Wg9NqU3Ke1vzWV2bUxtpTNuDEdEvALPtNvWh -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for this budget Info Action.\r\n\r\nTempo operates its own Cardano node and indexer, ensuring data integrity without relying on third-party infrastructure. Many DReps have used Tempo and found it offers useful governance features, a user-friendly UX/UI, and full independence from other governance tools or APIs.\r\n\r\nWhile this proposal does not include a detailed budget breakdown, it specifies that Selfdriven will serve as the administrator for fund management. Compared to other proposals, this adds a layer of accountability. I expect a clearer budget and financial oversight process in Tempo’s follow-up Treasury Withdrawal proposal.\r\n\r\nI support this proposal based on Tempo’s tangible value to Cardano governance today and its continued development goals.\r\n\r\nThis support acknowledges both Tempo’s current contributions and the areas that require further refinement.\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nTôi bỏ phiếu YES cho đề xuất này.\r\n\r\nTempo vận hành node và indexer riêng, không phụ thuộc bên thứ ba, giúp đảm bảo dữ liệu bỏ phiếu on-chain được chính xác và sẵn sàng phục vụ người dùng. Nhiều DRep đã trải nghiệm Tempo và đánh giá cao tính năng tiện ích, UX-UI thân thiện, hoạt động độc lập, không sử dụng API từ bên ngoài.\r\n\r\nMặc dù đề xuất này chưa đính kèm bảng ngân sách chi tiết, Tempo đã chỉ định Selfdriven làm đơn vị quản lý tài chính. So với một số đề xuất khác không nêu rõ đầu mối tài chính, đây là điểm thể hiện phần nào tính minh bạch. Tôi kỳ vọng các đề xuất rút ngân quỹ tiếp theo của Tempo sẽ bao gồm bảng ngân sách cụ thể và quy trình quản lý rõ ràng.\r\n\r\nViệc ủng hộ đề xuất này thể hiện sự ghi nhận với những đóng góp hiện tại của Tempo, đồng thời cũng thừa nhận rằng vẫn còn nhiều điểm cần hoàn thiện thêm.\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nJapanese\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\n本提案に賛成票を投じます。\r\n\r\nTempoは、Cardanoノードとインデクサーを独自に運用しており、第三者に依存せず、ガバナンスデータの正確性と可用性を確保しています。多くのDRepが実際にTempoを使用した経験があり、UX・UIが直感的で使いやすく、APIや外部サービスに依存しない点が評価されています。\r\n\r\n今回の提案には詳細な予算表が添付されていませんが、財務管理者としてSelfdrivenが指名されており、一部の提案に比べて財務管理体制に一定の透明性があると考えられます。今後のTreasury Withdrawalにおける提案では、具体的な予算と支出計画が提示されることが期待されます。\r\n\r\nこの提案への支持は、Tempoが現在果たしている役割を評価すると同時に、改善が必要な点が依然として存在することも認識するものです。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmTpNAaKJ8zaD9vAj2ECDEYEJm6BZ2iNb8Jegw1ieMk9r1 -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYes! Tempo has proven to deliver a governance portal that is in many ways even better than GovTool purely as a passion project. They should get the funds to sustain these developments. The funding request is much more reasonable and motivated well.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmd1R9Q7vv1uG3wkAef8f6LHbBM2dRswrXgXpwm7uq1VJM -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNeed more information on financial audit. Especially, staking address should be opened with Auto-Abstain following the Constitution Article 4 section 5. Tempo is also act as a DRep, so that they need to ensure that the fund should not include in any type of delegation.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Homer J",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hodlonaut/a/refs/heads/master/vote5.jsonld -->\r\n# Homer J\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rvnp40ea4zsl4hqm0ev4qju205jx7mz57u2vwjzzrf50c24jca9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nInsufficient detail provided with regards to current maintenance costs, as well as breakdown of what the requested funds will be spent on - 'optimize' and 'improve' are a bit vague for a treasury withdrawal, IMHO.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HOSKY",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaXRtjgwSCpQvZxvNwkdr5NjJhoaSxFZDWjKdpnx6noHN -->\r\n# HOSKY\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf2jzhuc4f7eu2yay9d9ta3dykxxcwn34wz8kak7nhd7vcgrxn7ns`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTemporary Abstention Rationale\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nTo ensure timely progression of proposals that meet constitutional thresholds, I am temporarily casting abstain votes on all active governance actions while I continue to review them individually. This avoids delaying enactment due to quorum issues and allows careful evaluation of each on its own merits.\r\n\r\nRationale Statement\r\nAs a DRep, I take seriously my responsibility to evaluate each proposal in alignment with the HOSKY Cardano First platform, prioritizing decentralization, responsible treasury use, and the long term integrity of Cardano\r\n\r\nRather than rush through the volume of proposals or risk being a bottleneck for those that meet required thresholds, I am temporarily abstaining on all proposals. This ensures that governance actions with sufficient community support can move forward without being held up by my pending vote\r\n\r\nThis abstention is not a sign of indecision or neglect. It is a reflection of my commitment to deliberate, well considered governance. I am reviewing each proposal carefully and will cast definitive YES or NO votes with rationale in the coming days\r\n\r\nThis approach allows me to maintain transparency, uphold voting integrity, and respect the time sensitive nature of decentralized decision making. It is a temporary mechanism to preserve network momentum while continuing to uphold the standards set by both the Constitution and the HOSKY dRep Platform",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdvRvvFrc9xeyBh1Ww43WCx9RiqzGQyyhqQbPD2SKnFkm -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEnglish version. The Japanese translation is below the English version.\r\n英語版。日本語訳は英語版の下にあります。\r\nLet me prefact this vote with this comment: I like what Tempo.vote contributed to Cardano governance. They provided an alternative way of voting for DReps and were very proactive in improving their platform. I regularly pinged them with problems over their Telegram group and they would respond usually in 24 hours max and fix the issue. I have a profile on Tempo.vote - so I am appreciative of what they have contributed. I am even going to submit this vote over Tempo.vote. \r\nNow that they built the product, they should probably consider the big picture future for Tempo. I was leaning to vote YES on a Tempo governance action - as Cardano governance (Minimum Viable - lets be truthful) is one of the key distinguishing features of Cardano. However, several problems in this budget are preventing me from doing this. \r\nI want to be clear that this is not just about this proposal. We are setting precedents in Cardano governance with every vote. So, I would rather that we set positive precedents (better budgetary proposal actions now) - than make exceptions (weaker budgetary info actions) that may lead to more issues down the line as they proliferate. \r\nI do not see any committment in this proposal to make it open source with a specific license and a definite date to do so. Not saying it is obligatory, but unless there are some extenuating circumstances - it makes it more difficult for me to vote YES - as governance is a key component of running Cardano. Locking governance into proprietary tools - requires a deeper explanation and rationale - especially if it is to be financed from the Treasury. Not saying that there is no argument to be made there, but the proposal lacks any argumentation on this topic. I want to see a future roadmap for Tempo - as we could see Tempo pack up and go after the 6 month period (1 Aug 2025 - 31 Jan 2026) that they are requesting funding for. And there would be no public good left after they leave. \r\nThe financial numbers should be disaggregated and could quote specific rates, identify roles and also look forward towards the financial future of Tempo and what are the plans downstream. \r\nI find the entire proposal a bit light-weight - and it is much less comprehensive than a typical Project Catalyst proposal. This is a Treasury Budget proposal and should be more - rather than less detailed. \r\nTempo.Vote tackles a real usability gap. Overall, I'd say the proposal seems - with the current sparse information - over-budgeted and under-specified. Committing to open-source transparency - with a clear future strategy - will significantly raise its chance of a Yes in the on-chain vote, in my view. However, that is just personal feedback.  \r\nSome more background about the administrator Selfdriven would have been helpful, as I am not aware of this company - although I recognize one or two Cardano community names from their webpage. \r\n\r\nJapanese translation via Google Translate:\r\n\r\nGoogle翻訳による日本語翻訳：\r\nこの投票の前に、一言付け加えさせてください。Tempo.voteがCardanoガバナンスに貢献してくれたことに感謝しています。彼らはDRepsへの投票方法を提供し、プラットフォームの改善にも積極的に取り組んでくれました。私はTelegramグループで定期的に問題を報告していましたが、通常24時間以内に返信があり、問題を解決してくれました。私はTempo.voteにプロフィールを登録しているので、彼らの貢献に感謝しています。この投票もTempo.voteから提出するつもりです。\r\n製品を構築した今、彼らはTempoの将来像を大局的に検討すべきでしょう。Cardanoガバナンス（正直に言って、最小限の実行可能なもの）はCardanoの重要な特徴の一つであるため、Tempoのガバナンスアクションには賛成票を投じようと考えていました。しかし、この予算にはいくつかの問題があり、賛成を阻んでいます。\r\nこれはこの提案だけの問題ではないことを明確にしておきたいと思います。私たちは、すべての投票を通してCardanoガバナンスの先例を作っています。したがって、例外（予算情報に関する対応が弱まる）を設けて、将来的に問題が拡大するリスクを高めるよりも、前向きな前例（より良い予算提案）を作る方が良いと思います。\r\n\r\nこの提案には、特定のライセンスと明確な日付でオープンソース化するという確約は見当たりません。義務だと言っているわけではありませんが、特別な事情がない限り、ガバナンスはCardano運営の重要な要素であるため、賛成票を投じることは難しくなります。ガバナンスを独自のツールに縛り付けるには、より深い説明と根拠が必要です。特に財務省からの資金提供となる場合はなおさらです。議論の余地がないと言っているわけではありませんが、この提案にはこの点に関する議論が欠けています。Tempoの将来のロードマップを見たいです。資金を要請している6ヶ月間（2025年8月1日から2026年1月31日）後にTempoが撤退する可能性もあるからです。そして、彼らが撤退した後には公共の利益は何も残らないでしょう。\r\n財務数値は細分化され、具体的なレートを引用し、役割を特定し、Tempoの財務的な将来像と今後の計画について言及できる必要があります。\r\n提案全体がやや軽薄で、典型的なProject Catalystの提案よりもはるかに包括的ではありません。これは財務予算案であり、詳細度が低いのではなく、より詳細であるべきです。\r\nTempo.Voteは、ユーザビリティのギャップを埋めるものです。全体として、現状の情報が乏しいため、この提案は予算超過で詳細度が不足しているように思われます。明確な将来戦略とともにオープンソースの透明性にコミットすることで、オンチェーン投票で賛成される可能性が大幅に高まると私は考えています。ただし、これはあくまで個人的な意見です。\r\n管理者であるSelfdrivenについて、もう少し背景情報があれば助かります。この会社についてはよく知りませんが、ウェブサイトでCardanoコミュニティの名前をいくつか見覚えがあります。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
