    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihe6uvukyjv7tc5ya45i3gv5kr6uemldr3iwzg2csqft7uvu7aeli -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough I appreciate the utility that Tempo brings to the Cardano governance space, I am unable to vote in favor of this proposal because there is insufficient information provided in the proposal. To feel comfortable voting in favor of this proposal, I would like to see how Tempo is positioning itself as a public good accountable to the community. As it stands, this tool is a private venture from what I can tell, and there is no information showing otherwise in the proposal. I do find that Tempo brings utility, and I believe that with a reformulation of the proposal, I would likely vote in favor in the future.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUt3merVNpFZinQTUBnTLadcQJb8cxRmGSoXEAe5Fapzq -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal, with some conditions.\r\n\r\nCurrently, Cardano governance relies on only two active user interfaces: GovTool and Tempo. Depending solely on one tool—whether it's GovTool or Tempo—would undermine resilience and decentralization. Tempo offers a lightweight, mobile-friendly experience, which I personally find intuitive and easy to use. Its mobile accessibility lowers the barrier for broader participation, especially for users who govern on the go.\r\n\r\nThat said, some parts remain unclear—particularly the fund management structure (delegated to Selfdriven, but without details on whether smart contracts or multisig are used) and the development roadmap (which lacks concrete milestones or deliverables).\r\n\r\nI support this proposal based on current utility and intent, but I strongly hope that future Treasury Withdrawal proposals will include clearer financial structures and more transparent development plans.\r\n\r\nSupporting this proposal contributes to keeping Cardano governance open, accessible, and resilient.\r\n\r\n\r\n条件付きではありますが、この提案にYES票を投じます。\r\n\r\n現在、CardanoのガバナンスはGovToolとTempoの2つのUIに依存しており、どちらか一方に集中することは分散性やレジリエンスの観点で望ましくありません。Tempoは軽量かつモバイルに最適化された体験を提供しており、私自身とても使いやすいと感じています。外出先でもガバナンスに関われるという意味で、モバイル対応は大きな価値があります。\r\n\r\n一方で、Selfdrivenに委託されるとされる資金管理体制がスマートコントラクトやマルチシグを用いているのかが不明確であり、また開発のロードマップも具体的なマイルストーンや成果物が記載されていません。\r\n\r\n現時点の有用性と意図を評価して本提案を支持しますが、次回のトレジャリー引き出し提案では、資金構造と開発計画の透明性をより高めてほしいと強く願います。\r\n\r\nこの提案を支援することは、Cardanoガバナンスをオープンでアクセス可能かつ回復力のあるものに保つことに繋がると考えます。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWWYDK82gMyG4NDogB1QMvj24V4b85WxmsDWmcvTN1kUr -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo was developed out of passion and a commitment to support Cardano’s on-chain governance, entirely without funding from the Cardano Treasury. As a DRep, I’ve used Tempo to cast all my votes. Its simple and intuitive UI has made it easy for non-technical DReps like myself to actively participate in on-chain decision-making. I believe the time is right to support the team behind Tempo so they can continue building and maintaining this valuable tool for the benefit of the entire Cardano ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaV4bNe2dikaJZLTmyau34VPhAwcmMmiGodFr6DHjKwfs -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTempo.Vote is a reliable governance tool that is widely used and mobile-friendly, making on-chain participation more accessible to a broad range of users. To ensure maximum accuracy of governance voting data, it independently operates its own Cardano node and backend indexer. This setup requires ongoing operational costs to maintain stable and precise service.\r\n\r\nThis proposal requests a budget of 380,000 ADA over six months, covering infrastructure operations, improved user experience, and the development of a lending feature to support governance proposal submissions. The requested budget aligns with the scope of infrastructure and functional development, and considering the six-month period and Tempo’s proven track record, we find the amount to be balanced, realistic, and appropriate.\r\n\r\nBased on these factors, we regard this proposal as an important initiative that strengthens Cardano’s decentralized governance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmexDyTzC7teC7ZPTRVLHdaAdeeicKSX6EB256t5HEjMdY -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSTORM Partners initially registered as a DRep via Tempo.vote, so we recognize the project’s importance and value to the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThat said, despite our support for its mission, we are voting No on this proposal for the following reasons: it lacks detailed budget justification, defined milestones, and on-chain accountability mechanisms. The absence of transparency, delivery guarantees, and alignment with Cardano’s constitutional guardrails undermines its legitimacy.\r\n\r\nAs one of the first governance actions, we believe it is essential to set a strong precedent. We expect a higher level of transparency, depth, and justification in future governance actions, even for “temp check” info actions.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(15).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this proposal as it strengthens decentralized governance by maintaining Tempo’s independent infrastructure and enhancing mobile-friendly on-chain voting. The planned features, including a governance lending pool and UX improvements, align with Cardano’s mission of accessibility and participation for all.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Dutch Drep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmcH6wvyT7nZH8B8q96gk9gG5movJNgXaga9144gTw8Vdf -->\r\n# The Dutch Drep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yvve4554njxyun2s5p9q70v88d5jl7r0h34pjhw5f5tmw3sjtrutp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Dutch DRep, vote No on this Budget Info Action.\r\n\r\nWhile we appreciate the early contributions of the Tempo.Vote team—especially during a time when governance tooling on Cardano was still nascent—we believe this proposal does not meet the standards now expected for public funding.\r\n\r\nThe quality of the current tooling remains limited, and there is no commitment to open-source the platform. In a decentralized ecosystem, transparency and composability are critical—especially for infrastructure intended to serve the governance process. Closed-source tools create silos and limit community trust, innovation, and auditability.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the gap Tempo.Vote initially helped fill has now been addressed by other governance tooling efforts. Proposals such as the gov.tool Info Action and the AdaStat/Cexplorer Treasury Withdrawal present more robust, transparent, and collaborative pathways for advancing Cardano governance infrastructure. These initiatives are better aligned with the community’s evolving standards for openness and usability.\r\n\r\nWe recommend that Tempo.Vote consider submitting a proposal for Project Catalyst, with a focus on improving its open-source approach to better align with community values and expectations.\r\n\r\nWe believe the Treasury should prioritize open, auditable, and broadly integrated tooling. As such, we cannot support this proposal in its current form.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcoqNXar6vxMB2ePDTaCfwRvDA4o85ByH3efV72KXKPvC -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting No on the proposal to withdraw funds for “Tempo for Cardano Governance – Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025.” While governance tooling is important, this proposal presents an overly high operational budget without sufficient justification or demonstrated cost-efficiency. It raises a broader concern about whether ongoing operational expenses—like hosting, maintenance, and staffing—should be funded by the Treasury at all, rather than focusing Treasury resources on ecosystem development and innovation. Additionally, the proposal lacks a clear, enforceable commitment to open-source licensing and transparency, which are essential for community governance tools. Without strong guarantees around accessibility, reuse, and decentralization of the platform, I cannot support this request.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdJPcqmd6v9G2puyo8AKuRYtU1trYNG2r36EeHdVN3EbY -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI would like to raise a few points of concern from a strategic governance perspective regarding the request by Tempo.Vote for 380k ADA over six months. \r\n\r\nI do not dispute the importance of an independent infrastructure to ensure data integrity and not depend on a centralized provider. However, **the cost of the proposed infrastructure (200k ADA) is too high and far from the industry standard for similar blockchain node and backend indexing services.** We need to be more business-minded in our approach to treasury spending. We need to ask ourselves if this cost is realistic or if it is a slippery slope that will lead to the treasury being depleted without any accountability. Running a Cardano node and an indexer is not a walk in the park but it should not cost hundreds of thousands of ADA per month in fiat terms. **With a good developer earning about 120k USD per year, the 180k ADA development budget over six months is also something we should ask ourselves if it is justified. **Especially without a detailed list of deliverables that are directly linked to measurable results. \r\n\r\nThe insistence on withdrawing the funds in ADA instead of a stablecoin pegged to fiat currency is also adding a lot of volatility risk to the budgeting and treasury management. **The ADA price can have a huge impact on the actual value of the funds that are being allocated and that will undermine the stability and predictability of the treasury. A stablecoin disbursement mechanism would be a much better way to protect the treasury's purchasing power and to align it with the real-world operational costs. **\r\n\r\nTempo.Vote's desire to make governance more accessible is laudable and the feature roadmap (improving UX, optimizing governance voting, and innovating with a lending pool to facilitate governance action submissions) is promising. But we need to be careful and not let ambition take over. Without a detailed list of costs and performance metrics, it is hard to approve such a large withdrawal of ADA and that will erode the trust of the community and put the long-term sustainability of Cardano's treasury at risk.\r\n\r\n**I appreciate the contribution of Tempo and I have been using their platform over others. I must however firmly reject this proposal as it is. We are the guardians of a fixed and disinflationary treasury and we need to be prudent in our stewardship.** We cannot allow the treasury to be depleted with high infrastructure costs and withdrawals in ADA without any accountability. We need to demand responsible and transparent spending that protects Cardano's future and respects the scientific rigor of this protocol.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYKbS6RLYxkcyDB9cEeyYNwyYDreuzYgtdmABfcsMEfbx -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe 380,000 ADA seems to be reasonable for a service that supports the ecosystem’s governance backbone. As a user of their platform, I'm aware this is a tool that keeps Cardano’s decentralized vision alive. Running an independent node and indexer isn’t cheap, and developing new features takes resources too. While we don’t have a detailed cost breakdown, their estimates seem plausible for the scope of work. And given that I am here today voting using their tech, I'm willing to give them a chance given their good track record so far building Cardano voting tools.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Voice of the People",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DRepVoiceOfThePeople/VOP_Repo/refs/heads/main/VC20250710InfoTempo2025.jsonld -->\r\n# Voice of the People\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ecrj7jd9alaxumvm49hgng9rp239nda5ucegd05ndvxfqftwr9f`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFor now, I understand we should focus in one Governance tool, focusing funds in one.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Tempo%20BIA.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep Committee, have voted NO on the Budget Info Governance Action titled “Tempo for Cardano Governance – Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025”. While we recognise the value of alternative governance interfaces and the importance of user-friendly mobile voting experiences, we found this proposal too vague and underdeveloped to earn our support at this stage of the process.\r\n\r\nAs a Budget Info Action, this proposal serves as a signal of community support or rejection for potential future Treasury disbursement. From that lens, it is vital that proposals demonstrate a clear plan, responsible budgeting, and public accountability, none of which are sufficiently evident here. While we do support the listed upgrade features, the proposal lacks basic structural elements we believe are necessary for a credible signal to proceed, including:\r\n1. A transparent budget breakdown with justification for the ₳380,000 request (especially ₳200,000 for infrastructure),\r\n2. A timeline of development milestones,\r\n3. Public details about the development team or maintainers,\r\n4. Defined success criteria or measurable impact projections.\r\n5. Roadmap to open-sourcing the project and updating already existing features like demographic representation, etc.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, while Selfdriven is named as the administrative entity, there is no description of how treasury funds would be governed if this Budget Info Action were to lead to a Treasury Withdrawal. This raises concerns about execution oversight and the stewardship of public funds.\r\n\r\nGiven our DRep responsibility to help shape a high-trust, effective governance funding system, we cannot support proposals that fail to meet the basic standards of clarity, feasibility, and community accountability. Although we recognise the potential of Tempo.Vote and are open to supporting its future iterations, we encourage the proposers to return with a more robust, well-documented submission that the community can confidently evaluate.\r\n\r\nAccordingly, we have voted NO on this Budget Info Governance Action.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/17_tempodotvote2025.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe deposit lending protocol has the potential to generate transactions on the L1 while making governance more accessible. However, the budget seems high. I particularly struggle with the infrastructure costs of 200k Ada for only six months of operation. That seems significantly higher than it should be. I am abstaining from voting on this project's budget due to having mixed feelings about it. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/willpiam/drep/blob/master/vote_context/markdown/17_tempodotvote.md",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Tempo.Vote.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep casts a NO vote on the Budget Info governance action titled Tempo for Cardano Governance – Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep values the spirit behind Tempo. Its focus on independent infrastructure and commitment to creating smoother, mobile-first governance experiences is something we believe the Cardano ecosystem needs more of. That said, this particular proposal lacks the transparency and structure required for us to signal support at this time.\r\n\r\nThere is limited visibility into the team behind the project, no clear accountability framework, and no explanation of how Selfdriven will govern and report on the use of treasury funds.\r\n\r\nWe see the potential in Tempo.Vote, but cannot endorse this iteration. Yoroi DRep encourages the team to resubmit with a more transparent, community-accountable approach so the broader Cardano ecosystem can confidently evaluate and support it.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSNqv6mJoM7fJeZ2q8A8oQVKKWhXWM48BvZa8NQgxEVH8 -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Tempo for Cardono Governance - Maintenance & Development Budget for 2025\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote YES for the Budget, provided that the following points are included when withdrawing treasury funds:\r\n\r\n- Plans for open sourcing are included.\r\n- Further details on costs and a roadmap are provided.\r\n- There have been some concerns about Tempo's IPFS metadata, which will be largely unusable if Tempo removes the PIN. I would be happy if those concerns are reasonably alleviated in some way.\r\n- DRep filtering functionality (labeling of DRep, such as the following) -  By selecting about five filtering items, 1,000 DReps are narrowed down to about 10 or less. The delegator can click five times and then choose the DRep they like from these 10, so there is no need to observe all 1,000 DReps or check their social media.\r\n\r\nトレジャリー引き出し時に次の点が含まれていることを前提としてYESをBudgetに投票しようと思います。\r\n・オープンソース化の計画が含まれている。\r\n・費用のさらなる詳細とロードマップが記載されている。\r\n・TempoのIPFSメタデータについて、TempoがPINを解除した場合ほとんど利用不可能になることを懸念している声がいくつかありました。その懸念について何らかの手段で合理的に軽減されていると嬉しいです。\r\n・DRepフィルタリング機能 - フィルタリング項目を5つ程度選択することで、1,000件のDRepが10件程度以下に絞り込まれます。委任者は5回クリックするだけで、この10件の中から気に入ったDRepを選択できるため、1,000件すべてのDRepを観察したり、ソーシャルメディアをチェックしたりする必要はありません。",
      "vote": "YES"
    }
  ],
  "[OriLife × TonFarm] Identifying 180 Million Durians Without Physical Labels": [],
  "Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement": [
    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/2025IntersectBudgetWithdrawals.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis vote aligns with my Ekklesia votes, where I voted yes to the highest priority budget line items that fit within my preferred 200m ADA budget, abstained from voting on any line items that I may have had personal interests in, and voted no to everything else.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "$Khale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CFMatrix/Metadata-storage/refs/heads/main/BloxBean.jsonld -->\r\n# $Khale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ltat8kjqrmnff3lkkpxy0j5tn66d3m0gy64dc92asft5g6dl9ws`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter a thorough review of the “Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement” proposal, I am confident this is a strategically important initiative that directly supports the stability, usability, and growth of the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nBloxBean’s Java tooling is a critical part of the developer infrastructure, widely used by Cardano developers, explorers, and enterprise integrations. Maintaining and enhancing these tools ensures Cardano has a robust, production-ready set of Java libraries and developer kits that improve integration, adoption, and interoperability.\r\n\r\nKey reasons to support this proposal include:\r\n\r\nAlignment with Cardano Roadmap: \r\nThis maintenance work supports ongoing ecosystem development goals by improving tool reliability and compatibility with the evolving Cardano protocol and node upgrades.\r\n\r\nEcosystem Impact: \r\nReliable Java tooling reduces barriers for developers and enterprises building on Cardano, facilitating faster development cycles and enabling more sophisticated applications.\r\n\r\nDemonstrated Track Record: \r\nBloxBean has a proven history of commitment and contributions to Cardano’s development stack, indicating competence and reliability.\r\n\r\nReasonable Funding: \r\nThe requested amount (~₳99,600) is proportionate for the scope of ongoing maintenance and targeted enhancements, representing good value for sustaining essential infrastructure.\r\n\r\nTransparent Oversight: \r\nThe proposal includes milestone-based funding releases with delivery assurance and public reporting, ensuring accountability and effective use of funds.\r\n\r\nOverall, this proposal is a sound investment in Cardano’s developer ecosystem, promoting a robust and accessible toolchain that benefits developers, projects, and the wider adoption of the platform. I vote YES to approve the disbursement.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote12-50.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I voted for all projects in the 2025 budget vote based on a very simple principle:\\n\\n- Yes if I believe the long-term value to the Cardano ecosystem exceeds the requested amount;\\n- No if it doesn't;\\n- Abstain if I'm unsure.\\n\\nAll of my votes are consistent with [my position in the May 2025 Ekklesia round](https://2025budget.intersectmbo.org/voters/drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u).",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
