    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmVz9ZAPztFnUueXJFgs2TavrWbq5LNbi1cZPitEZ5PG5t -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmUTYyiqgMRcfFKfyPoF2JbTo2mXmU6EUkU3E3Ea4FSmpA\r\n\r\nVoting decision was made to be consistent with my reconciliation back in May 2025;\r\nhttps://2025budget.intersectmbo.org/voters/drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg\r\n\r\nReady to move forward overall with the budgeting process and look forward to a smoother process next year. I voted for a lower NCL overall (200M), however found in supporting things that we really ought to have funded to keep momentum in development and enhancements on-chain (supporting both open and non-open-sourced projects) I came a bit higher than that (250M+). \r\n\r\nWe will need to strike a balance in treasury withdrawels for projects that push development forward (and therefore the chains efficiency, performance, resiliancy, and seucrity) -- and businsess that wish to participate, of any size, and extend the capabilities and real-world use cases of Cardano.\r\n\r\nMy votes, I hope, align with my overall goal as a DRep to see continuous improvement in the ecosystem. https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/mr_cata_gov%20.txt",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Crypto_Oaj",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdYKgpTwXCBWxJitizJsujPyTqwp1BELRrmiAT81d5LzK -->\r\n# Crypto_Oaj\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwlmrm6ksc8sa5fdhm63prqve6hjzvghdc3053zwz6hyeg0ayhg2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmcctTsC4Pib8AHGwhEyYacHJsjfFjQyrm9JHzMp6cvazr\r\n\r\nAs a software engineer with over a decade of experience in the Java ecosystem—particularly in developing enterprise applications using Java and the Spring framework—I strongly recognize the strategic importance of BloxBean in the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nIn our GovCircle project, we actively use several of BloxBean's tools, especially Yaci and related libraries. Our hands-on experience has shown us that BloxBean has created one of the most practical, developer-friendly, and open-source SDKs available for building on Cardano. It significantly reduces the complexity for Java developers entering the ecosystem and covers many of the essential components needed to interact with Cardano infrastructure.\r\n\r\nHowever, as it currently stands, BloxBean is being maintained by a small team. The tools need further development, improved documentation, and broader support to meet the growing needs of the community. The requested funding will allow the team to onboard another full-time developer, which is essential for scaling the tools, addressing developer feedback, and engaging the wider Java community.\r\n\r\nSupporting this proposal is not just a matter of maintaining existing tools—it’s a strategic investment in onboarding Java developers from Web2 into Web3, especially into the Cardano ecosystem. Considering the massive Java developer base globally, enhancing BloxBean could play a critical role in Cardano adoption.\r\n\r\nI also want to highlight that the requested amount (₳99,600) is modest when compared to similar SDK/library initiatives in other programming languages. It's a cost-effective proposal with a high impact-to-cost ratio.\r\n\r\nLastly, I encourage my fellow DReps to vote in favor of this proposal. Not supporting BloxBean risks breaking the development pipelines of projects that rely on it—including ours. Strengthening this foundation will benefit the entire Cardano ecosystem by enabling broader, enterprise-level developer engagement.\r\n\r\nLet’s invest wisely in the tools that can bring more builders to Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
