    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/r/25/250812_bloxbean_50d5c6418b4a.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBloxBean’s Java tools - CCL, Yaci, Yaci Store, and Yaci DevKit - are core to JVM developers on Cardano. Funding one developer for 12 months keeps these libraries current with network changes, fixes bugs, improves performance, and lifts documentation. The work is open source, used across the ecosystem, and covered under the approved 2025 budget. I vote YES because this strengthens developer tooling and lowers upgrade risk.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTcyboiyB7oSKnmfp8n1iB3RMsoCT2Aq3MoSMY331GyZh -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this Treasury Withdrawal proposal.\r\n\r\nBloxBean provides critical Java libraries for building on Cardano—including CCL, Yaci, Yaci Store, and Yaci DevKit—which are essential for Java developers. This proposal seeks funding to hire one additional full-time developer for 12 months to maintain and enhance these tools.\r\n\r\nGiven its open-source nature and the strategic value of strengthening Java development capabilities in the Cardano ecosystem, I support this proposal.\r\n\r\n本トレジャリー引き出し提案に YES票を投じます。\r\n\r\nBloxBeanは、Cardano上でアプリケーションを開発するためのJavaライブラリ群（CCL、Yaci、Yaci Store、Yaci DevKit）を提供しており、Java開発者にとって不可欠な基盤ツールとなっています。今回の資金引き出しは、これらのツールの継続的なメンテナンス・機能強化を目的とし、1名のフルタイム開発者を1年間追加で雇用するものです。\r\n\r\nオープンソースの継続的な支援と、Java領域の開発体験の底上げという観点から、Cardanoエコシステム全体にとって戦略的に意義のある提案と判断し、支持を表明します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/39_BloxBeanJavaTools_20250722/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this treasury withdrawal proposal because it plays a crucial role in strengthening developer infrastructure on Cardano, particularly for the Java ecosystem. The BloxBean suite—comprising Cardano Client Lib (CCL), Yaci, Yaci Store, and Yaci DevKit—has long been indispensable for Java, Scala, and Kotlin developers building decentralized applications and services on Cardano.\r\n\r\n1. Ecosystem Diversity and Developer Accessibility\r\n\r\nSIPO believes that ecosystem inclusivity means not only growing the user base but also empowering a diverse array of developers. Java remains one of the most widely used programming languages in the world. Tools like CCL and Yaci lower the barrier for traditional enterprise developers to adopt Cardano, thereby driving wider adoption and integration.\r\n\r\n2. Critical Maintenance and Future Readiness\r\n\r\nGiven the rapid pace of Cardano upgrades—including Leios, Plutus V3, and smart contract improvements—keeping developer libraries up to date is not optional, but essential. This funding ensures one full-time developer can maintain compatibility, fix bugs, and respond to urgent needs without delays.\r\n\r\n3. Support for Local Devnets and Prototyping\r\n\r\nYaci DevKit is widely used beyond the Java community to rapidly spin up local testnets for experimentation and prototyping. This general utility enhances productivity across many teams and accelerates testing cycles.\r\n\r\n4. Open Source, Transparent, and Maintained by Trusted Actors\r\n\r\nSIPO values that these tools are open-source, maintained publicly, and led by Satya—a long-standing contributor now employed by the Cardano Foundation. Transparency, trust, and community support are guaranteed.\r\n\r\n5. Well-Scoped Budget and Oversight\r\n\r\n₳99,600 is a reasonable ask for a full-time developer over 12 months. Furthermore, the involvement of Intersect, a legal contract with CDH, and oversight mechanisms via 3rd-party assurance provide accountability and delivery guarantees.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nThis proposal represents a practical, low-risk, and high-impact investment in the Cardano developer ecosystem. SIPO sees this as a foundational piece for long-term success and robust multi-language development support.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、この資金提案に「Yes」を投じます。なぜなら、本提案はCardanoにおける開発者基盤の強化、特にJava開発者へのアクセス性向上において極めて重要な役割を果たすからです。BloxBeanが提供するCardano Client Lib（CCL）、Yaci、Yaci Store、Yaci DevKitは、Cardano上でのアプリ開発において長年にわたり欠かせない存在となっています。\r\n\r\n1. エコシステムの多様性と開発者アクセシビリティの向上\r\n\r\nSIPOは、Cardanoが真に包括的なエコシステムを目指すのであれば、ユーザー層だけでなく、多様な開発者層を支援すべきだと考えます。Javaは世界的に広く使われている言語であり、CCLやYaciのようなツールはJava・Scala・Kotlin開発者にとっての障壁を大きく取り除きます。これにより、エンタープライズ領域での採用も加速されます。\r\n\r\n2. 継続的な保守と将来への対応力\r\n\r\nCardanoはLeiosやPlutus V3など、継続的なアップグレードが行われており、開発ツールがそれに追従することは必須です。今回の資金は、専任開発者1名の雇用を可能にし、保守・バグ修正・セキュリティ対応を機動的に行えるようにします。\r\n\r\n3. ローカルネットワーク構築と迅速な検証環境の支援\r\n\r\nYaci DevKitは、Javaに限らず多くの開発者がローカルでCardanoネットワークを立ち上げてテストする際に使用されています。実証実験やプロトタイピングを高速に行えるツールとして、エコシステム全体の開発スピード向上に貢献しています。\r\n\r\n4. オープンソース・透明性・信頼できる開発者による運営\r\n\r\nこれらのツールがオープンソースであること、GitHubを通じた透明な開発が行われていること、そして開発リーダーであるSatya氏がCardano Foundationに所属していることは、信頼性の高い技術基盤である証です。\r\n\r\n5. 適切な予算規模と強固なガバナンス体制\r\n\r\n1年間で₳99,600という資金要求は、専任開発者1名に対するコストとして妥当です。さらに、IntersectとCardano Development Holdings（CDH）との法的契約、第三者保証者による進捗監査など、ガバナンスの仕組みが整備されている点も評価できます。\r\n\r\n結論\r\n\r\nこの提案は、開発者支援という観点から非常に重要で、リスクは低く、インパクトは大きいと判断します。Javaを含むマルチランゲージ対応の強化は、Cardanoがより強靭で普遍的なプラットフォームになるための基盤です。SIPOは本提案の意義と成果に大きな期待を寄せています。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVaUuUjQhRzQTYEYEErBPXbEv6wTe5gisCpTtK77Ys2ZV -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳99,600 for BloxBean Java Tools Maintenance and Enhancement\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious has voted in favor of all 39 Treasury Withdrawal proposals submitted. These proposals were selected through a well-defined process, and we fully support them out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
