    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳424,800 for Hardware Wallets Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qme8nUJGxhvkUurtJ7FdPHpzydaZfmhKtp4dUHnnUb2NR1 -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳424,800 for Hardware Wallets Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal funds ongoing maintenance and development support for key hardware wallets such as Ledger, Trezor, and Keystone, which are essential for maintaining compatibility and security as Cardano evolves.\r\n\r\nGiven the pace of innovation on the Cardano roadmap, having experienced contributors like Vacuumlabs—who have been involved in HW wallet integrations since 2018—is critical. The proposal includes legal contracts, milestone definitions, and third-party milestone verification mechanisms, which provide transparency and assurance of delivery.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I vote YES on this treasury withdrawal.\r\n\r\n本提案には Ledger・Trezor・Keystone など、主要なハードウェアウォレットの保守・開発支援が含まれており、Cardanoのセキュリティと機能互換性の維持に不可欠です。特に今後のCardano機能の追加や仕様変更への対応が求められる中、Vacuumlabsのような経験豊富なチームによる継続的な保守は、利用者とdApp開発者の双方にとって非常に重要です。\r\n\r\n法的契約・マイルストーン定義・第三者保証付きの進捗確認といった管理体制も整備されており、信頼性も高いと評価しています。過去のCardanoハードウェアウォレット統合経験（2018年から）に裏打ちされたVacuumlabsの技術力にも期待できます。\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、本提案に対してYES票を投じます。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/05_HardwareWalletsMaintenanceIntersect_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳424,800 for Hardware Wallets Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO casts a Yes vote on the proposal “Withdraw ₳424,800 for Hardware Wallets Maintenance administered by Intersect.”\r\n\r\nThis proposal requests ₳424,800 from the Cardano Treasury to maintain and upgrade hardware wallet integrations (Ledger, Trezor, Keystone) with the Cardano blockchain.\r\n\r\n1. Ensuring Security and Functionality for All Users\r\n\r\nSIPO views hardware wallets as a cornerstone of Cardano’s security model. Without up-to-date firmware and interface libraries, users may lose access to new features—or worse, lose access to their funds.\r\n\r\nThis funding ensures:\r\n\t•\tTimely updates of Ledger and Trezor firmware in line with Cardano protocol upgrades\r\n\t•\tMaintenance of cardano-hw-cli and interop libraries\r\n\t•\tDeveloper support for Keystone integration\r\n\t•\tThird-party code audits required by Ledger\r\n\r\nBy maintaining compatibility with hardware wallets, Cardano upholds accessibility and security for its users.\r\n\r\n2. Proven Vendor with Long-Term Commitment\r\n\r\nVacuumlabs, the vendor selected, has been contributing to Cardano’s hardware wallet integrations since 2018. Their development on LedgerJS, Trezor firmware, and cardano-hw-cli ensures continuity and technical depth.\r\n\r\nThe proposal also includes required third-party security audits, ensuring high code quality and compliance with vendor standards like those from Ledger.\r\n\r\n3. Transparent Contract and Oversight Mechanism\r\n\r\nThis proposal will be executed under a legal agreement with Cardano Development Holdings (CDH), managed by Intersect, and governed by:\r\n\t•\tMilestone-based delivery and payment validation\r\n\t•\tIndependent assurance of deliverables by third-party reviewers\r\n\t•\tAuditable use of funds via Sundae Labs’ treasury smart contract system, tested by TxPipe and MLabs\r\n\r\nAn Oversight Committee of five independent entities (Cardano Foundation, Sundae Labs, NMKR, DQuadrant, Xerberus) ensures no single party can act unilaterally.\r\n\r\n4. Proactive Investment in Cardano’s Infrastructure\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this as a forward-looking infrastructure investment. As Cardano evolves—Plutus upgrades, Hydra, Ouroboros Leios, or potential new key management models—hardware wallets must keep up to avoid ecosystem fragmentation.\r\n\r\nThis proposal preserves accessibility and usability for all ADA holders relying on secure self-custody options.\r\n\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nSIPO believes this proposal is a prudent investment in the invisible, yet essential, infrastructure that protects the Cardano user experience and ecosystem continuity. We therefore vote Yes.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、提案「ハードウェアウォレット保守（Intersect管理）」にYesを投票します。\r\n\r\nこの提案は、LedgerおよびTrezorなどのハードウェアウォレットに関する重要な保守作業とCardanoとの継続的な互換性を確保するために、₳424,800のトレジャリー資金を拠出するものです。\r\n\r\n1. Cardanoの基本的安全性と機能性の維持\r\n\r\nSIPOは、ハードウェアウォレットが提供するオフライン署名というセキュリティの中核機能が、Cardanoユーザーの資産保護において極めて重要であると認識しています。この提案は、以下の課題に対処するものです：\r\n\t•\tCardano側の新機能・変更（Plutusアップデート、入力出力構造の変更など）にウォレットが対応しないと利用できなくなるリスク\r\n\t•\tハードウェアウォレットが壊れたまま放置されると、ユーザー資産にアクセスできなくなる可能性\r\n\t•\tKeystoneなど第三の選択肢に関するサポート不足の問題\r\n\r\nこの提案により、Ledger、Trezor、Keystoneのサポートが一貫して保たれ、cardano-hw-cliライブラリやインターフェースも定期的に更新されます。\r\n\r\n2. 長年の信頼と実績を持つ開発チーム：Vacuumlabs\r\n\r\nVacuumlabsは2018年からCardanoのハードウェアウォレット統合を手がけており、Ledger/Trezor両方のアップストリーム開発にも携わっています。これまでの長期的な実績からも、品質と安定性が期待できます。\r\n\r\nまた、Ledger社の要件である「認定された第三者によるコード監査」もこの予算で包括されており、外部セキュリティ水準の担保も可能です。\r\n\r\n3. 法的契約・進捗保証・監査体制の整備\r\n\r\nIntersectによる管理体制も明確であり、以下の点が保証されています：\r\n\t•\tカルダノ開発持株会社（CDH）とベンダー間で正式な契約が交わされる\r\n\t•\t各マイルストーンの完了はコミュニティまたは第三者保証人が監査する\r\n\t•\tSundae Labsのスマートコントラクトによる予算のトラッキングと透明性が確保される\r\n\r\nこうした透明性とチェック体制が整っていることで、資金の不正使用や不達成リスクも抑えられます。\r\n\r\n4. Cardanoの未来に備えるための「保全インフラ投資」\r\n\r\nSIPOは、Cardanoの将来のアップグレード（Ouroboros Leios、Plutus v3、L2統合など）において、ハードウェアウォレットがボトルネックにならないよう備える必要があると考えています。\r\n\r\nその意味で、今回の提案は「直接目立たないが、不可欠な保全インフラ」への投資であり、全ADA保有者の基本的なUX（資産アクセス）を守るものと評価します。\r\n\r\n結論\r\n\r\nSIPOはこの提案が「目立たないが不可欠なインフラ」への投資であり、Cardanoの長期的健全性を支えるために極めて重要であると判断しました。よって、Yes票を投じます。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
