    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQV9W5nmUgQboga5XrcP6sseboQYDEhFcwcwgrFPUYKhT -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I voted YES for the proposal: Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n\r\nIn general, Cardano needs funding for builders. On-chain governance is cumbersome and not suitable for smaller fundings.\r\n\r\nThe Catalyst Foundation's (CF) takeover of Catalyst was received positively by the community, despite the cancellation of Fund15. I also see this transition positively, as a change of control over the project has the potential to result in necessary changes.\r\n\r\nCatalyst has been criticized for what projects were funded and how the voting system worked. It is necessary to make radical changes to the system and set new rules.\r\n\r\nI believe CF can implement these changes and make Catalyst a well-functioning funding vehicle.\r\n\r\nAn important aspect is the builders. They are waiting for payments for the work that has already been done within Funds 10-14. Funding was promised, so it is fair to continue distributing funds for completed milestones.\r\n\r\nAlthough the transition could have happened without this governance action, I appreciate CF for submitting and getting feedback from DReps.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbTUb9ddtALVH8g93uBsVQ2fg35yQkMGsU7dSdtXQe6oz -->\r\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is an aligned internal actions amongst father and mother of Cardano. The founding entities should resolve this quickly and regain trust from community (eps with fund 15 bad reputation)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/Info_29.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on this proposal because I believe the existence of an Innovation fund is important to the growth and success of Cardano.  Historically I have been frustrated with the lack of much-needed improvements to the Catalyst program and I am optimistic that improvements will be made under new management.  In particular I would like to see the ability to vote entirely via web/desktop without the use of a mobile app.  I'd like to drop the requirement for registration at all, though it could optionally be used to link wallets together so that you can vote only a single time with more than one wallet.  I'd like to fix proposal/text spam and quality, especially now in the age of AI.  I'd also like to see more specific categories that are laser-targeted at exactly the products and use cases Cardano most desperately needs.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigg4zrgde6lxnlvdrnaxnqvdctlz5nx2dzok6kxf7ybo4rimvcubi -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES on the Cardano Foundation taking over Catalyst. This is to ensure continuity for existing Catalyst funds (10–14). Not approving this is unnecessarily punitive to the past commitments already made and unfair to those projects.\r\n\r\nAs for Fund 15–16 being “unrelated” while also being mentioned. My read is: those funds are already committed to be returned (with Intersects Administration), and this proposal doesn’t change that—it just ensures there’s a clear operator in place to execute responsibilities cleanly.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Crypto Eats Legacy",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmf5kg7ktQNWoHL1cJqefmHnjxijS8r84qt79d9PTe4UzV -->\r\n# Crypto Eats Legacy\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytd2mf58tfqv78z7e99fy0gnmfep0kscclnwpvx7qvwpc5srxwg5g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis needs to keep going and CF is most appropriate to manage.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXtkJfJdccDtpJjCRcwxpTVL4PxbKgoaK1YkWaLGLeywB -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmcGfj1YFcyHFKneUsyqHkV58hhs8xffHaVjfvQUuzRS22\r\n\r\nI am voting **YES** on this Info Action to appoint the Cardano Foundation (CF) as the new managing entity for Project Catalyst. \r\n\r\nBefore addressing the administrative transition, I want to express my profound appreciation for Project Catalyst, its hard-working team, and its massive impact on our ecosystem. The innovation and Catalyst-funded tooling were exactly what inspired me to personally learn and build on Cardano. It has been a foundational pillar of our community's growth and onboarding.\r\n\r\nAs we enter this new phase, I also want to state my sincere appreciation for the Cardano Foundation stepping up to take on this massive responsibility. Ensuring operational continuity so that builders from Funds 10-14 receive their milestone payouts without disruption is critical for maintaining trust with the teams doing the hard work. \r\n\r\nFrom a fiscally conservative perspective, this transition is the most responsible path forward. Not only does it protect active builders, but it also secures CF's explicit commitment to return the previously approved allocations for Funds 15 and 16 directly back to the Cardano Treasury. This aligns perfectly with my mandate to enforce strict fiscal discipline and protect our treasury by recovering these unspent funds. A clean handover to CF honors Catalyst's legacy, protects our builders, replenishes our treasury, and provides a much-needed reset.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dr. Navjit Dhaliwal",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWUFDeXdAUmsCCCdKDnxPtSjSESp9zXG6UuixtC5FqZNz -->\r\n# Dr. Navjit Dhaliwal\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfya5pwcm2zw0e60c3pkqscq6spge7m0k6jtxkfsymv68gs2z56e5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI applaud CF for using governance and putting this to a vote.\r\n\r\nI want to make it clear however that Catalyst is a broken system and needs to be removed completely from Cardano governance. We need to pave way for KPI based proposals like CB DAO.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep.collective",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafkreif5v3pd2va2der3hni5khk2z3wbwp35kixmxsner5zemt33vkzscu -->\r\n# drep.collective\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydwtnlvdd8atlj5c5ylgw4kg5e640vyt8resattrjmwufyg4qclf7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote YES on approving the Cardano Foundation as the new managing entity of Project Catalyst.\r\n\r\nProject Catalyst has been a key pillar of innovation within the Cardano ecosystem, enabling early-stage ideas, developer experimentation, and community-driven growth. Ensuring its operational continuity is therefore of high importance.\r\n\r\nWe support the transition of management responsibilities to the Cardano Foundation and trust the Cardano Foundation to take on this role responsibly. As one of the core institutions within the ecosystem, the Foundation has demonstrated its ability to operate with a long-term perspective and in alignment with Cardano’s broader interests.\r\n\r\nFrom our perspective, this transition represents a pragmatic and necessary step to avoid disruption of ongoing projects and funding processes. We currently do not see any substantial reason that would argue against this change, especially given the urgency of maintaining continuity for existing grantees.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, we support this proposal.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
