    {
      "voter": "Phil UPLC",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmVa7Tuca61DZk8LEe7BNe425qHQYagypRw9QPyo3o9srg -->\r\n# Phil UPLC\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg343cyuckglj48a6gpcey7fkfcy5x5f9g65wme3ne9q2mgaedmkm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmbNV6mV4Thn7Fs8RsES64CzCE1bdCooGy4HRPJKiJiiW7\r\n\r\nI do not believe CF has the relevant experience to manage an ecosystem grant system. Their perspective on the primary markets for Blockchain is incompatible with years of demonstrated history and the current market reality. CF has always prioritized supply-chain tracking, decentralized identity, and web2 partnerships (FIFA, FC Barcelona, Dubai missile tracking, and so on) and indicated essentially zero interest in the DeFi market, or in marketing / assisting any of the DeFi projects building on Cardano. This is incredibly dangerous, as it ignores the current reality which is that practical all onchain activity in the blockchain space is in the DeFi market, that DeFi is the only market in the blockchain domain to achieve product market fit. CF will likely guide catalyst towards funding dead markets like web3 supply-chain tracking solutions, decentralized identity, and other non-DeFi focused funds, as opposed to focusing primarily on the existing market (DeFi) and having smaller allocations for experimental markets that have yet to achieve any success (blockchain supply-chain tracking, DIDs, and so on)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQfTACpAA1mgq2FbPnQVFA5SEemDWbnAuLjZVuRL7VFAX -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA supports this Info Action as a necessary step to ensure continuity and responsible administration of existing Project Catalyst commitments.\r\n\r\nThis proposal addresses an operational requirement rather than a strategic or funding decision. It enables the transition of Catalyst management from Input Output Global to the Cardano Foundation in order to maintain uninterrupted administration of Funds 10–14, including milestone reviews and payments to funded projects. Without this transition, Catalyst operations may face disruption, creating delays and uncertainty for active participants.\r\n\r\nWe consider this action to be a matter of stewardship and continuity. It does not introduce new funding, expand the scope of Catalyst, or define its future direction. Instead, it ensures that previously approved commitments are fulfilled in a timely and responsible manner.\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation is an established and capable ecosystem entity with relevant governance and operational experience. In the absence of clearly defined alternative managing entities within the required timeframe, we consider this transition to be an appropriate and pragmatic solution.\r\n\r\nImportantly, this approval should not be interpreted as endorsement of any future structure, funding model, or long-term governance framework for Project Catalyst. Decisions regarding the future of Catalyst remain open and should be addressed through separate governance processes with full community consideration.\r\n\r\nRCADA’s YES vote reflects support for operational continuity, responsible fund administration, and protection of ecosystem participants currently engaged in Catalyst-funded projects.\r\n\r\nRCADA’s full vote assessment can be found here: https://brolloks.github.io/rcada-drep-votes/",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rod G",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmcn7LN25vjER9QbQHrYqtkTTVoqL6aeNtBLowXrxoqHkM -->\r\n# Rod G\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwscks2yt0na4fqpcdyqn0fare5v48y0mjgn2g478lnx8gue393e`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGiven the cancellation of most recent Catalyst Funds, it seems that turning management of the fund to CF is the only way forward. \r\n\r\nThis ecosystem needs what Catalyst brings, so I hope CF will revise the fund and develop new, beneficial opportunities for the ecosystem.",
