    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZ7YxcKoa1VydEoLSM47P3zpAunT7WG566fQMUCWzs4mp -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI understand this proposal not as an initiative for new spending or expansion, but as a transition of operational responsibility to ensure the proper continuation and completion of existing Project Catalyst activities.\r\n\r\nIn particular, ensuring continuity in milestone reviews and payments for projects under Funds 10–14 is critical. Avoiding operational disruption or delays is important from both a reliability and accountability perspective, and this proposal provides a reasonable path to achieve that.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, this proposal does not introduce new treasury outflows, but rather concerns a change in the managing entity within an already approved framework. Therefore, it does not impose additional financial burden on the Treasury.\r\n\r\nAt the same time, I believe that the overall effectiveness and future direction of Project Catalyst should be evaluated separately. This proposal should be understood as a measure to fulfill existing obligations, rather than an endorsement of Catalyst’s long-term design.\r\n\r\nTaking these points into account, I support this proposal from the perspective of maintaining operational continuity and fulfilling existing commitments.\r\n\r\n本提案は、新たな支出や拡張を目的としたものではなく、既存のProject Catalystにおける未処理の業務や資金配分を適切に完了させるための運営体制の移行であると理解しています。\r\n\r\n特に、Fund 10〜14における既存プロジェクトの進行および報酬支払いの継続性を確保する観点から、運営主体の不在や遅延を避けることは重要であり、そのための対応として本提案は一定の妥当性を有していると考えます。\r\n\r\nまた、本提案は新たな資金拠出を伴うものではなく、既に承認された枠組みの中での管理主体の変更である点において、トレジャリーに対する追加的な負担を生じさせるものではありません。\r\n\r\n一方で、Project Catalyst自体の有効性や今後の在り方については、別途検討されるべき重要な論点であると認識しています。本提案はあくまで既存の責任を適切に履行するための措置であり、Catalyst全体の評価や将来の方向性とは切り分けて考える必要があると考えます。\r\n\r\n以上を踏まえ、現時点では運営の継続性および既存義務の履行を優先する観点から、本提案を支持します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreideubnrrjwmos5b2eye5tqbe2cy7egeh4dgmdl6d4z3743k4uykhm -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep and co-founder of Cardano Ghana, I support this proposal to ensure continuity and stability in Project Catalyst. Approving the transition from Input Output Global to Cardano Foundation prevents delays in milestone reviews and payments for Funds 10–14, protecting builders and ongoing projects. This change follows established governance structures and ensures a smooth, accountable handover. A YES vote safeguards the Cardano Treasury, supports responsible management of legacy funds, and maintains trust across the ecosystem. Most importantly, it avoids disruption while the community continues shaping the future of decentralized governance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab Testing DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmTZQEsSq5UzvhaXmsqzDha1jxMPukEkDvAbkz1gZ6QsLu -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab Testing DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjrttn43cyz6sde85shqvl33k22ynjxx85j2h6h5ns42tqafqudl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\ntesting GA",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifek3oynhrgcuulap2kk7ns7kaokmozwt4q3ybzlr5sdiixu5u7qi -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep votes YES on Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst.\r\n\r\nThis Info Action is a necessary governance step to ensure continuity of Project Catalyst operations. With IOG stepping back from its administrator role, the Cardano Foundation is the only viable entity positioned to assume management of the Catalyst Foundation Company (CFC) and protect the 500+ active projects currently awaiting milestone reviews and fund disbursements.\r\n\r\nWhy SIPO votes YES\r\n\r\n1. Protecting 500+ active projects is the immediate priority\r\nProject Catalyst has distributed over $150 million across 2,200+ projects since inception. More than 500 projects from Funds 10-14 are currently active with outstanding milestones and pending disbursements. Without a legitimate administrator for the CFC, there is no legal entity authorized to approve milestones and release funds. Delaying this transition directly harms builders who are relying on committed funding.\r\n\r\n2. There is no alternative candidate\r\nIOG has signaled its withdrawal from the Catalyst administrator role. This is not a choice between CF and another entity — it is a choice between CF and a governance vacuum. If not approved by end of May 2026, Catalyst operations face an undetermined pause with no clear path to resumption.\r\n\r\n3. CFC statutes legally require community approval\r\nThe Catalyst Foundation Company was designed with a governance safeguard: any change of administrator must be validated by the Cardano community. This Info Action fulfills that requirement. It is a procedural necessity, not a policy endorsement of any particular vision for Catalyst's future.\r\n\r\n4. CF is institutionally appropriate for this role\r\nThe transition from a product organization (IOG) to a mission-driven Swiss nonprofit foundation (CF) reflects the maturation of Cardano's governance. CF has already begun onboarding Catalyst team members to ensure operational continuity.\r\n\r\n5. Fund 15/16 Treasury return is accelerated by approval\r\nCF has committed to working with Intersect to return the Fund 15/16 allocations (18.5M ADA + 250K USDM) to the Cardano Treasury as quickly as possible following approval.\r\n\r\n6. Future Catalyst direction remains under DRep governance\r\nApproving CF as administrator does not lock in any model for future Catalyst rounds. Under the 2026 Budget Process Framework, future Catalyst funding will need to be proposed through Intersect's budget process and approved by DReps.\r\n\r\nExpectations\r\n\r\n- Expeditious milestone administration: Clear the backlog of milestone reviews and disbursements for Funds 10-14 without further delay.\r\n- Transparent reporting on transition progress: Regular updates on timeline, team onboarding, and operational readiness.\r\n- Fund 15/16 Treasury return timeline: A concrete timeline, not an open-ended commitment.\r\n- Catalyst redesign with community input: Meaningful consultation on future direction, addressing regionalization risks (governance capture, fragmentation, cultural bias).\r\n- Avoiding excessive role concentration: CF assumes multiple governance roles (Catalyst, Orion Fund, ecosystem steward). Clear separation of responsibilities and transparent accountability for each.\r\n- CFC governance accountability: The same transparency, reporting, and oversight standards demanded of all treasury-funded operations.\r\n\r\nThis is not a vote about the future design of Project Catalyst. It is a vote about ensuring 500+ active projects receive their promised funding and the transition proceeds without a governance vacuum.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO DRep votes YES.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSIPODRepとして、本提案「Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst」に賛成（YES）を投じます。\r\n\r\n本Info Actionは、Project Catalystの運営継続を確保するために必要なガバナンスステップです。IOGが管理者の役割から撤退する中、Cardano FoundationはCatalyst Foundation Company（CFC）の管理を引き継ぎ、500+のアクティブプロジェクトを保護できる唯一の実行可能な主体です。\r\n\r\nSIPOがYESと判断する理由\r\n\r\n1. 500+のアクティブプロジェクト保護が最優先\r\nProject Catalystは2,200+プロジェクトに$150M以上を分配。Fund 10-14の500+プロジェクトが現在マイルストーンと資金支払いを待っています。正当な管理者なくしてマイルストーン承認と資金放出の権限を持つ法的主体は存在しません。\r\n\r\n2. 代替候補が存在しない\r\nIOGは撤退中。CFかガバナンスの真空かの選択です。2026年5月末までに承認されなければCatalyst運営は不定期停止に直面します。\r\n\r\n3. CFC定款が法的にコミュニティ承認を要求\r\n管理者変更にコミュニティ承認を要するガバナンスセーフガードの履行です。手続き上の必要性であり、将来の方向性への政策的是認ではありません。\r\n\r\n4. CFは制度的にこの役割に適切\r\nプロダクト組織（IOG）からスイス非営利財団（CF）への移行はCardanoガバナンスの成熟を反映しています。\r\n\r\n5. Fund 15/16のTreasury返還が承認により加速\r\nCFは18.5M ADA + 250K USDMの返還をIntersectと協力して迅速に行うと表明しています。\r\n\r\n6. 将来のCatalystはDRepガバナンスの下に残る\r\nCF管理者承認は将来のモデルを固定しません。2026年予算フレームワークの下で将来のCatalyst資金はDRep承認が必要です。\r\n\r\n期待事項\r\n\r\n- Fund 10-14のマイルストーン審査・支払いバックログの遅滞なき処理\r\n- 移行進捗の透明な定期報告\r\n- Fund 15/16 Treasury返還の具体的タイムライン\r\n- 将来のCatalyst再設計におけるコミュニティ協議（地域化リスクへの対応含む）\r\n- CFの複数役割（Catalyst・Orion Fund・エコシステム）における責任分離と透明な説明責任\r\n- CFC Treasury資金に対する受託者責任の維持\r\n\r\nこれはCatalystの将来設計についての投票ではなく、500+のアクティブプロジェクトを保護しガバナンスの真空を防ぐための投票です。\r\n\r\n以上の理由により、SIPO DRepとして賛成（YES）を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZ1BPJKMysMZmkYAL3wjhDTZwqwFooThzptxn9NdxCS13 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nProject Catalyst is one of the largest decentralized grant programs in the blockchain industry, having funded over 2,200 projects with more than 500 still active. Continuity of operations for these active grantees is paramount. The transition of the Catalyst team from IOG to the Cardano Foundation ensures that existing commitments are honored, milestone payments continue, and grantees are not left without administrative support.\r\nThe Cardano Foundation is a non-profit entity whose mission is explicitly focused on the long-term stewardship and adoption of the Cardano ecosystem. Moving Catalyst management from a commercial entity (IOG) to the Foundation aligns the program’s governance structure with its public-goods purpose. This separation also strengthens the argument for Cardano’s decentralization from a regulatory perspective, as the funding mechanism is no longer directed by a single private company.\r\nThe decision to pause Fund15 and Fund16 and return unallocated ada to the treasury demonstrates responsible capital management. Rather than continuing to deploy funds through a system undergoing structural transition, the Foundation is choosing to stabilize operations first and redesign the process before committing new capital. This is a sign of governance maturity.\r\nThe transition also creates an opportunity to address long-standing community criticisms of Catalyst, including concerns about accountability, the impact of funded projects, and the need for independent audits. The Foundation has signaled a more rigorous, high-assurance approach to grant administration, which should improve the quality of funded projects and strengthen community trust in the program.\r\nBoth IOG and the Cardano Foundation support this transition, and community forums show active discussion and broad acknowledgment that change was needed. Voting YES enables a smooth handover that protects existing grantees, strengthens governance, and positions Catalyst for a more transparent and accountable future under Foundation stewardship.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmeNxiAAjirFM89ku9m26sNqhd3UzuPh6MTsZQRH8CRMt7 -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote YES. The CFC's governing statutes require a community decision to transfer management to a new Administrator, and without one by end of May, fund disbursements to teams delivering on Funds 10-14 face an uncertain pause. Supporting continuity for those builders is the right call.\r\n\r\nWe do want to note that the communication surrounding the Fund 15 and 16 pause fell short. Proposers invested significant time preparing submissions in good faith, received little explanation mid-process, and were left without clarity for an extended period. We acknowledge that, and we expect Cardano Foundation to carry that lesson into how it manages the programme going forward.\r\n\r\nCatalyst has produced real value for the ecosystem and has also accumulated real lessons about process design, accountability, and what a public funding mechanism should optimize for. We see this transition as an opportunity to act on those lessons rather than carry forward the patterns that didn't work.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SudoScientist",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arpradio/drep/refs/heads/main/catalyst_cf-handover.jsonld -->\r\n# SudoScientist\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wtls7xh3a8gyepk540dgtzjzalk086gp4www6y0k0xjmqyk6gma`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEnsuring funds that have already been promised are disbursed is the function the results of such action would result in.  Therefore, I believe it is in the Cardano community's best interest to fulfill these commitments, without yet determining the future of Catalyst as a funding mechanism.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "This Corrosion",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXSKLLCBhPKx8xZ1DV9VrTLUE2uz1Q75oCyPmWy7ymnrM -->\r\n# This Corrosion\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytkzpmmukjy6qn6xd5skqm0ypcj5juw9rxddr5mmlzgjvtcghwqjr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNew manager, new ideas. Seems good.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TNT",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreig6fcc2ydj5itz7mejvnvt6e3bt7ksla62ffdwiaiysufaepkznzu -->\r\n# TNT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc0skj7ceaszyvpte75h4xrw0m6wcenj0kd2uj7lkq5vmcjryeec`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIf IOG proposes it and the Cardano Foundation accepts, they will have a good reason",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmS823e3ZKymA1ov5a6ifVCbCoUBTiXySAqpHbECSjGbKU -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes on this proposal.  While I have concerns about how well the Cardano Foundation reflects the best interests of Cardano, Project Catalyst is too important and shouldn't be disrupted.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbWFcqbP99cq6veFqdmoNbGeMMYZdS3BXKhcY1uFgtqRT -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFrankly, **the proposal reads more like “please prevent a mess” than “here is a compelling, high-performance operating model.”** I do not like being presented with that kind of asymmetry. It is a **sign of truly weak governance craftsmanship**.\r\n\r\nI vote \"Yes\", because I judge this to be a necessary continuity action. I do not find the case elegant, complete, or particularly impressive; I find it under-argued and overly reliant on urgency. But I would rather approve an operationally necessary administrator transition than risk avoidable paralysis in Project Catalyst. **My support is pragmatic, not enthusiastic: We are not rewarding excellence here; we are preventing governance failure.**",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYKMxNN86htzYyEfPqpkit5kNb3isuhKAgFfHeav8j6tL -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation's info action seeking community approval for transitioning the Catalyst processes demonstrates genuine respect for the community. I strongly approve this step forward for our ecosystem's most vital funding mechanism. I also recognize the numerous challenges and shortcomings in the current Catalyst model. At the same time, I have observed the Catalyst team's consistent efforts over the years to iterate, refine, and improve the system. \r\nI hold high hopes for this evolution and place my trust in the Cardano Foundation to execute the transition thoughtfully and effectively, in the best interest of the entire ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeHrk9Rgg5e8xtQEWTjEh2Bb1Tsc7M2H1MVKk6tWLuH9f -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTransferring stewardship from IOG to the CF will help ensure continuity and long-term sustainability of community funding. Lately, the Cardano Foundation has delivered several clear wins for the community including strong governance progress, successful startup accelerator partnerships supporting 70+ projects, new developer tools and challenges, cross-chain liquidity improvements (such as USDCx), and effective enterprise adoption initiatives. I believe they are well-positioned to run Catalyst efficiently going forward.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Viet_Cardano_Community",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXj8pxUJnLPwHyMgADssbRRW4UkwrEpitt2SNrpauHHSw -->\r\n# Viet_Cardano_Community\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygpzpm4q38rfueu2use5te4ylykn4smvs7cxj2ggvktcjkqpxhvf4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVote YES for this proposal because Catalyst needs an organization capable of operating more transparently and effectively than the previous group. The community expects that the operational capability of the Cardano Foundation will enable Catalyst to function efficiently and better support ecosystem growth.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibrjfpw45lc3zhjczw7dzqie7o75ht6j6ok2frvdm5qgkjn6qvg2y -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Wada DRep, we vote yes on the proposal to approve the Cardano Foundation as the new managing entity of Project Catalyst. Our support is grounded in the immediate need to ensure continuity of operations, particularly for ongoing commitments under Funds 10 - 14. At this stage, maintaining the integrity of existing grant agreements, ensuring timely milestone reviews, and preventing disruption to disbursements are critical to preserving trust in Cardano’s funding ecosystem. Given the statutory requirement for community approval to effect this transition, we consider this proposal a necessary step to avoid operational uncertainty.\r\n\r\nWe recognise the Cardano Foundation’s institutional capacity to assume this role and appreciate the intention to facilitate a smooth transition from IOG without interrupting active processes. The narrow scope of this proposal; focused purely on operational reassignment rather than expansion or additional funding, also provides clarity and reduces the risk of unintended commitments. Additionally, the stated intention to work toward returning unused allocations for Funds 15 - 16 to the treasury reflects alignment with broader ecosystem priorities around fiscal responsibility.\r\n\r\nThat said, our support should not be interpreted as a blanket endorsement of the current structural framing of Catalyst governance. The proposal leaves several important areas underdeveloped, particularly regarding transition execution details, accountability mechanisms, and long-term governance design. There is limited clarity on how the handover will be operationalised, what performance expectations will be placed on the new managing entity, and how the community can effectively monitor and evaluate this role over time. Furthermore, the absence of a clearly articulated framework for oversight, reporting, and potential future transition pathways introduces risks of continued centralisation under a different entity.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Will Norris",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihz2noe2c4kq74uds2wh2ibioskvhlyr6area3aojge7xkzpj6v3m -->\r\n# Will Norris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuufvd6maykgfcp20fxgpx7g6a9z2suchqehfejwdsx8cgpx80yg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this proposal as a necessary and pragmatic step to ensure the continuity of Project Catalyst operations. The transition of the managing entity from Input Output Global to the Cardano Foundation is required under the Catalyst Foundation Company’s statutes and helps prevent disruption to ongoing Fund 10–14 project delivery and payouts.\r\n\r\nThis action does not introduce new spending or alter governance structures but instead safeguards existing commitments and protects the integrity of the ecosystem. It aligns with the principles of accountability and responsible stewardship outlined in the Cardano Constitution.\r\n\r\nWhile broader improvements to Catalyst’s effectiveness and impact may still be needed, maintaining operational continuity is the correct and responsible course of action at this stage. For these reasons, I am voting YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiasjxf3u3o2benu3paqhp5v3frrc376hi7akgbmyc7pdaxloh5h3u -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Voting against the proposal to *Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst*\r\n\r\n## Summary \r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation wants to run Project Catalyst going forward. \r\n\r\n## Statement\r\n\r\nAbsolutely not. Catalyst should either be shut down or given to Intersect. Why should we give that responsibility to the CF? We don't even have a single community elected member on the board. \r\n\r\nSigned, <br/>\r\nWilliam Doyle\r\n\r\nYour friendly neighbourhood DRep! <br/>\r\n$computerman <br/>\r\ndrep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt <br/>\r\nhttps://x.com/william00000010 <br/>",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YOADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaaobddgfmnkgqv2pmrrqnrys5cssqkenvsv6hrkdfqquwi3bu2am -->\r\n# YOADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Approve Cardano Foundation as New Managing Entity of Project Catalyst\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26sfka2km0p4xw073ujdq406wxxczhdyfh9vw7yxpfselchzkdjn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCardano foundation is the perfect entity in our ecosytem to take the lead on this feature.",
