    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA039-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"Sim\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlpvhtd5td), pois a carteira Eternl é a mais completa e utilizada do ecossistema Cardano; financiar esse grupo de desenvolvedores é essencial para a melhoria contínua desta ferramenta, promovendo sustentabilidade, usabilidade para os usuários e garantia de inovações no produto. Além disso, a justificativa de gastos apresentada, bem como as métricas de avaliação e controle, foram bem apresentadas.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"Yes\" on this governance action (gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlpvhtd5td), because the Eternl wallet is the most complete and widely used in the Cardano ecosystem; funding this group of developers is essential for the continuous improvement of this tool, promoting sustainability, user-friendliness, and ensuring product innovation. Furthermore, the expense justification presented, as well as the evaluation and control metrics, were well presented.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "punkr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXYg13XXYA2zP8pxrjEq7G1vgT6YwsyQ59ujivM45cgoc -->\r\n# punkr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfyl9j6amk940g76r7ujnn5gywnjenv3kmun3a5tr5a83psl4vv64`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted in favor of the Eternl Maintenance treasury withdrawal. Eternl is one of my preferred Cardano wallets, and I believe its continued support is essential. However, I had some reservations due to its closed-source nature, which I consider a significant drawback.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYW514iM696Eq84Jjob51nXfgSR6mzsxheKEuDCHjtMo2 -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nEternl has been a reliable and feature-rich Cardano wallet since the early days of the ecosystem. I personally use it regularly and appreciate its accessibility across web and mobile platforms.\r\n\r\nMaintaining core infrastructure like this is essential for both users and developers. This proposal clearly outlines its operational needs and contributes to a more stable and accessible ecosystem.\r\n\r\nI support it.\r\n\r\n私はこの提案に Yes を投じます。\r\n\r\nEternlはCardano初期から存在する信頼性の高いウォレットであり、Web・モバイル両対応の多機能なUIは、私自身も日常的に利用しています。\r\nこうした基盤ツールの安定運用は、ユーザーと開発者双方にとって不可欠です。\r\n\r\n本提案は、その維持コストを透明に提示しつつ、継続的なサポートを実現しようとするものであり、エコシステム全体の利便性向上に直結すると判断し、支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/18_EternlMaintenance_administered_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports the ₳583,000 treasury withdrawal for the maintenance of Eternl, a long-standing, reliable, and community-driven Cardano wallet.\r\n\r\n1. Critical Infrastructure for Cardano Users\r\nEternl is a multi-platform wallet supporting web, extension, iOS, and Android. Since 2021, it has served as a trustworthy entry point to the Cardano blockchain for both developers and users. Maintaining this access point is critical to ensuring a robust and inclusive user experience across the ecosystem.\r\n\r\n2. Proven Track Record and Community Trust\r\nOver its four years of operation, Eternl has earned wide recognition for its responsiveness, feature richness, and active community support. It plays a vital role in user retention and adoption, especially in regions where mobile-first access is essential.\r\n\r\n3. Transparent Contractual Oversight by Intersect\r\nThe proposal includes a formal off-chain legal contract between the vendor and Cardano Development Holdings, administered by Intersect. Milestone-based payments, third-party assurance, and detailed on-chain auditability via Sundae Labs’ smart contracts ensure accountability and transparency.\r\n\r\n4. Aligned with Cardano’s Constitutional Treasury Framework\r\nThis proposal is one of 39 items aligned with the ₳275M budget approved under Intersect’s constitutional Info Action. The process complies with Article IV Sections 4 and 5 of the Constitution, including safeguards like Oversight Committee verification and verifiable treasury disbursement workflows.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nSIPO believes this funding is essential to sustain an open-source wallet that many ADA holders depend on. We commend the structured governance, technical oversight, and ecosystem value the proposal delivers.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、Eternlウォレットの保守継続のために申請された₳583,000の国庫引き出し提案に賛成票を投じます。\r\n\r\n1. カルダノユーザーに不可欠なインフラ\r\nEternlは、Web、ブラウザ拡張、iOS、Androidなど複数のプラットフォームに対応するウォレットであり、2021年以降、多くのユーザーと開発者にとってカルダノへの入り口となっています。このようなアクセス手段を維持することは、エコシステム全体の利便性と包摂性を確保する上で極めて重要です。\r\n\r\n2. 実績とコミュニティからの信頼\r\nEternlは4年間にわたり、機能性、信頼性、コミュニティ対応力に優れたウォレットとして評価されてきました。特にモバイルアクセスが主流の地域では、ユーザーの利用定着に貢献しており、カルダノ採用の裾野拡大に寄与しています。\r\n\r\n3. Intersectによる透明な契約・管理体制\r\n提案には、Intersectが管理するCardano Development Holdings（CDH）との正式なオフチェーン契約が含まれ、マイルストーンごとの支払、第三者による検証、Sundae Labsのスマートコントラクトを用いたオンチェーン監査可能性が確保されています。\r\n\r\n4. 憲法に則った財務プロセスとの整合性\r\nこの提案は、Intersectが進行する₳275M規模の予算措置の一部であり、カルダノ憲法第IV条第4・5節に準拠しています。Oversight Committeeによる検証や分配過程のトレーサビリティも担保されています。\r\n\r\n結論\r\nSIPOは、Eternlのようなオープンソースウォレットの継続的支援が、ADA保有者とカルダノ・エコシステムの健全な発展に不可欠であると判断しました。本提案が示すガバナンス体制と技術的透明性を評価し、賛成票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVaUuUjQhRzQTYEYEErBPXbEv6wTe5gisCpTtK77Ys2ZV -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious has voted in favor of all 39 Treasury Withdrawal proposals submitted. These proposals were selected through a well-defined process, and we fully support them out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZbhsZyRkKZHuSvqPwHTfzyopHWtT8znUrhcWcjvVK3yR -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEternl is a key user-facing infrastructure component of Cardano and remains one of the most widely adopted wallets across platforms. However, the closed-source nature of the product and the absence of long-term sustainability pathways raise red flags for us.\r\n\r\nWe acknowledge Eternl’s work, and our approach is to abstain on proposals that may have strong community backing but don’t yet present clear strategic value or sufficient delivery confidence. For supporting future treasury requests, we’d like to see either a plan to open-source core components, or a clear long-term sustainability pathway.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Terminada",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TerminadaDrep/vote-contexts/refs/heads/main/20250725/005.jsonld -->\r\n# Terminada\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytf9f78k7rkwk4cu6l2nvna22keu9yus4kqzc0hqspd36uszu0xc2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEternl can either remain proprietary and fund itself through subscription fees, advertising, and other business revenues, or it can commit to fully open source its code and request community funding.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXdumXdRfa3Cr8HyzQbi8ASS9UAvvEyZqi579kTEGdGen -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA couple of months ago, I supported the resolution to bundle all of the Intersect Budget Proposals into 1 or 2 formal on-chain governance votes.\r\n\r\nEach of these proposals has already undergone extensive scrutiny and received 50% or greater support from the active DReps in the ecosystem, and I will honor that prior decision and the work these prospective developers have put in by voting yes on all the proposals from the Intersect Budget team.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQJCW8aKqk5iPm1Tt6LHCerTMJpbRcM8NS3XTvASoTFTu -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting No. While Eternl is a popular wallet, this proposal primarily funds operational costs rather than development or innovation, raising concerns about whether Treasury resources are being used sustainably. Additionally, Eternl is not open-source, limiting transparency, community contribution, and long-term decentralization. Treasury funds should prioritize open, collaborative infrastructure and foundational tooling that directly supports ecosystem growth—this proposal does not meet that standard.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmdeez51eTPRzEHZjAiT9Bhsw8Skt3Rhi3Z9sKeBc5LU39 -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile Eternl’s multi-platform presence and community-driven nature are commendable, the proposal lacks a compelling articulation of unique value or innovation that justifies dedicated ongoing funding at this scale. The Cardano ecosystem already supports several wallets, including Lace (IOG-backed) and others, which have significant user bases and development momentum. The critical question remains: how many wallets does Cardano need to maintain publicly from treasury funds? Wallet proliferation risks fragmenting developer and user attention, diluting network effects, and increasing maintenance overhead.\r\n\r\nThe proposal does not provide a comparative analysis against existing wallet solutions, nor does it address whether coordination or consolidation efforts have been explored to optimize resource allocation. Without such strategic alignment, funding Eternl in isolation risks duplicative expenditure and missed opportunities for synergy. Given the ecosystem’s need for robust, scalable infrastructure, treasury funds should prioritize projects with clear, differentiated impact and collaborative frameworks.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmS6SksRQnZF57DHBc7twxChgisoNoXsVSDNzJnQ8oQm7N -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEternl has proven to be a reliable wallet over the years, and its contributions to the Cardano ecosystem are undeniable. However, allocating such a substantial amount to a single wallet seems disproportionate when our ecosystem benefits from a diverse range of wallets. I would prefer supporting a more balanced distribution of ADA across the top 5-10 wallets, for instance. Additionally, before endorsing this proposal, I would require further clarification, such as details on any revenue generated by the app that could offset the proposed 30k ADA monthly cost.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmdc3asqbeRBrpQspDXT64dtHmuW23LWjR32TrpwBwERHV -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nEternl is a trusted, community-driven wallet serving ~100,000 Cardano users with secure, multi-platform access to DeFi, staking, and governance. Its €30,000/month maintenance ensures reliability, complementing Lace’s IOG-funded model. While Lace leverages IOG’s resources, Eternl’s independent status necessitates treasury support to cover operational costs, sustaining ecosystem diversity and user choice. With Intersect’s transparent oversight, this investment drives adoption and dApp innovation, offering strong ROI for Cardano.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Intersect_TWGA18.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳583,000 for Eternl Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: This is a general rationale we have prepared to support our “yes” vote on all the 39 treasury withdrawal actions. This follows careful review and consideration of the metadata of these treasury withdrawal proposals and hence is not a blanket voting practice.\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep Committee, have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawal governance actions currently live on-chain and submitted under the administration of IntersectMBO. These actions are the necessary implementation step following the community's approval of the ₳275.3 million Cardano Ecosystem Budget, the necessary budget info action that precedes the treasury withdrawal process. Our support reflects not only continuity with our earlier \"yes\" votes on the overarching budget info action and its constituent proposals but also our confidence in the smart contract guide and project execution mechanisms Intersect has established as an administrative body for these proposals.\r\n\r\nEach of these 39 withdrawals corresponds directly to proposals that have already passed a respective Budget Info Action with wide community and DRep support of 64.23%. As Wada DRep, we reviewed, scored, and supported many of these initiatives during the budgeting phase, using our internal ₳280M Net Change Limit framework. Our endorsement of the full ₳275.3M package was not a blanket approval but the outcome of detailed deliberation. Therefore, we see it as our responsibility to honor those community-approved funding decisions by affirming these follow-up Treasury withdrawal governance actions.\r\n\r\nImportantly, we are confident in Intersect’s role as the administrator of these treasury disbursements. We have independently reviewed the Smart Contract Guide, disbursement architecture, and accountability structures associated with these withdrawals. The use of milestone-gated smart contracts, multi-signature treasuries, and on-chain/off-chain tracking mechanisms provides strong assurance of transparency, risk management, and community accountability. We are particularly satisfied that Intersect has adopted security-audited contract templates and provides public documentation on how treasury funds will be administered, paused if necessary, and even returned if unused.\r\n\r\nIn our view, rejecting or abstaining from these Treasury Withdrawals at this stage would risk destabilizing delivery timelines, undermining community trust, and introducing administrative conflicts that may violate the spirit of the Constitution’s Articles on budgeting. We believe that treasury funding is not just about allocation; it’s about consistent and credible execution. As such, the DRep role requires continuity and follow-through, especially when prior voting outcomes have clearly mandated action.\r\n\r\nTherefore, in alignment with our constitutional responsibilities, community-aligned decision-making, and our assessment of Intersect’s administrative protocols, we have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawals Governance Actions.",
