    {
      "voter": "FAIR Pool #01",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRr9a6FypVYfX8ez68TBJXDPG69Hat6VP2kdpEMA3D74A -->\r\n# FAIR Pool #01\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytamqncvuz2r0atkwxwgcn5zmgxm09j0g2lgcrp7ddqfsfcsgnr8s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted yes, consistent with my prior positions in the 2025 Cardano Budget Reconciliation.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Florian Volery",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcXpixKFLXfeBLWLfms4EqQKD3oPdqm2fBbD2UdUBNP6X -->\r\n# Florian Volery\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yguh6dsgx0g58v8pqmxgfrkq0x8vfv6tcp92uzzjrykwy8cjmelsy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs with all Intersect-related governance matters, I believe such initiatives should originate from individuals who have been elected on-chain. I would support this type of proposal—but only if it comes from legitimately elected representatives.\r\n\r\nAll committees should undergo reform to ensure transparent governance, with onchain elected members who present a clear strategy and corresponding budget.\r\n\r\nIn line with this position, and for the sake of consistency, I am voting NO on this proposal.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdwxjAuDJD7vq2CqJD1Pa6KjZYpSbjXmdm6GUp2zUWZEY -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI think this is unnecessary spending to deliver something that does not require the expense asked for.\r\n\r\nCardano has had a longstanding vision that has yet to be realized, and there is already plenty to deliver on that has been previously promised.\r\n\r\nBoth GAs and budgets will shape the future direction of Cardano, and this is not something that requires $750,000 ADA to decide.\r\n\r\nThat ADA could be better spent on projects that will deliver something to improve Cardano and realize the vision and promises already made to the Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWsBB4u8bPx694p2gTC9oy1VVLY4ZRfWxyLCkDU4QJFjS -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this proposal because:\r\n\r\n* Cardano needs a 2030 long-term vision and an annual roadmap shaped by the community, rather than continuing to follow only the founders’ vision.\r\n* This is the first structured, ecosystem-wide product research effort, aiming to identify real user needs, development barriers, and strategic priorities.\r\n* It will be executed by Intersect’s Product Committee, with independent oversight, legal contracting, and transparent results.\r\n\r\nInvesting in strategic research helps Cardano grow effectively and avoid wasting resources on misaligned efforts.\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nTôi ủng hộ đề xuất vì:\r\n\r\n* Cardano cần một tầm nhìn 2030 và roadmap hàng năm do cộng đồng định hình, thay vì tiếp tục phụ thuộc vào tầm nhìn của những người sáng lập.\r\n* Đây là lần đầu tiên có một quy trình nghiên cứu sản phẩm bài bản và quy mô toàn hệ sinh thái, nhằm xác định nhu cầu người dùng, rào cản phát triển, và hướng ưu tiên chiến lược.\r\n* Dự án được thực hiện bởi Ủy ban Sản phẩm của Intersect, có sự giám sát độc lập, hợp đồng pháp lý rõ ràng, và công khai kết quả.\r\n\r\nViệc đầu tư vào nghiên cứu chiến lược giúp Cardano phát triển hiệu quả, tránh lãng phí nguồn lực vào các hướng không phù hợp với nhu cầu thực tế.\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nJapanese\r\n-------------------------------------------\r\nこの提案に賛成する理由は以下の通りです：\r\n\r\n* Cardanoには、創設者のビジョンに依存し続けるのではなく、コミュニティ主導で策定された2030年の長期ビジョンと毎年のロードマップが必要です。\r\n* これは、Cardano全体で初めての体系的なプロダクトリサーチの取り組みであり、ユーザーの本当のニーズ、課題、戦略的優先事項を明らかにすることを目的としています。\r\n* このプロジェクトはIntersectのプロダクト委員会によって実行され、独立した監査、法的契約、および透明性のある成果報告が行われます。\r\n\r\n戦略的なリサーチへの投資は、Cardanoの持続的かつ効果的な発展に繋がります。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUzQCCB6VRWhX14BnrcPDNynrdr6M4RVtRvogrndgrgV7 -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFollowing the previous vote on Ekklesia.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HOSKY",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPajxPxfboMCYdC322KxLhhPASGjDWHua3bcn62bhSkgP -->\r\n# HOSKY\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf2jzhuc4f7eu2yay9d9ta3dykxxcwn34wz8kak7nhd7vcgrxn7ns`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSupporting this proposal advances Cardano’s long term health by replacing the founder set roadmap with a process owned by the community. This is fully in line with the HOSKY DRep Platform’s commitment to decentralization by giving a diverse range of stakeholders direct influence over Cardano’s strategic direction.\r\n\r\nThe initiative invests in structured research across the ecosystem, addressing a critical gap in understanding user needs, market opportunities, and barriers to adoption. This supports HOSKY’s emphasis on real world adoption and solving meaningful problems rather than speculative or vanity projects.\r\n\r\nOversight is built into the execution through audited smart contracts, independent third party assurance, and a multi signature governance model. This ensures fiscal conservatism, transparency, and accountability, which are core tenets of HOSKY’s governance philosophy.\r\n\r\nBy funding this work, the treasury supports an inclusive and evidence based vision that strengthens Cardano’s decentralization, scalability, and sustainability while protecting against waste and centralization risks.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I will vote YES on this proposal.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmciFkL5crohozaTMZFwVCErZdBrotLaEzqYSX3FvXEA97 -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will keep the rationale brief for expediency - as 38 proposals were submitted concurrently by Intersect today. I voted YES for this proposal in the previous Ekklesia temp check and will vote YES now again. \r\n\r\nThis proposal helps bridge two probably important goals. Ensuring a decentralized approach to developing Cardano further, while also maintaining core competency and experienced oversight through the Cardano Product Committee. As they say themselves,  we need an \"open, shared, and transparent process for the Cardano community to define a long-term vision and a roadmap\". Thumbs up.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_750k-Product-Committee-2030-Vision.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted in favor of this action to demonstrates my intention to execute without delays and move the treasury expenditure process forward. I also want to note that I will not seriously consider individual requests from the treasury for less that 1,500,000 ADA moving forward.  I reserve the right this round because I feel the process was not properly explained to proposers and DRep and it would be unfair to implement this personal guardrail at this time. Requests below that threshold are better suited for Catalyst funding or bundled together in MBO, DAO, or conglomerate entities.  TWA (Treasury Withdrawal Actions) need be comprehensive and not ad hoc as that makes oversight more costly and inefficient.\r\nA budget and all included line items has already been approved, and now is the time to disperse funding and enable further development of the Cardano network. The proposal was selected through a well-defined process, and I will fully support it out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community and a belief in respecting the consensus we achieved together under the Intersect-administered budget process. The process reflects a coordinated, strategic approach to funding Cardano’s ecosystem-critical infrastructure. The community has thoroughly reviewed the proposal. I was actively involved in the entire process and the proposal presented represents development that provides a tangible benefit to our ecosystem.  It would be a mistake to underfund our ecosystem’s development when we can sustainably provide the required funding with our available treasury reserves.\r\nFurthermore there are exceptional oversight mechanisms in place to ensure a minimum amount of wast, fraud, and abuse of treasury expenditures, such as Intersect’s smart contract framework (audited by TxPipe and MLabs), Multi-party oversight (including Cardano Foundation, Sundae Labs, NMKR, etc.), A clear milestone-driven disbursement model, and full transparency via TRSC/PSSC dashboards.\r\nThese governance and assurance systems meet the constitutional standards for accountability and risk management and provide confidence in efficiency and execution.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "JuanTheOne",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifw7gswe7xvxuxaxwqtoszzeqh5emhjptewrjw7um2wg7f2wdmv5i -->\r\n# JuanTheOne\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳750,000 for Cardano Product Committee Community-driven 2030 Carda\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf2yjggxr26kalsp3l4wutdf05s3ayxjg5gyaylp2hf4gegwceav4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDisclosure: As a voting member of the Product Committee involved in drafting this proposal, I recognize my role and affirm my rationale as transparent and aligned with ecosystem benefit.\r\n\r\nThis proposal addresses the gap left by the founder-led roadmap, enabling a community-driven vision and living roadmap beyond Voltaire. It consolidates scattered insights into a structured, data-driven process that informs builders, SPOs, and governance. Through inclusive participation, third-party assurance, and transparent auditing, it ensures accountable delivery. At ₳750k, the budget is modest relative to its ecosystem impact, offering strong value in shaping Cardano’s product-market fit and long-term direction.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
