    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳243,478 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Plutarch\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaZ1QujExvKQygka1JQsxt3Sqeyh4iSK8sKtiH7ou3EjM -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳243,478 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Plutarch\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nPlutarch is a widely used, production-grade eDSL in Haskell that plays a vital role in Cardano smart contract development. Maintaining and enhancing this tool is essential to ensure a stable, efficient, and forward-compatible development experience across the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nMLabs has a strong track record in this domain, and the proposed budget is reasonable given the ongoing value Plutarch provides to developers and toolmakers.\r\n\r\nSupporting this proposal ensures that the Cardano developer community continues to benefit from reliable and evolving infrastructure. I support it.\r\n\r\n私はこの提案に Yes を投じます。\r\n\r\nPlutarchは、HaskellベースのeDSLとしてCardanoのスマートコントラクト開発に広く利用されている重要な基盤ツールです。開発者にとっての利便性が高く、またPlutusと密接に関係するツールであるため、継続的な保守と機能強化はエコシステム全体の健全性に直結します。\r\n\r\nMLabsはこの分野で長年実績を積んできた信頼あるベンダーであり、過去の貢献からも品質と継続性への信頼が持てます。金額も比較的コンパクトで、費用対効果が高いと判断します。\r\n\r\nPlutarchの継続的発展は、開発者体験の向上とdAppsの品質向上につながるため、本提案を支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/15_MLabsCoreTool_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳243,478 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement Plutarch\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports the proposal titled “MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement: Plutarch” because it directly contributes to the health, resilience, and innovation capacity of the Cardano smart contract ecosystem.\r\n\r\nPlutarch is a production-grade eDSL (embedded domain-specific language) in Haskell, widely used by Cardano developers for building robust, type-safe smart contracts. As a foundational tool, it must be maintained continuously — especially during network upgrades and hard forks — to ensure developers have access to secure, up-to-date infrastructure.\r\n\r\nThis proposal, submitted by Intersect on behalf of MLabs, addresses critical needs including:\r\n\t•\tRegular bug fixes and compatibility updates for Plutarch\r\n\t•\tFeature enhancements based on real developer feedback (e.g., GitHub issues)\r\n\t•\tEnsuring alignment with the pace of protocol innovation\r\n\t•\tSupporting both core teams and new dApp builders with a reliable development stack\r\n\r\nSIPO recognizes that without sustained funding, even essential tools like Plutarch may degrade, undermining developer productivity and ecosystem growth. MLabs, a trusted and capable engineering partner with proven expertise (e.g., in Cardano.nix and budget contract audits), is well positioned to deliver this work.\r\n\r\nThe proposal is also supported by Intersect’s smart contract-based treasury governance system, including audit-backed disbursement and milestone-based accountability with oversight from independent third parties such as the Cardano Foundation, Sundae Labs, and others.\r\n\r\nIn short, maintaining Plutarch is not just a technical necessity — it is a strategic imperative for sustaining the quality and velocity of decentralized application development on Cardano.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、「MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement: Plutarch」という提案に賛成票を投じます。本提案は、カルダノ・スマートコントラクト開発に不可欠な基盤ツール「Plutarch」の維持・強化に直結するものであり、開発者の生産性やエコシステム全体の健全性を支える戦略的施策です。\r\n\r\nPlutarchは、Haskellで記述された本格的なeDSL（組込みドメイン特化言語）であり、型安全性と生産性を兼ね備えたスマートコントラクト開発を可能にします。このツールは、開発者の間で広く採用されており、その継続的な保守はカルダノの技術進化にとって必須です。\r\n\r\n本提案は、以下の課題とニーズに対応しています：\r\n\t•\tプロトコルのアップグレードやハードフォークに対応するための互換性維持・バグ修正\r\n\t•\tGitHub等を通じて寄せられた開発者の声に基づく機能拡張\r\n\t•\tdApp開発者にとっての開発環境の信頼性・効率性の確保\r\n\t•\tコアツールの品質保持によるエコシステム全体の成長支援\r\n\r\n資金を要する継続的メンテナンスが行われない場合、Plutarchの陳腐化は開発効率の低下を招き、ひいてはCardano全体の競争力低下につながります。SIPOはこれを重大なリスクと見なし、早期の対応を支持します。\r\n\r\n本提案は、Intersectのガバナンスフレームワークを通じて、以下の体制で実行されます：\r\n\t•\tMLabsによるプロジェクト遂行（Cardano.nixや監査実績を持つ技術集団）\r\n\t•\tSundae Labsによるスマートコントラクトベースの予算管理\r\n\t•\tCardano FoundationやNMKR等、外部独立団体による監視と評価\r\n\t•\t各マイルストーンでの成果物提出とコミュニティ可視化\r\n\r\nSIPOは、Cardanoの開発者支援体制の持続とツールチェーンの健全性維持が、カルダノ2.0の実現に向けた土台であると考えています。\r\n\r\nこの提案への賛同は、開発者体験とプロトコルの進化を両立させるカルダノの将来を支えるものです。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
