    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/gov_action10lty9xka3unprtvdfrqvcjgsz33sjwhv9p06afqzar8au782trtsq7dhd95.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIncreasing K: \r\n- Increases the number of effective stake pools on the network, increasing decentralization. \r\n- Causes multipools to go over maximum saturation, forcing their delegated ADA to spread out to already existing, smaller, single pools. \r\n- Multipools are hosted on centralized cloud services, so they won't double their number of pools as it would also double their operational costs. \r\n- Allows a0 to become more effective for smaller pools who can't afford millions of ADA in pledge.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tulibra1510/shouldincreaseK/refs/heads/main/shouldincreaseK.jsonld -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe abstained from voting on this governance action because we have not seen any clear benefits from increasing the K parameter. Additionally, we have not seen how the current K parameter negatively impacts the system.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardaFlow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CardaFlow/Cardano-GovTool/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# CardaFlow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIncreasing k parameter has been extensively discussed by the community, IOG and CF between 2022 and 2023, together with the proposal to decrease MinPoolCost. Increasing at least k parameter to 1000 may stimulate SPOs diversity and encourage further decentralization, while being safe in term of impact on the protocol.\r\n\r\nAs a Drep focused on safe guarding Cardano decentralization, I am strong supporter of this proposal !",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/info_3.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn the short term, I believe raising k will shake up stake and hopefully increase decentralization, so will vote yes.  However, I also think that k is currently ineffective. K represents the target number of stake pools and is set to 500, but there are over 3k stake pools.  Additionally, it measures POOLS, not OPERATORS.  The latter is more important for decentralization.  Raising it will punish saturated single SPOs, but will hopefully add more new SPOs.  Long term I think a new RSS is needed.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ptrdsh/notes/refs/heads/main/Cardano/DRep/003-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRaising k damages the stability of the ecosystem in many ways, but the primary reason is operational resilience of block producing nodes. With a larger k, the profitability of running a pool goes down, as the total epoch rewards remain the same, but are distributed to a larger set of block producers. At the same time, running a node doesnt get cheaper, meaning the majority of pools have even tighter margins than they already have, leading to a decrease in quality of node setups (cheaper).",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00003_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe oppose increasing the k parameter, as it would only raise Cardano’s operational costs without adding any real value. The Cardano mainnet has been running stably, securely, and with sufficient decentralization for over four years.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmYdD37tP89aRhhh8tqKAgjga4fWjzzB3owwXG9NCBdjz5 -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe action is poorly written and supporting links leave impression of pure promotion stunt without profound rationale.\r\n\r\nI don't believe that changing stakePoolTargetNum (\"k\") would help small stake pools much. The stake that will have to move due to this is limited and often managed by entities that can just open additional pools.\r\n\r\nMoreover, I am not sure if Cardano can even sustain 500 pools, let alone 1000.\r\n\r\nFinally, I believe we need a totally different, better reward sharing scheme.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://coffeepool.jp/voting/rationale_info_K20241016.json -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFor parameter changes, we must not make Yes/No decisions without objective indicators. This GA disregards the requirements of the research process and attempts to engage in a discussion about Yes/No without that foundation. If the question were “Should we discuss parameter changes?”, I might consider saying Yes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
