    {
      "voter": "intertreeJK",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmdFkhJ6X5sqR9nGQrjQJf2nvogzLQpf3UgULLvqnyesaN -->\r\n# intertreeJK\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfkg5ryqwaleunwqg0dtcj8g8yw8sgd9kskg2zlzdr8355gpghcvv`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am FOR the increasing of the K Parameter as there are already over 1,000 SPO Pools that contribute Blocks to the Chain on a semi regular basis today, and being able to help guide Stake to be more evenly spread among them will, I believe, aid with the sustainability of those 1,000+ Pools. Potentially helping to increase the Cardano MAV Score.\r\n\r\nI also think we need to test higher K On-Chain to have real world insight into latency issues it may cause. K can be reduced if it turns out not to suit.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_increaseK.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting no on this info action, because I don't believe K should be adjusted in isolation.  This has been done before and did not achieve the desired results, futhermore without also addressing a0 and minPoolFee at the same time would not provide an efficient solution.  K, a0, and minPoolCost work dynamically together to regulate nOpt (desired number of pools) and thus all prams effecting nOpt should be taken into account in the adjustment on one.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/10NOV2024-dhd95/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIn the matter of the proposed “Should k be increased?” Info Action, I vote ABSTAIN — supporting the proposer’s stated goal of increasing governance participation while reserving judgment on the substantive question of changing the k parameter. I look forward to a thorough exploration and discussion of this important question with the Cardano Community.\r\n\r\nFull rationale: https://github.com/cardanoesq/votes/blob/e597015d154527143986083ec87268b01711222e/Voting%20Rationale%20dhd95.pdf",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/K%20parameter%20Info%20action.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nInfo action regarding the K parameter is noted.\r\nThere is more to be considered regarding changing this.\r\nRef: Pledge, MinFees just to mention some.\r\nLooking forward to the debate regarding changing K parameter",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
