    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/master/vote_context/3_increaseK.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Should K increased\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I do think it is wise to increase K, this action provides no details about how much to increase K by. This leaves me, as a DRep, in a precarious situation; if I vote YES, it may indicate to delegates that I am in favor of moving K to 1000 immediately after change 2, which I am not. However, if I vote NO, it may indicate that I do not approve of any increase in K, which is also false. My current thinking is that we should adjust K slowly, increasing it by no more than 100 each quarter.",
