    {
      "voter": "Christopher Erckert Dotare",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPLSfn3RywwmaJL8tjh53ugxS2MDcRS2yYLbJetsQz4hD -->\r\n# Christopher Erckert Dotare\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg8aktnf09gdd0jpyhuz3fy22mfjrqrg2ru52907zeeeeqcra6xhe`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I support the growth of DeFi on Cardano, I believe treasury funds should not be used to artificially bootstrap liquidity. Sustainable liquidity comes from real demand, utility, and user participation.\r\n\r\nCardano’s ecosystem is still evolving. As DeFi protocols mature and Bitcoin integration expands, I expect liquidity to increase naturally without the need for short-term subsidies.",
