    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmTCcGFePdy1Cx4YWrC73fTHFiYYUqffeqfmA9dCyQE9rA -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting No on this governance action because it was submitted with invalid metadata and the proposers already said that they are planning to submit another action with correct metadata. If the proposal would have been technically correct, I would have tended to vote Yes since providing liquidity for stablecoins seems to be one of the less wasteful uses of treasury ADA to me and the proposers are qualified to execute that plan in my opinion.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmerBfn5ncVjsUUcD5E9tkEbBPYaemwsZfAv6mwpz2oZ5J -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI abstain from this vote as the proposers have indicated on social media that they intend to resubmit the proposal with some changes or adjustments to it.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_50M_DeFi_liquidity.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting no on the 50 million for DeFi liquidity due to significant concerns regarding its financial scope, governance structure, and overall feasibility.  The request for 50 million ada is exceptionally large, specifically with regards to the current active NCL (Net Change Limit) and community approved treasury expenditures. Such a substantial allocation of community funds is not justified by the proposal's contents, which lack clearly defined goals and key performance indicators (KPIs). Furthermore the reliance on a basic multi-sig wallet instead of a more secure and transparent smart contract-based solutions introduces too many fundamental weaknesses in its financial planning, oversight structure, and technical implementation.\r\n\r\nThis is all in addition to the most pressing issue of an accompanying invalid metadata anchor.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/08JUN2025-5lauu/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote No on the proposed “Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget” Info Action (Governance Action ID: gov_action1fpqwxp2kxvnntr8hpkh9q9djm78ccdww7qlhg5safugh4stmcwzqql5lauu). As a threshold matter, this on-chain Governance Action is not identical to the final off-chain version of the proposed action as required under Article III, Section 5 of the Cardano Constitution.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/yk6ddn7j -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting NO because the plan asks the treasury to sink 50 million ADA into fiat-backed stablecoins without even specifying which ones.\r\nToday Cardano's native stablecoin market is tiny—about $23 million total and almost all USD-pegged tokens.\r\nBacking only dollar coins would tether our ecosystem to U.S. monetary policy and concentrate regulatory risk, \r\nwhile monthly conversions of ADA to fiat could still pressure the price. \r\nThe scheme returns just 15 % of the yield to the treasury and puts principal at the mercy of smart-contract exploits or a stablecoin de-peg.\r\nA small, fully on-chain pilot—say 5-10 million ADA, \r\nmulti-currency, milestone-gated, with instant claw-backs—could test the \"sovereign-wealth\" idea safely. \r\nUntil such a scoped proposal appears, the prudent move is to preserve treasury funds and let open-market demand grow stablecoin liquidity organically.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kit Willow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmbme3C3Bp6SwiCJbfQWaNsSuvEznGaUYgKeBSaaktqC1D -->\r\n# Kit Willow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygk7qax0ztrv7a7unzgs4apj5mhk5a0058ne3fgfftj4tmgvuk5a7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI like the idea behind this info action. Indeed, the Cardano ecosystem is truly in need of an organization to drive the much needed liquidity to Cardano DEFI. \r\n\r\nHowever, while I recognize the presence and efforts of some respected and active community members in the community, I am voting NO on this proposal because there was no adequate strategy of how the solution will be implemented presented. Also, the proposers did not include a breakdown of budget and costs on how the requested 50,000 ADA will be utilized to execute this proposal. \r\n\r\nPS: As long as the vote is still open, my stance could change if I see evidence containing the resolution of the issue I have stated with this info action.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/10/invalid_meta.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on this proposal because of the invalid metadata. We cannot rely on a governance info action where the data is altered after submission. I expect the proposal to be resubmitted so that I can evaluate it again on its merits (not data integrity).",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kenerik/KryptoLabs/refs/heads/main/withdraw%20for%20stableCoin.jsonld -->\r\n# KryptoLabs\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nKrypto Labs as DRep votes NO on the Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget. A robust stablecoin ecosystem is organically built through community adoption and developer innovation, not by deploying treasury funds. The inherent yield generated from fiat-backed stablecoin reserves represents a perpetual income stream. Diverting this significant, long-term benefit to commercial entities without a substantial, independent stake in the Cardano ecosystem is fiscally irresponsible. This proposal risks subsidizing external ventures at the community's expense, rather than fostering genuine, self-sustaining growth within our decentralized finance landscape.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
