    {
      "voter": "Lourde",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LourdeP/DRep-Public-Votes/refs/heads/main/Data%20not%20available%20Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Lourde\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygtvnwgsucstvesms2hv9vc8hw3tye5zhzldmszrxqd2rxsje5c6m`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nABSTAIN until corrected at source\r\n\r\nData Not Verifiable\r\nThe data that was originally used when this Governance Action was created has changed.\r\n\r\nGovTool uses external sources for Governance Action data, and these sources are maintained by the proposers of the Actions. This error means that the data stored by the Proposer does not match the data when the Governance Action was originally posted.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0010 -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on this proposal.\r\n\r\nWhile I am fundamentally supportive of the objective — increasing DeFi liquidity on Cardano — there are procedural and substantive concerns that warrant a negative vote.\r\n\r\nFirst, there is a clear and definitive violation of Article III, Section 5 of the Cardano Constitution. The on-chain hash does not match the off-chain governance content. Procedural compliance is critical for maintaining the legitimacy and enforceability of governance outcomes. Allowing proposals that fail such basic checks would weaken trust in the system we are collectively building. Some might argue, that this is the CCs Job, but I won't vote yes for what I believe is unconstitutional to begin with.\r\n\r\nBeyond the procedural issues, although I support the concept of using treasury funds to catalyze DeFi liquidity, I believe the scale of the request — 50 million ADA — is too large for an initial deployment. A pilot-sized deployment would provide a valuable proof-of-concept. I understand going too low might not make any impact at all, so I hope there are some reductions to be made and for the project to validate its concept.\r\n\r\nI appreciate the design of the proposal’s governance structure. Creating a dedicated committee to manage funds is a positive step toward more specialized and efficient decision-making. I think this is the way to go in my personal opinion. The idea aligns with a concept of a “DAO of DAOs” — potentially enabling individuals to directly propose initiatives within specific governance domains. This is a governance evolution Cardano needs to foster for greater agility and effectiveness.\r\n\r\nIt appears likely that the proposers will resubmit after correcting the formatting and hash issues. I encourage this and would welcome a revised proposal that maintains the strong core ideas while addressing procedural compliance and adjusting the initial scope to a more conservative pilot phase.\r\n\r\nVOTE0010",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Marketing DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdT6iJ36KtrhBXmU68c3eePBxBjwiGSNCnJrYyzXQqHWs -->\r\n# Marketing DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23kumvpqgal3t6v4tamwrprjya453p3djam0eqg63usm9su77hjl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI applaud community initiatives focused on supporting increased liquidity on Cardano. Per the submitter, there is an updated version of this proposal being submitted so I am voting no on this version.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Maureen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPWhRCFPt7CU3qjW2AtcjJhTAm3ArU6KVdZJPjmQ5N1eV -->\r\n# Maureen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y22hlaj8wuyygpnjy5cf96tg9tgvjrz39kxvqgv898uj9scfc55t7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFirst off, Kudos to the proposers. I know how hard they work in the ecosystem and I really do respect the energy and thought that went into this. It’s clear they care deeply about Cardano and about pushing DeFi forward in the right direction.\r\nThat said… I’m voting no. Not because the idea is bad. Actually, I think it’s quite solid. But fifty million ADA is still… well, fifty million ADA. That’s a big number. A number that deserves a second, third, maybe even a fourth look. Especially with so many other proposals and ideas in motion, this just feels like bad timing. If the budget was smaller or rolled out in phases, I’d probably feel different.\r\nI also think we need a bit more clarity around transparency and who gets access to the funds. The team looks strong, no doubt about that. But strong teams still need strong guardrails, especially when you’re asking for 50m ada.\r\nSo I’m saying no, but it’s a soft no, not a slammed door. I hope they come back. I hope they tighten a few things, maybe ask for less, and I’d love to see this evolve into something the whole community can rally behind.\r\nMuch love to the team. \r\nI’m rooting for you. Just not voting yes this time.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmUnfPHSJwzwsjxN9nWRXPg5NXjL7AQH7TBV4tSaihTcqK -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting **NO** on the governance action \"Cardano Treasury DeFi Liquidity Budget\" (gov_action1fpqwxp2kxvnntr8hpkh9q9djm78ccdww7qlhg5safugh4stmcwzqql5lauu) due to significant concerns regarding its financial scope, governance structure, and overall feasibility.\r\n\r\nThe request for 50 million ada, which represents over 14% of the current Net Change Limit, is exceptionally large. Such a substantial allocation of community funds is not justified by the proposal's contents, which lack clearly defined goals, key performance indicators (KPIs), and a tangible projection of the return on investment for the treasury. Committing this amount of ada without a clear measure of success or benefit presents an unacceptable level of risk.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the governance framework outlined is insufficient. The reliance on non-binding \"info actions\" for crucial decisions is concerning. It proposes placing a considerable amount of ada under the control of a committee without robust accountability mechanisms or the rigorous oversight for withdrawals mandated by the Cardano Constitution (Art. IV, Sec. 2). This structure fails to provide adequate safeguards for the responsible management of treasury funds.\r\n\r\nThe proposal also suffers from several practical and technical shortcomings. The justifications provided for the very large budget are not compelling. Additionally, there is a metadata hash mismatch, the proposed timeline is vague and lacks detail, and the reliance on a basic multi-sig wallet instead of exploring more secure and transparent smart contract-based solutions is a missed opportunity for enhanced security and accountability.\r\n\r\nIn its current form, the proposal has too many fundamental weaknesses in its financial planning, oversight structure, and technical implementation. It requires a comprehensive revision to address these critical issues before it could be considered a responsible use of treasury resources.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
