    {
      "voter": "Big Lazy Cat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://doc.biglazycat.com/drep/d2db60c5307cb517c735e2d0138d2b6f10fc5b221d610fa187719bdc82af9a03_0.jsonld -->\r\n# Big Lazy Cat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffcjs0njfea09xhs6up429rhya5pxd7qz7hvmwq6vqy2nczwpj3g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI appreciate the importance of GovTool as a core governance platform for Cardano, and I recognize the value of keeping it actively maintained and updated. However, the requested withdrawal amount feels quite high for a 12-month period. It might be helpful to provide more detailed transparency on how the budget will be allocated, or consider whether a smaller phased budget with regular progress reviews could achieve the same stability while ensuring efficient use of treasury funds.",
