    {
      "voter": "Blockjock (James Meidinger)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreicefg2ozblle42zf55idtdxnppezdadxb7e2vigvgkypu3eunc4u4 -->\r\n# Blockjock (James Meidinger)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnypzfv2v8fmfelthahvn0rqyh54sf6z2aa5m7f3fkjgqqt8l2qq`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGovTool is the backbone of Cardano governance — open-source, community-owned, and the lowest barrier for ADA holders to register, delegate, propose, and vote.\r\n\r\n🔹 Keeps governance open and decentralized, not captured by private tools\r\n🔹 Direct treasury withdrawals with oversight = real progress in treasury maturity\r\n🔹 Clear budget, milestone-based, unused funds return to treasury\r\n🔹 Expands DRep functionality + liquid democracy features\r\n🔹 Built as a public good, maintained by an open consortium\r\n\r\nVoting YES means strengthening the one toolset that guarantees participation stays accessible to everyone.\r\n\r\nOne caveat though, this tool should show progress towards ease of use, lowering the barrier to understanding and using this tool in every iteration in th future. It should incorporate those things other tools are using, that give added utility to the user or it risks being made irrelevant. Keep Up:-)",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BTBF_XSP",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTWbA1kabJyfHD2YwKBjGfcFzX5xssnzFTKJCYW5qxkr8 -->\r\n# BTBF_XSP\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2vyrqh0fa4qh4tmy7322va6ryk78uh6szppezaft0watyqp5hdwx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this proposal as it will revitalize community governance.",
