    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreig5hk5gyxytp6qrdtvzg4vhbcqvkb4tpm6f6sjswwz7t7oqiyg6ea -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n賛成票。GovToolはカルダノのガバナンスを支える公共インフラとして不可欠であり、分散性とOSS性を維持する上で本資金は妥当と判断します。特にDRepの活動を強化する機能拡張と、余剰資金をトレジャリーに返還すると明記している点を高く評価し、支持します。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nYes. GovTool is essential public infrastructure for Cardano governance, and this funding is justified to preserve decentralization and open-source values. I especially value the planned features that strengthen DRep activities and the explicit commitment to return unused funds to the Treasury, which reinforces transparency and accountability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSwR1CCdaBKiptEr9XwkkSkE2ksmiXpVn7c3Q9Gc5kRQe -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe used Govtool in the first phase of our on-chain governance. More governance tools for the community are needed. I vote YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardaFlow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmX6V6CC5konMxG6TtZJK6mryEAQGUUauscTM5HsS6ijGi -->\r\n# CardaFlow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough withdrawal may seem excessive, maintenance and improvement of such open source foundational piece of Cardano decentralized governance is a must.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9oNWukyULxL5R44kZhXR9EJ8KcdSMtmRr5nmrauqV8k -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile GovTool remains a valuable public good for Cardano governance, the ₳1.15M budget request appears disproportionate to the project’s current maturity and deliverables. The proposed team size and cost per FTE exceed open-source standards and lack clear justification relative to outcomes. Treasury spending must remain efficient and proportionate to ensure sustainability and equitable funding across the ecosystem. We encourage the proposers to return with a leaner, milestone-based plan that preserves GovTool’s progress while improving cost efficiency.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Cypherpunks",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreid3s6dkdjjykj3c75raa35w527y4hiyz2voenqdhhihxfqqhzwj4m -->\r\n# Cardano Cypherpunks\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23wk4w6f2aumc92vl9m3x74xzm6jh4ha9wdq09yfq2sl6q8zlv4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nApproving after approved info action",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://bafybeig7gbtpizdu3m3gukehmb4qeokkr3efgpqzsvpyetmg2s4iufayqe.ipfs.dweb.link/ -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmZfKJ4hPLC9WpVpuA7r8qu23iRMGqjwNKUZFrJ9TSeZeG\r\n\r\nThis treasury withdrawal (gov\\_action16tdkp3fs0j6303e4utgp8rftdug0ckezr4sslgv8wxdaeq40ngpsq5sr06h) governance action aligns with the approved budget info action (gov\\_action1n5sn54mgf47a7men2ryq6ppx88kta4wvenz2qkl4f9v6ppje8easqxwm88m) for the continued maintenance and development of GovTool. Our continued support is based on several key factors:\r\n\r\n1. **Robust Administrative Framework:** The proposal's use of Intersect's smart contract framework provides a transparent structure for accountability. This directly addresses the need for clear oversight on a project of this scale.  \r\n2. **A Clear and Valuable Roadmap:** The planned development roadmap includes several high-impact features, such as script-based DReps, enhanced DRep voting history, and integration with the CoSponsor tool. These updates will significantly improve the functionality and accessibility of Cardano's governance system.  \r\n3. **Commitment to Ecosystem Decentralization:** The allocation of 250,000 ada for external contributions, to be distributed via the Andamio platform, is a commendable step. It encourages broader community participation and helps ensure the governance tooling landscape does not become dependent on a single tool or consortium.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Expectations for Future Sustainability**\r\n\r\nWhile we support this 12-month budget, it is important to state our expectations for the future. The 1.15M ada sum is substantial, and this level of funding should not be considered a recurring annual expense. With such a large withdrawal, we expect the GovTool Consortium to use this year to achieve two key goals for long-term sustainability:\r\n\r\n* **Infrastructure Optimization:** A primary goal should be to optimize the hosting and deployment infrastructure to reduce operational costs in the future.  \r\n* **Simplified Self-Hosting:** To further enhance decentralization and reduce reliance on a single point of failure, we strongly recommend the team prioritize making it straightforward for any community member to spin up and host their own instance of GovTool.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanolotus",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSZN5zVAUiGJWNCAZyNZczQa1Y6wTL5cdK4UuwAn98Ry7 -->\r\n# Cardanolotus\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt7hfdllz0l707unkh9g2fs9e35dl6d94tvjynnh4t5gw6gcmn4jn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nToo much ADA just to do maintenance for 12 months.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmUSFiPvG99vZBQ2CtxwhJMY11RZQ3Mh1r2L6TmS1DWQgE -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmY1BpLMj57SkLYvGJrh1fve4HzX99p7af2eHtdkn7DF2A\r\n\r\nI explained my reasons for supporting this project in the Info Governance Action. They are still valid.\r\n\r\nIn short, GovTool is a mission-critical infrastructure for Cardano governance.\r\n\r\nThe Cardano community needs to support open-source tools for governance. Decentralization is not only about block production, but also about tools that facilitate governance processes, namely DReps registration, overview of DReps and governance actions, voting, communication, etc.\r\n\r\nThe breakdown is fairly transparent with specific FTE allocations.\r\n\r\nIt includes ecosystem-wide incentives, not just one vendor.\r\n\r\nCardano governance will evolve, so we need to not only maintain the tools but also continue to improve them. Tools with a modern user experience can attract new people to governance, which is what we need.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/TreasuryWithdrawal_2.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is an expensive price tag, but as the only open-source and community-owned tool for proposing and voting on governance actions, I'm willing to vote YES on this proposal.  However, I expect to see notable improvements to the platform as a result of this funding.  Namely the ability to vote on multiple governance actions at once, a crowdfunding mechanism for governance action deposits, and the addition of all remaining governance action types to the list of proposals that can be submitted through the GovTools UI.  At a bare minimum I think these changes should be made before submitting for any further treasury funding.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Change_The_World_With_Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihmk57ceyfw3kcl3xpfgdfxaeh4s2rk4xvja23g53alrc3vvndicm -->\r\n# Change_The_World_With_Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7wnxu07kkxpyeul6mq5d20uuvk6m73rfgt3atsgtgg4hgfqgkyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis Gov tool should be integrated into every wallet and maybe even have a small bonus ADA allocated to those that do vote. Voting is so important, its like people need to turn up to the polls and people need to become members and use their voting power.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreib366sa4u4ul2ngqkb26sjgytyyhffrmccz5dlhqgiqmlj2trt7xa -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting yes as I did with the budget info action - this is tooling that needs to exist for the time being and be supported.  The platform continues to improve over time and I look forward to seeing Costs are also expected to go down over time.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Christopher Erckert Dotare",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWWxCYoD4uQZSYct6DQgUawB9CdjDAqTVRYJisR43fNux -->\r\n# Christopher Erckert Dotare\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg8aktnf09gdd0jpyhuz3fy22mfjrqrg2ru52907zeeeeqcra6xhe`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis funding keeps Cardano’s on-chain decision-making accessible, secure, and user-friendly, supporting updates, community feedback integration, and feature improvements essential for Voltaire’s success.",
