    {
      "voter": "drep1yfx2476p8smc8dyuvgz0lkgwgzdyuuaw9293ncnswy8cfac4xu0z3",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihcsfnmat77ekbd32fke3luavsf3kydqzwdy4pprmqghsi6c7g4pe -->\r\n# drep1yfx2476p8smc8dyuvgz0lkgwgzdyuuaw9293ncnswy8cfac4xu0z3\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfx2476p8smc8dyuvgz0lkgwgzdyuuaw9293ncnswy8cfac4xu0z3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n1.1 million for this nonsense shit looking user interface???!!!!! NO WAY!!! That money would cover the salary of a proper developer for TEN YEARS!!! What the hell costs 1.1 million on to upkeep this page???",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/Gov.ToolSupport/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(50).jsonld -->\r\n# drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES on this GovTool treasury withdrawal. This proposal addresses some of the most critical needs for Cardano governance today. What stands out most is the Key Features and Roadmap: supporting group DReps, showing DRep and Governance Action voting history, allowing multiple votes per transaction, integrating CoSponsor for crowdfunding deposits, expanding APIs, and optimizing infrastructure. These improvements make governance more transparent, accessible, and efficient for the entire community.\r\nThe Governance & Oversight structure is also excellent — administration via Intersect’s smart contracts with checks from the Oversight Committee and a public dashboard for on-chain auditing ensures accountability, reduces risk of mismanagement, and strengthens trust.\r\nWith contributions coordinated through the GovTool Consortium — including LidoNation, ByronNetwork, WeDeliver, and Dquadrant — this proposal ensures that the platform remains community-led, open-source, and sustainable. The rationale is clear: prevent fragmentation, maintain a neutral platform, and safeguard the long-term health of Cardano’s on-chain governance ecosystem.\r\nFor all these reasons, I fully support this withdrawal.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ytajpleue086e8jw0vetfl70qay0tgv8nccfv4aygkpt8xsjpgdys",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmekeQyxCfJVrnqRyGkLFDWokDsSuQ4HSFpdyDWnXQ6G49 -->\r\n# drep1ytajpleue086e8jw0vetfl70qay0tgv8nccfv4aygkpt8xsjpgdys\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytajpleue086e8jw0vetfl70qay0tgv8nccfv4aygkpt8xsjpgdys`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting NO because I generally use Tempo over GovTools due to its Frontend UI feels much easier & cleaner to navigate, search for proposals, vote and write rationales on them, and I don't see much value in maintaining the Frontend side of GovTools. If there's a separate & lower fund request to maintain the Backend side, probably i may consider to vote yes.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_GovtoolsTW.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n\r\nEMURGO as DRep abstains on the governance action to fund Cardano GovTool – Treasury Withdrawal for 12 months of active maintenance and development, following the previously approved Budget Info Action for ₳1.15M. \r\n\r\nRationale:\r\n\r\nEMURGO recognizes that GovTool has made clear progress since the previous Info Action, particularly in technical performance and delivery structure. The proposal presents a stronger framework for accountability and transparency under Intersect’s oversight.\r\n\r\nHowever, given the ongoing adjustments in Cardano’s governance landscape and the need to observe how these operational improvements perform over time, EMURGO believes a neutral position is most appropriate. Abstaining reflects continued support for the process and the principle of community-driven governance, while allowing room for further evaluation of execution consistency in the months ahead.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\n\r\nEMURGO as DRep abstains, acknowledging GovTool’s significance and progress, while maintaining a balanced and observant stance in alignment with EMURGO’s responsibility to support both accountability and long-term ecosystem stability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00054_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted ABSTAIN on gov_action16tdkp3fs0j6303e4utgp8rftdug0ckezr4sslgv8wxdaeq40ngpsq5sr06h;\r\n\r\nWe appreciate the role GovTool plays for Cardano's governance and recognize the team's ongoing contributions. However, we vote ABSTAIN due to the size of this treasury request; ₳1,150,000 is too high. We would vote YES for a revised proposal closer to 50% of the current amount.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "FAIR Pool #01",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaJhwxgpHfxH6fZWEqfzWXh9HYEhBu4U1CsDcKmWTW4md -->\r\n# FAIR Pool #01\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytamqncvuz2r0atkwxwgcn5zmgxm09j0g2lgcrp7ddqfsfcsgnr8s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGovTool is useful, but this request is too big and not clear enough about what will be delivered as it is simply not defined yet. The proposal doesn’t set firm milestones or KPIs, and funding isn’t tied to meeting them. I’m voting NO, but I would support a smaller, step-by-step plan with clear targets.",
      "vote": "NO"
