      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://amaranth-defensive-basilisk-269.mypinata.cloud/ipfs/bafkreighnt3egj35imeubpwfiso2iypfmsqe6oujasfp5xzdcb4jes6ug4 -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action16tdkp3fs0j6303e4utgp8rftdug0ckezr4sslgv8wxdaeq40ngpsq5sr06h), pois, conforme nosso voto na respectiva InfoAction, o GovTools é a principal ferramenta de participação na governança, oferecendo funcionalidades que ainda não estão disponíveis em algumas carteiras, como a carteira Lace. Portanto, sua manutenção e continuidade são essenciais para o amadurecimento do ecossistema de governança, favorecendo o aumento da participação da comunidade. Além disso, a justificativa de gastos apresentada, bem como as métricas de avaliação e controle, foram claras e bem estruturadas, demonstrando responsabilidade e alinhamento com os objetivos estratégicos da rede.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action (gov_action16tdkp3fs0j6303e4utgp8rftdug0ckezr4sslgv8wxdaeq40ngpsq5sr06h), as, in line with our vote on the corresponding InfoAction, GovTools is the main tool for participating in governance, offering features that are not yet available in some wallets, such as Lace. Therefore, its maintenance and continuity are essential for the maturation of the governance ecosystem, encouraging greater community participation. Furthermore, the expense justification presented, along with the evaluation and control metrics, was clear and well-structured, demonstrating responsibility and alignment with the networks strategic goals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "punkr",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreihuwlcytwoynaux4loh3ntolr2s7e7lmiu6ipyardniattlziehyi -->\r\n# punkr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfyl9j6amk940g76r7ujnn5gywnjenv3kmun3a5tr5a83psl4vv64`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGovTool is an essential open-source tool needed to keep Cardano's governance accessible and decentralised. I'm voting yes, because the benefits, like better tools and more participation, clearly outweigh any risks, backed by audits and past success.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeN8XdANnmvPRbLaQZzrnQERcKMmqi2nH4FFFES8voP5a -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA votes YES on this Treasury Withdrawal, implementing the previously approved ₳1.15 M GovTool budget.\r\n\r\nWe recognize GovTool as essential public-good infrastructure that underpins DRep registration, proposal submission, and voting across Cardano’s governance pillars. The proposal satisfies Article IV of the Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Constitution through:\r\n– clear administrative designation under Intersect,\r\n– milestone-based disbursement via audited smart-contract framework,\r\n– third-party oversight and on-chain auditability, and\r\n– proper non-delegation of custodial funds.\r\n\r\nWe note, however, community concerns regarding budget proportionality and long-term sustainability. To reflect fiscal prudence and reinforce transparency, RCADA expects:\r\n\r\nPublication of milestone hashes and acceptance criteria before each disbursement;\r\n\r\nQuarterly progress and expenditure reporting through the public dashboard;\r\n\r\nDelivery of cost-optimization and self-hosting capabilities to reduce future funding requirements; and\r\n\r\nDocumentation of conflict-of-interest management within the oversight committee.\r\n\r\nThis vote affirms support for open, verifiable governance tooling while echoing the community’s call for efficiency and accountability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Reshma_Mohan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/resgsh/drep-mainnet/refs/heads/main/voting-activity/7.Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Reshma_Mohan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfcgvh8rum7a9ma4gwgwuwutdu0dnrzaj98jytwyfqzd87q2nehvm`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhy I am voting Yes\r\nGovTool has already proven itself - over 50,000 people across 170+ countries are actively using it. It works, people rely on it, and it's completely open-source. Without funding, we risk losing this to proprietary alternatives that could fragment the community or put governance behind paywalls.\r\nThe Money Makes Sense\r\nThe team isn't asking for blind trust. There's proper oversight with multiple independent organizations checking the work, public dashboards showing where every ada goes, and they're even promising to return unused funds. That's the kind of accountability we should expect.\r\nIt's Actually Community-Driven\r\nThe roadmap is based on what the community has been asking for. Things like making it easier for smaller DReps to team up, better voting history so we can see what our DReps actually do, and lowering the barriers for anyone to submit proposals. Plus they're setting aside ₳250,000 to reward contributors and support other governance tools.\r\nSets a Good Standard\r\nThis proposal has detailed contracts, milestone-based payments, third-party verification. If we want future treasury withdrawals to be handled professionally, this is the kind of proposal we should be supporting.\r\nBottom line:- GovTool is already essential infrastructure that's working well. This keeps it running, makes it better, and does it all transparently.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibggehhhsrosb2ijgbkwvkrrdqlclhrmzfu3yxfslspce6wy5kyde -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am in favor of approving this funding request. The amount requested is significant and I believe that GOV TOOL in general has quite a few improvements to make, however it has one important reason why we absolutely should fun it: It is community managed and open source. It is great to have multiple tools from multiple teams out there to handle governance but we also must maintain enough tools that are in the control of the community if we want to remain fully decentralized. Community managed projects come with a certain set of difficulties and are generally a little more expensive but that is certainly worth the cost.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXfaTwUUJ1TJf93uaGnJoAjnTt65xW4Wm5VuNKXfaWW3c -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis withdrawal simply executes the already-approved ₳1.15M budget for GovTool’s 12 months of maintenance and development. GovTool is Cardano’s core public good for on-chain governance participation — without it, proposing, voting, and delegating would become significantly harder.\r\n\r\nThe funds will be managed via a smart contract with oversight from the independent Oversight Committee, and any unused funds will be returned to the treasury. This is a necessary step to ensure continuity, stability, and further improvement of Cardano’s governance infrastructure.\r\n\r\n僕はこの提案に賛成（YES）票を投じます。\r\n\r\nこのWithdrawalは、既に承認された₳1.15MのGovTool予算を実際に執行するためのものです。GovToolはCardanoのオンチェーンガバナンス参加の基盤であり、維持と改善が途切れれば投票や提案の参加障壁が一気に高くなります。\r\n\r\n今回の資金執行はスマートコントラクトとOversight Committeeによる監査付きで行われ、未使用資金はトレジャリーに返還されます。これは、透明性と安全性を確保しながらガバナンス基盤を支える重要なステップです。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Sebastien Guillemot セバ",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXApCWhqCWk3u4eFdsgoojSuj7J4UTj4hqcjM1Bk3UGoB -->\r\n# Sebastien Guillemot セバ\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,150,000 for GovTool 12 months active maintenance and development\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2csyxt7u2hl4674pl9cef5lknafaw5nraxvyx033kmd0es3awuv0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI don't think the amount asked matches the value gov.tools brings to the ecosystem",
