    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiegqlm7jrsbm4so65h7yggwlkkr5gvpsrhff3wm7wp5btkwn72jxu -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本提案は、スナップ選挙で選出された憲法委員会メンバーをオンチェーンで追加し、委員会の最小構成要件を回復するための技術的・制度的措置です。「技術的」とは、Cardanoが委員数・署名形式・任期をプロトコルで自動検証し、不備があれば憲法ガードレールが作動してガバナンスが停止する仕組みを指します。\r\n今回のスナップ選挙は、欠員によるガバナンス停止を避けるためにIntersectが実施した特別選挙で、DRepsのみが参加し、ステーク重みで集計され監査も行われました。私もDRepとして投票しており、本提案はその結果を正式にプロトコルへ反映する最終手続きです。本提案は新たな支出を伴わず、選挙結果も監査により透明性が担保されています。コミュニティの意思を確実に反映し、Cardanoの安定したガバナンス継続に資すると判断し、賛成します。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal adds the Constitutional Committee member elected in the recent snap election, restoring the committee to its required minimum size. “Technical” refers to Cardano’s protocol, which automatically verifies committee size, signatures, and term parameters, activating constitutional guardrails and halting governance if requirements are unmet.\r\nThe snap election was a special vote held by Intersect to quickly fill a vacant seat and avoid governance interruption. It was conducted off-chain through an election portal, limited to DReps and weighted by delegated stake. I participated in this election, and this proposal formalizes its audited results on-chain. As it requires no new treasury spending and preserves transparent community decision-making, I support the proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardaFlow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmabranWze6CCzPEvQhjAED5yMH9s7MojosEfPFk6zbnv8 -->\r\n# CardaFlow\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNo brainer. Although I supported Christina Gianelloni as an individual CC member, my second choice was Cardano Curia. Our new CC member will allow #Cardano Community to move forward with Pentad gov action and Treasury withdrawal.\r\n\r\nWhile moving forward, I hope that a second Gov action for the addition of a second CC member (e.g. based on second most voted in Ekklesia CC snap election) could be proposed to exceed CC min size by 1 member and thus provide more stability to our decentralized governance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNQBSbEWHQpiFdBQxYDjbr3ay1oLxGL2fjhNKiaJ7ESCH -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe support this action because adding the elected Constitutional Committee member restores the committee to its required minimum size, enabling full on-chain governance to function again. The snap election was transparent, audited, and compliant with constitutional guardrails, and Cardano Curia received the highest DRep stake in the vote. This proposal does not change any rules or powers - it simply implements the community’s decision and ensures governance continuity.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXQygKtSPFyB6CnxdajnYftXtMiQmSEmg4MSPbfEXww4o -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmadvwZbTb3Ft3RSQMBExANijQb9Atc1MTrwgNo6S6McFz\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Foundation acknowledges the need to bridge the gap between resignation of the Cardano Atlantic Council and the next committee elections in September 2026 with a new committee member appointment. This will ensure that critical governance actions between now and September 2026 can be voted on by the CC, which will be restored to a functional state.\r\nWe trust that the new elected CC member Cardano Curia will vote promptly and conscientiously, with full consideration for the Cardano Constitution and the proper role of a Constitutional Committee member. \r\nNote: While this is not a counterargument per se, we also note that this NewCommittee governance action suggests that CC consideration is needed in respect of Net Change Limit governance actions. While consideration can of course be given, we do not think the CC needs to vote on such governance actions per the wording of the Constitution, which contains no such requirement.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXpBCVQjGef4ZWzgxiaYKLmTZm4WXHGyZC5fFx5Lx2R8r -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I have decided to vote YES on the Add Constitutional Committee Member proposal.\r\n\r\nA new CC member, Cardano Curia, was elected in the Snap election. No one disputed the election results. I have no reason to disrespect this result.\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Curia members are well-known faces. I trust them and their ability to perform the CC role flawlessly.\r\n\r\nCardano governance needs to be able to approve proposals that require CC approval as soon as possible. This governance proposal is urgent, as there are other proposals waiting in the queue that require approval from CC members.\r\n\r\nI am pleased that Cardano governance is able to quickly and effectively replace the retired CC member. I hope that other DReps will vote soon.\r\n\r\nCongratulations to Cardano Curia on winning the Snap election, and I hope that they will soon become an active CC member.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
