    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXWAbEbDdZ9bVY75EsRnTvxykVHN8qUYsAJvB24oJupER -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Add Constitutional Committee Member\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes on this action to add Cardano Curia to the Constitutional Committee.\r\n\r\nThe committee dropped below the minimum size after Cardano Atlantic Council stepped down. That means it cannot ratify any actions that need committee approval. Governance has been partly stalled since epoch 597. Adding the elected member lifts the committee back to the required size and restores full governance flow.\r\n\r\nThe snap election followed the same model used earlier in the year. The process was open, verifiable, and aligned with the Constitution and CIP-1694. The audited results are published, and the elected member will serve the remainder of the original term. Nothing else in the committee structure changes.\r\n\r\nMy vote supports keeping the governance system working as intended and avoiding gaps in decision making across the network.",
      "vote": "YES"
