    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote94.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI decided to vote Yes, since I believe the long-term value for the ecosystem outweighs the requested funds.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Aichi Tokai_DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVfdfWpbV1C7ZbtymJMVxi3Y6gchdkDYHCGkhEZ38oYG8 -->\n# Aichi Tokai_DRep\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2xacakh0g8q4exfgmvywy62an74cj7ejcpcrgq6vh4dckqhtsyh5`\n\n---\n\nI am voting No on this proposal.\n\nThe cost-effectiveness of the revised Summit plan remains unclear, and the proposal does not demonstrate a convincing level of external value for Cardano. While community events have internal benefits, the expected impact on real-world adoption—bringing new users, developers, or enterprises into the ecosystem—appears limited.\n\nGiven the lack of clear return on investment and the weak pathway to meaningful external adoption, I cannot support this proposal.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmT3GJK2FN5xVGodkkSmVbEGXQi3RvVfEVg3goaN1dGq8X -->\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\n\n---\n\nこの提案は、Cardano Summit 2026をシンガポールで開催し、TOKEN2049直前の機関投資家・企業・規制関係者・開発者が集まる環境を活用する、戦略的意義の高い提案です。前回案から22%削減され、EMURGO提案とも切り離された点は、コミュニティの懸念に応えた改善として評価します。Cardanoが研究・技術中心のチェーンから、DeFi、RWA、stablecoin、AI、identityを含む実需市場へ進むうえで、Asiaの金融ハブで存在感を示すことには大きな意味があります。 本提案では、Enterprise MQL、戦略会議、技術デモ、開発者参加、ハッカソン提出数などのKPIが設定されており、単なる参加者数ではなく、採用導線を測ろうとしている点も評価できます。一方で、初回マイルストーンが80%前払いである点、KPIがまだ露出・参加者数・初期接点に寄っており、実装成果への接続が十分に明確ではない点は改善が必要です。 Treasury支出としての成果をより明確にするため、イベント後にはPoC（本格導入前の小規模な実証実験）、MOU（協力検討を文書化する覚書）、技術統合候補、DeFi・流動性関連の継続商談、ハッカソン後の開発継続率なども、可能な範囲で追跡・報告されることを期待します。これにより、Summitが単なる広報イベントではなく、Cardano上の実装・採用にどのように接続したかを、コミュニティがより具体的に評価できると考えます。 また、Cardano Foundationの自己資金力を踏まえると、今後はCF負担比率、収益のTreasury還元、成果連動型支払いをより明確にすべきです。以上を踏まえ、今回は戦略的価値を重視して賛成しますが、次回以降はより厳格な成果指標と資金配分設計を求めます\n\n---\n\n\u2028This proposal has strong strategic value because it brings Cardano Summit 2026 to Singapore and positions Cardano immediately before TOKEN2049, where institutional investors, enterprises, regulators, and developers will already be gathered. I also appreciate that the revised proposal reduces the budget by 22% and separates it from EMURGO’s TOKEN2049 sponsorship proposal, responding to community concerns. As Cardano moves from a research- and technology-focused chain toward real-world markets such as DeFi, RWA, stablecoins, AI, and identity, having a strong presence in Asia’s financial hub is meaningful.\n\nThe proposal also includes KPIs such as Enterprise MQLs, strategic meetings, technical demos, developer participation, and hackathon submissions. This is positive because it tries to measure adoption pathways, not only attendance. However, the first milestone releases 80% of the funds upfront, and the KPIs still lean toward visibility, attendance, and early-stage contacts. The connection to concrete implementation outcomes could be clearer.\n\nTo better evaluate the impact of Treasury spending, I would like to see post-event reporting, where possible, on additional outcome-oriented indicators such as Proofs of Concept, Memoranda of Understanding, technical integration opportunities, DeFi or liquidity-related follow-ups, and developer retention after the hackathon. These would help the community understand how the Summit connects to real implementation and adoption on Cardano, rather than only serving as a branding event.\n\nGiven the Cardano Foundation’s own financial capacity, future proposals should also clarify the CF funding share, possible revenue return to the Treasury, and more outcome-based milestone payments. Based on the strategic value of this event, I support this proposal, while asking for stricter outcome metrics and funding design in future proposals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardaFlow",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdCZs9BWJu4kutkZPQNVa1hPXvBiqfD2ZRnDGkxYVVhNL -->\n# CardaFlow\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y279cte2lujj9lde4lmz07wsku5fvra69htrleyx9ahr60cn42uaa`\n\n---\n\nShould have been right, first time\n\n\"Trust takes years to build, seconds to break, and forever to repair\"",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiaiivlurzv7krqhpg2aq6et3vwv2itezzmoyxgzyt7nwfml6erl7m -->\n# Cardanians\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\n\n---\n\nWe are voting ABSTAIN on the Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore proposal.\n\nThe revised version is clearly stronger: it is decoupled from TOKEN2049, reduced by 22% to 7,800,000 ADA / $1.95M, includes clearer KPIs, a detailed budget, oversight, refund conditions, and CF increased its internal contribution to $380,000.\n\nHowever, we are still not ready to vote YES. Even after the reduction, this remains a large treasury-funded event subsidy. The Summit is still far from self-sustaining, with a $450,000 revenue target against a $2.263M gross budget, and 6,240,000 ADA is available at kickoff before the event is delivered.\n\nI understand the timing constraints and why the proposal was submitted outside the regular budget process. Still, I’m not convinced that renting expensive event space is the only, or necessarily the most efficient, path to institutional adoption. Cardano needs institutional outreach, but we should compare this against cheaper and more targeted formats: smaller invite-only meetings, side events, direct BD trips, private roundtables, or co-hosted partner events.\n\nMy abstain recognizes the improvements, but I would like to see a stronger sustainability path and clearer evidence that this format produces concrete ecosystem outcomes.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Cypherpunks",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreicte5l6arlpbxbc7lxqlrzawljig7e6ct54tylohivctmn5cbh4eu -->\n# Cardano Cypherpunks\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23wk4w6f2aumc92vl9m3x74xzm6jh4ha9wdq09yfq2sl6q8zlv4l`\n\n---\n\nYES — but narrowly\n\nBecause:\n\nthe revised version appears substantially improved,\nthe strategic rationale is coherent,\nthe accountability structure is relatively mature,\nand ecosystem-level visibility probably does matter at this stage.\n\nBut I would also expect:\n\nfar harsher KPI enforcement in future years,\nstricter post-event ROI analysis,\nand progressively more sponsor-funded rather than treasury-funded summits.\n\nThe critical thing is whether this evolves into:\n\na self-sustaining institutional ecosystem event,\n\nor remains:\n\na subsidized ecosystem conference.\n\nThat distinction matters enormously over a 3–5 year horizon.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Feed",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreid6ywmej6jdtaahjck57kf2fjumrgm7sjp5ln3ovnpr5yds3gywqa -->\n# Cardano Feed\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftjewhpvtdd8t7swtmtp44px94ns3laytmjc3u7f93qvhswmwv5f`\n\n---\n\nI support this proposal as it combines cost reductions with meaningful adoption and ecosystem growth objectives.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmU2JgKcwu2BYzH83BHRph1SNM7YcP6AHpgHhFnoTkxQRc -->\n# Cardano Foundation\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\n\n---\n\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\n\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmetGEEYcsbeSfy2kbkrib8d5SFyY5PRXCKnhRKotBxrLf\n\nThe Cardano Foundation has submitted this revised Cardano Summit 2026 proposal in direct response to significant community feedback and input. It is clear that we did not sufficiently engage with the Community on this topic prior to the first proposal. We continue to believe in the strategic value and the leaner, optimized budget of this revised Cardano Summit.\n\nHowever, in light of the significant community feedback and as a signal that we continually strive to improve our engagement with the community, we feel that it is appropriate to ABSTAIN on this proposal, so that the community can independently direct its course.\n\nThis abstention is a reflection of the unique history of this specific proposal. It is not a precedent for how the Cardano Foundation will vote on any future proposals. We will continue to vote on any proposal based on the principles set out in “Our Cardano” and what we believe is in the best interests of Cardano and its ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmS38SmUkYB8L83CJVw5Lj3WQ3nFryjsyNKdFywERHiNtW -->\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\n\n---\n\nAs a DRep, I have decided to vote on the three crypto event proposals as follows:\n\n- Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore: ABSTAIN\n- TOKEN2049 Singapore 2026 Baseline “Platinum” Sponsorship proposed by EMURGO: YES\n- TOKEN2049 Singapore 2026 Top-Up “Title” Sponsorship Upgrade: NO\n\nGiven that DReps have to process a large number of proposals in the coming weeks, I will provide one short rationale for all three proposals.\n\nMy rationale:\n\nFirst of all, thank you to both the Cardano Foundation and EMURGO for accepting feedback and resubmitting proposals.\n\nI do not oppose the idea of a Cardano Summit. My concern is primarily about treasury allocation and long-term sustainability. Cardano Foundation owns and manages the Cardano brand and remains one of the strongest-capitalized entities in the ecosystem. According to its 2025 financial report, the Foundation held approximately $361M in assets at the end of 2025, including roughly $280M in crypto assets and approximately $80M in fiat and traditional financial assets. \n\nIf the Foundation believes the Summit is strategically critical for Cardano, I believe it should be willing to finance a larger portion of the event from its own resources.\n\nMy second concern is that the Foundation previously communicated that the Summit should become increasingly sustainable over time.\n\nThe current proposal does not provide enough clarity on what that actually means. I still do not know whether future Summits will require treasury funding, how much funding may be requested in future years, or when the Summit is expected to become financially self-sustaining.\n\nThe proposal mentions that revenue from the 2026 Summit will help fund future events, but it does not clearly state that future treasury requests will stop. Given the large funding requirements from IO, Intersect, infrastructure teams, and builders across the ecosystem, I am not comfortable approving both major event proposals.\n\nAt the same time, I recognize that other DReps support the Summit and consider it strategically important. My current position is somewhere between NO and ABSTAIN.\n\nThat is why I decided to abstain rather than vote NO.\n\nI decided to support the baseline TOKEN2049 Singapore 2026 proposal because it gives Cardano exposure beyond its own ecosystem. Unlike the Summit, which is naturally more focused on existing Cardano community members, TOKEN2049 puts Cardano in front of a much broader audience that includes investors, exchanges, market makers, media, founders, developers, enterprises, and builders from other ecosystems.\n\nI believe Cardano still needs stronger external visibility, and this proposal addresses that more directly.\n\nFor approximately $792,900, the baseline proposal gives Cardano a large booth at the event, a dedicated builder stage, live product demonstrations, lead generation tools, networking access, ecosystem tickets, and post-event reporting requirements.\n\nMore importantly, it gives Cardano builders direct access to people who are not already part of the ecosystem. That is a much stronger value proposition than spending significantly more money to create a separate event in the same city just two days earlier.\n\nI understand that EMURGO has faced criticism from parts of the community in the past. However, DReps should evaluate proposals based on current execution plans and expected outcomes. I appreciate that EMURGO recently addressed concerns related to DRep selection in Yoroi Wallet, and I am willing to give them a second chance.\n\nI want to make a pragmatic decision.\n\nIn this case, EMURGO is leveraging an existing global event, which significantly reduces operational complexity. The proposal also includes concrete deliverables such as builder showcases, live demos, partnership targets, media exposure, and measurable post-event reporting. While some KPIs should always be viewed critically, I believe the overall direction is pragmatic and focused on external ecosystem growth.\n\nI do not support the Top-Up proposal because I do not believe the additional $424,360 is justified. The extra spending mainly buys a larger booth, a keynote slot, lanyard branding, protein shake branding, and additional media exposure.\n\nIn my view, the baseline proposal already captures most of the meaningful value, and the upgrade feels like diminishing returns and unnecessary prestige spending.\n\nThis is ultimately a pragmatic treasury allocation decision. Cardano should not disappear from major crypto conversations, media, and broader crypto audiences. I believe supporting one meaningful external-facing marketing initiative is reasonable.\n\nAt the same time, treasury resources remain limited, and I do not believe it is responsible to fund multiple overlapping event proposals.\n\nIf one of these events is approved, I will likely be significantly more conservative when evaluating other marketing-related proposals.\n\nI may still change my mind before voting closes. If it becomes clear that the EMURGO proposals have no realistic path to approval while the Foundation proposal does, I may reconsider my position and adjust my votes accordingly.\n\nIf you'd like to support my work, consider delegating to the MANDA pool and backing me as a DRep. Your support is the only way I can get time for governance.\n\nMANDA Pool ID:\npool1c3fjkls7d2aujud8y5xy5e0azu0ueatwn34u7jy3ql85ze3xya8\n\nMy DRep ID:\ndrep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmT9A4VripzQwiZDQZbbXxELq8KpmDSMs1wuhpYXaAFpTU -->\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\n\n---\n\nThese MKT event should be covered by previous budget asks MKT of Intersect or Founding entities the original budget plan. Skeptical on the impact",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
