    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmX3ixtnCLN7VWcuQGkpxtNxUxqdmTZLbQQqx8YKcWtu8S -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHere’s a cleaner, more structured version that keeps your meaning and tone:\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes.\r\nThe proposal being separated from TOKEN2049 addresses one of my main concerns from the prior version. The more focused scope, along with a modest reduction in total cost and a leaner event structure, moves this in a better direction.\r\nI still believe there is opportunity cost here. My original concerns around pipeline, conversion, and post-event outcomes are not fully satisfied, but I’m also not sure they realistically can be at this stage. This is still partly an awareness and engagement effort, and the real test will come after the event.\r\nI don’t know that the Cardano Foundation can fully predict what this converts into, but I do think they understand where Cardano needs to be represented and who the target audience is. Given the location, timing, strategic opportunity, and Cardano’s position as an L1 that needs to show up in these conversations, I view this as an acceptable proposal and cost.\r\nThat said, support here should not be interpreted as a blank check for future Summits. We need to take a hard look at the results in the months after the event and evaluate what actually came from it. Future Summit proposals should be benchmarked against the outcomes of this one.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Christopher Erckert Dotare",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdehpkeHpxznUy2E1hb6ZCQmD2Fk5GWs8375AWnC8Mvtp -->\r\n# Christopher Erckert Dotare\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg8aktnf09gdd0jpyhuz3fy22mfjrqrg2ru52907zeeeeqcra6xhe`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAppreciate the decision to split the events, but voting no for now — would love to see the budget better aligned with ADA's current value and stronger matching contributions from the Cardano Foundation, particularly if attendance isn't subsidized for existing community members.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cryptotexty",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmW44u2CgMPLRpDrGsmBCurv98QmSHhjjo3yCZPYwAJuRA -->\r\n# Cryptotexty\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsrvdukj9unnxue5ffmrkjr9ve7yxz3wvccdstapmw696q8g2w9u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs I explained previously in past votes, I consider this (even reduced, even edited) as HUGE waste of funds. We had Community Events category in Project Catalyst - I think it's good practice to renew it and make each event go via community voting and discussion. Another option is to empower Ambassadors or DREps with (1/1000 or 1/100 of such budget).",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dori",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbykAuQVfRiHifkJNmZMHGcHcUJGZHyztkSupr1Fe13JS -->\n# Dori\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yteh8udkttzy7frwl6yj5wzyqc04kx65pwwrqefx9j52ymgr6kuak`\n\n---\n\nI vote YES on the Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore proposal.\n\nWhat stands out in this revised proposal is that CF's internal resource contribution has increased from $250,000 to $380,000, that the CF Summit has been decoupled from EMURGO's TOKEN2049 sponsorship into a separate proposal.\n\nI laid out my supporting rationale when voting on the original proposal as well, but the effect of networking and direct engagement that comes out of in-person events like this is enormous. Real business, collaborations, and unexpected ideas and opportunities happen through face-to-face meetings.\n\nThe content that gets reproduced and shared through international events of this scale also delivers Cardano's presence to the market.\n\nSome have suggested the community could organize this themselves, but that is nearly impossible. Every part of running an event of this scale, from the preparation work, to inviting speakers, to external promotion, can only be done by a credible and well-structured organization.\n\nAn inexperienced and unprepared organization hosting a low-quality event would actually damage the ecosystem's credibility and brand value externally. The fact that only the founding entities are currently capable of preparing an international event that represents Cardano is undeniable.\n\nSince this Summit is being held in conjunction with TOKEN2049, I expect CF to maximize the synergy that the timing and location bring.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dr. Navjit Dhaliwal",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcLq6acXEgEVbPPyBqLghZHTj8zsoWyL8c3cQak4F8UjL -->\n# Dr. Navjit Dhaliwal\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfya5pwcm2zw0e60c3pkqscq6spge7m0k6jtxkfsymv68gs2z56e5`\n\n---\n\nI voted NO on the TOKEN2049 Title Sponsorship top-up and YES on the Cardano Summit 2026 proposal.\n\nThe TOKEN2049 top-up is primarily an incremental spend on premium visibility - a larger booth, a keynote slot, additional branding, media introductions and related event optics. I do not think the marginal return on that extra spend is clear enough.\n\nThe Cardano Summit is different. It is a Cardano controlled platform with a dedicated agenda and a clearer structure for converting attention into meaningful ecosystem outcomes. The revised Summit proposal is no longer tied to the TOKEN2049 sponsorship proposal and has been reduced by 22% while preserving the core two day structure. It also defines more direct outcome targets, including 250 enterprise MQLs, 50 strategic meetings within 45 days, 10 live demos/workshops, 200 developer participants, and 30 hackathon submissions/applications.\n\nJust as importantly, prior Summits provide evidence that this format has already produced real value.\n\nThe official Cardano Summit 2025 results state that the event brought 1,460 in person attendees and 26,000 online viewers, while also recording strong participation from enterprises including Volvo, Wurth Group, Mastercard and many more. The same official recap reports that the Layer Up hackathon attracted 134 developers from 92 teams, resulting in 14 submitted projects. \n\nIt has acted as a meeting point for enterprise engagement and developer onboarding. There are also concrete examples from the ecosystem.\n\nExample - At the 2022 Lausanne Summit, I presented on data compliance, privacy, security and GDPR. This  speech was right before Charles' announcement of Midnight\n\nAt the 2025 Berlin Summit, the official agenda included \"Iagon & Würth Group: Enterprise Adoption -A Cardano Case Study.\" This was a direct example of a real enterprise use case being showcased through the Cardano Summit format. \n\nThe Summit gives Cardano:\n\n- a platform it controls\n- an agenda aligned to its priorities\n- a structured place for builders and enterprises to meet\n- a more direct path from visibility to follow-up and adoption\n\nThat is why I was comfortable supporting the Summit, while not supporting the premium TOKEN2049 top-up",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1y2q96n4hf0d8jnf6cf7h84z0tr0fn35wh7uv0q4w4hpzckqr8a70c",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://Qma2TcspyVzyVuAe7rNYSc9GAbAGbrqqbLs5RJ6xT4t8N1 -->\n# drep1y2q96n4hf0d8jnf6cf7h84z0tr0fn35wh7uv0q4w4hpzckqr8a70c\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2q96n4hf0d8jnf6cf7h84z0tr0fn35wh7uv0q4w4hpzckqr8a70c`\n\n---\n\nI abstainI abstain",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yfd635ljn7qc0z2qu7pnch3skktqq74ff35pkreyql2f02cs34940",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUdXTCxSDHzrWbkGBL7CmHnC6PZY7ZagPUj87rfytkB6V -->\n# drep1yfd635ljn7qc0z2qu7pnch3skktqq74ff35pkreyql2f02cs34940\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfd635ljn7qc0z2qu7pnch3skktqq74ff35pkreyql2f02cs34940`\n\n---\n\nHonestly, I am strongly against this kind of spending on summits, parties, guest artists, and what feels like excessive use of treasury funds, especially under current market conditions. First, I don’t see any clear direct impact from this kind of expenditure. There are no defined KPIs or measurable outcomes that justify the cost. On top of that, it feels like we are reinforcing the same echo chamber the same Cardano community gathering at a Cardano-focused event. In other words, we are staying within the same island instead of reaching new audiences. If the goal is growth and adoption, then we should be prioritizing initiatives that expand beyond the existing community and deliver measurable results.\nWe are not in a bull market with ADA at all-time highs to justify this kind of spending on events and celebrations. Additionally, there have already been several summits, and from my perspective, I don’t see the value this event brings especially when it is being funded by the treasury.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/RevisedSummit.jsonld -->\n# EMURGO\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\n\n---\n\nSummary\nActing in its capacity as a DRep, EMURGO formally casts a YES vote in favor of the treasury withdrawal request for the \"Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore.\" Our support is predicated on the proposal’s refined strategic focus, which balances high-impact global positioning with a significantly optimized fiscal framework. We recognize this initiative as a critical commercial vehicle designed to accelerate the protocol's transition into a mature, enterprise-grade financial operating system. By strategically co-locating this summit with TOKEN2049, we create a powerful value accelerator for Cardano’s visibility, allowing our builders to tap into a massive global footfall while offering the community a cost-effective way to attend two premier industry events in one journey. EMURGO’s affirmative vote reflects our confidence in the Foundation’s revised execution strategy and the substantial long-term value this summit will secure for the ecosystem.\n\nRationale\nEMURGO recognizes that hosting a flagship summit is a fundamental market requirement; every leading Layer 1 protocol maintains a major annual event as a cornerstone of its business development strategy, often with significantly higher capital outlays than what is proposed here. This investment is essential to maintain protocol parity and institutional mindshare within a hyper-competitive industry. The 2026 Summit is intentionally timed to coincide with TOKEN2049 in Singapore, a move that functions as a strategic value accelerator. By concentrating the world’s most influential institutional leaders and capital allocators in a single geography, Cardano can capture high-value attention and mainstream financial interest without the prohibitive costs of independent audience acquisition. Furthermore, this alignment provides a pragmatic benefit to the Cardano Community: by anchoring our event to the TOKEN2049 calendar, community members can effectively attend two of the year’s most significant industry gatherings in a single trip, drastically reducing individual travel, lodging, and per-diem expenses.\n\nThis move perfectly aligns with the Cardano Vision 2030, specifically our shared objective of transitioning the protocol into a self-sustaining, global financial and social operating system. We appreciate the Foundation’s responsiveness to community feedback, which has resulted in a significantly optimized proposal that demonstrates both fiscal responsibility and strategic maturity. Furthermore, the budget has been reduced by 22%, or approximately $550,000, through smart architectural changes such as consolidating from three stages to two. This leaner approach significantly lowers production and logistics overhead while maintaining the tier-one experience expected of a leading Layer 1 blockchain. This efficiency is further bolstered by increasing the Cardano Foundation’s internal resource contributions to $380,000, a commendable commitment that reduces reliance on external vendors and optimizes treasury use.\n\nEMURGO fully agrees with the defined KPIs, which provide the transparency and rigor necessary to measure real-world impact and growth throughout this transition. We also value the continued dedication to inclusivity through the provision of discounted tickets based on on-chain activity, ensuring our core supporters remain at the heart of the event. This more focused proposal remains dedicated to delivering tangible results for Cardano and its builders while demonstrating a sophisticated commitment to responsible treasury management. For these reasons, EMURGO confidently votes Yes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "erikdrep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZLfuSHfjMHgCdctPZM8gbpkpLdiij9w1hRRMpXDdwVdQ -->\n# erikdrep\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytrf7kdyhk6ft3fqzqqqaszam6gt2fljpsvwkvngamyrvks6faung`\n\n---\n\nOf the 3 event proposals, this is the only one I am willing to for in favor of.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Hermes Stakepool Germany (HRMS)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiduosp3awwvhhr5chng44m2u4a32dtl3pa6kal7xb5w3kct34l374 -->\n# Hermes Stakepool Germany (HRMS)\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygs5hngva3hymv7j4v0aewxpsjqskj9dnmy7j3jz5ven5zqvulq2t`\n\n---\n\namount still excessive",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfNLuM4BXbPSAUDf4C8fddkX2azSKM54H627o2tGJqQVf -->\n# hix_coffeepool\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\n\n---\n\nI am voting No on this proposal. As a DRep, I evaluate all treasury withdrawal governance actions against my published voting framework, with a focus on the healthy development and long-term sustainability of the ecosystem. This proposal does not meet the framework's requirements, and I am voting No on that basis. Reference: https://coffeepool.jp/notes/drep-voting-framework-for-sustainable-ecosystem/ [Japanese version follows] 本提案に反対票を投じます。私はすべてのトレジャリー出金ガバナンスアクションを、公開済みの投票フレームワークに基づいて、エコシステムの健全な発展と持続可能性を重視して評価しています。本提案はフレームワークの要件を満たさないため、反対票を投じます。参照: https://coffeepool.jp/notes/drep-voting-framework-for-sustainable-ecosystem-jp/",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeMX1jnVJQFPFgoPpLHtB8M1UjzX5XZvWHM1U4tDsHmjA -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHaving a Cardano Summit may be important, but trust in the Foundation is a bigger issue for me. I don't want to be in a position to second guess what the foundation presents to DReps. Unfortunately, I have to second guess now. \r\nIn the previous vote on the Cardano Summit I welcomed the proposal from the CF and Emurgo and voted No - one of the reasons was that the CF moved away from its own plan for achieving Cardano Summit sustainability that helped it get funding for the previous Cardano Summit. To me, this represents a breach of trust.\r\nMy point is that if the CF’s mandate is, broadly speaking, to support institutional adoption, Cardano usage and long-term sustainability, then this proposal undermines the very credibility the CF needs to perform that role.\r\nIt is difficult to reconcile the CF’s role as a credible institutional partner with its inability to maintain its own sustainability plan for a controlled event such as the Summit for even one year. Plans can change, and mistakes can happen. Not holding a Summit is not the end of the world.\r\nI could understand a mistake. However, the Cardano Foundation tweeted the following on April 14, 2026: \"We must be clear that there will be no modified Cardano Summit proposal. There simply isn't time on the calendar to reengineer an event of this size.\" That was just two weeks ago. \r\nI am losing trust in the CF as a body that is able to present reliable and consistent information in support of its proposals. The tweet could reasonably be read as putting pressure on undecided DReps to vote YES by implying that there would otherwise be no Summit in 2026.\r\nFinally, the proposal contains a revenue rollover mechanism, but not a credible, measurable path to Summit self-sustainability or reduced Treasury dependence. In my view, the sustainability of the Summit should be resolved before the Treasury is asked to fund it again. The long-term issue is much more important to me than holding the Cardano Summit in 2026.\r\nTo me, the CF appears to be transferring the consequences of an overextended event strategy to the Treasury. I cannot vote in good faith for this as I do not have sufficient confidence in the proposal, its assumptions, or its long-term funding model.\r\nPlease note that this vote does not reflect on all CF activities. It is specifically aimed at this proposal and the context in which it is being proposed.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifya7bv2ket7bvfyjv2a64vyhwfdbgixzc467wccha7crsrcpemqi -->\n# Kevin G Mohr\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\n\n---\n\nNeed to improve the ecosystem before partying.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmXCWAXLUZkSjGwpnfP8DwMw5WUStGbfXo1uxoHJmk37n3 -->\n# Kostas Panagias\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\n\n---\n\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\n\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/Qmez2HKUqaVog5qktHrU1KqZ8NJ6PD4Xue1GC9AHPy8meJ\n\nI am voting **YES** on the revised Cardano Summit 2026 proposal. I highly appreciate that the Cardano Foundation listened to community feedback by decoupling this request from EMURGO's proposal, significantly reducing the overall requested treasury amount, and increasing their own internal contributions.\n\nAs a top-tier blockchain, Cardano boasts unmatched technology but has historically lacked the marketing presence to match. We absolutely need a high-end, Tier-1 event to showcase our ecosystem to the world. Strategically positioning this Summit in Singapore immediately preceding Token2049 is an ideal move to capture institutional and enterprise attention.\n\nHowever, while I support this iteration, I'd like to see the following improvements in future event proposals:\n\n* **Greater Skin in the Game:** I believe that the Cardano Foundation should cover at least 50% of the total event costs from their own allocated funds, rather than relying heavily on the treasury.\n\n* **Path to Sustainability:** I highly advocate for a definitive roadmap demonstrating how the Summit can transition into a 100% self-sustained event, funded entirely by event revenues or the Foundation's own backing.\n\n* **Verifiable ROI:** Event outcomes must move beyond general \"brand awareness\" and translate directly into specific, measurable new business for our ecosystem. We need transparent tracking of how generated leads actively convert into tangible opportunities and partnerships.\n\nI appreciate the responsiveness shown in this revised proposal, which has my support today. Moving forward, we must continue pushing for fully sustainable events that deliver clearly measurable business value.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "KryptoLabs",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPXCzokedC5sNkokpmtpv7oBz1g2NWbPcPpuoKfyQBygw -->\n# KryptoLabs\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfeqm8wfd2h9pf2c9y934qskuw3z04selrpr7esf4gdsl2c5zvpgf`\n\n---\n\nAbstaining, as I’m part of the Cardano Constitution Committee Tingvard.\nReading proposals and staying updated, just like you.\nThanks to all fellow DReps who are also doing the hard work.\nFollow and DM me on X: @kenerik if you have any questions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifwex3atelya4bmnfphsntxfwkzppgskkfwz5doswqqwou67v6udi -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI appreciate the CF listening to the community by making this a separate proposal from the TOKEN2049 one, making adjustments, and even slightly increasing their own contribution. That said, I still think the CF should contribute more from their own allocated funds. I would also have liked to see some cooperation with Midnight to do something together and reduce costs.\r\nEven so, I acknowledge the importance of having a Cardano Summit, and I’m still convinced that holding it in Singapore right before TOKEN2049 makes sense, especially this year. The time is now to put Cardano in the spotlight, because we have a lot to make up for.\r\nWhile I still have reservations about the size of the requested amount and would have preferred a larger CF contribution, I believe the strategic value of holding the Summit in Singapore right before TOKEN2049 outweighs those concerns. I also appreciate the CF addressing the issue raised by one of the CC members regarding Tenet 8 in this revised proposal. For these reasons, I approve this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "phillerino",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmbw1z3wKYYWVdyc89Wa8AHmW6JkqrHzGM2VTqMTMJq6Hz -->\n# phillerino\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytu64qt7send5dw7wcd0z5geh4ka6qstgvtgval097hed7qqnqh2n`\n\n---\n\nDifficult to justify at current price. Let's do it another year.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWWg1c9SxbM2N2Zb6gofd4ksWtzTSs6TG2iQs1ME5TZAJ -->\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\n\n---\n\nI evaluated the three proposals — Cardano Summit 2026, TOKEN2049 Platinum Sponsorship, and the TOKEN2049 Title Upgrade — as part of one broader strategic direction.\n\nFirst, I strongly support Cardano having a presence at TOKEN2049. At this stage, I believe Cardano’s biggest challenge is no longer purely technology or research, but external adoption, business development, liquidity, institutional relationships, and attracting new builders into the ecosystem. TOKEN2049 represents one of the few global venues where over 25,000 participants — including investors, enterprises, exchanges, developers, and media — are already concentrated in one place. This makes it an extremely valuable opportunity for Cardano to expand beyond its existing ecosystem.\n\nIn particular, the Platinum Sponsorship proposal appears relatively practical and cost-conscious while still preserving the core strategic value. The builder stage, ecosystem booth presence, networking access, and builder ticket allocation provide direct opportunities for ecosystem exposure, relationship building, and potential onboarding. Given the current market conditions and the broader treasury environment, I believe this proposal has a reasonable chance of generating measurable external impact.\n\nHowever, I am more cautious regarding the Title Upgrade proposal. While the keynote slot, additional branding exposure, and media positioning certainly have value, I do not believe Cardano’s highest priority right now is maximizing prestige or brand visibility alone. The ecosystem’s larger issue is converting attention into real adoption, partnerships, liquidity, and users. Because of this, I am not fully convinced that the additional cost of the upgrade delivers proportional ROI at the current stage.\n\nRegarding Cardano Summit 2026, I understand and respect the overall vision behind the event. Community building, governance discussions, education, and ecosystem identity are all important for Cardano’s long-term health. However, I also believe there is a real risk of becoming too internally focused. Cardano already has strong technology, strong research, and a strong governance culture, but it still struggles with market penetration and external growth. In the current environment, I believe the higher priority should be attracting external participants rather than primarily reinforcing internal branding.\n\nOverall, my position is:\n\nTOKEN2049 Platinum Sponsorship → Support\nTOKEN2049 Title Upgrade → Cautious / leaning unnecessary at this stage\nCardano Summit 2026 → Worth reconsidering if there is sufficient remaining NCL capacity. However, a further reduction in scope and budget would make the proposal significantly easier to support\n\nFor Cardano to reach the next phase, it must evolve from being simply a technically strong blockchain into an ecosystem that naturally attracts capital, enterprises, developers, and users. In my view, external connection and market expansion should be prioritized right now.\n\n\n僕は、Cardano Summit 2026、TOKEN2049 Platinum Sponsorship、そしてTOKEN2049 Title Upgradeの3提案を一体として検討しました。\n\nまず、TOKEN2049への参加自体には強く賛成です。現在のCardanoに最も必要なのは、内側での認知や結束だけでなく、外部市場との接続、流動性、企業連携、そして新規ビルダーや機関投資家を引き込むための導線だと考えているからです。TOKEN2049は、25,000人規模のグローバル参加者が集まる数少ない場であり、Cardanoを「外」に届けるための非常に重要な機会だと考えています。\n\n特にPlatinum Sponsorship proposalは、Builder Stage、ブース展開、ネットワーキング、Builder ticket提供など、比較的コストを抑えながらも、実際の流入や事業開発につながる現実的な構成になっていると感じます。現在の市場環境やNCLの状況を踏まえても、一定の費用対効果は期待できると考えています。\n\n一方で、Title Upgrade proposalについては慎重です。メインステージ keynote、ランヤード、追加ブランド露出などは確かに価値がありますが、現時点のCardanoにおいて最優先なのは「ブランドを大きく見せること」より、「実際に人や企業を引き込むこと」だと考えています。追加コストに対するROIには疑問が残るため、現段階ではPlatinumのみで十分ではないかと感じています。\n\nまた、Cardano Summit 2026についても、方向性や思想には共感しています。特にコミュニティ形成、ガバナンス、教育、ブランド構築という観点では重要な役割を持つイベントだと思います。ただし、現在の市場環境では、どうしても“内輪で固まりやすい構造”になるリスクも感じています。今のCardanoは、技術力や研究力は非常に高い一方で、事業開発や市場への浸透に課題を抱えているため、優先順位としては、まず外部流入を強化するべきフェーズだと考えています。\n\nそのため総合的には、\n\nTOKEN2049 Platinum Sponsorship → 支持\nTOKEN2049 Title Upgrade → 慎重 / 現時点では不要寄り\nCardano Summit 2026 → NCLに余裕がある場合は検討余地あり。ただし、規模や予算をさらに縮小することで、より支持しやすい提案になると考えています\n\nという立場です。\n\nCardanoが次のフェーズへ進むためには、「強い技術を持つチェーン」から、「人・資本・企業・開発者が自然に集まるチェーン」へ進化する必要があると考えています。その意味で、今最も重要なのは“外に向けた接続”だと感じています。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Shawn McMurdo - SQUID",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmPhZtooW6D5HNn6Bcs2XVJvgE4XLKByPxWBqUeg8Lx4Rc -->\r\n# Shawn McMurdo - SQUID\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt99uyp9c8qura9spfgqe8uf7g2avmqc683x28zcugh0sycjd6wp0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXFEpBeRHg7zbhGPRkBZnBahEAkHWHtp66JD38VZnTsU6\r\n\r\nyes",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmacyALcjjhjGWZX93rDxawWia8j6rFuqC7F6ea1cEFCYG -->\n# Tony Boersma\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\n\n---\n\nI am voting Yes on Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore. I appreciate that the proposal substantially reduces costs and decouples the Summit from the broader TOKEN2049 package, resulting in a more focused and disciplined request. Promoting Cardano remains important for ecosystem growth and visibility, and this revised structure represents a more measured and fiscally responsible approach while still supporting meaningful outreach and engagement.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfRwHen22WTCuEPUK2kgFUvk39m6rXRy4Fub7FT2zRUEK -->\n# TriangleForces\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\n\n---\n\nYet another very expensive exercise in conference theatre courtesy of the treasury?\nTo me this looks like a weak strategic bet at a scale that is too expensive relative to what is actually proven. Show me hard evidence that this specific event format is the most efficient path to enterprise conversion! In plain English: I want to see a tightly evidenced adoption machine and not another flagship showcase with evening parties. \n\nThe budget reduction is noted, but it does not change the key question. A 22% trim is still lipstick on a very large pig if the underlying spend logic remains “we must be there at tier-one level or risk irrelevance.” I do not buy that framing. Cardano does not become institutionally credible because it rents expensive square meters in Singapore. It becomes credible by shipping integrations, onboarding usage, deepening liquidity, improving developer leverage, and funding repeatable adoption infrastructure. The summit may amplify those things; it is not a substitute for them!\n\nThe treasury must not bankroll premium event optics when the causal link between conference spend and durable ecosystem adoption is as soft as here. Cardano needs leverage, not pageantry.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmX7ziqbsNrH2q8rx5n78pTPYvxPsi79nYKNcQQg4R7aoV -->\n# Varavas\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\n\n---\n\nI appreciate the decision to decouple this proposal from Token2049. Having rejected EMURGO’s initiative, I will support the Cardano Foundation’s Cardano Summit in Singapore. I believe it delivers greater value between the two events and fully endorse the significant cost reduction.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Cardano%20Summit.jsonld -->\n# Yoroi W₳llet\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\n\n---\n\nSummary \nYoroi DRep votes YES on the \"Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\" by the Cardano Foundation. This position reflects our support for the strategic location, the optimized budget, and the anticipated return on investment for the ecosystem. By aligning with major global industry movements, we ensure Cardano remains at the forefront of the 2030 Vision.\n\nRationale\nMaximizing Ecosystem Visibility and Community Value\n- Competitive Market Presence: It is a standard industry reality that every leading Layer 1 protocol hosts a flagship summit; Cardano’s proposal is not only competitively priced but represents a significantly more efficient spend than many of our direct peers.\n\n- The Visibility Multiplier: Co-locating with TOKEN2049 allows us to leverage the massive concentration of international talent, developers, and media already in the city. This creates a \"halo effect\" where Cardano builders are positioned to capture the attention of over 25,000 external participants and potential partners.\n\n- Community Cost-Efficiency: By anchoring the Summit to the TOKEN2049 calendar, community members can attend two of the world's largest crypto events in a single trip, significantly reducing their individual travel, lodging, and logistics expenses.\n\n- Strategic Hub: Singapore's geographic advantage ensures that Cardano’s technical milestones are showcased within a high-density environment, providing brand exposure that would be far more costly to generate in isolation.\n\nProportionality and Fiscal Leanliness\n- The revised proposal directly addresses concerns regarding treasury impact through a budget reduced by 22% ($550,000).\n\n- This was achieved through intelligent streamlining, moving from three stages to two, which lowers production costs without compromising the tier-one experience required for an L1 blockchain.\n\n- By increasing internal resource contributions to $380,000, the Foundation has reduced external vendor reliance and optimized the use of community funds.\nImportantly, this proposal is fully decoupled from EMURGO’s TOKEN2049 sponsorship, ensuring a clean and transparent funding structure.\n\nCommunity Engagement and Vision 2030\n- A core pillar of our support is the value provided back to the builders, specifically the inclusion of discounted tickets for community members based on on-chain activity.\n\n- This ensures that the Summit remains accessible to the individuals who build on the network daily, keeping the event rooted in our decentralized community and the Cardano Vision 2030.\n\nAccountability and Agreed KPIs\n- Yoroi fully agrees with the proposed KPIs, which offer a clear framework for evaluating success through live demos, developer engagement, and enterprise leads.\n\n- The commitment to full KPI transparency and smart contract-based disbursement provides the high level of accountability we demand for treasury withdrawals.\n\nConclusion\nYoroi fully supports the vision and execution plan for the Cardano Summit 2026 in Singapore, basing our YES vote on the strategic timing, the responsible budget reduction, and the clear focus on driving adoption for our builders.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmbARPcYoM2DwgGiUcapsv8Xo6kJ2MPTSG7xnM6CkJeuB5 -->\n# YUTA\n\n**Proposal:** Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\n**Vote:** Abstain\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\n\n---\n\nI am voting Abstain on \"Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore\" and \"Cardano at TOKEN2049 Singapore 2026: Baseline 'Platinum' Sponsorship Proposal.\"\nGiven the cancellation of Dubai token 2049, it is reasonable to bet on this. Emurgo and CF will likely be able to achieve the KPIs stated in the proposals.\nHowever, looking at CF's and Emurgo's events from last year, I was unable to find convincing evidence as to whether these directly or indirectly succeeded in driving transactions, ADA purchases, or sustained developer onboarding—and, if they didn't, what has been improved this time around.\nOn the other hand, I also agree that it would be a mistake to take pride in doing no promotion at all, and that TOKEN2049 is a good venue for it. There is also no alternative team.\nTaking all of this into account, I find it hard to firmly say YES but also hard to firmly say NO, so I am voting Abstain. I may still change my vote going forward based on feedback from everyone.\n\nーーー\n\n私は「Revised Cardano Summit 2026 Singapore」「Cardano at TOKEN2049 Singapore 2026: Baseline ‘Platinum' Sponsorship Proposal」にAbstainを投票します。\n\nドバイのキャンセルを加味するとここに賭けることは合理的です。emurgoとcfは提案書に書かれたKPIを達成することは可能でしょう。\n\nただし、cfとemurgoの去年のイベントで、これが直接的、間接的にTxや ADAの購入、継続的な開発者のオンボードに成功しているかどうか、そして、それがうまくいかなかった場合、今回は何が改善されているのかについて、自信を持てる証拠を見つけることができませんでした。\n\n一方で私たちは何も宣伝しないことを誇ることは誤りであり、token2049はそのための良い場所であることにも同意します。また他に代替チームありません。\n\nこれらを踏まえてYESと断言しづらいがNOとも断言しづらいと考え、abstainを投票します。今後皆さんのフィードバックでさらに投票を変える可能性があります。",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    }
  ],
  "Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026": [
    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote86.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Abstain on the 'Amaru 2026' treasury withdrawal, not because of the proposal itself, but due to concerns about the overall voting process.\r\n\r\nAt the moment, there is an approved total budget (350M), yet funding requests are being submitted independently as separate governance actions. This creates a fragmented and unclear landscape: it's difficult to understand the total number of proposals, the combined requested amount, or how close we are to exceeding the available budget.\r\n\r\nWithout this broader context, it becomes challenging to properly prioritize proposals, assess trade-offs, or compare similar initiatives. If the total requested funds exceed the budget, there is no clear framework for how decisions should be made across competing proposals.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I believe the current process lacks the structure needed for effective decision-making, and I am abstaining on that basis rather than on the merits of this specific proposal.",
      "vote": "ABSTAIN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmT8BJedtXsF9N6mnH4zcCN72GN7RRYZEPLsEepSDmvog4 -->\r\n# Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9dq806jcm56wzhnv2yrf6gcyq7h4gap8gxewfykk0dtfs7vf843`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n`## Governance Action Review\r\n\r\n**Governance Action:** `Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026`\r\n\r\nI am voting **NO** on this Treasury Withdrawal at this stage.\r\n\r\nThis vote should not be interpreted as a rejection of the proposal itself or of treasury funding in principle. My concern relates primarily to the **timing and coordination of treasury allocations** under the current governance environment.\r\n\r\nAt present, the ecosystem still lacks a sufficiently clear view of the **full pipeline of proposals that may seek funding within the current NCL window**.\r\n\r\nApproving Treasury Withdrawals before proposers have had a meaningful opportunity to participate in a broader coordination process risks reinforcing an uncoordinated funding dynamic, where requests are assessed in isolation rather than in relation to the wider ecosystem’s needs, trade-offs, and budget constraints. My concern is not with individual submissions as such, but with the absence of a more collaborative and comparative process through which scope, budget, and priority can be better optimized across the current funding cycle.\r\n\r\nGiven the expectation that Intersect’s budgeting process may surface a broader set of requests in the coming weeks, I believe a short delay would likely improve decision quality and reduce the risk of inefficient allocation.\r\n\r\nApproving withdrawals too early may also create **downstream pressure to expand the NCL** in order to accommodate proposals that emerge later but may prove strategically more relevant.\r\n\r\nThis should not be read as an attempt to block funding or paralyze governance. The ecosystem has already had roughly a full year to learn from the weaknesses of the previous cycle and to build a more credible coordination layer for the next one. That response has progressed more slowly than it should have.\r\n\r\nI was willing to accept greater urgency last year because continuity of development mattered and the system was still in an early transition phase. But if we never reach the point where dReps are willing to demand greater accountability, coordination, and rigor, then the ecosystem simply carries the same loose standards into yet another funding cycle.\r\n\r\nI do not consider that acceptable after the time already available to improve the process.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I believe it is preferable to **delay approvals temporarily rather than normalize allocation decisions under incomplete and uncoordinated information**.\r\n\r\nThis vote reflects a preference for **better coordination and prioritization of treasury spending**, not opposition to the goals of `Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Revisão de Ação de Governança\r\n\r\n**Ação de Governança:** `Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026`\r\n\r\nEstou votando **NÃO** nesta Treasury Withdrawal neste momento.\r\n\r\nEste voto não deve ser interpretado como uma rejeição da proposta em si ou do financiamento via tesouro em princípio. Minha preocupação está principalmente relacionada ao **timing e à coordenação das alocações do tesouro** no atual ambiente de governança.\r\n\r\nNo momento, o ecossistema ainda não possui uma visão suficientemente clara do **conjunto completo de propostas que podem buscar financiamento dentro da janela atual de NCL**.\r\n\r\nAprovar Treasury Withdrawals antes que os proponentes tenham tido uma oportunidade real de participar de algum processo mais amplo de coordenação corre o risco de reforçar uma dinâmica de financiamento descoordenada, na qual pedidos são avaliados isoladamente, em vez de serem analisados em relação às necessidades mais amplas do ecossistema, aos trade-offs existentes e às restrições orçamentárias.\r\n\r\nMinha preocupação não é com submissões individuais em si, mas com a ausência de um processo mais colaborativo e comparativo por meio do qual escopo, orçamento e prioridade possam ser melhor otimizados ao longo deste ciclo de financiamento.\r\n\r\nConsiderando que o processo de orçamento conduzido pela Intersect pode trazer à tona um conjunto mais amplo de solicitações nas próximas semanas, acredito que um pequeno atraso provavelmente melhoraria a qualidade das decisões e reduziria o risco de alocações ineficientes.\r\n\r\nAprovar retiradas muito cedo também pode gerar **pressão posterior para expandir o NCL**, a fim de acomodar propostas que venham a surgir depois e que eventualmente se revelem mais relevantes do ponto de vista estratégico.\r\n\r\nIsso não deve ser interpretado como uma tentativa de bloquear financiamento ou paralisar a governança. O ecossistema já teve aproximadamente um ano inteiro para aprender com as fragilidades do ciclo anterior e desenvolver uma camada de coordenação mais sólida para o próximo ciclo. Essa resposta avançou mais lentamente do que deveria.\r\n\r\nNo ano passado eu aceitei um maior senso de urgência porque a continuidade do desenvolvimento era importante e o sistema ainda estava em uma fase inicial de transição. No entanto, se nunca chegarmos ao ponto em que os dReps estejam dispostos a exigir maior accountability, coordenação e rigor, o ecossistema simplesmente carregará os mesmos padrões frouxos para mais um ciclo inteiro de financiamento.\r\n\r\nDepois do tempo que já tivemos para melhorar o processo, não considero isso aceitável.\r\n\r\nPor essas razões, acredito ser preferível **adiar temporariamente as aprovações em vez de normalizar decisões de alocação baseadas em informações incompletas e descoordenadas**.\r\n\r\nEste voto reflete uma preferência por **maior coordenação e melhor priorização do gasto do tesouro**, e não uma oposição aos objetivos da `Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026`.`",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Aichi Tokai_DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidrrf2weixlownoelbxlng3dh74lazprhdmw3zrx6dnoo26sfqxni -->\r\n# Aichi Tokai_DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2xacakh0g8q4exfgmvywy62an74cj7ejcpcrgq6vh4dckqhtsyh5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nCompared with other core development initiatives in the Cardano ecosystem, the overall budget and FTE cost assumptions appear reasonable and consistent with industry standards. The team has also demonstrated a strong commitment to transparency through clear reporting, on‑chain treasury management, and the return of unused funds in the previous cycle.\r\n\r\nWhile I acknowledge that some parts of the 2025 roadmap experienced delays, I will continue to monitor the project’s delivery pace and technical progress closely. Even so, I believe the work Amaru is doing is strategically important for node diversity and long‑term network resilience, and I want to support their continued development.\r\n\r\nI look forward to seeing the technical advancements they bring to Cardano in the coming year.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmazy6J4yDaKZXWA11swUUtu8uRJKrwWWx58f3M7nnX2qf -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本提案に賛成票を投じます。Amaruは、Haskell実装に依存しないRust製ノードとしてCardanoのノード実装の多様性を高める重要な取り組みであり、ネットワークの分散性とレジリエンスの向上につながると考えます。\\n\\nI vote Yes on this proposal. Amaru is an important initiative that increases node implementation diversity in Cardano as a Rust-based node independent from the Haskell implementation, contributing to the network’s decentralization and resilience.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BEACNpool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidpiuzikllifxh7ufyvpug5mvmkwuy37qylhsrc545firi6atneoq -->\r\n# BEACNpool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jn8fk0cn6wd6et3evnykea0glhw7t20xnhwss4xxjlczq29343n`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBEACN supports node diversity and recognizes Amaru as strategically valuable to Cardano’s long-term resilience. However, this withdrawal is too large, too bundled, and too contingency-heavy for a clean yes. Core security, conformance, and block-production milestones are fundable priorities; speculative integrations, workshops, and treasury-side price buffering should not all be rolled into one massive ask. Until the proposal is narrowed to essential deliverables or staged more tightly, BEACN is Abstain, leaning No.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Big Lazy Cat",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibxybthasdewpr5djvvhfpe4zeu3jyqvju55n4fxnhkxa4zz26mny -->\r\n# Big Lazy Cat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffcjs0njfea09xhs6up429rhya5pxd7qz7hvmwq6vqy2nczwpj3g`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’d prefer to see a production-ready block-producing node delivered and validated first, before funding additional expansions or research. Combining unfinished core work with new scope feels a bit early to me, so I’m abstaining.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Blockjock (James Meidinger)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPALzmwjbmViTjmsB5MuSEh1jKDrMBD4sN4SGTb6jWsWA -->\r\n# Blockjock (James Meidinger)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnypzfv2v8fmfelthahvn0rqyh54sf6z2aa5m7f3fkjgqqt8l2qq`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAmuru has done nothing but provide real value in pushing our chain forward, this particular proposal is critical, quoting here \"There’s no more doubt that Amaru contributes to the decentralization and resilience of the Cardano ecosystem.\" This is a understatement and we need more developers like this providing things that actually, functionally make our entire blockchain better.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreievw6pmtadcymmdjta4yh2et6if743glepntrvujkzpwfa7lbnkpu -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Amaru Treasury Withdrawal 2026\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本提案は、Cardanoにおけるブロック生成ノードの多様性を高める戦略的投資と評価します。AmaruはRustベースの新たなノード実装であり、低ハードウェア要件や開発者層の拡大を通じて、ネットワークの分散性と耐障害性の向上が期待されます。単一実装依存のリスク低減は中長期的に重要です。一方で本件は比較的大型案件であり、費用対効果の観点からは明確なKPI設定が不可欠です。SPOによる採用数、実際のブロック生成割合、今後のプロトコル進化への適応計画などの具体的指標の明示と継続的な進捗開示を求めます。以上を踏まえ、戦略的意義を重視し賛成します。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal represents a strategic investment in client diversity for Cardano. Amaru is a Rust-based block-producing node that aims to improve accessibility and broaden the developer base, potentially strengthening network resilience and decentralization over the long term. Reducing reliance on a single implementation is important for the ecosystem’s sustainability.\r\nHowever, this is a relatively large funding request. Clear and measurable KPIs are necessary to ensure responsible treasury use. In particular, I expect transparency regarding SPO adoption, actual block production share, and compatibility with future protocol upgrades.\r\nConsidering its strategic value, I vote in favor while emphasizing the need for clear performance metrics and ongoing accountability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
