      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfVJy5HZevNhaZvA6hqdpP9ZF8zcyx2hnxFk7VYM2F8PZ -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nUpdated/Changed Vote:  After some further review and consideration, I am opting to support this due to what I hope is a net benefit to the ecosystem with these events down the road.  While I'm personally wary of the key founding entities that are taking part in operating these initiatives - I consider this a last change through 2025-2026 to see them make something of this. The track record, from my perspective, doesn't show a lot of positivity from past events and results - it's costs with no real revenues.  Traction for Cardano's ecosystem however remains a top priority of mine to move things forward - and sometimes that means taking some risks and continuing the effort to bring more key businesses and developers into the ecosystem.  A vote for YES here is to help support that.\r\n\r\nAs always - We will need to strike a balance in treasury withdrawals for projects that push development forward (and therefore the chains efficiency, performance, resiliency, and security) -- and business that wish to participate, of any size, and extend the capabilities and real-world use cases of Cardano.\r\n\r\nMy votes, I hope, align with my overall goal as a DRep to see continuous improvement in the ecosystem. https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/mr_cata_gov%20.txt",
