      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmYyQfoDMyDoWz6bCkerC4o9vzgQrz4YHnuwmJqTJphm2E -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmUAjzyQTZqugEoizuCVx7NAUhtrckY9MbsYCpu9eHCvw9\r\n\r\nI'm voting **NO**. This top-down marketing strategy, led by founding entities, conflicts with my principles on **decentralization** and **sustainability**.\r\n\r\nA decentralized brand should emerge from the community, not be directed by its founders. Furthermore, this is an unsustainable use of public funds. If the founding entities see value in these events, they should contribute from their own revenues. Our treasury is for common goods, not to subsidize the marketing of established organizations.",
