    {
      "voter": "Maureen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTHyV1mUmvAeoUzzjUqURqS4nSRUgKMQNQrV43L83WNBo -->\r\n# Maureen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y22hlaj8wuyygpnjy5cf96tg9tgvjrz39kxvqgv898uj9scfc55t7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI read the PDF strategy of this document and honestly felt embarrassed for everyone involved. What they're calling a \"unified globall events marketing stategy\" is actually just three organizations splitting treasury money to sponsor random conferences with zero coordination. The Cardano Foundation wants to do enterprise events, EMURGO wants to do their usual ineffective ecosystem theater, and Rare Network wants to organize parties. The worst part is the vendor combination. Having EMURGO as a key partner when they've consistently failed to demonstrate measurable ecosystem value is like hiring your least competent friend to handle your most important project. Some partnerships make you weaker, not stronger, and this is definitely one of those. \r\nHard NO.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Mike Rogero (羅邁凱）",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qma31pnK871pxRiBMaDkpvoJk6U8b8qR2FUgtaAmA1W87S -->\r\n# Mike Rogero (羅邁凱）\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2lhe7wn2sr6vme8gnca4jrkhv47uh3tklsykmrqvwzdq4g5s8wju`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am not comfortable with this proposal due to its large size, the move to stop funding an event previous justified as being part of their obligation from the interest earned on genesis ADA by the Cardano Foundation, and the additional funding for Emergo, which has not performed their duties expected with their Genesis ADA for expected similar tasks.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://nimuepool.io/metadata/context-intersect-budget-withdrawals-2025.jsonld -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI decided to vote ✅ YES on 37 treasury withdrawals, ➖ ABSTAIN on none, and ❌ NO on 2 treasury withdrawals from the Intersect 2025 budget.\r\n\r\nIt’s obvious I consider all proposals I approved in the budget vote on Ekklesia beneficial for Cardano, so those all receive a ✅ YES vote.\r\n\r\nI also vote ✅ YES for most proposals I initially abstained from or voted against in the Ekklesia vote. There are a few reasons for this:\r\n- Some proposals gained strong community support after all, so I don’t want to be the one standing in the way, especially when the requested amount is negligible in the bigger picture.\r\n- Some proposals I actually liked, but I found them more suitable for Catalyst. However, with all the delays, it now makes more sense to fund them as soon as possible.\r\n- Some didn’t get my initial support because I thought the requested amount was too high. But I now believe it’s better for the ecosystem to fund them, despite the larger budget, than not fund them at all.\r\n- I needed to vote for budget proposals with my own NCL in mind. Not all those I approved made it, however, so that leaves some room for other ones.\r\n\r\nI won’t approve the treasury withdrawal for two proposals:\r\n\r\n❌ Withdraw ₳3,000,000 for High-yield RWA Asset for Cardano: Tokenized Real Estate\r\nThis proposal won’t bring much value to our ecosystem, imho.\r\n\r\n❌ Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst: Extended Quadratic Funding---Zero Operational Costs\r\nWhile the proposal includes some interesting ideas for a fairer voting mechanism, I now support Catalyst and don’t see the need for an additional funding system at this moment, especially considering total spending. The requested amount also seems too small to meaningfully fund multiple projects. While the model relies on donations, it’s unclear what the donor incentive is. Since voting power is tied to donation size, why wouldn’t donors just support specific fundraisers run directly by the projects they care about? That way, they can ensure their contribution goes straight to their preferred initiative without needing it to win a vote first.\r\nI do appreciate the idea of a hybrid funding model where the treasury covers part of a project, but ideally, the remaining portion should come from investors rather than donations, imho.\r\nLastly, I don’t appreciate that the proposal’s title refers to Catalyst, even though it has no relationship to it. This seems intended to mislead people into thinking Catalyst would benefit from this proposal, which it doesn’t...\r\n\r\nI acknowledge there’s a metadata issue in the proposal “Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement: Cardano.nix”, but I approved it nonetheless, as the problem is minor and not worth obstructing the process.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "No stress",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVcoimAQgqU4YLXuDTVShPySfGLNNeepDodw7dEThgJZq -->\r\n# No stress\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t3t35yx7j8nnh3wkqn2zzhgwqksksn85zv62pjrwzjawczwgyv7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am changing from No to Yes on this proposal. I have realized that I was biasing toward proposals (tech proposals) that I understood. Being no marketer myself, I have decided to trust in the people closest to this. I think this proposal will create some consistency from event to event and further drive a strong Cardano brand. I appreciate all the professional discussions on X to understand this proposal better. Now, let's get to work.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Patrick_Tobler",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUGfbYAevgurqBzHKLWcufQqgi97Cwxf34iEK12tpgrmD -->\r\n# Patrick_Tobler\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygm9wxzrrdqpt0hek5kj7ys6tmsc8dycp7tkjwqxqrhjr6csq3s3t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a good marketing proposal by multiple reputable entities but the amount of ADA requested is calculated at a very low ADA price. If funded the entities should return the additional ADA if price continuies to stay higher than the calculated price.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/r/25/250812_events-global_84772ee63eba.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal funds a coordinated, Cardano-branded global events strategy to match the presence and influence of competing L1 chains. While outcomes are harder to measure, consistent visibility at high-profile conferences can drive developer interest, enterprise engagement, and broader ecosystem recognition. Competitors have successfully leveraged similar strategies to grow adoption and attract talent. The scale of funding is significant but proportionate to the strategic need to position Cardano as a leading blockchain in a competitive market.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmY92JpHL5Y4esqAGN1uKhmvhxAcwduejp4imy86CCFwAN -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA has chosen to** abstain at this time while reserving the option to review and update this vote prior to the voting deadline**. This approach allows RCADA to allocate focus where immediate evaluation is most impactful, particularly on proposals that are close to threshold or raise significant procedural or constitutional concerns. If this proposal reaches the approv-al threshold prior to our review, the abstention will stand as a neutral signal of deferral, not op-position. Should further analysis be warranted, RCADA will update this vote accordingly.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWDeZCoCzKg4kHb8YWAXmQxvktyLkvrxZJjS3C7rEzt1V -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlthough I initially voted No during the Ekklesia phase, after further review and evaluation, I have decided to vote Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nWhile Cardano has taken a more cautious approach to global visibility compared to competitors like Solana or Aptos, those ecosystems have effectively expanded developer adoption and brand presence. A protocol-level marketing initiative is essential if Cardano is to maintain relevance and attract talent on a global scale.\r\n\r\nThis proposal is part of a unified event strategy led by Intersect and executed by reputable organizations—Cardano Foundation, EMURGO, and Rare Network. It will be managed via smart contracts and overseen by independent auditors, ensuring a reasonable degree of transparency and delivery assurance.\r\n\r\nThough precise KPIs for marketing can be challenging to define, I believe the strategic vision and execution plan outlined here serve Cardano’s long-term interests. Given the scale of funding and the structure in place, this initiative deserves support.\r\n\r\nEkklesia投票では一時的にNo票を投じていましたが、精査の結果、Yesへと転じることにしました。\r\n\r\nCardanoがSolanaやAptosのような開発者流入・認知拡大戦略を取らずにいる間に、競合は確実に市場を押さえています。そうした現実に対抗するためにも、プロトコル単位でブランドを前面に出した広報・マーケティング施策は必要不可欠です。\r\n\r\n本提案は、Intersectが主導する統一的なイベント戦略の一環として、Cardano Foundation・EMURGO・Rare Networkという信頼性の高い組織によって運営されます。実施体制や進行状況はIntersectによるスマートコントラクト管理と外部監査体制のもとでモニタリングされる予定であり、資金の透明性や進捗確認の仕組みも一定水準を満たしていると判断しました。\r\n\r\nマーケティングという性質上、定量的なKPIを完全に定めるのは難しい面もありますが、戦略全体がCardano全体にとって長期的な利益をもたらすと判断し、今回の予算規模と体制であれば支持に値すると考えます。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdEXsfBYfs2FyxYLad981grnWNv5U5n9C71Gc4Ho7pkkp -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmP55SMaxEHgxgRhjsPCyKmTX3dE71nTFkpV22cn9UA7V6\r\n\r\nUpon further review and additional information received, we now support this proposal. The initiative demonstrates strategic value for ecosystem visibility through unified marketing presence at major global events like Token 2049. We've received clarification that the marketing efforts will actively include regional startups and building teams, creating collaborative opportunities for ecosystem participants to gain brand exposure and business development connections. This approach aligns with our guidelines prioritizing ecosystem growth and developer visibility. The proposal now demonstrates sufficient alignment with ecosystem development priorities by creating platforms where building teams can showcase their work to broader audiences through coordinated event participation, ultimately supporting Cardano's adoption goals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/27_Unveiling_the_First_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO votes Yes to the proposal “Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing Strategy for Cardano” for the following reasons:\r\n\r\n1. Strategic Branding Alignment\r\n\r\nCardano has long lacked a unified presence at global blockchain events. This proposal corrects that by establishing a centralized marketing strategy that explicitly carries the “Cardano” brand—free from third-party business dilution. This allows for consistent messaging, stronger brand recognition, and a clearer identity in the competitive L1 space.\r\n\r\n2. Direct Response to a Recognized Problem\r\n\r\nThe proposal addresses a critical gap: fragmented Catalyst-funded events that often omit the Cardano brand. This leads to low visibility and fragmented outreach. In contrast, competitors like Solana and Aptos have shown the success of unified branding through recurring global developer events. Cardano must catch up.\r\n\r\n3. Experienced and Credible Implementers\r\n\r\nThe campaign will be executed by a trusted consortium:\r\n\t•\tCardano Foundation: Ensures mission-aligned nonprofit governance.\r\n\t•\tEMURGO: Brings commercial outreach and Japan-based infrastructure.\r\n\t•\tRare Network: Offers Web3-native event execution experience (RareEvo).\r\n\r\nTheir combined expertise ensures professional execution and global reach.\r\n\r\n4. Well-Planned, Global-Scale Impact\r\n\r\nThe proposed strategy includes branded sponsorships at major global events in 2025 and 2026, directly engaging developers, enterprises, policymakers, and enthusiasts. The event list is published and thoughtfully selected to maximize visibility and engagement.\r\n\r\n5. Strong Governance and Transparency\r\n\r\nThe treasury disbursement is governed by:\r\n\t•\tSmart contracts audited by MLabs and TxPipe\r\n\t•\tA multi-party Oversight Committee\r\n\t•\tMilestone-based payments with third-party assurance\r\n\r\nThese mechanisms ensure transparency, accountability, and delivery monitoring—crucial in handling a ₳6M request.\r\n\r\n6. Alignment with the Intersect Budget Framework\r\n\r\nThis proposal is one of the 39 items under the Intersect-administered ₳275M budget, which has already passed the constitutional info-action. The structure conforms to Articles IV.4 and IV.5 of the Constitution, ensuring process legitimacy.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nSIPO supports this proposal as it provides a comprehensive, Cardano-branded, globally strategic initiative to strengthen visibility, credibility, and adoption. With credible implementers and robust governance, it is a timely and impactful step forward.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、提案「カルダノ初の統一的なグローバル・イベント・マーケティング戦略の展開（Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing Strategy for Cardano）」に**賛成（Yes）**票を投じます。その理由は以下のとおりです。\r\n\r\n1. ブランド戦略の一元化による競争力強化\r\n\r\nこれまでカルダノは世界各地のイベントで統一された存在感を持たず、ブランディングが分散していました。本提案は、「カルダノ」というブランド名を明確に掲げ、第三者のビジネス目的に左右されないイベント戦略を打ち出すものです。これにより、一貫性のあるメッセージングとブランドの明確な認知が可能となり、L1競争における地位強化が期待されます。\r\n\r\n2. 既知の課題への的確な対応\r\n\r\n本提案は、Catalyst資金によるイベントの多くが「Cardano」ブランドを前面に出していないという問題に対処するものです。一方、SolanaやAptosは開発者向けイベントを繰り返し開催し、TVLやエコシステムを拡大しています。カルダノも同様の戦略が不可欠です。\r\n\r\n3. 実績ある主要団体による実行\r\n\r\n本プロジェクトは以下の信頼できるパートナーによって遂行されます：\r\n\t•\tCardano Foundation：非営利で中立的なガバナンスを提供\r\n\t•\tEMURGO：商業展開と日本基盤のネットワークを持つ\r\n\t•\tRare Network：Web3に特化したイベント企画・運営実績（RareEvo運営）\r\n\r\nこの体制により、専門的かつグローバルな実行力が担保されています。\r\n\r\n4. 計画性と広範な国際的影響\r\n\r\n本提案では、2025年・2026年の世界主要イベントでのカルダノブランド露出が予定されており、開発者・企業・政策立案者・エンドユーザーと幅広く接点を持つことが見込まれます。公開されたイベントリストは、最大効果を見込めるイベントを選定しています。\r\n\r\n5. スマートコントラクトによる透明性と監査体制\r\n\r\n本提案の資金執行には以下が含まれます：\r\n\t•\tMLabsとTxPipeによるスマートコントラクト監査済\r\n\t•\t複数の第三者による監視委員会\r\n\t•\tマイルストーンベースの支払いと第三者保証\r\n\r\nこれにより、透明性・説明責任・進捗確認が制度的に担保されます。\r\n\r\n6. Intersect予算プロセスとの整合性\r\n\r\nこの提案は、すでに合意されたIntersect予算₳275Mの39提案の1つであり、憲法第IV条第4・5節に準拠して正当なプロセスを経ています。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n結論：\r\nSIPOは、本提案がカルダノの国際的認知度とブランド価値を高める戦略的施策であり、実行体制や資金管理も信頼に足ると判断し、Yes票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
