    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdNCPXzMLWzuKKPXZR3WVs3gZ61QDpK1nMeMhuipVQpjL -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\nYoroi votes YES on the governance action to fund the Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing Strategy for Cardano proposal.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\n- Strengthens Cardano’s global presence: \r\nBrings unified, professional branding to global blockchain events, improving visibility and perception.\r\n\r\n- Targets developer and institutional engagement: \r\nFocused outreach can attract partnerships, adoption, and new talent into the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nBy voting YES, we see this as a timely investment to reinforce Cardano’s identity in a competitive space.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSu36TSJ59V4dpdp69Lu1cejfryyhorKNn14KYCcYyizZ -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳6,000,000 for Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing S\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES to the 6 million ada event proposal.\r\n\r\nI have confirmed that the KPIs for the 6 million ADA event proposal exclude any impacts outside of that proposal.\r\n\r\n(For example, the 10-15% YoY growth in new developers due to the 6 million ADA Cardano Summit is excluded. Other increases in developers due to contexts unrelated to this proposal are also excluded.)\r\n\r\nSummit\r\nhttps://x.com/CardanoSummit/status/1952376959004029201\r\n\r\nEvent\r\nhttps://x.com/Cardano_CF/status/1953063601113031005\r\n\r\nIn other words, EMURGO, CF, and RareEVO will be putting their reputation on the line to achieve 25-35% dev growth.\r\n(Summit 15-20%+Booth 10-15%)\r\n\r\nDepending on how you measure it, this is a fairly ambitious target, given the statistics on Cardano's developer numbers over time.\r\n\r\nCardano Dev Report\r\nhttps://www.developerreport.com/ecosystems/cardano\r\n\r\nThe Booth proposal is not just about setting up a booth, but is a package that also includes hosting side events such as a hackathon.\r\n\r\nThere are also KPI targets other than those related to developers, as well as specific KPI targets for each event (which will apparently be made public later).\r\n\r\nWhile some have suggested that the founding entities should use Genesis ADA, I believe it makes sense to hold the founding entities accountable for achieving 25-35% dev growth(+α) with 12m ADA.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私は600万ADAのイベントの提案書にYESを投票します。\r\n\r\n私は600万ADAのイベントの提案書のKPIは、その提案書以外のインパクトは除外されることを確認しました。\r\n\r\n（例えば、600万ADAのCardano Summitによる10-15% YoY growth in new developersは除外されます。その他、この提案書と関係のない文脈で増加した開発者を除く。）\r\n\r\nSummit\r\nhttps://x.com/CardanoSummit/status/1952376959004029201\r\n\r\nEvent\r\nhttps://x.com/Cardano_CF/status/1953063601113031005\r\n\r\nすなわち、25-35%ほどのdev の成長をEMURGOやCFやRareEVOがその威信にかけて取り組むことになります。\r\n\r\nどう計測するかにもよりますが、これはCardanoの開発者数の推移に関する統計から見てもかなり意欲的なターゲットです。\r\n\r\nCardano Dev Report\r\nhttps://www.developerreport.com/ecosystems/cardano\r\n\r\nBoothの提案書は単にブースを設立するだけではなく、ハッカソンといったサイドイベント開催を含むパッケージになっています。\r\n\r\n開発者に関連する以外のKPIターゲットもあり、また、各々のイベント毎に細かく決められたKPIターゲット（これに関しては後ほど公開されるようです）もあります。\r\n\r\n創業エンティティは、Genesis ADAを使ってほしいという意見もいくつかありますが、私は12m ADAで、25-35%ほどのdev の成長(+α)を達成する責任を創業エンティティに課すことは意味があると思います。",
      "vote": "YES"
    }
  ],
  "Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin": [
    {
      "voter": "$brock",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://brock.iagon.net/votes/2025IntersectBudgetWithdrawals.jsonld -->\r\n# $brock\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytjyvm958ywjkp57f8wm3havj72lc653tp7ajttxxt6ftgcmcmdk2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis vote aligns with my Ekklesia votes, where I voted yes to the highest priority budget line items that fit within my preferred 200m ADA budget, abstained from voting on any line items that I may have had personal interests in, and voted no to everything else.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "$Khale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CFMatrix/Metadata-storage/refs/heads/main/Minimum_Viable_Governance.jsonld -->\r\n# $Khale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2ltat8kjqrmnff3lkkpxy0j5tn66d3m0gy64dc92asft5g6dl9ws`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI recommend a YES vote for the ₳592,780 treasury withdrawal for \"Beyond Minimum Viable Governance: Iteratively Improving.\" This proposal addresses a fundamental gap in the Cardano ecosystem by enabling continuous, transparent, and community-validated governance measurement and improvement.\r\n\r\nThe delivery team, led by IOG’s Voltaire specialists with backing from constitutional committee members, WADA, Intersect, and community partners, brings unparalleled experience in Cardano’s governance mechanics and stakeholder engagement. The project will create the first systematic, data-driven “State of Governance” report, track and publish governance KPIs, synthesize community feedback through multiple engagement pathways, author actionable CIPs/CPSs, and publish a replicable playbook for future improvement cycles.\r\n\r\nThe budget is reasonable for the scope, the delivery controls are strong, and the outputs will benefit DReps, committees, protocol maintainers, and ordinary users. The framework and open process will raise the standard of Cardano governance by providing a clear baseline, methodology, and improvement pathway, promoting greater transparency and resilience in decentralized decision-making.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaLovelace777",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/81125/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(23).jsonld -->\r\n# AdaLovelace777\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygehgu65kchqm929zp69xhl06hqkpcjv0rzy44sx40qhufqgh3xv2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA Yes vote would release ₳592,780 from the Cardano Treasury to fund “Beyond Minimum Viable Governance,” led by Intersect in collaboration with Input Output’s Voltaire team—experienced in CIP-1694 workshops, constitution drafting, and CIP authoring—alongside WADA, members of the Constitutional Delegate Committee (Ken-Erik Ølmheim, Max van Rossem, Tevo Saks), and the Intersect Constitution team. Independent oversight would come from five trusted entities: Sundae Labs, Cardano Foundation, Dquadrant, Xerberus, and NMKR. The rationale is that Cardano currently lacks a transparent, data-driven framework for assessing the effectiveness of its governance system, which risks decisions being made reactively without clear metrics or community-wide insights. This project would deliver a comprehensive State of Governance report tracking KPIs, mapping the governance ecosystem, and identifying improvement areas; engage the community through workshops, surveys, and interviews; produce a repeatable playbook so the process can be run annually; and draft Cardano Problem Statements (CPSs) or Cardano Improvement Proposals (CIPs) based on findings. I think this is genius because we as a protocol need a way to verify that our government is working as intended. This data driven framework will help identify specific areas we can improve and take targeted, evidence-based action to improve transparency, decision-making, and alignment with the community's vision.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfH4Qa1V6ARgguPhZRQwHxAuKYJQPHW8x6mHFs99v9Ytc -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA focused analysis of our first round of governance and clarity on potential improvement vectors keeps the Voltaire era rolling in a positive direction.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AdaStat",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://adastat.net/_meta/drep/vote12-50.jsonld -->\r\n# AdaStat\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I voted for all projects in the 2025 budget vote based on a very simple principle:\\n\\n- Yes if I believe the long-term value to the Cardano ecosystem exceeds the requested amount;\\n- No if it doesn't;\\n- Abstain if I'm unsure.\\n\\nAll of my votes are consistent with [my position in the May 2025 Ekklesia round](https://2025budget.intersectmbo.org/voters/drep1yfe9en4hsgc3r6nhtmwjeljh06hgnvt9yzzkwqcftvdj34cdxdg7u).",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWrM9XFTGvGhBgSZyvVRfECvYenZH3b1GQQufVQFoWGWM -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n「275M ADA Administered by Intersect」に含まれるすべての個別提案に対して、エクレシア投票の段階では必ずしもすべてに賛成していたわけではありませんが、最終的には本ガバナンスアクションに賛成票を投じました。Cardanoエコシステム全体への貢献を高く評価し、その前進を後押しする立場から、今回提出された39件すべての提案に賛成票を投じる判断をいたしました。\\\\n\\\\nWhile I did not necessarily support every individual proposal included in \"275M ADA Administered by Intersect\" during the Ekklesia vote, I ultimately voted Yes on this governance action. Recognizing its overall contribution to the Cardano ecosystem and in support of continued progress, I cast a Yes vote on all 39 proposals submitted under this initiative.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AltcoinOracle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeJrn7NYJgJ6tZcekCNawMnq9ecMxVhbwf8JtXRKNexM5 -->\r\n# AltcoinOracle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygvgk3899qm38zth07z5clhfjvzfhe2mf2kvkqrfxp93r5srjre5s`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote NO, not a priority of my DRep, too much capital for not enough clarity.\r\n\r\nStrength and honor.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Andreas Sosilo",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSAcGMdKKVFmNKpjmTDMjVEzx5axeud9ywhagaZG8De2X -->\r\n# Andreas Sosilo\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y20w8vxwd3venlvp0muxwzmdlr7a006dpz580czmaj422sqng6fkg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI prioritized funding open-source tools and proposals that I believe will most effectively support Cardano’s long-term growth. I voted in favor of the highest-priority items that fit within my preferred budget cap of 250 million ADA, abstained from proposals where I may have had a personal interest, and voted NO on all remaining proposals after reaching that budget limit.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "ArcadianComputers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmf3LfhsW81s68Tnm6tsMTWFtjZPLD9NUPhRfAjbfCXZvf -->\r\n# ArcadianComputers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg7xcypymvedd0nn2gcn3zhwhv2d25nfteuxs9re5a7j97c3v4dxw`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting no here because funding only covers the initial research phase, we would prefer to see a full cost schedule up front to weigh that cost against what is being delivered.\r\n\r\n✅ Pros\r\nProactive and Data-Driven Approach: 🧐 This initiative aims to establish a structured, evidence-based process for evolving governance. Instead of reacting to problems as they arise, it proactively seeks to measure the health of the system, identify risks, and make informed improvements, professionalizing a critical aspect of the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nLed by a Highly Experienced and Credible Team: 🧑‍🏫 The project is driven by Input Output's Voltaire team, the very people who designed and implemented the core components of the current governance system (CIP-1694, Constitution). Their deep expertise is supplemented by a coalition including Constitutional Delegates, WADA, and Intersect, which minimizes execution risk and ensures a high-quality outcome.\r\n\r\nFocus on Community Engagement: 🤝 The plan isn't just an internal review. It heavily incorporates community feedback through workshops, surveys, and interviews. This ensures that the final recommendations are grounded in the real-world experiences and pain points of the people participating in governance (DReps, SPOs, ada holders).\r\n\r\nDelivers Tangible and Actionable Outcomes: 📝 While the project involves research, its outputs are concrete. It will deliver a public 'State of Governance' report, a playbook for repeating the process, and, most importantly, initial drafts of CPSs or CIPs. This directly translates research into the formal mechanisms for enacting change on Cardano.\r\n\r\nStrong Governance and Fund Management: The treasury withdrawal is managed by Intersect using audited smart contracts and is overseen by a committee of trusted community entities (Cardano Foundation, Sundae Labs, etc.). This structure provides high accountability and transparency for how the funds are used.\r\n\r\n❌ Cons\r\nRisk of Centralized Influence: 🤔 While the team's experience is a pro, the leadership from Input Output (IOG), Cardano's founding entity, could also be seen as a con. There is a risk that IOG's inherent biases or vision could disproportionately steer the outcome, potentially centralizing the direction of governance evolution rather than it being a purely grassroots effort.\r\n\r\nLack of a Direct, Quantifiable Financial ROI: 💰 Unlike a proposal for a dApp or infrastructure, the value of this project is abstract. It's difficult to calculate the direct financial return on a \"healthier governance system.\" For those who prioritize treasury spending on things with clear, measurable utility or profit potential, this expenditure may seem too intangible.\r\n\r\nSignificant Cost for Non-Technical Deliverables: The request is for nearly 600,000 Ada. Critics could argue this is a high price for what is essentially a research, consultation, and report-writing project. It raises the question of whether this work could be accomplished more affordably or through volunteer community efforts.\r\n\r\nFunding Only Covers the Initial Research Phase: ➡️ The proposal explicitly states that this funding is for the research and initial drafting of proposals. It clarifies that \"further funding would be required\" to advance a CPS to a CIP or to implement a CIP. This means the community is paying a significant sum for what is only the first step in a much longer and potentially more expensive process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Arturo",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibp4balmypvaldda52itsvnps7m7mo5zmngikgyein5omaxhjljay -->\r\n# Arturo\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytmr6kcyhmj3pp62peueqyc85fl5qvsp8mpkwsplg629alqkp478c`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting \"Yes\" on this proposal because it’s a crucial step toward evolving Cardano’s governance beyond Minimum Viable Governance. With this initiative, we’ll establish a transparent, data-driven process to measure key governance metrics, publish a detailed \"State of Governance\" report, and create actionable recommendations shaped directly by our community through workshops, surveys, and interviews. By turning these insights into Cardano Problem Statements or Improvement Proposals, we’ll ensure our governance grows in ways that reflect our shared priorities. Backed by experienced leaders, broad collaboration, and strong accountability, this project sets the stage for continuous, community-driven improvement in Cardano governance.",
