      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmZdmEsPBUo6MsUCnodcbFPhmi47t5aNrsjhJYLxrChyov -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmVXev36AfMAFoDqCBTdoUTxsBBRbKhM3eSkpDv2qS9QSC\r\n\r\nWhile improving our governance framework is critical for **sustainability** and I do like the proposal in question, I must however vote **NO** due to a fundamental conflict of interest in this proposal's leadership.\r\n\r\nIt states that Input Output's Voltaire team will lead the work. For **true decentralization** to flourish, the architects of a system cannot be the primary arbiters of its success and future direction. This vital research must be led by neutral, independent community bodies to ensure legitimacy and prevent entrenching the incumbent's vision.",
