    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA045-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlzyc3clg6), pois o estado de participação da comunidade ainda é muito baixo em comparação ao potencial saudável, visando diminuir o poder das baleias e descentralizar a tomada de decisão. Para isso, é necessário continuar estudando, debatendo e modificando as estruturas de governança. Além disso, a justificativa de gastos apresentada, bem como as métricas de avaliação e controle, foram bem apresentadas.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action (gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlzyc3clg6), because the level of community participation is still very low compared to a healthy potential, aiming to reduce the power of whales and decentralize decision-making. For this, it is necessary to continue studying, debating, and modifying governance structures. Furthermore, the expense justification presented, as well as the evaluation and control metrics, were well presented.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rbaker2024",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmZqnM5tJrcpiAy3VrXMuUoALX6YAtx1e5bv4RzJ5Ugrsy -->\r\n# Rbaker2024\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg7k2kqw0ghh5r3auvazthsrh20x74mcecfyt997za679pqxchhlr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmcGqn29xQeVDKkyXoywLQixqEA7FRK7VvqXQmHGN4pEfp\r\n\r\n## This is an unnecessary effort/level of management.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmY92JpHL5Y4esqAGN1uKhmvhxAcwduejp4imy86CCFwAN -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA has chosen to** abstain at this time while reserving the option to review and update this vote prior to the voting deadline**. This approach allows RCADA to allocate focus where immediate evaluation is most impactful, particularly on proposals that are close to threshold or raise significant procedural or constitutional concerns. If this proposal reaches the approv-al threshold prior to our review, the abstention will stand as a neutral signal of deferral, not op-position. Should further analysis be warranted, RCADA will update this vote accordingly.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRfAya21NjFzP84B8Y56fso9xL4H4gniQddeVXG9Mmn2s -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal marks a crucial step in Cardano’s post-MVG evolution. By grounding governance evaluation in data and real-world insights, it enables concrete improvements via actionable CIPs and CPSs, rather than reactive discussions.\r\n\r\nLed by experienced contributors and supported by a transparent framework with third-party oversight, the initiative offers both credibility and repeatability.\r\n\r\nこの提案は、CardanoのガバナンスをMVG以後も継続的に進化させるための重要な一歩です。単なる感覚的な議論ではなく、データと実地経験に基づいた健全性評価を行い、実効性のある改善提案（CIPやCPS）にまでつなげる姿勢は評価に値します。\r\n\r\nすでに実績のあるメンバーと信頼できる管理体制、公開型の成果物、第三者検証など、ガバナンスプロジェクトとして高い透明性と再現性が期待されます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/24_BeyondMinimumViable_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳592,780 for Beyond Minimum Viable Governance Iteratively Improvin\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this proposal because it addresses a critical need in Cardano’s ongoing governance evolution: moving beyond the Minimum Viable Governance (MVG) framework toward a more data-driven, inclusive, and community-informed governance model.\r\n\r\nThe project will deliver a comprehensive “State of Governance” report, benchmark KPIs, and produce actionable recommendations based on community feedback gathered through workshops, interviews, and surveys. These outcomes are essential to ensuring that Cardano’s governance system evolves based on evidence, not speculation.\r\n\r\nWhat sets this proposal apart is its coalition of proven contributors, including the Voltaire team from Input Output and key community leaders. Their past successes—such as CIP-1694 workshops and the global constitutional drafting process—demonstrate their capacity to lead this initiative effectively.\r\n\r\nThis project not only evaluates but also proposes improvements. If community consensus is reached, it will generate Cardano Problem Statements (CPSs) or Improvement Proposals (CIPs), reinforcing iterative governance as a living system. It also offers transparency, verifiability, and reuse by publishing a process playbook and open participation.\r\n\r\nGiven that this effort is embedded within Intersect’s budget framework and uses auditable smart contracts with third-party assurance, SIPO believes this initiative is a responsible and strategic use of treasury funds. It will provide long-term value by helping the ecosystem identify risks early, measure participation health, and elevate governance maturity through evidence-based refinement.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, SIPO casts a “Yes” vote for this proposal.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOはこの提案に「Yes」と投票します。その理由は、カルダノのガバナンスを「最小限の実装（MVG）」から、データに基づいた持続的かつ包括的な発展モデルへと進化させるために不可欠な取り組みだからです。\r\n\r\n本提案では、コミュニティ参加状況やKPIを測定する「State of Governance（ガバナンスの現状）」レポートが作成され、ワークショップやインタビュー、調査を通じて得られた実体験に基づく知見から、改善提案が導き出されます。これにより、感覚や印象ではなく、証拠に基づいたガバナンスの改善が可能になります。\r\n\r\n特筆すべきは、本プロジェクトが、Voltaireチームをはじめとした経験豊富なメンバーとコミュニティリーダーによる連携体制で構成されていることです。CIP-1694ワークショップや憲法起草プロセスなど、過去の実績からも信頼性は高く、本プロジェクトを成功に導く力があると判断できます。\r\n\r\nまた、本プロジェクトは単なる評価で終わるのではなく、Cardano Problem Statement（CPS）やCardano Improvement Proposal（CIP）など、具体的な改善策の提案にまで踏み込みます。さらに、再利用可能なプロセスプレイブックの公開や、外部からの参加も受け入れる設計となっており、透明性とオープン性が担保されています。\r\n\r\nIntersectによる管理の下、Sundae Labsのスマートコントラクトを活用し、第三者機関によるアシュアランス（検証）も含まれるなど、予算執行の信頼性も高く評価できます。\r\n\r\n本提案は、カルダノのガバナンスの健全性や参加状況を可視化し、リスクや課題を早期に特定して進化を促す重要な土台を築くものです。長期的に見ても、エコシステム全体にとって非常に価値ある取り組みです。\r\n\r\n以上の理由から、SIPOは本提案に賛成票を投じます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
