    {
      "voter": "Medusa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmZ2DD4He9ULFn9MGMLabiyTjksuD9spZo2orHxzHzxb7L -->\r\n# Medusa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yg5pzxhp0lu0m7757ww2hke8qhcuqgqt3c2ezphngwytz4gjr6yge`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI don’t consider this proposal important enough for the Cardano ecosystem to warrant funding from the treasury. It feels more like an investment pitch. Why should the ecosystem fund a closed, private project? On top of that, it uses vague phrasing like “expanding native asset support in wallets” — why be so abstract?",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://nimuepool.io/metadata/context-intersect-budget-withdrawals-2025.jsonld -->\r\n# Nimuë Lady of the Lake Pool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygj02llvuusnhphvhlxf7d2cxhs53twjnwwl5at3zwht4xc6xdgl4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI decided to vote ✅ YES on 37 treasury withdrawals, ➖ ABSTAIN on none, and ❌ NO on 2 treasury withdrawals from the Intersect 2025 budget.\r\n\r\nIt’s obvious I consider all proposals I approved in the budget vote on Ekklesia beneficial for Cardano, so those all receive a ✅ YES vote.\r\n\r\nI also vote ✅ YES for most proposals I initially abstained from or voted against in the Ekklesia vote. There are a few reasons for this:\r\n- Some proposals gained strong community support after all, so I don’t want to be the one standing in the way, especially when the requested amount is negligible in the bigger picture.\r\n- Some proposals I actually liked, but I found them more suitable for Catalyst. However, with all the delays, it now makes more sense to fund them as soon as possible.\r\n- Some didn’t get my initial support because I thought the requested amount was too high. But I now believe it’s better for the ecosystem to fund them, despite the larger budget, than not fund them at all.\r\n- I needed to vote for budget proposals with my own NCL in mind. Not all those I approved made it, however, so that leaves some room for other ones.\r\n\r\nI won’t approve the treasury withdrawal for two proposals:\r\n\r\n❌ Withdraw ₳3,000,000 for High-yield RWA Asset for Cardano: Tokenized Real Estate\r\nThis proposal won’t bring much value to our ecosystem, imho.\r\n\r\n❌ Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst: Extended Quadratic Funding---Zero Operational Costs\r\nWhile the proposal includes some interesting ideas for a fairer voting mechanism, I now support Catalyst and don’t see the need for an additional funding system at this moment, especially considering total spending. The requested amount also seems too small to meaningfully fund multiple projects. While the model relies on donations, it’s unclear what the donor incentive is. Since voting power is tied to donation size, why wouldn’t donors just support specific fundraisers run directly by the projects they care about? That way, they can ensure their contribution goes straight to their preferred initiative without needing it to win a vote first.\r\nI do appreciate the idea of a hybrid funding model where the treasury covers part of a project, but ideally, the remaining portion should come from investors rather than donations, imho.\r\nLastly, I don’t appreciate that the proposal’s title refers to Catalyst, even though it has no relationship to it. This seems intended to mislead people into thinking Catalyst would benefit from this proposal, which it doesn’t...\r\n\r\nI acknowledge there’s a metadata issue in the proposal “Withdraw ₳45,217 for MLabs Core Tool Maintenance & Enhancement: Cardano.nix”, but I approved it nonetheless, as the problem is minor and not worth obstructing the process.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "No stress",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWF4AtFaVF6oadAeVCdL2jjDWSxmK7D5x5j2RuQyZiL1X -->\r\n# No stress\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t3t35yx7j8nnh3wkqn2zzhgwqksksn85zv62pjrwzjawczwgyv7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is a large ask for a private company. I realize this is not Emurgo anymore so they dont have the genesis ada bank at their disposal. With USDA and USDM at basically the same market cap it seems unfair to pick a single winner at this time. If we could instead invest in both with liquidity and not private funds I would get behind that. The Treasury is supposed to fund public goods.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Patrick_Tobler",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSyEWUYHAaupLQirCM6zKweZ333LHs5DrwVz3ghSxatPs -->\r\n# Patrick_Tobler\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygm9wxzrrdqpt0hek5kj7ys6tmsc8dycp7tkjwqxqrhjr6csq3s3t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I would like to see Emurgo pay for this themselves, I still believe this will overall positively impact Cardano and thus I'm voting yes.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYJnQVqVNzG9tKR8bcYzNy4YrB6bGd5Eos9JwJhcNYEVH -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI cast a strong YES vote on this proposal.\r\n\r\nAt present, Cardano lacks a high-liquidity native stablecoin compared to ecosystems like Ethereum, and this is a major bottleneck for the growth of DeFi, user onboarding, and real-world utility. USDA has the potential to fill this critical gap, especially in the context of payments, remittances, and fiat interoperability.\r\n\r\nThis proposal also comes at a highly strategic moment: the recent passage of the GENIUS Act in the United States marks the first comprehensive legal framework for stablecoins. It signals that stablecoins are now being formally recognized as legitimate instruments within the global financial system. Given this shift, if Cardano fails to invest in this area now, it risks losing ground at a time when institutional momentum and regulatory clarity are rapidly accelerating.\r\n\r\nStablecoins are not just price-stable assets—they are foundational infrastructure for on-chain economies and essential to bridging the gap between blockchain and traditional finance. From my perspective, this is the most critical area for Cardano to prioritize, not just today but over the next decade.\r\n\r\nThis proposal represents a timely and high-impact initiative that aligns closely with Cardano’s long-term vision. I believe it deserves full support from the community.\r\n\r\n本提案に対し、強い支持のもとYES票を投じます。\r\n\r\n現在のCardanoには、Ethereumなど他の主要チェーンと比べて十分な流動性を持つネイティブステーブルコインが存在せず、これはDeFiの成長やユーザーの参入、実世界でのユースケース創出において大きな制約となっています。\r\nその中でUSDAは、この重大なギャップを埋める可能性を持った資産であり、特に決済・送金・法定通貨との接続という観点でCardanoにとって極めて重要なインフラとなり得ます。\r\n\r\nまた、本提案は非常に戦略的なタイミングでもあります。米国でジーニアス法（GENIUS Act）が正式に可決・成立し、ステーブルコインに関する包括的な法的枠組みが初めて整備されました。これは、ステーブルコインがグローバル金融システムの正式な手段として認識され始めていることを示しており、業界全体の信頼性・実用性に大きな追い風となっています。\r\n\r\nこのようなタイミングでCardanoが投資を怠れば、制度的・市場的な波に乗り遅れ、大きな機会損失を被るリスクが高いと考えています。\r\n\r\nステーブルコインは単なる価格安定資産ではなく、オンチェーン経済の土台であり、ブロックチェーンと現実世界をつなぐ中核的なコンポーネントです。私は個人的に、この分野こそがCardanoが最も優先的に力を入れるべき領域であり、今後10年を見据えたときにも、その重要性はさらに増していくと確信しています。\r\n\r\n本提案は、まさにその方向性と合致する、タイミングと内容の両面で非常に意義深いプロジェクトだと評価しています。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/33_ExpandingStablecoin_20250722/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳4,000,000 for Expanding Stablecoin Cardano Native Asset Support\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO’s Reason for Voting “Yes”\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this proposal because it addresses fundamental infrastructure gaps that currently limit the adoption, utility, and liquidity of Cardano-native assets and stablecoins. In particular, the proposal directly tackles the absence of institutional-grade custody, limited listings on exchanges, lack of fiat on/off-ramps in emerging markets, and the insufficient real-world use of Cardano-native stablecoins like USDA.\r\n\r\nBy allocating ₳4,000,000 from the Cardano Treasury, the project promises the following:\r\n\t•\tCustody Enablement: Strategic engagement with BitGo, Zodia, CipherBC, and others will allow USDA and other native assets to be held by top custodians. This is essential for institutional adoption.\r\n\t•\tMarket Access Expansion: Listing USDA pairs on centralized exchanges (CEXs), NEO banks, and OTC desks will significantly enhance liquidity and improve user access.\r\n\t•\tReal-world Utility: Integration with payment companies, real estate networks, and remittance providers will extend the use of USDA beyond DeFi into high-impact sectors.\r\n\t•\tAccessible Fiat Ramps: Low-cost fiat conversion for ADA and native assets, particularly in Africa, LATAM, and Asia, will break down one of the largest barriers to entry for real users.\r\n\r\nSIPO believes that stablecoins are the bridge between traditional finance and blockchain utility, and that Cardano must compete on infrastructure, usability, and accessibility.\r\n\r\nThis proposal is also compliant with constitutional treasury withdrawal processes via Intersect, includes legally binding contracts, delivery milestones, external audits, and an Oversight Committee involving trusted entities like Cardano Foundation, Sundae Labs, and NMKR. The risk management structure is robust.\r\n\r\nIn summary, SIPO votes “Yes” because this initiative strategically strengthens the Cardano ecosystem’s financial infrastructure, expands the reach of its stablecoins, and provides real economic rails that drive adoption globally.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOが「Yes」と投票する理由\r\n\r\nSIPOは本提案に賛成票を投じます。なぜなら、この提案は現在Cardanoエコシステムが直面している安定した資産運用基盤の不足という根本的課題を解決する重要な取り組みだからです。\r\n\r\n特に、以下のような課題に対して具体的なソリューションが提示されています。\r\n\t•\tカストディ（資産保管）支援の欠如： BitGoやZodiaなど主要カストディ業者との連携により、USDAなどのCardanoネイティブ資産が機関レベルで安全に保管可能となり、機関投資家の参入を促進します。\r\n\t•\tマーケットアクセスの不足： USDAを中心とした取引ペアをCEXやNEOバンク、OTC市場に広げ、流動性と取引機会を拡大します。\r\n\t•\t実社会でのユースケース不足： 不動産決済、送金、B2B決済などにUSDAを統合することで、DeFi以外のセクターでの利用を現実のものにします。\r\n\t•\tフロンティア市場における法定通貨との橋渡し： アフリカ・ラテンアメリカ・アジアなどで、低コストの法定通貨出入口（オン・オフランプ）を提供し、実需層の参入障壁を大きく下げます。\r\n\r\nSIPOは、安定したステーブルコイン流通こそがブロックチェーンと実世界をつなぐインフラの中核であると考えています。Cardanoはその基盤整備に真剣に取り組む必要があります。\r\n\r\nまた、この提案はIntersectを通じて憲法に則った手続きで提出されており、オフチェーン契約、成果物のマイルストーン設定、外部監査、Cardano FoundationやNMKRなど第三者による監督体制も整備されています。リスクマネジメントの観点からも信頼できる枠組みです。\r\n\r\n総じて、SIPOは本提案がCardanoのステーブルコイン・資産運用基盤の拡張を通じて、エコシステムの成長・採用拡大に直結する戦略的な一手であると判断し、「Yes」と投票します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
