    {
      "voter": "Patrick_Tobler",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNXLWy4vpGExKqCj3swH65Q1ELLGZJwDgpmXRPnFQczPw -->\r\n# Patrick_Tobler\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳130,903 for Lucid Evolution Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygm9wxzrrdqpt0hek5kj7ys6tmsc8dycp7tkjwqxqrhjr6csq3s3t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVery important tooling that absolutely needs to get funded!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳130,903 for Lucid Evolution Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVqzfKQF3R2MifXERi7b9WdkeBaT5iAJesPAZwvamRbzD -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳130,903 for Lucid Evolution Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nLucid is a widely adopted off-chain library that simplifies smart contract interactions on Cardano and plays a key role in enhancing the developer experience. It helps reduce complexity and accelerate dApp development across the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThis proposal ensures continued maintenance, feature enhancements, and improved documentation for Lucid—essential efforts to sustain a reliable and accessible development toolchain for Cardano.\r\n\r\nAnastasia Labs serves as the official maintainer of Lucid and has contributed to multiple open-source libraries and tools within the Cardano ecosystem. Their ongoing commitment to open-source development and transparency adds confidence to this initiative.\r\n\r\nI support this proposal as a meaningful investment in the long-term strength and usability of the Cardano developer environment.\r\n\r\n私はこの提案に Yes を投じます。\r\n\r\nLucidは、Cardanoにおけるオフチェーン処理を簡素化し、スマートコントラクトとの連携を効率化するために広く利用されている重要なライブラリです。開発者にとっての導入障壁を下げ、dApp開発の迅速化に貢献しています。\r\n\r\n本提案は、そのLucidの継続的な保守・機能改善・ドキュメント整備を目的とするものであり、エコシステム全体の開発基盤を支える重要な取り組みと判断します。\r\n\r\nAnastasia LabsはLucidの公式メンテナーとして継続的に開発を行っており、他にも複数のCardano関連ツールやライブラリに貢献してきた実績があります。オープンソースでの透明性と継続性も評価できるポイントです。\r\n\r\n開発者体験の向上と、Cardanoエコシステムの持続的発展に資する基盤整備として、本提案を支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/08_LucidEvolution_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳130,903 for Lucid Evolution Maintenance administered by Intersect\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO casts a “Yes” vote on the proposal titled “Withdraw ₳130,903 for Lucid Evolution Maintenance administered by Intersect.”\r\n\r\nOur reasoning is outlined below:\r\n\r\n1. Critical Infrastructure for the Cardano Developer Ecosystem\r\n\r\nLucid Evolution is a vital open-source library that enables seamless interaction with smart contracts in the Cardano ecosystem using JavaScript/TypeScript. It serves as a backbone for many DApps and significantly improves the developer experience. Continuous maintenance is essential to keep up with protocol changes and ensure network-wide reliability.\r\n\r\n2. Open-Source Commitment and Transparency\r\n\r\nLucid Evolution is fully open-source and publicly accessible on GitHub. This transparency encourages external contributions, community review, and helps maintain the tool as a public good.\r\n\r\n3. Proven Track Record of Anastasia Labs\r\n\r\nAnastasia Labs has contributed to almost every major dApp on Cardano and maintains over 50 open-source tools and libraries. Their long-term involvement and technical leadership bring reliability and accountability to this maintenance work.\r\n\r\n4. Intersect’s Oversight and Smart Contract-Based Budget Governance\r\n\r\nThis proposal is administered under Intersect’s legal and operational framework. Treasury funds will be managed using audited smart contracts by Sundae Labs, with safeguards in place via a five-member Oversight Committee. This structure ensures integrity, transparency, and proper milestone validation.\r\n\r\n5. Alignment with the Constitutionally Approved Budget Process\r\n\r\nThe proposal is part of a constitutionally authorized ₳275M budget action administered by Intersect. It complies with Article IV Sections 4 and 5 of the Cardano Constitution and follows a legitimate, community-backed process.\r\n\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this proposal as it sustains a strategic and foundational piece of infrastructure for Cardano’s future, under a transparent and accountable governance framework.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、本提案「Lucid Evolution Maintenance」に賛成票を投じました。\r\n\r\nその理由は以下の通りです。\r\n\r\n1. Cardano開発者基盤の中核的インフラの維持\r\n\r\nLucid Evolutionは、Cardano上でスマートコントラクトとオフチェーンコードを接続する主要なJavaScript/TypeScriptライブラリです。現在、非常に多くのdAppがこのライブラリを使用しており、開発者体験（DX）を大きく向上させています。このような基盤的インフラの継続的メンテナンスは、エコシステム全体の健全性と成長に不可欠です。\r\n\r\n2. 完全なオープンソースと透明性\r\n\r\nLucid Evolutionは完全にオープンソースであり、GitHub上でコードが公開されています。この透明性は、コミュニティ監査や協力を促進し、公共財としての価値を最大限に引き出す仕組みとなっています。\r\n\r\n3. Anastasia Labsの実績と信頼性\r\n\r\nこのライブラリを開発・保守しているAnastasia Labsは、Cardano上で多数のdApp開発を支援してきた経験豊富な開発集団です。また、50以上のオープンソースプロジェクトをメンテナンスしている実績もあり、その継続性と技術力は高く評価されています。\r\n\r\n4. Intersectによる契約管理と予算統制\r\n\r\n本プロジェクトはIntersectが契約・監督主体として関与し、Sundae Labsが構築したスマートコントラクト管理ツールによって資金管理・支出の透明性が確保されます。また、Oversight Committee（監査委員会）による三重チェック体制により、ガバナンスリスクも適切に管理されます。\r\n\r\n5. Cardano予算方針との整合\r\n\r\nこの提案は、事前に承認されたIntersectによる275M ADA予算配分の一部であり、憲法第IV条に準拠したプロセスに基づいています。Cardanoの分散的な予算プロセスの模範的な例と言えます。\r\n\r\n結論 \r\n\r\nSIPOは、Lucid Evolutionの持続可能な開発とCardanoエコシステム全体への貢献を高く評価し、この提案への資金配分は正当かつ戦略的に重要であると判断しました。よって「Yes」を投じました。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
