    {
      "voter": "BTBF_XSP",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmP7RpEbhTbAwZRNsvicrBJPiFLXMc1GNLzC3jR9rxe3a9 -->\r\n# BTBF_XSP\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2vyrqh0fa4qh4tmy7322va6ryk78uh6szppezaft0watyqp5hdwx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私の投票ポリシーはCARDANO2025ロードマップを実現するべく基盤技術の維持と強化、コア開発と研究、マーケティングの強化を支持しています。事前のオフチェーン投票ではNoにした提案においても、提案内容に関しては一定の必要性を感じているため資金調達プロセスのスケジュールや提案内容を精査したうえでYESに投じます。\r\nMy voting policy supports the maintenance and enhancement of foundational technologies, core development and research, and the strengthening of marketing efforts to realize the CARDANO 2025 roadmap. Even for proposals I previously voted \"No\" on during the off-chain voting phase, I recognize a certain level of necessity in their content. Therefore, after carefully reviewing both the proposal content and the funding schedule, I will cast a \"Yes\" vote.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSHuTMLNhbrbvvDvuSWoasumTH8ftUpsjyRjR7PexTUW4 -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNFTCDNを18ヶ月間無料提供することで、ネイティブアセットを扱う開発者のコスト・実装負荷を大幅に削減する実用的な提案です。既に稼働中のインフラを無償化するモデルであり、実績とスケーラビリティを兼ね備えているため、賛成します。\r\n*******\r\nThis proposal makes the already operational NFTCDN free for Cardano developers for 18 months. It provides scalable infrastructure for native assets and significantly lowers development barriers. Given its clear utility and modest cost, I vote in favor.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcNyrUCUNMZFVJmC5iHKbP4zqpq1KyRcDJ9z5sQ5RW4Bt -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe voted yes because they presented the content in great detail. Their solution has positive impacts on the Cardano ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZQkyxECXDqRpANGPgQoQ5HzHXAJ7oRDghZgefFqGeEJG -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Long-Term Sustainability**\r\nThe idea of a native asset CDN—serving token icons, metadata, and branding—is helpful for improving UX and consistency across wallets and dApps. However, it is not a critical protocol service and does not directly impact network resilience or security.\r\n\r\n**Builder and Ecosystem Growth**\r\nA well-executed CDN could make asset integration smoother for developers and improve token discoverability for users. Yet, the technical complexity and impact are limited, and much of the value can be delivered using existing web infrastructure at a fraction of the proposed cost.\r\n\r\n**Decentralization and Community Engagement**\r\nThe service would be public-facing and improve uniformity in asset presentation across interfaces. Still, it does not meaningfully increase decentralization or empower new participants, and the proposal lacks a clear open governance or stewardship model for long-term sustainability.\r\n\r\n**Treasury Spending Concerns**\r\n₳605,000 for a relatively lightweight web service is excessive. Comparable services—static asset hosting, cache/CDN distribution, metadata indexing—could be delivered reliably for ₳100,000–₳150,000 with ongoing maintenance. The proposal does not justify the inflated cost with itemized budgeting or technical constraints. Given the overestimation, lack of critical urgency, and weak accountability mechanisms, we recommend voting NO on this proposal. If resubmitted with a leaner scope and clearer delivery plan, it may be reconsidered.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Africa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Abdulazizkarma1/Cardano-Africa-DRep-Data/refs/heads/main/NTFCDN%20BUDGET.jsonld -->\r\n# Cardano Africa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytj9kz0n5yamacgcj8jr6apn36hx5suzqpefxvhy4cvfqmsqangtx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis treasury withdrawal request is to fund a free Content Delivery Network (CDN) for Cardano NFTs and native assets, by making NFTCDN, an existing service, free-to-use for 18 months.\r\n\r\nThis proposalis great because building infrastructure to reliably display Cardano NFTs (images, metadata, etc.) is hard, slow, and expensive. NFTCDN already exists and works and they just want to remove the paywall and open it up to all devs.\r\n\r\nHowever, let's talk about long-term sustainability. After 18 months, what happens? Do they go back to being paid only? Will smaller devs get locked out again? There’s no clear exit strategy post-18 months. It could become a Trojan horse for vendor lock.\r\n\r\nits no doubt this project solves a critical technical problem for Cardano devs especially smaller projects and we at Cardano Africa Academy supports this initiative.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://bafybeib652u6d6mihjpw6tp64xadrh3sez6cnae2np3nr5izsfztzey3fa.ipfs.dweb.link/ -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmSwBobJWfJ9sVZew4PH2v9UN6scWLUPtuU4ciecHUv2Cw\r\n\r\nOur initial 'no' vote was based on financial and funding concerns, which have been addressed by additional information from the NFTCDN team, found in the reference materials.\r\n\r\nThis proposal funds a free Native Asset Content Delivery Network (CDN) for all Cardano developers for 18 months. This infrastructure solves a complex and expensive problem for builders, and the service is already trusted and utilized by key ecosystem projects like the Eternl and Vespr wallets. Making it free removes high-cost barriers, especially for low-revenue and non-profit projects.\r\n\r\nKey points that justify this change:\r\n\r\n* **Addressed Financial Concerns:** The NFTCDN team provided a clear budget breakdown for salaries and infrastructure costs based on current usage patterns.  \r\n* **Clear Long-Term Strategy:** The 18-month funding period is strategic. It will be used to gather meaningful data to allow DReps to vote on one of three sustainable future paths for the service: making it open-source, decentralizing it, or transferring ownership to a non-profit.  \r\n* **Appropriate Funding Venue:** Our initial assessment suggested Project Catalyst as a more suitable venue. However, the NFTCDN team clarified that no appropriate funding category exists in Catalyst for this type of infrastructure project, which led them to the Treasury Withdrawal process.\r\n\r\nWe now consider this proposal to be a suitably justified, strategic investment in public infrastructure that offers a clear path to long-term sustainability and provides immediate value to the entire Cardano developer community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmRbV7unnH6eMRo1WDfGDqqnjf9hr8NHZEjCvxXSnphGSM -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳605,000 for A free Native Asset CDN for Cardano Developers\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmZQ5z9s3tSff2tZxdsDwnWP2emKPbHXrvjvJQPenX5Quz\r\n\r\nI plan to vote YES on most projects I’ve supported in Ekklesia. To stay transparent, I’ll rate each project across six categories, scoring 0 to 2 per category (max 12 points). Projects scoring below 6 won’t get my support. I’ll consider supporting those with 7–8 points, and will fully support any scoring 9 or more.\r\n\r\nThe categories are:\r\n\r\n- Key infrastructure, research, or essential funding: 0\r\n- Team strength, feasibility, and track record: 1\r\n- Impact on the Cardano ecosystem: 1\r\n- Value for money: 1\r\n- Cost compared to similar proposals: 1\r\n- Personal or community usage and benefit: 1\r\n\r\nTotal score: 5",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
