    {
      "voter": "ADAR_Chris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPhyW1HbYdnKP33J3ZXSyy5rRyqRLSY5oZDyYxShSn4BC -->\r\n# ADAR_Chris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26nj0u86z00s2c6yteecduedrzxxrxrn39th5mau0h0r5gszp025`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile not in full agreement with the number itself, a vote YES here is an attempt to be pragmatic. The 200M NCL, which I preferred, failed. I prefer this proposal over the 350M competing proposal from Intersect because it is a more conservative limit, extends the timeline, and is community sourced. Most importantly, I feel that we need to clear the NCL hurdle to avoid funding delays.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Agora-Cardano/dRep_metadata_storage/refs/heads/main/Governance_Actions/NCL_300M.jsonld -->\r\n# Agora Cardano (by Rodrigo Pacini)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9dq806jcm56wzhnv2yrf6gcyq7h4gap8gxewfykk0dtfs7vf843`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRationale – Abstain Vote on the 300M ADA NCL (Epochs 563–635)\r\nAs a dRep, I am casting an abstain vote on this governance action.\r\n\r\nThe proposed 300M ADA cap for Epochs 563–635 is technically reasonable and aligned with the Treasury’s projected inflows. It also represents roughly double the annual withdrawal amount previously seen in the Project Catalyst program (~50M ADA per four-month cycle), which should not result in exaggerated sell pressure — especially considering that most proposals will likely be disbursed over time in tranches tied to deliverables.\r\n\r\nStill, I cannot fully endorse the way this NCL has been structured. My concerns include:\r\n\r\nIt initiates a budget cycle mid-calendar year, which may further confuse proposers and dReps. While not the most critical issue, this desynchronization introduces unnecessary inconsistency and reduces predictability in treasury coordination and planning.\r\n\r\nIt includes no mechanism to limit how much a single entity, group, or proposal may request from the total NCL amount. This leaves room for excessive concentration of funds and repeats problematic dynamics seen previously — such as budget dominance by large actors.\r\n\r\nI acknowledge that including such limits within the NCL governance action itself would likely violate the Cardano Constitution, which defines the NCL solely as a cap on total withdrawals.\r\nHowever, I believe it is good practice for any group proposing an NCL to also outline a strategy to establish such guardrails and percentage limits in a follow-up governance action.\r\nSo far, this concern has not been addressed or signaled as a priority by any of the current proposers.\r\n\r\nSuch a complementary governance action could provide political guidance for dReps when voting on future Budget or Treasury Withdrawal Actions, promoting fairer and more decentralized distribution of Treasury resources — a principle this community is proud to stand for.\r\n\r\nWhile I voted NO on the previous 200M ADA NCL due to the risk of centralizing nearly all treasury funds around IOG proposals, I am abstaining here because I see the 300M ADA limit as a more appropriate compromise — one that could still allow critical community-led initiatives to receive funding and reduce overconcentration in the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nMy abstention is a rejection of the current structure, without blocking the continuity of treasury operations. I remain committed to pushing for structural reforms that strengthen the legitimacy, predictability, and fairness of Cardano’s budget process.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "AKYO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWE2zPdgNy6m5VhyNK9QCJufX2sPqfid624BouJkG9QX3 -->\r\n# AKYO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yts3qdjsqcnhld4r3uek2uu0n2tnh824tgnf75a83q3yhequuy54u`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n本提案に賛成票を投じます。これまで350M ADAの純変動上限（NCL）を支持してきましたが、その期間の約40％が経過していることを踏まえ、Epoch 563〜635に向けた本提案の300M ADAという上限は、財務運営における予測可能性と継続性を確保するための実務的な判断であると考え、支持します。\\nI vote YES on this proposal. While I have supported the 350M ADA Net Change Limit (NCL), considering that around 40% of that period has already passed, I view the proposed 300M ADA limit for Epochs 563–635 as a practical measure to ensure predictability and continuity in treasury management, and I support it.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BTBF_XSP",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmT6MUw5hcJzq8BAy7xCzdHnKKPpQ6p1C9WBDkuc3QrytF -->\r\n# BTBF_XSP\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2vyrqh0fa4qh4tmy7322va6ryk78uh6szppezaft0watyqp5hdwx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the proposal may seem reasonable at first glance, I believe that using the calendar year as a clear and familiar reference point is easier for people to understand. Setting a budget period that spans across years creates an awkward timeframe and risks disrupting future cycles.This also raises the issue that a clearly defined fiscal year needs to be established for future NCLs.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "BWtake(長崎)Japan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BWtake/DRepdata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context20250515NCL300M.jsonld -->\r\n# BWtake(長崎)Japan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcw6qzpqqclx2yd0zy64ztvlkkhnf6yrzza8whgnq4vz5gh89626`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n私は、本提案に対してNO票を投じます。これは、私が以前350M ADAのNCL提案に対して慎重ながらも賛同の意を示した判断と軸を一にするものです。\r\n 2025年前半は、Cardanoにとって分散型ガバナンスの制度実装、L2技術の導入、ミドルウェアとトークノミクス設計の革新など、全方位的な基盤強化が求められている局面です。私は当時、この重要なフェーズにおいて、資金制約が進展の障害とならぬよう、例外的な支出上限拡大に賛同する立場をとりました。\r\n 今回の提案は、まだ審議中または承認直後の複数の重要提案の執行余地に影響を及ぼす可能性があり、現段階では時期尚早とも考えられます。また、350Mからの引き下げについては、その必要性や緊急性を裏付ける根拠が十分に共有されていないと感じています。結果として、先に設定された財政方針との整合性が揺らぐ懸念もあります。\r\n したがって私は、1. 現行の350M NCLを当面維持、2. 実行フェーズにある重要提案を財政的に支援、3. 将来的なNCL見直しは次期財政年度の状況を見据えて検討すべき、という立場をとります。\r\n 本判断は、拡張的支出の常態化を望むものではなく、今この時期に必要な柔軟性を確保するための戦略的意思表示です。\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI cast a NO vote on this proposal. This decision is consistent with the position I previously took when I supported the 350M ADA NCL proposal, with a cautious but strategic outlook.\r\n\r\nThe first half of 2025 marks a critical period for Cardano—one that requires foundational development across multiple domains, including the implementation of decentralized governance, the deployment of L2 technologies, and innovation in middleware and tokenomics. At that time, I expressed support for an exceptional increase in the spending cap, recognizing the need for flexibility in such a pivotal phase.\r\n\r\nThis proposal, however, may constrain the execution of several important initiatives that are still under review or were only recently approved. At this stage, it may be premature. Furthermore, the rationale for reducing the limit from 350M ADA has not been clearly substantiated in terms of necessity or urgency. As such, it raises concerns about consistency with the fiscal direction already established.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I advocate the following: 1. Maintain the current 350M ADA NCL in the near term, 2. Support critical proposals already in the execution pipeline, and 3. Reassess the NCL in light of the next fiscal cycle.\r\n\r\nThis is not a call for continued high spending, but rather a strategic expression in favor of preserving the flexibility needed at this particular juncture.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmP76xZuNcrDdrxeDtPZPyZtPE2zJQMGPckjos6xxkb5SF -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe budget process has been going on for months, with many proposals spanning 12 months, so we feel it makes sense to set up the NCL to include a plan for 2026.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Africa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Abdulazizkarma1/Cardano-Africa-DRep-Data/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(1).jsonld -->\r\n# Cardano Africa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytj9kz0n5yamacgcj8jr6apn36hx5suzqpefxvhy4cvfqmsqangtx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal seeks to establish a Net Change Limit (NCL) of 300 million ADA for the period from epoch 563 (8 June 2025) to epoch 635 (3 June 2026). The NCL defines the maximum amount of ADA that can be withdrawn from the Cardano Treasury during this period.\r\n\r\nThe set NCL of 300 million ADA is reasonable considering the fact that it covers ~72 epochs.\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I support this NCL proposal because it upholds the constitutional requirement for controlled Treasury spending, supports the funding of year-long proposals starting in mid-2025, and ensures governance continuity. The 300M ADA cap is aligned with projected Treasury inflows, maintaining a responsible balance between innovation and sustainability.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmWExL9U66wtWuqa9ZdvbQHwfPXJ5NHN2dpbZL5XXNAHnd -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmTS68ewzGwKwhNZ6n1ma7BarW4uaz5vPTadACWLMEcL3t\r\n\r\nAn NCL for the entirety of 2025 (350 million ada, Epochs 532-604) has already been approved by DReps. This new proposal seeks to alter a significant portion of that approved 2025 NCL and define an NCL for part of 2026. While we acknowledge the constitutional provision for NCLs (Article IV, Section 3), this proposal, in the current context, raises serious concerns regarding governance stability, procedural prudence, and the necessity of such a change at this time.\r\n\r\nOur decision to vote 'NO' is based on the following primary reasons:\r\n\r\n**1. Undermining Stability of the Approved 2025 NCL:** The Foundation believes, barring compelling reasons for a change, it is critical to uphold the stability and predictability of the already-approved NCL for the 2025 calendar year. Attempting to alter this ratified NCL mid-year, as this proposal suggests, risks undermining trust in Cardano's fiscal parameters and the finality of governance decisions. Teams and projects require a stable NCL to confidently prepare and submit budget proposals for the current cycle.\r\n\r\n**2. Premature and Fragmented Approach for 2026 NCL Coverage:** Defining a portion of the 2026 NCL now, before the 2025 budget cycle has substantially progressed and its learnings can be assessed, is premature. A more thorough, deliberate, and holistic approach should be taken to establish the NCL for 2026 later in 2025. Deciding a new NCL so far in advance complicates long-term planning.\r\n\r\n**3. Insufficient Justification for Revision and Extension:** The motivation that some budgets span 12 months and extend into 2026 does not inherently necessitate an immediate revision of the 2025 NCL or an early partial definition of the 2026 NCL. Budgets spanning across NCL periods can have their withdrawals managed within the respective active NCLs. Although we welcome proactive strategy on the 2026 budget, the proposal does not provide a compelling enough reason to disrupt the current NCL and ongoing budget processes aligned with the 350M ada limit.\r\n\r\n**4. Focus on Current Governance Cycle Learnings:** With the first on-chain budget cycle under the approved 350M NCL for 2025 yet to be fully implemented and evaluated, the priority should be on gaining experience and insights from this initial period to inform 2026 strategy. Introducing further changes to the NCL framework before these learnings are consolidated is not advisable.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> **_NOTE on \"Internal Voting\":_** \r\n> \r\n> The fields _constitutional_ and _unconstitutional_ below reflect the CF governance teams' individual opinions whether they are _for_ or _against_ the proposal. \r\n> Reason for this inconsistency is, that CIP-136 is at the moment only applicable to CC rationales, but we want to record the internal opinions of our DRep assessment transparently as well.\r\n\r\n---",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Whale",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXxR6pgRJuFjpgKCuEyUqTN8K4UxDVrqbok1uBpDfg4a1 -->\r\n# Cardano Whale\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfnuetvunwfl83qaq4e7vlg5w8dwwjmtt4j6tr9fegqvgmgtq5scg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe timeline for this NCL is more clearly described than the other NCL votes. However, I want to clarify that it had always been my intention that an NCL gets consumed pro rata. E.g. if the NCL is 200m and commences in July, no more than give or take 100m should be spent in that half a year, and no more than 200m over the full 72 epochs (1y). In this sense, I recognise a 300m ADA as too high an ask and hence I will reject it like the previously proposed 300m and 350m NCL votes. Rationales for my NCL target (personal preference 150m) can be found in previous votes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Satuchac/DRep/refs/heads/main/008_My%20Rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for the governance action setting a 300M ADA Net Change Limit (NCL) for epochs 563–635.\r\n\r\nAs I’ve emphasized in previous discussions on NCL, it’s essential to balance monetary policy protection with ecosystem investment while also accounting for delays in the budget process.\r\n\r\nDReps approved a budget of approximately 281M ADA, but the governance action for it has yet to be submitted. Setting the NCL at 300M ADA ensures an additional ~20M ADA remains available for spending if needed.\r\n\r\nA one-year NCL period makes sense, beginning in Q3 2025 and ending in Q2 2026—one year after this governance action’s potential ratification.\r\n\r\nWhile I personally favor a lower NCL of around 250M ADA, the majority of the voting stake supports higher spending, and that decision must be respected.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/Info_10_3.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDue to the failure of the 200M Net Change Limit proposal, I am switching my vote to YES for the 300M ADA limit. The 300M cap replaces the existing 350M cap with a noticeably tighter ceiling while still covering every budget item that cleared the 50% off-chain vote.  Several of those items are unlikely to also secure the 67% withdrawal vote, meaning that real spending is expected to be comfortably below 300M ADA. Furthermore, ADA’s market price has risen roughly 50% since those budgets were priced, making further restraint both feasible and prudent. This compromise keeps spending within expected inflows, preserves continuity for approved projects, and moves us toward more conservative treasury management until the governance framework matures.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tarrant64/mr_cata_gov/refs/heads/main/300M_Through2026_proposal.jsonld -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe idea behind the proposal adjusting the NCL to cover 2026 can make sense, however I disagree with the motivation.  It's letting an NCL be driven budget proposal timelines.  I also do not see a need to have an NCL timeline match exactly to a budget proposal length. There is nothing to stop a treasury withdraw prior to the end of 2025 for a project that will not be completed until some time in 2026, or even later.  NCLs do not have a need to stay open to meet budget timelines - it would never end.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dave",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZLw2ECSa9T5gJsMLbcQriwiAdgiXofH7RvF2doa2uQbg -->\r\n# Dave\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygsgfhcydhlfglamhzkjn97rz3edef8a4z99fwl2frcwnrcmgurt3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI previously voted Yes on an NCL proposal at 200 million ADA, and No on proposals targeting 300 million ADA or more. For this current 300 million ADA proposal, I’m voting No again, for the same reasons. I continue to believe these limits are too high for the current stage of Cardano governance.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmciFzrtj9ku4PQow6DSDpy5tp9R14gWEw8pimN4NKwyxV -->\r\n# drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nbetter define smth until EOY, instead of a random date in the middle. \r\nAlso, no reason to define a NCL for such a far-away time period when the learnings about the first cycle are just about to happen.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/300M_NCL.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, EMURGO votes No on the Info Action titled Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nRepeatedly adjusting the cap could create delays in the governance process, which may prevent critical funding from reaching the necessary projects, ultimately slowing down Cardano’s development.\r\nTo conclude, 2025 Net Change Limit(9b62b3c632f329016a968ac25211825bb4f84b12461121c7da3aa11df92370f900), which was approved by the majority of DReps, represents the maximum possible withdrawal amount from the Treasury, but it’s not a fixed target that must be fully used. EMURGO believes this is a reasonable initial cap for the year.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00012_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted YES on gov_action1vdlrcftd48qn2zz8egepr6xyfcmxpfz8r69k769gc5mhg662adesq9yy8pl. 300m NCL for the remainder of 2025 and the first half of 2026 should cover most proposal costs. A new NCL can be proposed in early 2026, if need be.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZenhXGePLNvNuyQw8vjMxpqLe7bpLzfrS22uoXj9UJ7c -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis NCL surpasses my personal NCL of 250M ADA and violates my stance on fiscal responsibility. I went through the Ekklesia budget voting process, and could not find enough worthwhile proposals to surpass my NCL of 250M ADA. I am concerned that NCL will end up being a spending cap that will be filled every time, so I have to vote as such.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ha-Nguyen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmaNQpkj29XZbjZofWUqK4Z8TWxYPYacfNp4S5mvQBE4ab -->\r\n# Ha-Nguyen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2z8gktqj27kwmmxesd0y484f7p4z9tjf5xu8m4sucstm3gvtywlp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES on this proposal because:\r\n\r\n1) This is a necessary next step to ensure continuity for 12-month budget cycles. Many current proposals are structured to begin in Q3 2025 and span one year. Without a Net Change Limit (NCL) that covers this full fiscal period, project implementation could be disrupted.\r\n\r\n2) The 300M ADA limit aligns with the spending direction already approved by the community. DReps have previously approved a budget of approximately 281M ADA, but the corresponding withdrawal governance action has not yet been submitted. Setting the NCL at 300M ADA provides a buffer to adjust if needed.\r\n\r\n3) Epochs 563–635 correspond to Q3 2025 through Q2 2026, making this a practical reference frame for future annual budget cycles. Having a fixed time window also helps stakeholders plan more effectively.\r\n\r\n*Setting a 300M ADA NCL for this period is a reasonable step that balances fiscal prudence with the need for strategic ecosystem investment during a critical phase of the Voltaire era.\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\nJapanese Translation\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n私はこの提案にYES票を投じます。その理由は以下の通りです：\r\n\r\n1) 本提案は、12か月予算サイクルの継続性を維持するために必要な次のステップです。現在の多くの提案は2025年第3四半期に開始し、1年間を予定しています。この期間全体をカバーするNet Change Limit（NCL）がなければ、プロジェクトの実行が中断される可能性があります。\r\n\r\n2) 300M ADAの上限は、すでにコミュニティによって承認された支出方針と整合しています。DRepたちは以前、約281M ADAの予算を承認しましたが、資金引き出しのガバナンスアクションはまだ提出されていません。NCLを300M ADAに設定することで、必要に応じた調整の余地が確保されます。\r\n\r\n3) Epoch 563～635は2025年第3四半期から2026年第2四半期に対応し、将来の年間予算サイクルにおける標準的な時間枠としても妥当です。固定された期間を設けることで、関係者の計画立案が容易になります。\r\n\r\n※この時期に300M ADAのNCLを設定することは、財政的慎重さとエコシステムへの戦略的投資の必要性のバランスを取る合理的な判断であり、Voltaire時代の重要な局面において極めて適切なステップです。\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\nVietnamese Translation\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nTôi bỏ phiếu YES cho đề xuất này vì:\r\n\r\n1) Đây là bước tiếp theo cần thiết để duy trì tính liên tục cho các ngân sách 12 tháng. Nhiều đề xuất hiện tại được thiết kế theo chu kỳ một năm, bắt đầu từ quý 3/2025. Nếu không có NCL bao phủ cả năm tài chính này, tiến trình triển khai sẽ bị gián đoạn.\r\n\r\n2) Mức giới hạn 300M ADA phù hợp với định hướng chi tiêu đã được cộng đồng chấp thuận. Trước đó, các DRep đã phê duyệt ngân sách khoảng 281M ADA, nhưng hành động rút quỹ vẫn chưa được đệ trình. Thiết lập NCL ở mức 300M ADA đảm bảo có khoảng đệm tài chính để điều chỉnh nếu cần thiết.\r\n\r\n3) Giai đoạn Epoch 563–635 tương ứng với Q3/2025 đến Q2/2026, rất hợp lý để sử dụng làm khung NCL chuẩn cho các chu kỳ ngân sách hằng năm về sau. Việc thiết lập khung thời gian cố định cũng giúp các bên lập kế hoạch dễ dàng hơn.\r\n\r\n* Thiết lập NCL 300M ADA cho giai đoạn này là một bước đi hợp lý, dung hòa giữa quản trị tài chính thận trọng và nhu cầu đầu tư phát triển hệ sinh thái trong thời điểm quan trọng của giai đoạn Voltaire.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HeptaSean",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmRrwGfWo8JGKc5abZEcC7QQADAfLNBoeCksW67NPs6zej -->\r\n# HeptaSean\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf8p623g9s0yxnlnjzealgajyxl57k7n6saeavc7azg0crcahnul9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting Yes on a treasury net change limit of 300 million ADA for the coming 12 months. This is a conservative maximum that only allows to spend what the treasury will probably earn in that time according to my predictions in https://forum.cardano.org/t/fundamental-critcism-of-the-budget-process/143519#p-367722-net-change-limit-2. Also, extending the validity of the net change limit into 2026 makes a lot of sense since we have already wasted so much time on this mindless budget bureaucracy.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmeGxPD8SJUbJEb6XGEwbbwu69myvLDp3WsdC2geaBHc4m -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting \"Yes\" to Net Change Limit for e563 to 635. Although I believe the Net Change Limit should be much lower, 300M ada limit would be better than non-limitation for now. I would vote Yes if we have lower NCL info action emerged.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZu5LGaG2s7Ct7LTpZGdJYyBUP9prxUysn5mSQrXMuZtE -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will change my vote for the 300M NCL from NO to YES. \r\n\r\na. It is not backdated to the start of the 2025 calendar year, meaning that a new NCL will not be needed for a full year\r\nb. The spending period matches a full year from now (around May 17 when epoch 563 started), and the rate is more sustainable than the 350M ADA NCL that has been approved. \r\n\r\nGiven we're still figuring out the budgeting process, this is a more responsible choice than the already approved 350M ADA NCL.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOLD RATIONALE FOR NO VOTE BELOW\r\n==================\r\n\r\nI voted YES for an earlier previous NCL action that sought to set the NCL at ₳200M for 8 months until the end of the calendar year. I saw that as a better choice than the initially proposed ₳350M NCL motion. That vote still stands and I think it would help to jumpstart the budget process. \r\n\r\nThis current action proposes to set the NCL at ₳300M for 12 months from Epoch 532 to the end of Epoch 604. On the face of it, they may be similar. \r\n\r\nYet, for a 12 month period, I do not support ₳300M ADA in spending. \r\n\r\nI favor an annual (12 month) NCL of up to ₳200M - 250M ADA at a time when budgetary \r\nprocesses are weak, auditing capacity is unproven, DRep resistance to outside pressure is low, the fate of Intersect MBO is uncertain and the entire process remains convoluted because it is minimum viable governance. \r\n\r\nA complex Minimum Viable Governance voting stage means that many small DReps who cannot devote hours and hours to the process with the current rugged tooling and shifts - are either unable to participate or unwilling to participate. \r\n\r\nMore organized institutional DReps or holders some of whom may be both DReps and also requesting funds from the treasury - face lower barriers to accessing funds. I see this as a danger. \r\n\r\nOver the Ekklesia tool, I have voted YES for ₳141.43m in funding requests. I have abstained from voting on Catalyst that is a further 70M ADA (likely to pass) and from voting on Intersect's budget (max 20M ADA, possibly lower after recent changes). \r\n\r\nIf my voting tally were to be added up with the Intersect and the Catalyst requests - the total would still be below ₳250M. \r\n\r\nBy voting NO on this proposal, I am signaling that a NCL of up to ₳200M - 250M ADA would be my preferred choice as it is more responsible at this stage of minimum viable governance.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jonahkoch/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_NCL_300M_Epoch_563-635.jsonld -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting yes on the proposal to, Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635. Setting the NCL at 300 million ADA matches the expected annual treasury inflow, ensuring that we maintain fiscal responsibility while still enabling meaningful investment in Cardano’s continued growth. This figure strikes the right balance between prudent spending and supporting the ecosystem’s development needs. I also appreciate the structuring of this NCL to cover the remainder of 2025 as well as a significant portion of 2026, thus moving the budgetary cycle away from the calendar year end and holiday seasons.  Moving key decision making processes to a summer fall cadence will make for more reliable participation.  This approach also provides continuity for ongoing and upcoming budget proposals, many of which are designed around 12-month cycles.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Ken Ladd",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoesq/08JUN2025-yy8pl/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# Ken Ladd\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygkfv2u7aazrfhqgh0qssramjd6av09rsh3ejd0rd95cmusezderl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote No on the proposed “Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635” Info Action (Governance Action ID: gov_action1vdlrcftd48qn2zz8egepr6xyfcmxpfz8r69k769gc5mhg662adesq9yy8pl). \r\n\r\nAs of the time of this vote, the in-force Net Change Limit of 350M ada spans the start of Epoch 532 through the end of Epoch 604 (Governance Action ID: 9b62b3c632f329016a968ac25211825bb4f84b12461121c7da3aa11df92370f9#0). This roughly corresponds to the calendar year 2025. This action would set a 300M ada Net Change Limit from the start of Epoch 563 through the end of Epoch 635, a period roughly spanning June 2025 through June 2026. I don’t disagree with the Proposer’s observations that the existing NCL only covers 2025 and that forthcoming withdrawals secondary to approved budgets may result in 12-month timelines spanning 2025 and 2026. At the same time, a forthcoming 2026 NCL could achieve the same effect, with the same priority of fiscal responsibility, while maintaining calendar year NCL periods. Because I see merit to the alternative means of achieving the same ends, I vote no on this action.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kronoshus/KevinMohr/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20333.jsonld -->\r\n# Kevin G Mohr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting no because I want a lower NCL so we are forced to reform Catalyst or get rid of it.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/ye5cht8y -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this NCL because 300M ADA matches the treasury’s expected inflow for the same 73-epoch window (Epoch 563 – 635), keeping withdrawals in line with deposits. It gives teams approved for 2025 a clear budget runway into early 2026 while staying below the 350 M cap I previously endorsed, preserving reserves for future cycles. A simple, inflation-neutral ceiling maintains fiscal discipline yet leaves room for essential infrastructure and governance work—exactly the balance our earlier votes aimed to achieve.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kostas Panagias",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kostaspanagias/drep/refs/heads/main/voting/2025/09/NCL25_26_300M.jsonld -->\r\n# Kostas Panagias\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc29nv90qqtf7qwlp5eqwnscdmvk5utnul9arfm9eklw9cphfhhu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Rationale for Voting YES on the 300M ADA Net Change Limit (Epochs 563–635)\r\n\r\nI am voting **YES** on this Net Change Limit (NCL) proposal, as it aligns perfectly with the position I have consistently advocated for in my previous rationales.\r\n\r\nSetting the NCL at 300 million ADA matches the expected annual treasury inflow, ensuring that we maintain fiscal responsibility while still enabling meaningful investment in Cardano’s continued growth. This figure strikes the right balance between prudent spending and supporting the ecosystem’s development needs.\r\n\r\nI also appreciate the thoughtful structuring of this NCL to cover not only the remainder of 2025 but also a significant portion of 2026. This approach provides continuity for ongoing and upcoming budget proposals, many of which are designed around 12-month cycles, and ensures that essential development can continue without unnecessary interruptions while we debate future budgets.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons, I am in strong support of this Info Action and I am voting YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kyle Solomon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adosiawolf/drep-rationale/refs/heads/main/0003 -->\r\n# Kyle Solomon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytzshxuma6cwrnlv2ucyclfqw3k4nu4nuudmh2z87j9hncsk9dhy4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have voted NO on the current proposal to set the NCL to 300M Ada.\r\n\r\nWhile I am an advocate for fiscal responsibility and firmly believe our absolute top priority must be establishing ecosystem sustainability, I have already voted YES to support the passing a 350M NCL.\r\n\r\nI beleive it strategically short-sighted to limit our latitude for flexibility earlier than later when visibility is always more clear, hence I will be most critical when voting on treasurty withdrawal actions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LALKUL",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Juana-Attieh/lalkul/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(5).jsonld -->\r\n# LALKUL\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytnjaqmwq9qk9yv2a5ff79qj2r2mgmcmpm0683993ssy86s77kavf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLalkul is voting YES on this proposal to set the Net Change Limit (NCL) at 300 million ADA for Epochs 563-635. This adjustment reflects a moderate and measured reduction from the 2025 limit of 350 million ADA, which aligns with the emerging community sentiment in favor of fiscal restraint, without compromising ongoing or planned initiatives that are already being developed within the current budget framework.\r\nSetting a one-year NCL at this level provides flexibility for future governance decisions while establishing a steady and transparent trajectory for treasury management.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LallyMcClay",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPmPhiKRistoFQ4mLtLutAjP1FkKtz6dztjArbkA4VLBo -->\r\n# LallyMcClay\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2dptycrks2ggae95leeh66m0l0svet98c44hl4rmaec7as6hgpp3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have chosen to vote no on the proposal to set the NCL at 300 million ADA. While this figure is not inherently unreasonable, I believe it is insufficient to ensure the robustness and flexibility needed for effective treasury management.\r\n\r\nA higher NCL would not imply immediate or full expenditure of those funds. Rather, it would provide contingency capacity, enabling the ecosystem to respond to unforeseen circumstances, critical opportunities, or systemic risks that may arise.\r\n\r\nBy setting the threshold too low, I believe we risk introducing constraints that could hinder our ability to act decisively in moments that demand it. This could result in delays or missed opportunities at key junctures in Cardano’s growth and governance evolution.\r\n\r\nIn my view, a more prudent approach would be to maintain a higher NCL, offering necessary headroom without obligating use, thereby strengthening our preparedness for an uncertain future.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Latam Cardano",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LatamCardanoDRep/DREP/refs/heads/main/Vote%20NCL300%208-5-25.jsonld -->\r\n# Latam Cardano\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytgsdkfznvjnwdxrzvf8x6tn4ctfukqqphsammzkfwatgsqgnpf2w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBeing consistent with our view expressed in previous NCL proposals we are voting NO because we believe the NCL should be defined as a maximum percentual change of the balance of the treasury in a dynamic window of time so it doesn't need to be approved every year.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LEADStakePool",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lead-pool/DRep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context3.jsonld -->\r\n# LEADStakePool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytnvazqpsj98pu7w6vtmeddcy9pnn6y6nl0psr5ajzge52s82zz8t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe previously supported a lower NCL which did not pass. We are now at a point where we believe the community has spoken and we should therefore just proceed with the NCL that has been voted yes on. Additional proposals at this stage just add additional confusion and we should now just be getting on with what has been agreed",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "LloydDuhon",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZm8vRGZkLmZAVCG4ksGMqczWGC7sKzXWwHkhtU1AY31R -->\r\n# LloydDuhon\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfvw769lf7g5p4hx0cl2f8jxdcufdcqqj36u0n9escjcwdswcj4h6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe should not be re-litigating the Net Change Limit. I supported the 350M NCL that used the previous years (2024) funds. I will support a new NCL for 2026 that will use the funds deposited in 2025 within +/- 5%.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lourde",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWEkBwJhtCfmb3cNqmHfkpgS3e4WvzhTknYDh4koMK1Xh -->\r\n# Lourde\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygtvnwgsucstvesms2hv9vc8hw3tye5zhzldmszrxqd2rxsje5c6m`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe limits between 275M and 300M NCL is consistently the available options among the polls and submissions for budget NCL, I find value in the higher of the 2 for the future build out of the ecosystem.\r\n\r\n-LOURDE-\r\nOuroborus\r\nImperator\r\nAeternalis",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Lucas.Macchiavelli",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lucasmac9/drep/refs/heads/main/Vote0011 -->\r\n# Lucas.Macchiavelli\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jd3c4hgg0tdua58z6c64k9rf58lz3jlcjlxcjfeaspl6q2e9zm6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote YES to establish a Net Change Limit (NCL) of 300 million ADA covering epochs 563 to 635.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\nPrior Voting Behavior\r\nI have consistently supported a disciplined yet pragmatic approach to Treasury management.\r\n\r\nI previously voted NO on a 200M ADA NCL (too restrictive) and YES on a 350M ADA NCL (more aligned with strategic flexibility).\r\n\r\nIn the Intersect budget temperature check, I backed around 345M ADA worth of proposals — higher than my ideal comfort level, but in recognition of the critical need to fund governance and ecosystem infrastructure.\r\n\r\nThe Intersect proposal has since been refined to 275M ADA. It is still a significant amount of ADA, but I agree with the areas covered in the budget for critical infrastructure and growth. Therefore, I am now more comfortable with reducing the NCL from 350M ADA to 300M ADA. 300 MM ADa leaves an extra 25M ADA for other proposals, such as the Amaru Node proposal, which I have voted YES on.\r\n\r\nApproving a 300M ADA NCL balances fiscal prudence with strategic investment. I feel comfortable with 300M ADA as a middle ground — it is high enough to fund critical initiatives, but low enough to prevent excessive overspending. A 300M ADA NCL aligns with projected Treasury inflows. It sends a signal of responsibility and ambition: that we are serious about scaling Cardano while also committed to preserving Treasury sustainability.\r\n\r\nAlthough it is not guaranteed, I am writing this rationale assuming the Intersect info action will be approved, based on the results observed so far.\r\n\r\nI fully acknowledge we are authorizing the withdrawal of a significant amount of ADA. Treasury stewardship must remain paramount. However, platforms operating within exponential technology ecosystems like Cardano cannot afford underinvestment at a critical growth phase.\r\n\r\nThe risks of underfunding key infrastructure and governance maturation far outweigh the carefully managed risks of targeted investment. This is the time to establish a robust foundation — and it requires deliberate, well-scoped financial commitments.\r\n\r\nVOTE0011",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Maureen",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPgYc4qrhqPKYgMeNpPuQ73SDpidE1dSg62doWpbabReb -->\r\n# Maureen\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y22hlaj8wuyygpnjy5cf96tg9tgvjrz39kxvqgv898uj9scfc55t7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFirst and foremost, I have already voted in favor of the 200M ADA NCL proposal, which I firmly believe represents the more prudent fiscal approach for Cardano's treasury management. Having multiple NCLs creates unnecessary governance confusion and dilutes voting power across competing proposals addressing the same need.\r\nThe Cardano Treasury is a finite resource that deserves rigorous stewardship. While Treasury inflows are currently estimated at approximately 300M ADA annually, these inflows are projected to decline over time as the reserve gradually depletes. The 200M limit better accounts for this inevitable trajectory, establishing a more sustainable withdrawal pattern that will serve the ecosystem for years to come.\r\nMarket dynamics must also be considered. Treasury withdrawals create selling pressure that can negatively impact ADA price. A more conservative 200M limit mitigates this risk while still enabling critical development. We must balance immediate funding needs against long-term value preservation for all stakeholders, including SPOs and ADA holders who depend on price stability.\r\nThe 300M proposal appears to be predicated on accommodating all funding requests rather than enforcing the difficult but necessary prioritization of resources. Effective treasury management requires making hard choices - not simply expanding limits to avoid them. The 200M NCL creates an appropriate constraint that will drive more efficient allocation decisions and greater accountability from funding recipients.\r\nMost importantly, the precedent we set with this first major NCL will shape future governance expectations. Starting with a more conservative approach gives us flexibility to adjust upward if necessary, while beginning with a higher limit risks normalizing excessive withdrawals that the ecosystem may come to depend on.\r\nI believe the 200M NCL better supports Cardano's long-term sustainability while still providing ample resources for essential development, maintenance, and growth initiatives. For these reasons, I must vote against this 300M proposal despite its well-intentioned aims.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "MiyatakeJapan",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYZT6CxTWQiFP6hferQeE1g83HMzLTtGnZoFKcurB2oKm -->\r\n# MiyatakeJapan\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytaunswwpytxjk2ja7c5suxrjz57vtq4ryzu7prkxmm4wdqs7c9wn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n予算の確認に費やす時間と労力はとても大きくなっています。\r\n見直すべきことはたくさんありますが、まずはCardanoの歩みを止めないことが重要です。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Nicolas Cerny",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmeEheWbGBnEFZZFBB3uQeNJQ5CvuPsvJDF7wjuvyBJz2m -->\r\n# Nicolas Cerny\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yttcav7gh3xlkqd876gmgma32c7qj555ajnn3fnp9kl6l4g97vcyz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on the governance action \"Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563-635\" (gov_action1vdlrcftd48qn2zz8egepr6xyfcmxpfz8r69k769gc5mhg662adesq9yy8pl). While the constitution allows for the Net Change Limit (NCL) to be modified, making frequent adjustments is reckless and undermines trust in the stability of Cardano's fiscal policy.  \r\n\r\nA predictable and stable NCL is essential for teams and builders to confidently create long-term budgets. This proposal disrupts the current 2025 NCL period, introducing uncertainty that could interrupt development on the platform.  \r\n\r\nWhile some proposed budgets may extend beyond the current NCL timeframe, this does not necessitate a hasty and reactive change to the limit itself. The proposed solution overcomplicates the matter when existing constitutional mechanics already accommodate for it.  \r\n\r\nAlthough the proposed 300M ada figure is logically sound for the specified period, the process is flawed. I advocate for a more disciplined and predictable approach to setting the NCL. We should establish a tradition of setting the NCL on an annual basis (1 January – 31 December). This would involve a thorough discussion in Q3 and a vote in Q4, providing the ecosystem with the foresight it needs. This process should also include a more comprehensive selection of choices for DReps, rather than a simple binary vote.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "No stress",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYngyaa2R5sLqGYouTU7PGUupzfjNUoxMUydRUbGeLCJD -->\r\n# No stress\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t3t35yx7j8nnh3wkqn2zzhgwqksksn85zv62pjrwzjawczwgyv7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI would like to see 150-250 as anything higher does not fully ensure the treasury will continue to grow.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action1vdlr/Vote_Context%20.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted NO on the proposal to set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit (NCL) for Epochs 563–635 because it does not align with Cardano’s current treasury inflows and may hinder the ecosystem's growth.\r\n\r\nOver the past 12 months, the Cardano treasury has received approximately 315 million ADA, averaging about 4.32 million ADA per epoch . Setting the NCL below this replenishment rate could restrict funding for essential projects, including long-term initiatives that span multiple epochs.\r\n\r\nA more appropriate NCL would match or slightly exceed the annual inflow, ensuring that the treasury can support ongoing and future proposals without unnecessary constraints. This approach would provide flexibility and stability, fostering innovation and development within the Cardano ecosystem.\r\n\r\nPlus, I've voted YES for the 350 NCL, which is set to pass and be enacted.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I believe that the proposed 300 million ADA NCL is insufficient and recommend adjusting it to better reflect the treasury's capacity and the community's needs.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA016-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"Não\" nesta ação de governança (637e3c256da9c1350847ca3211e8c44e3660a4471e8b6f68a8c537746b4aeb7300), pois alterar o limite de gastos previamente definido, neste momento, colocaria em risco a continuidade do desenvolvimento e geraria incertezas para os construtores.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"No\" on this governance action (637e3c256da9c1350847ca3211e8c44e3660a4471e8b6f68a8c537746b4aeb7300) because changing the previously defined spending limit at this time would risk the continuity of development and create uncertainty for builders.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSd8v2yqnhwvVkgVRUTZ8UAdYpCzmanG17sivQq7YZF2E -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting **No **on the proposal to set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit (NCL) for Epochs 563 to 635. While the intent to provide continuity for treasury spending into 2026 is reasonable, this proposal fails to address several foundational concerns I've raised in previous votes and rationales.\r\n\r\nFirst, this proposal overrides a previously supported 200 million ADA NCL—one I voted for—without a clear justification or explanation of how overlapping NCLs are reconciled. The lack of a structured fiscal framework remains a key issue. I continue to believe that Cardano would benefit from defining a loosely coordinated fiscal year to align treasury budgeting, project timelines and NCL enactments. While this need not be rigid, it would enhance transparency, predictability, and stewardship of treasury resources.\r\n\r\nMoreover, this proposal sets the new NCL to take effect **immediately after the info action expires**, which feels rushed. It suggests a queue of budget proposals ready to flood the governance process, eager to tap into the treasury. That sense of urgency, absent clear prioritization or safeguards, undermines the principle of sustainable and equitable resource allocation—especially when we know the Treasury cannot fund all the proposals that will come forward.\r\n\r\nI’m also uneasy with the proposal’s use of **projected **treasury inflows as its benchmark. Treasury governance should be grounded in conservative, **realized **inflows from the prior fiscal period IMO, not optimistic forward-looking estimates that may not materialize. Spending based on future projections increases the risk of over-allocation and funding gaps, especially if treasury income slows due to market or protocol-level variables.\r\n\r\nFinally, while the proposal meets constitutional requirements procedurally, it still lacks the modeling rigor, phased allocation strategies, or contingency safeguards that would make such an NCL both practical and responsible.\r\nFor these reasons, I cannot support this proposal in its current form and will vote No.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RudianosDrep/RudianosDrep/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%209.jsonld -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have decided to vote in favor of this proposal. I believe that a 300 million ADA NCL is appropriate for the time period listed and I prefer it to the current 350 million NCL. Additionally the setting of a roughly one year period (ending epoch 562) to fund projects and work out the general budget implementation, is an improvement on the current approved NCL which would end too soon (Dec 2025) to properly fund the projects that have put forward proposals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nagamarupanda/Drep-voting/refs/heads/main/300%20million%20ADA%20Net%20Change%20Limit.jsonld -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNCLは、支出そのものを制限するためのものというより、先に上限を明確にしてから、提案ごとの判断を行うための基盤だと考えています。実際、今のように複数の予算提案が同時進行している状況では、まずNCLをしっかり定めることが大前提だと感じています。個人的には、NCLは300〜350M ADAの範囲であれば現実的だと思っており、今回の300Mはその中でも比較的慎重な設定と言えます。支出の精査は今後のDRepの責任ですが、その前にルールを整える意味で、今回はYESを選びました。\r\n\r\nAt this stage, I think it's important that we set the limit first—before diving too deep into individual funding decisions. There are multiple budget proposals in motion, and without a clear ceiling, it’s hard to manage things responsibly. Personally, I see the 300M–350M ADA range as a realistic zone, and this 300M proposal sits at the more cautious end of that spectrum. It’s not about pushing spending—it’s about having a clear structure to operate within, so DReps can make sound judgments. This feels like a necessary step to keep the overall process on track.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Seidu Ziblim",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQBssBwFncah4at4CwpfNMhDQVnLKxUqAUDpUcy4pxV35 -->\r\n# Seidu Ziblim\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygrnrg598f38xxg83cg6hudq209w0t578lq9ceh9np99d8cgn67wp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile my primary support remains with the 200M ada NCL, which I believe best reflects a prudent, community-first governance framework, I also see this 300M ada NCL as a reasonable compromise that moves us in the right direction. It still represents a reduction from the highest proposals and signals a willingness to balance sustainability with inclusiveness. For this reason, I am supporting it as a second-preference option, in the spirit of constructive progress and unity.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmXheqKJeFiQuQtkJUHQwVoWjKKC2kirzDLzPiUCgdrkNC -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**SIDAN Lab is voting YES on the proposal to set a 300M ADA Net Change Limit (NCL) for Epochs 563–635.**\r\n\r\n🟦 **Not ideal, but better than 350M**\r\n\r\nThe previously approved 350M ADA NCL felt excessive given the current state of oversight. 300M ADA is still high, but more aligned with expected treasury inflows and far less aggressive. It reflects some moderation.\r\n\r\n🟦 **200M proposal was our first choice — but it didn’t pass**\r\n\r\nWe previously supported the 200M NCL because it promoted discipline and encouraged focused spending. But with that option off the table, 300M is the more cautious choice left.\r\n\r\n🟦 **One-year scope makes sense**\r\n\r\nA fixed 12-month window provides predictability for proposers while allowing the community to reassess and adjust before locking in the future.\r\n\r\n🟦 **Governance is still early**\r\n\r\nUntil we see stronger safeguards or maturity, lower limits should be the default.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/info/20250517_02/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs the DRep representing SIPO, we vote YES on the proposal to set a Net Change Limit (NCL) of 300 million ADA for the period covering Epochs 563 to 635.\r\n\r\nThis proposal is not a new request for funds but a necessary infrastructure mechanism to support the continuity of approved treasury disbursements—specifically, the unified 275M ADA budget submitted by Intersect and endorsed by a majority of DReps. Many of the proposals included in the Intersect budget follow a 12-month funding cycle, meaning that part of their execution extends into the first half of 2026 (Epoch 563 onward). Without a valid NCL covering that period, those proposals—even though previously approved—would become technically ineligible for treasury withdrawals.\r\n\r\nAccording to Article IV of the Cardano Constitution, all Treasury Withdrawals must occur within an active and approved NCL. This proposal ensures that the second half of the Intersect budget, including mission-critical initiatives in infrastructure, marketing, research, and governance, can be executed legally and smoothly without delay.\r\n\r\nWe also believe this proposal strikes a reasonable balance between fiscal prudence and ecosystem stability. The proposed 300M ADA is close to the expected treasury inflows for the relevant period (approx. 265M ADA in 2026), representing a conservative but realistic upper limit. Moreover, it offers a natural transition from the 350M ADA limit ratified for 2025, forming a sustainable year-over-year curve that supports planning and confidence across the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nIn summary, we support this proposal as a technical and constitutional necessity to uphold the integrity of the Intersect budget and ensure continuous delivery of approved programs beyond 2025.\r\n\r\nThis is a conditional but clear YES vote—anchored in the principle that fiscal continuity is essential for decentralized execution.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQui8N86E7kRcz2CVwdzyxpbcsTMNGumywpDwq7dJjizQ -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are voting against this proposal. While this proposal covers a slightly longer period of 13 months and may appear flexible on the surface, we have already supported an NCL proposal for 350M ADA covering an equivalent period (epochs 532-604), and this proposal is inconsistent with that position. We have determined that it lacks fiscal policy consistency, as the cap has been lowered despite the extended period. Furthermore, Cardano is currently in a critical development phase involving the implementation of decentralized governance and scalability enhancements, requiring agility in strategic investments. Even with an extended spending period, maintaining strict caps could limit our ability to deploy necessary funds when needed, potentially reducing flexibility. Additionally, the proposal takes a conservative approach by setting the cap equal to expected treasury income, which raises concerns about constraints on contingency spending and emergency responses. For these reasons, Socious prioritizes sustainable and strategic fund management and takes a position against this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tempo.Vote",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmThLet14ngqxqcqQaYA35nEmtCcjuMDpGyymuq8m5t5b6 -->\r\n# Tempo.Vote\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2eu92qwy875nlslg3ahlh0hy5vhzpkrjay88ptvdp0z6cqm9h25x`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile the NCL of 300M ADA is still higher than what we think Cardano should spend in 2025, it is lower than the currently approved 350M ADA. Also now that ADA price is significantly higher than $0.5, it makes sense to lower NCL from the current 350M ADA proposed when ADA price was $0.5",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Terminada",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmS67mvBYb5LLvS9GyXGPboNjV6QfFWmCVsZLcdftyzTt2 -->\r\n# Terminada\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytf9f78k7rkwk4cu6l2nvna22keu9yus4kqzc0hqspd36uszu0xc2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nStop all these competing net change limit info actions that span different epoch windows.  A majority of DReps already supported a net change limit info action for 2025 of 350M.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Dutch Drep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmYD9bETFSsrKx8jjpuX1hMX9XsrfPtaeStNaTPuTLU3yX -->\r\n# The Dutch Drep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yvve4554njxyun2s5p9q70v88d5jl7r0h34pjhw5f5tmw3sjtrutp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe, the Dutch DRep, vote No on this proposal.\r\n\r\nWe are aligned with the existing Net Change Limit (NCL) proposed by Intersect for the 2026 period. Introducing an alternative NCL at this stage creates unnecessary confusion and risks fragmenting consensus around treasury planning.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "The Victor",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://bafybeicwmt4aiamda6un5o52kj4k3lttyk6ds7nqaa4gwpi2ce2q3rikdm.ipfs.dweb.link/ -->\r\n# The Victor\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv824m4rjeglnwessh59v4hz8u3glz5pgexxff5md7wytsccjj68`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe last time I voted Yes for the 350M ADA NCL, noting that I find it too high and that I will support a subsequent proposal for a reduction. I could not however support the 200M ADA NCL, as I found that to be dangerously restrictive, given we cannot be sure where the ADA valuation ends up throughout the year. This 300M NCL however, is something I can get behind. Although valuation risks still cannot be eliminated, I firmly believe a $2 value is the bare minimum that ADA can and will reach, and hold its value above that for a considerable amount of time. Bearing this in mind, +$600M should be plenty for the next 12 months to come.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSSatg1Z5R6e79DhWkLzKpS4XB5K6L6omFMY7BqAKxR6F -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe proposal to set a Net Change Limit (NCL) of 300M ADA spanning epochs 563 to 635 raises serious concerns from a governance and financial stewardship perspective. First, it is important to recall that the community has already sanctioned an NCL of 200M ADA, explicitly covering the entirety of 2025. This existing limit was established to ensure prudent, measured disbursement of Treasury funds aligned with clear accountability and project milestones.\r\n\r\nRequesting an immediate increase to 300M ADA, effectively front-loading additional funds for both 2025 and 2026, circumvents the discipline of periodic review and assessment. It undermines the principle of incremental funding based on demonstrated outcomes, which is essential in safeguarding the Treasury and maintaining trust within the community. Approving a larger NCL now, without the benefit of evaluating the tangible results of projects funded under the current 200M ADA limit, risks diluting financial rigor and could set a precedent for less transparent budget expansions in the future.\r\n\r\nMoreover, this approach conflicts with the strategic imperative to align financial governance with a business-minded, outcome-driven framework. The Cardano ecosystem’s long-term stability depends on measured, evidence-based decisions rather than speculative or convenience-driven increases. A more responsible and sustainable path would be to approve a new NCL for 2026 during Q3 2025, post comprehensive review of project milestones and Treasury inflows. This timing respects the community’s right to informed decision-making and ensures that Treasury allocations remain firmly tethered to performance and strategic priorities.\r\n\r\nIn light of these considerations, I strongly oppose the proposed NCL increase to 300M ADA at this juncture. Upholding financial discipline and transparency is paramount to preserving the integrity of Cardano’s governance and securing its future as the most decentralized, scientifically grounded PoS network. I therefore vote \"No\" on this governance action.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_300mADA_NCL_For_Ep_563_635.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs Wada DRep, we represent a decentralized and globally connected network of Cardano community builders, innovators, and voters, many based across Africa and the diaspora. Our role in constitutional governance is to act in the best interests of the ecosystem while reflecting the priorities of our community and honoring our internal deliberative frameworks.\r\n\r\nWe have voted YES on this proposal to establish a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit (NCL) for the period covering Epochs 563 to 635, and we offer the following rationale:\r\n\r\nAs part of our review of community proposals during the 2025 budget cycle, the Wada DRep adopted an internal NCL ceiling of 280 million ADA. This number reflected a balanced position: conservative enough to avoid excessive Treasury depletion but generous enough to allow meaningful investments in Cardano’s decentralized future.\r\nThe 300M NCL now under vote is closely aligned with this internal benchmark, offering a realistic and responsible ceiling that supports the continuity of projects we already endorsed. For us, voting “Yes” on this proposal reinforces the integrity of the internal budgeting framework we shared with our stakeholders.\r\n\r\nWe are in a critical phase of implementation. The Cardano community has approved over ₳275.3 million worth of proposals, including those administered by Intersect, alongside other important initiatives like the Amaru node development, which is up for voting.\r\nMany of these projects have 12-month roadmaps that will extend into 2026. A 300M ADA NCL for Epochs 563 to 635 ensures that disbursements tied to milestones in 2026 remain viable and that there is no break in Treasury availability when it’s most needed to sustain development momentum.\r\nIn this sense, the 300M NCL is not speculative. It is a realistic reflection of existing commitments that now require a supportive fiscal framework.\r\n\r\nWe understand that some in the community favor a lower NCL (such as the 200M proposal) out of caution and a desire to protect Treasury longevity. We share the value of sustainability, but we also recognize the risks of underfunding an ecosystem that is entering a new phase of decentralized governance.\r\nThe 300M proposal is a responsible compromise. It is lower than the 350M NCL already approved for 2025 but high enough to enable critical functions, including:\r\nDRep tooling and compensation\r\nOngoing constitutional committee operations\r\nDeveloper audits and milestone reviews\r\nOutreach, education, and regional capacity-building\r\nInfrastructure delivery and protocol experimentation\r\n\r\nBy voting \"Yes,\" we endorse a path that supports responsible spending without limiting our ability to learn, adapt, and iterate.\r\n\r\nOne of the worst outcomes we can invite as a decentralized ecosystem is uncertainty, especially after budgets have been approved. A delayed or insufficient NCL would create ambiguity about whether or how proposals will be funded beyond 2025.\r\n\r\nThe 300M ADA limit reduces this ambiguity and offers DReps, proposers, and contributors a clearer framework for long-term planning. It also allows Treasury Withdrawal governance actions to proceed with confidence that funds are available up to a predictable ceiling.\r\n\r\nOur “Yes” vote on the 300 million ADA NCL proposal reflects a careful balance between fiscal responsibility and ecosystem stewardship. This limit:\r\nAligns with our internal 280M fiscal model,\r\nSupports funding continuity for already-approved projects,\r\nAvoids disrupting long-term roadmaps,\r\nProvides a safe, sustainable alternative to both overly high and overly restrictive limits.\r\nIn short, it is a measured, community-informed, and execution-ready fiscal guardrail.\r\n\r\nAs the Wada DRep, we believe this proposal offers Cardano a stable foundation to advance its 2025–2026 governance and development agenda.\r\n\r\nLet’s build Cardano’s next chapter boldly and responsibly.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/willpiam/drep/refs/heads/master/vote_context/13_ncl.jsonld -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI agree that we should define an NCL that extends into the next year to avoid a period without an NCL. However, I believe this NCL is too low for this period given our current situation.\r\n\r\nShould this proposal be enacted, the Intersect budget of ₳275M would leave only ₳25M for anything else the dReps choose to fund until June 3, 2026. With the current NCL of ₳350M, the dReps would remain in control of ₳75M.\r\n\r\nThe dReps, as a collective, need to develop resource allocation skills. The only way to achieve this is by giving them a sufficiently large budget that allows for a few mistakes.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/willpiam/drep/blob/master/vote_context/markdown/13_ncl.md",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/NCL.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi, as a DRep, votes No on this Info Action regarding the setting a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635 (637e3c256da9c1350847ca3211e8c44e3660a4471e8b6f68a8c537746b4aeb7300).\r\n\r\nRationale\r\nAs Yoroi previously voted in favor of the 2025 Net Change Limit (9b62b3c632f329016a968ac25211825bb4f84b12461121c7da3aa11df92370f900) proposed by Intersect, we will continue to align with that voting stance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YourHotDate",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YourHotDate/YourHotDrep/refs/heads/main/2025-5-17%20Drep%20Net%20Change%20Limit.jsonld -->\r\n# YourHotDate\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwrv7gk8w28wml2hupnvw605exugufukxsvvq2z52t2mksxg2alp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCardano now holding over 1.5 billion ADA. Setting a net change limit of 300 million is fair for this year. Assuming Cardano will be able to handle more transactions and execute more transactions in the coming years I suspect that this NCL will be increased as functionality and useability increase. Despite previous stances I had thinking the NCL should be on the conservative side (100-200 million ADA), I believe that in these early years we as a community should be aggressive  with the NCL in order to fund projects, companies, and innovation. This is necessary stay competitive and bring builders to this ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cardanoz/drep/46ea2a797d8c20881d46dbf365a753831120a108/ga16.jsonld -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Set a 300 million ADA Net Change Limit for Epochs 563–635\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will vote YES on both of the next two GAs.\r\n\r\n200 M ADA NCL for 2025\r\n300 M ADA NCL for 2025 3Q- 2026 2Q\r\n\r\nBecause I think the following order is good, in which case it would be reasonable to vote YES for both:\r\n\r\n1. 300 M ADA NCL for 2025 3Q- 2026 2Q\r\n2. 200 M ADA NCL for 2025\r\n3. 350 M ADA NCL for 2025（now）\r\n\r\nThe approach of determining spending based on inflows has been well-received by the community.\r\n\r\nThe 350M ADA NCL is too large for the second half of 2025 alone.\r\n\r\nThe 200M ADA NCL may be appropriate for the second half of 2025 alone, but many of the current Cardano budget proposals are expected to cover a 12-month period, i.e., up to mid-2026. From that perspective, it seems insufficient without a separate NCL for 2026.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I would vote YES on both and recommend setting the 2026 NCL in the case where the 200M ADA NCL is approved and the 300M ADA NCL is rejected.\r\n\r\nBut personally, I think it would be better to set it as 3Q2025-2Q2026, rather than setting separate NCL 2025 and NCL 2026. This is easier to manage, since most of the Cardano budget work will probably be set in 3Q2025-2Q2026. \r\n---\r\n私は次の2つのGAの両方に賛成票を投じます。\r\n\r\n200 M ADA NCL for 2025\r\n300 M ADA NCL for 2025 3Q- 2026 2Q\r\n\r\n以下の順序が良いと考えているため、両方に賛成票を投じるのが妥当です。\r\n\r\n①300 M ADA NCL for 2025 3Q- 2026 2Q\r\n②200 M ADA NCL for 2025\r\n③350 M ADA NCL for 2025（now）\r\n\r\n流入額に基づいて支出額を決定するというアプローチは、コミュニティから支持を得ています。とすると、\r\n\r\n③は2025後半だけを考えると流入に対して多すぎます。\r\n\r\n②は、2025年後半のみに適用すると、妥当かもしれませんが、現在のCardano予算案の多くは12ヶ月間、つまり2026年半ばまでを対象としています。この観点からすると、2026年用のNCLを別途設定しなければ不十分であるように思われます。\r\n\r\nしたがって、私は両方に賛成票を投じ、②が承認され、③が却下された場合は、2026年のNCLを設定することを推奨します。\r\n\r\nしかし、個人的には、2025年のNCLと2026年のNCLを別々に設定するよりも、2025年第3四半期から2026年第2四半期に設定する方が良いと考えています。Cardano予算作業の大部分は2025年第3四半期から2026年第2四半期に設定されると思われるため、管理が容易になります。",
      "vote": "YES"
    }
  ],
