      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVaUuUjQhRzQTYEYEErBPXbEv6wTe5gisCpTtK77Ys2ZV -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSocious has voted in favor of all 39 Treasury Withdrawal proposals submitted. These proposals were selected through a well-defined process, and we fully support them out of respect for the will of the broader Cardano community.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "STORM Partners",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTN27GSnMZ8x9md7NgYKBZNz31P2ZGockDWzXFd7L2ecP -->\r\n# STORM Partners\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf0s5guxklwlqn7ttdpfwmmkaucwaqkkm6hzncy8nful5fgemurcj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal advances Cardano’s technical maturity through a combination of high-impact infrastructure initiatives. It aligns with STORM Partners’ mission to back proposals that enhance ecosystem efficiency, developer experience, and long-term resilience.\r\nWe believe having several independent contributors to the core development of Cardano beyond IOG is beneficial, as we shift toward a decentralized development model. However, we stress the importance of strong coordination with the TSC to avoid overlapping and duplication of spending.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SureWealthNG",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Henro1975/SureWealthNG/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(13).jsonld -->\r\n# SureWealthNG\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2t8w2rtcyfh3f863gqcwmru7lafuszmvy0xhg7xjwdpwgcf2kz87`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVote: YES\r\n\r\nThis proposal funds 12 critical infrastructure projects by TWEAG, a trusted core contributor to Cardano. The work targets protocol correctness, network performance, and developer tooling—advancing scalability, security, and long-term sustainability.\r\n\r\nIt’s part of the approved ₳275M ecosystem budget and includes clear milestones, audited smart contracts, and third-party oversight. A high-impact, technically sound investment in Cardano’s future.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tobias Ilskov",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmdGYJcC83HdNcqfca9tMj2jsGzRQPQdrv6VSzwRiwJPNy -->\r\n# Tobias Ilskov\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt9xg7l0dlgxj3lyewmndzrq5wzj3f4nusdkpfa9n7zf4ssayqnk0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA couple of months ago, I supported the resolution to bundle all of the Intersect Budget Proposals into 1 or 2 formal on-chain governance votes.\r\n\r\nEach of these proposals has already undergone extensive scrutiny and received 50% or greater support from the active DReps in the ecosystem, and I will honor that prior decision and the work these prospective developers have put in by voting yes on all the proposals from the Intersect Budget team.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmczs7JLQU9h7fQFBgV9xJfvKyDgDezgCMXBPVqEY6g52N -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes. This proposal spans multiple critical initiatives that directly support Cardano’s long-term robustness and innovation at the protocol level. The work is transparent, well-scoped, and aligned with the ecosystem’s strategic direction. In contrast to many high-cost proposals, this one demonstrates clear technical value, accountability, and ecosystem alignment. It is exactly the kind of work the Treasury should be supporting at scale.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNdRz2gCEJEtCjQkSqeikkXA4DCoYJ1K4Pw8wDnMReSdb -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is an ambitious scope of work in important technical areas: ledger and consensus conformance testing, Plutus script tooling, genesis sync acceleration, node emulation, history expiry and codec improvements. This is all relevant and is related to scalability, performance, verifiability, developer experience, all of which are important for Cardano's future. \r\n\r\n₳11m is a large amount, especially if we consider that the total amount approved for 39 proposals is ₳275m. The proposal bundles multiple projects into one, making it difficult to understand the cost/benefit of each. Since we need to be responsible with the Cardano treasury, I think we should vote NO at this time. The proposal needs to be sharpened and clear how it differs from current work and how the budget is justified.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQnVpXfdqVJS6kjk7jXN8m8gPJigLDL3hvKZNLxqBj9L7 -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe 11 million ADA proposal from a team I am less familiar with lacks sufficient detail on how the funds will be allocated across the 11 proposed bullet points. As a DRep, I find it challenging to evaluate the total cost without deeper technical expertise, and I believe many DReps share this concern. I would support reviewing each of the 11 points individually to ensure transparency and justify the substantial funding request.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcjuMrVPHJKM2odNVDKyRQi2D2GQr7TXvVbExhN6Uhj5Q -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n. While the projects aim to enhance Cardano’s scalability, performance, and developer tools, the 11-project scope is too complex and convoluted, lacking clear prioritization and cost breakdowns. The 11M ADA request is excessive, especially given potential overlap with IOG’s protocol upgrades and existing treasury resources. I support TWEAG’s expertise but urge a smaller, focused proposal (e.g., 2-3M ADA for Plutus and Genesis projects) to ensure feasible execution and stronger ROI. Intersect’s governance is robust, but clarity and restraint are needed for community trust.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NanaSafo01/drep-metadata/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context_Intersect_TWGA16.jsonld -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳11,070,323 for TWEAG's Proposals for multiple core budget project\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: This is a general rationale we have prepared to support our “yes” vote on all the 39 treasury withdrawal actions. This follows careful review and consideration of the metadata of these treasury withdrawal proposals and hence is not a blanket voting practice.\r\n\r\nWe, the Wada DRep Committee, have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawal governance actions currently live on-chain and submitted under the administration of IntersectMBO. These actions are the necessary implementation step following the community's approval of the ₳275.3 million Cardano Ecosystem Budget, the necessary budget info action that precedes the treasury withdrawal process. Our support reflects not only continuity with our earlier \"yes\" votes on the overarching budget info action and its constituent proposals but also our confidence in the smart contract guide and project execution mechanisms Intersect has established as an administrative body for these proposals.\r\n\r\nEach of these 39 withdrawals corresponds directly to proposals that have already passed a respective Budget Info Action with wide community and DRep support of 64.23%. As Wada DRep, we reviewed, scored, and supported many of these initiatives during the budgeting phase, using our internal ₳280M Net Change Limit framework. Our endorsement of the full ₳275.3M package was not a blanket approval but the outcome of detailed deliberation. Therefore, we see it as our responsibility to honor those community-approved funding decisions by affirming these follow-up Treasury withdrawal governance actions.\r\n\r\nImportantly, we are confident in Intersect’s role as the administrator of these treasury disbursements. We have independently reviewed the Smart Contract Guide, disbursement architecture, and accountability structures associated with these withdrawals. The use of milestone-gated smart contracts, multi-signature treasuries, and on-chain/off-chain tracking mechanisms provides strong assurance of transparency, risk management, and community accountability. We are particularly satisfied that Intersect has adopted security-audited contract templates and provides public documentation on how treasury funds will be administered, paused if necessary, and even returned if unused.\r\n\r\nIn our view, rejecting or abstaining from these Treasury Withdrawals at this stage would risk destabilizing delivery timelines, undermining community trust, and introducing administrative conflicts that may violate the spirit of the Constitution’s Articles on budgeting. We believe that treasury funding is not just about allocation; it’s about consistent and credible execution. As such, the DRep role requires continuity and follow-through, especially when prior voting outcomes have clearly mandated action.\r\n\r\nTherefore, in alignment with our constitutional responsibilities, community-aligned decision-making, and our assessment of Intersect’s administrative protocols, we have decided to upvote on all 39 Treasury Withdrawals Governance Actions.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
