      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmYH2Zj9q9Tnv99TLoZ4FjmX2qK6aS7D8cuAJv9qXmEMDk -->\r\n# A$Y\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf94hp0xetd87e5stlxwrtlqwjq6qhqx6zfdu94wdr5dfagp38nd4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES because keeping the net change limit in place is simply a safety measure. It protects the system from sudden or unnecessary constitutional changes while governance continues to mature. There’s no downside to extending this safeguard, and it keeps things stable.",
