    {
      "voter": "drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmPJ55bKZpXyx6sCPXWofWuzzLxsK9hmiF3sVbrqkMtdVf -->\r\n# drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf6xkrz2w4fdkwjw9u98u3pmzk7c7a0amq95hakcj649dns2r4upl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis is an ad-hoc, rushed, temporary solution to a unnecessarily created problem (submitting a TW GA that vacuums up the remainder of the NCL last minute). That GA could easily wait until an NCL 26, or, even better, an alternative budget control mechanism than a speed limit, is defined. \r\nA) There is no issue with NOT spending the whole amount of the NCL, in fact, it would be a great sign of ecosystem maturity, if the speed limit isnt maxed out immediately. \r\nB) There is no reason why the Critical Integrations Budget TW gets a special treatment and shouldnt wait until things are in order again. After all, defining a new NCL takes the same time as accepting this weird short time extension. \r\nC) chill the f out and think forwardly. dont just look 2cm in front of your toes.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/2025NCL-Extension/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(65).jsonld -->\r\n# drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes because this does not increase the current Net Change Limit. It simply extends the existing NCL so that Treasury operations can continue smoothly while we work on passing a new one. It also ensures that, if the Tier 1 Listings proposal fails on December 30 (Epoch 604), a revised or resubmitted version would still have time to be voted on and enacted within a valid NCL window. Overall, the extension maintains the same spending limit while preventing unnecessary operational roadblocks.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Duc Tiger",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdDknjiLtUnSjTUYV3tWbEtmonNheitiAMe3kkFfoXXq7 -->\r\n# Duc Tiger\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt0cvg2649d34afclefrxvyn2ctys87a5jt84ckczyjlvgcu7nxyr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting YES on this proposal, as it is a necessary administrative action to ensure the operational continuity of the Cardano Treasury. A failure to pass this extension would result in a complete halt of all treasury disbursements, an outcome that would be profoundly disruptive and irresponsible to the entire ecosystem.\r\nHowever, it must be stated that this extension is clearly a short-term, stop-gap measure. The necessity of such a last-minute extension suggests a delay in the planning and proposal process for the full 2026 Net Change Limit.\r\nMy affirmative vote is therefore cast with the explicit expectation that the Cardano Budget Committee is working diligently to present a comprehensive NCL proposal for 2026 to the community in the very near future. This will ensure dReps have adequate time for review and deliberation, avoiding the need for further emergency extensions.\r\nThis vote is about maintaining function, not debating policy, and on that basis, it has my full support.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dynamic Strategies",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmPbiHvy8gfVw6ovdcUwBJ64ubgeXLrMtEf9WMGKu3adYY -->\r\n# Dynamic Strategies\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr93aecehnm95wr7ufpd2m6jyh2mc8vnr77f0w33g8upyc6m8ayz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmcV4eKbE567BWf5guuBr7TVUCzbwtBMf9E9oVjM5RZzm5\r\n\r\n-",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
