    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreieygbw4zz2nf54im4zjm46ymrgqxc3vs7sq5l4djjkrqbrxd3z4e4 -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am in favor this proposal. This extension to the NCL is a relatively small change that is required to maintain the constitutionality of the integrations budget proposal. Although changing the length of something like an NCL should never be done without serious consideration, in this case the affected proposal warrants the change in my view. It would be detrimental to the community to have this budget fail and be delayed due to a constitutional technicality. Thank you to those who identified this issue and acted quickly to rectify it.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
