    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiact7tmxcbbz7bkfsdv57wbsmffrrbgqyjbzrsknzs5w4ijdd2hhq -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nProposal: 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep will vote YES on this proposal.\r\n\r\nI am supporting this extension because it is essential to keep Cardano’s treasury operations functioning smoothly and safely during a critical transition period at the end of 2025 and the beginning of 2026. This proposal does not increase the Net Change Limit (NCL) and does not authorize any additional spending beyond what the community has already agreed on. It simply extends the validity period of the existing NCL so that Cardano’s treasury withdrawals can continue without interruption.\r\n\r\nThe current NCL is scheduled to expire at the end of Epoch 604. If it expires without an extension, Cardano will not be able to execute any Treasury Withdrawal Governance Actions (TWGAs) after that point until a new NCL is approved. This would create an unintended “governance freeze” for about a month, causing strategic ecosystem initiatives to stall at a time when Cardano is preparing major infrastructure upgrades and integrations.\r\n\r\nThis is particularly relevant because several important treasury-related governance actions—including the ₳70,000,000 Cardano Critical Integrations Budget—rely on the current NCL’s validity to execute correctly. Those actions are operating on a tight schedule that intersects with the transition to the new Constitutional Committee. Any delay or unforeseen issue during this transition could prevent these proposals from being enacted, even if the DReps approve them, simply because the NCL expires before execution.\r\n\r\nBy extending the NCL for an additional eight epochs (until Epoch 612), we ensure that:\r\n\t•\tCardano’s treasury operations do not stop due to a technical timing issue.\r\n\t•\tLegitimate proposals already progressing through governance can be executed safely.\r\n\t•\tThe ecosystem retains financial continuity during an important governance transition.\r\n\t•\tThe community’s previously agreed spending limit (350M ADA) remains fully respected.\r\n\r\nThis proposal is a practical and responsible measure to protect the network from an avoidable disruption. It does not loosen fiscal discipline, it does not raise spending caps, and it does not grant new powers. It simply preserves operational continuity and maintains constitutional compliance.\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I believe it is our responsibility to prevent gaps or failures in the governance system, especially during periods of transition. Based on these reasons, I am casting a YES vote on this proposal.\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n提案名：2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep は、この提案に 「Yes」 を投じます。\r\n\r\n今回の延長提案を支持する理由は、2025年末から2026年初頭にかけての重要な移行時期において、カルダノの財務（トレジャリー）運営を安全かつ途切れなく継続させるために欠かせない措置だからです。この提案は NCL（年間支出上限）を増やすものではありません。コミュニティがすでに合意した支出枠をそのまま維持したうえで、その有効期間だけを延長するという、非常に限定的かつ技術的な措置です。\r\n\r\n現行のNCLは Epoch 604 で期限切れになります。もし期限切れのまま放置されると、新しいNCLが成立するまで一切のトレジャリー出金が不可能となり、カードとしての財務ガバナンスが約1ヶ月程度「完全停止」してしまう可能性があります。\r\n\r\nこれは単なる技術的問題に見えて、実際にはかなり重大で、特に：\r\n\t•\tカルダノの基盤整備を担う大型提案（例：₳70,000,000 Critical Integrations Budget）\r\n\t•\tVoltaire移行期の予算実行\r\n\t•\tMidnight・インフラ統合系の共同計画\r\n\r\nなど、多くの戦略的プロジェクトがこの期間に実行タイミングを迎えています。\r\n\r\nこれらは現行のNCLが有効であることを前提に設計されているため、NCLが期切れになると、DRepが承認しても、憲法上「執行できなくなる」リスクがあります。\r\n\r\nこの延長提案を通すことで：\r\n\t•\tトレジャリー運営が止まらずに継続できる\r\n\t•\t現在進行中の重要な予算提案が安全に実行できる\r\n\t•\t憲法の要件を満たし続けたまま、移行期の混乱を回避できる\r\n\t•\tコミュニティが決めた「年間350M ADA上限」をそのまま尊重できる\r\n\r\nというメリットがあります。\r\n\r\nこの提案は支出規律を緩めるものではなく、財務上限を広げるものでもありません。ガバナンスの技術的な隙間によって起こり得る運用停止を、防ぐための安全装置にすぎません。\r\n\r\nDRepとして私は、カルダノのガバナンスが空白期間によって機能不全に陥ることを避けることが責務であると考えています。その観点から、今回の提案に 「Yes」 を投じる判断が最も適切であり、カルダノ全体の利益につながると確信しています。\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Socious",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWhAE4LgTFs4JQrTk83M3qtQiSZ9SiRt9B7D3wVtvsve4 -->\r\n# Socious\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcv4ax77s0enqef56qjflf4d8zjgxulukme9uf5p8cfaagysjppn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote yes, because the eight-epoch extension is reasonable and it is necessary to maintain the governance process uninterrupted.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SudoScientist",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arpradio/drep/refs/heads/main/ncl_extend.jsonld -->\r\n# SudoScientist\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2wtls7xh3a8gyepk540dgtzjzalk086gp4www6y0k0xjmqyk6gma`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nConsidering the Budget Info Actions that have been presented, I believe that it is in the best interest of the future Ecosystem Budgets are not burdened with the large impending withdrawals that will soon be up for vote.  We have a more immediate need to address the Constitutional Committee resiliency, as no withdrawals are possible without it.  The next NCL amounts also need to be considered, and focusing on the core issues that enable functional governance will take some time, and the outcome of this action will provide us a period of time to prepare for this.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Talos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSHzvEPYgrcUHHUzALNBQ1hhUFopeQktS3hXQ5YWAni4W -->\r\n# Talos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfqt3wt0v2uvhawx9anzfqty4x7gwwu04wzr9ucga4yd7mct7dup8`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> Vote: NO\r\n\r\nWhy:\r\nThe NCL extension just gives the 70 M request by the founding entities more breathing room. It doesn’t fix the missing breakdown, the founding entities’ track‑record, or the confidentiality clauses that hide how the money will actually be spent. In fact, a longer window makes it easier for a shaky proposal to slip through, so I see it as a net‑negative for the 70 M plan. \r\n\r\nExtending the deadline only prolongs the risk of a poorly justified withdrawal. If the treasury can’t commit to a transparent, well‑justified spend, giving it more time isn’t a good trade‑off.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmWFHfCtNL123bwZxaJgBxrrJxKWkhGZ2DiDXQkXnz8H1D -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLet me be unequivocally clear: while this proposal is operationally necessary, its very existence is an indictment of a profound lack of strategic foresight within our ecosystem's budget management bodies. **We are being asked to sanction an eight-epoch extension—a mere 40 days—to prevent the Cardano Treasury from becoming constitutionally paralyzed. This is not governance; this is crisis management.\r\n**\r\nThe rationale is sound on its face. Article IV of our Constitution and the associated Guardrails are unambiguous: no withdrawals from the Treasury are permitted without a valid NCL in place. With the current NCL expiring at the end of Epoch 604 (January 4, 2026), **failure to act would indeed freeze all Treasury operations, jeopardizing every single funded project and the operational continuity of our ecosystem. **\r\n\r\nHowever, **a mere eight-epoch extension is a tactical patch, not a visionary plan. It kicks the can down the road, creating a recurring cycle of uncertainty.** Managing a treasury of this magnitude requires long-term, predictable, and stable financial frameworks! **Presenting the community with a last-minute stopgap measure, with just weeks to spare, demonstrates a reactive posture that is fundamentally at odds with the prudent and forward-thinking stewardship this ecosystem demands.**\r\n\r\n**I vote to prevent catastrophe, not to endorse this manner of governance. This action is a necessary evil, a bandage applied to a wound that should never have been inflicted.**",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmS7SbzaPPo1Evq7eiCAHf5aNuHkXiheyAQNy4mUU8hTMc -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote yes with the following understanding:\r\n* Maintains continuity in treasury operations without increasing the overall spending cap—all prior withdrawals continue to count against the original 350M ADA limit.\r\n* Preserves the community-agreed guardrails under Article IV of the Cardano Constitution, ensuring fiscal responsibility and sustainability.\r\n* Provides a brief bridge period while the community prepares and socializes a new Net Change Limit for 2026, avoiding any unnecessary governance vacuum.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Wada DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiev7sw4rjs4tqnsf6bbar2tmscwjs7yooba2r5jtdvng2audx7oki -->\r\n# Wada DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2jnqfamg4tq5aepxhggzhqg7pq5gunph4wypkyh9q3qt2cru5m2j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile there were valid reasons for us to consider declining this proposal, one critical factor prevented us from voting no. The governance action seeks to correct a timeline inconsistency in the original 350M ADA Net Change Limit proposal, where the stated end date did not fully align with the epoch-based mechanics of treasury withdrawals. Addressing this mismatch is necessary to ensure that previously approved spending decisions are not rendered invalid due to a procedural oversight rather than substantive governance intent.\r\n\r\nWe also acknowledge our shared responsibility in this outcome. As DReps and members of the broader governance process, including the Constitutional Committee, this discrepancy was not identified or challenged during the review of the original NCL proposal. That oversight contributed directly to the need for this corrective action. Recognising this context, we view the extension not as an expansion of authority, but as a practical adjustment to restore coherence between the original decision and how treasury governance operates in practice.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiep5prqvd5qiuhoy3lsas6j42s6od3idvpt7j4rmv3rd43et6lgqm -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThanks to the good dog HOSKY for noticing this. I see no issue with this proposal. This proposal is also important to ensure the Critical Integrations budget and withdrawal can proceed without issue. I am voting in favour of this proposal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yoroi W₳llet",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YoroiDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_2025NCLExtension.jsonld -->\r\n# Yoroi W₳llet\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr9tuapcanc3kpeyy4dc3vmrz9cfe5q7v9wj3x9j0ap3tswtre9j`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nYoroi DRep votes YES on the 2025 Net Change Limit Extension Info Action. We support this as a necessary measure to ensure that ongoing Treasury processes remain uninterrupted and constitutionally compliant.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nCritical Integrations Budget timing\r\n\r\nThe Net Change Limit (NCL) sets a withdrawal limit for the Cardano treasury over a defined period, and the current NCL expires at the conclusion of Epoch 604. Extending it by eight epochs will help keep the current limit active long enough for the Critical Integrations Budget to be enacted within the budget that the community has approved, rather than being pushed into the next NCL period.\r\n\r\nMaintaining the treasury safeguard\r\n\r\nThe extension does not raise or reset the ₳350M limit. It only extends the timeframe, with prior spending still counted inside the same ceiling. This keeps treasury discipline exactly as the community approved it.\r\n\r\nA healthy governance collaboration\r\n\r\nYoroi gives credit to the proposers for moving quickly on this on-chain safeguard. It reflects a strong alignment between the founding entities and the community, showing that we support each other when governance requires a timely bridge.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\nYoroi DRep supports this extension because it upholds the Critical Integrations Budget timeline, maintains the current NCL cap, and demonstrates healthy governance collaboration. Therefore, we vote YES.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Yosh",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUZ2pW9CJX3MYahYLfN9TgRd94eRtSTBNnQR5gqJjWyuq -->\r\n# Yosh\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytd7s3he5rgxhkx0t2vnun25wy3t263877czxw8nelcld8ce66v4c`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoted Yes. With the massive support of the Cardano Critical Integrations Budget GA, this necessitates the need for a small extension in the NCL timeframe to allow for the CCIB to have enough time to pass and get approved for its TW. Both are mutually exclusive.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "youthpromo",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreih2xvyjlcpy4ju2ptzqradmrlqgo36qn572zq3ivs5mwtwsbqbure -->\r\n# youthpromo\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** 2025 Net Change Limit Extension\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuvsulm46gydp6cqzdupg6evx49g28qwf3aaw0gr7sy0lqwmvhhy`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSounds great to me!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
