    {
      "voter": "This Corrosion",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcHBGgxyh9bB2k1NFMwG32gRyJkKPuW9aELHUMTWWwW6k -->\r\n# This Corrosion\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳96,817,080 for 2025 Input Output Engineering Core Development Proposal\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytkzpmmukjy6qn6xd5skqm0ypcj5juw9rxddr5mmlzgjvtcghwqjr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am frustrated by the price tag on this proposal since it went from \"I'll fund it myself if I have to\" to 97 mil or GTFO. That alone is in extremely poor taste. As promised to my delegators, I am supporting this because I consider it critically important for the future of the chain and expect this to be the last real year for relevancy if we upgrade now. That said. I expect results and the proposal does not give me a warm fussy on deliverables. So I vote yes, with the warning that it better produce results.",
