    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳104,347 for MLabs Research towards Tooling for Elliptical Curves\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVnnMUXF88HyckXCt3iYNW4hskJYgXaLB4eK28H23xEhk -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳104,347 for MLabs Research towards Tooling for Elliptical Curves\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis initiative focuses on delivering reusable elliptic curve and finite field arithmetic for Cardano smart contracts—critical components for enabling on-chain zero-knowledge proof verification and advancing privacy-focused applications.\r\n\r\nPlutarch, the smart contract language used here, provides strong optimization and type safety within Cardano’s architecture, making it a flexible and effective choice for implementing cryptographic logic on-chain.\r\n\r\nThis proposal strengthens the foundation for ZK tooling on Cardano and supports broader developer needs. I support it.\r\n\r\n私はこの提案に Yes を投じます。\r\n\r\n本提案は、楕円曲線や有限体演算をCardanoのスマートコントラクト上で扱える汎用ライブラリを構築するものであり、ゼロ知識証明（ZK）やプライバシー技術を活用したdAppの基盤として重要な意義を持ちます。\r\n\r\n今回使用されるPlutarchは、Cardanoのスマートコントラクト実装において最適化性と型安全性に優れ、暗号処理や検証ロジックを記述する上でも十分な柔軟性を備えています。\r\n\r\nZKアプリケーションの発展と開発者支援の両面に貢献する基盤整備として、本提案を支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/38_MLabsResearch_20250722/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳104,347 for MLabs Research towards Tooling for Elliptical Curves\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO Vote Rationale – YES to “MLabs Research: Tooling for Elliptical Curves”\r\n\r\nSIPO supports this proposal as it directly addresses a foundational gap in Cardano’s smart contract capabilities: the lack of reusable and composable on-chain elliptic curve and finite field cryptographic tooling. The “GrumpleStiltSkin” framework proposed by MLabs is a meaningful step toward enabling native zero-knowledge proof (ZK) verifications on Cardano in a general, developer-friendly manner.\r\n\r\nKey Reasons for Support:\r\n\t•\tCritical Infrastructure for Privacy and ZK Applications:\r\nElliptic curve cryptography and finite field arithmetic are essential for building ZK systems. This proposal creates a parameterized, open-source framework that will drastically reduce the barrier for developers to build privacy-preserving and scalable dApps on Cardano.\r\n\t•\tDeveloper Empowerment through Plutarch Tooling:\r\nBy using Plutarch and the YTxP interface, developers can easily integrate ZK verification without deep cryptographic knowledge. This aligns with the broader goal of democratizing smart contract development.\r\n\t•\tSecurity and Composability Benefits:\r\nStandardized, tested cryptographic primitives lower the risk of security flaws and promote reuse across projects. The design encourages modularity and long-term sustainability.\r\n\t•\tAlignment with Ecosystem Priorities:\r\nThe proposal is one of 39 Intersect-administered projects under the ₳275M budget action, demonstrating community consensus and process transparency.\r\n\t•\tProven Team with Deep Expertise:\r\nMLabs has a strong track record in Plutarch, CTL, and ZK research. Their prior work (e.g., CIP-123 for bitwise ops) shows their ability to deliver impactful, low-level tooling for Cardano.\r\n\r\nSIPO believes that advancing cryptographic primitives on-chain is a strategic move toward Cardano’s long-term competitiveness in privacy and identity use cases.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは本提案に賛成票を投じます。本提案は、Cardanoが抱える根本的な課題──すなわち、楕円曲線および有限体に基づく暗号ツールの再利用可能で安全なオンチェーン実装が存在しないという点──に的確に応えるものです。MLabsが提案する「GrumpleStiltSkin」は、ゼロ知識証明（ZK）をCardano上で一般的かつ開発者フレンドリーに利用可能にするための重要な布石となります。\r\n\r\n主な賛成理由：\r\n\t•\tプライバシーとZKアプリに必要不可欠な基盤：\r\n楕円曲線暗号と有限体演算は、ゼロ知識証明（ZK）やプライバシー重視のアプリケーションに不可欠な技術です。本提案はそれをパラメータ化・汎用化し、開発者が安全かつ容易にZKを活用できるフレームワークを提供します。\r\n\t•\tPlutarch対応で開発者支援：\r\n本提案は、低レベルの暗号知識がなくてもZK機能を組み込めるよう、PlutarchとYTxPインターフェースを活用します。これはスマートコントラクト開発の民主化にも貢献します。\r\n\t•\tセキュリティと再利用性の向上：\r\nテスト済かつ標準化された暗号プリミティブは、開発の重複やセキュリティリスクを減らし、複数プロジェクトでの再利用と相互運用性を促進します。\r\n\t•\tCardano全体予算方針との整合性：\r\n本提案は、Intersectによる₳2.75億の予算管理枠内の39提案の1つとして承認されており、コミュニティコンセンサスに基づいて進められています。\r\n\t•\tMLabsによる信頼性の高い実装：\r\nMLabsはPlutarchやCTL、ZK関連の研究実績が豊富で、過去にはCIP-123（bitwise演算）など、低レイヤーにおける有用なツール提供を実現してきました。\r\n\r\nSIPOは、こうした基盤技術の整備こそが、Cardanoが長期的にプライバシー、ID、ZK領域で競争力を保つための重要な一歩と考えます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
