    {
      "voter": "Cardano Foundation",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://Qmbk3D7U55gK5R25W7Tr9DHzndnaiZD7jNQCuxn79JhhDa -->\r\n# Cardano Foundation\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ydpfkyjxzeqvalf6fgvj7lznrk8kcmfnvy9hyl6gr6ez6wgsjaelx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmSQNCuGSef5wVLYFnNKNLPwkz1u8fJXi1364m4Su5aogu\r\n\r\nThis proposal to adopt Constitution v2.3 is a continuation of a community-led effort that we previously supported. Consistent with our rationale for v2.0, we believe that the Constitution is a living document, and we support incremental, community-driven improvements that are judged on their substance.\r\n\r\nThis new version demonstrates a healthy and responsive governance cycle. Following a review of v2.0, which saw participation from over 86% of the DRep active stake, the proposer integrates lessons learned and directly addresses feedback received in this v2.3.\r\n\r\nThe  new version makes several key enhancements that we believe will make Cardano's governance more effective:\r\n\r\n1. **A More Efficient Treasury Process:** As with version 2.0 submitted in a previous governance action, this version 2.3 streamlines the treasury process by removing the separate \"budget info action\" and integrating its requirements directly into a single, more comprehensive treasury withdrawal governance action type. Between versions 2.0 and 2.3 there was the removal of a provision requiring disclosure \r\n2. **Enhanced Clarity and Governance Hygiene:** The draft introduces clearer definitions, fixes many inconsistencies, and removes outdated or unused clauses. These changes make the Constitution a more precise and self-contained document while reducing ambiguity for all governance participants. \r\n3. **Upholding Core Governance Principles:** This update refines the Constitution's mechanics without altering the fundamental balance of power or the core roles of DReps, SPOs, and the Constitutional Committee.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmNiwWyoGgpenqAgKo69UYs5wBucmZjmtv6LCwqLpEBzSb -->\r\n# CardanoYoda (MANDA Pool)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2m0g4r66pyaw3p7u454wc0p4f0ygm8ueaev0mgd3tvwm7sskqwqp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmVcYQCHhfYNmxLVBMmyXz7EMC9mHiEQGyNqVWSNoq7WCC\r\n\r\nSlight adjustments to the texts and definitions make sense and simplify the understanding of the Constitution.\r\n\r\nChanges regarding Info governance actions, strengthening accountability, and ensuring document mutability also make sense and streamline governance.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "CASIA- Cardano Asia Team",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmZERQAfGTBY7YbrZXiDT5nZMiWFdr15ZMM9yCTHKa91si -->\r\n# CASIA- Cardano Asia Team\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytcy6lfas0zu4axuzw2ncal2k2mh6u8srt5c63fpgq3zg8cd2437d`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nyes, this version is showing the continuous effort of Yuta and the team \r\nthey listen to feedback from the community and help shaping the goverannce for the nearest future",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cerkoryn",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cerkoryn/governance-reference/refs/heads/main/voting-history/info/new_constitution_2.jsonld -->\r\n# Cerkoryn\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yglrf4el8gghum239fggvfrau25k2576y4dvcz65r2ukj8sqpsc2k`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’m voting YES on Constitution v2.3 because it is more clear and concise, which is a step in the right direction. Removing the Budget Info Action requirement will streamline treasury withdrawals and mitigate redundant voting.  Removing codes of conduct is also an improvement because that is not something that is enforceable by the Constitutional Committee.\r\n\r\nThat said, there are still more improvements to be desired and unenforceable rules that should be removed.  In my opinion one of the most troublesome sections are the CRITICAL & SECURITY parameter categories in the guardrails. Article II Section 5 tells SPOs to vote on “security-relevant” parameter updates, but these parameters are called \"CRITICAL parameters\" and listed in Section 2.1 of the guardrails.  Even more confusingly, Section 2.4 has a different category called \"Technical/Security Parameters\", but these are different from the CRITICAL parameters or the \"security-relevant\" parameters mention in Article II Section 5. This confusing categorization desperately needs to be clarified in a future revision of the Constitution.  However, since this iteration is an improvement over the current constitution I will be voting YES on this proposal.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Chris Cata",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiagmrnl6yrove2qzjsn5b7ona7wjdsuwnpobw4uora7vu3iyrmw6m -->\r\n# Chris Cata\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfdfs28uwafjgmrkatdektlzrvha2cmvqjhuz700e04mawq23rmrg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am in favor of this constitutional update to make improvements to how governance operates in Cardano.  It simplifies process, adds clarity to some definitions, and attempts to firm up the immutability of what is done on-chain.  While I would have liked to see some of this broken out, particularly changes to budget info action process, consensus based on feedback from many throughout the community suggests this will ultimately be a net positive and I agree.  It's an iterative leap but one that's needed as over time I have growing concerns of governance participation waning due to process fatigue and confusion/interpretation efforts due to these improvements being needed.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
