      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yfa2s82ahzdudyhup5jy4xwztpmgppgxk7amvm2smr2xx3ggapruw",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibgl7wqtn7q255nhvzi4pcht6y7tqphgm6iq654b7oqrlollbtlyy -->\r\n# drep1yfa2s82ahzdudyhup5jy4xwztpmgppgxk7amvm2smr2xx3ggapruw\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfa2s82ahzdudyhup5jy4xwztpmgppgxk7amvm2smr2xx3ggapruw`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile some ideas in the amendment are helpful - streamlining the budget process and reorganizing some certain repeated sections to fall in one - the changes introduce new problems. This amendment requires more review and edits before passing.  A few specific issues - there's no longer an expectation of community coordination to develop an ecosystem budget, there's no longer a requirement to allocate funding for audit/oversight as part of a treasury withdrawal, it is no longer required to specify dispute resolution related to withdrawn funds.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1yfx2476p8smc8dyuvgz0lkgwgzdyuuaw9293ncnswy8cfac4xu0z3",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiah5pb6hvbyc2n2kucll4vytoo2eawtos6iyb2jri7b72ooaag3gi -->\r\n# drep1yfx2476p8smc8dyuvgz0lkgwgzdyuuaw9293ncnswy8cfac4xu0z3\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfx2476p8smc8dyuvgz0lkgwgzdyuuaw9293ncnswy8cfac4xu0z3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt is an acceptable update but what missing is the adoption of upper limiting drep powers. With that decisions would be more versatile and only a handful of dreps mostly like wallet owners yoroi and eternl would not hove majority just on their own already.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AdaLovelace777/2.3-Constitute-/refs/heads/main/Vote_Context%20(52).jsonld -->\r\n# drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygn28gh7gpr53re3e4nnvqqz4kv2pve0nty44qrfgqfk74gxqavlg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote YES for Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Constitution v2.3. This update is exactly the kind of practical, thoughtful refinement our governance needs. It streamlines processes, removes non-binding clutter, and reinforces accountability for all treasury withdrawals — principles that are central to sustainable, community-led governance. I appreciate the clarity and consistency brought by unified terminology, clear definitions, and immutable proposal documents. These changes protect the integrity of the process and prevent ambiguity or manipulation. Most importantly, v2.3 builds on community feedback from v2.0, showing that the Constitution evolves responsibly while maintaining decentralization, transparency, and legitimacy. This is a solid, sensible update that strengthens Cardano’s governance framework without overcomplicating it. This aligns perfectly with my values: supporting clear rules, strong oversight, and a decentralized, community-driven ecosystem.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Duc Tiger",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVAxKNAbgBTPZTVMLfzCvsJTqAxqkxhCe4D32e9Q6ku3d -->\r\n# Duc Tiger\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt0cvg2649d34afclefrxvyn2ctys87a5jt84ckczyjlvgcu7nxyr`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMy vote is a decisive **YES** for the ratification of Constitution v2.3. \r\n\r\nThis is a critical and necessary step in the maturation of our on-chain governance framework.\r\n\r\nWhile the entire document represents an improvement in clarity and simplicity, one change stands above all others: the universal application of treasury safeguards to all withdrawal actions.\r\n\r\nIn my experience as a dRep, I have observed numerous well-crafted proposals for several hundred thousand ADA. While persuasive on the surface, they often fell into a grey area, lacking the rigorous financial oversight and mandatory audit requirements that were previously reserved only for multi-million ADA projects. This has been a significant and concerning loophole.\r\n\r\nVersion 2.3 closes this loophole decisively. By mandating that every treasury withdrawal, regardless of size, be subject to the highest standards of administration and independent auditing, we are fundamentally strengthening the security and integrity of our collective Treasury.\r\n\r\nWhile the removal of the Budget Info Action is a notable change to our process, I view it as a more than acceptable trade-off. We are exchanging a procedural step for a foundational upgrade in accountability. This vote ensures that every single lovelace is treated with the same level of scrutiny, reinforcing trust and ensuring the long-term sustainability of our ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Dynamic Strategies",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmS4ac7icNpRSJ7n5hWsBUijEZuQF4PXbyHr2vDT6RKUrV -->\r\n# Dynamic Strategies\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygr93aecehnm95wr7ufpd2m6jyh2mc8vnr77f0w33g8upyc6m8ayz`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmdPekfnXrvwre4PMMS5Fz4BxyA3Yg5VBciwkhxVLbZRWY\r\n\r\n-",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "EMURGO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMGDRep/rationale/refs/heads/main/Vote_Constitutiton%20v2.3.jsonld -->\r\n# EMURGO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytvlwvyjmzfyn56n0zz4f6lj94wxhmsl5zky6knnzrf4jygpyahug`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n\r\nEMURGO as DRep votes NO on the governance action to adopt Cardano Constitution v2.3.\r\n\r\nRationale\r\n\r\nEMURGO deeply appreciates Yuta’s leadership and continued dedication in advancing the Cardano Constitution. The proposed v2.3 introduces valuable refinements to structure, consistency, and readability that contribute to the ongoing evolution of Cardano’s governance framework.\r\n\r\nHowever, several changes in this version raise substantive concerns regarding governance clarity and decentralization safeguards. The revised Net Change Limit weakens the explicit link between approved budgets and treasury withdrawals, potentially diluting fiscal accountability. \r\n\r\nThe updated Audit Requirement creates uncertainty around execution and funding responsibility, reducing procedural clarity. Additionally, the expanded Custodian Consent clause broadens custodial authority, which may inadvertently increase centralization risks and weaken user consent protections.\r\n\r\nWhile these issues may stem from good intentions to streamline the Constitution and the governance process, the current wording introduces ambiguity in areas that are foundational to Cardano’s accountability and decentralized governance model.\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nEMURGO’s NO vote reflects a commitment to preserving procedural integrity, transparency, and decentralization within Cardano’s constitutional design. We commend Yuta’s continued effort and emphasize that EMURGO remains ready to collaborate and facilitate further discussions to refine these sections in future amendments, ensuring clarity and balance in the governance framework moving forward.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Eternl DRep Committee",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Tastenkunst/eternl-drep/refs/heads/main/gov_action_00055_vote_context.jsonld -->\r\n# Eternl DRep Committee\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y29h2q6cst2pvkl2sqqvf5ljcy36uv7pmy482xnczddzgqshus24w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTL;DR: EDC voted YES on gov_action1ezp0r9rgf4njx93p9uq7l3kjs9m739jm0ntf26vplcmucec4jc0qqxjlfrc;\r\n\r\nThanks Yuta for putting in the work to update the Constitution. The update brings clarity on definitions (now being part of the document body), removed budget info actions, reducing the amounts of votes DReps have to do (though in reality only a on-chain proposal brings attention to a topic ecosystem wide and proposals will pop up multiple times with refinements and feedback from previous votes.)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmcpzvi5nEmVA3LSRr9QVaFMjZhVnF4KS5Dpd3Sj2WmBs7 -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGlad to see this proposal resubmitted with changes from feedback integrated. I sincerely hope this improvement to the Cardano Constitution passes. Thank you YUTA for your hard work in creating further clarity and simplification of the Cardano Constitution. Also, thank you to everyone who submitted constructive feedback. I appreciate the improvements made for the betterment of Cardano governance :)",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Goofycrisp",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigdnjd3i6w4u5xtwp3aox5iiomngvufv7xekz4kl5b6hyiogpud3q -->\r\n# Goofycrisp\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygxasnzmrevqra9vscpsy4xf4rqthzkp6rr6zzft2lc7nscahj9r9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support the new Cardano Constitution because it creates a clear, transparent, and accountable governance framework. It defines the roles of DReps, SPOs, and the Constitutional Committee while embedding guardrails that protect the Treasury and align governance with long-term sustainability.\r\n\r\nI also support the removal of non-binding expectations like the Budget Info Action, as it simplifies the proposal process. This change lowers friction and encourages more agile, community-driven initiatives which decentralized governance should enable.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Hermes Stakepool Germany (HRMS)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreieoco5o7ogxti37mfghqovde5miprcl5dieuu4dy2p2y47jpdwst4 -->\r\n# Hermes Stakepool Germany (HRMS)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygs5hngva3hymv7j4v0aewxpsjqskj9dnmy7j3jz5ven5zqvulq2t`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\"UTxO Balance Insufficient\"",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "hix_coffeepool",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmNLjDph3MjtW1Jq5GWms9gFXNyXKHKn5ZWfSHR4YD91rA -->\r\n# hix_coffeepool\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygnh2uf4wkc8ldgfxwz7rzuga3m8jtqew9xh5g3n587mg6g3ge0sj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmNii6cwYz4xjwD8x1bcz9rKuAsFxAwo8PRsEydaZ9P9q2\r\n\r\nI am voting No on this Governance Action.\r\nWhile I acknowledge the intention to move forward with a new version of the Cardano Constitution, I believe the process and validation behind this draft are insufficient to ensure legitimacy and community consensus at a global scale.\r\nA constitutional framework is the highest form of governance expression within the Cardano ecosystem. Therefore, its revision or replacement must be conducted with the same depth of discussion, inclusivity, and deliberative process as the original Constitutional Convention — including open workshops, community feedback cycles, and peer-reviewed validation.\r\nHowever, this proposal does not appear to have undergone comparable community engagement. The time elapsed since the last major constitutional debate has been too short, and no evidence of extensive global consultation or multilingual deliberation has been presented.\r\nEven in the most recent governance workshops held in Japan, this topic was not discussed or formally raised as an agenda item, suggesting that awareness and understanding remain limited across regions.\r\nMoreover, the editing and review process lacks transparency and objectivity. There is no public record of expert peer review, nor clear documentation of how revisions were proposed, debated, or approved. As a result, it is difficult to consider this version a sufficiently validated draft from the perspective of ecosystem safety, governance integrity, and long-term constitutional stability.\r\nIt is also concerning that the primary author and submitter of this Governance Action, who holds significant voting power, has voted in favor of their own draft. This concentration of influence raises questions about impartiality and sets a potentially dangerous precedent for future governance actions, where individuals or entities with large voting weight could unilaterally shape fundamental rules of the ecosystem.\r\nFinally, community participation metrics remain relatively low, and the proposal has not reached the level of global engagement or voting thresholds that would justify enacting a new Constitution.\r\nFor these reasons, I cannot support this Governance Action at this stage. A new Constitution should emerge from a transparent, peer-reviewed, and globally inclusive process — one that reflects the collective will of the entire Cardano community, not the initiative of a few.\r\n[Japanese ver. follows]\r\n私はこのガバナンスアクションに対して 反対票（No） を投じます。\r\n新しいカルダノ憲法の制定という意図自体は理解しますが、この草案の作成・検証プロセスは、正統性やグローバルな合意形成を担保するには不十分であると考えます。\r\n憲法はカルダノ・エコシステムにおける最高位のガバナンス文書です。したがって、その改定や再制定は、初期の憲法制定会議と同等の議論の深さ、包摂性、熟議のプロセスを経る必要があります。具体的には、オープンなワークショップ、コミュニティ・フィードバックの反映、専門家によるピアレビューなどが不可欠です。\r\nしかし、この提案はそれらに相当するコミュニティ・エンゲージメントを経ていません。前回の主要な憲法議論から十分な時間が経過しておらず、グローバル規模での議論や多言語での検討も確認されていません。\r\n直近で日本で開催されたガバナンス・ワークショップにおいても、この件は議題として取り上げられておらず、地域をまたいだ理解と関心が十分に広がっていないことが示唆されます。\r\nさらに、編集およびレビューのプロセスは透明性と客観性を欠いています。\r\n専門家によるピアレビューの記録も、どのように修正や承認が行われたかの詳細なドキュメントも公開されていません。そのため、エコシステムの安全性やガバナンスの健全性、長期的な安定性の観点から、この草案を十分に検証済みの文書と見なすことは困難です。\r\nまた、このガバナンスアクションの主要作成者であり、かつ大きな投票力を持つ当人が、自身の草案に賛成票を投じている点も懸念されます。\r\nこれは公正性や客観性に疑問を生じさせ、将来のガバナンスアクションにおいて、影響力を持つ個人や組織が一方的に基本ルールを形成するという、危険な前例を残しかねません。\r\nさらに、投票参加率も依然として低く、グローバルな関心や十分な投票密度が確認できない状況です。これをもって新憲法を制定するのは、時期尚早だと考えます。\r\n以上の理由から、私は現段階でこのガバナンスアクションを支持することはできません。\r\n新しいカルダノ憲法は、透明性・専門的検証・グローバルな包摂性を備えたプロセスから生まれるべきであり、限られた個人の主導で決定されるべきではありません。",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Homer J",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmdPczSzsNKijyD37GuWVXbpXzMwoiEvcfesGjSrtbwDNG -->\r\n# Homer J\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2rvnp40ea4zsl4hqm0ev4qju205jx7mz57u2vwjzzrf50c24jca9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nPLEASE FIX YOUR CAPSLOCK YUTA!",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "HOSKY",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmW5PW4dTLYPCuKbHumQAcYdoAJGEbXT6tnYKdtgnT6JpW -->\r\n# HOSKY\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf2jzhuc4f7eu2yay9d9ta3dykxxcwn34wz8kak7nhd7vcgrxn7ns`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmUneBaFwZ5u5sh5PGUKhkjfFRY16nhynJWtPheMpbwXb1\r\n\r\nThe Cardano Constitution v2.3 update simplifies the governance and budget processes while maintaining alignment with the ecosystem’s core principles of decentralization, transparency, and fiscal responsibility.\r\n\r\nThis revision removes unnecessary complexity and redundant sections, improving readability and operational efficiency without weakening constitutional safeguards. The streamlined budget process enhances accountability and enables more agile decision-making in the management of community resources.\r\n\r\nBy focusing on clarity, sustainability, and efficiency, the v2.3 update strengthens Cardano’s governance framework and supports long-term ecosystem growth. Therefore, the vote is YES.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "InputEndorsers",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreig2osetdtsxv6o577l6nppgr2mc5lygu45af4fjm7waen3tml53tq -->\r\n# InputEndorsers\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2hlgh9600zjlt39dh54z7z8d65kahneck8yhh7ugmzc9as0xrzqd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRalph Waldo Emerson: \r\n\r\n\"The other terror that scares us from self-trust is our consistency; a reverence for our past act or word\"  and \"Why drag about this corpse of your memory?\" \r\n\r\nThis is a better version than the existing constitution 1.0 and the proposed v 2.0 in my opinion. More precise, less typos and some important improvements, including immutable documents. More clarity about the term Net Change Limit is a big win. The unified terminology will be of help to the Constitutional Committee. The elimination of the Budget Info Action mechanism could simplify governance and help with DRep fatigue. \r\n\r\nFinally, the biggest point of this proposal for me is to show that our constitutions are but snapshots in time of an ephemeral consensus -not a national constitution. They can and should be improved by the community without waiting for one of the big entities to spearhead the process. If this is a permissionless process and someone is proposing a clearly better, tighter, less ambiguous constitution, why would I vote No?\r\n\r\nLet's move forward. If we can improve the constitution - let's be proud that we can do it and do it again. \r\n\r\nThis is a dynamic space. We might need to revisit the constitution many more times. \r\n\r\nEvolution waits for no one.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "jonahkoch",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiab7twq2wpezyryuie3yrpfla5ozttpwir32i4xei4uo6k3ou7qhi -->\r\n# jonahkoch\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt8trnz8e5cnylmyygt0pyzrfw92rt9s42kg8t4rhm6t0dstyvmdn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm voting no because Constitution v2.3 removes critical financial safeguards without adequate justification, creating exploitable governance vulnerabilities that could drain the treasury. The elimination of the Budget Info Action mechanism isn't efficiency, it's recklessness disguised as simplification. Under the current constitution, treasury withdrawals require a two-step process: first an info_action to establish budget parameters and community review, then withdrawal actions tied to that approved framework. This creates mandatory deliberation time and forces proposers to demonstrate strategic alignment before touching funds. Constitution v2.3 scraps this entirely, collapsing treasury withdrawals into single-step actions with no binding budget coordination. Here's the mathematical problem: with the info_action requirement removed and assuming no Constitutional Committee dissent, or a CC size set to minimum threshold, a treasury withdrawal could be enacted in as little as six days, at the epoch boundary following the first full epoch where the action remains active, provided the 67% DRep threshold is met. Today, that means only 23 individuals, who control the sufficient voting stake could authorize withdrawals without strategic review, public vetting, or ecosystem-wide budget discipline. With the majority of ADA still undelegated, governance becomes an exploitable attack surface during low participation periods or voting fatigue. The removal of budget requirements eliminates the forcing function that makes hard choices about technological priorities and resource allocation. Without holistic budgeting, governance devolves into disconnected withdrawal requests lacking coordination, accountability, or protection against waste and capture. A budget framework compels the ecosystem to prioritize competing demands, by removing it you invite chaotic financial management that accelerates treasury depletion. The original constitution emerged from transparent, line-by-line deliberations across continents with hundreds of elected representatives. Constitution v2.3 introduces extensive changes without undergoing comparable community engagement. Additionally the primary author holds significant voting power and voted for their own draft showing some amount of self-interested motivation, which can be a concentration of influence that sets a dangerous precedent. This is not an iterative improvement it's weakening institutional safeguards in a misguided desire to streamline a process. The budget info_action with a threshold requirement of 100% provides a necessary safeguard against expedited treasury withdrawals, by ensuring at least one full gov_action lifetime is required for any treasury withdrawal.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin G Mohr",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreieiyllmkbykmnjkocfnpfqnvydbqs6uprcf7xyzb4dbtamqukifna -->\r\n# Kevin G Mohr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwn2u7qpy4ur7k3xqd7eehft3g2yjpxf46rugwzmndkyesd0m5nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNothing makes sense",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Kevin_ALBERT",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://tinyurl.com/nhb6sn6u -->\r\n# Kevin_ALBERT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2gh7lj3jt89vs63rtr4vj5g4ulxhmp7t0dkh6hcel90mlsujgqlu`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’ve reviewed the changes from Cardano Constitution v2.0 to v2.3, as detailed in the IPFS link (https://cardano.mypinata.cloud/ipfs/bafybeihjegoita5u67sr6q2cplb33zglytwdo7355u6f2wn4wayhq6uy4e). I’m voting YES because it simplifies governance, speeds up funding for developers and users, and aligns with Cardano’s decentralized vision, building on my support for v2.0. It clarifies terms like “Ada Holders,” defines “Net Change Limit” (the cap on treasury spending), and ensures proposals can’t be changed after submission (ARTICLE II, Section 6), boosting trust. Combining the Budget Info step into a single withdrawal action with a checklist makes funding faster, and requiring audits for all withdrawals ensures community safety, a key priority for me.\r\n\r\nHowever, there are risks. The removal of the requirement to name recipients of treasury withdrawals (ARTICLE II, Section 7) could obscure who gets funds, reducing transparency and risking misuse, as noted in other DReps’ concerns about accountability. Not mandating funds for audits in withdrawal proposals might lead to weaker oversight, as audits could be underfunded, potentially allowing sloppy spending. Dropping the Constitutional Committee’s code of conduct mandate (ARTICLE VII, Section 6) means the CC, which approves governance actions, isn’t required to follow clear ethical rules. This could lead to inconsistent decisions, eroding community trust, as some DReps argue it makes the Constitution feel less authoritative. The new “Stake Pool Operator” definition as “the entity controlling cold keys” (ARTICLE II, Section 5) might confuse voting rights in multi-party pool setups, where the keyholder isn’t the main operator, potentially disrupting fair governance.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
