      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA070-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action1ezp0r9rgf4njx93p9uq7l3kjs9m739jm0ntf26vplcmucec4jc0qqxjlfrc), pois ela reflete o desejo da comunidade em amadurecer os processos de governança, especialmente ao propor a remoção da “Info Action” para ações de saque orçamentário, além de tornar obrigatórios os requisitos administrativos e de auditoria para todos os saques do tesouro. Trata-se de uma medida que reforça a transparência, a responsabilidade e a integridade dos processos de gestão de recursos da rede, fortalecendo a confiança e a maturidade institucional do ecossistema.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action (gov_action1ezp0r9rgf4njx93p9uq7l3kjs9m739jm0ntf26vplcmucec4jc0qqxjlfrc), because it reflects the community’s desire to advance the maturity of governance processes, particularly by proposing the removal of the “Info Action” for budget withdrawal actions, and by making administrative and auditing requirements mandatory for all treasury withdrawals. This measure strengthens transparency, accountability, and integrity in the networks resource management processes, reinforcing trust and institutional maturity within the ecosystem.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigcymlgrappp2v7qapfrrz5un2mclrffbq4kqa7vgrfaahqinskw4 -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe changes to the constitution being made by this proposal are well thought through and there has been extensive community input. The result I believe is a better, more concise document. The most important change is the removal of the info action requirement for budget withdrawals. I believe this to be a good change to try and make the governance process less onerous on both DReps and proposers. It's important to note that some of the requirements that were part of the info action process still exist but are now part of the withdrawal request process. This should maintain the safety of the system while improving its agility. I find the changes here to be positive and therefore I am voting in favor of this proposal. Thank you to everyone who has put in extensive effort into this action.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmezWZSfgjGbDXWd8ronsB6EEVdJWpm7VvuYh2fbe5Q3DP -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support Cardano Constitution v2.3.\r\n\r\nThis constitutional reform streamlines governance by removing non-binding expectations and redundant mechanisms,\r\nreducing unnecessary workload and making the framework more consistent, practical, and sustainable.\r\nBy applying audit and accountability safeguards to all Treasury withdrawals\r\nand enforcing immutability of proposal documents,\r\nv2.3 strengthens integrity, transparency, and trust across the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nAs a DRep, I believe this reform advances Cardano’s governance\r\nfrom goodwill-based participation toward a more mature and durable institutional model —\r\none that protects decentralization by ensuring that community members are not overburdened.\r\n\r\nCardano Constitution v2.3 に賛成します。\r\n\r\n本改正は、非拘束的な期待条項や冗長なメカニズムを整理し、\r\nコミュニティに過度な負担をかけることなく、\r\nガバナンス構造をより明確かつ実務的で持続可能なものにしています。\r\nすべてのトレジャリー支出に監査・説明責任を適用し、\r\n提案文書の不変性を明文化することで、透明性と信頼性が一層強化されます。\r\n\r\nDRepとして、善意への依存から脱し、分散性を守りながら現実的に機能する制度へと前進する\r\n成熟したガバナンスの姿を示す改正だと考えます。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifwu6mkv6dawinbwlesxjgjt7aqappgfxxds7cm5hzfzy6lmfgmmy -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** CARDANO BLOCKCHAIN ECOSYSTEM CONSTITUTION v2.3\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep Position: Conditional Support (Yes with Recommendations)\r\n\r\nSIPO supports the “Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Constitution v2.3” proposal as an important step toward a more transparent, accountable, and immutable governance framework. However, we adopt a “Conditional Yes” stance, as some aspects need further improvement in future versions.\r\n\r\nReasons for Support:\r\nv2.3 strengthens Cardano’s institutional trust through:\r\n\t1.\tClear immutability of proposal documents, ensuring proposals cannot be altered after submission.\r\n\t2.\tUniversal audit and accountability safeguards for all treasury withdrawals.\r\n\t3.\tRemoval of non-binding or aspirational clauses, simplifying governance and making it more enforceable.\r\n\r\nThese reforms make Cardano’s governance more consistent, transparent, and aligned with the principles of decentralized public infrastructure. They represent progress from an advisory framework toward a practical and legally functional constitution.\r\n\r\nPoints for Improvement:\r\n\t1.\tThe removal of the “Budget Info Action” simplifies the process but reduces pre-execution transparency. SIPO recommends introducing a pre-disclosure or review mechanism before treasury withdrawals to preserve open deliberation.\r\n\t2.\tThe removal of the mandatory “Code of Conduct” for the Constitutional Committee grants flexibility, but SIPO believes that ethical standards for DReps and the Committee remain essential for maintaining public trust.\r\n\t3.\tImmutability is a valuable improvement, yet Cardano governance must remain adaptive and human-centered. SIPO encourages including continuous discussion phases for feedback and reflection in future versions (v2.4+).\r\n\r\nBroader Context:\r\nThis constitutional update positions Cardano at the forefront of on-chain governance globally. It enhances institutional reliability and sets a precedent for transparent, auditable, and democratic decision-making. For SIPO, this version lays a stronger foundation for initiatives like AIRA and future real-world applications that depend on Cardano’s public trust layer.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nSIPO votes YES (Conditional Support) for Cardano Constitution v2.3.\r\nWe support its direction and structure as a step toward a more mature, transparent, and trustworthy ecosystem. At the same time, we call for the following improvements in v2.4 and beyond:\r\n\t•\tReintroduction of transparent pre-budget disclosure mechanisms.\r\n\t•\tReaffirmation of behavioral and ethical standards for DReps and Committees.\r\n\t•\tEstablishment of an ongoing discussion phase to balance formal rules with human collaboration.\r\n\r\nv2.3 builds institutional trust. The next evolution should strengthen human trust — ensuring Cardano’s governance embodies both decentralization in code and collaboration in community.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nSIPO DRepの立場：条件付き賛成（Yes with Recommendations）\r\n\r\nSIPOは、「Cardano Blockchain Ecosystem Constitution v2.3」提案に条件付きで賛成します。\r\nこの改訂は、カルダノのガバナンスをより透明で、説明責任のある制度へ進化させる重要な一歩だと考えます。\r\n\r\n支持する理由:\r\nv2.3では、次の3点が特に高く評価できます。\r\n\t1.\t提案文書の不変性を明文化し、改ざんを防ぐことで信頼性を確立。\r\n\t2.\tすべてのトレジャリー出金に対して監査を義務化し、公共資金の透明性を強化。\r\n\t3.\t非拘束的条項を整理し、実務的かつ法的に明確な憲法構造を確立。\r\n\r\nこれにより、カルダノは「公共インフラとしての分散型信頼システム」へと一歩前進します。\r\n\r\n改善を求める点:\r\n\t1.\tBudget Info Actionの削除により手続きが簡素化された一方で、資金執行前の透明性が減少しました。今後は、出金前の情報開示やレビューの仕組みを制度的に設けることを提案します。\r\n\t2.\t憲法委員会（CC）の行動規範義務が削除されましたが、DRepやCCに共通する倫理指針の維持は不可欠です。コミュニティ主導での行動規範再整備を期待します。\r\n\t3.\t不変性の強化は重要ですが、ガバナンスは柔軟性と人間的対話も必要です。v2.4以降では、オンチェーン投票と並行して意見交換を続けるディスカッションフェーズの制度化を提案します。\r\n\r\n全体的意義:\r\nv2.3は、カルダノが暗号資産ネットワークを超えて、透明で説明責任のある分散型公共インフラへ進化することを示しています。SIPOは、AIRAなどの現実社会連携プロジェクトにおいて、この憲法が信頼の基盤になると考えています。\r\n\r\n結論:\r\nSIPOは本提案に**賛成（Yes）**票を投じます。\r\nただし、以下の改善を今後の改訂に求めます。\r\n\t•\t予算情報の事前開示プロセスの再設計\r\n\t•\t倫理規範・行動指針の明文化\r\n\t•\t継続的ディスカッションの制度化\r\n\r\nv2.3は制度としての信頼を確立しました。\r\n次は、人間的信頼と協働を強化する段階へ。\r\nそれこそが、カルダノが「分散化された文明のガバナンス」を体現するための道だとSIPOは考えています。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
