    {
      "voter": "GAIA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmcnBMMargYUepr8yJeUZZXoAW22AeKgYPx3r5S848b3ki -->\r\n# GAIA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytxr0lhg5j72wysva9ac2gsn4lck4gyen8ywxkqfchsqg3qs8uy44`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHell no! After last year's Cardano Summit fiasco where the community was exploited with abusive ticket prices, there is no way I am voting yes for this.\r\n\r\nBoth the Cardano Foundation and EMURGO should be using genesis ADA to pay for building Cardano, not exploiting the treasury every week or two.\r\n\r\nIt is not in Cardano's best interest to burn through the treasury on wasteful spending like this during a bear market. Burn some genesis ADA instead if you want to actually support Cardano.\r\n\r\nAlso, if EMURGO or YOROI votes anything but abstain on this proposal, it is 100% a conflict of interest and we all know it!",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "GOMA-DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreib4xcncsja5x4rd4nes2capnqs2u3n5fpgi2gcf3lftdtfzj5qjfq -->\r\n# GOMA-DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2cm9w2egseygejydtgdddnsw9zdpc6ayyf8xh5ascfq4tqkpj06v`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI have chosen to abstain on this treasury withdrawal proposal after careful consideration of both its strategic value and its associated costs.\r\n\r\nOn one hand, I recognize the importance of global visibility and ecosystem positioning. Participation in major international events such as TOKEN2049, alongside the organization of the Cardano Summit 2026, can contribute to strengthening institutional relationships, increasing awareness, and showcasing the maturity of the Cardano ecosystem. The proposal is well-structured, includes clear objectives, and builds on prior event experience.\r\n\r\nHowever, I remain uncertain about the proportional return on investment relative to the scale of the requested funding (~14 million ADA). While key performance indicators are outlined, the direct and measurable impact of such events on long-term ecosystem growth, user adoption, and on-chain activity remains difficult to assess with high confidence.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, given the current stage of the ecosystem, I believe there is a valid argument for prioritizing treasury allocations toward infrastructure development, developer tooling, and initiatives with more direct and verifiable impact on network usage and resilience.\r\n\r\nMy abstention reflects a neutral stance: I do not oppose the strategic intent of the proposal, but I am not sufficiently convinced that this represents the most effective use of treasury resources at this time.\r\n\r\nI encourage continued transparency, post-event reporting, and clearer frameworks for evaluating the tangible outcomes of large-scale marketing and ecosystem events in future proposals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Goofycrisp",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreietmhv7hdofp5wbrrsn2pah7i3zp35pcvrelyma2mjw3ujkd3vg4u -->\r\n# Goofycrisp\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygxasnzmrevqra9vscpsy4xf4rqthzkp6rr6zzft2lc7nscahj9r9`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile I support this proposal because Cardano needs stronger marketing and visibility, I find the withdrawal amount to be too much. Perhaps we should divide this proposal into 2 withdrawals. A presence at Token2049 Singapore is a necessity and will help attract users, partners, and opportunities, while ensuring Cardano stays relevant and competitive in the broader crypto space. With the low value of ADA, we could think of something more cost effective for the Summit.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "heo.keo",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmenChk3xrrcWeNwWnauutXnHYSeY9U9T8EHQ2PSPHFtiT -->\r\n# heo.keo\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytwltt6ywdu4gtuxagz0s0wudwtm35kknp25z8cpmwwnlpc0xage6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nwith that $3 million, we can spend on other activities, marketing, our own event",
