      "voter": "Musa Ridwan Itopa",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmRMaUpLqRpF3tZKioY9oSXYWSF5piBs1iJzCzDwyCEkFB -->\r\n# Musa Ridwan Itopa\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yggumgdxdpa2dgr85etak35s4v00k07vdhvn5y3xxw33yac77c9hp`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nVoting NO on Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore (Treasury Withdrawal).  As elected Cardano Civics Committee member, Unified Cardano Student Club President in Nigeria, and advocate for real adoption + Africa/student inclusion, I believe visibility matters. However, bundling a full Summit with expensive TOKEN2049 sponsorship feels like high-cost marketing when treasury discipline is critical.  We need clearer, measurable ROI focused on on-chain growth, developer onboarding, and emerging market participation not just big-stage presence. Let's prioritize funds that directly empower builders and users in Africa and beyond. Happy to revisit if split into separate, more targeted proposals with strong KPIs.",
