    {
      "voter": "Rod G",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNPVAZGfjXF3z3KvuD4rcAeoZ8oJrrhJnhTSsZXAxs5xY -->\r\n# Rod G\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygwscks2yt0na4fqpcdyqn0fare5v48y0mjgn2g478lnx8gue393e`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile recognizing that I’m a strong supporter of conferences, networking, and ecosystem-building events, I am voting NO on this proposal. Though I believe in their value, these efforts too often lack transparency in terms of measurable success, and this proposal does not sufficiently address that gap.\r\n\r\nThe 2025 Summit did not provide clear, verifiable evidence of developer growth or enterprise adoption, and the 2026 proposal moves further away from outcome-based evaluation by emphasizing surface-level outputs (contacts, sign-ups, impressions) without clear linkage to meaningful ecosystem impact.\r\n\r\nFrom what I’ve observed at similar events, there are also valid concerns about execution at this scale, and the proposal’s focus on enterprise adoption lacks a clear structural pathway to on-chain activity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, much of the agenda appears internally focused, which makes it difficult to justify a high-cost international event when more efficient alternatives may exist.\r\n\r\nUltimately, without clearer data, stronger KPIs, and demonstrated outcomes, I’m not confident this level of funding will deliver proportional value to the ecosystem.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreifcl2ccsfz2nz3vvhef7ekiegjf3cdn7t4jomil2566ssonmob6h4 -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting against this proposal. My primary objection is two-fold: fiscal responsibility and the lack of a measurable framework to assess impact. As this proposal is essentially a marketing initiative, I believe it should be evaluated within the context of a dedicated marketing budget rather than as a standalone treasury withdrawal.\r\n\r\nTo clarify my position, I have recently supported several proposals that presented clear, quantifiable outcomes or addressed critical infrastructure needs. For instance, I strongly support initiatives to increase node diversity, as this is a tangible security requirement. In such cases, I am prepared to vote in favor of credible teams working toward that specific goal until a sufficient threshold is met. These are strategic imperatives that do not require an overarching budget to justify.\r\n\r\nConversely, treating marketing initiatives as ad-hoc, standalone proposals is inefficient. We should have a comprehensive strategy that outlines our total marketing spend and community priorities before approving individual, fragmented requests. While I acknowledge the proposal’s rationale for bypassing the Intersect budget process, I cannot justify a 'Yes' vote based on a time constraint alone. We need a more structured approach to capital allocation for marketing efforts.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmazEBNssEgr9hkw8vBPD2BXRBhQEWWn4EZxebHg1mAwHr -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI will abstain on this proposal.\r\n\r\nAt the current stage of Cardano’s development, I believe that in addition to building products and infrastructure, it is essential to strengthen awareness and business engagement to connect those offerings with external users and partners. Expanding supply alone is not sufficient if it does not translate into real usage, partnerships, and sustainable ecosystem growth.\r\n\r\nFrom this perspective, hosting the Cardano Summit in Singapore alongside TOKEN2049 is a strategically sound approach. Singapore serves as a major hub for finance and Web3, and this co-location can help expand Cardano’s visibility and create meaningful touchpoints with institutions, enterprises, and developers.\r\n\r\nI also recognize that events of this scale cannot realistically be executed by the community alone, and that it is appropriate for entities such as the Cardano Foundation and EMURGO to take responsibility for organizing them, with treasury support as a reasonable funding mechanism.\r\n\r\nHowever, I remain concerned about the overall scale of the budget. At this time, I do not have sufficient confidence in the return on investment, particularly regarding how event-driven exposure will translate into measurable on-chain activity and sustained ecosystem growth. More clarity is needed on the target segments, types of organizations being pursued, and the expected tangible outcomes such as partnerships and ecosystem impact.\r\n\r\nIn summary, while I acknowledge the strategic direction and intent of this proposal, I do not believe the current level of detail and cost justification is sufficient to support a definitive vote. For these reasons, I choose to abstain and look forward to a refined proposal with clearer cost optimization and outcome visibility.\r\n\r\n本提案については、最終的に棄権とします。\r\n\r\n現在のCardanoにおいては、プロダクトやインフラの開発に加え、それらを外部に届けるための認知拡大およびビジネス接続の強化が不可欠であると考えています。供給のみが拡大しても、それが実際の利用やパートナーシップに結びつかなければ、エコシステム全体としての成長には繋がりません。\r\n\r\nその観点から、シンガポールという金融・Web3のハブにおいて、TOKEN2049と連動してCardano Summitを開催する戦略は、外部への認知拡大および機関・企業・開発者との接点を拡張する上で合理的であり、一定の意義があると評価しています。\r\n\r\nまた、本規模のイベントをコミュニティ主導で実行することは現実的に難しく、Cardano FoundationおよびEMURGOのような主体が責任を持って推進し、その活動に対してトレジャリーから支援を行うこと自体についても理解しています。\r\n\r\n一方で、本提案は規模が大きく、費用水準に対する懸念が残るとともに、費用対効果やイベント後の成果がどのようにオンチェーンでの利用や継続的なエコシステム成長へと接続されるのかについて、現時点では十分な確信を持つには至っていません。特に、どのような企業・分野をターゲットとし、どの程度の提携や具体的な成果を見込んでいるのかについて、より明確な指標と説明が求められると考えています。\r\n\r\n以上を踏まえ、本提案の戦略的方向性および必要性には一定の理解を示しつつも、現時点の設計および情報では明確な賛否を判断するには不十分であると判断し、棄権とします。今後、コスト最適化および成果の可視化がより強化された形での再提案を期待します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Shawn McMurdo - SQUID",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://QmYAFwCVnYXRTARdtFZEJQHyut2Azg8etZyEicZYkRjxkg -->\r\n# Shawn McMurdo - SQUID\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt99uyp9c8qura9spfgqe8uf7g2avmqc683x28zcugh0sycjd6wp0`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nA [PDF version][pdf-link] of this rationale is also made available.\r\n\r\n[pdf-link]: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmRiJsiQk9Xyyp2tabPpjLbeps352Awi1dbgvjp9q9KCsa\r\n\r\nYes",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibwkktrvqjnl3dznw66ymz6cpunl5b42wvnpv2cwgp4rzftwl5nci -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[VOTE: NO]\r\n\r\nSIPO DRep Vote Context — Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\nGovernance Action ID: gov_action1hkgl5l4fknsf7aktmcatkz6kfl7xpvn7rzh5vnxwexl0n3cc6zrsqt5459v\r\nDRep: drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh\r\nDate: 2026-04-18\r\n\r\n================================\r\nENGLISH\r\n================================\r\n\r\nVote: NO\r\n\r\nSIPO is voting NO on this proposal. To be explicit: we are not opposed to Cardano Summit 2026 being held, not opposed to Cardano having a presence at TOKEN2049, and not opposed to the Cardano Foundation or EMURGO as organizations. We are opposed to the specific structure of this treasury withdrawal, for four reasons rooted in our fiduciary duty as a DRep.\r\n\r\n1. Self-funding capacity — a treasury-fit question\r\n\r\nThe 2025 Financial Insights and Activity Report referenced in this very proposal documents a CF financial position sufficient to cover Summit costs without a treasury withdrawal. CF self-funded the Summits from 2022 through 2024. CF has already secured the 2026 Singapore location using 2025 Summit revenue, as stated in this proposal. We acknowledge that 2025 was the first year CF accessed treasury funding for the Summit (under \"Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing Strategy\"). Voting YES on 2026 would consolidate that as a recurring pattern. For a well-capitalized entity, treasury should be the funding source of last resort, not first, and the case for crossing that line should be explicitly argued. This proposal does not make that argument.\r\n\r\n2. Three-way conflict-of-interest structure\r\n\r\nCardano Foundation (DRep with approx. ₳133m delegated) and EMURGO (DRep with approx. ₳297m delegated) are simultaneously (a) the proposers, (b) the direct beneficiaries of the withdrawal, and (c) active DReps voting on the outcome. This is not illegal under CIP-1694, but it is in structural tension with the spirit of Article II of the Constitution. The proposal could have mitigated this by publicly pre-committing both DReps to Abstain on their own action, or by routing the request through a neutral third-party sponsor. It does neither.\r\n\r\n3. Public goods vs. brand marketing characterization\r\n\r\nThe Sundae Labs treasury contracts framework — which this proposal appropriately adopts — was designed to fund public goods, infrastructure, and direct builder support. Within the USD 3.66M requested, the TOKEN2049 Title Sponsorship fee alone is USD 699,900, and the full TOKEN2049 budget is USD 1.16M. The deliverables of that package (mainstage keynote exclusive to title sponsors, premium booth positioning, social channel mentions, priority check-in) are classic brand marketing outputs, not public goods. By comparison, hackathon, prizes, and builder incentives total USD 54,830 across the entire proposal — 1.95 percent of the Summit subtotal. We believe this ratio inverts the priorities a community treasury should express.\r\n\r\n4. IOG absence and the \"unified Cardano\" framing\r\n\r\nThe proposal positions Summit 2026 + TOKEN2049 as a flagship unified Cardano event. Historically, unified Cardano initiatives have included Input Output (IOG/IOHK) as one of three founding entities alongside CF and EMURGO. This proposal is signed by CF and EMURGO only. No statement is provided explaining IOG's non-participation, nor any indication of whether IOG was invited to co-sign. For a treasury withdrawal of this size carrying \"unified Cardano\" branding, community clarity on the relationship among the three founding entities is a reasonable minimum disclosure.\r\n\r\nConsistency with SIPO's prior votes\r\n\r\nSIPO has consistently voted YES on treasury withdrawals for:\r\n- Protocol and node diversity (Amaru, Dingo, HLabs Pebble + Gerolamo)\r\n- Capital formation infrastructure (DeFi Liquidity Budget, Orion Fund with conditions)\r\n- Governance institutions (Constitutional Committee compensation, NCL, Budget Framework)\r\n- Critical integrations\r\n\r\nAll of these fit within \"public goods, infrastructure, or ecosystem growth capital.\" This proposal does not fit those categories. A NO here does not contradict our prior YES pattern; it clarifies the line we draw.\r\n\r\nConstructive alternatives\r\n\r\n- CF funds Cardano Summit 2026 from its own reserves, consistent with 2022–2024 practice and with 2025 Summit revenue already ring-fenced for 2026.\r\n- EMURGO pursues TOKEN2049 Title Sponsorship through commercial partnership funding, or accepts a scaled-down non-title booth, or resubmits through the Intersect budget process for the 2027 cycle with adequate lead time.\r\n- Any future treasury-funded event proposal should include (a) an explicit public-goods justification, (b) disclosure of the positions of all three founding entities, (c) pre-committed Abstain from proposer DReps, and (d) a higher builder-direct allocation ratio.\r\n\r\nWe thank Cardano Foundation and EMURGO for their consistent event execution over the past four years, and we look forward to supporting future proposals that are structured as public goods investments.\r\n\r\n================================\r\n日本語\r\n================================\r\n\r\n投票: NO（反対）\r\n\r\nSIPO は本提案に反対票を投じます。はじめに明確にします。私たちは Cardano Summit 2026 の開催自体に反対ではありません。TOKEN2049 における Cardano のプレゼンスに反対でもありません。Cardano Foundation や EMURGO という組織に反対でもありません。私たちが反対するのは、この Treasury Withdrawal の「構造」です。DRep としての受託者責任に基づく4つの理由を以下に述べます。\r\n\r\n1. 自己資金調達能力 — Treasury 適合性の問題\r\n\r\n本提案自身が参照している「Cardano Foundation 2025 Financial Insights and Activity Report」には、Summit 費用を Treasury に頼らずに賄える財務状態が記されています。CF は 2022 年から 2024 年までの Summit を自己資金で開催してきました。2026 年の Singapore 会場も、CF は 2025 年 Summit の収益を用いて既に確保済みであると本提案自身が述べています。2025 年が Summit で Treasury 資金に初めてアクセスした年であったことは認識しています（\"Unveiling the First Unified Global Events Marketing Strategy\"）。ここで 2026 年も YES とすれば、それを恒常的パターンとして定着させることになります。十分な資本を持つ組織にとって、Treasury は「最後の資金源」であるべきで「最初の資金源」ではないというのが私たちの考えです。そしてその線を越えるのであれば、越える理由を明示的に論じる必要がありますが、本提案にその論証はありません。\r\n\r\n2. 三重の利益相反構造\r\n\r\nCardano Foundation（DRep 委任額 約 ₳133m）と EMURGO（DRep 委任額 約 ₳297m）は、本提案において同時に (a) 提案者、(b) 直接受益者、(c) 投票権を行使する DRep の三者を兼ねています。これは CIP-1694 の下で違法ではありませんが、Cardano Constitution 第 II 条の精神と構造的に緊張関係にあります。緩和策として、両 DRep が本提案に対して Abstain を事前表明するか、または中立的な第三者スポンサー経由で提出するという選択肢がありました。本提案はそのいずれも採っていません。\r\n\r\n3. 公共財 vs ブランドマーケティングの性質\r\n\r\n本提案が採用している Sundae Labs treasury contracts フレームワークは、公共財・インフラ・ビルダー直接支援のために設計されたものです。要求額 USD 3.66M のうち、TOKEN2049 Title Sponsorship 費用だけで USD 699,900、TOKEN2049 総予算では USD 1.16M に達しますが、その対価（Title Sponsor 専用のメインステージ基調講演、優先ブース位置、ソーシャルチャネル告知、優先チェックイン）は典型的なブランドマーケティング成果物であり、公共財ではありません。対照的に、Hackathon・賞金・ビルダーインセンティブの合計は USD 54,830、Summit サブトータルの 1.95 パーセントに過ぎません。コミュニティ Treasury が表現すべき優先順位として、この配分比率は逆であると考えます。\r\n\r\n4. IOG 不在と「統合 Cardano イベント」の主張\r\n\r\n本提案は Summit 2026 + TOKEN2049 を Cardano の統合旗艦イベントと位置づけています。歴史的に、Cardano の統合イニシアチブは CF・EMURGO に加え Input Output（IOG/IOHK）を創設 3 エンティティの一角として含んできました。本提案の署名者は CF と EMURGO のみです。IOG が不参加である理由、あるいは IOG が共同署名を打診されたかどうかに関する説明はありません。この規模の Treasury Withdrawal で、かつ「統合 Cardano」というブランディングを掲げるのであれば、3 エンティティ間の関係性に関するコミュニティへの説明は最低限の情報開示であると考えます。\r\n\r\n過去の SIPO 投票との整合性\r\n\r\nSIPO が YES を投じてきた Treasury Withdrawal は以下のカテゴリに属します。\r\n- プロトコルとノード多様性（Amaru、Dingo、HLabs Pebble + Gerolamo）\r\n- 資本形成インフラ（DeFi Liquidity Budget、Orion Fund 条件付き）\r\n- ガバナンス制度（Constitutional Committee 報酬、NCL、Budget Framework）\r\n- 重要統合（Critical Integrations Budget）\r\n\r\nいずれも「公共財・インフラ・エコシステム成長資本」の範疇にあります。本提案はこのいずれにも該当しません。本提案への NO は、過去の YES パターンとの矛盾ではなく、Treasury を適用すべき線を明確化するものです。\r\n\r\n建設的代替案\r\n\r\n- CF は Cardano Summit 2026 を自己資金で開催する（2022–2024 の実務および 2026 向けに既に確保済みの 2025 Summit 収益と整合）。\r\n- EMURGO は TOKEN2049 Title Sponsorship を商業パートナーシップ資金で追求するか、Title 未取得のスケールダウンしたブース出展に変更するか、または 2027 年度分として Intersect 予算プロセス経由で十分なリードタイムを持って再提出する。\r\n- 今後の Treasury 資金型イベント提案には、(a) 公共財としての明示的正当化、(b) 創設 3 エンティティの立場の開示、(c) 提案者 DRep からの事前 Abstain 表明、(d) ビルダー直接配分比の引き上げ、を含めることを期待します。\r\n\r\n過去 4 年にわたる Cardano Foundation と EMURGO のイベント運営実績には敬意を表します。今後、公共財投資として構造化された提案については、積極的に支持してまいります。\r\n\r\n— SIPO DRep\r\ndrep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh\r\n2026-04-18",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
