    {
      "voter": "TNT",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreibljuxy2i3xi74ihb6p2ycopd55dwp4m2ervmfhwzrn4v7ilcvyf4 -->\r\n# TNT\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygc0skj7ceaszyvpte75h4xrw0m6wcenj0kd2uj7lkq5vmcjryeec`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIt's an optimal proposal at a really tough moment. That said, this year's Cardano Summit should be the most interesting one yet, with DeFi applications incubating and Bitcoin starting to make its presence felt, and TOKEN2049 is packed with external audience.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Tony Boersma",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmVmDSXjxbr5XZAthY1fBguRSGwgg4K8zwXkhSjbHKtZRj -->\r\n# Tony Boersma\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7rhr6k8gfecdn8z5r38uqyaafcfr785lsgzsvc7ye3m9g3z20kj`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting Yes on funding Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore. While it is difficult to justify large expenditures during a period of lower market valuation, I believe strategic promotion and visibility are critical to long-term ecosystem growth. High-profile events like these provide important opportunities to attract developers, partners, and capital, and to ensure Cardano remains competitive with other ecosystems that are actively investing in their presence. In this context, continued outreach and brand-building are necessary to support adoption and future demand, even if the timing requires careful consideration of costs.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "TriangleForces",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU9opriX6rW6qg6T3azQaCcxG4qdDsFeW7aUAD2ALaWXN -->\r\n# TriangleForces\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2y3euudfnw48xeulsfupsttlx8c4xphhaw90d66dvcrazgjdm5uc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Let's get this straight: Treasury money is not marketing pocket money, and prestige is not a public good!**\r\n\r\nSome 14M ADAD are going to be split between the Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 sponsorship. In plain terms, the value proposition is: we need to be seen at a very big event because important people will be there. I find that strategically weak. Granted, a premium title sponsorship at TOKEN2049 is a good way to achieve exposure, but that's not enough for me. A large booth, mainstage slot, media mentions, receptions, and branded presence may be impressive, but impressive is not synonymous with treasury-worthy. **When the pitch depends this much on foot traffic, audience scale, and industry buzz, I start hearing FOMO dressed up as strategy.**\r\n\r\nThere's also a **duplication problem by bundling a standalone Cardano Summit and a large external sponsorship. If the Summit already exists to showcase Cardano’s technology, governance maturity, enterprise use cases, and ecosystem projects, then the proposal must clear a high bar to prove why a second, expensive layer of event visibility is necessary rather than merely additive**. I do not think it clears that bar. “More reach” is not the same as “better outcomes.” Treasury spending must be judged by strategic necessity and likely long-term return, not by vanity-scale exposure metrics.\r\n\r\n**I also see this initiative as a concentrated influence asking the treasury to fund Cardano Foundation's and EMURGO's own strategic agenda.** Even if managed cleanly, that should trigger a higher burden of proof, not a lower one.\r\n\r\nIf this initiative is truly so valuable, there are **better alternatives than a treasury ask: a smaller, narrowly targeted delegation; private partner roadshows; bespoke institutional meetings in Singapore; or direct self-funding by the founding entities with later evidence-based review of actual ecosystem impact. I would far rather see precision than spectacle.** Treasury discipline must mean something precisely when prestige proposals arrive wearing institutional suits.\r\n\r\nIf anything, this proposal reeks of kindergarten-level thinking: shouting loudest in the biggest room instead of whispering strategically in the right ears. Cardano’s time and budget deserve better than a scattergun approach masquerading as ambition. It’s time to get serious. Ditch the FOMO-driven “big boys’ club” mindset and focus on razor-sharp precision. Otherwise, we’re just paying to be wallpaper at a party that doesn’t move the needle.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Varavas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmU5UY59AaBBb4ms1kcgxpSZqUNv1jto9YXau3UZwT4Pu4 -->\r\n# Varavas\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yte3chru8m7d3gzgpwvmgan0gjfxru9r9cyvrkkcerc0wcg6qfvtc`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBoth the Cardano Summit and our presence at Token2049 are important and strategically well-placed, especially with the Summit being held in Singapore.  \r\nHowever, given the significant amount of treasury funds involved (and particularly since the Summit allocation is double last year’s projection) I do not understand why these are bundled into a single governance action rather than presented separately.  This proposal comes at a sensitive time when the community is exercising heightened scrutiny over treasury spending, amid ongoing mistrust toward the founding entities regarding multiple DRep accounts and the use of genesis ADA as voting power.  I would like to see both events take place, but the current timing for committing treasury funds to support them is not ideal.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Victor.Villagomez",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUeD4J6t9ZKiGqG2cbpUoy2GyVehDYUJqZG5dbAzEUxQD -->\r\n# Victor.Villagomez\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2utmer3m25qvcfrmglld88yueq9se3d8hqjnj20wk4q0cgz92za6`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI'm starting to get really concerned about our spend rate. Especially after the Draper deal. So I'm starting to vote no on withdrawals just on principle in order to provide a counter weight (as small as my vote might be). I will only vote yes on withdrawals that are very high priority.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Viet_Cardano_Community",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSwkoLgZkjp1YochxKBZYorTzvGNPZWpPDXh4QVwvJrn7 -->\r\n# Viet_Cardano_Community\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygpzpm4q38rfueu2use5te4ylykn4smvs7cxj2ggvktcjkqpxhvf4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe are not rejecting this idea because it is bad. Positioning Cardano alongside TOKEN2049 is strategically sound and can expand visibility beyond the existing ecosystem.\r\n\r\nOur concern is about measurable outcomes. For a proposal requesting significant treasury funding, it is critical to show what concrete value returns to the ecosystem.\r\n\r\nMetrics like reach, sentiment, or media mentions do not directly translate into growth. What matters more are outcomes such as partnerships, integrations, investor engagement, or real opportunities for projects. These are not clearly defined in the proposal.\r\n\r\nEven the stronger KPIs still lack clarity. There is no clear definition of what counts as a qualified lead or collaboration, who verifies them, and what happens after the event. Without this, the measurement framework is too weak.\r\n\r\nA strong presence at a major event does not automatically create value. Visibility alone is not enough to justify treasury spending without clear, trackable results.\r\n\r\nWe support Cardano being present on global stages. But treasury usage must be measurable and accountable. In its current form, this proposal does not provide enough clarity on impact to justify the funding.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Will Norris",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmUkbE84S4k4zA5EvTYhsGz7HX1tSNE46dUfguByGiwX1Q -->\r\n# Will Norris\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuufvd6maykgfcp20fxgpx7g6a9z2suchqehfejwdsx8cgpx80yg`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting NO on the original Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore treasury withdrawal. I support Cardano having a strong global presence, and I am not opposed to a Cardano Summit or a targeted TOKEN2049 strategy in principle. However, this proposal bundles two materially different spending decisions into one vote, requests a very large treasury allocation, and does not provide a sufficiently convincing ROI case for the scale of spend. The subsequent community pushback and the move toward revised standalone Summit and TOKEN2049 proposals confirms that the original structure was not the right approach. Treasury funds should be deployed with strong discipline, clear voter choice, measurable ecosystem impact, and the highest possible accountability. For those reasons, I believe the original bundled proposal should be rejected and considered only through leaner, separate, better-scoped proposals.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "William Doyle",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigcv5uennvhl54xknsf7bcw3mf36n4rdgbqfjbfa7xs5vkmm324wi -->\r\n# William Doyle\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Voting Against Funding *Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore*\r\n\r\n## Summary \r\n\r\nCardano Foundation and EMURGO are asking for 14,076,539 ADA to fund the 2026 Cardano Summit and to sponsor TOKEN2049.\r\n\r\n## Grievances\r\n\r\n- The Cardano Foundation has resisted all attempts to allow for a community-elected board member.\r\n- For years, the Cardano Foundation has neglected many of its responsibilities.\r\n- EMURGO has abused its position as a wallet service provider to accumulate an unnatural amount of voting power across multiple dReps under its control (BTW, this is why I created [drep-of-the-month.williamdoyle.ca](https://drep-of-the-month.williamdoyle.ca/) - please check it out if you are looking for a new dRep or SPO).\r\n- I refuse to finance parties with treasury funds. That's pretty much what these summits are.\r\n- The Summit and TOKEN2049 are entirely separate events. They should be separate withdrawals as well.\r\n\r\n## Conclusion\r\n\r\nThis is incredibly silly, especially when the market is as bad as it is these days. Would these two events bring value to the ecosystem? Maybe... but would they bring in 14M ADA worth of value? I doubt it. That money would be better spent on Google Ads - a lot less fun, but probably a lot more profitable. I want to be clear: I enjoy a good party. I really do. But parties are not priorities. I am voting against this proposal.\r\n\r\n\r\nSigned, <br/>\r\nWilliam Doyle\r\n\r\nYour friendly neighbourhood DRep! <br/>\r\n$computerman <br/>\r\ndrep1yfpgzfymq6tt9c684e7vzata8r5pl4w84fmrjqeztdqw0sgpzw3nt <br/>\r\nhttps://x.com/william00000010 <br/>\r\n\r\nNote: [drep-of-the-month.onrender.com](https://drep-of-the-month.onrender.com/) may work better, especially on mobile.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "wolf31o2 (Chris Gianelloni)",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmecBmdkrBXSZad1XHnA6LtpbY8YVkNkDrNRmWBXm2mkWh -->\r\n# wolf31o2 (Chris Gianelloni)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfa8r8r36x7x05htftce7qhafrn5nzzr6vazy95pzy6y5dqac0ss7`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThey're splitting the vote. No on the combined vote here.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YOADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreigl4llbubej6lsk76dp6nauxk45cxbttksvp5ljsahdjrq7aiukam -->\r\n# YOADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y26sfka2km0p4xw073ujdq406wxxczhdyfh9vw7yxpfselchzkdjn`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI’ve decided to abstain as I have mixed feelings. While the event offers great networking opportunities, I believe our budget might be better utilized elsewhere given the current bear market. Have you considered moving to a biennial summit instead?",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "YUTA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmTtEHn2ATQUmS18Sgdc1PuFingF8CJ8tRmKAUCDnxFwGt -->\r\n# YUTA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y2200we9c904un36tzaearntzzl63snffuul9qsk0te4utqfkke0w`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI voted NO on \"Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore\" for the following five reasons.\r\n\r\n1.Lack of verifiable 2025 outcomes, and a regression in 2026 KPIs\r\nThe 2025 proposal set a clear outcome metric: 15-20% year-on-year growth in developer numbers. That was the primary reason I voted YES at the time. It is to CF's credit that they have openly acknowledged this target was not met, but the problem lies beyond that acknowledgment.\r\nThe only concrete success case CF cited in the 2025 Summit context was hackathon silver medalist Ryan Williams. However, he had been deeply involved in Cardano's core standard-setting work well before the Summit, and was not a new developer acquired or onboarded through it. In other words, the number of cases that concretely demonstrate the 2025 goal of \"acquiring and retaining new developers\" is effectively zero.\r\nThe enterprise side is similarly vague. The proposal cites \"Cardano Foundation's proven delivery of four consecutive, globally impactful Cardano Summits,\" and participation from J&J, Volvo, and Mastercard was reported — yet no PoC, production deployment, MOU, or on-chain contribution has been shown.\r\nThe 2026 proposal should have taken a two-step path: (a) demonstrate in a verifiable way what the 2025 investment actually brought to the ecosystem, and (b) explain concretely how 2026 will improve based on that reflection. Instead, the opposite has happened. The developer retention metric has been removed from the proposal and replaced with output indicators such as booth contacts, media impressions, and wallet sign-ups.\r\nLooking at the KPIs in the proposal, TOKEN2049 is measured by booth contacts 1,440, new strategic collaborations 15, wallet sign-ups 200, and Cardano Academy subscribers 200. These are all output indicators — \"number contacted\" and \"number registered\" — not outcome indicators that measure meaningful ecosystem contribution. As the consideration for entrusting ₳14,076,539, this KPI structure lacks proportionality.\r\n\r\n2.Insufficient professionalism to justify a ₳14M-scale allocation\r\nThe proposal allocates $200,000 to \"Project Management, Staffing and Delivery\" on the TOKEN2049 side, with substantial operational budget on the Summit side as well. The question is not the absolute amount, but whether there is, at this point, demonstrable operational professionalism to be trusted with a combined ₳14,076,539 (~$3.66MM).\r\nMy firsthand observations at TEAMZ recently did not support that level of confidence.\r\n* On Day 2, when I arrived at the booth several hours into the event, there were no CF or EMURGO representatives, no client companies, and no English-capable staff present. I did not measure precisely, but in my perception this was not a momentary absence right at my arrival or a brief restroom break — the state continued for a while. At the reception there was one enthusiastic member of the Japanese community, but she was not an English speaker, so handling overseas visitors was realistically difficult. To be clear, I am not claiming they were absent all day; this is a snapshot of the time window during which I was present. This was not during setup — it was during the event itself.\r\n* Cardano had the second largest booth at the venue, and several builders gave presentations, but the audience was under ten people, about 90% of whom were regulars at Cardano events. The underlying goal of reaching new audiences was not achieved.\r\n* While the adjacent Binance booth was bustling throughout the day, there were stretches when the many staff behind the Cardano counter were looking at their smartphones. In my 2025 visit to TEAMZ, attendees were mainly Japanese SWAG collectors, some retail investors, and short-term overseas visitors. Honestly, it was hard for me to imagine real Cardano business originating from this venue, and I recall sharing that feedback in the past. Both EMURGO and CF exhibited in 2025 and should have known the nature of this venue. So I do not intend to fault them for the 2026 booth not being especially lively — but the decision to exhibit there was theirs.\r\n* The TEAMZ booth that CF funded last year was also unattended at the time I arrived \r\n\r\n3.Lack of foundation for placing enterprise adoption at the core\r\nThe proposal positions Day 2 as Industry Day — dedicated to enterprise and institutional adoption. The narrative is attractive, but I have strong doubts.\r\nOver the past several years, significant spending toward enterprise adoption has flowed through multiple channels — IOG, CF, EMURGO, Catalyst — in the form of events, tooling, and direct investment. Despite that, in recent epoch 622 I was unable to identify a single transaction submission attributable to an enterprise (see adatool.net/tx-stats). 99% of usage is retail. This is not Cardano-specific; other major chains show similar patterns.\r\nThe questions the proposal should answer are:\r\n* What are the structural reasons enterprise adoption remains low across the industry?\r\n* Why have Cardano's past efforts not taken root?\r\n* Which of those structural factors does this Summit spend resolve, and through what mechanism?\r\n* Is enterprise adoption really a problem explained by \"lack of awareness\" and \"lack of exposure\"?\r\nThe proposal does not answer these. Unless the mechanism by which Day 2 content connects to on-chain activity or TVL is shown, this becomes hard to elevate above \"producing press release material for retail investors.\" And even for that purpose, I can hardly recall a Cardano-Summit-derived press release that retail investors have highly valued. If enterprise adoption is going to be the banner, the proposal should include structural analysis commensurate with that banner.\r\n\r\n4.Internal-facing nature of the Summit agenda, and the weak case for running it at this scale\r\nLooking at the proposal's agenda, Day 1 (Ecosystem Day) — governance workshops, DRep meetings, committee meetings, Battle of the Builders, internal masterclasses — is largely \"Cardano ecosystem internal-facing\" content.\r\nI do not deny the value of these activities. Governance discussions and builder-community interaction are important and should continue. The question is whether this content warrants a physical event in Singapore — a high-cost location — at a ₳14M-scale budget.\r\nMuch of the internal-facing discussion can be conducted just as well, or more efficiently, online. The intrinsic value of a physical Singapore venue really only applies to content that involves interaction with external audiences — enterprises, institutional investors, external developers, media.\r\nA reasonable response to this concern would look like one of the following:\r\n* Demonstrate, based on past results, what outcomes physical hosting of internal content produces that online hosting cannot\r\n* Or: shift internal-facing content online, narrow the physical portion to external-audience content, show a budget-compression estimate for that alternative, and explain why the current plan is nonetheless superior\r\n\r\n5. Framing the sell-pressure concern, and the proposal's own persuasiveness as a sample\r\n₳14,076,539 corresponds to roughly 2.08 epochs worth of the ~6.77M ADA staking rewards distributed per epoch, and Cardano absorbs this level of sell pressure fairly routinely. What concerns me is not that — it is the higher-order disappointment pressure that sits behind it. I have received strong concerns via DM even from individuals who hold well over twice ₳14,076,539 worth of ADA, and I do not have data with which to reasonably refute their concern. In the Japanese Cardano community chats, this topic is discussed with frustration on a daily basis. If the proposal passes with support this thin, the sell pressure that arrives in the market may not be limited to ₳14,076,539 — and its ceiling is hard to predict.\r\nThe fact that even within a small and relatively friendly Cardano community, this proposal has failed to build marketing consensus, itself raises concern about the ability to execute $3.66MM of marketing in the far harsher environment outside the ecosystem.\r\n\r\n\r\n私は次の５つの理由から「Cardano Summit 2026 and TOKEN2049 Singapore」にNOを投票しました。\r\n\r\n1. 2025年成果の検証可能性不足と、2026年KPIの退行\r\n2025年提案には「開発者数の前年比15–20%成長」という明確なアウトカム指標が掲げられており、当時私がYESを投じた主要理由もここにありました。CFご自身がこの目標未達を率直に認められた点は誠実ですが、問題はその先にあります。\r\n2025年Summit文脈でCFが挙げられた具体的成功事例は、Hackathon銀メダリストのRyan Williams氏お一方のみでした。しかし同氏はSummit以前からCardanoのコア標準策定に深く関与されていた方であり、Summit経由で新規獲得・オンボードされた開発者ではありません。つまり、「2025年提案のゴールであった新規開発者の獲得と定着」を具体的に示すケース数は、事実上ゼロです。\r\nエンタープライズ領域も同様に曖昧です。提案書は「Cardano Foundation's proven delivery of four consecutive, globally impactful Cardano Summits」という実績を掲げていますが、J&J、Volvo、Mastercardらの参加が報告された一方で、PoC、本番導入、MOU、オンチェーン活動への寄与のいずれも示されていません。\r\n本来、2026年提案が取るべき筋道は次の二段階だったはずです — (a) 2025年投資が実際に何をもたらしたかを検証可能な形で示すこと、(b) その反省に基づく2026年の改善点を具体的に説明すること。しかし実際には逆のことが起きています。開発者定着指標は提案書から削除され、代わりに「ブース接触数」「メディア露出」「ウォレットサインアップ数」といったアウトプット指標に置き換えられました。\r\n提案書のKPIを見ると、TOKEN2049については booth contacts 1,440、new strategic collaborations 15、wallet sign-ups 200、Cardano Academy subscribers 200 が並びますが、これらはいずれも「接触した数」「登録した数」のアウトプット指標であり、エコシステムへの実効的寄与を測るアウトカム指標ではありません。\r\n\r\n2. ₳14M規模の資金提供を合理化するプロフェッショナリズムの不足\r\n提案書にはTOKEN2049側の「Project Management, Staffing and Delivery」として $200,000、Summit側にも多額の運営予算が計上されています。金額単体ではなく、合計₳14,076,539(約$3.66MM)という規模の資金をお任せするに足る運営プロフェッショナリズムが、現時点で確認できるかが論点です。\r\nしかし先日のTEAMZでの実観察は、この水準を裏付ける方向には働きませんでした。\r\n\r\n* 2日目、イベント開始から数時間経過した時点で私がブースに到達した際、CF/EMURGO関係者、クライアント企業、英語対応可能なスタッフのいずれも不在でした。正確に計測したわけではありませんが、これは到着直後の一瞬の話やトイレ休憩といった一時的な不在ではなく、しばらくの間その状態が続いていたと私は認識しています。受付には熱心な日本コミュニティのメンバーが1名いらっしゃいましたが英語話者ではなかったため、海外来訪者への対応は困難な状態でした(念のため補足すると、これは「終日不在だった」という意味ではなく、私が滞在していた時間帯のスナップショットです)。準備時間ではなく、イベント本番中の状況です。\r\n* Cardanoは会場で2番目に大きいブースを構え、複数のビルダーがプレゼンを実施されていましたが、聴衆は10名未満で、その9割がCardanoイベントの常連でした。新規層へのリーチという本来目的は果たされていません。\r\n* 隣のBinanceブースが終日活況だった一方、Cardanoブースでは多数のカウンタースタッフがスマートフォンを見て時間を過ごす時間帯がありました。2025年に現地を訪れた経験では、来場者層は主に日本のSWAGコレクター、一部の個人投資家、そして海外からの短期来訪者が中心で、正直なところ、ここからCardanoの実ビジネスが立ち上がるイメージは私には持ちづらく、その旨のフィードバックも過去にお伝えしていた記憶があります。EMURGOもCFも2025年に出展されており、この会場の性質はご存じだったはずです。したがって、2026年のブースがあまり賑わっていなかったこと自体を彼らの責に帰すつもりはありません。ただし、そのイベントに出展を決められたのは他ならぬ彼ら自身です。\r\n* 昨年CFが資金提供されたTEAMZブースについても、私が到達した時点で無人でした\r\n\r\n3. エンタープライズ採用を中核に据えることの根拠不在\r\n提案書ではDay 2が Industry Day — dedicated to enterprise and institutional adoption として設計されています。物語として美しいのですが、私は強い疑問を持っています。\r\n過去数年にわたり、IOG、CF、EMURGO、Catalystなど複数のチャネルから、イベント・ツール・直接投資の形で多額の支出がこの目的のために行われてきました。それにもかかわらず、直近エポック622において、私はエンタープライズ由来と識別可能なトランザクション送信を単一も検出できていません(adatool.net/tx-stats参照)。利用の99%はリテールであり、これはCardano固有ではなく他の主要チェーンでも同様の傾向です。\r\n提案書が答えるべき問いは次のものです。\r\n* 業界全体でエンタープライズ採用が低水準にとどまる構造的要因は何か\r\n* なぜCardano過去の取り組みが定着に至らなかったのか\r\n* 今回のSummit支出がその構造的要因のどれを、どのメカニズムで解消するのか\r\n* エンタープライズ採用は本当に「認知不足」と「接触機会不足」で説明される問題なのか\r\n提案書はこれらに答えていません。Day 2のコンテンツがオンチェーン活動やTVLに結び付くメカニズムが示されない限り、これは「リテール投資家向けのプレスリリース素材作り」以上のものになりにくいと思われます。しかもその効用ですら、過去Summit由来でリテール投資家が高く評価されたプレスリリースを私はほとんど思い出せません。エンタープライズ採用を旗印に掲げられる以上、それに見合う構造分析が提案書に含まれるべきだと考えます。\r\n\r\n4. Summitアジェンダの内部向け性と、この支出規模で実施する必要性の低さ\r\n提案書のアジェンダを見ると、Day 1 (Ecosystem Day) はガバナンスワークショップ、DRepミーティング、Committeeミーティング、Battle of the Builders、内部向けマスタークラスなど、性質として「Cardanoエコシステム内部向け」のコンテンツが相当な比重を占めています。\r\nこれらのコンテンツそのものの価値を否定するつもりはありません。ガバナンス議論やビルダーコミュニティの内部交流は重要であり、継続的に行われるべきです。しかし問題は、これらがSingaporeという高コスト地での物理イベントとして、₳14M規模の予算をかけて実施されるべき性質のコンテンツなのかという点です。\r\n内部向けの議論の多くは、オンラインでも十分に(あるいはむしろ効率的に)実施可能です。Singaporeで物理開催するだけの固有価値があるのは、外部オーディエンス — エンタープライズ、機関投資家、外部開発者、メディア — とのインタラクションが発生するコンテンツに限られると考えます。\r\nこの点に対する合理的な応答があるとすれば、次のいずれかだと思います。\r\n* 内部向けコンテンツを物理開催することで、オンライン開催では得られないどのような成果が生まれるのか、過去実績ベースで示すこと\r\n* あるいは、内部向けコンテンツをオンラインに移し、物理開催部分を外部オーディエンス向けに絞った場合の予算圧縮試算を示した上で、現行案がそれよりなお優れる理由を説明すること\r\n\r\n5. 売り圧論点の整理と、提案書の説得力そのもののサンプル性\r\n₳14,076,539はエポックあたり約6.77M ADAのステーキング報酬配布の約2.08エポック分に相当し、Cardanoはこのレベルの売り圧に対してある程度日常的に吸収していますが心配なのは、その先にあるより高次の失望圧です。すでに₳14,076,539の倍以上のADAを保有する人物からも強い懸念のDMをもらっています。私はその懸念に合理的に反論できるデータを持っていません。Cardano日本コミュニティのチャットでは毎日この話題が怒りと共に話されています。このような低いコミュニティの支持のままに、可決された場合は、₳14,076,539に留まらない、上限の予測の難しい売り圧がマーケットに訪れる可能性があります。\r\n小規模で相対的に友好的なCardanoコミュニティ内ですら、この提案書ではマーケティングの合意形成ができていないという事実そのものが、エコシステム外部のはるかに厳しい環境で$3.66MM規模のマーケティングを実行する能力への懸念を、それ自体として惹起します。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    }
  ],
