    {
      "voter": "CaFi",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSSdNLdzxtxXLH45aEzmm79AV8pYDvTowJTYarFuwctxg -->\r\n# CaFi\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23djskdpwsutv5xz34dz4nmkhvqfdxnmu7r7cfye4e2exc5slwpf`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote yes because the Extended Quadratic Funding model doesn't replace Project Catalyst but complements it, bringing additional funding, greater participation, and enhanced accountability to Cardano's innovation ecosystem.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardanians",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmfJckcuNwmLmihrYwy6ToJtQC874bN5LZPfmApSjNUPSX -->\r\n# Cardanians\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yt4lyf0fwlrz8k6j5evd3rxw0sqp67qkh36su98a97q3qsc0h03y4`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Long-Term Sustainability**\r\nExploring complementary funding models like Quadratic Funding can add value to Cardano’s governance system. It supports experimentation in decentralized grant distribution, which is aligned with long-term ecosystem evolution.\r\n\r\n**Builder and Ecosystem Growth**\r\nIf executed well, this could channel funds to underrepresented community builders and broaden funding access. However, it remains experimental and does not directly support tooling, infrastructure, or builders in its current form.\r\n\r\n**Decentralization and Community Engagement**\r\nQuadratic Funding promotes more democratic participation in treasury allocation. That said, the proposal lacks clarity on how outcomes will be measured, how feedback will be incorporated, and how this pilot integrates with existing Catalyst structures.\r\n\r\n**Responsible Treasury Spending**\r\n₳1.5 million is excessive for an experimental pilot with unclear deliverables and no phased rollout plan. While we support the idea, the scope should be reduced and focused. We recommend voting NO on this version and encourage a leaner resubmission with tighter milestones, community co-design, and measurable outcomes.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Africa DRep",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreiatbkmk5ns6jj5k63zpc7u5p4gc6qo3oop2lzwyq3cnbh3ayqltca -->\r\n# Cardano Africa DRep\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytj9kz0n5yamacgcj8jr6apn36hx5suzqpefxvhy4cvfqmsqangtx`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe vote YES on the treasury withdrawal of ₳1,500,000 for “Complement Catalyst: Extended Quadratic Funding Zero Operational Costs” based on the rationale below:\r\n\r\nProject Catalyst has proven its value, but it has also revealed structural weaknesses: concentrated voter power, slow milestone processes, and a lack of standardized impact reporting. This proposal does not seek to replace Catalyst, but to strengthen it with a complementary quadratic funding model that democratizes decision-making, attracts co-funding, and enforces accountability through measurable impact\r\n\r\nThe vendor, Socious, has a proven track record in identity, impact measurement, and funding platforms. Coupled with Intersect’s oversight and Sundae Labs’ audited treasury management tooling, delivery risk appears manageable.",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Cardano Cypherpunks",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmSDfd9x9DUWDLeuJDLxnZA5e7CmGvJK5aM8bean8vKrKs -->\r\n# Cardano Cypherpunks\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** No\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1y23wk4w6f2aumc92vl9m3x74xzm6jh4ha9wdq09yfq2sl6q8zlv4l`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nQuadratic voting is devaluation of ADA.\r\nBig no.",
