    {
      "voter": "Peter Bui",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pbwebdev/drep/refs/heads/main/r/25/250812_quadfunding_e0b3334da88a.jsonld -->\r\n# Peter Bui\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yftc8zs7gjcj4a9nxzplz4wg6cwweya0kxp8adnw59vsyrqvrysud`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis proposal pilots quadratic funding with a reputation factor to broaden participation and match donations with treasury funds. The team has a strong record from past Catalyst work and relevant Identus expertise. Intersect’s process includes separate accounts, milestone reviews, and third-party oversight. The ₳1.5M request is part of the approved budget and has support from other DReps assessing similar withdrawals.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/portocripto/drep-entry/refs/heads/main/votes/GA050-info-ncl-rationale.jsonld -->\r\n# Porto Cripto DRep 🇧🇷 🇵🇹 (Atico & Bosco, from Cardanistas Stake Pool - CARDs)\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ywuk39acvmkzda9e8kfmy7fwf946jd5uaa4l696atlas66s68f0fl`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n[Portuguese]\r\nOptamos por votar \"SIM\" nesta ação de governança (gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlzw4qas92), pois é preciso avaliar outros modelos de financiamento coletivo comunitário além do modelo do Catalyst, e o modelo de Financiamento Quadrático Estendido proposto está alinhado com princípios que podem beneficiar o próprio Catalyst a partir do seu resultado. Além disso, a justificativa de gastos apresentada, bem como as métricas de avaliação e controle, foram bem apresentadas.\r\n[English]\r\nWe chose to vote \"YES\" on this governance action (gov_action13tfag48nf94rtjcdq7c06vhkslmxxw9h6c88sl7q5g5nnewcsvlzw4qas92), because it is necessary to evaluate other models of community crowdfunding beyond the Catalyst model, and the proposed Extended Quadratic Funding model is aligned with principles that can benefit Catalyst itself based on its results. Furthermore, the expense justification presented, as well as the evaluation and control metrics, were well presented.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "punkr",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmNP1TLmyXreBSwJJ1Q1y5n9wo5h6eNLW4ttX8p2uYpdWK -->\r\n# punkr\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfyl9j6amk940g76r7ujnn5gywnjenv3kmun3a5tr5a83psl4vv64`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI support this treasury withdrawal for Complement Catalyst because it offers a new funding approach that tackles issues like concentrated voting power, making Cardano more appealing to new projects and participants.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "RCADA",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmY92JpHL5Y4esqAGN1uKhmvhxAcwduejp4imy86CCFwAN -->\r\n# RCADA\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Abstain\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yf7kjx5rlyuyzxkr4dzyccdfs8tesh29amrtcpyplu3asnqjgmdz3`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRCADA has chosen to** abstain at this time while reserving the option to review and update this vote prior to the voting deadline**. This approach allows RCADA to allocate focus where immediate evaluation is most impactful, particularly on proposals that are close to threshold or raise significant procedural or constitutional concerns. If this proposal reaches the approv-al threshold prior to our review, the abstention will stand as a neutral signal of deferral, not op-position. Should further analysis be warranted, RCADA will update this vote accordingly.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Rudianos",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/Qmb9PFz8JoRogdyaCMaQghhtJAHvH8DMhhhaffhg65djve -->\r\n# Rudianos\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfv77z2fsz7nucy59lx2pkafamathf8q783lalkr3quju0gv93lq2`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am voting in favor of approving the treasury withdrawal for all 39 withdrawal actions that are part of the approved ecosystem budget administered by Intersect. I am voting this way for several reasons, as I will outline here. This rationale will be included in all 39 withdrawal votes.\r\nFirst and foremost, I believe that we would be making a mistake in underfunding our community with our available treasury funds. The budget system as it currently stands has some flaws, as should be expected from a first version of any system. Of the current proposals, I voted to include several in the budget when it was being formed; however, I also did not vote in favor of several others. This is, of course, the case for most DReps. If I were to vote only for the proposals I initially favoured, and all other DReps did the same, we would likely approve only 2 or 3 proposals out of 39 due to the vote split. In my view, this is not an acceptable outcome for the community, and this is why I was also opposed to the idea of having 39 separate treasury withdrawal actions. I have reviewed all 39 requests, and they all have merit. Are they exactly in line with the priorities I wanted as part of the initial budget? No. Is that reason enough to vote no on several of these and end up approving only 2 or 3 proposals in the end? I certainly don't believe so.\r\nIn addition to this, the total amount of the intersect budget is roughly 10% higher than what I voted for, and I find that to be within an acceptable margin to approve all the withdrawals.\r\nThe individual proposals also all received at least 50% community approval to be included and will be subject to reviews and milestones to receive funds.\r\nFor these reasons, I am casting my vote to approve and am wishing the best of luck to all the teams waiting for funding through this process.",
      "vote": "NO"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SASA_nagamaru_ながまる",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://most-brass-sun.quicknode-ipfs.com/ipfs/QmQff1kBRmmF8tcWf7V45q5uUbd95XvuM3SkUPQLrXFPXr -->\r\n# SASA_nagamaru_ながまる\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ytuddrgqca0xd4aams6pl9zndpcmxg0rs7z3mggjelm6kscp4arg5`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI vote Yes on this proposal.\r\n\r\nThis initiative introduces an extended quadratic funding model to complement Catalyst, aiming to address issues such as vote centralization, unclear ROI, and inefficient milestone processes.\r\n\r\nKey components—like donation matching, reputation-weighted voting, Sybil resistance via Hyperledger Identus, and decentralized dispute resolution—are based on existing technologies and models. While the system is ambitious, the design reflects a thoughtful integration of proven mechanisms, making the implementation path relatively grounded.\r\n\r\nI support this proposal as a promising step toward diversifying Cardano’s funding architecture and improving the ecosystem’s overall accountability and inclusiveness.\r\n\r\n私はこの提案に Yes を投じます。\r\n\r\n本提案は、Catalystを補完する拡張型二次資金配分モデルを通じて、投票権の偏りやROIの不透明さといった課題に挑む意欲的な試みです。\r\n\r\n寄付マッチングやレピュテーションスコア、Hyperledger Identusを活用したSybil耐性など、構想の多くは既存技術に基づいており、実装に向けた要素設計も一定の現実性を持っています。\r\n\r\nCardanoの資金配分とエコシステム成長の多様化に貢献する提案として支持します。",
      "vote": "YES"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIDAN Lab",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreieanomlr5im3xm7okq2ijjcznhwejlaji53cmtunotp2ufx7pefku -->\r\n# SIDAN Lab\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yfjez5zup0gystdvc933w2mn8k64hcy3krvc2namluwjxdcfhm8wd`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWe initially access a no vote for this since the budget seems too high for an experimental project like this. We also acknowledge that even the chance of achieving all potential impacts is not as certain. However, upon further understanding, we eventually determined to cast a yes vote due to the fact that the proposal would attract external donations to the Cardano ecosystem, plus the feedback can be provided back to other projects like Catalyst to improve the system.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "SIPO",
      "content": "<!-- url: https://sipo.tokyo/drep/ga/GA_TreasuryWithdrawal2025_01/29_Complement_Catalyst_20250721/Vote_Context.jsonld -->\r\n# SIPO\r\n\r\n**Proposal:** Withdraw ₳1,500,000 for Complement Catalyst Extended Quadratic Funding---Zer\r\n**Vote:** Yes\r\n**Voter ID:** `drep1yffld2866p00cyg3ejjdewtvazgah7jjgk0s9m7m5ytmmdq33v3zh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSIPO has voted “Yes” on this proposal because it offers a complementary and innovative funding mechanism that amplifies the impact of the Cardano Treasury while promoting fairness, transparency, and long-term sustainability.\r\n\r\nKey Reasons for Support\r\n\r\n1. A Complementary Extended Quadratic Funding Model\r\n\t•\tThis proposal does not aim to replace Project Catalyst, but rather to enhance and complement it.\r\n\t•\tIt integrates Quadratic Funding with a reputation-based voting system, balancing community influence and financial commitment while avoiding concentration of voting power.\r\n\t•\tZK-KYC via Hyperledger Identus ensures Sybil resistance while preserving user privacy.\r\n\r\n2. Treasury as a Funding Catalyst, Not Sole Funder\r\n\t•\tThe model encourages co-funding from individual donors, potentially boosting the effective funding pool by over 50%.\r\n\t•\t501(c)(3) tax deduction eligibility for U.S. donors offers incentives beyond the crypto-native community.\r\n\r\n3. Standardized Impact Reporting for Real ROI Measurement\r\n\t•\tAll funded projects must report on KPIs such as on-chain transactions, new wallets, active users, etc.\r\n\t•\tThis would be the first standardized ROI dataset in Cardano’s innovation ecosystem, enabling informed governance and better treasury management.\r\n\r\n4. Sustainable Ecosystem Value Capture\r\n\t•\tFunded projects are encouraged to return value to the ecosystem via token allocation, equity, or revenue-sharing.\r\n\t•\tThe goal is a 5% annual return within 10 years, aligning with venture fund benchmarks for sustainable impact.\r\n\r\n5. Streamlined Milestone Process\r\n\t•\tThe model addresses Catalyst’s slow milestone approval with token-based reviewer incentives, penalties for inaccurate judgments, and a decentralized dispute resolution process.\r\n\t•\tThis is especially beneficial for smaller projects that often suffer from procedural bottlenecks.\r\n\r\n6. Execution Capacity and Governance Integrity\r\n\t•\tSocious is a fast-growing impact startup supported by major players like Google, Microsoft, Amazon, and 500Global, with deep expertise in funding mechanisms, identity systems, and blockchain.\r\n\t•\tThe implementation will be legally bound under Intersect-led smart contract frameworks, with oversight from trusted third-party organizations (e.g., Cardano Foundation, NMKR, Xerberus, etc.).\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nSIPO believes that this proposal will advance Cardano’s funding infrastructure by enabling a more equitable and participatory distribution of resources. In particular, the effective utilization of treasury funds, democratization of participation, transparent impact evaluation, and the design of sustainable returns are seen as essential enhancements toward the foundation of Cardano 2.0.\r\n\r\nTherefore, SIPO has voted in favor of this proposal.\r\n\r\n⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻⸻\r\n\r\nSIPOは、本提案がカルダノ・エコシステム全体に対して革新的かつ持続可能な資金配分モデルを提供するものであると評価し、「Yes」として投票しました。\r\n\r\n賛成の主な理由\r\n\r\n① カルダノ・トレジャリーの資金インパクトを増幅させる「拡張型二次投票」モデル\r\n\t•\t本提案は、既存のProject Catalystを代替するものではなく、補完する仕組みとして、財務効率・民主性・透明性の向上を目指しています。\r\n\t•\t**Quadratic Funding（QF）と評判スコア（300–850の範囲）**を組み合わせることで、少額多数の支援者の声を反映し、富の集中を防ぎながら貢献度を重視した投票システムを実現します。\r\n\t•\tハイパーレジャーIdentusを用いたZK-KYCにより、プライバシーを守りつつ、Sybil耐性を確保しています。\r\n\r\n② トレジャリー資金のレバレッジ効果\r\n\t•\t提案モデルは、トレジャリーを単独出資者ではなく、「呼び水」として活用。寄付参加者によるマッチング資金調達により、最大で50%以上の追加資金流入を促します。\r\n\t•\t米国の501(c)(3)認定による寄付控除インセンティブも活用され、暗号資産圏外からの参加も期待されます。\r\n\r\n③ エコシステム全体のROIを可視化する「標準化されたインパクト報告」\r\n\t•\t支援プロジェクトには、オンチェーン活動、ユーザー数、新規ウォレット数などのKPIを含む報告義務が課され、カルダノ初のイノベーションROIデータセットが構築されます。\r\n\r\n④ 持続可能な価値還元モデル\r\n\t•\tトークン・株式・収益シェア等によるエコシステムへの還元を奨励し、VC標準に基づく年5%のリターン目標を設定。\r\n\t•\tこれはカルダノトレジャリーの中長期的な持続可能性確保に資すると判断しました。\r\n\r\n⑤ マイルストーン管理の合理化\r\n\t•\tCatalystでの小規模提案が直面する審査遅延問題を回避するため、審査報酬・ペナルティ・分散型紛争解決を導入した仕組みを設計。\r\n\t•\tスピードと正確性のバランスをとる自己調整型のプロセスが構築されています。\r\n\r\n⑥ 信頼性の高い実行体制と透明性\r\n\t•\tSociousは、Project Catalyst、Deep Funding、Gitcoinでの経験を持ち、Microsoft・Google・Amazon・500Globalの支援を受ける急成長スタートアップです。\r\n\t•\t開発・運営チームは、日本や国際的なカルダノコミュニティと連携しており、公正性・説明責任・法的整合性に基づいた運用が約束されています。\r\n\t•\tIntersectによるスマートコントラクト管理と5団体による第三者監査体制も信頼性を裏付けています。\r\n\r\n結論\r\n\r\nSIPOは、本提案がカルダノの資金調達インフラを進化させ、より公平で参加型の資金分配を実現すると信じています。とくに、トレジャリー資金の最大活用、参加の民主化、透明なインパクト評価、持続可能なリターン設計は、Cardano 2.0に向けた重要な基盤強化であると考えます。\r\n\r\nしたがって、SIPOはこの提案に賛成票を投じました。",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
