    {
      "voter": "Goofycrisp",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreidpbs5h6ayy55shf5obbdxv3lsp6adb6a4q4vqphb5ehyhokc5uiq -->\n# Goofycrisp\n\n**Proposal:** IO & Midgard Labs L2 Scalability Initiative\n**Vote:** Yes\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygxasnzmrevqra9vscpsy4xf4rqthzkp6rr6zzft2lc7nscahj9r9`\n\n---\n\nScaling is one of Cardano’s most important priorities, and supporting multiple paths for growth is strategically important. This proposal carries execution risk, but it is led by highly respected builders and presents a differentiated approach to L2 development that could strengthen Cardano without simply copying the more extractive L2 models seen elsewhere. I believe this is worth supporting.",
      "vote": "UNKNOWN"
    },
    {
      "voter": "Hermes Stakepool Germany (HRMS)",
      "content": "<!-- url: ipfs://bafkreige2jfc2mplvo3teflqq6imfchyjr62x46dnvqmafwhfax6m4qlqq -->\n# Hermes Stakepool Germany (HRMS)\n\n**Proposal:** IO & Midgard Labs L2 Scalability Initiative\n**Vote:** No\n**Voter ID:** `drep1ygs5hngva3hymv7j4v0aewxpsjqskj9dnmy7j3jz5ven5zqvulq2t`\n\n---\n\nAs Cardanians say: \"I’m voting NO because this proposal asks for ₳ 10 million while bundling multiple workstreams with different maturity and risk profiles, without providing the level of cost traceability and milestone evidence that a multi-million-ADA treasury withdrawal requires.\"",
      "vote": "NO"
